{
  "raw": {
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Building-a-Local-AI-Personalized-assistant-for-Hand-Drawn-Animation-Artist-with-ComfyUI-_R00025674": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Building a Local AI Personalized assistant for Hand Drawn Animation Artist with ComfyUI)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Art, Design and Media (ADM) is a premier creative hub in Singapore, renowned for combining art, technology, and design. We are seeking a Research Assistant to work on an exciting project using ComfyUI to build a personalized, local AI assistant for a hand-drawn animation artist. You will support world-renowned animator Professor Raimund Krumme during his two-month residency at ADM (Mid Sept–Mid Nov 2026), helping to bring his strictly analogue, ink-and-brush process into a local, privacy-safe AI workflow — one that is genuinely simple for a non-technical artist to pick up and use. Key Responsibilities: Set up and optimize local, open-source AI models (Stable Diffusion/ComfyUI) on high-end workstation hardware, with no cloud dependency. Train local LoRAs and ControlNets on a curated archive of the artist's analogue sketches and scans. Package the ComfyUI workflow into a simple, easy-to-run form (e.g. presets, node groups, or a lightweight Gradio front-end) that the artist can operate independently. Provide on-the-ground technical support during Prof. Krumme's residency (14 Sept – 13 Nov 2026). Document the system architecture and user-testing feedback for the final research report. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Animation, Film Studies, Media Studies or a related discipline. Hands-on experience with ComfyUI and local AI deployments (Automatic1111, Forge, etc.), including training LoRAs/ControlNets. Understanding of local hardware optimization (GPU/VRAM management). Comfortable putting together a simple working interface for a workflow (e.g. Gradio) — no formal UX/UI design background required. Able to translate an artist's creative intent into technical parameters, with patience for working with a non-technical collaborator. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-Chinese-Linguistics--SOH-_R00025679": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in Chinese Linguistics (SOH)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Humanities at NTU invites applications for part-time teaching of courses in the Department of Chinese in the field of Linguistics (and/or any sub-disciplines in Linguistics and Languages, including but not limited to Chinese Pragmatics, Discourse Analysis, Language Typology, Language Acquisition, Sociolinguistics etc.). For each course, the instructor will be responsible for leading classes as well as planning the syllabus, class preparation, devising and marking assignments, and handling student consultations. The course is to be taught in Chinese. Candidates should have an advanced degree and a proven track-record in teaching. That is, candidates will only be considered if they have the following: Master’s degree or higher Teaching experience at a tertiary level Applications should include the following: CV Evidence of teaching excellence if any (e.g., teaching evaluations or reference letters) Only shortlisted candidates will be notified​.  Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Synthetic-Biology---Enzyme-Design-_R00023788": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Synthetic Biology & Enzyme Design)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance biological and biomedical sciences. At SBS, our research spans various areas, including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative diseases, telomere biology, and genome function. Over the years, SBS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sbs . We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow (RF) to join our team in the field of synthetic biology and enzyme design. This role focuses on developing novel biocatalysts and synthetic pathways through cutting-edge research. The successful candidate will contribute to impactful projects while gaining exposure to advanced methodologies in synthetic biology. Key Responsibilities: Lead the design, construction, and optimization of synthetic biological systems and enzyme engineering workflows. Execute advanced molecular biology techniques, including DNA manipulation, PCR, and molecular cloning. Conduct protein expression, purification, and characterization using methods such as spectrophotometry, HPLC, and SDS-PAGE. Analyze experimental data, maintain meticulous records, and contribute to manuscript preparation for high-impact journals. Job Requirements: PhD in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Synthetic Biology, or a related field (completed or near completion). Strong expertise in molecular cloning, protein engineering, and synthetic biology tools (e.g., CRISPR, metabolic pathway design). Ability to work independently, solve complex problems, and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced research environment. Interested candidates should submit the following documents: A cover letter detailing research interests and relevant experience. A current CV, including contact information for two references. Transcripts (if applicable). The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Content---Web-Management-Specialist_R00025671": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Content & Web Management Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAbout Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Nanyang Technological University, Singapore is a research-intensive public university that ranks consistently among the world's leading institutions. Our colleges span engineering, science, medicine, business, and the humanities, arts and social sciences, and our campus is regularly recognised as one of the greenest in the world. Sustainability and the environment sit at the heart of what the University researches, teaches, and stands for. About the Asian School of the Environment The Asian School of the Environment brings together earth science, ecology, environmental social science, and engineering to tackle the environmental and climate challenges facing Asia. The School works closely with the Earth Observatory of Singapore, a research centre that studies earthquakes, volcanoes, tsunamis, and climate change across Southeast Asia and beyond. Our communications team carries that work to students, research partners, policymakers, and the wider public. The role We are looking for a Senior Assistant Manager, Content & Web Management Specialist Content & Web Management Specialist to build and run our websites, and to design the graphics and animations that bring our research to life online. This is a hands-on role that pairs technical website work with real creative production. Three things that make this role worth your attention: You will own the web presence. This is not a role where you wait for a queue of tickets. You will manage our sites end to end, decide how they are built and structured, and see your work go live in front of a global audience. The work is genuinely varied. In a single week you might fix a domain configuration, build a new landing page, illustrate a research finding, and animate a title sequence. If you have been looking for a role that uses both halves of your skill set, this is one. The subject matter matters. You will be communicating research on climate, natural hazards, and sustainability, working directly with the scientists doing it. What you will do Manage, update, and publish content across our websites, which run on a mix of platforms including Sitefinity, Wix, GoDaddy Website Builder, and WordPress. Build new pages, landing pages, and microsites, and support redesigns and platform migrations from planning through to launch. Look after the technical health of our sites, covering domains, records, certificates, redirects, page speed, search visibility, and accessibility. Design graphics, illustrations, infographics, banners, and layouts for our websites, social media channels, events, and publications. Create motion graphics and animations for the web and for social media, including explainer sequences, titles, and lightweight web animations. Produce visual content for our social media channels, including Instagram, LinkedIn, TikTok, X, Bluesky, Facebook, and YouTube. Work with faculty, researchers, and colleagues across the School and the Earth Observatory to turn complex research into clear, well-designed digital content. Build the templates, workflows, and design systems that let the whole team work faster and more consistently. The position is based at the University's Yunnan Garden campus at 50 Nanyang Avenue, Singapore, within the Asian School of the Environment. Why join us Scope to grow. You will work across web development, design, motion graphics, and analytics, and have room to deepen whichever of those you want to build a career on. Learning and development. Staff have access to the University's professional development programmes, course subsidies, and internal training. Career progression. Clear progression pathways within the University's professional and administrative career tracks, with the option to move across schools, centres, and central functions. A working environment built around people. Flexible and hybrid working arrangements, generous leave, comprehensive healthcare and insurance coverage, and staff wellbeing, recreation, and community activities including Campus Recreation and Wellness (CREW). A campus worth showing up to. One of the greenest university campuses in the world, with sports and recreation facilities, food options, and on-campus amenities. Work that has an audience. Our research reaches national and international media, policymakers, and the public, and the design and web work you do is a visible part of how it lands. What you must have A degree or diploma in communications, digital media, interactive media, graphic or visual design, computer science, information technology, or a related field. Equivalent professional experience with a strong portfolio will also be considered. At least [3] years of hands-on experience combining website management with graphic design and motion graphics. Proven experience managing several live websites at once, on more than one platform, including day-to-day updates and building new pages. Working knowledge of website builders and content management systems such as Sitefinity, Wix, GoDaddy Website Builder, and WordPress. Practical front-end skills in HTML and CSS, with enough JavaScript to handle embeds, third-party scripts, and basic troubleshooting in browser developer tools. Confidence with domain and hosting basics, including domain records, redirects, and certificates. Strong command of Adobe Illustrator, Photoshop, and InDesign. Strong command of Adobe After Effects for motion graphics and animation. An understanding of responsive design, web accessibility, page performance, and on-page search optimisation. A portfolio and showreel showing both website work and design or animation work. Please tell us what your specific role was on each piece. The ability to manage several projects and deadlines at once, and to explain technical constraints clearly to people who are not technical. Good to have Direct experience with Progress Sitefinity specifically. Figma, for web and interface design, prototyping, and design handoff. Lottie or Bodymovin, for exporting animations to the web. DaVinci Resolve, or equivalent experience in another professional video editing application. Experience communicating scientific, research, or technical subjects to general audiences. Experience in a university, research institute, public sector, or non-profit setting. Google Analytics 4, Search Console, and Tag Manager. Experience with website redesigns, replatforming, or content management system migrations. Version control with Git, and CSS frameworks such as Bootstrap or Tailwind. 3D or advanced motion tools such as Blender or Cinema 4D, data visualisation, or scientific illustration. Photography or videography, and experience directing freelancers or student assistants. How to apply Please submit your CV together with a portfolio or personal website and a showreel. Include links to live websites you have built or managed. We review every application but regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Visiting-Professor_R00025673": {
      "title": "Visiting Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. The School of Social Sciences (SSS) and Nanyang Centre for Public Administration (NCPA) of College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences at NTU Singapore is seeking outstanding candidates with a well-deﬁned research vision and an outstanding track record of publications in top journals to apply for a Visiting Professorship position. The successful applicant will collaborate and mentor with faculty members and researchers. Appointee will be required to teach on areas relating to seminars in Human Geography and Public Administration. Appointee may be required to mentor junior faculty and researchers in these areas may be involved in giving a few seminars to the faculty and the postgraduate students. The appointee is expected to Contribute to the development and implementation of postgraduate curricula in public policly and publc adminstration and related fields. Enhance NCPA’s visibility as an international leader in education and research. Collaborate and mentor junior faculty and researchers Deliver engaging and effective teaching to graduate students. Mentor and supervise gradutes students. Requirements: PhD in Human Geography or Public Administration. Strong research record and relevant publications in reputable peer-reviewed international journals and conferences. A good track record of supervising research staff, postdocs, graduate students in relevant fields Experienced in cross-disciplinary research initiatives and collaboration. Demonstrated excellence in research, evidenced by a strong publication record in reputable journals Recognition in the research community, such as invited talks, awards, or memberships in professional societies. Applicants are invited to submit their applications through the NTU career portal by clicking on the “Apply” button above. The closing date for applications is 11 Sep 2026. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified via email. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Head-Payroll--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00025159": {
      "title": "Assistant Head/Payroll (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Assistant Head/Payroll with the Finance Department . Responsibilities Reporting to the Head/Finance, you will play a key role in supporting payroll administration, budget monitoring, financial operations and related governance matters. Your responsibilities will include: Oversee and administer the full spectrum of payroll operations, ensuring timely and accurate processing of salaries, payments and related payroll transactions. Ensure compliance with relevant statutory and regulatory requirements, including the CPF Act, Employment Act, Income Tax Act and other applicable payroll-related legislation. Monitor manpower budgets, track utilisation and prepare manpower expenditure forecasts to support financial planning and management reporting. Administer the Institute’s Operating budget, including budget allocation, utilisation review and follow-up on variances or funding requirements. Oversee the processing, review and governance of overseas travel claims, ensuring compliance with institutional policies and financial guidelines. Oversee accounting matters relating to self-financing programmes and conference funds, including fund monitoring, reconciliations and financial reporting. Administer NIE’s insurance policies, including policy renewals, claims coordination and liaison with relevant stakeholders on insurance-related matters. Work closely with internal stakeholders to improve finance processes, strengthen controls and support the effective delivery of finance services. Requirements A University degree in Accountancy or a related field. At least 5 years of accounting and managerial experience. A member of the ISCA (The Institute of Singapore Chartered Accountants). Strong interpersonal, organizational, communication and writing skills. Strong conceptualization and analytical skills. Highly Proficient in Microsoft Office Applications. Self-motivated, able to work independently and as a team player. Knowledge of SAP S/4Hana would be an advantage. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 10 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Learning-Innovations--Centre-for-Innovation-in-Learning---NIE-_R00024614": {
      "title": "Manager, Learning Innovations (Centre for Innovation in Learning) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE is seeking a highly organised and detail-oriented Learning Innovations Manager to join the Centre for Innovation in Learning. Reporting directly to the Senior Assistant Head, the appointee will be essential in advancing data-driven innovations in teaching and learning, providing strategic direction for integrating emerging technologies and learning analytics. The appointee will work closely with other teams to adopt proven educational technologies and data-driven tools that enable real-time feedback loops for faculty and students to foster personalised learning. The appointee should understand the higher education landscape deeply and demonstrate strong leadership and facilitation skills, particularly in guiding faculty and teams to leverage learning analytics for optimising teaching practices and student outcomes. This is a 2-year contract position. Responsibilities Strategic Leadership: Provide strategic direction and establish clear, achievable goals for the Learning Innovations team, fostering a culture of innovation and data-driven decision-making. Manage the team’s resources (e.g., tools, software, training) to ensure the effective integration of learning analytics dashboards and other emerging technologies to support teaching and learning innovations. Oversee the team’s performance by assigning tasks strategically, offering guidance, and developing the team's skills to ensure alignment with institutional goals. Communicate team achievements and project outcomes related to learning analytics, and data-driven innovations in teaching and learning to IN-Learning’s management through comprehensive reports. Oversee team performance reviews, provide coaching, and create an environment that fosters collaboration and open communication. Champion Data-Driven Innovation in Teaching and Learning: Lead the development and integration of evidence-based frameworks and pedagogically sound design solutions, incorporating teacher-facing and student-facing learning analytics dashboards to optimise teaching and learning experiences. Analyse teaching and learning datasets, uncover insights, and identify opportunities for continuous improvement in teaching practices and learning environments at NIE. Present data-driven findings and innovative design solutions to stakeholders, ensuring alignment with best practices in educational technology and learning sciences. Collaborate on faculty professional development programs, equipping faculty with the skills to utilise learning analytics dashboards effectively in their teaching practices. Collaboration for Faculty Professional Development: Work with cross-departmental teams to develop strategies for faculty engagement and professional development, leveraging learning analytics insights to inform instructional design and personalised learning approaches. Spearhead the development and facilitation of professional development programmes that help faculty integrate learning analytics into their course design, enabling data-driven decisions that improve student outcomes. Lead collaboration efforts to share institute-wide knowledge on data-driven teaching and learning. Research and Stay Abreast of Best Practices: Stay informed about emerging trends in educational technologies and learning analytics on a local and global scale, ensuring that the Learning Innovations team remains at the forefront of data-driven teaching and learning innovations. Conduct research on the latest educational technology advancements and synthesise findings to continuously enhance teaching and learning experiences. Lead Special Projects: Participate in and lead special projects to advance teaching and learning through data analytics, AI edtech and other innovative educational technologies. Collaborate across teams to develop and implement data-informed instructional strategies, using teacher-facing and student-facing dashboards to provide real-time feedback for continuous improvement in both faculty performance and student learning outcomes. Requirements A University degree in Learning Sciences, Instructional Design, Educational Technology or a related field. A minimum of 5 years of experience in educational technology, learning analytics, or a related field within a higher education setting, with demonstrated leadership in integrating learning analytics into teaching and learning. Proven supervisory experience, including managing or mentoring others in a data-driven educational technology environment. Strong knowledge of emerging educational technologies and the ability to integrate these into data-informed teaching and learning practices. Experience in data analysis to uncover themes and trends and the ability to interpret teacher-facing and student-facing learning analytics to support data-driven decision-making. Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and meet deadlines. Experience in delivering education programmes that support faculty in leveraging learning analytics and using emerging educational tools effectively. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present complex data in a clear and actionable manner for diverse stakeholders, including faculty and senior leadership. Experience with data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, PowerBI) will be an advantage, particularly in the creation of interactive dashboards for faculty and students. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 16 September 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Behavioural-Research---Community-Archetype-Analysis-_R00024702": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Climate Risk Perception & Community Behavioural Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE), Nanyang Technological University, is the host school for the project “Building Community Resilience Against Sea-Level Rise” (Grant H2_2024-3_T10). The project is funded by the National Parks Board (NParks) under the Marine Climate Change Science Coastal Protection (MCCS) call and brings together CEE and the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) to integrate geospatial modelling, behavioural risk-perception research, agent-based simulation, and community engagement design in support of Singapore’s coastal adaptation efforts. We are looking for a Research Fellow (Climate Risk Perception & Community Behavioural Research) to lead Modules A and B for the NParks MCCS project: baseline research on how residents and businesses perceive and respond to sea-level rise and coastal flood risk, behavioural experiments, and community archetype identification via LCA. Key Responsibilities : Lead Module A: Baseline behavioural research on risk perception, risk tolerance, and adaptation readiness among residents and businesses, using surveys, in-depth interviews, focus groups, and behavioural experiments. Lead Module B: Community archetype identification and mapping using latent-class methods. Coordinate cross-module integration of archetype outputs across the project team. Present findings to the project team, NParks and other agency partners, and community stakeholders. Co-author the Risk Perception and Adaptation Readiness Report. Contribution to conference presentations and top-tier journal publications. Job Requirements: PhD in Communication Studies, Psychology, Behavioural Science, Sociology, Public Policy, Environmental Social Science, Environmental Psychology, Human Geography, or related. Familiarity with environmental, climate change, sea-level rise, or sustainability-related behavioural research, including risk perception, climate adaptation behaviour, or science/risk communication. Survey/instrument design, behavioural experimental design, and large-scale data collection experience. LCA, multinomial logistic regression, SEM, factor analysis (R/Stata/SPSS/Mplus). Qualitative research skills: in-depth interviewing, focus group facilitation, and qualitative analysis (NVivo). Strong spoken and written communication, including oral presentation of findings to academic, agency, and community audiences, and a track record of academic writing. Ability to coordinate cross-functional research teams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Health---Safety--LKCMedicine-_R00025670": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Health & Safety [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The jobholder will support the Health and Safety (H&S) team lead in LKCMedicine and enhance H&S culture within the School. He/she will influence stakeholders such as the H&S committee and safety reps in LKCMedicine to achieve objectives for the team. The jobholder will be based at Experimental Medicine Building (EMB) and is expected to commute to Novena campus on a regular basis. Responsibilities: Contribute to safety culture within LKCMedicine Support the lead of H&S branch to implement safety programmes to improve staff and students’ knowledge of safety and to monitor the effectiveness of such initiatives Conduct safety briefings, e.g. for new staff, students on scholarly research projects Organise quarterly safety representatives meeting to disseminate key H&S information, solicit ground inputs and discuss issues related to safety Provide secretariat support for LKCMedicine Health & Safety committee which will discuss and deliberate on matters related to SOPs, safety practices Drive implementation of the Safety Management System and maintain documentation of implementation Conduct periodic safety inspections and audits and maintain documentations and records Investigate reported incidents and accidents, identify root causes and develop mitigation plans to avoid future occurrences for laboratory groups Track and monitor follow up actions on all reported incidents and accidents concerning breach of safety. Develop emergency response plan with the lead of H&S branch and organise drills for emergency scenarios such as fire and chemical spills Maintain records of risk assessments, training, legal documentation and processes as per the legal requirements and as required by NTU Office of Health & Safety Contribute to fulfilment of regulatory requirements related to H&S matters Work with NTU Office of Health & Safety for the audits of laboratories & workplaces and implement corrective measures to close the gaps Conduct monthly inspections and annual internal SMS audits, workplace health & safety, biological safety and regulatory audits for permit applications Maintain records of observations and track & document status of follow up actions Plan and conduct emergency drills for stakeholders Provide strong administrative support Ensure that the chemical/ biological inventory and MSDS for all the chemical/biological compounds are updated and maintained by the labs. Prepare, compile, track and monitor department budget and expenditure Ensure that  necessary supplies and services funded from the H&S budget are procured in a timely manner. Manage inventories of emergency supplies for the School Administer LKCMedicine Safety Awards and organise appreciation events Serve as key liaison person for staff at EMB for all H&S related matters and support CSB, if necessary Requirements: Tertiary education qualifications with at least 3 years of research or safety management experience in a biomedical laboratory Knowledge of local safety regulations and guidelines relevant to typical research and laboratory activities in a medical school Excellent written and verbal communication skills to communicate effectively with stakeholders at all levels Strong interpersonal skills to build influence and communicate effectively across diverse groups Leadership skills to lead teams and manage projects effectively, providing direction, feedback and support when needed Keen ability to grasp issues, identify root causes, propose and implement effective mitigation controls Ability to build good rapport with internal and external stakeholders Ability to multi-task, work independently and within tight deadlines Meticulous and detail-oriented We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow-Senior-Research-Fellow--X-Ray-Facilities-_R00016900": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow / Research Fellow (X-Ray Facilities)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFACTS is NTU's central shared facility specialising in characterisation using electron microscopy and X-ray techniques. FACTS invites applications for the position of Research Fellow / Senior Research Fellow. The role will focus on Key Responsibilities: Responsible for running of X-ray diffraction/scattering and/or X-ray fluorescence/photoemission spectroscopy instruments and support users in terms of training, consultation, usage, etc, so as to enable a broad user base to use the machines efficiently and safely. Conduct maintenance on the above machines, liaising with vendor engineers and trouble-shooting regular problems and issues. A strong knowledge of X-ray diffraction and scattering concepts. With knowledge and experience of advanced quantitative Rietveld, in-situ measurements and PDF analysis. A good understanding of principles in X-ray photoemission spectroscopy (photoelectric effect, electron attenuation factor, chemical shifts, spin-orbit splitting, surface charging and neutralization, significance of differential charging, depth profiling and angle-resolved technique). Understand surface charging and apply appropriate sample mounting technique for various types of samples. Able to perform spectral and quantitative analyses on XPS data. Deliver courses on X-ray diffraction and/or X-ray photoemission spectroscopy. These range from single lecture through to multi-day, in-depth courses that take users from beginners through to advanced. Organise, lecture and provide support for those users, in collaboration with external vendors. Provide consultancy for various ongoing university projects on the subjects of crystal chemistry and crystallography. Write up experimental reports and paper sections in accordance to the work done. Fulfil any other assigned duties as needed. Job Requirements: PhD in Materials Science, Physics, Chemistry, or a closely related discipline with more than 4 years of experience. Strong expertise in crystallography, including single-crystal diffraction, powder diffraction, and pair distribution function (PDF) analysis. Proven experience in advanced quantitative structure analysis, including Rietveld refinement, in situ/operando diffraction studies, and total scattering/PDF techniques. Proficiency in data interpretation, scientific reporting, and presenting research findings to diverse audiences. Excellent communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills, with strong attention to detail. Ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Counsellor_R00025660": {
      "title": "Counsellor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nStudent wellbeing and support is a top priority and a key foundation for NTU Education 2025. It enables NTU students to thrive and flourish in their educational journey. As a Counsellor in NTU, you will play a crucial role to enable NTU to fulfil its mission for student wellbeing and support. As a team member of the University Counselling Centre, you will provide counselling for undergraduate and graduate students and engage with various internal and external stakeholders to promote a NTU campus community approach to mental health. The responsibilities include: Counselling assessments and interventions Provide professional counselling services, including conducting risk and need assessments and delivering intervention plans over a variety of modes and approaches such as in person or online Facilitate case formulation, including preparation of assessment reports, delivery of case presentations, and referrals to relevant organisations in social services ecosystem Escalate and co-manage sensitive crisis cases with more experienced mental health practitioners Provide consultation to staff on concerns they have regarding students at-risk Document and maintain proper clinical records in accordance with policies and procedures of the University Counselling Centre Design, develop and/or facilitate wellbeing training initiatives and wellbeing portfolio / project annually Maintain professional, legal and ethical standards Adhere to professional standards in clinical, legal and ethical practices, ensuring client consent and confidentiality and proper data privacy protocol in counselling Participate in quality improvement projects led by more experienced mental health practitioners Document and maintain proper clinical records in accordance with policies and procedures of the University Counselling Centre Perform data collection and analysis which will aid in improvement of mental health support for students Participate actively in training to develop professional counselling expertise Community approach to case intervention Work collaboratively with and make recommendations to schools, student service offices, Halls of Residence, Support and Care Team, etc. to facilitate a campus community approach towards managing students with complex/severe mental health issues Work in inter-disciplinary teams (e.g. Educational/Clinical/ Counselling Psychologist, SEN specialist) to provide evidence-based psychotherapeutic interventions/treatment to students with complex/severe mental health issues and/or co-morbid issues (e.g. Special Education Needs and mental health issues) Liaise with other professionals (e.g. psychiatrists, doctors) and Social Service Agencies to mobilise community resources to provide care and support for the students Refer and/or recommend external service interventions (e.g. family therapy) as part of the student’s overall treatment plan Administrative support in University Counselling Centre (UCC) Support the daily operations of UCC, ensuring efficient and effective functioning Perform additional duties as assigned by Head, UCC or Director, UWO The requirements include: Master’s degree in counselling Preferably a clinical member and registered counsellor with the Singapore Association for Counselling (SAC) or equivalent At least three (3) years of professional counselling experience Proficiency in professional counselling approaches and tools to help clients with diverse issues and conditions Experience in working with young adults, preferably in an educational setting Experience in working in a multi-disciplinary team is advantageous Strong attention to details and commitment to maintaining accuracy in all operational aspects Strong organisational and multitasking skills, with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple tasks and responsibilities Possess professional values that are in line with the Code of Ethics of SAC Possess good interpersonal and communication skills Proficiency in IT skills (e.g. Microsoft 365, use of Apps, appointment booking systems, case management systems) A good team player who is able to work independently We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Data-Analytics--Senior-Analyst--Applied-AI---Data-Science-_R00024761": {
      "title": "Manager, Data Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. SASD works collaboratively with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey for all students. This position sits within the Digital Innovations Team (DIT), which develops AI-enabled solutions, automates administrative processes, and delivers data-driven insights to improve staff efficiency and student experience. We are looking for a hands-on analytics professional who can independently deliver BI, analytics, and applied AI solutions end to end. The role also provides guidance to junior team members and requires strong problem-solving and communication skills in a cross-functional environment. Key Responsibilities: Independently lead data analytics and AI projects from problem definition and data exploration through solution development, evaluation, and implementation. Develop and oversee BI dashboards and reporting solutions, including providing hands-on support for more complex requirements where needed.  Conduct data analysis and develop decision-support solutions that translate data into actionable insights; experience with AI-enabled analytics or analytics agents is an advantage. Develop and evaluate AI solutions, including RAG, AI-enabled workflows, and AI agents, where relevant to business needs. Apply data science approaches such as forecasting, predictive analytics, or recommendation to support business decision-making. Collaborate with technical teams to integrate analytics and AI solutions into operational workflows and existing platforms. Guide junior team members in dashboard development, data analytics, analytical problem solving, and emerging AI-enabled analytics approaches. Requirements: Bachelor's or Master's degree in Data Science, Business Analytics, Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, Mathematics, Statistics, or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant experience. Typically 5–8 years of relevant professional experience in data analytics, business intelligence, data science, or related areas, with demonstrated ability to independently own and deliver projects. Strong proficiency in SQL and Python, with hands-on experience in data analysis and data science using libraries such as pandas, NumPy, and scikit-learn. Hands-on experience developing dashboards and analytical solutions using tools such as Power BI, Qlik Sense, Tableau, or similar BI platforms. Strong data analysis and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify meaningful trends and translate findings into practical business recommendations. Experience with forecasting, predictive analytics, recommendation, or other applied data science use cases, with the ability to apply appropriate techniques to practical business problems. Practical exposure to Generative AI applications, such as RAG, AI-enabled workflows, or AI agents, would be preferred; familiarity with agent development frameworks or platforms such as LangChain/LangGraph, Microsoft Agent Framework, or Google ADK would be an advantage. Experience working with cloud-based data, analytics, or AI platforms; Microsoft Azure experience is preferred. Strong communication skills with the ability to explain analytical and technical work clearly to non-technical stakeholders. Ability to work independently in a dynamic, cross-functional environment and provide guidance to junior team members. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Gift-Stewardship-and-Reporting_R00025339": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Gift Stewardship and Reporting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University Advancement Office (UAO) supports NTU’s giving mission by fostering meaningful relationships and strategic partnerships with philanthropists, alumni, business community partners, corporations that result in goodwill and philanthropy towards education and research that underpin a shared sustainable future. Reporting to the Manager, Gift Stewardship and Reporting, the Assistant Manager’s role is responsible for the stewardship of donors, primarily in ensuring accurate and impactful reporting and driving targeted campaigns aimed at various donor segments. This role involves preparing detailed impact reports, working closely with other departments to enhance donor relationships and communication, and supporting donor engagement programs and activities. Key responsibilities include : Reporting: Prepare and deliver detailed impact reports, track donor data, and ensure accurate reporting of donor activities. Conceptualize impact reports in other content formats (e.g. video) Stewardship Management: Develop and implement stewardship plans, particularly for top tier donor groups. Event Coordination: Support the organizing and execution of donor recognition events, ensuring exceptional experiences for participants. Requirements: A Bachelor’s Degree in any discipline. Understanding of philanthropy as it relates to higher education. Knowledge of good donor relationship management. Minimum of 3 - 4 years’ experience preferably in higher education (or a comparably complex organization) in development, stewardship, advancement, or a related function, involving a range of senior stakeholders. Demonstrated success in achieving strategic outcomes in a large and complex environment. Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate to a wide range of audiences with gravitas. Excellent ability to innovate and deal with ambiguity and organizational sensitivity with tact and diplomacy; to be opportunistic, responsive, resourceful, and resilient. Demonstrate a clear understanding and awareness of ethical considerations pertaining to advancement work, as well as an understanding and appreciation of cultural and intercultural sensitivities. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Global-China-_R00025668-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Global China)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences seeks to appoint a research fellow under the theme of “Global China” as a part of Professor Liu Hong’s on-going research programmes. The applicant must have a PhD in one of the relevant fields of Chinese studies, political science, ethnic studies, international relations, and global history, or a related field. Have good knowledge about contemporary China and its relations with the world, especially in relation to Chinese businesses going abroad at a time of globalization and technological innovation. Preferably to have bilingual capacities such as English and a relevant language that can facilitate research activities and publications - essential for data analysis and communication with stakeholders Work closely with the PI and his research team on a regularly basis. Conduct independent research, develop research proposals, collaborate on projects, and contribute to academic publications on a collaborative basis. Key Responsibilities: Conduct independent, high-quality research on themes related to Global China, including Chinese studies, international political economy, public policy, and global history. Collaborate closely with PI, Professor Liu Hong and the research team to design, develop, and execute research projects. Prepare and submit research proposals, grant applications, and progress reports in alignment with the School of Social Sciences’ objectives. Publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals, edited volumes, and other reputable academic outlets. Present research outcomes at international conferences, workshops, and seminars, enhancing NTU’s visibility in the field. Mentor junior researchers, research assistants, and graduate students, fostering a collaborative and supportive research environment. Support the dissemination of research insights to policymakers, industry stakeholders, and the wider public through policy briefs, public lectures, and outreach activities. Uphold the highest standards of academic integrity, research ethics, and professional conduct in all activities. Job Requirements: PhD (for Research Fellow and above equivalent) qualification degree in domain discipline or related field Good written and oral communication skills Competent in interpersonal skill (e.g. Ability to work independently / develop solutions under strict timelines, meticulous and eye for details / excellent organizational / time management skills) Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Possesses international experience, with a strong network of contacts in the region . Application Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, a detailed CV, a writing sample, and a 3-page research proposal by Sept 21, 2026. Two reference letters from those who are in a position to assess the candidates’ academic and research capacities, on official letterhead and signed by the referees, are to be sent directly by the referees to D-NCPA@ntu.edu.sg, also by Sept 21, 2026. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoctoral---Research-Fellow--AI-Algorithms-_R00025666": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral / Research Fellow (AI Algorithms)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. The School is globally known for its cutting-edge research and world-class infrastructure, and generous funding. The School ranks 4th (globally) in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. The postdoctoral fellow will work in a laboratory that was one of the pioneers in the field of neuromorphic computing, and one that has influenced today’s widely used AI products. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Postdoctoral Fellow to lead research on AI training algorithms. The role will focus on developing AI algorithms (especially for training) aimed at post-digital hardware. Specifically, the project targets numerical and local learning algorithms beyond backpropagation. Key Responsibilities: Defining detailed experimental steps. Conducting experiments Reporting of results in publications Presentations at major conferences Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science or related field At least 3 years of relevant experiences in a similar role with hands-on experience in AI algorithms, including experience gained during PhD Familiarity with neuromorphic computing and AI models Good written and oral communication skills, with papers published in leading conferences or journals Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoctoral---Research-Fellow--AI-accelerators-_R00025667": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral / Research Fellow (AI accelerators)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. The School is globally known for its cutting-edge research and world-class infrastructure, and generous funding. The School ranks 4th (globally) in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. The postdoctoral fellow will work in a laboratory that was one of the pioneers in the field of neuromorphic computing, and one that has influenced today’s widely used AI products. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Postdoctoral Fellow to lead research on neuromorphic circuits and systems. The role will focus on experimentally designing and building circuits of crossbars and other architectures that can employ post-CMOS devices and accelerate computing. Specifically, the project targets building accelerators for problems that are not efficiently handled by digital systems, such as AI training, real-time optimization, etc. Key Responsibilities: Defining detailed experimental steps. Conducting experiments Reporting of results in publications Presentations at major conferences Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science or related field At least 3 years of relevant experiences in a similar role with hands-on experience in experimental building and testing of circuits, including experience gained during PhD Familiarity with neuromorphic computing and AI models Good written and oral communication skills, with papers published in leading conferences or journals Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoctoral---Research-Fellow--Neuromorphic-Materials---Devices-_R00025665": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral / Research Fellow (Neuromorphic Materials & Devices)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. The School is globally known for its cutting-edge research and world-class infrastructure, and generous funding. The School ranks 4th (globally) in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. The postdoctoral fellow will work in a laboratory that was one of the pioneers in the field of neuromorphic computing, and one that has influenced today’s widely used AI products. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Postdoctoral Fellow to lead research on neuromorphic materials and devices. The role will focus on experimental post-CMOS and novel electronic devices (such as memristors) that behave like neurons. Specifically, the project targets 2D materials, phase transition materials, spintronic, and other nonlinear materials that lead to neuromorphic dynamical behavior. Key Responsibilities: Defining detailed experimental steps. Conducting experiments Reporting of results in publications Presentations at major conferences Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Physics or related field At least 3 years of relevant experiences in a similar role with hands-on experience in experimental device fabrication and/or testing, including experience gained during PhD Experience with 2D materials, memristors and optically materials is a plus. Familiarity with neuromorphic computing and AI models is a plus. Good written and oral communication skills, with papers published in leading conferences or journals Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Semiconductor-Laser-Diode-_R00025664": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Semiconductor Laser Diode)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTemasek Laboratories@NTU is looking for a candidate to join them as a Research Scientist who has a research background on semiconductor laser diode/semiconductor photonics/semiconductor material. The staff will be involved in semiconductor laser diode related project. Key Responsibilities: To assist with research operations, including the procurement of laboratory supplies, experimental setup, literature reviews, evaluation of product specifications, and establishment of safe work processes. To lead the fabrication, characterization, and analysis of laser diodes. To support project-related activities, including events, publications, proposal preparation, planning, monitoring, and reporting, as required. Job Requirements: PhD degree or Master’s with at least 8 years relevant experience in Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Materials Engineering, Applied Physics, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field. Prior hands-on experience with cleanroom processes, including lithography, PECVD deposition, metal deposition, and rapid thermal annealing; optical mask design; optical simulation (BPM or FDTD); and the fabrication and characterization of semiconductor laser diodes/semiconductor photonics/semiconductor material is preferred. Good writing skills for writing proposals, reports and publications in good academic journals We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Assistant-Manager--Research-Administration---Grants-Support--Administrative-Support-_R00023595": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, Research Administration & Grants Support (Administrative Support)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU & EOS A research-intensive public university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has about 35,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in the Business, Computing & Data Science, Engineering, Humanities, Arts, & Social Sciences, Medicine, Science, and Graduate colleges. NTU is also home to world-renowned autonomous institutes – the National Institute of Education, S Rajaratnam School of International Studies and Singapore Centre for Environmental Life Sciences Engineering – and various leading research centres such as the Earth Observatory of Singapore, Nanyang Environment & Water Research Institute and Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N). Under the NTU Smart Campus vision, the University harnesses the power of digital technology and tech-enabled solutions to support better learning and living experiences, the discovery of new knowledge, and the sustainability of resources. Ranked amongst the world’s top universities, the University’s main campus is also frequently listed among the world’s most beautiful. Known for its sustainability, NTU has achieved 100% Green Mark Platinum certification for all its eligible building projects. Apart from its main campus, NTU also has a medical campus in Novena, Singapore’s healthcare district. About the Role We are hiring a Senior Executive/ Assistant Manager (Research Administration & Grants Management) to support EOS’s large and diverse research portfolio by managing research administration, grants management, financial governance, and operational coordination. Working under the direction of the EOS Director and reporting directly to the Assistant Director, Grants Management, the incumbent is responsible for ensuring the effective execution of funded projects across all stages of the grant lifecycle, directly contributing to the foundation for potential scientific breakthroughs and ultimately making a meaningful impact on society. Key Responsibilities Support the full lifecycle of research grants, ensuring seamless execution across all stages of funded projects while adhering to grant protocols and guidelines. Monitor budgets, review expenditures, prepare financial reports and virements, and ensure audit readiness. Oversee procurement processes, vendor management, and coordination of operational logistics, including travel, workshops, and fieldwork in accordance with NTU and funder guidelines. Collaborate closely with academic staff, management, and University offices to address and manage administrative matters pertaining to grants. Prepare research contracts and research collaboration agreements with individuals or organisations. Serve as the point of contact between academic staff and internal/external stakeholders to support the management of research projects including but not limited to grant calls, grant proposal submission and recruitment-related functions. Support process improvements by participating in the development and implementation of AI-driven automated workflows to enhance administrative efficiency. Mentor junior administrative staff. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, Public Administration, or related fields. Preferably with at least 2 to 4 years of research administration experience in an administrative position within academic or research sector. Strong knowledge of procurement, budgeting, compliance, and audit processes. Excellent organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills with the ability to multitask and prioritize tasks in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, able to interact professionally with stakeholders at all levels. Meticulous with strong attention to detail. Able to work independently with minimal supervision and collaboratively in a team. Adaptable and resilient with a willingness to learn and acquire new skills as required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and other productivity/collaboration tools; familiarity with grant management systems is a plus. EOS seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. Please submit your application through the NTU Career Portal, by clicking the 'APPLY' button. All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Part-Time-Work-Study-Degree-Programmes_R00025136": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Part-Time Work-Study Degree Programmes",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, is a leading university committed to nurturing leaders and creating societal impact through education, research, and service. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to the growth of workforce-relevant undergraduate pathways, work closely with academic and industry stakeholders, and help shape new models of lifelong and work-integrated learning at the University. Why Join NTU This is an opportunity to play a key role in shaping innovative undergraduate pathways that support lifelong learning and workforce development. The role offers exposure to strategic cross-University initiatives, collaboration with academic, government, and industry stakeholders, and the chance to contribute meaningfully to programme growth, learner success, and institutional impact. NTU also highlights staff wellbeing as part of its broader wellbeing ecosystem for staff and students. About the Role The Assistant Director will lead the management and development of NTU’s Part-Time Work-Study undergraduate programme portfolio. The role combines strategic programme development, stakeholder engagement, operational leadership, and team management to ensure high-quality programme delivery, strong student experience, and alignment with institutional and national workforce priorities. Key Responsibilities Oversee the end-to-end management of Part-Time Work-Study undergraduate programmes, including marketing coordination, admissions, programme administration, student servicing, and graduation-related processes. Support the launch and ongoing delivery of new programmes and future portfolio offerings. Work closely with Colleges, Schools, faculty, and central administrative units to ensure smooth programme operations, service excellence, and compliance with University requirements. Lead or coordinate the development of new programme proposals in partnership with internal and external stakeholders, including government agencies, professional bodies, employers, and industry partners. Support outreach and promotional efforts for the programme portfolio, including recruitment activities, information sessions, and stakeholder engagement sessions. Oversee reporting, data consolidation, quality assurance, accreditation-related processes, and administrative governance for the portfolio. Build and maintain strong stakeholder relationships to support programme relevance, partnership development, and institutional objectives. Lead and supervise a small team, providing direction, support, and performance oversight. Requirements Must-Haves A good Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university. Relevant experience in programme management, higher education administration, continuing education, partnership development, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to manage complex programmes or projects involving multiple stakeholders and competing timelines. Strong stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively across academic, administrative, and external partner groups. Strong organisational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Ability to lead operations with attention to quality, service standards, compliance, and continuous improvement. Experience in supervising or guiding staff, with the ability to lead a small team effectively. Good-to-Have A postgraduate qualification in education, business, management, public administration, or a related field. Experience in higher education, lifelong learning, work-study, or industry-linked education environments. Familiarity with quality assurance, accreditation, academic governance, or reporting requirements in an education setting. Experience in new programme development, policy implementation, or cross-sector partnership management. Confidence in using data, digital systems, and reporting tools to support decision-making and programme management. Personal Attributes Proactive, resourceful, and solutions-oriented. Professional and confident in engaging stakeholders at different levels. Able to balance strategic thinking with operational execution. Meticulous, responsive, and committed to service excellence. Adaptable and effective in a dynamic and evolving environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Growth-Partnership--CRM-and-Insights_R00025451": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Growth Partnership, CRM and Insights",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU and NTU PACE Nanyang Technological University, Singapore is a leading technological university committed to developing leaders and creating societal impact through education, research and service. The University brings together talent across disciplines to advance education, innovation and partnerships that address the evolving needs of society. The NTU Academy for Professional and Continuing Education draws on NTU’s academic expertise and strong industry connections to provide professional, executive and continuing education programmes for working adults, organisations and institutional partners. It plays an important role in advancing lifelong learning and equipping professionals with relevant knowledge and skills for a rapidly changing economy. The Role We are seeking an experienced and forward-looking leader to head the Growth Partnership, Customer Relationship Management and Insights function within NTU PACE. The Assistant Director will shape the Academy’s integrated growth and customer-engagement strategy, strengthen its use of customer data and marketing technology, and partner programme value streams to improve market reach, lead quality, conversion and sustained engagement. The role offers the opportunity to establish scalable growth capabilities across a diverse portfolio serving individual learners, corporate clients and institutional partners. Following NTU PACE’s reorganisation, this enabling function supports the Career Transitions, Enterprise and Institutional Solutions, and Micro-credentials value streams through growth partnership, HubSpot governance and automation, customer insights, content, events and engagement. Key Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Lead the development and implementation of integrated growth and marketing strategies aligned with NTU PACE’s institutional, portfolio, enrolment and revenue objectives. Serve as a strategic growth partner to programme value streams, advising on target audiences, market positioning, customer propositions, demand generation and go-to-market plans. Establish and govern the effective use of HubSpot across NTU PACE, including customer lifecycle definitions, data standards, ownership rules, lead routing, access controls and reporting practices. Design customer segmentation, lead-scoring, nurture, re-engagement and marketing-automation frameworks to support relevant and scalable customer journeys. Set priorities for campaigns, channels, content, events and engagement activities based on customer needs, market opportunities and expected organisational impact. Define lead-quality standards and work with programme, enrolment and customer-facing teams to improve follow-up, funnel progression and conversion. Develop dashboards and management insights covering campaign performance, customer behaviour, lead quality, funnel movement, channel contribution and return on marketing investment. Use customer, campaign and funnel data to identify growth opportunities, performance gaps and areas for continuous improvement. Prioritise staff, budgets, systems and external resources across competing portfolio requirements, within approved plans and delegated authority. Lead and develop a multidisciplinary team covering growth partnership, customer relationship management, automation, analytics, content and engagement. Manage relevant agencies, technology providers and vendors, ensuring effective delivery, governance and value. Build effective relationships with senior leaders, value-stream teams, NTU colleges and schools, central University functions, industry partners and government or institutional stakeholders. Why Join NTU This role provides the opportunity to: Shape the growth and customer-engagement capabilities of NTU’s professional and continuing education portfolio. Build an integrated, data-informed approach to lifelong-learning marketing and customer management. Influence institutional growth across individual, enterprise and institutional markets. Work closely with academic leaders, professional teams, industry partners and public-sector stakeholders. Lead a newly established enabling function and develop capabilities in customer relationship management, automation and analytics. Contribute to NTU’s broader mission of developing talent and creating societal impact through education and service. NTU is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment in which staff from different backgrounds can contribute, develop and thrive. Requirements Essential Qualifications and Experience Candidates should possess: A recognised bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration, Communications, Data Analytics, Information Systems or a related discipline. At least eight years of relevant experience in growth marketing, customer engagement, customer relationship management, digital marketing, marketing operations, customer analytics or a related field. At least three years of experience in a managerial or functional leadership capacity, with responsibility for people, budgets, systems, projects or cross-functional outcomes. Demonstrated experience developing and implementing growth or marketing strategies that have contributed to measurable improvements in lead generation, customer engagement, conversion, enrolment or revenue. Practical experience governing or managing an enterprise customer relationship management or marketing-automation platform. Experience designing customer lifecycle stages, segmentation approaches, lead-scoring models, nurture journeys, automated workflows and performance reporting. Strong knowledge of integrated campaign planning, content and channel strategy, customer acquisition, engagement and re-engagement. Strong analytical ability, including experience interpreting campaign, customer and funnel data and translating findings into clear recommendations. Experience managing competing priorities and allocating resources across multiple programmes, products or customer segments. Demonstrated ability to influence senior and cross-functional stakeholders where accountability is shared and direct reporting authority may be limited. Strong written, verbal, presentation and stakeholder-management skills. Sound understanding of customer-data quality, privacy, consent and governance requirements. Preferred Qualifications and Experience The following would be advantageous: A postgraduate qualification in marketing, business, analytics, digital transformation or a related discipline. Professional certification in customer relationship management, marketing automation, digital marketing, data analytics or project management. Advanced experience using HubSpot, including lifecycle configuration, workflows, segmentation, lead scoring, dashboards and governance. Experience working across both individual-consumer and corporate or institutional customer markets. Experience in higher education, professional and continuing education, adult learning, workforce development or another complex service environment. Experience integrating customer relationship management data with student, programme, enrolment or operational systems. Experience managing marketing agencies, technology vendors and externally delivered services. Skills and Attributes The successful candidate should demonstrate: Strategic and commercial judgement, with a strong focus on measurable organisational and customer outcomes. Customer-centric thinking and the ability to translate customer needs into effective engagement strategies and journeys. Strong leadership, people-management and capability-development skills. The ability to combine strategic thinking with disciplined operational execution. Confidence in using evidence and insight to challenge assumptions and influence decisions. Strong collaboration and relationship-building skills across academic, professional and external stakeholder groups. Sound judgement when balancing innovation, speed, governance and institutional risk. Adaptability, resilience and the ability to operate effectively in an evolving organisational environment. A proactive approach to continuous improvement, automation and scalable ways of working. High standards of integrity, professionalism, accountability and attention to detail. . We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be informed. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Student-Experience-and-Development_R00025450": {
      "title": "Manager, Student Experience and Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU PACE is seeking a Manager for Student Experience and Development. This role involves coordinating and supporting various activities, working collaboratively with relevant NTU Offices, Colleges, and Schools to enhance NTU’s capacity and capability for educating PGC students. The incumbent will also be responsible for streamlining processes and workflows, as well as developing services and support aimed at enriching the development and overall experience of the expanding self-financed postgraduate population. Key responsibilities include but are not limited to: Student Engagement and Support: To develop strategies and initiatives that foster student development, engagement, well-being, and overall satisfaction. Process Coordination and Support: To coordinate and improve the efficiency of key processes and workflows. This includes the management of application, admission, enrollment, course offerings, internships, attachments, job placements, and accommodations. Facilitating student service and support: To coordinate and facilitate the expansion of services that contribute to PGC students' academic and skills development, career and internship preparation, time and stress management, social engagement, and overall mental health and holistic well-being. Administrative Support: To provide general administrative support to Senior Management (e.g., scheduling, correspondence, record-keeping), and manage team communications to ensure smooth information flow. Collaboration and Communication: To liaise with relevant departments and stakeholders to improve the student experience and participate in cross-functional projects and initiatives. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree qualification. Minimum of 5 years of relevant experience in student life, support, and development. Possesses strong communication skills and problem-solving skills with good time management. Able to handle stress and passionate in assisting students. Experience in counselling and mentoring will be an advantage. Possesses a “can-do” attitude, ability to work fast and independently. A team player with strong interpersonal skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Research---Centre-Support_R00025164": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research & Centre Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading research-intensive university, recognised internationally for its excellence in education, research, and innovation. NTU fosters a collaborative and inclusive work environment that supports professional growth and continuous learning. About the Role We are looking for an organised and proactive Assistant Manager to support the institute’s communications, events, and operational activities. This role works closely with internal stakeholders and leadership to ensure effective coordination, high-quality delivery, and smooth day‑to‑day operations. The position offers meaningful exposure to institutional initiatives and provides opportunities to contribute to process improvement and stakeholder engagement. Why Join Us Opportunity to work in a dynamic and collaborative university environment Exposure to a broad range of institutional and cross‑functional initiatives Supportive culture that values professional development and continuous improvement Key Responsibilities Provide end‑to‑end administrative and operational coordination support across communications, events, and outreach activities Support the development, editing, and dissemination of communications materials, including digital and online platforms Coordinate the planning and execution of events, including logistics, stakeholder coordination, and post‑event follow‑up Liaise with internal teams, university offices, and external partners to ensure timely delivery of activities and tasks Support financial and operational processes, including basic budgeting coordination, reimbursements, and workflow tracking Assist with documentation, reporting, and maintenance of accurate records in line with institutional requirements Requirements Bachelor’s degree or equivalent professional qualification Relevant experience in administrative, operational, communications, or events coordination roles Strong organisational, coordination, and time‑management skills Clear written and verbal communication skills Proficiency in digital tools (e.g. Microsoft Excel, collaboration and content platforms) Ability to work collaboratively and manage multiple priorities effectively We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Mechanical--Electrical--Power-engineering-_R00025657": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Mechanical/ Electrical/ Power engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. ERI@N has multiple Interdisciplinary Research Programmes which focus on translational Research, Development & Deployment which focus on specific area of the energy value chain, and a number of Living labs and Testbeds which facilitate large scale technology deployment enabling validation and demonstration of real-world applications. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/erian We are looking for a Research Associate to conduct numerical modelling work as well as to develop optimal control strategies for energy systems including building energy systems, energy storage systems and fire systems . The role will focus on conducting comprehensive data collection from both experimental and numerical sources, gathering relevant test and simulation data available globally, organizing the collected data to support model and control algorithm development and validation, and ensuring the accuracy and robustness. Key Responsibilities: Identify credible data sources, standardize data formats, and integrate diverse datasets to enhance the reliability of simulations and predictions. Use cutting-edge methodologies such as A.I. and machine-learning to accelerate the numerical simulation processes. Develop optimal control strategies for energy systems Publish high-quality journal papers, conference papers and apply for TD/patents. Periodically provide updates on individual research progress to the PI and team members. Job Requirements: Master’s (for Research Associate equivalent) degree in mechanical/electrical/power engineering or related field At least 1 year of relevant experience in numerical simulations and control Familiarity with building energy system modelling tools (e.g. Matlab, Modelica, TRNSYS, FDS, OpenFOAM, etc.) Familiarity with experimental methods in energy systems and battery energy storage systems (BESS) Familiarity with thermal management methods including heat exchangers, heat sink, phase-change materials (PCM), etc. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in numeric and analytical skill s Ability to work independently and develop solutions under strict timelines We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Executive--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00025272": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Executive (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applications for the position of Senior Executive/Executive in the Finance Department . The appointee will support day-to-day financial operations and service delivery to internal and external stakeholders. Roles & Responsibilities Key responsibilities include: Process staff-related payments, invoices and related enquiries. Compute liquidated damages for staff development schemes and prepare MOE funding claims. Support accounting matters for donations, endowment funds, insurance and assigned fund accounts. Review and improve finance processes with the Reporting Officer. Provide administrative and secretarial support to the Head of Finance. Perform other finance and administrative duties as assigned. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma, preferably in Accountancy, Finance or a related discipline. Preferably 2 to 3 years of relevant experience in accounting or finance operations. Organised, meticulous, and comfortable working with numbers and financial records. Positive team player with a strong sense of responsibility and willingness to learn. Proficient in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel; SAP experience is an advantage. Able to manage priorities and meet deadlines. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 8 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Building-Energy-System-Control-_R00025656": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Building Energy System Control)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. We are looking for a  Research Fellow to support and drive excellence in scientific research and technological innovations . The role will focus on sustainable and advanced building technologies . Key Responsibilities: Support research activities Support research project management Produce research outputs including reports, publications, presentations, etc. Coordinate different stakeholders in research projects Support research strategic development and securing funding Support research data management and documentation Job Requirements: PhD degree in Mechanical/Electrical Engineering or related field At least 1 years of relevant experience in scientific research / technical hands-on experience in building energy/power system control & optimisation. Familiarity with building energy/power system control & optimisation, building automation and control (BAC) system, Artificial Intelligence (AI) & Machine-Learning (ML) applications. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in power system modelling, advanced control theory (e.g., model-predictive control, etc.), data-driven modelling and control methods (e.g., reinforcement learning, transfer learning, etc.) Proficiency in programming tools and languages, e.g., MatLab, Python, Modelica, C, ForTran, etc. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Affairs---Admin_R00025658-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs & Admin",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager (Faculty Affairs & Admin) reports to Assistant Director (Faculty Affairs), assisting in the management of documentation, prioritization of incoming requests, handling of sensitive information and facilitation of inputs and recommendations for decision-making. He/She also supports the various internal and external faculty initiatives, activities, and day-to-day operations with the objectives of enhancing the overall productivity, efficiency and alignment across NTU Colleges and Schools, and Autonomous Institutes (AIs). In addition, he/she provides holistic administrative and secretariat support to Vice Provost, Faculty Affairs (VPFA) in executing a full spectrum of services in relation to VPFA role-based email account, schedule and calendar, event and programme management, and organizational communication. The incumbent should also exercise flexibility and willingness to assume additional and/or certain tasks/duties that may arise which require his/her assistance. Key Responsibilities: 1) Faculty initiatives and activities Coordinate university-level initiatives and leadership engagements, including preparation of materials, documentation of decisions, and tracking of action items, including the briefing sessions on faculty promotion and tenure preparation, quarterly meetings with Associate Deans/ Associate Chairs/ Vice Dean from NTU Colleges and Schools and AIs, Faculty Orientation Program, NTU Leadership Academy (NLA) workshops etc. 2) Faculty Talent Candidate Network Provide support in planning, organizing and follow through of overseas outreach trips at the University level with active participation from Colleges/ Schools and AIs Maintain the database of faculty talent candidate pipeline 3) Management Reporting and Presentation Develop high-quality briefing materials, presentations, and reports to support decision-making and engagements Collate and maintain database for matters pertaining to faculty affairs Prepare and collate management reports and presentation slides in an accurate and succinct manner Provide secretariat support to draft minutes of meetings and disseminate for review and circulation 4) Planning and Administration Set up and maintain structured tracking systems and identify opportunities to improve workflows and processes within VPFA’s Office Establish and implement procedures to ensure proper endorsement/approval requests Set up requisite workflow templates, protocols and standard operating procedures for VPFA Office to ensure smooth execution for requests, programmes and activities Manage proper database and filing system for key sensitive information for VPFA Office Assist with VPA Office budget submissions, finance claims, obtaining quotations etc 5) Calendar, Schedule, Travel, and Meeting Management Support the effective management of VPFA’s and AVPFA’s engagements, including scheduling, prioritisation, and preparation of meeting materials Coordinate meetings with internal or/and external stakeholders  Prepare meeting agenda and materials and organize meeting logistics in relation to faculty affairs matters Requirements: Good planning, organizational and problem-solving skills Good written and verbal communication skills Flexibility and adaptability in a fast-paced environment IT savvy and proficient in Microsoft Office Applications Ability to work independently as well as in a team to achieve organizational goals Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion and prudence Ability to manage and disseminate all communications with tact We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Unit-Head--Human-Resource-and-Finance--Office-for-Research--NIE-_R00025650": {
      "title": "Unit Head, Human Resource and Finance, Office for Research [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Unit Head, Human Resource and Finance (HRF) , Office for Research. As the Unit Head of HRF, you will lead a team overseeing human resource, finance, administrative and research support processes. You will play a lead role in research support operations in HR and finance and governance across the Office, working closely with institutional stakeholders to ensure compliance and effective support. This is a contract post till 31 Mar 2028. Responsibilities Lead the OfR Human Resource and Finance team in all operations and processes. Provide supervision to team members and manage performance. Ensure strong internal controls and compliance with HR and financial policies and institutional guidelines. Oversee all HR related processes including faculty matters (appointment, reappointment, appraisal, and promotion). Manage research staff appointment, reappointment and temporary staffing processes. Review alignment in processes across research staff hiring for Education Research Funding Programme (ERFP) and Non-ERFP grants. Support in administrative staff related matters where required. Provide HR advisory and ensure accurate and timely reporting to management on HR-related research support matters. Liaise with NIE HRD and programme offices on faculty and research staff matters. Oversee faculty mentoring matters, including ERS/SERS/PERS-related processes, and coordinate with Research Centres to support implementation and follow-up. Oversee all financial operations related to research funding, 5th tranche funding and OfR funding. Work with the team to ensure smooth day-to-day operations in procurement, budgeting, claims processing, and financial reporting. Ensure compliance with institutional financial and procurement policies. Provide financial consultations to Principal Investigators (PIs) and stakeholders. Provide accurate and timely reporting to management on 5th tranche funding. Support in 6th tranche proposal budget planning. Oversee and provide input on budget estimates, cashflow projections, and funder reporting. Serve as Delegation of Authority for research and non-research related expenditure where required. Liaise with NIE Finance and MOE to maintain strong operational and funding relationships. Work with Research Centres (RC) on HR and Finance shared services that cut across. Keep SOPs, NTU ServiceNow articles, and financial guidelines updated. Monitor and report KPIs for the ERFP and assist in data compilation for tranche reporting and other institutional reporting. Drive process improvement initiatives in HR and financial workflows and systems, leveraging AI where appropriate. Support change management efforts and organizational alignment across OfR and Research Centres, particularly where shared-service processes intersect. Support in OfR level events and any other duties, as assigned by the reporting officer. Requirements A University Degree. At least 5 to 8 years of Administrative/HR/financial/procurement experience required. Meticulous with good analytical skills. Excellent interpersonal, communication, writing and organization skills. A strong team lead who is highly motivated and also able to collaborate within and across teams. Able to problem solve and work within tight deadlines. Integrity and discretion when handling confidential information. Proficient in Excel and MS Word. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 15 September 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Tectonics----InVEST-Component-F-_R00025652": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Tectonics -  InVEST Component F)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) is a Research Centre at Nanyang Technological University Singapore that conducts fundamental research on earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis, and climate change in and around Southeast Asia, towards safer and more sustainable societies. EOS maintains a regional network of geophysical observation stations in collaboration with neighboring countries in Southeast Asia, that are supported by the EOS Centre for Geohazard Observations, as well as a Remote Sensing Lab (EOS-RS). Computational resources are available through a dedicated cluster and collaboration with the High-Performance Computing Centre of NTU. In addition, EOS hosts state-of-the-art analytical facilities for petrological and geochemical analysis, and a Community Engagement office that co-creates learning opportunities for a range of audiences to promote a safer and more sustainable future. EOS seeks a Research Associate to work on understanding earthquake hazard and rapid and accurate quantification of disasters using remote sensing and space geodesy. The candidate will work under the supervision of Associate Prof Sang-Ho Yun and will collaborate with the researchers from the ‘ Integrating Volcano and Earthquake Science and Technology (InVEST) in Southeast Asia’ project, a 5-year project that aims to provide a holistic understanding of regional tectonics, volcanoes, the linkages between the two, and their cascading hazards and impacts in Singapore and Southeast Asia.  The Research Associate will work on understanding earthquake hazard through fault geometry and rheology and rapid and accurate quantification of disasters using remote sensing and space geodesy. They will also advance InSAR processing algorithms to optimise deformation mapping and change detection capability in Southeast Asia, where SAR analysis is complicated by tropospheric and ionospheric effects, dense vegetation, and soil moisture. Responsibilities will include: Conduct research on fault geometry and rheology that drives the future earthquake hazards Rapid generation of disaster maps (damage proxy) for earthquakes and volcanic activities Engage machine learning techniques to improve the InSAR deformation and coherence time series analysis Collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams and stakeholders to translate research outcomes into operational applications. The successful candidate will be encouraged to publish 1 peer-reviewed technical papers per year. Requirements: Master degree in Geophysics, Geomatics, Geodesy, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Natural Hazards, or a related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in remote sensing, image processing, inverse problems, and machine learning. Proven experience in the analysis and interpretation of a wide range of geospatial and geodetic datasets. Strong programming skills in Python, MATLAB, C, and Fortran. Strong written and verbal communication skills in English, as English is the primary working language used to communicate and collaborate effectively with internal and external stakeholders, including researchers, industry partners, funding agencies, and academic collaborators. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research while contributing effectively within a collaborative team environment. EOS seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, CV, list of publications, and statement of research interests. Applications will be reviewed immediately. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Academic-Planning---Governance_R00025645": {
      "title": "Manager, Academic Planning & Governance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admissions and matriculation to graduation and beyond. Working closely with Schools, Colleges and autonomous institutes, SASD plays a key role in delivering high-quality academic administration and enhancing the student experience. This position is part of the Graduate Education Academic Planning and Governance Unit within the Registrar’s office. Reporting to the Deputy Director, the successful candidate will support the University’s postgraduate academic planning including the postgraduate intake and enrolment planning and institutional performance monitoring through the tracking and reporting of key performance indicators. Working closely with the schools and key internal stakeholders, the incumbent will contribute to academic planning excellence strengthening governance processes, leverage data and insights to inform planning and driving continuous process improvements to advance the University’s graduate education objectives.  Key responsibilities: Lead and manage the annual Graduate Intake and Enrolment Planning (GIEP) exercise to support institutional academic planning.  This involves partnering with schools for their intake and enrolment projections, ensuring data quality and compliance with MOE funding principles, reporting requirements and University policies, reviewing and analysing the projections to facilitate discussion by the GIEP committee. Responsible for the preparation and submission of postgraduate intake and enrolment reports and supporting its certification process.   Coordinate the collection, consolidation and validation of information from Schools and other stakeholders to support strategic initiatives, management reporting and institutional planning exercises.  Prepare reports and presentation materials for senior management discussions, strategic reviews and decision-making.  Identify information gaps, emerging trends and potential risks, and recommend follow-up actions to strengthen planning outcomes. Contribute to strengthening reporting frameworks and stakeholder engagement processes to enhance institutional governance and decision-making. Requirements: Degree in a relevant discipline with 6 to 8 years of relevant work experience. Experience in higher education, particularly in institutional planning, governance or policy compliance, will be an advantage.  Experience in management reporting and performance monitoring, with strong analytical skills and ability to synthesise complex information into clear, concise reports and presentation materials for senior leadership and governance committees.  Good understanding of governance, compliance and data governance principles.   Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, PowerPoint, and Viso, with strong capabilities in data analysis and visual presentation. Familiarity with AI-enabled productivity tools will be an advantage.  Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage and collaborate effectively with stakeholders at all levels.  Meticulous, proactive and resourceful, with a strong sense of accountability, commitment to data integrity and a continuous improvement mindset.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Adjunct-Assistant-Professor_R00025649": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Biological Sciences Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Adjunct Assistant Professor The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), College of Science (CoS) at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) in Singapore seeks outstanding candidates to apply for an Adjunct Assistant Professor in the area of plant biology, taxonomy and conservation. SBS is searching for individuals with a well-deﬁned research vision and an outstanding track record of publications in top journals. The successful candidate should establish and maintain an independent extramurally funded research program. The successful candidate is expected to show a strong commitment to departmental undergraduate and graduate mentoring and teaching. SBS and CoS seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Visiting-Professor--Geophysics-and-Seismology-_R00025289": {
      "title": "Visiting Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore A research-intensive public university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has about 40,700 undergraduate and postgraduate students in the Business, Computing & Data Science, Engineering, Humanities, Arts, & Social Sciences, Medicine, Science, and Graduate colleges. NTU is also home to world-renowned autonomous institutes – the National Institute of Education, S Rajaratnam School of International Studies and Singapore Centre for Environmental Life Sciences Engineering – and various leading research centres such as the Earth Observatory of Singapore, Nanyang Environment & Water Research Institute and Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N). Under the NTU Smart Campus vision, the University harnesses the power of digital technology and tech-enabled solutions to support better learning and living experiences, the discovery of new knowledge, and the sustainability of resources. Ranked amongst the world’s top universities, the University’s main campus is also frequently listed among the world’s most beautiful. Known for its sustainability, NTU has achieved 100% Green Mark Platinum certification for all its eligible building projects. Apart from its main campus, NTU also has a medical campus in Novena, Singapore’s healthcare district. Asian School of the Environment (ASE) Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The Asian School of the Environment (ASE) ( https://www.ntu.edu.sg/ase ) is an interdisciplinary school at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) that uses Earth and environmental science, engineering, technology, and the social sciences to address key environmental challenges. ASE is a school within the NTU College of Science (CoS). The Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) ( https://earthobservatory.sg/ ) is a research institute with the mission to conduct fundamental research on earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis and climate change in and around Southeast Asia, toward safer and more sustainable societies. Visiting Professor in Seismology A Visiting Professor position in Seismology is available at the Asian School of the Environment, Nanyang Technological University. The position will strengthen our research and educational capabilities in seismology and geophysics and contribute actively to the research culture of ASE and the Earth Observatory of Singapore. Responsibilities: Deliver lectures and seminars for the ASE community, including undergraduate and graduate students Co-advise and mentor junior researchers Engage with ASE and EOS faculty and research staff to develop research collaborations, including but not limited to conference and workshop organization, joint publications, and research proposals Requirements: A relevant Ph.D. from a reputable University Strong expertise in geophysics and seismology High international standing and visibility in their field of research An excellent track record of research publications Relevant university-level teaching experience Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Application Procedure We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. Applicants are invited to submit their applications through the NTU career portal by clicking on the “Apply” button above. Please provide the following in your application: Cover letter; Curriculum vitae (including records of competitive grants and graduate supervision, if applicable); All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Technical-Specialist--Mathematics---Mathematics-Education-Department---NIE-_R00025170": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Specialist (Mathematics & Mathematics Education Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE) , Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applications for the position of Senior Technical Specialist in the Mathematics & Mathematics Education Department. Responsibilities Managing the MME Outreach events to the Singapore schools, Ministry of Education and the academic faculties. The key events for MME include (1) the annual Mathematics Teachers Conference; (2) the bi-annual MME colloquium; (3) NIE / MME Mathematics challenge; (4) developing and maintaining social media outreach for MME. Provide IT/AV support for MME Department in the following areas: (a) coding and programming lessons; (b) cert in Primary Math Education course; (c) MME E- learning system; (d) manage MME labs for the IT/AV and facilities; (e) loaning of MME teaching manipulative, IT equipments and accessories; (f) MME representative for registering the removable storage media (RSM) in CAMs; (g) support MME lecturer with technical problem on the new laptop; (h) stamping of MME calculator for students before end-of-term examination. MME Website, social media and MME server management. Website management includes (1) School Mathematics Mastery Test; and (2) MME Math Qualify Test (MQT) system. Social media includes Facebook, X and Xiaohongshu. Video recording and video editing of MME events. Provide support roles in (a) assist Head MME for the NIE workload system; (b) MME facilities lab Booking Administrator; (c) manage and maintain Computer Labs and Math Labs; (d) MME Staff Welfare Committee (SWC) member. Provide Finance support in (a) Economy Drive Saving; (b) collating purchase requests for computer hardware and software; (c) supporting Good Receipt Officer; (d) keeping track of MME software and maintenance fund usage; (e) annual Software License Renewal; (f) managing MME fixed assets and records of inventories. Any other tasks assigned. Requirements A Bachelor’s Degree in any discipline, preferably related to Computer and Technologies. At least one year of experience as a technical support staff. Strong technical support and administrative skills, with experience in website/social media management, video recording and video editing, will be an added advantage. Ability to multi-task, work independently and effectively in a team. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both written and oral.   Hard working, self-discipline, responsible, committed.  Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 2 Sep 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Unit-Head--Research-Support-and-Grants-Management--RSGM---Office-for-Research--NIE-_R00024794-1": {
      "title": "Unit Head, Research Support and Grants Management (RSGM), Office for Research [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Unit Head, Research Support and Grants Management , Office for Research. The Research Support and Grants Management Unit manages pre and post award administration of internal and external research grants, enabling NIE faculty to secure research funding and administer grants effectively in compliance with funding and institutional requirements.  The unit also oversees all Research Support functions in capacity building faculty staff.   As the Unit Head of RSGM, you will lead a team overseeing research support, grants management and administration and play a key leadership role in providing strategic oversight and direction in strengthening institutional research capabilities and drive NIE’s strategic research agenda. Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership and oversight of the Research Support and Grants Management Unit within the Office for Research. Work closely with the Dean, Associate Deans and Assistant Deans in strategic planning and implementation of research support and grants management initiatives. Ensure alignment of unit activities, processes and initiatives with NIE’s institutional priorities and research agenda. Bridge and integrate research support and grants management functions to ensure coherent and effective operations. Provide guidance and advisory support to team members on research support, grants administration and related operational matters. Liaise with academic departments, research centres, administrative units and external parties on grants-related matters. Oversee grants management compliance, audit readiness and adherence to funder and institutional guidelines. Prepare and present reports on grants matters, research funding and research support initiatives to senior management and stakeholders. Lead the planning, coordination and implementation of research support initiatives and capacity-building programmes. Represent the unit in roadshows, presentations and engagement sessions on research support initiatives. Work with academic departments to promote and implement research support programmes and related activities. Oversee the administration of Education Research Funding Programme (ERFP) and non-ERFP grant programmes. Coordinate research data management and governance matters where relevant. Drive process reviews and improvements, including the adoption of AI initiatives, to strengthen governance, operational efficiency and service delivery. Oversee and maintain standard operating procedures, ensuring workflows remain current and effective. Supervise, mentor and support the team to ensure operational excellence and strategic alignment. Plan team workload, support capacity building and promote continuous professional development. Support in any other duties, as assigned by the reporting officer. Requirements A University Degree. Minimum 5 to 8 years of relevant experience in research administration, grants management, research support, policy coordination, or a similar administrative leadership role. Knowledge of audit, risk, and compliance frameworks related to grants and research administration. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to review processes and implement improvements. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare reports, briefs, presentations, and updates for senior management. A strong team lead who is highly motivated and also able to collaborate within and across teams. Strong interpersonal and relationship management skills. Integrity and discretion when handling confidential information. Proficient in using Microsoft Office applications and administrative systems relevant to grants or research operations. Closing Date   14 September 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Assessment_R00025473": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Assessment",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. SASD works collaboratively with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey for all students. This position sits with the Office of Academic Services (OAS), which plays a key role in advancing the University's educational goals through implementing and administering the academic policies and services within the University.  Being part of a team that manages students’ assessment, progression and award, the key responsibilities of the role are as follows: Processing of academic results: creation of exam records, course withdrawal, handle dissertation results related matters, marks processing, release and review of results. Maintain and update academic records for students on Leave of Absence, credit transfer, exemptions, programme withdrawal and change of programme. Post release of results activities: support administration of Medals and Prizes, compile and filing of mark lists and reports, and provide the relevant student academic information to stakeholders within the NTU community. Support the degree conferment process and regular data provision to MOE. Manage queries received from role-based mailbox and maintain access for secured folders. Attend to queries from stakeholders (e.g. students and Schools) on areas related to academic records. Support senior officers implementing policies and guidelines for proper governance, and to assist in advising Schools on procedures and guidelines. Support business process streamlining, designing of workflow, process automation and system enhancements. Requirements:  Degree/ Diploma holders with at least 3 years of working experience in administration functions. Entry-level candidates are welcome. Candidates with prior experience in administrative roles will have an added advantage. Proficient in office IT applications and Microsoft Office suite of application. Possess working knowledge of database and process management. Familiar with the Personal Data Protection Act, in relation to collection, use and disclosure of student personal data. Working knowledge of VQL will be an added advantage. Experience and exposure to Robotic Process Automation (RPA) or AI tools will be an added advantage. Meticulous and organised. Proactive, efficient and able to multi-task. Able to work independently and be a good team player. Good communication skills, able to express ideas clearly and concisely (written and oral). Good interpersonal skills and able to collaborate with people at different levels of the organization. Service-oriented mindset. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Housekeeping-Manager--Nanyang-Executive-Centre--Hospitality-_R00025647": {
      "title": "Housekeeping Manager, Nanyang Executive Centre (Hospitality)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. NEC features 150 refurbished guestrooms and refreshed event spaces that aims to offer a premier venue for high-level conferences, workshops, executive programmes, and industry engagements.    We are looking for an experienced person to join us as the Housekeeping Manager. The Housekeeping Manager will be responsible for establishing and maintaining high standards of cleanliness and organization throughout the NEC, including guest rooms, public areas, and back-of-house spaces. This role involves leading and training the housekeeping team, managing inventory, and collaborating with other departments to ensure a positive guest experience. Pre-opening duties will include setting up the housekeeping department, developing procedures, and preparing the team for the NEC’s launch. You will be responsible for executing Pre-Opening Tasks, assisting with the setup and organization of the housekeeping operations, participating in the development of operational procedures, standards & training staff on all aspects of service standards. KEY RESPONSIBILITES Create and implement housekeeping procedures and standards to ensure a clean, safe, and comfortable environment for guests and staff. Manage the daily activities of the housekeeping staff, including scheduling, training, and performance management. Ensure that all rooms and public spaces are cleaned and maintained to the highest standards. Accountable for departmental budgeting and P&L. Monitor the inventory of housekeeping supplies and equipment and make recommendations for purchases. Ensure compliance with all safety and health regulations and standards. Work with other departments to ensure the overall guest experience is positive and consistent. Participate in the recruitment and hiring process of new housekeeping staff. Essential Skills: Leadership and Team Management:  The ability to motivate, guide, and manage a team of housekeepers.  Communication:  Effective communication skills to interact with staff, guests, and other departments.  Organizational Skills:  The ability to plan, prioritize, and manage multiple tasks and responsibilities.  Attention to Detail:  The ability to notice and correct even minor imperfections in cleanliness and maintenance.  Knowledge of Cleaning Products and Techniques:  Understanding the appropriate use of cleaning supplies and equipment.  Problem-Solving:  The ability to identify and resolve issues related to housekeeping operations and guest requests.  Financial Management:  Understanding budgeting and cost control principles.  Customer Centric:  Service oriented style with professional presentations skills. REQUIREMENT Bachelor’s degree in Sales & Marketing, Hotel Management or relevant discipline. Diploma holders with extensive experience may be considered. Minimum 3-5 years of experience in housekeeping management within a hotel. Experience with accommodation/hotel pre-opening would be highly advantageous. Strong organizational and leadership skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Knowledge of safety and health regulations and standards. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager---Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Affairs_R00025648": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager / Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore offers a dynamic environment for education, research and innovation in materials science and engineering. The Senior Assistant Manager/Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs provides strategic and operational leadership for the School’s faculty affairs portfolio, covering recruitment and appointments, faculty lifecycle administration, engagement and recognition, space and infrastructure matters, academic events, reporting and related operations. Working within the governance framework and directions of the College of Engineering and the University, the role translates College and University requirements into effective School-level plans and processes. The role works closely with School leadership, faculty committees, the College, HR and relevant University offices to deliver accurate, timely and professional outcomes. Key Responsibilities: 1. Faculty Recruitment, Appointment and Reappointment Lead and manage the end-to-end faculty recruitment lifecycle, including recruitment, appointments, onboarding, appraisal, promotion, and reappointment. Develop and implement recruitment strategies to attract and retain high-calibre academic talent. Ensure all faculty appointment processes are accurate, efficient, and compliant with University policies, governance requirements, and timelines. Drive continuous process improvements to deliver a seamless and positive experience for faculty and stakeholders. 2. Faculty Development, Culture & Engagement Drive initiatives to foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing faculty culture. Lead the annual faculty performance appraisal process from planning to completion, ensuring timely completion, data integrity, data confidentiality, fairness and compliance with institutional policies.  Support faculty career development, leadership development and succession planning initiatives. Manage faculty welfare and case matters, including well-being, peer-to-peer issues, and student-faculty matters. 3. Space & Infrastructure Planning Lead the planning and management of faculty offices, researcher workspaces, research-focused laboratories, and shared facilities to optimize space utilization and support the School’s academic and research priorities.  Support policy development, strategic planning, data analysis, and documentation related to space and infrastructure management.  4. Stakeholder Management & Governance Serve as the primary liaison for faculty affairs-related queries from the Chair and senior leadership. Coordinate with College of Engineering to ensure consistent implementation of faculty-related policies, procedures and strategic initiatives. Engage with HR, finance, and administrative teams to align faculty affairs with broader institutional goals. 5. Strategic Planning, Data Management & Operations     Maintain accurate and up-to-date faculty records and databases to support budgeting, reporting, and strategic decision-making. Analyse faculty-related data and prepare management reports, dashboards, presentations, and briefing materials for senior leadership. Identify opportunities for continuous process improvement through data analysis and operational review. Provide operational guidance and support to team members, contributing to an effective, collaborative, and service-oriented work environment. Qualifications: A recognised Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD degree (or equivalent) with at least 5 years of relevant experience in people management, faculty administration, human resources, or a related field. Strong organisational, planning, and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Excellent stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships across all levels. Ability to balance strategic thinking with hands-on operational execution. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a data-driven approach to decision-making. High level of integrity, professionalism, and discretion in managing confidential and sensitive information. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Executive--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00023103": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Executive (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applicants for a Senior Executive / Executive position in the Finance Department . The Senior Executive / Executive plays a critical role in providing payroll and claims administration support for the Institute and ensuring accurate and timely payroll posting and claim processing for all employees within the organization. He/She oversees the payroll posting and claims administration, ensures compliance with statutory requirements, government legislation and group policies and standards, supports reporting needs and attends to queries from staff and stakeholders.  Responsibilities Manage payroll administration support including the monthly payroll postings for both full-time and part-time staff, statutory contributions and period end closing activities. Process payroll-related payments including but not limited to education allowances, passage claims and other miscellaneous payments. Perform finance related activities including but not limited to journal entries, reclassifications, and general ledger (GL) postings. Ensure employee claims submissions are accurate and in compliance with group policies and standards. Support budget submission and evaluation. Prepare and maintain regular and ad hoc requests of management reports/data by staff. Provide payroll posting related information for internal and external audits. Address employee inquiries and concerns related to payroll and claim posting. Educate employees on payroll and claim-related policies and procedures. Ensure the confidentiality of payroll data. Ensure service levels and targets are consistent with standards and timeliness, and service is delivered to customers in accordance with pre-defined Service Level Agreement. Support in various payroll and claim related projects and initiatives. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma or Degree preferably in Accountancy, Business or its equivalent. Preferably 2 or more years of working experience in handling payroll or claims. Some experience in finance matters, with accounting knowledge, will be an advantage. Organized, meticulous in handling data and a service-oriented mind-set. A positive attitude and willingness to learn and adapt, with problem-solving skills. An effective team player with the ability to work independently is preferred. Ability to prioritize and plan work activities in an organized manner, able to multi-task, track and deliver assignments on schedule. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Excel is a must. Experience in SAP and Ariba would be an added advantage. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 7 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Clinical-Trials---Translational-Research-_R00025393": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Clinical Trials & Translational Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance biological and biomedical sciences. At SBS, our research spans various areas, including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative diseases, telomere biology, and genome function. Over the years, SBS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sbs. We are looking for a Project Officer with a background and strong interest in integrative oncology, traditional Chinese medicine, Tai Chi and exercise therapy, massage therapy, or music therapy, to join the Yang Lab at NTU (https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sbs/Research/lab-pages/yang-mingxiao-lab). The successful candidate will contribute to an interdisciplinary project evaluating the clinical efficacy and biological mechanisms of traditional, complementary, and integrative medicine (TCIM) interventions for symptom management in cancer populations. The role will focus on coordinating clinical trials and supporting laboratory operations, bridging patient-centered trial activities with bench-based biospecimen handling and multiomics investigations. Through this work, the candidate will be well-positioned to grow at the interface of clinical and laboratory science, while shaping a distinctive academic and professional trajectory. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate randomized clinical trials, including ethics/IRB application and regulatory compliance Manage trial logistics, patient recruitment, scheduling, and follow-up Provide and/or coordinate integrative medicine treatments to study participants Oversee collection, processing, and management of clinical data and biospecimens Conduct data entry, curation, quality control, and preliminary analyses Oversee laboratory operations, ensuring compliance with institutional and local safety regulations and good laboratory practices Manage procurement of equipment, reagents, and consumables Train and onboard new research staff and students Liaise with clinical collaborators, institutional partners, and external stakeholders Support project reporting and documentation for funding and administrative purposes Engage in and contribute to other research activities the Lab is focusing on Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in life sciences, biomedical sciences, public health, social sciences, or related field A practitioner license issued by a foreign or international authority (i.e., traditional Chinese medicine, massage therapy, physical therapy, exercise therapy, etc.) registerable in Singapore Training or experience in complementary and integrative medicine practice or research from a reputable university At least 1-2 years of relevant experiences in clinical trial coordination, IRB submissions, or patient-facing research (entry-level candidates with strong interest are welcome to apply) Familiarity with biospecimen collection and handling, molecular biology, or omics techniques Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in data management, statistical analysis, or clinical research software Strong organizational and project management skills Excellent interpersonal skills to work both independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team Demonstrated interest in integrative medicine, oncology, or translational research The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager--Student-Care---Pastoral-Support_R00025643": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, Student Care & Pastoral Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Undergraduate Office is seeking a Senior Executive/Assistant Manager to support the Lead, Student Care & Development in providing timely and caring support to undergraduate students who may be experiencing academic, personal, social or adjustment difficulties. This is a developmental role with structured exposure, coaching and on-the-job learning to build capability in student care and pastoral support. Key Responsibilities: Provide first-line support, information and regular follow-up to students, and escalate concerns requiring further assessment or professional intervention. Coordinate student case follow-up, appointments, referrals and administrative support, including relevant academic support processes. Maintain accurate, timely and confidential case records, trackers, summaries and reports. Support academic intervention and outreach for students experiencing academic or attendance difficulties, including faculty mentoring referrals. Support student wellbeing, transition, adjustment and integration programmes, including logistics, communications, participation tracking and feedback. Maintain student-care data, assist with reporting and simple analysis, and support process improvement, digitalisation and student-facing resources. Work collaboratively across the Undergraduate Office and with relevant faculty and University support units. Role Boundary: The incumbent is not expected to independently manage high-risk or complex cases, provide professional counselling, or make crisis-intervention decisions. Such matters are escalated to the Lead and/or appropriate University professional services. Requirements: Diploma or Degree in Education, Psychology, Social Sciences, Social Work, Counselling, Community Services or a related discipline; candidates from other disciplines with a strong interest in student development and pastoral care may also be considered. 1–3 years of relevant working experience would be advantageous. Relevant education, youth work, student services, social services, community engagement, internship, volunteering, mentoring or student-development experience is useful. Empathy, patience, good listening and interpersonal skills, strong follow-up and organisation, appropriate judgement and escalation, confidentiality and discretion, and good written and verbal communication. Proficiency in Microsoft Office; familiarity with databases, Microsoft Forms, SharePoint or similar digital tools would be advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTUOne-North-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Legal_R00025646": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Legal",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Investment Office which manages the University’s multi-billion-dollar global investment fund, is seeking to add an experienced Fund Counsel to join its team. The successful candidate will work on complex investments across a broad range of asset classes, transaction structures and geographies. Reporting to the Chief Investment Officer, the Fund Counsel will work closely with investment professionals and key stakeholders, providing legal support throughout the investment lifecycle and helping to identify and manage legal, regulatory and contractual risks. Responsibilities: Review and advise on fund and investment structures, transaction terms and related legal documentation. Negotiate investment terms and transaction documentation with counterparties and external counsel. Advise investment teams on key legal, contractual, governance and regulatory considerations. Provide commercially focused legal advice that balances investment objectives with appropriate risk management. Requirements: Degree in Law from a reputable institution. Minimum 10 years of post-qualification legal experience. Strong experience in investment transactions, fund structures, corporate transactions, private markets and/or financial investments. Ability to work independently and manage multiple matters in a fast-paced investment environment. Strong communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Student-Experience-and-Vibrancy_R00025385": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Experience and Vibrancy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) provides comprehensive support across the student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond. SASD works closely with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey. Within SASD, the Student Affairs Office (SAO) plays a central role in shaping student life through leadership development, student-led activities, residential life, integration efforts, community engagement, arts, and sports. The successful candidate will support in the planning and execution of two flagship initiatives – the NTU Varsity Arts Programme and the inaugural NTU Arts Festival, while extending NTU’s Cultural presence into the western precinct and enriching arts and cultural life across the Halls of Residence. Key Responsibilities NTU Varsity Arts Programme Support year-round planning and delivery – coordinating performances, showcases and development opportunities for student artists. Work with Varsity Arts groups, coaches, and venues to keep programme on schedule and within budget, and establish the routines (calendars, booking, logistics). Inaugural NTU Arts Festival Assist in programme development, stakeholder engagement and partnership coordination. Manage festival project timelines, logistics, procurement and budget tracking. Coordinate marketing and publicity effors with internal and external stakeholders. Support onsite festival operations and ensure smooth event execution. Arts & Cultural Vibrancy in Halls of Residence Bring arts and culture into residential life by working with residential experience stakeholders to seed performances, workshops, pop-ups and student-led creative activities within the halls. Connect hall-based arts activity to the wider Varsity Arts Programme and Festival so residential life becomes a feeder and stage for campus arts. Neighbourhood & Stakeholder Engagement  Support the mission in broadening the reach of NTU Arts Festival beyond campus by establishing partnerships with residents, community groups, and public/private organisations. Through community-based arts activations and outreach initiatives, create meaningful opportunities for public participation and engagement, contributing to stronger community connections and elevating NTU's reputation as a vibrant arts and cultural hub. Requirements Degree in any discipline; entry-level candidates are welcome to apply. Candidates with experience in arts/cultural programming, event or festival management and/or related field will have an added advantage.  Strong interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build positive working relationships and engage effectively with diverse groups of stakeholders. Good organisational and project management capabilities, with the ability to coordinate multiple workstreams, manage timelines, and ensure smooth execution of programmes and events. A collaborative team player with a service-oriented mindset and the ability to work independently when required. Comfortable managing operational, logistical, and administrative aspects of events and programmes, including procurement, budgeting, and stakeholder coordination. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications. Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends to support programme delivery, performances, festivals, and student engagement activities as required. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager---Lab-Operations-and-Tech-support_R00025642": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager – Lab Operations and Tech support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is one of the world’s top research-intensive universities, committed to nurturing talent and creating knowledge for a better world. Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) is a leading research unit within NTU dedicated to advancing understanding of Earth’s systems, environmental change, and natural hazards. As teaching and research in Asian School of the Environment (ASE) is closely tied with EOS; we work closely with each other ensuring that all lab environments meet regulatory standards and are well-equipped to support research and academic activities. About the Role We are looking for a proactive and detail-oriented professional to join the team within ASE/EOS at NTU. In this role, you will play a key part in ensuring our research laboratories and office facilities are safe, compliant, operating efficiently and aligned with NTU’s research and education goals – directly supporting world-class scientific research. The incumbent will also work closely with and influence stakeholders to achieve the team’s operational and strategic objectives. Key Responsibilities Oversee laboratories equipment maintenance/certification, ensuring equipment under the custodian of the laboratory are always in safe working condition, complying with local regulations as well as OEM requirements. Liaise and coordinate with service engineers, vendors and contractors for laboratories maintenance, repairs, site surveys and facilities related works. Oversee the chemical inventory management system and hazardous waste disposal processes, ensuring proper documentation, safe handling practices, and compliance with Singapore regulatory and institutional safety requirements. Ensure chemical inventories are properly maintained, updated, and reconciled by laboratories in compliance with institutional safety policies. Plan, conduct, and support laboratory and office safety inspections, audits, and compliance reviews, ensuring proper documentation, audit readiness, and timely closure of findings. Lead the investigation of safety incidents, accidents, and non-compliance cases, including root cause analysis, and development of corrective and preventive actions to prevent recurrence. Track, monitor, and ensure timely follow-up and closure of all safety-related incidents, breaches, and rectification actions across laboratories and office facilities. Conduct safety induction briefings and training sessions for new staff, students, and research personnel, including fieldwork safety awareness and laboratory safety requirements. Monitor the completion of mandatory Online Safety Modules for staff and students, in accordance with University requirements. Oversee the maintenance and readiness of emergency response equipment, including first aid and fire safety equipment in laboratories and office areas. Support the preparation of fieldwork safety equipment and consumables. Support continuous improvement initiatives in laboratory operations, workplace safety and health, and facilities management to enhance efficiency, compliance, and service quality. Serve as a key operational point of contact for laboratory operations, safety, and facilities matters, ensuring adherence to safety standards and regulatory compliance. Provide backup support to other laboratories and safety personnel as required to ensure continuity of laboratory operations and safety coverage. Provide administrative and operational support to the OPS team, including coordination, documentation, reporting, and other ad-hoc duties as required. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in related field is preferred. At least 1–2 years of relevant experience in laboratory operations, facilities management, or safety administration. Knowledge of local safety regulations and guidelines relevant to typical research and laboratory activities, preferably in an IHL setting. Strong organisational and coordination skills with the ability to effectively manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage and collaborate effectively with diverse internal and external stakeholders at all levels. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, with the capability to identify issues, determine root causes, and implement appropriate corrective and preventive measures. High attention to detail, particularly in maintaining accurate records, documentation, and compliance-related reporting requirements. A proactive team player who is also able to work independently with minimal supervision and demonstrate initiative when required. We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Administration_R00025640": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Air Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, was established in 2013 through a collaboration between NTU and the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). Its mission is to conduct cutting-edge research in air traffic management (ATM) to support Singapore's position as a leading air hub and drive innovation in the Asia-Pacific region. ATMRI focuses on modernizing and harmonizing regional airspace operations to sustain the rapid growth of air transportation in the region. Its strategic research areas include artificial intelligence and data analytics for ATM, urban aerial transport systems, regional ATM modernization, exploratory studies on emerging technologies, and talent development through PhD programs. The institute aims to generate world-class ATM research, find innovative solutions, and catalyze transformation in the field. It plays a pivotal role in advancing the efficiency, safety, and sustainability of air traffic management systems. The Assistant Director, Administration provides strategic and operational leadership for ATMRI’s administrative functions. Reporting to the Director, the job holder oversees governance, finance, human resources, research programme administration, agreements, stakeholder engagement and institutional communications. The role supports the effective operation of the Institute, ensures compliance with University and funding-agency requirements, and facilitates the timely delivery of programme and institutional objectives. Job responsibilities: Lead the development, implementation and review of administrative policies, processes and operational plans. Oversee budget planning, expenditure monitoring, claims, financial reporting and audit readiness in accordance with NTU policies and funding requirements. Coordinate recruitment, onboarding, contract renewal, performance appraisal and other HR matters for research and administrative staff. Supervise and develop the administrative team, allocate responsibilities and ensure effective service delivery. Coordinate Governing Council and Scientific Advisory Panel appointments, meetings, papers, minutes, decisions and follow-up actions. Establish and maintain systems for monitoring research programme budgets, milestones, KPIs, deliverables, risks and contractual obligations. Coordinate programme reviews, claims, audits and submissions to funding agencies and oversight bodies. Manage the administrative coordination of MOAs, Project Agreements, Variation Agreements, MOUs, NDAs and other institutional agreements with NTU corporate offices and external partners. Maintain appropriate registers, records and evidence trails for governance, finance, agreements, programme reporting and compliance. Act as a key liaison with NTU corporate offices, government agencies, funding bodies, academic institutions and industry partners. Coordinate institutional communications, events, website content and outreach activities in accordance with NTU policies. Provide advice and administrative support to the Director and Institute Management Team on operational, governance and programme matters. Education qualifications: Recognised Bachelor’s Degree in Business Administration, Finance, Public Policy, Human Resource Management, or a related field. Postgraduate qualifications (e.g., MBA, MPA) will be advantageous. Relevant experience: Minimum 8 years of relevant working experience is preferred. Proven experience in administrative management, financial oversight, HR management, research programme management, and stakeholder engagement in a research center or university setting. Experience working with senior leadership, managing committees (e.g., Governing Councils, Scientific Advisory Panels), and coordinating large-scale institutional projects. Skills: Financial management skills. Human resource management skills. Corporate communication skills. Administrative skills. Statistical and data analysis. Competencies: Excellent written and oral communication skills. Good planning and organisation skills. Good problem solving and analytical skills. Good public relations, communication and influencing skills. Strong leadership and interpersonal skills. Able to work independently and as a team. Good supervisory skills. Proficiency in financial management tools and marketing platforms. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Finance--Accounts-Receivable-_R00024812": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Finance (Accounts Receivable)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU Shared Services (NSS) Finance is responsible for the efficient and effective operation of the finance related transaction services. One of the divisions in Accounts Receivables function is Student Finance. Student Finance oversees the end-to-end process of student billing and collection. Key responsibilities include monitoring accounts receivable, managing outstanding debts, enforcing credit control, and preparing management reports. This position is part of the Student Finance team reporting to Account Receivables Team. The job is required to process timely and accurate billing, collection of revenue, journal posting, prepare management reporting and financial aid disbursement. It ensures completeness in revenue recognition and compliance to University’s standard guideline and policy. This role will support functional process improvement and streamlining to meet university mission and vision. Candidate has an opportunity to learn more than 1 system in billing and collection, involve in system implementation and learn automated tools in process improvement. Qualification: Knowledge and Experience Minimum Degree / Equivalent Qualification in Accounting Minimum 5 years of relevant working experience Key Competency Requirements Able to work in a fast-paced environment and to work under pressure Service oriented, be hands-on, meticulous, analytical and have initiative Good interpersonal & communication skills Proficient in MS Excel and IT savvy, SAP knowledge is preferred Knowledge of Power Query or Power Automate is an advantage Able to work independently and collaboratively within a team We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate---Research-Fellow--Electrical---Electronics-_R00025242": {
      "title": "Research Associate / Research Fellow (Electronics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Emerging nanoscience Research Institute (EnRI) focuses its research on advanced materials, computational modelling & simulation and development of small-scale testing and materials characterization.  We are looking for a Research Associate / Research Fellow to support micro device research and development work. The role will work closely with the project team on the full spectrum of project activities, including experimental design, device fabrication, testing, and data analysis. Key Responsibilities: Design, develop and fabricate micro devices with desired performance that meet project requirement Provide research support to the project team and laboratory, including equipment maintenance, troubleshooting issues, and managing consumables Document methodologies, results, and findings in technical reports and presentations Job Requirements: Master’s (for Research Associate equivalent) / PhD (for Research Fellow equivalent) qualification degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science, Applied Physics, or related field Experience in high-reliability microelectronics Familiar with micro-fabrication techniques and semiconductor processing Experience in conducting electrical pulse testing Good written and oral communication skills A collaborative team player with strong interpersonal skills and a proactive and willingness to learn mindset Actual appointment grade will depend on candidate’s qualification and experience We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Construction-Technology-and-Protective-Engineering--CTPE--Laboratory_R00025548": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Construction Technology and Protective Engineering (CTPE) Laboratory",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Senior Executive, Construction Technology and Protective Engineering (CTPE) Laboratory is responsible for overseeing the day-to-day operations of the CTPE Laboratory in the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE), ensuring the efficient management of facilities, equipment, resources, and safety compliance. This key role drives operational excellence through the optimization of workflows, implementation of process improvements, and adoption of innovative laboratory and workshop practices Key Responsibilities: Serve as the primary person in charge of the workshop, managing laboratory and workshop operations, facilities, equipment, resources and schedules. Provide technical expertise in machining, fabrication and Computer Numerical Control (CNC) operations. Support faculty, researchers and students with fabrication, laboratory and technical requirements. Ensure safety, risk management, compliance and equipment maintenance. Oversee procurement, inventory, asset management and operational budgets. Train and mentor students, researchers and staff in equipment use and safe workshop practices. Drive process improvement, innovation and digital transformation in laboratory operations. Requirements Degree in Civil, Environmental, Mechanical Engineering or a related field, with at least 3 years’ relevant experience in laboratory/workshop operations, preferably in an academic or research environment. A Diploma in Engineering or related field with at least 5 years’ relevant experience may be considered. Proven expertise in machining, fabrication, CNC tools and workshop operations. Knowledge of construction technology, protective engineering equipment, laboratory safety and digital tools. Strong commitment to safety, compliance and operational excellence. Excellent organisation, communication, collaboration and mentoring skills, with strong attention to detail and multitasking ability. Passion for innovation, digital transformation and sustainable solutions. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Librarian--Digital-Scholarship---Education_R00025634": {
      "title": "Senior Librarian, Digital Scholarship & Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a leading research-intensive university known for its strong focus on innovation, interdisciplinary learning, and creating meaningful impact through education and research. The Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) plays an important role in supporting students across their academic journey, from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. Working closely with schools, colleges, and other partners across the University, SASD helps to create a seamless, enriching, and student-centred experience at NTU. Within this broader mission, NTU Libraries , under the Office of Information, Knowledge and Library Services (OIKLS) , provide essential learning, research, and collaborative environments that support the University community. We are seeking an experienced Senior Librarian, Digital Scholarship & Education to lead digital scholarship, academic integrity, reference management and library learning services that support the University’s teaching, learning and research needs. Key Responsibilities Lead the planning, delivery and evaluation of digital scholarship programmes, tools and learning resources. Champion responsible reference management and academic integrity practices through training, outreach and expert support. Evaluate and enhance reference management software and related digital scholarship tools based on user needs and service priorities. Develop instructional frameworks, learning programmes and online resources for undergraduate, postgraduate and Continuing Education and Training learners. Build stakeholder partnerships and outreach initiatives to increase awareness, engagement and adoption of library services. Monitor emerging trends in digital scholarship, AI-enabled tools and instructional practices to guide service improvement. Requirements Master’s degree in information studies or equivalent, with a bachelor’s degree in any field. At least seven years of relevant experience in academic, research or special libraries. Strong knowledge of reference and citation management, digital scholarship and information literacy instruction. Good research, communication, collaboration, organisational and stakeholder engagement skills. Proactive, adaptable and committed to continuous learning and service improvement. At NTU, you will join a collaborative and forward-looking university environment committed to continuous learning, innovation, and service excellence. This role offers the opportunity to work across diverse library settings, partner stakeholders across the University, and contribute to improvements that have meaningful and visible impact on the campus community. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00022754": {
      "title": "Executive (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applicants for an Executive position in the Finance Department . This is a 3-year contract position . Responsibilities You will be part of the team which handles undergraduate billing and other student-related financial matters for the institute. Your responsibilities will include: Billing for undergraduate courses, hostels and facilities. Checking that all payment transactions have appropriate certification and approvals before being processed for payments. Responding to enquiries pertaining to facilities and student matters. Assisting in the design, implementation and review of financial processes, policies and guidelines for continuous improvements, through streamlining and automation. Participating in system implementation, enhancements, and user acceptance testing. Handling ad hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma in Accountancy or its equivalent. At least 2 years of financial administration and accounting work experience. Good organizational and communication skills. A positive attitude and willingness to learn and adapt, with problem-solving skills. An effective team player with the ability to work independently is preferred. Ability to prioritize and plan work activities in an organized manner, able to multi-task, track and deliver assignments on schedule. Self-motivated, energetic and results oriented. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Microsoft Word and Excel. Experience in SAP and Ariba would be an added advantage. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 1 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--EdTech-Solutions_R00025633": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, EdTech Solutions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nShape the Future of Learning: Senior Assistant Manager, Educational Technology Solutions About Nanyang Technological University (NTU) Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a world-class, research-intensive public university dedicated to providing a transformative education, advancing research, and nurturing global leaders. Driven by innovation, excellence, and a commitment to positive global impact, NTU fosters an inclusive and vibrant ecosystem where cutting-edge technology meets education. At InsPIRE - Educational Services, we implements, integrates, and optimises our digital learning ecosystem to deliver a seamless, user-centric and high-impact teaching and learning experience. We lead the deployment, integration, and enhancement of next-generation educational technologies and artificial intelligence (AI) solutions, ensuring world-class learning outcomes for faculty and students alike. The Opportunity We are seeking a dynamic, forward-thinking Senior Assistant Manager, EdTech  Solutions to join our dedicated team. In this pivotal role, you will be at the forefront of educational technology innovation, designing and deploying enterprise AI applications that directly transform teaching and learning across the university. Key Highlights of the Role Drive AI-Powered Innovation: Build and implement modern AI tools, smart agent frameworks, and enterprise educational applications that directly enhance student and faculty engagement. High-Impact Collaboration: Work closely with educators, technologists, and university leaders to solve complex educational challenges and transform digital learning paradigms. Modern Cloud & Systems Architecture: Architect, integrate, and manage scalable cloud applications on leading cloud infrastructure platforms. Role & Responsibilities Department: InsPIRE Educational Services Location: Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (Main Campus) Reporting To: Senior Assistant Director, Educational EdTech Solutions   As a Senior Assistant Manager, you will play a hands-on role in software development, AI tool integration, and stakeholder empowerment. Primary Duties: Solution Delivery & Software Development: Design, test, and deploy enterprise-grade software applications and AI-driven educational tools using Python and Java to improve learning outcomes and engagement metrics. Systems Integration & Scalability: Build secure, reliable integrations between learning management platforms and enterprise databases to enable smooth data flow and seamless user experiences. AI Tool Development & Framework Management: Harness Large Language Model application programming interfaces (APIs) and modern AI agent frameworks to build intelligent educational assistants and workflow automations. Stakeholder Enablement & Engagement: Partner with academic units and operational teams to understand user needs, provide technical guidance, and empower faculty and students to maximize the value of new technologies. Technical Documentation & Support: Maintain standardized, high-quality system architecture documentation to ensure smooth onboarding, efficient troubleshooting, and minimal system downtime. Technology Exploration: Continuously research, evaluate, and prototype emerging technologies in artificial intelligence, automation, and analytics to elevate educational service delivery. Why Join NTU? At NTU, we value our people as our greatest strength. Joining InsPIRE Educational Services means becoming part of an inspiring, supportive, and growth-oriented work environment. Continuous Learning & Professional Growth: Access extensive learning and development opportunities, professional certification programs, and workshops to keep your technical skills sharp in fast-evolving fields like AI and DevOps. Career Progression: Enjoy structured career development opportunities within a leading global university system. Staff Welfare & Hybrid Work Initiatives: Benefit from flexible work arrangements (including Work-From-Home options), comprehensive medical coverage, and regular university-wide employee engagement and team-building activities (CREW initiatives). Vibrant Campus Community: Experience a diverse, inclusive, and collaborative campus atmosphere equipped with world-class facilities. Candidate Qualifications & Requirements Must-Have Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a relevant technical discipline. Software Engineering Experience: At least 3+ years of hands-on backend software development experience using Python or Java in an enterprise environment. AI & Machine Learning Exposure: Practical experience building applications using Large Language Model (LLM) APIs (e.g., Gemini, OpenAI, Claude) and prompt engineering techniques. AI Agent Frameworks: Hands-on experience working with modern AI agent frameworks (e.g., LangGraph, Google ADK, Bedrock Agents). Cloud & DevOps Skills: Practical experience deploying containerized applications (using Docker) on cloud platforms (AWS or GCP) with standard Continuous Integration / Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines. Core Competencies: Excellent problem-solving skills, strong stakeholder engagement abilities, adaptable thinking, and high integrity. Good-to-Have Skills (Preferred): Experience with Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) tools such as Terraform. Familiarity with container orchestration using Kubernetes. Prior experience working within higher education or ed-tech environments. How to Apply If you are passionate about leveraging technology to shape the future of education, we would love to hear from you! Please submit your updated CV and cover letter through the NTU Careers Portal. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Research-Grant-Administration_R00023325": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Research Grant Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nRoles and Responsibilities: The position will be responsible for the administration of research grants handled by NTU’s Research Support Office. This includes: Submission of research proposals and coordination of review panel meetings and the administration of awarded research grants. Be part of a team to handle the governance aspect of research data management relevant to research grants.  The role will also be involved in ad-hoc initiatives undertaken by the Office. Requirements: Degree in a relevant field with at least 5 years of proven experience in research grant administration. Strong time management, planning, and organisational skills, with the ability to handle multiple assignments. Fast learner who can work independently and adapt quickly. Strong analytical skills with keen attention to detail. Excellent writing, communication, and interpersonal skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Research-Grant-Administration_R00023326": {
      "title": "Manager, Research Grant Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRoles and Responsibilities: The position will be responsible for the administration of research grants handled by NTU’s Research Support Office. This includes: Submission of research proposals and coordination of review panel meetings and the administration of awarded research grants. Be part of a team to handle the governance aspect of research data management relevant to research grants.  The role will also be involved in ad-hoc initiatives undertaken by the Office. Requirements: Degree in a relevant field with at least 7 years of proven experience in research grant administration. Strong time management, planning, and organisational skills, with the ability to handle multiple assignments. Fast learner who can work independently and adapt quickly. Strong analytical skills with keen attention to detail. Excellent writing, communication, and interpersonal skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Grant-Management-_R00024908": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (Grant Management)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe CyberSG R&D Programme Office (CRPO) is a new national centre at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. CRPO will focus its efforts on three main thrusts to advance cybersecurity comprehensively: cutting-edge research and development, advancements in technology and translational development, and fostering ecosystem/industry growth and training. CRPO aspires to propel Singapore to the forefront of cybersecurity innovation and implementation, fueled by funding from the Cybersecurity Agency of Singapore (CSA). This financial backing empowers CRPO to finance visionary projects proposed by diverse entities, including research institutes (RIs), institutions of higher learning (IHLs), and industries. The scope of these initiatives spans the entire Technology Readiness Level (TRL) spectrum, from nascent concepts at TRL 1 to advanced, field-tested solutions at TRL 9, all within the dynamic realm of cybersecurity. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/crpo . As Assistant Manager (Grants Management), you will assist Team Lead to oversee the full lifecycle of grant programmes, ensuring robust governance, strategic alignment, and impactful outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Assist Team lead in grant strategy & programme design Co-Lead the design and implementation of grant programmes, including funding frameworks, thematic priorities, and evaluation approaches aligned with national cybersecurity objectives. Governance & Policy Development Enforce and maintain strong policies, procedures, and controls to ensure transparency, compliance, and accountability in grant administration. Evaluation & Funding Decisions Assist Team lead to oversee proposal evaluation processes, working with expert panels to ensure fair, rigorous, and strategic selection of projects with strong innovation and translation potential. Stakeholder Engagement Build and manage partnerships across universities, research institutes, industry, and government agencies to drive collaboration and alignment. Financial Stewardship Manage grant budgets and funding allocation, ensuring effective utilisation of resources and adherence to financial and audit requirements. Project Monitoring & Impact Delivery Oversee project performance, ensuring milestones, deliverables, and outcomes are achieved, with a focus on real-world cybersecurity impact. Programme Improvement Continuously enhance grant frameworks and processes through data-driven insights, stakeholder feedback, and benchmarking against global best practices. Leadership & Team Development Lead and develop a multidisciplinary team, fostering a high-performance culture and strong collaboration across functions. Job Requirements: At least a degree in a relevant field (e.g., business management, project management, cybersecurity, engineering, computer science, public policy, or related disciplines) At least 3 years of relevant experience in grant management, research administration, project or programme management Good understanding of research and innovation ecosystems, preferably in cybersecurity or deep technology domains Proven experience in designing and managing funding programmes or large-scale initiatives Good stakeholder management skills, with experience engaging across academia, industry, and government Demonstrated experience in complex projects Prior experience in coordination of internal review, approval, and submission processes Good analytical, strategic thinking, and decision-making capabilities Good-to-Have: Experience in public sector or national-level R&D programmes Familiarity with research translation, commercialisation, or innovation ecosystems Knowledge of financial governance, audit processes, and compliance frameworks Established network within the cybersecurity or technology community We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Data-and-Analytics_R00025570": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Data and Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Data and Analytics (ODA) at Nanyang Technological University is seeking a Senior Assistant Manager, Data and Analytics to support NTU’s strategic decision-making through rigorous data analysis, statistical modelling and evidence-based insights. The role contributes to institutional planning, university rankings and reputation, faculty and student outcomes, research analytics, and continuous improvement of data processes across the University. Job Responsibilities: Generate insights from both external and internal data to facilitate evidence-based decision making at all levels of the University.  Build databases, develop data analytics and implement strategies to optimize statistical efficiency. Refine existing processes and define new processes in data collection to support decision-making at all levels of the University. Work in teams of stakeholders across various units. Job Requirements: PhD in Social Sciences, Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics or a related discipline. Strong knowledge of applied statistics, empirical research methods and quantitative analysis. Experience handling, cleaning, validating and analysing complex datasets. Good coding skills; familiarity with Python and R will be advantageous. Ability to develop analytical models and communicate complex findings clearly to diverse stakeholders. Resourceful, resilient and collaborative, with good communication skills; data visualisation skills will be an added advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Research-Management_R00025530": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Research Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Office at College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences oversees high quality college internal grant initiatives in addressing research funding needs of faculty. The Office provides seed funding to faculty members and commit to bolstering excellence in their external grant applications through grant admin support, high profile grant consultancy, and organisation of workshops that disseminate knowledge on grant writing and foster interdisciplinary research collaboration. This is in line with NTU's aspiration and continued rise as a leading research university, with research evolved to be more collaborative, global and interdisciplinary in nature. The incumbent works closely within CoHASS Research Administration at the College level to mobilise resources with the aim to increase discussions at conferences, symposia and workshops to bring forth interesting and important ideas leading to further research and collaboration, publications, and proposals for external grant applications. The incumbent would also provide secretariat support to Associate Dean (Research). Key Responsibilities: Research Grants Administration Co-lead and oversee the end-to-end administration of research grants , Drive and coordinate grant call launches with CoHASS Research Offices and Research Offices in other NTU colleges and institutions by facilitating review, approval and account creation processes with various parties. Take ownership of internal seed grant funding schemes of the College Research Office (including grants, such as the Startup Grants and MOE Tier 1 Seed grants) and SSHR 2030 Seed Grant scheme, throughout the entire lifecycle of the funding/grant scheme. Review seed grants administrative processes, analyse and recommend areas of process improvements, and follow through with providing consultation to School Research Offices on implementation of process improvements. Proactively engage and build relationships with PIs and research managers across Colleges’ and Institutes’ School Research Offices and obtain grant data, information and grant reports for application and variation/virement processing, and for regular monitoring. Serve as trusted advisor and problem solver , addressing complex faculty queries on research grants matters. Research publicity Co-lead the strategic planning and execution of innovative initiatives to enhance research engagement and participation in CoHASS internal grants, external competitive grants and SSHR 2030. Drive and oversee the activities of the College Research Centres fostering collaboration and multidisciplinary research partnerships among Schools to strengthen research impact and visibility. Co-lead research event publicity planning and execution efforts , proactively coordinate dissemination strategies, liasing with key NTU stakeholders and ensuring high quality content across websites, posters and electronic mailers that effectively showcase the college research office and research Centres, analyse and make recommendations on publicity initiatives that will enhance participation in key college events across schools and research centres. Data Management and Reporting Co-lead the development and implementation of robust processes and tools to enhance data management and reporting for the College Research Office and Centres, and SSHR 2030, ensuring accuracy, efficiency, and strategic alignment. Drive data governance and integrity by co-supervising the collection, management and reporting of research metrics, including research outputs at the College, Schools and Research Centre levels, as well as SSHR 2030 progress. Administrative and Secretarial support Provide high level administrative leadership and strategic support to Associate Dean (Faculty), ensuring seamless coordination of faculty related initiatives and operational efficiency. Drive collaboration and process improvements by working proactively with School Associate Chair (Faculty) Offices to enhance service excellence, make recommendations on streamlining administrative workflows, and ensure timely resolution of complex faculty-related requests. Lead the end-to-end management and delivery of the college driven programmes, working closely with Dean and relevant stakeholders to drive successful implementation and outcomes. Requirements: At least a degree in a relevant field (e.g., business management, project management, finance). Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in research development, grant writing, funding strategy or research management, preferably in a university, research institute, or R&D environment. Familiarity with Singapore research funding landscape (e.g., NRF, MOE, A*STAR) is advantageous. Experience in preparing large competitive research grant proposals or coordinating multi-investigator submissions. Excellent technical writing, analytical, organisational, and stakeholder engagement skills. Relevant experience in administration, research, grants, finance, compliance or stakeholder support would be advantageous. Strong organisational and analytical skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines, track deliverables and follow through on outstanding matters. Good communication skills and comfortable working with different stakeholders. Adaptable and willing to learn. Proficient in using digital tools for tracking, documentation and collaboration; familiarity with grant management systems would be an advantage. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive--Outreach--Industry-Partnerships-_R00025495": {
      "title": "Executive, Outreach (Industry Partnerships)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) in NTU is renowned for its research prowess in advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, industrial, maritime engineering, and robotics. Aligned with Singapore’s RIE2030 strategy, MAE drives technological innovation, bolstering local manufacturing and engineering sectors. MAE offers comprehensive undergraduate programmes in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering, ensuring students gain a robust engineering foundation and modern technological expertise. At the graduate level, MAE provides Master of Science programmes and Ph.D. opportunities that emphasize industry-relevant skills and cutting-edge research, preparing students for leadership roles in their fields. The Executive, Outreach (Industry Partnerships) supports the University’s mission by strengthening industry engagement, creating meaningful employment and internship opportunities for MAE graduate students, and enhancing graduate employability through coordinated outreach initiatives and strategic partnerships. Key Responsibilities: 1. Outreach & Stakeholder Engagement Identify target industries, associations, and potential partner organizations. Engage industry partners to identify and secure employment and internship opportunities for students. Event Planning & Coordination with Students and Programme Directors. Manage end-to-end planning for seminars and industry visits (concept, agenda, speakers, venues, logistics). Coordinate with speakers, venues, vendors, and internal teams to ensure seamless execution. Act as a backup or support lead for other organizational events (workshops, seminars) as needed, including planning, logistics, and on-site support. 2. Marketing & Communications Support Collaborate with Marketing to promote events through email campaigns, social media, and industry networks. Maintain accurate contact records, track outreach activities, and monitor attendance and engagement metrics. Requirements: Diploma in Business, Communications, Marketing, Public Relations, Human Resource or a related field. At least 3 years’ experience in partnerships or business development; experience with industry seminars or corporate visits is a plus; demonstrated ability to support other types of events is beneficial. Excellent written and verbal communication; persuasive and professional presentation skills. Project management with the ability to manage multiple events concurrently. Strong networking and relationship-building capabilities. Budgeting, vendor management, and contract negotiation skills. Skills & Competencies: Strategic thinker with a results-oriented mindset. Detail-oriented, organized, and proactive problem-solver. Ability to work collaboratively across departments and with external partners. Comfort with travel for on-site visits and events as required. Other Personal Attributes Team player. High Integrity & Confidentiality. Adaptability & Resilience. Customer-Centric Mindset. Financial Awareness. Collaborative & Team-Oriented. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Data-Infra_R00025373": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Data Infra",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI.  AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. This position will be hosted at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. We're looking for an AI Engineer to join the Platform team within AI Products at AISG. In this role, you will design, build, and scale the data infrastructure that powers large language model (LLM) training, fine-tuning, evaluation, and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) across the organisation. Your work will directly contribute to the architecture and reliability of data storage systems, data pipelines, and the compute infrastructure that supports large-scale AI workloads. Responsibilities: Data infrastructure and architecture Develop and maintain the overall data architecture, ensuring it scales to support AI training, fine-tuning, evaluation, and RAG workloads. Define and manage the data technology stack, evaluating and adopting tools that best fit evolving data needs. Build automation for data transfer and backup, and support data cataloging/discovery tools. Design and maintain data pipelines (batch and streaming) using tools like AWS Glue and Amazon EMR. Data governance and management Architect and govern org-level IAM policy across AWS Organizations including SCPs, cross-account roles, and permission boundaries to enforce least-privilege access at scale. Review and enhance data access patterns for performance and cost optimization. Develop and manage data analytics and dashboarding capabilities using tools like Amazon Athena and QuickSight to give stakeholders visibility into platform usage and cost. AI-assisted ops and continuous improvement Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) appropriately in your daily work responsibilities. Build internal tools leveraging AI to reduce manual effort in day-to-day operations. Requirements: You should be a hands-on engineer who enjoys both building robust infrastructure and designing tools that other engineers and researchers want to use. You should be comfortable balancing platform ownership (architecture, cost, governance) with product thinking (usability, self-service, adoption). A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. At least 2–4 years of data infrastructure, platform or systems engineering experience, with a track record of operating production systems at scale. Strong knowledge of distributed data systems and storage technologies (object storage, data lakes, distributed file systems, vector databases) and data pipelining tools (e.g. Apache Spark, Apache Airflow, Ray, Dagster). Working knowledge of data access control and data orchestration. Familiarity with cloud organisational structures (e.g. AWS Organizations, GCP folder/project hierarchy), including multi-account/multi-project setups, org-level IAM, and billing/cost allocation. Hands-on experience operating workloads on different cloud providers including IaC (e.g. Terraform), containers and orchestration (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes), and managed services for compute, storage, and networking. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering — for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation — with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Solid scripting/programming skills (e.g. Python, SQL) and comfortable reading other people's code across the stack. Strong communication skills and a team collaborator. Good to Have: Experience with LLM training dataset (e.g. Common Crawl). C/C++/Rust/Go or other relevant programming languages. Contributions to open-source AI/ML projects. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Platforms_R00025364": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Platforms",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. We're looking for an AI Engineer to join the Platform team within AI Products at AISG. In this role, you will be collaborating with different internal teams to design and implement optimized inference workflows and support the team to build customized LLM-based solutions. Your work will directly contribute to the deployment, optimisation and management of large language models (LLMs) in production, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) services, AI agent orchestration platforms and GPU-enabled AI infrastructure. Responsibilities: Platform operations and reliability Own day-to-day operations of SEA-LION API Farm, our multi-cloud LLM inference platform — monitoring environment health, GPU capacity, performance, cost, and security posture. Optimise LLM inference across various modalities to drive business value and support production goals. Diagnose and troubleshoot performance and reliability issues on API Farm. Build new API services such as batch API services, MCP services. Infrastructure, CI/CD, and automation Manage high performance AI clusters and storage systems using infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform) across different cloud providers. Develop and maintain CI/CD pipelines, container build/registry workflows, and deployment automation so teams can ship safely and frequently. Strengthen observability across the stack including logs, metrics, traces, and dashboards, and reduce toil by automating repetitive operational tasks. AI-assisted ops and continuous improvement Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) appropriately in your daily work responsibilities. Build internal tools leveraging AI to reduce manual effort in day-to-day operations. Requirements: You should be a hands-on engineer who is comfortable operating cloud and GPU infrastructure end-to-end, who understands how to deploy and run large language models reliably in production, and who actively uses AI tools to make platform work faster and more reliable. A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. 1–3 years of DevOps, SRE, or platform engineering experience, with a track record of operating production systems at scale. Hands-on experience operating workloads on different cloud providers including IaC (e.g. Terraform), containers and orchestration (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes), and managed services for compute, storage, and networking. Strong knowledge on Inference frameworks and libraries (e.g., vLLM, SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, Transformers). Hands-on experience deploying and serving LLMs in production — model serving, GPU scheduling, autoscaling, latency/throughput optimisation, and inference cost management. REST API design, model context protocol (MCP), Internet authentication patterns (e.g. OAuth). Strong fundamentals in CI/CD, observability (logs/metrics/traces), and incident response. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering — for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation — with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Solid scripting/programming skills (e.g. Python, Bash) and comfortable reading other people's code across the stack. Strong communication skills with the ability to explain technical concepts. Good to Have: Experience with multimodal AI models (e.g. vision language models, audio language models). C/C++/Rust/Go or other relevant programming languages. Contributions to open-source AI/ML projects. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--AI-Products-_R00024969": {
      "title": "AI Engineer (AI Products)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI.  AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. The AI Products Pillar of AI Singapore develops AI-powered products and solutions that benefit Singapore and the region. We are looking for an AI Engineer to contribute to the development, training, evaluation and engineering of state-of-the-art multilingual, multicultural and multimodal foundation Large Language Models (LLMs), with a focus on underrepresented languages and cultures and real-world AI applications. The role involves working at the intersection of frontier LLM research, large-scale data engineering, distributed model training, evaluation, and productisation. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Key Responsibilities: Develop, train, fine-tune and evaluate multilingual, multicultural and multimodal foundation LLMs and related technologies, including continued pre-training, supervised fine-tuning, instruction tuning, preference optimisation and model adaptation. Build and maintain scalable data pipelines for multilingual text ingestion, cleaning, filtering, deduplication, tokenisation, contamination detection and dataset mixture creation. Support large-scale distributed model training workflows, including experiment tracking, checkpointing, training monitoring, debugging, profiling and compute optimisation. Review frontier AI and LLM research papers, reproduce relevant methods, and translate research findings into practical improvements in model training, evaluation and deployment workflows. Contribute to reusable engineering assets such as training scripts, evaluation tools, model artefacts, APIs, documentation and deployment-ready components. Collaborate with internal teams, external research labs, academic institutions, industry partners and ecosystem stakeholders on LLM research, development and knowledge-sharing activities. Support AI Singapore’s community-building efforts through technical sharing, seminars, workshops, publications or other outreach activities where relevant. Requirements: We welcome applicants from all disciplines and qualification pathways, including NITEC, Diploma, Bachelor’s, Master’s or PhD holders, as well as candidates with equivalent practical experience. A formal qualification in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Data Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Computational Linguistics or a related field would be advantageous but is not mandatory. Candidates should be able to demonstrate the following skills and experience: Strong AI/ML engineering capability:  Proficient in Python with strong software engineering practices, including clean and modular code, Git, testing, documentation and code review. Hands-on experience with PyTorch and modern NLP/LLM frameworks, especially the Hugging Face ecosystem such as Transformers, Datasets, Tokenizers, Accelerate and TRL. LLM development and multilingual NLP expertise:  Experience or strong working knowledge in LLM pre-training, continued pre-training, fine-tuning, instruction tuning, preference optimisation, evaluation and model adaptation. Familiarity with multilingual NLP challenges such as low-resource languages, code-switching, language imbalance, script diversity, tokenisation issues and multilingual benchmark design. Large-scale data and training pipeline development:  Ability to build scalable pipelines for text processing, dataset preparation and model training. Familiarity with distributed training concepts, GPU-based training, checkpointing, experiment tracking, training stability and compute optimisation. MLOps, infrastructure and deployment:  Familiarity with Linux environments, Docker, CI/CD concepts, cloud platforms or GPU/HPC clusters. Experience with reproducible model development workflows, model versioning, evaluation automation and deployment through APIs or serving frameworks such as vLLM, SGLang, TGI or equivalent tools would be advantageous. Research, problem-solving and communication:  Able to read and evaluate research papers, design experiments, conduct ablation studies, analyse results and translate findings into practical model or system improvements. Able to communicate technical concepts, trade-offs and evaluation outcomes clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders. Personal attributes:  Self-directed learner with strong curiosity, high ownership and resilience. Collaborative, rigorous and engineering-minded, with a commitment to reproducibility, reliability, documentation and responsible AI development. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Grant-Support_R00023364": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Grant Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Air Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, was established in 2013 through a collaboration between NTU and the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). Its mission is to conduct cutting-edge research in air traffic management (ATM) to support Singapore's position as a leading air hub and drive innovation in the Asia-Pacific region. ATMRI focuses on modernizing and harmonizing regional airspace operations to sustain the rapid growth of air transportation in the region. Its strategic research areas include artificial intelligence and data analytics for ATM, urban aerial transport systems, regional ATM modernization, exploratory studies on emerging technologies, and talent development through PhD programs. The institute aims to generate world-class ATM research, find innovative solutions, and catalyze transformation in the field. It plays a pivotal role in advancing the efficiency, safety, and sustainability of air traffic management systems. Key Responsibilities: Oversee manpower planning and administration through RISE, including approvals, budget checks, expenditure monitoring, and reporting. Lead finance functions and timely reporting. Act as the point of contact for finance and operational matters with research teams, institutional offices, and external partners. Oversee planning and execution of events, meetings, visits and institute-wide activities. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in Business, Communications, Public Policy, or related discipline. 6–8 years of relevant experience in project administration and programme coordination. Experience in higher education, research administration, or public-sector programmes preferred. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Effective communication and stakeholder management abilities. Familiarity with project management tools and MS Office suite. This is a yearly renewable contract position subject to performance and funding requirements.  We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director-Senior-Assistant-Director--Gift-Stewardship-and-Reporting--Stewardship_R00024899": {
      "title": "Assistant Director/Senior Assistant Director, Gift Stewardship and Reporting, Stewardship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University Advancement Office (UAO) supports NTU’s giving mission by fostering meaningful relationships and strategic partnerships with philanthropists, alumni, business community partners, corporations that result in goodwill and philanthropy towards education and research that underpin a shared sustainable future. Reporting into the Deputy Director, Stewardship, the Senior Assistant Director of Gift Stewardship and Reporting plays a pivotal role in managing the stewardship and reporting functions for major donors at NTU. This role is primarily responsible for developing and executing comprehensive fund stewardship procedures. Working collaboratively with faculties, the position ensures effective donor fund utilisation by aligning donor contributions with institutional needs, while maintaining adherence to donor intentions and organisational priorities. Key responsibilities include Monitoring of Donor Fund Utilisation: Work with Faculties to ensure the allocation and administration of donor funds are used according to donor intentions and organisational priorities. Monitor the effectiveness of fund utilisation and provide transparent reporting on fund impacts. Develop, implement and improve upon processes to aid the accurate monitoring of these funds. Impact Reporting: Supervise the preparation and delivery of detailed impact reports for major donors. Ensure reports accurately reflect the outcomes and achievements resulting from their contributions, and maintain high standards of reporting accuracy and integrity. Data Management and Analysis: Ensure the accuracy and confidentiality of donor records within the CRM system. Track and analyse donor engagement data to inform strategic decisions and maintain compliance with reporting standards. Stewardship and Donor Engagement: Develop and implement strategic plans to recognise and engage major donors. This involves creating tailored recognition programs, managing personalised communications, and fostering strong donor relationships to enhance engagement and retention. Faculty Engagement: Collaborate with faculty members to ensure that donor funds are utilised effectively. Align donor contributions with faculty needs and projects and facilitate communication between faculty and donors to demonstrate the impact of their support. Strategic Alignment: Work closely with leadership to align stewardship initiatives with NTU’s strategic goals. Contribute to long-term planning and goal-setting to support the university’s growth and success. Requirements: A good university Degree, preferably Master’s Degree in Accountancy, Finance, Economics, or Engineering fields. Minimum of 10 - 12 years’ progressive experience, preferably within higher education, philanthropic organisations or a comparably complex organisation. Demonstrated success in achieving strategic outcomes in a large and complex environment. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to think strategically and critically. Proficiency in numerical analysis to derive insights that can improve strategies, polices and processes is essential. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of engaging stakeholders across all levels. Excellent ability to innovate and deal with ambiguity and organisational sensitivity with tact and diplomacy; to be opportunistic, responsive, resourceful, and resilient. Demonstrate a clear understanding and awareness of ethical considerations pertaining to advancement work, as well as an understanding and appreciation of cultural and intercultural sensitivities. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Full-Stack_R00024983": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Full Stack",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in Artificial Intelligence (AI). Hosted by the Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AISG brings together all Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies developing AI products to perform use-inspired research, grow the knowledge, create the tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. We're looking for an AI Engineer, Full Stack to join the Data Platform team within AI Products at AISG. ATLAS Data Platform is a data platform which supports a global effort to collect multimodal language and cultural data. You'll develop modules end-to-end for this platform from UI/UX through to backend services and deploy them on cloud infrastructure. You'll work heavily with AI tools in your day-to-day engineering workflow, and you'll build features that support evaluations, benchmarks, and data annotation across our internal teams and external partner communities. This role calls for solid engineering fundamentals, comfort working across the stack, and an appetite for shipping. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Duties & Responsibilities: Platform development and engineering Design, build, and maintain modules of the data platform across the full stack such as frontend interfaces, backend services, APIs, and data models to support multimodal data collection, curation, and access. Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) deliberately in your engineering workflow for code generation, refactoring, code review, debugging, and documentation and help the team codify good practices around AI-assisted development. Write clean, well-tested, maintainable code; participate in code reviews and design discussions; and contribute to the platform's technical documentation. Domain workstreams: evaluations, benchmarks, and annotation Build features and tooling that support model and data evaluations, benchmark execution, and result tracking across the platform. Develop interfaces and workflows for data annotation used by internal teams and external community partners including task design, quality control, reviewer workflows, and progress tracking. Integrate with relevant evaluation frameworks, benchmark suites, and annotation tools, and help the team make sound build-vs-adopt decisions. Infrastructure and deployment Deploy and maintain platform UI/UX and backend services on Google Cloud Platform (GCP) and Amazon Web Services (AWS), including configuration, networking, and storage. Set up and maintain CI/CD pipelines, monitoring, logging, and alerting to ensure reliability, performance, and security across environments. Manage cloud resources cost-effectively, and contribute to architecture decisions on scalability, multi-region considerations, and data residency. Collaboration and delivery Work closely with the Project Manager, data engineers, researchers, and external partners to translate requirements into shippable features at a steady cadence. Participate in incident response, post-mortems, and continuous improvement of the platform's operations. Requirements: You should be a hands-on full stack engineer who is comfortable across frontend, backend, and cloud, and who actively uses AI tools to move faster and produce higher-quality work. The ideal candidate would have: A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. Around 2-3 years of full stack development experience, shipping production features in a modern web stack (e.g. TypeScript/React on the frontend; Python or Node.js on the backend; REST/GraphQL APIs; SQL and/or NoSQL data stores). Hands-on experience deploying applications on GCP and AWS, including containerised workloads, managed services, and CI/CD. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Familiarity with data platform concepts: pipelines, storage, metadata, catalogues, and access controls. Working knowledge of AI/ML evaluation, benchmarking, and/or data annotation workflows, and the tooling ecosystem around them (e.g. evaluation harnesses, annotation platforms). Strong communication skills and the ability to work with both technical and non-technical stakeholders across cultures and time zones. Bonus: experience with multimodal data systems (text, audio, image, video); contributions to open-source AI/data tooling; experience operating within Singapore public sector or research programmes. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Research_R00023946": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking an exceptional strategic leader to serve as Senior Assistant Director, Research within the College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS). Working closely with the Dean, Associate Dean (Research), and Director (Operations), you will play a pivotal role in shaping and delivering the College’s research strategy, translating vision into programmes, structures and support systems that enable academic excellence, interdisciplinary collaboration, and global visibility. As the senior professional lead for research, you will oversee the College’s research ecosystem, driving performance, strengthening research impact, and fostering connections across Schools, Research Centres, and external partners. You will lead and enhance research support operations, ensuring high-quality and efficient systems that enable both investigator-led and collaborative research to thrive, while also supporting the development of research centres, major initiatives, and competitive funding opportunities. Working in close partnership with the Director (Operations), you will help ensure alignment between research strategy, operations, and resource planning across the College, translating strategic priorities into coordinated execution. With a strong focus on data-informed decision-making, you will provide strategic insight on research performance and influence, while contributing to a research environment that supports diverse scholarship and intellectual leadership. This is a unique opportunity for a collaborative and forward-looking leader to shape the future of research in a globally ambitious and interdisciplinary environment. Relevant Experience: Bachelor’s degree from a recognized university. At least 10 years of relevant work experience in research administration especially in grant sourcing, grant administration (pre-grant award and post-grand award) in an academic and (or) research institutions.  At least 3 years of people management/ leadership experience. Skills & Competencies: Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholders across levels and cultures. Highly proficient in data analysis and reporting of grant information and research output, financial projection and budgeting. Able to handle confidential information sensitively. Strong working knowledge of MS Office applications. Knowledge of quantitative data analysis would be a plus. Proactive, resourceful, adaptable, hands-on, meticulous, organised and motivated to take on new challenges. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Dev-Ops_R00024968": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Dev Ops",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI.  AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. We're looking for an AI Engineer, Dev Ops to join the Data Platform team within AI Products at AISG. The role is to keep the Data Platform and the central data management infrastructure that sits beneath it running reliably, securely, and efficiently. You'll own the day-to-day operations of cloud infrastructure across GCP and AWS, the CI/CD and observability stack that the engineering team relies on, and the data pipelines, storage layers, and access controls that move data through the platform. You'll also bring strong AI fluency to the role: we expect the engineer to have knowledge in using AI tools deliberately for ops work such as incident triage, runbook generation, log analysis, IaC drafting, and automation and to help the team raise its operational bar by codifying those practices. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Duties & Responsibilities: Platform operations and reliability Own day-to-day operations of the Data Platform across GCP and AWS which includes environment health, capacity, performance, cost, security posture and define and uphold SLOs, alerting policies, and on-call practices. Lead incident response: triage, mitigate, run blameless post-mortems, and drive preventive actions through to completion. Central data management and data engineering ops Operate the central data management infrastructure which includes data pipelines, storage layers, catalogues, access control, and lineage tooling and partnering with engineering team on reliability, throughput, cost, and data quality. Implement and maintain backup, retention, disaster recovery, and data residency controls aligned to programme and funder requirements. Infrastructure, CI/CD, and automation Manage infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform) across GCP and AWS, and maintain CI/CD pipelines, container build/registry workflows, and deployment automation so teams can ship safely and frequently. Strengthen observability across the stack using logs, metrics, traces, dashboards and reduce toil by automating repetitive operational tasks. AI-assisted ops and continuous improvement Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) deliberately in your ops workflow for incident triage, log and metric analysis, runbook drafting, IaC generation and review, and on-call support and codify good patterns for the team. Build lightweight internal tooling that leverages AI to reduce operational load (e.g. summarising incidents, suggesting remediations, generating change reports), and contribute to security, compliance, and access reviews (secrets management, IAM hygiene, vulnerability patching, audit-readiness). Requirements: You should be a hands-on Dev Ops engineer who is comfortable operating cloud infrastructure end-to-end, who understands data engineering well enough to keep central data systems healthy, and who actively uses AI tools to make ops work faster and more reliable. The ideal candidate would have: A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. At least 3–5 years of Dev Ops, SRE, or platform engineering experience, with a track record of operating production systems at non-trivial scale. Hands-on experience operating workloads on both GCP and AWS including IaC (e.g. Terraform), containers and orchestration (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes), and managed services for compute, storage, and networking. Strong cybersecurity knowledge and hands-on practice including IAM and least-privilege design, secrets management, network security, vulnerability and patch management, audit logging, and security incident response. Familiarity with relevant standards and frameworks (e.g. ISO 27001, NIST, OWASP) and with data protection requirements (e.g. Singapore PDPA, GDPR where applicable) is expected. Working knowledge of data engineering and central data management including pipelines, storage formats, catalogues, access controls, and data quality/observability concepts. Strong fundamentals in CI/CD, observability (logs/metrics/traces), and incident response. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Solid scripting/programming skills (e.g. Python, Bash, Go) and comfort reading other people's code across the stack. Strong communication skills and the ability to work with both technical and non-technical stakeholders across cultures and time zones. Working knowledge of AI/ML evaluation, benchmarking, and/or data annotation workflows, and the tooling ecosystem around them (e.g. evaluation harnesses, annotation platforms). Bonus: experience with multimodal data systems (text, audio, image, video); contributions to open-source AI/data tooling; experience operating within Singapore public sector or research programmes. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Operations_R00024053": {
      "title": "Director, College Strategy & Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) invites applications for the position of Director, College Strategy & Operations.   This is one of the most senior professional leadership role within the College and offers a unique opportunity to shape the strategic and organisational effectiveness of one of NTU's largest and most diverse academic colleges. Reporting directly to the Dean and serving as a key member of the College Leadership Team, the Director, College Strategy & Operations, will lead the transformation and delivery of a broad portfolio encompassing academic administration, postgraduate education, research administration, communications, external relations, governance, finance, and operational services.   We are seeking a strategic, forward-thinking leader with a strong track record of driving organisational excellence, leading large and diverse teams, and partnering with senior stakeholders to deliver institutional impact. The successful candidate will play a critical role in advancing the College's strategic priorities, fostering innovation, strengthening operational capabilities, and enabling excellence in teaching, research, and engagement.   Role Impact and Opportunity: As Director, College Strategy & Operations, you will: Serve as a trusted strategic advisor and thought partner to the Dean and College Leadership Team, translating vision into actionable plans and measurable outcomes. Lead and inspire a high-performing team of senior administrators and matrix teams across Schools, Centres, and College functions, fostering a culture of collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement. Drive organisational transformation by redesigning processes, implementing scalable operating models, and strengthening service delivery across the College. Champion operational excellence, ensuring efficient, effective, and sustainable management of resources, systems, and services. Build strong partnerships across the University to advance interdisciplinary initiatives, institutional priorities, and shared operational goals. Lead complex strategic projects and change initiatives that enhance organisational effectiveness and position the College for future growth and success. Strengthen governance, risk management, and compliance frameworks while ensuring sound stewardship of financial and operational resources.   Key Responsibilities: Strategic Leadership and Institutional Planning Lead the planning, execution, and monitoring of College-wide strategic initiatives and transformation programmes. Partner with the Dean and senior leadership to develop and implement long-term strategies aligned with University priorities. Provide strategic advice on organisational design, policy development, governance, resource planning, and institutional effectiveness. Anticipate emerging challenges and opportunities, recommending innovative solutions to support the College's evolving needs.   Organisational Effectiveness and Service Excellence Oversee the delivery of a comprehensive portfolio of operational and academic services, including academic administration, postgraduate education, research administration, communications, external relations, and related operational functions. Review, redesign, and optimise business processes, service delivery models, and organisational structures to improve effectiveness and efficiency. Lead cross-functional initiatives to harmonise practices, improve stakeholder experience, and enhance operational performance across Schools and Centres. Promote data-informed decision-making and leverage technology to drive innovation and continuous improvement.   Governance, Risk and Compliance Ensure compliance with University policies, regulatory requirements, and governance standards. Strengthen risk management frameworks, internal controls, and operational resilience across the College. Provide expert guidance to College leadership on governance, policy implementation, and risk-related matters.   Financial and Operational Leadership Oversee the College's financial planning, budgeting, resource allocation, procurement, and operational management. Ensure prudent stewardship of financial and physical resources while aligning investments with strategic priorities. Identify opportunities to improve operational efficiency, optimise resource utilisation, and deliver sustainable outcomes.   Stakeholder Engagement and Partnership Building Develop and maintain strong relationships with academic leaders, professional staff, University offices, external partners, and other stakeholders. Facilitate collaboration across organisational boundaries to support strategic initiatives and operational excellence. Represent the College on University committees, taskforces, governance bodies, and institutional projects.   Leadership and Talent Development Lead, mentor, and develop a diverse team of professional staff leaders, fostering engagement, capability building, and succession planning. Build a high-performance culture that encourages innovation, accountability, collaboration, and continuous learning. Champion change management and organisational development initiatives that enhance team effectiveness and employee experience.   Qualifications and Experiences: Bachelor's degree from a recognised university. A postgraduate qualification in Management, Business Administration, Public Administration, Higher Education Leadership, or a related discipline will be advantageous. At least 15 years of progressive leadership experience in higher education, public sector organisations, or other large and complex institutions. Demonstrated success leading broad corporate services, operations, administration, or shared services functions at a senior level. Proven track record in organisational transformation, strategic planning, operational excellence, and change management. Strong experience leading diverse teams and influencing outcomes in complex matrix environments. Sound understanding of governance, compliance, risk management, financial stewardship, and institutional operations.   Key Competencies: Strategic leadership and organisational transformation. Executive stakeholder management and influencing skills. Strong commercial, operational, and financial acumen. Ability to lead through complexity, ambiguity, and change. Excellence in programme and project leadership. Analytical thinking, problem-solving, and sound judgment. Exceptional communication, relationship-building, and collaboration skills. Digital and data literacy with an appreciation of technology-enabled transformation.   Personal Attributes: Visionary yet pragmatic, with the ability to translate strategy into execution. Collaborative, inclusive, and relationship-oriented. Resilient, adaptable, and comfortable operating in a dynamic environment. Highly credible, professional, and trusted in handling complex and sensitive matters. Results-driven with a strong commitment to excellence and continuous improvement. Innovative and future-focused, with a passion for building organisational capability and impact.   Join us in shaping the future of one of Asia's leading universities and contribute to an environment that advances excellence in education, research, and societal impact. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Internship_R00024396": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Internship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager, Internship serves as both an individual contributor and deputizes for the Team Manager in the administration of designated internship programmes under the NTU Career & Attachment Office’s Internship team.  The Internship team facilitates internships for all NTU undergraduates to enhance their career readiness. It strives to improve internship participation and experiences for both students and host organisations by providing a unified platform for engagement, communication, and support.    The incumbent's role is to take responsibility towards the following areas of work: Programme Operations and Service Management Oversee the end-to-end management of internship programmes, including: Manage the internship operations and work processes. Develop strategies to increase internship opportunities and facilitate students’ participation and placement. Monitoring the internship progress and proactively identify and pre-emptively address potential issues that may arise to support successful effective placement and completion. Provide guidance and advice to students on internship matters. Addressing and resolving common internship-related issues raised by either students or host organisations, including supporting the team on complex case management issues. Account Management and Stakeholders Management Engage with the college and/or schools to collaborate in managing and optimizing internship placement and increase student’s career readiness for internship. Develop & maintain new and existing partners (host internship organisations) to support their requisition and increase their uptake of students in internship. Collaborate with the respective internal stakeholders to ensure the provision of support for students’ internship search journey for an internship placement. Team Management Support team members in performing their assigned roles and responsibilities. Support the Team Manager to ensure continuity of operations and overcome potential changes and challenges. Collaborate across intra-teams to drive optimal operational performance through strong partnerships and coordinated. Performance Reporting Supervision and Management Prepare and work with data and statistics for tracking and reporting. Analyse data and develop data insights for strategic planning. Adhoc Projects and Initiatives Lead and play a key role adhoc projects in areas of operations, data analysis and/or communications. Seek to adopt and use new technology/system to improve overall performance and outcome. Contributes in the solutioning for continuous improvement on workflows and stakeholder management. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree in any discipline from a recognised university. Candidates with a polytechnic diploma and extensive relevant work experience are also welcome to apply. Relevant work experience preferably in internship management, programme/project management, customer service management and process engineering. Successful track record in the managing of internships and cooperative education is highly advantageous. Minimum 5 years of work experience. Basic understanding about tertiary education landscape, career development and job market. Strong written and verbal communication skills. A collaborative team player who contributes actively to team success. Demonstrated passion for supporting youth in their career journeys. Comfortable with data, systems, managing structured processes and adhering to established policies and administrative frameworks. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Administrations_R00024217": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Administrations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs the Deputy Director, Administrations (DD) of MAE, the incumbent plays a vital role in supporting the Chair of MAE to provide leadership in various aspects of the school’s administrative initiatives including technical operations to drive organizational excellence to achieve the strategic goals and objectives of MAE. He/She is expected to lead in the development and implementation of organisational strategies, policies, standards, structures, systems and practices to achieve the overall goals of the School. In overseeing business operations, processes, initiatives and resources, the DD will provide integrated efficient and effective administrative services within the school, which is aligned with the School’s strategic goals and objectives and the University’s policies and processes. The DD will also provide foremost support to the School Management on strategizing and setting up of new initiatives, such as Capital Campaigns, Continuing Education, Community Engagement and External Relations. As a member of the School Management Committee, the DD will work closely with Chair and Associate Chairs in the formulation and review of policies to ensure the smooth and efficient operation of the administrative systems and processes throughout the School. This would also include active participation in the evolution of college-school relationship, organization reviews and partnering the central administrative offices in various administrative excellence projects in the university. Your key responsibilities include (but not limited to): Chart the strategic directions and roadmaps of MAE in alignment with University’s goals / new or changes to policies of the school by reviewing, recommending and driving process improvements to MAE’s structure, systems, policies and procedures with the aim of improving productivity, efficiency and effectiveness in operations. Work with the central administrative offices and College to align and coordinate workflow processes between functions and departments within NTU. Provide leadership and guidance to administrative / technical functions of the school and ensure all services are carried out smoothly and efficiently. Plan and review manpower allocation in order to achieve efficient use of resources and adequate support provided to faculty members, students and other stakeholders. Conduct and review performance appraisals for all direct reporting MSOs. Assist and advise Chair in MSO performance appraisal calibration exercise. Proactively develop, review and drive improvements in the School’s structure, systems, policies, processes and procedures with the aim of enhancing organizational effectiveness and creating an effective and conducive work environment. Oversee the overall financial operations of the school including financial reporting and analysis, budget planning and monitoring, as well as asset management, for financial effectiveness. Analyze, provide recommendations and proposals to redesign and reinvent current MAE space to further enhance and optimize usage for admin office, teaching and research facilities. Ensure lab and admin operations are in line with the Statutory requirement and University's safety standards. Ensure operations are in accordance with ISO45001/BizSAFE Star safety standard. Requirements: A recognized university degree, preferably from Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering. Prior experience in an institute of higher learning will be an added advantage. At least 15 years of working experience, with at least 8 years of experience in a senior managerial role with a proven track record. Knowledgeable about MAE industry trends, challenges, and opportunities. Strong verbal and written communication skills, with an excellent command of the English language, as the incumbent will represent MAE and engage with a wide range of stakeholders, including senior management and external partners or sponsors. Excellent collaborative, influencing and leadership skills. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to build a sense of community within the school. Strong in strategic thinking and has an analytical mind. Confident and proactive with demonstrated dynamism and resourcefulness in problem solving. Highly adaptable and self-motivated with lots of initiative to take on new challenges. Able to redesign processes to achieve better and more efficient work performance. Attention to details. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Communications_R00024051": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences (CoHASS) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is seeking a forward-thinking and experienced communications professional to lead its newly established College Communications team. As the Senior Assistant Director, Communications, you will play a pivotal role in shaping and executing integrated communications plans that align with NTU’s institutional goals and enhance the College’s visibility and engagement with stakeholders across its schools and research centres. This is an exciting opportunity to build a new function that will drive coherence, storytelling, and stakeholder alignment in a matrix academic environment. Job Responsibilities: Lead the development and implementation of a College-wide communications strategy, branding, and messaging framework that reflects CoHASS’s academic mission and evolving priorities. Drive alignment and coherence across school and centre communications teams through collaborative platforms, joint initiatives, and stakeholder engagement mechanisms. Develop and oversee campaigns that highlight emerging cross-college research themes, interdisciplinary initiatives, and newly established research centres to strengthen CoHASS’s positioning as a thought leader. Lead international communications efforts to build partnerships with global universities and academic networks, with the goal of improving CoHASS’s visibility and contributing to NTU’s standing in global reputation rankings (e.g., QS). Oversee the production of high-impact content that highlights CoHASS’s research, academic strengths, events, and societal contributions. Provide strategic advice to the Dean’s Office on media engagement, reputational matters, and institutional positioning, including responses during sensitive issues or crises. Establish editorial and visual standards for College publications, digital platforms, and campaigns to ensure consistency and brand integrity. Manage vendor relationships and communications budgets to deliver cost-effective, high-quality creative, media, and digital services. Monitor communications performance through analytics and reporting, applying data-driven insights to inform strategy and continuous improvement. Lead and mentor the College Communications team to foster capability development and a culture of collaboration, innovation, and excellence. Job Requirements: At least 10 years of relevant experience, with 3–5 years in a leadership or supervisory role, preferably in higher education, government, or public sector. Strong track record in strategic communications, campaign development, and stakeholder management. Excellent writing, storytelling, and editorial judgement for diverse internal and external audiences. Proven ability to lead through influence and collaboration, particularly in dynamic, matrixed environments. Experience in media relations, digital communications and brand management. Experience in managing vendors, projects, and communications-related budgets. Professional presence, sound judgment, and the ability to balance strategic vision with operational demands. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Platforms-Engineer--MLOps_R00023688": {
      "title": "Platforms Engineer, MLOps",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is Singapore's national programme in artificial intelligence, launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in AI. Hosted at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AI Singapore brings together Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to perform use-inspired research, grow knowledge, create tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. Since our inception in 2017, we have established a culture of respect, continuous learning, experimentation and curiosity, centred around innovation. The Platforms Engineering Group builds and operates the infrastructure and systems that enable AI practitioners across AISG's programmes to develop, train, and deploy machine learning models at scale. The group comprises four teams: Infrastructure Operations (InfraOps), Data Operations (DataOps), Machine Learning Operations (MLOps), and Experiences (EX). As a Platforms Engineer, MLOps in the Platforms Engineering Group, you will help build and operate modern infrastructure and systems to run large-scale machine learning and deep learning workloads. You will also design, develop, and maintain the AISG platform and tooling stack to enable project teams and partners to build products better and faster. You will serve as a domain expert to nurture AI talents and play a key part in driving the growth of Singapore's AI sector. In this role, you will: Design, build and maintain the platform and tooling stack that empowers AISG engineers to deliver their work effectively. Serve as the liaison between Platforms Engineering and AI project teams, ensuring they have the right ML tooling, infrastructure, and CI/CD processes in place. Develop and implement MLOps practices and processes, including CI/CD pipelines for ML models, automated testing, and model monitoring and versioning. Collaborate with data scientists, data engineers, and other stakeholders to ensure that ML solutions meet AISG's needs and are aligned with operational goals. Build and maintain production infrastructure to be resilient, secure, and high-performing. Implement infrastructure-as-code to automate systems configuration, provisioning, deployment, and monitoring. Document and investigate issues arising from our systems when they occur. Develop tools and software that improve and automate infrastructure. Propose and drive technical decisions to completion. Mentor AISG Apprentices and contribute to the MLOps curriculum for the AI Apprenticeship Programme (AIAP). To succeed in this role, you should have: Must-haves: At least 3 years of experience in an engineering or infrastructure position. Proficiency in at least one programming language such as Python, Go, Rust, or JavaScript/TypeScript (proficiency in Python and TypeScript is highly preferable). Proficiency in administering Linux systems. Proficiency in at least one automation tool (e.g., Ansible, Terraform, Bash). Familiarity with container and container orchestration technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes, Helm). Familiarity with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform. A systematic approach to development and engineering, including debugging, DevOps/MLOps practices, and agile development. Excellent communication skills, including the ability to express complex ideas clearly. Good-to-haves: Basic proficiency in machine learning concepts, including data analysis, predictive modelling, and model evaluation. Experience with ML experiment tracking tools (e.g., MLflow, Weights & Biases). Experience with infrastructure-as-code and GitOps workflows. Familiarity with observability tools (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana). Experience mentoring or training others in a technical capacity. Candidates with relevant professional experience or graduates of the AI Singapore AI Apprenticeship Programme (AIAP) are welcome to apply. We offer a dynamic environment at the forefront of Singapore's national AI efforts, opportunities to work with cutting-edge AI/ML infrastructure, and a culture that values continuous learning and professional development. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Computer-Science---Artificial-Intelligence---Data-Science---Electrical-Engineering-_R00025627": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Computer Science / Artificial Intelligence / Data Science / Electrical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking a highly motivated Research Engineer to develop next-generation Green AI technologies that improve the efficiency, sustainability, and scalability of artificial intelligence systems. The successful candidate will contribute to cutting-edge research and engineering in large language models (LLMs), efficient machine learning, and AI systems, translating research innovations into practical solutions for sustainable computing and real-world applications. This role offers opportunities to work at the intersection of AI research, software engineering, and sustainability, collaborating with multidisciplinary teams across academia and industry. Job Description: Support the design, development, and implementation novel machine learning and large language model (LLM) algorithms for Green AI applications. Support the research of efficient AI techniques, including model optimization, parameter-efficient fine-tuning, self-training, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), prompt engineering, and efficient inference. Conduct experiments, benchmark algorithms, and analyze performance using rigorous scientific methodologies. Contribute to publications in leading AI conferences and journals. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to translate research outcomes into deployable technologies. Keep abreast of the latest developments in Green AI, foundation models, code intelligence, and AI systems. Job Requirements: Bachelor's in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related discipline. Strong background in machine learning, deep learning, and large language models. Experience working with large-scale datasets and distributed model training. Strong programming skills in Python. Experience with modern deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities. Good written and verbal communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Artificial-Intelligence---Computer-Science---Machine-Learning---Natural-Language-Processing---Information-Retrieval---Data-Science-_R00025626": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Artificial Intelligence / Computer Science / Machine Learning / Natural Language Processing / Information Retrieval / Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking an outstanding Research Scientist to join our Green AI research team. You will conduct cutting-edge research on efficient and sustainable artificial intelligence technologies, advancing the development of foundation models that are both high-performing and environmentally responsible. You will work closely with interdisciplinary researchers and engineers to develop novel AI algorithms, publish in top-tier venues, and translate research innovations into real-world sustainability solutions. Job Description: Conduct research in Green AI, with a focus on improving the efficiency, scalability, and sustainability of large AI models. Design and develop novel algorithms for efficient training, inference, retrieval, and deployment of large language models (LLMs) and multimodal foundation models. Develop AI technologies that contribute to sustainability applications. Publish research findings in leading AI conferences and journals Collaborate with internal and external research partners to deliver innovative Green AI solutions. Mentor junior researchers and contribute to research proposal development and strategic initiatives. Job Requirements: Ph.D. in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Machine Learning, Natural Language Processing, Information Retrieval, Data Science, or a closely related discipline. Strong research background in Large Language Models (LLMs), Green AI and efficient machine learning, LLM-based Agents, Distributed AI systems and scalable model serving, etc Strong publication records in reputable journals/conferences Strong programming skills in Python and modern AI frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, Hugging Face). Ability to work independently and collaborate across multidisciplinary teams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Computer-Science---Artificial-Intelligence---Machine-Learning---Natural-Language-Processing-_R00025624": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Computer Science / Artificial Intelligence / Machine Learning / Natural Language Processing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking an outstanding Research Scientist – Green AI to conduct cutting-edge research on efficient, sustainable, and scalable artificial intelligence technologies. The successful candidate will develop novel algorithms and system-level innovations that significantly improve the energy efficiency, computational efficiency, and deployment of large AI models while maintaining high model performance. The ideal candidate has a strong research background in large language models (LLMs), efficient deep learning, natural language processing, model optimization, and AI systems, with a proven publication record at top-tier AI conferences and journals. Job Description: Conduct research on Green AI technologies, including efficient training and inference of foundation models and large language models (LLMs). Develop scalable AI systems that enable practical deployment of foundation models on resource-constrained computing platforms. Develop AI technologies that contribute to sustainability applications. Publish research findings in leading AI conferences and journals Collaborate with internal and external research partners to deliver innovative Green AI solutions. Mentor junior researchers and contribute to research proposal development and strategic initiatives. Job Requirements: PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Natural Language Processing, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in Large Language Models (LLMs), Natural Language Processing, Efficient Deep Learning, AI Model Optimization, etc. Research experience in Green AI, sustainable computing, or energy-efficient machine learning. Excellent publication records in reputable journals/conferences Strong programming skills in Python and modern AI frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, Hugging Face). Ability to work independently and collaborate across multidisciplinary teams. Strong publication record in top-tier AI conferences and/or journals. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Graduate-Career-Development_R00025622": {
      "title": "Manager, Graduate Career Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Business School competes with top business schools worldwide to attract graduate students from diverse backgrounds to join its graduate programmes. The Graduate Studies Career Development (“GSCD”) team is an instrumental part of NBS’s Graduate Studies division, and aims to provide world-class career services to post-graduate students to develop them into career-savvy professionals and in helping NBS’s post-grad students find the ideal job after graduation. The position holder will be part of the GSCD team. The key purpose of the role is to provide world-class career services to NBS’s graduate students, manage employer relationships in key sectors, and source for suitable positions for NBS’s graduate students. The position holder is responsible for employer engagement with companies in Singapore and international markets, to bring jobs for 900+ students. Responsibilities: GSCD strategy & implementation: Engage with the GSCD team in providing multi-faceted career workshops, networking events, company presentations, etc. Identify and support implementation of strategic initiatives for GSCD to lift the level of career services for all GS participants. Support business development and employer engagement to secure full-time jobs and internship opportunities in Singapore and globally: Identify global career opportunities for graduate students, and develop strategies to engage key hiring organisations in identified markets. Develop tiering and engagement of companies in key markets, with a view to securing full-time jobs, internships and industry projects for students. Identify and build strong partnerships with recruiters and hiring managers globally, particularly in key hiring sectors. Work closely with internal NTU/NBS stakeholders such as Associate Deans, Academic Directors, Program and Management Office, NTU Career Office, Alumni Affairs Offices, Development Offices to source for full-time jobs and internship placements from existing and new industry contacts. Maintain a deep understanding of market factors relative to employer organisations in key markets. Cultivate relationships with alumni in key markets, particularly in identified hiring sectors, to help build and provide pipeline of full-time jobs and internships for students. Provide timely and comprehensive administrative support necessary in securing and matching students to jobs and internships Thought Leader for all international roles: Be the key thought partner to GSCD Career Leads in areas of understanding employers and employment trends. Support NBS endeavours in key markets e.g., sourcing for industry projects and managing industry visits. Provide student counselling to give insights into sectors/ countries: Develop a calendar of recruitment activities to ensure pipeline of jobs are availed to all post-graduate students. Place students in their desired roles (full-time jobs and internships). Monitor student performance and growth during internships and propose win-win solutions for students and industry partners. Coach and counsel students interested in relevant sectors / geographies to ensure readiness for career-related interactions with employers. All other tasks assigned to the role. Requirements: Degree from a top-tier global business school is required. An MBA or a Master's degree will be an advantage. Good knowledge of practices and hiring mandates of companies across different sectors in Singapore and in key international markets. At least 7 years' work experience, possessing strong and deep networks with hiring companies. Proven track record of business development including internal and external successful collaborative and leadership experience. Work experience in international markets will be a distinct advantage. Outstanding ability to manage senior stakeholders, and interact effectively with people of varying levels and backgrounds. Excellent interpersonal skills and presentation skills, including the ability to deliver high impact presentations to senior executives. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Takes initiative and is a good team player. Meticulous with a good eye for details. Able to work under tight deadlines. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--External-Relations_R00025045": {
      "title": "Manager, External Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe incumbent will drive the School’s external relations and stakeholder engagement strategies, and manage events and initiatives that strengthen partnerships and enhance the School’s visibility as a nexus for innovation, research, and business education locally and internationally. Job Responsibilities: External Relations Engagement and Partnership Development Promote and elevate awareness of College of Business/Nanyang Business School (NBS) Spearhead and execute appropriate strategies to advance the College’s external relations agenda Cultivate partnerships for the College for a wide spectrum of initiatives for teaching and research. Identify new opportunities for partnerships, collaborations and engagements. Formulate action plans and establish relations with industry. Drive integrated and coordinated external relations programmes and activities across units within the College. Support networking at relevant industry/research forums and business meetings. Act as the primary administrative contact for external engagements and corporate partners. Event Management and Operations Develop and implement comprehensive event planning for partner events and collaborative initiatives with industry. Lead and coordinate with internal and external stakeholders to effectively plan and execute partner events and engagement activities Select suitable event venues and negotiate contracts Coordinate with NTU Events Office for events. Manage and host visits to the College by external parties, visitors and guests. Manage the College’s external relations budget which includes budget planning and accounts management Develop and manage event budgets Track expenses, reconcile invoices, and provide regular financial updates to stakeholders. Collaborate with the marketing team to create promotional materials and strategies for events. Conduct post-event evaluations to gather feedback and assess the success of each event, and prepare relevant reports for management where applicable. Streamline work processes and workflows Support to leadership and strategy development Lead consultation with the College Management to strategise, strengthen and establish industry partnerships and engagements.  Support the formulation of the College’s external relations strategies and implementation plans. Support College management in building relationships with local, regional, and international partners. Requirements: Degree from a recognized university At least 8 years of relevant work experience in events management and partnership engagement Able to connect with people at all levels, establish and maintain a network of relationships and partnerships Proficient in IT, experienced in managing in-person, virtual and hybrid events; and engaging online communities Resourceful and driven, with the ability to think strategically, creatively and analytically Excellent presentation and communication skills Able to influence and engage internal and external stakeholders Team player and must be able to work within tight deadlines Highly relationship-oriented while balancing stakeholder needs with institutional priorities We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Student-Administration_R00025400": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences is seeking a dedicated and proactive Senior Executive to join the Undergraduate Academic Office. Reporting to the Manager, you will play a pivotal role in supporting the school’s academic team, ensuring the smooth delivery of academic services, and enhancing students’ learning journeys. Job Description Admission Oversee administration of student programmes (e.g. internships, attachments, exchange, integrated programme, and special initiatives). Coordinate student mobility opportunities and liaise with internal/external stakeholders. Manage student applications and required documentation. Prepare official correspondence for students. Handle general enquiries via phone, email, and in person. Academic Services Administer course registration and related academic processes. Manage online learning platforms and course evaluations. Process applications for academic support and financial assistance. Provide secretariat support for reviews and quality assurance. Manage instructor hiring for courses. Deliver general academic support services (e.g., scheduling, waiver handling). Examinations Support planning and logistics for assessments. Administer exam-related documentation and formatting. Assist with the administration of exam scripts checking. Events Organize student-related events and trips, including logistics and budgeting. Manage procurement requests for event needs. Prepare and disseminate event communications. Coordinate venue bookings and related arrangements. Other Administrative Duties Manage role-based email accounts. Prepare official letters and certificates. Administer students/faculty awards. Support ad hoc administrative tasks as assigned. Requirements Bachelor’s degree with at least 1 year of relevant experience or Diploma with 3-4 years of relevant experience. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and relevant software. Strong organizational and project management skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong problem-solving and analytical abilities. Strong ability to communicate (verbal and written) effectively with students, faculty and team members. Familiarity with higher education policies and regulations is a plus. Responsible and reliable. Proactive and positive attitude towards work tasks. Possesses characteristics of being assertive and meticulous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Research-Development_R00024733": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Research Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences in NTU invites applications for the position of Senior Assistant Manager for Chair’s Office Central Administration. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in strengthening School’s research funding portfolio by supporting funding strategy development, preparing large competitive research grant proposals, and assisting faculty in overseeing research grant expenditure. The appointee will work closely with Principal Investigators (PIs) to identify strategic funding opportunities, coordinate multidisciplinary inputs, and facilitate high-quality submissions to national, industry and international funding programmes. Key Responsibilities Develop and implement strategic funding initiatives to expand School’s research portfolio and align proposals with national and international research priorities. Identify and evaluate funding opportunities from national agencies, industry partners and international programmes, advising PIs on the alignment with NTU / School strategy and funding criteria. Drive and coordinate the preparation of large competitive research grant proposals, including drafting technical narratives, consolidating multidisciplinary inputs, and ensuring alignment with funding agency requirements. Manage the end-to-end proposal development process, including timeline coordination, budget planning and compliance checks. Collaborate with PIs to refine research concepts, articulate project significance and innovation, and position proposals to maximize funding potential. Provide advisory support on grant budgeting during proposal development and coordinate with relevant offices on post-award financial matters. Support faculty in post-award activities, including progress reporting, grant variations and administrative coordination where required. Support the implementation of School’s research data governance practices as School’s Research Data Governance Manager, advise faculty on compliance with institutional and funder requirements. Requirements Advanced Degree (Master’s or PhD) in Science or Engineering, or a related discipline. Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in research development, grant writing, funding strategy or research management, preferably in a university, research institute, or R&D environment. Familiarity with Singapore research funding landscape (e.g., NRF, MOE, A*STAR) is advantageous. Experience in preparing large competitive research grant proposals or coordinating multi-investigator submissions. Excellent technical writing, analytical, organisational, and stakeholder engagement skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive---Senior-Executive--Teaching-Lab_R00025231": {
      "title": "Executive / Senior Executive, Teaching Lab",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science at Nanyang Technological University, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance excellence in biological and biomedical sciences. Our research spans diverse and impactful areas including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative disorders, telomere biology, and genome function. SBS is home to a vibrant, international community of scientific leaders, researchers, and professionals dedicated to innovation, discovery, and education. We are seeking a motivated and proactive Executive / Senior Executive (Teaching Laboratory) to support the planning, preparation, and smooth operation of undergraduate teaching laboratories. Job Description Teaching Laboratory Operations Support the planning, preparation, and delivery of undergraduate laboratory practical sessions. Liaise with course coordinators on practical requirements, schedules, and laboratory safety matters. Prepare laboratory reagents, consumables, specimens, and equipment required for practical sessions. Set up, calibrate, and relocate laboratory equipment as required for teaching activities. Brief Teaching Assistants on laboratory procedures, experimental protocols, and safety requirements. Provide safety and technical support to undergraduate students during laboratory practical. Conduct trial runs of new and existing practical protocols, troubleshoot technical issues, and ensure experiments are reproducible and effective. Procurement and Inventory Management Assist in the preparation and monitoring of teaching laboratory budgets. Procure laboratory consumables, chemicals, equipment, and other teaching-related materials. Maintain accurate procurement records and documentation according to University’s policies. Maintain inventory records for assets, consumables, chemicals, and teaching materials. Support inter-department activities on asset sighting. Laboratory and Equipment Management Ensure laboratories are well-maintained, organised, and operational. Perform routine cleaning, maintenance, and functional checks of laboratory equipment before and after semester periods. Coordinate equipment servicing, repairs, and preventive maintenance. Monitor stock levels of laboratory consumables and chemicals and replenish supplies as required. Report laboratory infrastructure defects and coordinate rectification with relevant stakeholders. Laboratory Safety and Compliance Maintain proper storage, handling, and documentation of chemicals and biological materials in compliance with University and Workplace Safety & Health (WSH) requirements. Ensure timely updating of chemical inventories. Oversee and handle safe disposal of laboratory waste. Reinforce laboratory safety practices and procedures during practical sessions. Participate in emergency preparedness activities, including first aid, chemical spill response, and fire drills. Prepare and review Risk Assessments for laboratory activities and experimental protocols. Ensure compliance with University and School’s safety policies and updates for audit preparation. School Support Provide administrative support for teaching laboratory operations. Assist in school events, outreach activities, and other duties as assigned. Requirements Diploma in Life Sciences or a related discipline. Entry-level candidates are welcome to apply. Candidates with relevant experience in teaching or research laboratory, preferably within an Institution of Higher Learning, will have an advantage. Basic knowledge of laboratory operations, reagent preparation, and laboratory housekeeping. Familiarity with laboratory techniques in molecular biology, biochemistry, cell biology, and mammalian and/or insect cell culture is preferred. Proficiency in the operation of common laboratory equipment, such as biological safety cabinets, centrifuges, compound microscopes, and pH meters. Good understanding of laboratory safety practices and chemical handling procedures. Good organisational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Able to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team environment. Adaptable and able to respond effectively to changing operational requirements. Demonstrates initiative, attention to detail, and a strong sense of responsibility and accountability. Able to identify operational issues, troubleshoot effectively, and implement appropriate solutions. Experience in data recording, analysis, and presentation would be an advantage. The School of Biological Sciences seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Research---Partnership_R00024732": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Research & Partnership",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a proactive and detail-oriented Senior Executive, Research & Partnerships to join the School’s growing central administration team. This role provides key administrative, operational and engagement support, contributing directly to the School’s mission of advancing research excellence and strengthening global partnerships. You will work closely with faculty members, research staff and institutional stakeholders to ensure smooth delivery and effective implementation of research-related central administrative functions and initiatives. Key Responsibilities:              Research Manpower Administration Serve as Superuser for RISE as Unit Manpower Officer (UMO), supporting end-to-end research hiring, contract renewals and transfers for Division Principal Investigators (PIs). Advise PIs on RISE processes and provide hands-on troubleshooting support. Handle researcher manpower cost matters, including tracking and analysis. Work with PIs to monitor funding utilisation and flag potential shortfalls. Coordinate with HR and Finance to ensure accurate WBS setup and correct cost charging. Research Events & Engagement Support the administration and coordination of research events such as symposiums, colloquia, conferences, and workshops. Prepare materials, compile information, and coordinate event communications to deliver impactful and well‑run engagements. Contribute to continuous improvement of administration processes. Perform any other duties as assigned to support the team’s and school’s objectives. Executive & Administrative Support Provide administrative and operational support for school research activities and related initiatives to facilitate efficient coordination. Requirements: Degree or Diploma from a recognised university, with at least 1 year of relevant experience, preferably in a university or research environment. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite & relevant software. Strong organisational skills with attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to manage deadlines and perform reliably under pressure. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with service‑oriented mindset. Team player with initiative, adaptability and positive attitude. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Chief-Information-Officer---IT-Director_R00025388": {
      "title": "Deputy Chief Information Officer / IT Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs the Deputy Chief Information Officer (CIO) / IT Director, you will serve as a key executive partner to the CIO, providing operational leadership and strategic guidance across the university's central technology division. You will oversee multi-disciplinary IT teams, drive large-scale digital transformation initiatives, and ensure that IT infrastructure, services, and governance align seamlessly with NTU's academic, research, and administrative goals. Key Responsibilities: Strategic IT Leadership: Partner the CIO in defining and executing the university’s multi-year digital and AI roadmap, ensuring technology initiatives actively support research excellence, education, and administrative operations. End-to-End Operational Excellence: Enterprise IT operations—including IT infrastructure, enterprise applications, cybersecurity, cloud architecture, and end-user support services—maintaining high reliability and performance. Lead operational transformation through AI-driven operations to increase efficiency and user satisfaction. Digital Transformation & Enterprise Architecture: Lead complex enterprise-wide transformation programs, modernizing legacy systems, optimizing workflows, and integrating cloud-native solutions. Exploit AI-assisted coding tools, automated testing, and CI/CD pipelines in enterprise application development workflows. Institutional AI & Data Hub Adoption: Champion the adoption of the university-wide Data Hubs and Enterprise AI Platform across administrative units and academic schools, bridging strategic vision with operational reality. Governance, Risk & Compliance: Ensure robust enterprise cybersecurity, data privacy, business continuity, and regulatory compliance frameworks across all digital platforms and university assets. Support the CIO in formulating enterprise data policies and institutional AI frameworks. Resource & Financial Stewardship: Manage multi-million-dollar capital and operational IT budgets, establishing rigorous financial modelling, ROI tracking, and procurement governance. People Leadership & Capability: Mentor, empower, and develop a high-performing team of IT directors, managers, and technical specialists, fostering a culture of continuous learning, agility, and service excellence. Vendor & Stakeholder Engagement: Manage strategic vendor relationships, evaluate major IT investments, and maintain strong, collaborative relationships with academic deans, administrative leaders, and governance committees. Job Requirements: Must-Have Qualifications & Skills: Education: A Master’s or Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, Business Information Systems, or a related field. Experience: At least 20 years of extensive progressive leadership experience in complex, large scale IT environments, with at least 5 years in a senior IT management role. Proven Executive Leadership: Demonstrated track record of leading large, multi-disciplinary IT teams and managing multi-million dollar technology budgets and enterprise portfolios. Complex Operational Management: Proven track record of managing end-to-end IT operations within large, decentralized, or matrixed organization, ensuring high operational resiliency, strict service-level agreements, and seamless business continuity. Transformation Expertise: Proven success delivering enterprise-grade digital transformations, cloud migrations, modernizing legacy enterprise systems, and scaling AI Ops or AI workflows in complex enterprise environments. Cybersecurity & Governance: Good understanding of enterprise risk management, cloud and AI governance frameworks, and modern cybersecurity principles. Communication & Influence: Superior stakeholder management, communication and negotiation skills, with a proven ability to present complex technical strategy clearly to executive stakeholders. Good-To-Have Skills: Executive industry certifications (e.g., ITIL, CISSP, TOGAF, PMP), in cloud platforms (AWS/Azure/GCP Architect), AI Operations, or data management (e.g., TOGAF, CISM, CDMP). Leadership experience within higher education, public sector, or research-intensive organizations. Hands-on familiarity with enterprise AI applications, AI platforms integration or big data virtualization tools. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Sales-Manager--Nanyang-Executive-Centre--Hospitality-_R00025366": {
      "title": "Sales Manager, Nanyang Executive Centre (Hospitality)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. NEC features 150 refurbished guestrooms and refreshed event spaces that aims to offer a premier venue for high-level conferences, workshops, executive programmes, and industry engagements.    We are seeking a results-driven Sales Manager to drive room sales and event bookings, develop new business opportunities, and build strong client relationships to maximise NEC's revenue and occupancy. Key Responsibilities Business Development Establish and execute sales plan aligned with NEC’s revenue targets and objectives. Prioritise NTU's educational and institutional needs. Identify and pursue affiliated business opportunities, such as training programmes and events, to optimize NEC’s revenue. Develop strategies to drive room sales and maximise facility utilisation. Build and maintain strong relationships with internal NTU stakeholders and external clients to develop business leads. Establish and build rapport with all business partners. Handle contract negotiations and client inquiries professionally. Achieve monthly and annual targets for room revenue, occupancy, and average rates. Sales Administration Maintain accurate records and prepare monthly sales reports. Analyse sales performance and provide recommendations to improve results. Contribute insights to annual business planning and pricing strategies. Conduct market analysis and stay up to date on the industry trends and competitor activities. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Sales & Marketing, Hotel Management or relevant discipline. Diploma holders with extensive experience may be considered. Minimum 2 years of experience in Sales, preferably in hospitality industry. Proven track record of achieving sales targets. Capable of dealing skilfully with new environment, new or difficult situations and overcoming challenges creatively. Adaptability and agility. Strong relationship-building/ management and negotiation skills. Team player.  Excellent communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Digital-Platforms---AI-Transformation_R00025343": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Digital Platforms & AI Transformation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe role presents an exciting opportunity to shape NTU’s digital future by driving digital transformation and AI initiatives that enhance the university’s operations and campus experience. Reporting to the Director of Enterprise IT, the job holder will provide strategic vision, governance, and technical leadership across core enterprise platforms, including NTU’s websites, mobile applications, chatbots, and IT solutions and services. Acting as a key bridge between central IT leadership and decentralised business units, the job holder will lead the delivery of innovative AI and digital solutions that optimise operations, enable organisational growth, and transform the campus living experience. The role will also ensure that NTU’s technology landscape remains secure, sustainable, scalable, and aligned with long-term enterprise architecture and strategic priorities. Responsibilities: Engage stakeholders across multiple domain areas to understand their needs, define and implement technology solutions and enhancements; and assist them in planning and managing budget for their digital transformation initiatives. Stay abreast of emerging technologies, formulate multi-year strategic technology roadmaps and present business cases to executive steering committees and senior stakeholders. Lead the planning and implementation of technology solutions, overseeing the overall design, development, integration, and deployment of multiple systems/platforms. Drive change management and digital adoption strategies to ensure smooth transitions and minimal operational friction for end-users. Oversee the digital platforms and services, ensuring adherence to best practices, security standards, and performance optimisation. Manage procurement processes, contract renewals, and operational expenditure budgets to maximise technology return on investment. Oversee external system integrators, technology partners, and software vendors to ensure full SLA compliance, fiscal discipline, and project delivery velocity. Maintain rigorous IT audit readiness, ensuring zero high or medium risk findings across all managed digital ecosystems. Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering or related discipline; or Bachelor's degree in Business Administration or Marketing, coupled with relevant technical experience. Minimum 15 years of experience in IT-related industries with at least 10 years of progressive leadership experience in enterprise IT management, digital transformation or platform engineering within large and complex organisation. Proven track record in orchestrating multi-site web enterprise consolidations and decentralised operational models. Possesses strong technical understanding of cloud architectures, enterprise content management systems, GenAI chatbot workflows, mobile app development, and API integrations. Ability to communicate complex technical concepts through storytelling capabilities to a diverse group of users, including senior stakeholders. Excellent stakeholder management, interpersonal, and managerial skills, with strong change management capabilities. Ability to multi-task, work under pressure and deliver results in a timely manner. Tenacity to take on challenges and handle ambiguity; and manage diverse views and seek consensus through open discussion. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Chemical-Store_R00025619": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Chemical Store",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking for a dynamic individual to assist the Store manager with daily operations and safety of the Chemical Store at the School of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB). The Senior Executive supports the Chemical Store Assistant Manager in managing the high-volume needs of students, research teams, and faculty at the School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, and Biotechnology (CCEB). Responsibilities include handling bulk purchases of chemicals and consumables, forecasting, data analysis, negotiating with suppliers, managing deliveries, and overseeing the online inventory system. The role also involves monitoring stock availability, managing monthly invoicing and intra-billings for research teams, and coordinating chemical waste disposal. Responsibilities Safety compliance Adhere to and promote safety protocols and procedures to ensure and uphold safety compliance. Implement proper handling and storage practices for hazardous materials. Assist the safety committee in maintaining a safe and organized work environment. Ensure storage of chemicals and solvents is kept within the allowed maximum capacity approved by statutory authorities. To work closely with the Safety committee and safety officer on the safety regulations for the Chemical Store at both Nanyang Link and Nanyang Drive. To assist the safety officer with the safety regulations and enforcement for flammable hazardous substances, bio and chemical waste regulations, SCDF and SPF-regulated chemicals such as explosive precursors, etc. Ensure proper documentation of controlled chemicals. Conducting regular safety inspections on chemical storage facility, arranging repairs or maintenance, and providing training to staff/intern student on safe handling procedures. Daily Store Operations Accept supplier deliveries and process delivery orders for the research groups and Chemical Store, inspecting and checking that actual item received are in satisfactory condition. To execute product and material handling and movement within the chemical store in compliance with established policies, procedures and standards. Organize received items within the receiving area or designated storage locations. Ensure that items are stored safely and securely to prevent damage or loss. Processing of internal purchases by research groups. Perform periodic cycle counts on goods. Sourcing quotations and negotiating with suppliers to enable competitive bulk purchasing, achieving cost savings and financial efficiency for the Chemical Store. Forecasting and monitoring inventory availability in the Chemical Store to ensure continuous supplies to meet the demands of the undergraduate teaching labs and research labs activities. Regular stock availability updates in the in-house CBC Store Online Inventory System. Communicate, negotiate and provide feedback to vendors on any issues pertaining to the above. Assisting in any other ad-hoc duties assigned by the reporting manager. Waste Management Proper waste management in accordance with current government regulations and safety requirements from collection to disposal. Submission of NEA E-tracking documentation for waste collection. Ensure all waste disposal by research groups adheres to safety requirements as set down by the relevant statutory authorities, including NEA and SCDF. Work closely with internal Safety Team in waste management, ad-hoc disposal of chemicals. Finance On-time generation and processing of monthly invoices from the inventory system to research groups. Maintain an up-to-date record of invoices, accounts and special grants. Liaising with all stakeholders including inter / intra schools and departments to ensure all transactions are processed and credited into the school operating budget. Process billing and intrabilling for Chemical Store supplies, laboratory equipment, shared facilities teaching laboratories and other chargeable services. Maintain detailed records of all financial transactions involving chemical store. Requirements Possess at least a Diploma/Degree in Logistics/Warehousing/Chemistry/Engineering/science-related discipline. 1-3 years prior experience in the educational/logistics/warehouse with a science background is preferred. Possess knowledge of basic chemistry/biology/engineering, safety regulations, waste management, basic finance. Knowledge in SAP System is an added advantage. Ability to use data and apply robust analytics to analyse cost, impact, risk and benefits. Knowledge of chemical safety regulations and best practices. Effective negotiation skills and resourceful in finding competitive pricing for the consumables/ chemicals/solvents for stakeholders. Resourceful and independent. Ability to work effectively under pressure. Proactive and a positive attitude towards work tasks. Conscientious team player. The School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Transition---Integration_R00025087": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Transition & Integration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. SASD works collaboratively with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey for all students. This position sits with the Student Affairs Office (SAO), which is one of the functions within SASD. The SAO plays a key role in co-creating a meaningful and enriching student life experience through student-led activities, leadership development initiatives, residential life programmed, integration efforts, community engagement initiatives, arts and sports. The Assistant Manager designs and delivers Transition & Integration initiatives. Specifically, Transition initiatives aim to enable students to transit effectively into and through their university journey, while Integration initiatives aim to enable a positive international student experience and meaningful social integration between local and international students. Through these efforts, the role promotes intercultural understanding, a strong sense of belonging, and student success across the community. Key Responsibilities: International Student Experience and Integration Manage the design, implementation, and continuous improvement of targeted initiatives that support international students’ transition across academic, social, and cultural domains. Develop university-wide Integration initiatives that promotes meaningful social mixing between local and international students, including buddy programmes, intercultural dialogues, and community projects. Partner with schools, student organisations, residential halls, and central offices to embed integration agenda into the broader student experience. Develop metrics and evaluation frameworks to assess Integration outcomes for continuous improvement.  Transition Journey Mapping and Programmes Support the planning, execution, and continuous improvement of centralised Transition programmes with the aim of delivering a robust first year transition experience for freshmen. Manage the development of a Transition journey map as a guide for students to transit effectively in their first semester, including ensuring its dissemination and active adoption by students. Scholars Engagement Collaborate with various internal stakeholders to ensure that the wellbeing of S&T and ASEAN scholars, both academic and co-curricular, are taken care of throughout their undergraduate years.  Prepare university-wide reporting to MOE with regards to Integration matters and scholar status. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in any discipline. At least 3 - 5 years of relevant experience which involves considerable interaction with students; experience in the tertiary education sector will be advantageous. Experience in youth development and/or IHL orientation programmes and integration of international students. Project management skills in coordinating large-scale projects. Proven track record in stakeholder management.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Examination_R00024107": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Examination",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. It is one of the largest EEE schools in the world, with more than 120 faculty members and an enrolment of more than 4,000, of which about 2,000 are graduate students. We invite applications for the position of Senior Assistant Manager at EEE, NTU. The role is to manage the examination management process and serve as one of the key points of contact for examination matters to ensure excellence in delivery and execution while maintaining high level of integrity and confidentiality.  Key Responsibilities: Contributing as a key staff in the Curriculum and Examination Team on undergraduate assessment, examination and award matters. Managing examination mark processing and administer Mark Entry System (MES), including preparing reports for School Board of Examiners (BOE) meeting. Acting as a key liaison between the team and key stakeholders to drive critical processes such as BOE, exam paper preparation, student results appeal and special student arrangements for assessment. Coordinating the nomination and award of academic medals and book prizes in accordance with academic policy and guidelines. Qualifications:  Bachelor's degree in a relevant field. Minimum of 5 years of experience in educational administration or program management. Strong interpersonal, communication, and analytical skills. Ability to work collaboratively in a diverse team environment. Previous experience in data analytics and workflow improvement is advantageous. Familiarity with higher education policies and accreditation standards is beneficial. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Computer-Science-Computer-Engineering-Electrical-Engineering-_R00025616": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Computer Science/Computer Engineering/Electrical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: The Research Assistant will conduct research on cellular network security, with a particular focus on 4G/5G mobile networks and core network systems. The candidate will analyse cellular network architectures, protocols, and implementations to identify potential security vulnerabilities. The candidate will design and conduct experiments to validate identified security issues and evaluate their practical impact. The role may also involve developing experimental testbeds, prototypes, and security analysis tools. The candidate will contribute to research publications, technical reports, presentations, and other project deliverables, and work closely with the PI and research team. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. Good knowledge of computer networks and network security. Good programming and experimental research skills. Familiarity with cellular networks, including 4G/5G systems and core network architectures. Experience in network protocol analysis, system security, or security research. Demonstrated research experience in cellular network security, as evidenced by publications in high-quality venues. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director---Deputy-Director--IT-Operations_R00024423": {
      "title": "Head, IT Operations (College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is a research-intensive university ranked among the world’s top institutions. The Centre for IT Services (CITS) enables the University’s teaching, learning, and research through secure, scalable, and reliable IT infrastructure, platforms, and services. We are seeking a Head, IT Operations to provide senior College-level IT leadership for the College of Engineering (CoE) . The role is accountable for shaping and driving IT strategy, service delivery, and operational outcomes across multiple Schools, ensuring alignment with University direction and CITS operating models, standards, and governance frameworks. This is a senior leadership role operating in a complex, multi-stakeholder environment , with responsibility for balancing College priorities, enterprise IT direction, and resource constraints, while delivering consistent and scalable IT outcomes across the College. Key Responsibilities Define and drive the College IT roadmap and operating model, aligned to University priorities and CITS strategies. Lead and prioritise IT demand across multiple Schools, making trade-offs to optimise outcomes at College level. Oversee and be accountable for delivery of IT programmes and initiatives at scale, ensuring alignment with enterprise architecture, security, and governance requirements. Own IT service delivery performance across the College, ensuring reliability, consistency, and quality of end-user experience. Drive standardisation of platforms, systems, and processes, reducing fragmentation and improving scalability across Schools. Establish and enforce governance frameworks for demand, delivery, and service performance across Schools. Lead and develop a federated organisation of School IT teams, establishing clear operating structures, accountability, and capability across the College. Act as the senior IT interface between the College and CITS, engaging Deans and senior stakeholders to align priorities and drive outcomes. Act as a strategic business enabler for the College, proactively engaging stakeholders to anticipate emerging needs, identify operational pain points, and translate business requirements into scalable, enterprise-aligned IT solutions. Drive operational excellence through service optimisation, process standardisation, continuous improvement, and measurable business outcomes. Influence stakeholder behaviour and decision-making, ensuring alignment with enterprise IT strategies and operating models. Optimise utilisation of IT resources and investments, ensuring value realisation and alignment with strategic priorities. Requirements Must-have Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Engineering, or a related discipline. At least 15 years of relevant IT experience, including leadership roles in infrastructure, operations, or service delivery at scale. Experience leading IT across complex, multi-entity environments (e.g. multiple departments, business units, or institutions). Strong understanding of enterprise IT operations, service delivery, and governance frameworks. Proven track record in driving large-scale IT initiatives and programmes across multiple stakeholder groups. Strong stakeholder management and influencing skills, with experience engaging senior leadership and decision-makers. Demonstrated business partnering capabilities with a strong business-enabler and operational-excellence mindset. Good-to-have Experience in higher education or public sector environments. Familiarity with enterprise architecture, cybersecurity, and data governance practices. Experience operating within centralised or federated IT organisational models. Why Join NTU Opportunity to lead IT at scale across one of the University’s largest and most complex academic Colleges. Direct exposure to enterprise-wide IT strategy, operating models, and digital transformation initiatives. Work in a collaborative environment with strong emphasis on governance, innovation, and service excellence. Play a key role in shaping and delivering IT capabilities that support education, research, and institutional priorities. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00024025": {
      "title": "Executive (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applicants to join the Finance Department as an Executive . Responsibilities You will be part of the team which handles payments and other student-related financial matters for the institute. Your responsibilities will include: Administering Financial Aid schemes, e.g. PSEA, CPF, Mendaki, Tuition Fee loan, Study loan, scholarships and bursaries. Checking that payment transactions (e.g. supplier invoices, student claims) have appropriate certification and approvals before processing payments. Handling the financial accounts, preparing GST, audit schedules and financial statements for NIE Student Union. Responding timely to enquiries pertaining to student matters. Assisting in the design, implementation and review of financial processes, policies and guidelines for continuous improvements, through streamlining and automation. Handling ad hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma in Accountancy or its equivalent. 2 or 3 years of working experience in accounting. Organized and meticulous in handling numbers and data. A team player with a positive working attitude and is willing to learn and adapt. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Excel pivot tables and formulas. Experience in SAP would be an added advantage. Able to adhere to timelines. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 1 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior---Cyber-Security-Governance-Specialist_R00025173": {
      "title": "Senior / Cyber Assurance & AI Security Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU's Centre for IT Services (CITS) manages the University's campus-wide IT infrastructure and delivers enterprise IT, learning systems and digital services that support NTU's education, research and administrative functions. As part of CITS, the Cyber Security team is responsible for strengthening the University's cybersecurity posture through Cyber Security Governance, Cyber Security Operations and Cyber Incident Management. We are seeking an experienced Senior / Cyber Assurance & AI Security Specialist to join our Cyber Security Governance team. In this role, you will play a key part in defining and governing enterprise cybersecurity frameworks, leading technical cyber assurance initiatives, and enhancing the University's resilience against evolving cyber threats. Key Responsibilities Lead technical cyber assurance initiatives by defining and governing the scope, schedules, methodologies and standards for internal and external web, mobile, network and API penetration testing. Conduct security reviews and audits of enterprise security infrastructure, maintain security documentation, and oversee complex access control administration and security-related issues. Design risk assessment frameworks and security guardrails for applications developed using AI-assisted software development platforms and establish testing methodologies to identify vulnerabilities in AI-generated code. Review and approve secure system architectures, ensuring security principles are embedded into system designs and technology implementations. Evaluate authentication solutions, network security configurations, security software updates and technical implementations to safeguard enterprise systems. Plan, manage and deliver cybersecurity risk assurance projects, ensuring project objectives, timelines, resources and budgets are effectively managed. Partner with Schools and stakeholders across the University to identify cybersecurity risks, provide expert technical consultation, and recommend appropriate risk mitigation strategies. Build trusted relationships with stakeholders by providing cybersecurity advisory services, supporting key business and technology initiatives, and promoting cybersecurity governance across the University. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Cyber Security or a related discipline. Professional certification in OSCP or CREST is required. Additional certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CISM or GIAC will be an advantage. At least 8 years of relevant IT experience, including at least 2 years in Cyber Security Engineering, Cyber Assurance, Penetration Testing or IT Risk and Governance. Strong knowledge of security issues in code written by AI agents (e.g., OWASP Top 10 for LLMs). Good understanding of cybersecurity frameworks and methodologies such as NIST Incident Handling Guidelines, Cyber Kill Chain, MITRE ATT&CK framework. Proficient in penetration testing methodologies, secure software development lifecycle (SSDLC), and security assessment of code repositories such as GitHub and GitLab. Demonstrated ability to perform cyber risk assessments, analyse complex technical environments, and develop effective security solutions. Proven project management capabilities with experience leading cybersecurity initiatives from planning through implementation. Excellent communication, stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, with the ability to provide expert technical consultation and influence cybersecurity outcomes across technical and business stakeholders. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Evaluation-_R00024988": {
      "title": "AI Engineer (Evaluation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is Singapore's national programme in artificial intelligence, launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in AI. Hosted at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AI Singapore brings together Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to perform use-inspired research, grow knowledge, create tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. Since our inception in 2017, we have established a culture of respect, continuous learning, experimentation and curiosity, centred around innovation. The candidate will join a team of AI scientists, apprentices, data and software engineers. With the team, he or she will be responsible for building evaluations that test the limits of AI models especially in terms of its multilingual, multicultural and multimodal capabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Develop and maintain evaluation frameworks and pipelines to measure the capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs). Keep up to date and experiment with the latest research in multilingual, multicultural, and multimodal LLM evaluations such as the LLM-as-a-Judge paradigm. Work with partners to collect, translate and verify evaluation datasets. Perform the necessary data preparation and analysis, AI modelling, coding, testing, validation and deployment to ensure reliable and scalable AI solutions. Collaborate with cross-functional teams within AI Products to design and resolve issues. Maintain code repository and documentation standards. Contribute to community engagement activities such as sharings via technical session meet-ups and article write-ups, and participating in discussion forums. Requirements: Graduate from a degree program in computer science, AI, data science or related fields (or equivalent practical experience). Deep understanding of LLM evaluation experimental design and the advantages/limitations of various LLM evaluation methods. Experience in LLM inference frameworks such as vLLM and AI/Deep Learning frameworks such as PyTorch. Writing production level code in Python and using version control systems such as Git. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Independent learner that is capable of reading and understanding research papers. Fluent in English and one other Southeast Asian language for the purposes of understanding how to build quality evaluations from a multilingual and multicultural perspective. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager--Industry-and-Research-Collaborations_R00024746": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, Industry and Research Collaborations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering (CoE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore invites applications for the position of Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, Industry and Research Collaborations. CoE is NTU’s largest and most research‑intensive college, comprising five internationally recognised engineering schools and sitting at the strategic core of the University’s academic mission. Working within CoE offers the opportunity to operate at College level, supporting impactful research collaborations that span disciplines, Schools, and external partners, within a collaborative and mission‑driven environment committed to research excellence and institutional impact. Role Overview As part of the College of Engineering’s Research & Partnerships Team, you will support the end‑to‑end administration of industry and research agreements that enable impactful research collaborations at NTU. Working under the guidance of senior team members, you will contribute to the accurate, timely and compliant processing of research agreements and post‑award activities. This role offers hands‑on exposure to how research collaborations are structured, reviewed, executed and supported within a leading research‑intensive university environment. Job Responsibilities: Your responsibilities will focus on agreement management execution and coordination, including: Supporting the administration of the full lifecycle of industry and research agreements (e.g. Non-Disclosure Agreements, Materials Transfer Agreements, Project Agreements, Research Collaboration Agreements, MoUs and Variation Agreements), from initiation to execution and closure Assisting with the preparation of agreement drafts using approved institutional templates and ensuring supporting documentation is complete and accurate Coordinating internal review and approval workflows with relevant offices such as Legal & Secretary Office, NTUitive and Finance, under established processes Coordinating closely across Schools, central offices, faculty, and external stakeholders to facilitate timely review, negotiation, resolution of issues, and execution of agreements Supporting the setup and maintenance of project records and post‑award information in the University’s research management systems Assisting with agreement variations, extensions and project closure processes in accordance with approved terms and guidance Maintaining tracking records and reports to monitor agreement status and pending actions Contributing to the upkeep of standard operating procedures, checklists and process documentation related to agreement handling Any other ad-hoc initiatives and assignments undertaken by the Office Requirements: Bachelor's degree in any discipline. Degree in engineering, business, law, public policy, administration or related fields will be advantageous. Entry-level candidates with a strong interest in research administration, contracts or higher‑education research environments are welcome to apply Prior exposure to research administration, agreements, grants, contracts or compliance‑related work will be an advantage but is not required Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and follow structured processes Good written and verbal communication skills, with attention to clarity, accuracy and professionalism Attention to detail and willingness to learn institutional policies, systems and workflows IT‑savvy, with working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Administrative-Support_R00025611": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking an experienced administrative professional to take on a senior role providing strategic and operational support across procurement and grants administration for the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) and the Asian School of the Environment (ASE). As EOS and ASE research activities are closely integrated, this role extends support across both units to ensure smooth coordination, financial stewardship, and policy compliance. In this role, you will act as the primary subject-matter expert and advisor on procurement and grants administration, independently managing end-to-end workflows and advising Principal Investigators and researchers on funding compliance. You will take ownership of grant financial management — including budget monitoring, virement submissions, and grant claims for key research projects such as the seismic project — while also managing the engagement of external professionals for fieldwork and the design of costing and charging frameworks. Working closely with internal and external stakeholders, you will provide senior-level administrative and operational support for research-related activities and organisational initiatives within EOS & ASE. Job Responsibilities Serve as the primary subject-matter expert and first point of contact for all procurement matters across ASE and EOS, providing strategic advisory and independently managing end-to-end Ariba procurement processes including SVP, ITQ, ITT, Online Payment, Advance Payment, and Cash Advance, in compliance with University guidelines. Advise on Advance Payment requests and Cash Advance applications under exceptional circumstances, proactively guiding requestors toward more efficient and compliant alternatives. Provide senior-level procurement advisory and administrative support to ASE/EOS stakeholders, including procurement of research equipment, consumables, software and services, ensuring alignment with Delegation of Authority (DOA) and grant funding terms. Monitor grant budgets and expenditures, prepare financial reports, and process grant virements, ensuring expenditure remains aligned with approved budgets and funding agency guidelines. Manage the submission of grant claims, including but not limited for the seismic project, ensuring timely, accurate, and compliant reporting to funding agencies. Keep abreast of university procurement and grant policy updates, and proactively communicate implications to internal stakeholders. Provide strategic guidance to research clusters (e.g. Centre of Geohazards Operation (CGO), Remote Sensing (RS), seismic project on fieldwork-related matters, including the engagement of external professionals through Contract for Service (CFS) or Research Consultancy Agreement (RCA). Lead and oversee logistics for open houses and workshops across researcher clusters, including but not limited to CGO and RS. Drive the design and development of costing and charging frameworks, including CGO, EOS-RS, and other applicable units, by establishing standardised cost models for fieldwork activities, projects, and related services.Conduct benchmarking and market analysis of pricing and costing models used by industry partners, companies, and peer universities to enhance and optimise charging strategies. Perform any other duties as assigned to support the team’s and school/research center’s objectives. Job Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Business Management, Finance, or a related field. At least 4-6 years of relevant experience in administrative, procurement, or grants/financial administration, preferably in a university or research environment, with demonstrated ability to operate independently at a senior level. Strong understanding of procurement processes and grant/financial administration, with extensive working knowledge of ARIBA/SAP. Proven experience in grant management, including budget monitoring, virement processing, and grant claims submission. Strong proficiency in Microsoft applications, including Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with strong stakeholder management, advisory capability, and a service-oriented mindset. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities independently, exercising sound judgement on both operational and strategic matters. Meticulous, with strong analytical, problem-solving, and organisational skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Assessment-Operations-and-Partnerships_R00025606": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Assessment Operations and Partnerships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Academic Services (OAS) plays a vital role in enabling student success across the entire academic journey by implementing and administering academic policies established by the University's academic bodies. OAS delivers comprehensive academic services from matriculation to graduation, empowering students, upholding excellence, and partnering stakeholders to provide a seamless, student-centred experience while maintaining the highest standards of integrity, governance, and professionalism. Within OAS, the Examinations team is responsible for the planning, administration, and continuous enhancement of the University's assessment ecosystem. The team ensures that assessments are conducted securely, fairly, and efficiently while safeguarding academic standards and upholding the principles of academic integrity. As the University expands its digital assessment capabilities, the team also plays a key role in supporting digital transformation initiatives and driving the adoption of technology-enabled assessment practices. Key Responsibilities: Assessment Operations: Plan and administer centralised and decentralised assessments in compliance with University assessment regulations, policies, and procedures. This includes the delivery of large-scale face-to-face centralised assessments, assessment scheduling, venue allocation, seating arrangements, logistics coordination, invigilator deployment, assessment material management, and the administration of assessment-related student cases such as medical certificate submissions and special consideration requests. Digital Assessment Operations & Adoption: Oversee the operations, readiness, and utilisation of the University's digital assessment halls, ensuring seamless assessment delivery, efficient turnaround between bookings, and consistently high facility utilisation. Partner with Schools and faculty members to support the implementation and adoption of digital assessment practices by providing operational guidance, assessment planning support, and expertise on assessment technologies and processes. Assessment Partnerships, Engagement & Service Delivery: Build trusted partnerships with stakeholders to coordinate examination operations, address operational issues and identify emerging requirements. Design and deliver engagement, communications, and outreach initiatives that strengthen stakeholder understanding, readiness, and confidence in digital assessment. Governance, Risk Management & Continuous Improvement: Support academic integrity initiatives and drive process improvements, automation, and digital transformation efforts to improve efficiency, service quality, and user experience. Resource Management & Projects: Manage procurement and vendor coordination activities and analyse operational data and performance indicators to support informed decision-making. Participate in and support cross-functional projects and institutional initiatives related to digital transformation, stakeholder engagement, and service excellence initiatives that advance OAS' strategic and operational objectives. Support administrative and governance processes to support organisational planning, financial stewardship, compliance, and operational effectiveness within OAS. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Information Systems, Data Analytics, Education, or a related field. Experience in examination administration, assessment operations, digital assessments, event management, communications, customer experience, service design or large-scale operational environments. Experience supporting high-stakes, mission-critical operations involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and tight timelines will be highly advantageous. At least 3 years of relevant working experience, preferably in academic services within a higher education institution.  Demonstrated ability to manage multiple stakeholders and coordinate complex operational activities under tight timelines. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organisational skills with the ability to interpret data and recommend process improvements. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and data management tools. Meticulous, proactive, and able to work effectively in a fast-paced environment with competing priorities. Results oriented and accountable, focused on achieving outcomes that meet business needs and stakeholder expectations. Proactive and improvement minded, taking initiative to identify issues early and drive continuous enhancement of processes and systems. Adaptable, organised, and resilient, able to manage multiple tasks, stay calm under pressure, and approach problems in a structured and analytical way. Demonstrates high integrity, professionalism, and a commitment to upholding governance, service excellence, and academic integrity.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Engagement-Manager--AISG_R00025607": {
      "title": "Engagement Manager, AISG",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. ​This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. We are looking for an Engagement Manager to join the Data Platform team within AI Products at AISG. The team runs a data platform which supports a global effort to collect multimodal language and cultural data — cataloguing the datasets that help AI understand the world’s underrepresented languages, and bringing together linguists, researchers, contributors, and partner organisations across Asia and beyond. This is a self-directed role focused on growing and sustaining that community and on helping to grow the data that powers the platform. Your primary mandate is outreach, growth, and data acquisition — attracting new users, contributors, and traffic to the platform, encouraging and facilitating data contributions, and keeping the community engaged and invested over time. Working towards goals and guardrails agreed with the team, you will exercise your own judgement on where and how to reach each community, whether online, in person, or through partners. You will draw on the team’s partner ecosystem as a primary means of extending reach and shape the community’s direction with a considerable degree of autonomy. This role is offered on a part-time basis and is suitable for candidates seeking flexible working arrangements. Duties and Responsibilities: Outreach and growth Attract new users, contributors, and traffic to the platform — identifying and reaching researchers, linguists, developers, and underrepresented-language communities in the venues where they already gather, from research networks and developer platforms to regional AI groups and social channels. Conceive and deliver outreach campaigns and initiatives that raise awareness of the platform, its datasets, and the opportunities to contribute. Data acquisition and contributor facilitation Serve as the first point of contact for prospective data contributors — welcoming interest and connecting willing contributors with the team. Act as the bridge between prospective contributors and the team — clarifying what contributing involves and coordinating a smooth handover for the technical process. Community engagement and retention Sustain an active, returning community — encouraging repeat contributions, supporting established contributors, and cultivating first-time visitors into lasting participants. Foster constructive conversation and support across online forums and communities and respond thoughtfully to the needs of contributors and users. Partnerships and ecosystem Cultivate relationships with the team’s research and community partners across the region and work through them to extend the platform’s reach into their audiences. Represent the platform with credibility before academic, research and community stakeholders, both online and at events where appropriate. Content, communication and measurement Develop and distribute compelling content — post, updates and materials — that stimulate participation and advocate the platform’s mission and value. Monitor engagement and growth signals — new users, contributions, platform usage, referral traffic and community activity — and refine your approach considering what works. Qualifications: You should be an accomplished community builder who works with autonomy, moves fluidly between online, in-person, and partner-led channels, and represents a research-focused, mission-driven platform with credibility before technical and non-technical audiences alike. Our ideal candidate would have: A degree in communications, marketing, public relations, the social sciences, or a related field — or equivalent professional experience. Minimum 7 years of experience in community engagement, community management, developer relations, or outreach, with a demonstrable record of growing and sustaining an active community. Proven strength in stakeholder and partnership management — establishing and sustaining productive relationships with external partners, community organisations, and other stakeholders. The ability to engage prospective data contributors — understanding their needs at a high level, explaining what contributing involves, and coordinating a smooth handover to the team. Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build relationships and engage audiences across cultures and time zones. The judgement to select and run the right mix of channels — online (forums, social, newsletters), in person (meetups, events), and through partners — and to plan and deliver events, programmes, and campaigns. A sound grasp of engagement metrics, with the ability to track growth and activity and adapt your approach accordingly. A high degree of self-direction: resourceful, proactive, and able to set your own rhythm and exercise sound judgement amid ambiguity with light oversight. Bonus: experience within a technology, research, or academic ecosystem; familiarity with underrepresented-language, open-data, or open-source communities; relevant regional-language ability; or experience operating within Singapore public sector or research programmes. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Analyst-Programmer--Digital-Solutions-Department---NIE-_R00025587-1": {
      "title": "Analyst Programmer (Digital Solutions Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . The National Institute of Education (NIE) invites suitable candidates to join the Division of Academic Computing & Information Services (ACIS) as an Analyst Programmer (25-month contract). Key Responsibilities Design, develop, test, and implement application systems based on user requirements and project timelines. Find opportunities to design and implement AI-driven features that enhance and personalize the student digital experience. Explore and propose innovative ways to modernize student information systems by leveraging the latest technology stacks and AI-assisted development methodologies. Maintain and enhance existing in-house applications to ensure optimal performance and user experience. Collaborate with cross-functional IT teams for system deployment and integration. Ensure high standards of code quality, test coverage, and participate actively in code reviews. Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade applications as needed. Independently manage IT projects from initiation to completion. Ensure compliance with regards to Data Governance, IT Audit, and Security policies and standards. Any other ad hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A University degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering or a related discipline.   Minimum of 3 years of relevant experience in software development and IT project management. Sound understanding of student and examination-related business processes. Familiarity with the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) and Agile methodologies. Proficiency in .Net programming. Experience in GitHub Copilot or similar tools. Experience in system integration via APIs and database layers. Experience with relational databases and ORM frameworks (e.g. Hibernate). Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to adapt quickly to new technologies. Effective team player with a proactive attitude and the ability to meet tight deadlines. Possessing the following skillsets will give the applicant an added advantage: Jira for Project Management AI-Driven Automation Data Analytics tools such as Power BI Low-code development platforms (e.g. Power Apps) Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 9 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Accreditation-_R00025604-1": {
      "title": "Manager (Accreditation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. The Accreditation and Data Management Office (ADMO) at Nanyang Business School oversees AACSB and EQUIS accreditation, supports teaching and learning, and manages data for institutional and external reporting. We are seeking a Manager (Accreditations) to undertake the following responsibilities: Manage Assurance of Learning (AoL) reporting workflows for academic programmes and work with faculty in implementing e-assessment tools. Review course outlines to ensure alignment with Outcomes-Based Teaching and Learning (OBTL) frameworks and institutional learning goals. Manage the execution of AACSB and EQUIS accreditation processes, including coordination of timelines, milestones, deliverables and visit logistics Contribute to the development of accreditation reports and supporting documentation. Oversee data governance operations, ensuring audit readiness and compliance with institutional standards. Drive continuous improvement across key operational processes. Requirements: Must-have: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university Minimum 8 years working experience with at least 3 years of relevant experience in accreditation, quality assurance, compliance, or related areas Strong project management and coordination skills Strong written and verbal communication skills including the ability to frame narratives and develop clear, concise, and well‑structured reports. Ability to analyse and interpret large datasets to draw meaningful insights Meticulous, with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Ability to engage, influence, and build effective working relationships across a wide range of stakeholders, including academic, administrative, and external partners. Strong IT skills, including proficiency in MS Office and use of AI tools to enhance productivity and work processes. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team, with a flexible approach and the capacity to learn and adapt to new areas quickly. Resourceful and creative in problem-solving. Good to have: Experience with academic accreditation frameworks (e.g. AACSB, EQUIS or similar) Familiarity with curriculum and assessment design Experience working in a higher education environment We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/ICT-Support-Engineer--Service-Management-Department---NIE-_R00025588": {
      "title": "ICT Support Engineer (Service Management Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore is Singapore’s national teacher training institute. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education , and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . The Academic Computing and Information Services (ACIS) division oversees NIE’s ICT needs. We invite applications for the position of ICT Support Engineer to support our efforts in transforming the education landscape in Singapore. Job Summary The ICT Support Engineer supports the IT Service Operations Manager in delivering ICT support to NIE stakeholders. The role diagnoses and resolves hardware, software and service issues, identifies root causes, and escalates to external vendors when required. The engineer also uses AI-driven diagnostic tools and ITSM platforms to improve resolution efficiency. The role maintains knowledge of ICT infrastructure and works with service desk staff, technical teams, end users, and project managers to ensure smooth operations and a positive user experience. Job Responsibilities 1. End-User Support and Service Delivery Act as the first point of contact for IT and AV issues and service requests, including monitoring and escalating AI service desk chatbot inquiries. Analyse and troubleshoot incidents and perform corrective and preventive maintenance. Provide IT/AV support for events, meetings, video conferences and lessons, including after-hours support when required. Deliver IT/AV services that meet user needs and satisfaction. Track task completion and ensure adherence to service level agreements (SLAs). 2. IT/AV Systems Maintenance and Operations Perform preventive and corrective maintenance of IT/AV systems in lecture theatres, classrooms, tutorial rooms, labs and meeting rooms. Assist in the evaluation, procurement and deployment of IT/AV equipment and solutions, including AI-enhanced hardware such as intelligent auto-framing cameras and AI noise-cancellation audio systems. Participate in IT/AV projects and initiatives to improve service efficiency and user experience. 3. Documentation and Knowledge Management Document incident resolutions, best practices and standard procedures in the internal Knowledge Base. Maintain technical documentation for IT/AV configurations and deployment guides, using generative AI tools where applicable. 4. Asset and Inventory Management Maintain IT/AV asset records and update asset databases. Conduct physical asset verification and report findings for audit reconciliation and compliance. 5. Security and Compliance Collaborate with the cybersecurity team to enhance endpoint security using AI-driven threat detection and endpoint response (EDR) systems. Ensure compliance with NIE IT security policies, relevant regulatory requirements and acceptable AI usage policies. 6. Business Continuity and Process Improvement Participate in IT Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery (BCDR) programmes. Contribute to service improvement through innovation, feedback and cross-functional projects. Identify opportunities to automate routine support tasks using AI, scripts and robotic process automation (RPA). Requirements 1. Educational Background and Certifications A Polytechnic Diploma in Information & Communication Technology (ICT) or a related field, with strong knowledge of technology and systems supporting IT and AV infrastructure. ITIL Foundation certification and experience with ITIL best practices are preferred. 2. Experience and Technical Skills At least 2 years of experience in ICT support, with a proven track record in customer service and technical support. Familiarity with Generative AI assistants such as Microsoft Copilot and ChatGPT for troubleshooting, scripting and workflow automation. Solid knowledge of computer troubleshooting, networking, applications and operating systems, including Microsoft Windows, Microsoft Office, Macintosh OS and mobile devices. Knowledge of networking protocols and common software tools. Familiarity with audio/video equipment, including AV troubleshooting and setup for events, lessons and meetings. Ability to diagnose and resolve technical issues independently with minimal supervision. 3. Key Personal Attributes Proactive, self-motivated and resilient, with a strong sense of urgency and ability to work under pressure. Result-oriented and responsible, with the ability to meet deadlines and deliver work to a high standard. Collaborative team player with creativity, resourcefulness and strong problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills. 4. Innovation and Continuous Improvement Strong interest in new technologies, particularly AI and automation tools, to improve productivity and service efficiency. Ability to stay current with relevant technology trends and tools. Ability to collaborate with peers and technical teams across the organisation to resolve issues and implement solutions. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 8 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist---Fellow--Fibre-Optics-_R00025599": {
      "title": "Research Scientist / Fellow (Fibre Optics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a highly motivated and skilled Research Scientist /Research Fellow to join our cutting-edge fiber optics team. The role will focus on developing next-generation high-power fiber beam combiners. The successful candidate will be responsible for developing advanced modeling and simulation (M&S) tools and the establishment of comprehensive diagnostic and characterization tools. This position requires a strong background in optical physics and hands-on experience in both computational modeling and experimental characterization of optical components. Key Responsibilities: 1. Modelling & Simulation (M&S) Tool Development Develop and customize simulation templates using Beam Propagation Method (BPM) software (e.g., BeamProp) to model optical behavior in fiber combiners, focusing on critical areas like taper transitions and fusion zones. Utilize Finite Element Method (FEM) software (e.g., COMSOL) to perform thermal analysis, modeling heat distribution and dissipation in high-power operational conditions. Define theoretical performance benchmarks for optical characteristics such as insertion loss and beam quality by integrating real-world data, such as empirical beam profiles from high-power laser diodes. Validate simulation models by calibrating them against established literature and comparing them with empirical data from fabricated components. Collaborate with the fabrication team to diagnose sub-optimal performance by identifying discrepancies between theoretical and experimental results. 2. Diagnostic Characterisation & Validation Design, build, and maintain dedicated experimental setups for the characterization of high-power fiber optic components. Conduct precise measurements of key performance metrics, including insertion loss, beam quality (M²), and thermal performance under high-power loads (> 200 W/port). Develop and standardize testing procedures to ensure consistent and reliable data collection across multiple samples. Implement diagnostic methods, such as fiber index profiling and microscopic visual inspection, to analyze post-processing effects on signal fibers. Provide crucial feedback to the M&S and fabrication teams by supplying accurate characterization data, creating a closed-loop development cycle. Job Requirements: PhD qualification degree in Physics, Optical Engineering, Electrical Engineering or related field At least 4 years of relevant experiences / technical hands-on experience in an optics lab, including the design and construction of test benches and characterization of optical components (e.g., measuring insertion loss, beam quality). Familiarity with optical and thermal simulation software, and high-power laser systems Solid theoretical understanding of fiber optics, laser physics, and heat transfer. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in BPM and COMSOL is highly essential. Competent in analytical skills with the ability to bridge the gap between theoretical models and experimental results. Excellent problem-solving abilities and a methodical, data-driven approach to research. Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Community-Executive--AISG_R00025602": {
      "title": "Community Executive, AISG",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. ​This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Key Responsibilities: Event planning and promotion Plan and execute regular and ad-hoc online and offline community events (e.g., webinars, AMAs, meetups, workshops). Support industry and community-building activities stemming from, but not limited to, AIxTech, AIAP, AIAP (Industry), LADP, and AIIP programmes. Community engagement and support Act as the primary point of contact for community members on online community platforms. Respond to user inquiries, comments, and messages in a timely and professional manner, ensuring high satisfaction. Monitor brand mentions and sentiment to identify potential crises, escalating them according to guidelines. Coordinate with a roster of technical staff to facilitate community support. Work with internal stakeholders to align community strategies with broader business goals. Manage member onboarding and nurture relationships to improve retention. Build followership of online community platforms and social media pages. Content creation and management Adapt content from internal/external resources and coordinate content writers to develop insightful, engaging narratives. Constantly test and optimise existing content and calibrate best practices for engagement and lead generation. Manage community comms and editorial calendar that supports the acquisition and retention of community members. Insights and reporting Gather member feedback and identify key trends to report to internal teams - industry development, marketing, programme and curriculum development. Monitor and analyse community metrics to evaluate engagement levels and ROI, with emphasis on consistent growth and engagement. Requirements: Degree with at least 3 years of experience in DevRel, community operations, corporate communications, hospitality management (e.g., co-working spaces or guest relations), or digital communications role in an agency. Platform-savvy. Knowledge of media platforms and community engagement tools, as well as marketing automation and digital communication tools. Proficient with Microsoft Office and Google Workspace tools. Provide portfolio, website, links to communities managed, or other samples of work. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Assistant-Manager--Outreach--Admissions---Scholarships_R00024972": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, Outreach, Admissions & Scholarships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering at NTU Singapore is seeking a Senior Executive/Assistant Manager for the Outreach, Admissions and Scholarships team. The individual will be part of the College’s Undergraduate Outreach, Admissions and Scholarship team. Reporting to the Lead, Outreach, Admissions & Scholarships, the candidate will play a key role in developing, planning, and leading the implementation of outreach and engagement strategies targeted at prospective undergraduates, with the aim of achieving the College’s outreach and undergraduate recruitment objectives. The role involves planning and executing outreach events and activities, as well as driving post-event reporting and analysis to measure impact, extract insights, and shape data-driven strategies that enhance the effectiveness of future outreach, ensuring the College consistently meets its goals. The individual will also support the College’s outreach, admissions and scholarship process. This position serves as the liaison between the College and the Engineering Schools to align and harmonise outreach strategies, implementation plans, and efforts. Key responsibilities include (but not limited to): Develop, plan, and lead outreach and engagement strategies for prospective undergraduates to achieve the College’s recruitment objectives. Liaise with Engineering Schools to align and harmonise outreach strategies and implementation plans. Plan and execute outreach events and activities, ensuring high-quality delivery and engagement. Conduct post-event analysis to measure impact, extract insights, and drive data-informed improvements. Organise and coordinate whole of College effort for the annual EASE Tea Party. Lead and organise engagement events for Returning NS men. Support the College’s admissions and scholarship process. Build and maintain strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders, including faculty, alumni, schools, and industry partners, to support and enhance the College’s outreach and recruitment objectives. Able to work independently while collaborating effectively across teams. Any other ad-hoc initiatives and assignments undertaken by the Office. Requirements: Recognised university degree in any discipline. At least 1 to 3 years of work experience, preferably in Outreach, Student Recruitment, Student Engagement in the higher education industry. Entry-level candidates are welcome to apply. Experience in event execution and management. Resourceful team player with good interpersonal, stakeholder engagement and coordination skills. Highly motivated and meticulous individual with strong analytic and problem-solving skills and keen eye for details. Excellent organisational, time management and planning skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and tasks in an efficient, effective, and timely manner. Excellent oral and written communication and presentation skills. IT savvy and proficient in MS Office applications. Knowledge of the higher education market in Singapore and Asia-Pacific region is advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate-Research-Fellow--Plant-Biology-and-Bioinformatics-_R00023895": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Plant Biology and Bioinformatics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) at NTU Singapore, in collaboration with Wageningen University & Research (WUR), is part of Singapore Indoor Farming System (SingFarm)—a CREATE-NRF programme focused on building a sustainable, data-driven food production model with strong industry relevance to contribute Singapore’s ambition in achieving 20 per cent local production of its fiber (vegetables, mushrooms etc.) by 2035. The candidate would be working in a multinational team at the forefront of Singapore’s agricultural innovation and food security. The position of Research Associate will focus on developing advanced high throughput phenotyping tools for assessing the performance of genotypes under abiotic and biotic stresses that occur in indoor farming systems for vegetables (e.g. too high humidity, too high VPD, low light intensity, low or high water potential in the root environment, salinity, bacterial and fungal diseases) and to optimize performance (yields of economic product in indoor cultivation) through breeding. Key Responsibilities:  Develop high throughput phenotyping protocols (e.g. for testing nutrient deficiency responses, transpiration response, biomass accumulation, quality of produce) using automated determination of transpiration, imaging (side view imaging with RGB), 3D-imaging, chlorophyll fluorescence imaging. Develop analysis tools for the large data stream of HTP phenotyping for assessment of abiotic and biotic stress tolerance (e.g. determine extent of damage to a disease or functional response to humidity); also involving use of AI in image analysis and predictive modelling Develop prediction models that can predict product yield and quality from HTP data either for cultivation management or for predicting which genotypes have best performance in practice Set up test of products (e.g. CRISPR or EMS mutants) from other work packages (e.g. with modified Engineer molecular pathways for enhanced crop performance Document results and contribute to reports, publications, and presentations Job Requirements: Master’s degree covering topics in Plant Biology, Bioinformatics, Data Science, Statistics, Image analysis Basic understanding of plant phenotyping and analysis of large data sets, preferably also using AI tools for image analysis Strong analytical skills and ability to work independently and as part of a team We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Counsellor_R00025258": {
      "title": "Counsellor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nStudent wellbeing and support is a top priority and a key foundation for NTU Education 2030. It enables NTU students to thrive and flourish in their educational journey. As a Counsellor in NTU, you will play a crucial role to enable NTU to fulfil its mission for student wellbeing and support. As a team member of the University Counselling Centre, you will provide counselling for undergraduate and graduate students and engage with various internal and external stakeholders to promote an NTU campus community approach to mental health. The responsibilities include: Counselling assessments and interventions Provide professional counselling services, including conducting risk and need assessments and delivering intervention plans over a variety of modes and approaches such as in-person or online Facilitate case formulation, including preparation of assessment reports, delivery of case presentations, and referrals to relevant organisations in the social services ecosystem Escalate and co-manage sensitive crisis cases with more experienced mental health practitioners Provide consultation to staff on concerns they have regarding students at-risk Design, develop and/or facilitate wellbeing training initiatives and wellbeing portfolio/project annually Maintain professional, legal and ethical standards Adhere to professional standards in clinical, legal and ethical practices, ensuring client consent and confidentiality and proper data privacy protocols in counselling Participate in quality improvement projects led by more experienced mental health practitioners Document and maintain proper clinical records in accordance with policies and procedures of the University Counselling Centre Perform data collection and analysis which will aid in improvement of mental health support for students Participate actively in training to develop professional counselling expertise Community approach to case intervention Work collaboratively with and make recommendations to schools, student service offices, Halls of Residence, Support and Care Team, etc. to facilitate a campus community approach towards managing students with complex/severe mental health issues Work in inter-disciplinary teams (e.g. Educational/Clinical/ Counselling Psychologist, SEN specialist) to provide evidence-based psychotherapeutic interventions/treatment to students with complex/severe mental health issues and/or co-morbid issues (e.g. Special Education Needs and mental health issues) Liaise with other professionals (e.g. psychiatrists, doctors) and Social Service Agencies to mobilise community resources to provide care and support for the students Refer and/or recommend external service interventions (e.g. family therapy) as part of the student’s overall treatment plan Administrative support in University Counselling Centre (UCC) Support the daily operations of UCC, ensuring efficient and effective functioning Perform additional duties as assigned by Head, UCC or Director, UWO Requirements: Master’s degree in counselling Preferably a clinical member and registered counsellor with the Singapore Association for Counselling (SAC) or equivalent At least three (3) years of professional counselling experience Proficiency in professional counselling approaches and tools to help clients with diverse issues and conditions Experience in working with young adults, preferably in an educational setting Experience in working in a multi-disciplinary team is advantageous Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining accuracy in all operational aspects Strong organisational and multitasking skills, with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple tasks and responsibilities Possess professional values that aligned with the Code of Ethics of SAC Strong interpersonal and communication skills Proficiency in IT skills (e.g. Microsoft 365, use of Apps, appointment booking systems, case management systems) A good team player who is able to work independently Proficiency in spoken Mandarin would be an advantage to support counselling and engagement with undergraduates and graduates who are more comfortable communicating in Mandarin. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager-Assistant-Manager--Research-Support-_R00025244": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager/Assistant Manager (Research Support)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading research-intensive university in Singapore. The Research Support Office is seeking a motivated individual to support the administration and continuous improvement of NTU's research systems. Working closely with the Research Systems Lead, the successful candidate will support daily system operations, user management, system enhancements, testing, documentation, and stakeholder engagement. Key Responsibilities: User Support and Management Provide first-level support for research system users and resolve functional issues. Monitor and manage user queries through service portals. Liaise with IT teams and vendors on system issues and enhancements. Support system testing, maintenance, audits, and change requests. Training and Documentation: Maintain user guides, FAQs, and training materials. Coordinate user training sessions, briefings, and system communications. System Support, Maintenance and Management: Participate in system review meetings and track follow-up actions. Support process reviews and system enhancement initiatives. Work with internal stakeholders, IT teams, and vendors to improve user experience and operational effectiveness. Grant Management and Research-Related Activities: Support grant management and research administration activities to strengthen understanding of research workflows and system requirements. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree, preferably with background in systems, business, administration, projects, or a related field. Strong interest or experience in systems support, research administration, grant management, or process improvement. Fast learner who is comfortable navigating and using specialized IT systems; quick-thinking, resilient, resourceful, and equipped with strong problem-solving and critical-thinking skills. Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Prior experience in an end-user support environment, research/project management, or implementing, managing, or supporting IT applications will be an advantage. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Master-of-Science--MSc--Game-Design-Art-and-Technology--GDAT--_R00024991": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Master of Science (MSc) Game Design Art and Technology (GDAT)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is one of Asia's leading research-intensive universities, ranked among the world's top universities. The School of Art, Design and Media (ADM), within the College of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences, invites applications for the position of Assistant Manager for the Master of Science (MSc) in Game Design, Art, and Technology (GDAT) - a pioneering interdisciplinary programme jointly delivered by ADM and the College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS). This is an exciting opportunity to play a central role in shaping the operational excellence of a new and growing postgraduate programme at the intersection of art, design, and technology Key Responsibilities: Lead strategic planning, scheduling, budgeting, and operational management of the MSc in GDAT programme. Lead the end-to-end graduate admissions process, including the design and execution of outreach strategies, application screening, interview coordination, appeals handling, and post-offer follow-ups. Manage course registration processes, oversee curriculum updates and submissions for College approval, coordinate timetable scheduling, and liaise with the Office of Academic Services for cross-school registration matters. Lead, supervise, and develop the Senior Executive responsible for day-to-day operational tasks including enrolment, assessments, faculty hiring support, and final project submissions. Manage the end-to-end PTL hiring process, including coordinating teaching needs with Programme Co-Directors, sourcing and shortlisting candidates, processing appointments through HR, and overseeing onboarding, contractual requirements, and ongoing faculty administration. Oversee the preparation and submission of exam results and grades, ensuring accuracy and compliance with institutional academic policies. Plan, direct, and evaluate orientation programmes for each student intake, and oversee the resolution of student queries and feedback in line with institutional protocols. Prepare, monitor, and report on programme budgets, including technology-related procurement and asset management. Collaborate with internal departments, faculty, and external stakeholders to address programme-related matters and ensure operational alignment. Job Requirements: A Bachelor’s degree in any discipline. 5 to 7 years of relevant experience in admissions, operations, or administration, preferably in a higher education setting. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (particularly Word, Excel, PowerPoint); comfortable learning new IT systems or platforms. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both written and verbal. Excellent planning, coordination, and organizational abilities. A self-starter with the ability to work independently and collaboratively across teams and departments. Proactive and adaptable, with a solution-oriented mindset. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Experiential-Learning_R00024848": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Experiential Learning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRanked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides education within the University and the region. The incumbent is responsible for initiating and implementing existing and new initiatives to drive, facilitate and execute student ventures pathways. The role is responsible for identifying and facilitating collaboration between NTU community, especially with NTUitive, and external stakeholders. The incumbent will facilitate the connection of NTU students to available resources (for example, equipment) and facilities (Innovation Ports and Makers’ Labs) on campus. This role will work with multiple internal stakeholders in NTU to identify and provide the necessary support for high potential tech entrepreneurial projects. Where possible, the incumbent will co-lead the integration of major activities with the I&E Office and NTUitive. The incumbent will work closely with the Manager, Experiential Learning, to strengthen, design and implement co-curricular activities related to innovation and entrepreneurship, and support the Deputy Director, NTUpreneur in driving the alignment of NTUpreneur’s students' I&E activities, and where possible co-lead the integration of major activities with the I&E Office and NTUitive. Job Responsibilities: 1. Coordinate with Programme Leads, faculty/ instructors and other NTU schools to identify potential Tech-enabled or Tech-driven I&E student projects for NTUpreneur’s venture creation support Work closely with the Manager, Experiential Learning, Academic Leads, Faculty and NTU schools to identify, support and motivate students to continue and grow their I&E tech projects. Outreach to promote and communicate available support for students’ I&E pathway. Facilitate students’ access to such support and network. 2. Track progress of students’ I&E projects and ventures and provide support to acceleration Maintain a database tracking all students’ I&E projects. Monitor and regularly follow up with students, updating the status of their progress. Assess situations/challenges students may be facing, and initiate discussions with Manager, Experiential Learning, faculty and instructors to provide further assistance. 3. Identify and facilitate collaborations with reputable organisations/ individuals of the local and international I&E ecosystem, government or government funded institutions, top overseas universities, and corporations. Be familiar with active and reputable partners in the I&E ecosystem. Seek opportunities for collaborations with partners (internal and external). Design a sustainable industry engagement framework to engage these partners, and translate to actionable plans to benefit the NTU community. 4. Design I&E co-curricular activities with internal and external stakeholders, and bring external content to enrich students’ exposure and learnings to increase capabilities and opportunities for venture building. Work with NTUpreneur’s academic programme Leads or their Managers to organise approved initiatives at the Innovation spaces such as Innovation Port at Wee Cho Yaw Plaza, One North at Blk 79 Ayer Rajah and allocated space at NTU Innovation Hub. Work with representatives of NTU’s Student Clubs and Societies such as NTUpreneur’s Student Ambassador and Interest Groups, Entrepreneur Society (ES), Orientation Clubs of NTU Schools. Manage space and I&E activities at Innovation Port at Wee Cho Yaw Plaza, One North at Blk 79 Ayer Rajah and allocated space at NTU Innovation Hub. Manage bookings and ensure that these facilities are well-maintained and conducive. 5. Oversee the implementation of the annual Chua Thian Poh Pinnacle Prize to ensure its continued success. Drive the processes in the competition from receiving entries to pre-selection (for Finalist Shortlisting) to the Grand Finale through working Committees. Coordinate and arrange competition-funded programmes such as fireside chats and masterclasses for the finalists and NTU community. Work with multiple stakeholders to coordinate and implement the full logistics leading to the Grand Finale. 6. Provide mentorship in I&E (ventures and portfolio) for NTU students Reach out to students who are in pre-ideation or ideation stages to provide mentorship. Encourage and guide them to available resources in NTU. Suppport student intrapreneurs by providing advice for their I&E portfolio.  Match student teams to collaborate and accelerate the projects. Match students to mentors in Mentorship Clinic. Track impact by gathering feedback, and monitor growth for potential to create ventures. Requirements : Bachelor’s degree in engineering or business. At least 3 years relevant work experience in a university and multi-disciplinary environment. Experience in the startup eco-system is a plus. Experience in fact finding and analysing data Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Experience in working with professors, I&E government funding agencies Enjoy working with students, empowering and helping them to accelerate their I&E journeys Capability to work independently to drive the execution of projects, but with strong attributes of a team player Demonstrated resourcefulness, strong problem-solving skills, and the ability to multitask efficiently, even under tight deadlines Good communication and presentation skills Meticulous with an eye for detail in organising information and tracking work progress Knowledge in entrepreneurship, start-up development and ecosystem Knowledge of best practices in venture support in world-class universities as part of a holistic entrepreneurship education Knowledge in government grants, and other available support from related agencies for startups in Singapore Experience in venture mentorship Experience in budget planning, managing and processing claims in grants We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computational-electromagnetism-and-nanophotonics-_R00025593": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computational electromagnetism and nanophotonics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University, ranking 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. We are looking for a Research Fellow to pursue cutting-edge research in simulations and theory pertaining to novel mechanisms of extreme ultraviolet (EUV) light generation for applications such as EUV spectroscopy and EUV nanolithography Key Responsibilities: Computationally solve electrodynamics problems involving electron-photon and electron-matter interactions in the extreme ultraviolet (EUV) regime Develop new, efficient software for modeling unprecedented electromagnetic phenomena, using languages such as C++ and Python Formulate new theories pertaining to EUV generation, obtained ab initio from Maxwell’s equations and quantum electrodynamics/quantum field theory Job Requirements: PhD degree in physics, mathematics, engineering or related field Strong background in electrodynamics simulations techniques Strong background in C++, Python or similar languages Strong background in theoretical physics and mathematical physics We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Fire-Resistant-Materials-_R00025595": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Fire Resistant Materials)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . We are looking for a Project Officer with passion to work on the development of fire resistant materials. The role will focus on polymer composites and development of fire resistant materials to be used in building and construction sector. Experience working on related fields is a plus. Understanding of the standards is critical. Key Responsibilities: Work within the framework of the project to achieve and go beyond the project objectives. The candidate’s primary responsibility is to understand and improve the fire resistance characteristics of polymer composite panels that are used for construction applications. The candidate is expected to interact and closely work within a multi-disciplinary and multi-cultural team.  Expected to display a very high degree of professional ethics The candidate is expected to maintain higher standards when it comes to risk assessments and maintenance of lab or equipment or supplies that include procurement and liaison with suppliers Assist in and produce high quality reports and documents that consolidate research findings Job Requirements: Bachelor qualification degree in Materials Science and Engineering or related field At least 1 year of relevant experience in similar role / technical hands-on experience in related scope Familiarity with fire resistant tests, materials and principles of fire retardancy and resistance Good written and oral communication skills Good numeric and analytical skills Competent in information visualization, interaction design Good interpersonal skills (e.g. Ability to work independently / develop solutions under strict timelines, meticulous with keen eye for details / excellent organizational / time management skills) We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive---Public--International-and-Alumni-Relations--PIAR--Department--NIE-_R00022757": {
      "title": "Executive – Public, International and Alumni Relations (PIAR) Department [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable candidates for the position of Executive with the Public, International and Alumni Relations (PIAR) department . Responsibilities The Executive supports NIE’s institutional communications and stakeholder engagement efforts across hospitality relations, media relations, and integrated marketing. The role contributes to delivering meaningful guest experiences, strengthening NIE’s public visibility, and supporting branding and alumni initiatives through coordinated communications and operational support. Media Relations Assist in pitching story ideas to local and international media to raise NIE’s visibility and profile. Support media engagement activities including responding to queries, issuing media releases, and coordinating interviews. Track media coverage, compile reports and analyse performance metrics to inform communication strategies. Hospitality Relations Support the management of official visits to NIE, contributing to guest experience and institutional relationship-building. Assist in the operations and visitor experience of the NIE Visitors Learning Centre. Support the organisation of graduation ceremonies including guest coordination, video production, and reception arrangements. Assist in Institute and University-level events and engagements as required. Integrated Marketing & Alumni Relations Work with the social media team to ensure content is accurate, current and engaging across platforms. Assist NIE departments with branding and marketing needs, including coordinating print, digital or motion production for institutional campaigns. Support the preparation and submission of corporate reports to key internal and external stakeholders. Assist the alumni team in implementing engagement strategies and supporting alumni programmes and activities. Requirements A polytechnic diploma in Business, Communications, Hospitality, Marketing or a related field. Prior experience in hospitality management, marketing, media relations or event operations in an agency will be an advantage. At least two years of working experience. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact professionally with diverse stakeholders. Good organisational and project coordination skills, with attention to details. Able to multi-task and work under tight timelines. Interest in communications, hospitality, branding or alumni engagement. Familiarity with digital tools, social media platforms and basic content development is essential. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 18 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Finance-Planning-and-Analysis_R00025594": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Finance Planning and Analysis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Senior Assistant Manager, Financial Planning & Analysis, leads the business unit’s financial planning activities, operational finance oversight, and financial governance support. The role strengthens its financial performance through structured analysis, operational visibility, financial controls, and risk identification. It also focuses on performance monitoring, ensuring completeness of revenue, compliance with institutional and external requirements, and supporting informed decision‑making for the senior leadership team. This role complements the Finance Business Partner by managing execution, planning cycles, policy impact assessment, and communication of financial implications. This enables the Finance Business Partner to lead higher‑level planning, intra‑university initiatives, and strategic transformation efforts. Responsibilities Manage financial planning, budgeting and forecasting. Drive financial analysis, performance evaluation, pricing and margin review. Oversee finance governance and financial controls. Perform policy impact assessments and communicate implications of policy/system changes. Ensure compliance with financial, regulatory and audit requirements. Provide insightful KPI and performance reporting for management. Support continuous improvement and provide oversight to finance staff. Requirements Degree in Accountancy/Finance or equivalent professional qualifications. Chartered Accountant with at least 8 years of relevant experience. Highly adaptable, good time management skills & problem-solving skills. Demonstrate outstanding working relation management. Advantageous to know SAP, Ariba, Denodo, Workday, PowerBI. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Teaching-Assignment---Graduation-Matters_R00025591": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Teaching Assignment & Graduation Matters",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTo lead and oversee the effective delivery of faculty workforce, financial and student academic administration, ensuring compliant, timely and high-quality services that support the School’s teaching and operational priorities. The role provides end-to-end governance of key administrative processes, drives resource optimisation and continuous improvement, and works closely with academic and central stakeholders to deliver a seamless and sustainable operating environment. Key Responsibilities: Lead the end-to-end administration of Part-Time Lecturer (PTL) appointments, contracts and service agreements. Manage the PTL budget, remuneration processes and workforce resource planning. Oversee Teaching Assistant (TA) allocation and deployment to support teaching requirements. Administer student academic processes, including Leave of Absence, MOOC credit transfers and other academic requests, in accordance with university policies. Ensure compliance with governance, financial, audit and data management requirements. Collaborate with Schools, HR, Finance and other central offices to ensure timely and effective service delivery. Analyse operational and financial data to support management reporting, resource planning and informed decision-making. Review, streamline and digitalise administrative processes to improve operational efficiency and service quality. Develop and maintain standard operating procedures, documentation and records to ensure consistency and audit readiness. Foster strong stakeholder relationships and deliver responsive, customer-focused administrative support in alignment with the School’s strategic objectives. Other duties: handling role-base email accounts, answering student enquiries, participating in events eg. orientation and counter duties, formatting of exam question papers, checking of marked exam scripts, preparing certification letters, booking of facilities and fault reporting etc. Overall Role Outcome The role delivers effective governance and operational oversight across faculty workforce, financial, student and teaching support administration, ensuring that resources are well managed, processes are compliant and efficient, and stakeholders receive timely and high-quality support. The role also contributes to the School’s longer-term operational sustainability through process standardisation, digitalisation, data-driven planning and continuous improvement. Requirements: Recognized degree in any discipline. Sound understanding of academic administration processes and university policies, particularly in areas such as faculty appointment, student records, and budget management. Familiarity with HR and Finance systems (e.g. Workday) and student information systems. Working knowledge of budgeting principles, contract management, and data governance. Awareness of audit and compliance requirements within a higher education or public sector environment. Administrative experience in an academic, research, or public sector setting. Proven track record in managing contract or HR-related documentation, budget tracking, or student administration. Exposure to multi-stakeholder coordination, e.g. between academic staff, HR, Finance, and students, would be highly valued. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--Greenhouse-Manager--Greenhouse-Management-_R00024721": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Crop Experiments & Sensing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . We are looking for a Research Assistant (Crop Experiments and Sensing) to join an interdisciplinary project, funded by National Research Foundation Singapore (NRF) under the AI-for-Science Catalytic Grant, which aims to develop AI-driven urban farming systems for crop yield and trait optimisation. The researcher will join a multidisciplinary research team, with primary responsibilities in greenhouse operations, crop experimentation, and plant proximal/remote sensing. Experimental duties include coordinating and monitoring the successful execution of crop experiments, ensuring that all technical and manpower requirements are in place. Plant sensing duties include overseeing the operation of the remote sensing systems (RGB, 3D, hyperspectral, and thermal imaging) for crop monitoring. The researcher will also liaise with industry collaborators and funding agencies. Key Responsibilities: Assist in the deployment, operation, and maintenance of proximal sensing systems for Controlled Environment Agriculture (CEA), including RGB, 3D, hyperspectral, and thermal imaging cameras, as well as agritech sensors. Procure experimental equipment, sensors, and peripherals. Maintain data pipelines for greenhouse and CEA experiments, including adapting source code to different crop types (e.g., camera height calibration and image segmentation algorithms). Consolidate data from different sources to input machine learning modelling. This includes near-continuous interventions or treatments, plant sensing, ground-truth data of yield and mineral content, and metadata. Maintain databases, ensuring data integrity. Execute backup policies. Coordinate with vendors to troubleshoot and resolve operational sensing-related issues. Monitor active experiments using phenotyping software, including dynamic irrigation scheduling. Coordinate greenhouse experiment operations with the greenhouse manager, including manpower planning, seedling production, fertigation tank refilling, and hardware support. Prepare technical progress reports and respond to information requests from funding agencies. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s in Remote Sensing, Agricultural/Electronic/or Biosystems Engineering, Plant/or Computer Science, Agronomy or relevant fields from a reputable institution. Advanced knowledge in proximal/remote sensing, cameras. Advanced knowledge in image processing and programming. At least 2 years of relevant experience, and willingness to work with agritech IoT equipment. Experience in plant/crop experiments and phenotyping is an advantage. Ability to work well with multiple competing priorities, manage projects and meet deadlines. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, and ability to work in a diverse, international, and inter-disciplinary research environment. A good team player and able to work independently with minimum supervision. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Medical-Librarian-Medical-Librarian--LKCMedicine-_R00024323": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager/Manager, Library [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. This role will manage the strategic development and delivery of an effective and engaging information literacy program that supports the institution's learning, teaching, and research activities. This role will enable students, faculty, and researchers to confidently gather, manage, evaluate, synthesize, and ethically use information and data. Additionally, the Librarian will lead professional services and initiatives that support the full research lifecycle—from planning and discovery to publication, impact, and archiving—to promote the scholarly output of the community.   Responsibilities: Direct, manage, and deliver a comprehensive information literacy program through in-person and online instruction, workshops, and consultations. Provide expert guidance and training on advanced search strategies, literature reviews, the research process, reference management tools, and academic writing. Collaborate with faculty to strategically embed information literacy into the curriculum, providing instructional support for various teaching methods, including Team-Based Learning (TBL). Develop, manage, and promote the library's collections—including books, journals, and electronic databases—to ensure they are relevant and critical for user needs. Create and disseminate a wide range of instructional and support materials, such as online tutorials, learning activities, interactive tools, and print guides, to promote academic integrity and self-paced learning. Manage and promote services and resources related to scholarly communication, including author rights, open access, and research impact. Lead an effective search service to support faculty and researchers in their advanced research and publishing endeavors. Continuously monitor trends, user feedback, and institutional policies to ensure the ongoing improvement and innovation of library operations and services. Assist in managing the daily operations of the library, which may include supervising support staff and contributing to administrative tasks. Undertake additional responsibilities and lead assigned projects or service improvement initiatives. Requirements: A good bachelor’s degree plus a master’s degree in Library or Information Science or equivalent postgraduate qualification recognized by the Library Association of Singapore (LAS) At least 5 years work experience in a tertiary/research/medical library Good communication skills (writing and speaking) Good independent learning skills with a strong desire for continual life-long learning Good organizational and time management skills Embraces changes in technology and environment Good inter-personal skills and able to relate well to users and colleagues We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Executive--Admin---Finance--Office-for-Research---NIE-_R00024436": {
      "title": "Executive, Admin & Finance (Office for Research) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Executive, Admin & Finance with the Office for Research (OfR) . This role is responsible for supporting day-to-day administrative, financial and procurement operations, ensuring timely processing, accuracy and compliance with organizational policies and funding requirements. This is a contract post till 31 Mar 2028. Responsibilities: Process claims and invoice submissions received from Project Teams, Office for Research and Research Centres in a timely and accurate manner. Handle manual and system-based claims, including transport, general, transcriber claims and visiting consultant claims. Verify supporting documents, funding availability, and compliance with established financial policies and guidelines. Process agency invoices for Part-time Research Staff and liaise with relevant stakeholders on any discrepancies or clarifications. Check, review, and process manual and system-based Purchase Requests (PRs) in accordance with procurement procedures. Review and verify Invitation to ITQ documents to ensure completeness, accuracy, and compliance with institutional and audit requirements. Coordinate with project teams, vendors, and procurement units to resolve procurement-related queries. Provide general administrative support to the Office for Research and project teams (during events) to ensure smooth day-to-day operations. Perform Goods Receipt (GR) for project purchases in a timely manner to facilitate payment processing and ensure compliance with procurement and financial procedures. Support centralized inventory management by tracking assets, ensuring accuracy and consistency of records, and maintaining well-organized, accessible storage areas. Assist with asset-related activities such as asset loaning and returns, proper labelling of devices, and conducting physical verification and stocktaking exercises. Support handling asset losses and disposals, and preparing reports for assessment and endorsement. Assist in other ad-hoc administrative and financial tasks as assigned. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma in Finance, Business Administration or a related field. At least 2-3 years of relevant working experience. Responsible, systematic, and able to work independently with minimal supervision. Strong attention to detail and accuracy in handling financial documents. Proficient in Microsoft Office, especially Excel and Word. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 31 August 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/ICT-Support-Engineer--Service-Management-Department---NIE-_R00025586": {
      "title": "ICT Support Engineer (Service Management Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore is Singapore’s national teacher training institute. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education , and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . The Academic Computing and Information Services (ACIS) division oversees NIE’s ICT needs. We invite applications for the position of ICT Support Engineer to support our efforts in transforming the education landscape in Singapore. Job Summary The ICT Support Engineer supports the IT Service Operations Manager in delivering ICT support to NIE stakeholders. The role diagnoses and resolves hardware, software and service issues, identifies root causes, and escalates to external vendors when required. The engineer also uses AI-driven diagnostic tools and ITSM platforms to improve resolution efficiency. The role maintains knowledge of ICT infrastructure and works with service desk staff, technical teams, end users, and project managers to ensure smooth operations and a positive user experience. Job Responsibilities 1. End-User Support and Service Delivery Act as the first point of contact for IT and AV issues and service requests, including monitoring and escalating AI service desk chatbot inquiries. Analyse and troubleshoot incidents and perform corrective and preventive maintenance. Provide IT/AV support for events, meetings, video conferences and lessons, including after-hours support when required. Deliver IT/AV services that meet user needs and satisfaction. Track task completion and ensure adherence to service level agreements (SLAs). 2. IT/AV Systems Maintenance and Operations Perform preventive and corrective maintenance of IT/AV systems in lecture theatres, classrooms, tutorial rooms, labs and meeting rooms. Assist in the evaluation, procurement and deployment of IT/AV equipment and solutions, including AI-enhanced hardware such as intelligent auto-framing cameras and AI noise-cancellation audio systems. Participate in IT/AV projects and initiatives to improve service efficiency and user experience. 3. Documentation and Knowledge Management Document incident resolutions, best practices and standard procedures in the internal Knowledge Base. Maintain technical documentation for IT/AV configurations and deployment guides, using generative AI tools where applicable. 4. Asset and Inventory Management Maintain IT/AV asset records and update asset databases. Conduct physical asset verification and report findings for audit reconciliation and compliance. 5. Security and Compliance Collaborate with the cybersecurity team to enhance endpoint security using AI-driven threat detection and endpoint response (EDR) systems. Ensure compliance with NIE IT security policies, relevant regulatory requirements and acceptable AI usage policies. 6. Business Continuity and Process Improvement Participate in IT Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery (BCDR) programmes. Contribute to service improvement through innovation, feedback and cross-functional projects. Identify opportunities to automate routine support tasks using AI, scripts and robotic process automation (RPA). Requirements 1. Educational Background and Certifications A Polytechnic Diploma in Information & Communication Technology (ICT) or a related field, with strong knowledge of technology and systems supporting IT and AV infrastructure. ITIL Foundation certification and experience with ITIL best practices are preferred. 2. Experience and Technical Skills At least 2 years of experience in ICT support, with a proven track record in customer service and technical support. Familiarity with Generative AI assistants such as Microsoft Copilot and ChatGPT for troubleshooting, scripting and workflow automation. Solid knowledge of computer troubleshooting, networking, applications and operating systems, including Microsoft Windows, Microsoft Office, Macintosh OS and mobile devices. Knowledge of networking protocols and common software tools. Familiarity with audio/video equipment, including AV troubleshooting and setup for events, lessons and meetings. Ability to diagnose and resolve technical issues independently with minimal supervision. 3. Key Personal Attributes Proactive, self-motivated and resilient, with a strong sense of urgency and ability to work under pressure. Result-oriented and responsible, with the ability to meet deadlines and deliver work to a high standard. Collaborative team player with creativity, resourcefulness and strong problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills. 4. Innovation and Continuous Improvement Strong interest in new technologies, particularly AI and automation tools, to improve productivity and service efficiency. Ability to stay current with relevant technology trends and tools. Ability to collaborate with peers and technical teams across the organisation to resolve issues and implement solutions. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 4 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Researcher--Social-Cohesion-Research-Programme---RSIS-_R00025585": {
      "title": "Researcher (Social Cohesion Research Programme) [RSIS]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nResearcher (Social Cohesion Research Programme) The S. Rajaratnam School of International Studies (RSIS) , a Graduate School of Nanyang Technological University (NTU), is a leading research-intensive and teaching institution on security research in the Asia-Pacific region. The person will assist the Social Cohesion Research Programme with research and administrative duties. The work will cover areas such as how the social and built environment shapes the practice of multiculturalism and inclusion, the various forms of religious digitisation, and the detection of online trends. The research involves conducting in-depth literature reviews on topics such as social cohesion, religiosity, ethnicity, and nationalism, as well as carrying out multivariate analyses on cross-national data to assess social cohesion patterns. Administrative responsibilities include supporting strategic events and meetings, managing relevant databases, and providing key insights to aid decision-making and facilitate effective communication. The person should have a PhD/Master/Degree in social sciences/data analytics and have an appreciation of the cultural dynamics in Singapore and the region. He/she needs to be comfortable with report writing and statistical analyses, and possesses a basic understanding of multivariate statistics, including multiple regressions, factor analysis, and statistical tabulations on Excel and charts. All applicants should submit the following: •           A cover letter specifying how your qualifications match the job description. •           A detailed curriculum vitae; •           2 published articles or writing samples; and •           3 reference letters. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For further information about RSIS, please visit our website: www.rsis.edu.sg Hiring Institution: RSIS"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Autonomous-Drone-Swarm-_R00025584-1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Autonomous Drone Swarm)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Engineer in Autonomous Drone Swarms for GPS-Denied Environments to develop and integrate the hardware and software required for coordinated multirotor operations in complex, cluttered environments. The role will focus on designing and implementing onboard sensing, communication, computing, localisation, navigation, and control systems for autonomous drone swarms operating without reliable GPS. The Research Engineer will also develop and validate swarm coordination, collaborative perception, mapping, obstacle avoidance, and multi-agent path-planning algorithms, and integrate these capabilities on physical drone platforms. The work will involve system integration, simulation, hardware-in-the-loop testing, flight experimentation, and performance evaluation under realistic GPS-denied conditions. Key Responsibilities: Develop and integrate hardware and software architectures for autonomous multirotor drone swarms operating in GPS-denied and cluttered environments. Design and implement onboard sensing, localisation, mapping, navigation, obstacle-avoidance, communication, and flight-control systems. Develop swarm coordination, task allocation, multi-agent path-planning, collaborative perception, and inter-drone information-sharing algorithms. Conduct simulation, hardware-in-the-loop testing, system integration, and flight experiments to evaluate robustness, scalability, and performance under realistic operating conditions. Work with researchers and project collaborators to support system demonstrations and prepare technical reports, publications, project deliverables, and documentation. Job Requirements: Education qualifications Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Aerospace Engineering, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Robotics, Computer Science, or a closely related discipline. Strong academic or project background in autonomous systems, robotics, unmanned aerial vehicles, embedded systems, or multi-agent systems. Research or project experience in autonomous drone navigation, drone swarms, or GPS-denied operations would be advantageous. Soft skills Strong communication, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Strong sense of ownership, responsibility, and initiative. Ability to work effectively with researchers, engineers, students, industry partners, and project stakeholders. Willingness to support flight testing, system demonstrations, project reporting, and milestone reviews. Hard skills Demonstrated hands-on experience in the hardware and software integration of autonomous robots or multirotor drones. Proficiency in C++, Python, MATLAB, or equivalent programming languages for robotics and autonomous-system development. Experience with robotic middleware and simulation environments such as ROS/ROS 2, Gazebo, AirSim, or equivalent platforms. Experience integrating sensors, embedded computers, communication modules, flight controllers, and other onboard hardware. Familiarity with autopilot platforms such as PX4 or ArduPilot and communication protocols such as MAVLink would be advantageous. Knowledge of localisation, visual-inertial odometry, simultaneous localisation and mapping, obstacle avoidance, path planning, and flight-control algorithms. Familiarity with multi-agent coordination, task allocation, formation control, collaborative perception, or distributed swarm algorithms would be advantageous. Experience Experience integrating sensing, localisation, navigation, communication, control, and decision-making components within a robotics or autonomous-drone project. Practical experience assembling, configuring, troubleshooting, and flight-testing multirotor platforms would be highly advantageous. Competencies Ability to independently design, integrate, test, and troubleshoot autonomous-drone hardware and software systems. Ability to work across robotics, embedded systems, perception, navigation, control, and multi-agent coordination domains. Ability to conduct systematic experiments and evaluate system performance, robustness, scalability, and reliability. Ability to deliver research outcomes within project timelines and contribute to technical reports, project demonstrations, and high-quality publications. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Librarian---Senior-Assistant-Manager--Digital-Technology-and-Analytics_R00025213": {
      "title": "Librarian / Senior Assistant Manager, Digital Technology and Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a leading research-intensive university known for its strong focus on innovation, interdisciplinary learning, and creating meaningful impact through education and research.   The Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) plays an important role in supporting students across their academic journey, from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. Working closely with schools, colleges, and other partners across the University, SASD helps to create a seamless, enriching, and student-centred experience at NTU.   Within this broader mission, NTU Library , under the Office of Information, Knowledge and Library Services (OIKLS) , provide essential learning, research, and collaborative environments that support the University community. We are seeking an experienced and forward-looking Librarian / Senior Assistant Manager to strengthen the Library’s data, analytics, and AI capabilities to improve operational efficiency and user experience. Job Responsibilities Develop, enhance, and maintain library data models, dashboards, data visualisations, and data integration pipelines. Work with library stakeholders to understand business requirements, assess data needs, and deliver practical analytics solutions. Support the review, improvement, and maintenance of analytics platforms and related data environments, including Qlik Sense, Denodo, Alma Analytics, and other relevant systems. Evaluate new analytics tools, platform features, and data visualisation approaches for possible adoption. Apply emerging technologies, including AI workflows, AI agents, and related tools, to improve library analytics, operational efficiency, and user experience. Support staff adoption of dashboards, data tools, and technology-enabled solutions through communication, guidance, and training. Job Requirements Recognised degree in a related discipline, such as Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Data Science, or a related field. At least 5 years of relevant working experience in data engineering, data analytics, business intelligence, or related areas. Proficient in data engineering, ETL/data pipeline development, REST API data sources, SQL, and dashboard/BI development tools such as Qlik Sense, Power BI, Tableau, or similar. Programming or scripting skills, such as Python, for data processing and automation. Knowledge of AI/LLM concepts, agentic frameworks, RAG pipelines, vector databases, and cloud AI services such as Azure OpenAI or similar would be an advantage. Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical users. Service-oriented, agile, and able to manage priorities and work within deadlines. At NTU, you will join a collaborative and forward-looking university environment committed to continuous learning, innovation, and service excellence. This role offers the opportunity to work across diverse library settings, partner stakeholders across the University, and contribute to improvements that have meaningful and visible impact on the campus community. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Business-Operations--Finance--Marketing---Strategy-_R00024817": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Business Operations (Finance, Marketing & Strategy)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading global university known for its excellence in research, innovation, and education. About the Role We are seeking a dynamic and strategic professional to join as Assistant Director, overseeing communications, strategy, outreach, and operations for the institute. This role offers the opportunity to work closely with leadership to shape institutional positioning, drive impactful initiatives, and engage a wide range of stakeholders. Key Responsibilities Strategic Leadership & Institute Development Support the Director in shaping and executing GIFTS’ medium- and long-term strategies to strengthen Singapore’s international trading ecosystem. Translate institutional and national objectives into clear plans, initiatives, and KPIs, ensuring effective execution and measurable outcomes. Identify strategic opportunities for growth, partnerships, and new initiatives that enhance GIFTS’ relevance and impact. Industry Development & Corporate Engagement Lead and deepen strategic partnerships with government agencies, corporate partners, and industry stakeholders. Drive initiatives that enhance industry collaboration, experiential learning, and ecosystem development. Represent GIFTS as a credible and trusted partner within the international trading and policy ecosystem, both locally and globally. Student, Alumni & Talent Development Oversee initiatives that enhance student engagement, industry exposure, and career readiness across the programme lifecycle. Guide the development and continuous improvement of platforms and programmes supporting internships, careers, mentorship, and alumni engagement. Leverage alumni networks to strengthen industry ties and long-term ecosystem outcomes. Fundraising & Financial Sustainability Ensure GIFTS remains financially sustainable and self-funding through effective corporate partner engagement. Cultivate, retain, and expand corporate funding relationships by demonstrating clear value, relevance, and impact. Oversee contribution agreements, funding initiatives, and donor-related engagements in alignment with strategic priorities. Strategic Communications, Branding & Media Oversight Provide strategic direction on communications, branding, and outreach to position GIFTS as a leading hub for international trading education and engagement. Oversee media, digital, and public engagement efforts, ensuring clear, consistent, and responsible messaging. Manage reputational risks and advise leadership on communication strategies and public positioning. Events, Engagement & Executive Support Conceptualise and oversee high-impact events, including industry dialogues, conferences, experiential learning programmes, and donor engagements. Ensure events are strategically leveraged for visibility, partnerships, fundraising, and thought leadership. Support senior leadership in strategic engagements, external representation, and VIP or high-level stakeholder interactions. Governance, Planning & Performance Management Oversee planning, reporting, and governance processes, including KPIs linked to student outcomes, partnerships, and funding. Ensure compliance with institutional, donor, and government requirements, including audit readiness. Support continuous improvement of programmes, processes, and operational effectiveness. Stakeholder, Team & Vendor Management Work effectively across the university ecosystem, including NBS, Finance, UAO, CAO, and other units, to ensure alignment and smooth execution. Influence and align stakeholders in a matrixed environment without direct authority. Manage external vendors and service providers to ensure quality delivery and value for money. Provide guidance, mentorship, and leadership to team members, fostering a collaborative and high-performance culture. Why Join Us Opportunity to work at the intersection of academia, policy, and industry Exposure to senior leadership and high-impact initiatives Collaborative and dynamic work environment Requirements GIFTS aims to provide a well-qualified talent pipeline for and build a strong linkage between the university and the international industry. It is looking for a Assistant Director (AD) who will work closely with various parts of the university and the industry to achieve its goals.  This position provides the platform for the AD to play an important part in creating future leaders in the international industry, and to exert his or her abilities to build a strong linkage between the university and the industry.   The candidate should have: A good bachelor’s degree and proven high quality academic achievements.   At least 12-15 years of work experience, prior relevant experience will be an added advantage. Knowledge and experience in business development and programme/operations management. Strong strategic thinking and possess an analytical mind. Excellent writing, communication and organizational skills. Confident and proactive with demonstrated dynamism and resourcefulness in problem solving. Ability to work with people of various levels and cultures, with excellent interpersonal skills. Good commercial understanding of the local marketplace, coupled with an ability to establish wide networks and strong relationships with management of different companies. Strong influencing skills, with a proven ability to provide pragmatic solutions. Ability to proactively identify and prioritize tasks and be able to escalate matters of significance while retaining the responsibility for them. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Research---Centre-Support_R00024815": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research & Centre Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading research-intensive university, recognised internationally for its excellence in education, research, and innovation. NTU fosters a collaborative and inclusive work environment that supports professional growth and continuous learning. About the Role We are looking for an organised and proactive Assistant Manager to support the institute’s communications, events, and operational activities. This role works closely with internal stakeholders and leadership to ensure effective coordination, high-quality delivery, and smooth day to day operations. The position offers meaningful exposure to institutional initiatives and provides opportunities to contribute to process improvement and stakeholder engagement. Key Responsibilities Provide end‑to‑end administrative and operational coordination support across communications, events, and outreach activities. Support the development, editing, and dissemination of communications materials, including digital and online platforms. Coordinate the planning and execution of events, including logistics, stakeholder coordination, and post‑event follow‑up. Liaise with internal teams, university offices, and external partners to ensure timely delivery of activities and tasks. Support financial and operational processes, including basic budgeting coordination, reimbursements, and workflow tracking. Assist with documentation, reporting, and maintenance of accurate records in line with institutional requirements. Why Join Us Opportunity to work in a dynamic and collaborative university environment. Exposure to a broad range of institutional and cross‑functional initiatives. Supportive culture that values professional development and continuous improvement. Requirements Bachelor’s degree or equivalent professional qualification. Relevant experience in administrative, operational, communications, or events coordination roles. Strong organisational, coordination, and time‑management skills. Clear written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in digital tools (e.g. Microsoft Excel, collaboration and content platforms). Ability to work collaboratively and manage multiple priorities effectively. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--IT-System---Cybersecurity-_R00023712": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (IT System & Cybersecurity)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTemasek Laboratories@NTU (TL@NTU) explore frontiers in science and develops strategic technologies to enhance the defence and security of Singapore. TL@NTU forms part of the defence technology community in Singapore alongside DSO National Laboratories, Defence Science and Technology Agency (DSTA), Temasek Laboratories @ NUS and @SUTD and the local defence industry. The administration team is seeking an IT cybersecurity individual to contribute to the following areas Key Responsibilities: Manage and secure IT infrastructure and systems.  Monitor system performance and respond to cyber incidents.  Implement access controls, patching, and security measures.  Support cybersecurity governance, compliance, and risk management initiatives.  Ensure stable and secure IT operations across TL@NTU and NTU. Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree in Cybersecurity, Information Technology, Computer Science, Information system. 3–5 years’ experience in:  - Cybersecurity operations. - Information security governance, risk, and compliance (GRC). -  IT infrastructure security management. Experience in supporting:  - Security certification and compliance programmes (e.g. ISO27001, Cyber Trust Mark). - Cybersecurity risk assessments and audits. -  Implementation of security controls and policies. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive--Resident-Relation_R00025174": {
      "title": "Executive, Resident Relation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Campus Housing (OCH) serves to make NTU the hub and destination to deliver best-in-class campus for learning, working, and living. OCH is a critical department responsible for student and faculty housing on campus, the sports and recreational facilities, and its related services. We are looking for individuals who have a strong passion for delivering exceptional service to residents of the University’s student and faculty housing, and athletes and users of sports & recreation facilities on campus. The role provides the successful candidate with the opportunity to develop, contribute and grow oneself holistically across areas of excellence in customer relationship management, facilities & contracts management and/or quality and corporate functions (e.g. finance / billing, quality management, etc.) within the Department. If you are a diploma holder with at least 3 years of relevant working experience in residential management / services, customer service / resident relations management, or housing operation support and contract management, quality, and corporate service (finance / billing), you may be the one whom we are looking for.  Having an experience in student hostels, staff housing or hospitality services would be a plus for this role!  The incumbent is required to: Hostel application processing and the assignment of rooms / housing units, including the management of waitlist and students’ appeal for on-campus accommodation. Ensure the high quality of rooms / housing units for students’ check-in through comprehensive inspections. Ensure accurate billing of hall fees and other payable items as well as timely collection and follow-up where necessary. This includes accurate and timely refunds to students where applicable. Collaborate with colleagues and external vendors / contractors to get update on the status of maintenance / repairs to student hostels. Proactively engage student residents in understanding and addressing residents’ needs and contributing to problem-solving and resolution of concerns. This includes addressing and resolving student residents’ requests, feedback, and complaints promptly to meet SLA requirements. Communicate and inform student residents in advance on scheduled maintenance, adhoc repairs and other matters that may cause inconvenience to residents. Conduct routine walkthroughs of OCH managed premises to evaluate safety and security measures. This includes follow-up actions for enhancement and refinements of measures. Conduct investigations and compile supporting documentation for incident reports. This includes proposal of suitable sanctions for rule violations based on the severity and frequency of infractions, and prompt escalation of persistent and / or severe breaches for further enforcement measures, as well as implementation of approved sanctions. Maintenance of up-to-date and precise records, including resident details, occupancy status, and availability, to facilitate billing processes and management reporting. Ensure that facilities reservations are made through established booking channels, and all pre-event and post-event arrangements are properly managed. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Student-Administration_R00022893": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the school is renowned for its high academic standards and research. It is one of the largest EEE schools in the world, with about 120 faculty members and an enrolment of more than 5,000, of which about 2,000 are graduate students. We invite applications for the position of Assistant Manager. The Assistant Manager will play a crucial role in supporting the Master of Science (coursework) academic and program management tasks, contributing to the smooth operation of academic programs and student success. Key responsibilities: Handling dissertation-related workflows, including calls for proposals, dissertation allocation, submission tracking and examination management. Support student-related activities such as registration, orientation and attending to programme/candidature-related enquiries.  Managing program administration across the student lifecycle, covering processes such as leave of absence, withdrawal, dismissal, appeals, academic offenses, and fee waivers. Facilitating the processing of financial aid applications, including scholarships, awards, study grants, and travel grants.  Assisting in the coordination of pre-exam preparation and post-exam processing, including tasks such as exam paper preparation, marks verification and processing, and managing exam result appeals.  Conducting follow-ups on overdue fees.  Compiling and preparing reports related to assigned tasks. Any other administrative duties as assigned. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree Experience in academic administration, exam operation with students’ interaction in an education setting is preferred. Familiarity in financial workflow is an advantage. Strong organizational skills with ability to manage multiple deadlines. High accuracy, attention to details and sound judgment. Ability to handle confidential information. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint); knowledge of Power Automate will be an added advantage. Team player and able to work independently. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Scientist--Trust-Technologies-_R00025580": {
      "title": "Senior Research Scientist (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for people and businesses in the digital transformation by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize.  We are seeking a dynamic, commercially driven individual to lead the end-to-end commercialization, technology translation, and industry engagement strategy for DTC. The successful candidate will bridge the gap between world-class researchers and industry stakeholders by translating advanced TrustTech and AI Safety research into real-world business solutions, identifying high-impact enterprise use cases, driving adoption across strategic industry verticals (e.g., Financial Services, Telecommunications, Healthcare, and Tech), and executing joint industry Proof-of-Concepts (PoCs). The successful candidate will work closely with DTC leadership, Principal Investigators (PIs), research engineers, external corporate partners, and public sector agencies. Key Responsibilities:  Evaluate R&D outcomes across Privacy-Enhancing Technologies, Decentralization & Blockchain, and AI Risk Management for commercial viability and translate them into products and services. Conduct market readiness assessments and develop value propositions tailored to enterprise, regulatory, and public sector requirements. Drive outreach and build strategic partnerships with corporate leaders, multinational corporations (MNCs), local enterprises, and technology startups across key sectors, including Financial Services, Telecommunications, Technology, and the Public Sector. Manage and scale the industry engagement pipeline, converting technical discussions into formal industry collaborations, Joint Labs, and paid Proof-of-Concept (PoC) implementations. Oversee existing and incoming industry PoCs to ensure that target metrics and business outcomes are achieved. Represent DTC at flagship industry events, roundtables, and international showcases to build mindshare and drive enterprise leads. Collaborate with key government and ecosystem partners, including IMDA and NRF, to align commercialization efforts with national strategic priorities. Prepare and deliver presentations highlighting DTC research achievements and innovations. Track and evaluate progress on DTC’s Innovation & Enterprise (I&E) Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), including the number of technologies deployed and licensing/IP revenue. Support the preparation of progress reports and commercialization proposals for DTC Management and funding agencies. Job Requirements: The candidate should possess a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Business, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or a relevant technical or quantitative field. At least 8–10 years of relevant experience in technology commercialization, corporate innovation, product management, business development, or venture building, preferably within deep-tech or enterprise software sectors. Proven track record in translating complex technologies from early-stage R&D into commercial deployment, enterprise adoption, or industry Proof-of-Concepts (PoCs). Demonstrated experience in engaging, negotiating with, and managing senior stakeholders across financial institutions, MNCs, and government agencies. Familiarity with one or more of the following areas is highly preferred: Privacy-Preserving Technologies (PETs), Federated Learning, Fully Homomorphic Encryption, Secure Multi-Party Computation, AI Safety, AI Testing & Evaluation, Trustworthy AI Governance, Blockchain, or Decentralization. Strong ability to bridge academic research and industry needs, translating complex technical concepts into clear business value propositions and commercial use cases. Strong communication, presentation, networking, negotiation, and stakeholder management skills. Proactive, self-motivated, entrepreneurial, and able to work effectively in a fast-paced, multi-stakeholder environment and deliver under tight timelines. Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple technical PoCs, industry opportunities, and funding or grant calls concurrently. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--International-Admissions_R00025579": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, International Admissions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. SASD works collaboratively with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey for all students.  This position sits with the Office of Admissions (OA) and supports the University in bringing in international students. This position also contributes to broader initiatives aimed at enhancing student experience, ensuring that every interaction—from inquiry to enrollment—is welcoming, efficient, and student-centered. The Assistant Manager will play a key role in managing the day-to-day operations of the international admissions team. He/she will act as a bridge between partner institutions, government agencies, potential applicants, colleges, and administrative staff, ensuring smooth and efficient admissions processes. Key Responsibilities: 1.    Admissions application and selection Understand the education systems in new markets and propose admissions selection criteria based on market practices, intake targets, and applicant quality. Work with supervisors and schools to manage the issuance of offers, monitor acceptances, and handle appeals to meet the University’s mission.  Update and adhere to admissions policies and Standard Operating Procedures (SOP). Handle enquiries from prospective students, parents, schools, and education agents in a timely and professional manner. Contribute to projects and initiatives that support continuous improvement of admissions services and student experience. 2.    Partnership Management Engage principals and further education counselors of high school partners.  Establish and cultivate strong relationships with international high schools and education partners through regular engagement. Gather market intelligence on political, economic, or educational developments that could impact student recruitment. Execute market-specific outreach and recruitment activities. 3.    Marketing and Event Management Execute outreach activities for visiting partners in coordination with internal stakeholders  (e.g. liaising with centres/labs to on visits etc).  Host local and foreign visitors from partner institutions when they visit NTU and conduct admission talks. Liaise with internal stakeholders to ensure that information provided in marketing collaterals are relevant, updated and available. Requirements: Degree from any discipline, entry-level candidates are welcome to apply. Prior experience in admissions/ student recruitment and/or general administrative positions. Candidates with experience in planning executing outreach programmes would have an added advantage.  Ability to perform data analysis to interpret market information to support recruitment strategies and decision-making. Knowledge of Denodo and/or SQL, BI analytics would be an added advantage. Strong interpersonal and networking skills with the ability to build effective relationships with diverse stakeholders. As the role involves conducting admission talks/events, the successful candidate must be comfortable with some level of public speaking (approximately 5 to 6 events per year with audience size ranging from 30 to 200).  Proactive, resourceful and possess the ability to manage multiple priorities. Occasional travelling required. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Programme-Lead--GEMBA_R00025578": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Programme Lead, GEMBA",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore is a leading global university committed to nurturing leaders and creating societal impact through education, research, and service. Nanyang Business School invites applications for the role of Programme Lead, Global EMBA Programme. This is a senior leadership role responsible for driving the strategic growth, market positioning, recruitment, admissions, operations, stakeholder engagement, and business development of the Global Executive MBA programme. The role offers the opportunity to shape a high-impact executive education platform, work closely with senior business leaders and faculty, and contribute to the School’s graduate and lifelong learning ambitions. Why Join NTU Opportunity to lead and grow a flagship executive education programme. Exposure to senior executives, entrepreneurs, faculty, alumni, corporate partners, and international stakeholders. Meaningful role in developing leaders and strengthening industry engagement. Collaborative university environment with opportunities for professional development and cross-functional partnership. Contribution to the continued growth of graduate management education and lifelong learning. Key Responsibilities Lead the strategic planning and growth of the Global EMBA programme in alignment with School and University priorities. Provide direction for marketing, recruitment, admissions, brand positioning, market messaging, and recruitment pipeline performance. Oversee programme operations to ensure smooth delivery of classes, global modules, study trips, company visits, events, student services, and faculty support. Build and maintain senior-level relationships with students, alumni, faculty, corporate clients, industry associations, HR and learning leaders, international partners, and internal stakeholders. Manage programme budgets, revenue, costs, marketing spend, enrolment performance, student satisfaction, and operational quality. Lead and develop cross-functional teams supporting marketing, recruitment, admissions, operations, business development, and programme administration. Prepare reports and recommendations on recruitment, financial performance, student experience, operational risks, partnerships, pricing, and programme improvement. ​ Requirements: Must-Have Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university. At least 10-15 years of relevant experience , including 5 years in a leadership role , with strong expertise in strategic leadership, business development, executive programme management, recruitment, admissions, and stakeholder engagement. Significant relevant experience in executive education, EMBA, MBA, business school programmes, corporate training, executive learning, professional education, or a related field. Proven experience in at least several of the following areas: marketing, recruitment, admissions, programme operations, business development, corporate client management, student experience, or stakeholder engagement. Experience working with senior executives, faculty members, alumni, corporate clients, and senior internal stakeholders. Strong leadership, communication, stakeholder management, project management, problem-solving, and operational skills. Strong financial and performance management capability, including budget monitoring, revenue tracking, reporting, and resource planning. Proficiency in both English and Chinese for professional communication to support engagement with English-speaking and Chinese-speaking students, alumni, corporate clients, partners, and other stakeholders. Ability to support evening or weekend programme activities and travel where required. Good-to-Have MBA, EMBA, Master’s degree, or postgraduate qualification in business, education, management, marketing, or a related discipline. Experience in a university, business school, executive education provider, corporate academy, consulting firm, or professional services environment. Experience developing short courses, certificate programmes, or executive workshops. Regional or international market exposure. Key Competencies Executive education expertise. Strategic programme leadership. Marketing, recruitment, and admissions capability. Business development and corporate client management. Programme operations and delivery excellence. Financial and performance management. Student experience and stakeholder engagement. Team leadership and cross-functional collaboration. Senior-level communication and influencing skills. Data-informed decision-making. Performance Indicators Global EMBA applications and enrolments. Quality of admitted candidates. Recruitment conversion rate. Programme revenue and budget performance. Marketing return on investment. Student satisfaction and Net Promoter Score. Alumni engagement and referral rate. Corporate client engagement. Operational quality and service standards. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Head--Strategic-Planning---Engagement--NIE-_R00025562": {
      "title": "Assistant Head, Strategic Planning & Engagement [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Assistant Head, Strategic Planning & Engagement in the department of Strategic Planning & Engagement (SPE), NIE Director’s Office. Responsibilities Assist the HOD in overseeing and executing NIE’s strategic planning and engagement processes through ─ Providing effective secretariat support and follow-through for key leadership and board meetings to drive effective executive-level decision-making.  Developing, monitoring, communicating and reporting on institutional strategic initiatives and success indicators. Conceptualising, organising and managing appropriate strategic engagement activities for the NIE senior leadership, appointment holders and senior staff – including leadership retreats, annual strategic reviews, annual addresses, etc. Supporting and facilitating specific cross-institutional project initiatives arising from the Strategic Plan such as Steering Committees / Taskforces / Programme Reviews / Strategic Projects. Support the HOD in the management of NIE-level intellectual property. Support the HOD in the management of the office, which may include the department’s budget, assets and physical spaces. Assist in special or ad-hoc projects / institutional events as assigned by the HOD / reporting officer. Requirements A University degree. Minimally 3 to 5 years of relevant working experience with a strong interest and/or track record in strategic planning, organisational development and/or copywriting and editing. Excellent conceptualisation and analytical skills. Excellent written communication and copywriting skills. Highly meticulous and able to analyse / make sense of large quantities of text and numerical information on a daily basis. Working knowledge of statistics and/or data analysis an advantage. Some working knowledge of corporate work planning and budgeting at the organisation level will be useful. High proficiency in MS Office with some working knowledge of document / information management systems. Strong team player with a pleasant disposition. Strong ability to work independently under pressure and to meet tight timelines. Willingness to learn and develop capabilities and to acquire and share new knowledge. Values and attributes demonstrating integrity, professionalism and a service mentality. Working experience in a public-funded educational institution would be advantageous. Application Closing Date 4 Sep 2026 Application We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other information NIE Staff can take chartered buses at their own expenses from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Faculty-Ops---Support_R00025423": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Faculty Ops & Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager (Faculty Operations & Support) role in the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) is responsible for managing and coordinating the School’s administrative operations, facilities and space management, examination support, resource management and operational improvement initiatives. The role works closely with faculty, staff, university departments, internal stakeholders and external vendors to ensure smooth delivery of services, effective resource utilisation and compliance with institutional policies and procedures. Job Responsibilities: Oversee daily administrative operations, including office services, room and space administration, access management, enquiries management and service delivery standards.  Manage office space planning, renovation works, relocation projects, furniture procurement, maintenance coordination and facilities improvement initiatives.  Oversee asset management, inventory records, access control and shared facilities to ensure proper accountability and compliance.  Manage stakeholder and vendor relationships to support procurement, maintenance, events and operational activities.  Develop and improve SOPs, workflows and operational processes to enhance efficiency and service quality.  Prepare operational reports, analyse data and provide recommendations to support management decision-making.  Coordinate examination administration and logistics, including venue arrangements, examination processes and quality assurance activities  Ensure compliance with university policies, governance requirements, safety procedures and audit requirements.  Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree from a recognised university.  At least 3 to 5 years of relevant experience in administration, operations, facilities management or a similar role, preferably in a higher education or large organisational environment.  Experience in managing administrative operations, facilities coordination, project coordination and stakeholder engagement.  Strong organisational, analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities.  Good knowledge of procurement processes, vendor management, compliance requirements and operational procedures.  Proficient in Microsoft Office applications; experience with enterprise systems will be advantageous.  Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at all levels. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Head--Strategy_R00025440": {
      "title": "Head, Strategy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil & Environmental Engineering (CEE) is seeking a dynamic and strategic leader to serve as Head, Strategy . Reporting directly to the School Chair, you will be a key member of the School's leadership team, driving strategic planning, organisational excellence, and operational effectiveness. You will provide strategic oversight of the School's administrative, financial, and operational functions while partnering with academic and administrative leaders to translate the School's vision into actionable plans. The role is instrumental in strengthening governance, optimising resources, enhancing organisational performance, and enabling the successful delivery of the School's academic, research, and outreach priorities. Job Responsibilities: Lead the development, implementation, and review of the School's strategic and operational plans.  Partner with the School Chair and leadership team to drive strategic initiatives and organisational transformation.  Oversee the School's administrative, financial, governance, and operational functions to ensure efficient and effective service delivery.  Develop and monitor organisational performance indicators, providing data-driven insights to support strategic decision-making.  Lead budgeting, resource planning, and financial stewardship to optimise resource utilisation.  Strengthen governance frameworks, risk management, and policy compliance across the School.  Drive process improvement, organisational effectiveness, and service excellence through innovation and continuous improvement.  Build collaborative partnerships with University stakeholders, industry partners, and external agencies to support the School's strategic objectives.  Lead and develop the School's professional services team, fostering a high-performing, collaborative, and customer-focused culture. Job Requirements: A recognised bachelor's degree; a postgraduate qualification in Business Administration, Public Administration, Higher Education, or a related discipline is advantageous.  At least 10–12 years of relevant experience in strategic planning, organisational development, administration, or operations, with 8 years in a leadership or managerial role.  Demonstrated experience in leading organisation-wide strategic initiatives, change management, and cross-functional projects.  Strong understanding of governance, financial planning, budgeting, and organisational performance management.  Excellent analytical, strategic thinking, and problem-solving skills with the ability to translate strategy into execution.  Proven ability to engage and influence senior stakeholders across diverse functions.  Strong communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills.  Experience in the higher education or public sector environment will be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Administrative-Support_R00024956": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Protective Technology Research Centre (PTRC) is seeking a highly organised, proactive, and motivated Senior Executive to join our administrative team and play a key role in supporting the Centre's research, academic, and operational activities. Reporting to the Centre Director, the successful candidate will provide comprehensive administrative, coordination, and secretariat support to the Centre and its research team. This role offers the opportunity to work closely with researchers, students, university stakeholders, collaborator, funding agencies and external partners, contributing to a vibrant and intellectually stimulating research environment. As an integral member of the Centre's administrative team, the successful candidate will help ensure the smooth and efficient delivery of research programmes, collaborative initiatives, and academic activities. Through effective coordination, accurate record management, and proactive stakeholder engagement, the role contributes to the Centre's mission of advancing high-quality research, fostering interdisciplinary collaboration, and supporting research excellence. Key Responsibilities: Provide executive and administrative support to the Centre Director, including managing schedules, coordinating appointments, and facilitating engagement with internal and external stakeholders. Organize and coordinate meetings, workshops, and events, including scheduling, preparation of agendas and meeting materials, recording minutes, and monitoring follow-up actions. Support the financial administration of research projects by maintaining accurate records, tracking expenditures, and ensuring timely updates of project-related financial information. Coordinate contract renewal processes for research staff, including monitoring key timelines, preparing documentation, and liaising with relevant university departments. Support recruitment activities for research staff, including preparing job advertisements, coordinating interviews, managing candidate documentation, and working closely with Human Resources team throughout the hiring process. Facilitate administrative support for exchange students, serving as a key point of contact and coordinating necessary documentation and arrangements. Act as a liaison between the Centre and university offices, research collaborators, funding agencies, industry partners, and other external stakeholders to ensure smooth administrative operations. Maintain accurate and well-organized records relating to meetings, research finance, staff administration, student matters, and general office operations, ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. Contribute to the efficient day-to-day operations of the Centre by proactively identifying administrative needs and supporting continuous process improvement initiatives. Requirements: Diploma or Bachelor's degree in any discipline. At least 2–3 years of relevant experience in administrative, executive support, secretarial, or office management roles. Experience in academic, research, higher education, or project administration will be an advantage. Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to prioritise tasks effectively and manage multiple deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to interact professionally with a diverse range of stakeholders. Meticulous and detail-oriented, particularly in managing documentation, financial records, and administrative processes. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Self-motivated and able to work independently while maintaining regular communication and updates with stakeholders. Professional, dependable, and able to exercise discretion when handling confidential and sensitive information. Strong interpersonal skills and a collaborative mindset, with the ability to work effectively with faculty members, researchers, students, university offices, internal and external stakeholders. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Affairs_R00025192": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) in NTU is a World-leading school in sustainability. The School plays an integral role in advancing research innovations and providing professional services in a number of key disciplines in Civil and Environmental Engineering, with the objective of contributing to the technological and economic advancement of Singapore and beyond.  Job Purpose: The Senior Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs provides strategic and operational leadership in managing all faculty-related activities within the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE). The role oversees faculty recruitment and appointment, culture and development, space and infrastructure, and operations, ensuring that faculty are well-supported in the areas of teaching, research, service and career development. This position plays a critical role in shaping faculty experience, enhancing engagement, and ensuring alignment with the School’s strategic objectives.  Key Responsibilities: 1. Faculty Recruitment, Appointment and Reappointment Lead and manage the end-to-end faculty recruitment lifecycle, including recruitment, appointments, onboarding, appraisal, promotion, and reappointment. Develop and implement recruitment strategies to attract and retain high-calibre academic talent. Ensure all faculty appointment processes are accurate, efficient, and compliant with University policies, governance requirements, and timelines. Drive continuous process improvements to deliver a seamless and positive experience for faculty and stakeholders. 2. Faculty Development, Culture & Engagement Drive initiatives to foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing faculty culture. Lead the annual faculty performance appraisal process from planning to completion, ensuring timely completion, data integrity, data confidentiality, fairness and compliance with institutional policies.  Support faculty career development, leadership development and succession planning initiatives. Manage faculty welfare and case matters, including well-being, peer-to-peer issues, and student-faculty matters. 3. Space & Infrastructure Planning Lead the planning and management of faculty offices, researcher workspaces, research-focused laboratories, and shared facilities to optimize space utilization and support the School’s academic and research priorities.  Support policy development, strategic planning, data analysis, and documentation related to space and infrastructure management.  4. Stakeholder Management & Governance Serve as the primary liaison for faculty affairs-related queries from the Chair and senior leadership. Coordinate with College of Engineering to ensure consistent implementation of faculty-related policies, procedures and strategic initiatives. Engage with HR, finance, and administrative teams to align faculty affairs with broader institutional goals. 5. Strategic Planning, Data Management & Operations     Maintain accurate and up-to-date faculty records and databases to support budgeting, reporting, and strategic decision-making. Analyse faculty-related data and prepare management reports, dashboards, presentations, and briefing materials for senior leadership. Identify opportunities for continuous process improvement through data analysis and operational review. Provide operational guidance and support to team members, contributing to an effective, collaborative, and service-oriented work environment. Qualifications: A recognised Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD degree (or equivalent) with at least 5 years of relevant experience in people management, faculty administration, human resources, or a related field. Strong organisational, planning, and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Excellent stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships across all levels. Ability to balance strategic thinking with hands-on operational execution. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a data-driven approach to decision-making. High level of integrity, professionalism, and discretion in managing confidential and sensitive information. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Digital-IC-design-and-EDA-_R00025569": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Digital IC design and EDA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to focus on open-source processor and accelerator architectures. The role focuses on advancing research in integrated circuit (IC) design and electronic design automation (EDA), with particular emphasis on RISC-V based processors, AI accelerators, and open-source hardware toolchains. The Research Fellow contributes to the University’s mission by conducting high-impact research, developing innovative hardware architectures and design methodologies, and disseminating research outcomes through publications, collaborations, and open-source contributions. Key Responsibilities: Conduct independent and collaborative research on open-source processor architectures and hardware accelerators, including RISC-V based designs. Design, implement, and evaluate digital ICs using Verilog/SystemVerilog and related hardware description languages. Develop and optimize EDA workflows for processor and accelerator design, verification, and physical implementation using open-source tools. Explore architecture-algorithm co-design for machine learning and AI acceleration. Perform performance, power, and area (PPA) analysis of processor and accelerator designs. Publish research findings in top-tier conferences and journals and contribute to open-source hardware and EDA communities. Supervise and mentor PhD students, junior Research Assistants, and Master students. Collaborate with faculty members, graduate students, and external partners, and support research project execution and reporting. Job Requirements: A completed PhD in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a closely related discipline. Strong research expertise in RISC-V architecture, processor microarchitecture, and AI accelerators. Experience with ASIC design methodologies and open-source IC design and EDA tools. Proven experience in digital hardware design using Verilog/SystemVerilog or equivalent HDLs. Sound knowledge of machine learning algorithms and their hardware implementation considerations. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent, high-quality research and publish in reputable venues. Demonstrated ability to lead research projects, supervise researchers, and mentor junior staff. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively. Good written and oral communication skills. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Research-Assistant--NMPs-_R00025571": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (NMPs)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGlobally recognized as a leading research and technology organization, the Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI) addresses national priorities through its diverse expertise in Biotechnology and Bioprocesses, Membrane Technology, Chemicals and Materials, Resource Recovery, and Modeling & Artificial Intelligence. By harnessing its cross-cutting, interdisciplinary, and transformative capabilities, NEWRI drives innovation in water circularity and sustainability, next-generation solid waste solutions, circular economy resource recovery, climate resilience and digitalization. For more details, please view NEWRI website . We are looking for a Research Assistant to support the research for the project titled: Novel approaches for nano-microplastics (NMPs) characterization in water systems in Singapore – NMPWaterSG. The role will focus on detecting nano-microplastics and contribute to establishing standard methods for detecting nano-microplastics in Singapore. Key Responsibilities: Work synergistically with the RFs and assist the PI and Co-PIs in experimental designs, conducting experiments, and troubleshooting. Understand and follow the experimental protocols. Perform experiments on on-site sampling of nano-microplastics in different water sources. Operate instruments such as tubular furnace, muffle furnace, laser direct infrared (LDIR), Raman, thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) and pyrolysis–gas chromatography–mass spectrometry (Py-GCMS). Process and analyze the data from the instruments Assist in summarizing the findings in this project and produce the progress reports, final report and scientific recommendations. Job Requirements: B.Eng./B.Sc. in analytical chemistry, environmental engineering, chemistry or a relevant field. Good analytical chemistry experimental operation skills, especially analytical testing. Extensive knowledge of chemistry and analytical techniques. High motivation and strong responsibility for research and development. Good interpersonal skills. Good report writing and communication skills. Excellent teamwork awareness. Productive, hard-working and dedicated to the completion of any task assigned. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Organic-Synthesis-Laboratory-_R00025194": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Organic Synthesis Laboratory)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) is a newly established interdisciplinary joint school under College of Engineering and College of Science at NTU Singapore.  The Nicewicz group in CCEB is pursing development of new sustainable molecular transformations for the synthesis of complex small molecules.  The Nicewicz’s group is seeking to hire a Project Officer to facilitate the group’s research. Key Responsibilities: The candidate will be expected: to maintain the progress of the respective research projects by monitoring the usage of consumables and conditions of laboratory assets. to manage the purchase, procurement, and safety matters of the group. to assist the data collection of the ongoing project to arrange weekly group meetings Job Requirements: BSc in Chemistry Skills and experiences in handling of various reagents and solvents in synthetic organic chemistry We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--AIEH-_R00025566": {
      "title": "AI Engineer (AIEH)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. The AI Engineering Hub (AIEH) aims to promote AI usage in the industry by developing AI solutions for companies. These industry engagements also serve as real-world projects for the AI Apprenticeship Programme (AIAP), which is dedicated to groom local AI talent and enhance their career with AI-related skills. We are seeking an AI Engineer to join the AIEH team. In this role, you will mentor AIAP apprentices by guiding project delivery, defining industry-relevant use cases, and providing technical coaching on cutting-edge AI technologies. You will also contribute to the development of innovative AI solutions and internal technology initiatives. The incumbent will collaborate with external partners to identify meaningful project opportunities while balancing development work with talent nurturing responsibilities, playing a key role in strengthening Singapore's AI ecosystem. Duties & Responsibilities: Drive and work on tasks stemming from AIEH industry partnership projects and other AIAP-related programmes. Lead end-to-end solution development for industry AI projects, from scoping to deployment and maintenance. Train and mentor AI apprentices during the Deep-skilling and Project phase, and other umbrella programmes. Collaborate with industry partners to identify, scope, and define project requirements and deliverables. Conduct technical assessments and feasibility studies for potential industry collaborations. Participate, prepare and execute the AIAP recruitment stages. Support AI Singapore’s industry and community-building activities by contributing to talks, seminars, workshops, journals and other outreach programmes. Requirements: Degree with at least 4 years of work experience. We welcome applicants from all disciplines who can demonstrate the following skills: End-to-End Project Delivery: Have a strong portfolio of AI/ML project(s) that showcases ability to deliver solutions from scoping and data analysis through deployment and documentation. Applied Machine Learning:  Possess deep, practical knowledge of machine learning fundamentals, with proven experience applying algorithms to solve problems in areas like NLP, Computer Vision, or on tabular data. Generative AI & LLMs:  Hands-on experience developing LLM-powered applications, including Prompt Engineering, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and fine-tuning using modern frameworks. Software Engineering Excellence:  Demonstrates expert-level Python skills and a strong commitment to Software Engineering best practices, writing code that is clean, modular, and maintainable. MLOps & Cloud Proficiency:  Fluent in the essential MLOps toolkit, including Git, Docker, and CI/CD principles. Have experience building data and model pipelines on at least one major cloud platform (AWS, Azure, or GCP). Passionate Mentor:  Eager to guide and develop the next generation of AI talent, contributing to AISG Innovation’s collaborative and supportive team culture. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Civil-Engineering-_R00025565": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Civil Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU, CEE is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. We are looking for a  research fellow to support the development of algorithms for anomaly detection, simulate and test it on Reinforced Concrete (RC) substructures. Key Responsibilities: Simulate RC substructures under different boundary conditions. Design and fabricate test models. Develop algorithms for anomaly detections. Publish several papers in top journals. Write proposals for further development. Mentor students. Job Requirements: PhD degree in civil engineering or related field At least 1 year of relevant experience in structural health monitoring and simulation. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in ABAQUS , and lab test skill Ability to work independently and develop solutions under strict timelines We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Horticulture-and-Plant-Physiology-_R00024028": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Horticulture and Plant Physiology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) at NTU Singapore, in collaboration with Wageningen University & Research (WUR), is part of the Singapore Indoor Farming System (SingFarm)—a CREATE-NRF programme focused on building a sustainable, data-driven food production model with strong industry relevance. The programme contributes to Singapore’s ambition of achieving 20 per cent local production of its fibre (vegetables, mushrooms, etc.) by 2035. The candidate will work in a multinational team at the forefront of Singapore’s agricultural innovation and food security. The Research Associate will take on a significant role in developing and applying simulation and machine learning models for Asian leafy vegetables to predict growth, transpiration, resource use, and yield under controlled environments, with a focus on production under higher temperature and humidity. The Research Associate will also build self-learning models using continuous sensor data, calibrate and validate them with experimental datasets, and collaborate with project partners to support predictive climate and crop control strategies for indoor farming in Singapore. Key Responsibilities: Conduct climate room experiments by varying environmental conditions for the growth of pak choi Develop, calibrate, and validate an explanatory, dynamic crop growth model for pak choi Write scientific papers and participate in international conferences Job Requirements: A Master’s degree in plant science, biology, agronomy, or related fields ​ Strong command of written and communication skills Knowledge of plant and crop physiology Experience or a demonstrated interest in a quantitative approach to crop growth Knowledge or experience in programming is preferred Strong presentation skills for both academic and non-academic audiences Good collaboration skills and ability to work effectively in a team We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Sustainable-Batteries-_R00025561": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Sustainable Batteries)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterization Materials Science, Defense Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . We are seeking a Senior Research Fellow to conduct research on sustainable battery technologies, including aqueous batteries, solid-state batteries, and other emerging battery systems. The role will focus on establishing and leading the existing battery research team and expanding research activities in sustainable batteries, working closely with our research team and collaborators to advance materials development and mechanistic understanding. Demonstrating capability, creativity and high-impact outcomes in sustainable batteries will be a key requirement. The Senior Research Fellow will also contribute to the development of shared laboratory platforms, actively pursue external research funding from government and industry , mentor junior researchers, and interpret research results for academic publications and technical reports. The position also requires collaboration with international team members and support for project coordination, documentation, and dissemination of research outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Lead the research and development of next-generation sustainable battery systems. Purchase, manage, maintain, and service laboratory and equipment. Prepare and contribute to grant applications and conference presentations. Assist or produce high quality research results in top journals relevant to materials sciences and energy. Supervise and mentor junior researchers, research engineers, and postdoc researchers within the team. Engage and communicate with existing or future industrial and academic collaborators to advance the developed technologies from lab-scale verification to pilot implementation. Job Requirements: Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, or a closely related discipline. Strong research background in electrochemical energy systems, with demonstrated expertise in aqueous batteries, metal-air batteries, or related electrochemical technologies. At least 10 years of research experience in sustainable energy storage technologies or related areas. Demonstrated leadership experience in leading multidisciplinary research projects. Excellent track record of publications in reputable peer-reviewed journals and presentations at international conferences. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with team members and collaborators. Experience in project management and coordinating research activities across multiple workstreams. Strong passion for research and addressing real-world sustainability challenges in energy storage and conversion. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Autonomous-Materials-Discovery-_R00025560": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Autonomous Materials Discovery)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defense Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . MLab is seeking a Research Fellow to support the development and establishment of a robotic and autonomous laboratory for accelerated materials discovery and battery research. The role will focus on assisting with the integration of automated materials synthesis, sample handling, characterization, electrochemical testing, and data acquisition into coordinated experimental workflows. The Research Fellow will contribute to the development of high-throughput and autonomous experimentation platforms, including robotic systems, laboratory automation, and AI/machine learning-assisted approaches for experimental design, optimization, and materials discovery. The research will target advanced materials and interfaces for solid-state batteries, aqueous batteries, and other emerging energy-storage technologies. The successful candidate will work closely with senior researchers, engineers, software developers, and collaborators to establish automated experimental protocols, optimize materials synthesis and screening processes, develop reliable data pipelines, and integrate experimental results with data-driven and machine-learning models. The role will also involve conducting materials synthesis and electrochemical studies, troubleshooting and improving automated workflows, analyzing research data, and contributing to research publications, technical reports, and project deliverables. Key Responsibilities: Support the development and operation of autonomous laboratory platforms for materials discovery. Conduct automated materials synthesis, characterization, electrochemical testing, and data analysis for battery systems. Participate in project planning, data collection and analysis to generate high-quality, reproducible research outcomes. Prepare manuscripts for publication in high-impact journals and contribute to grant proposals and research reports. Report on research progress and/or literature update in scheduled group meetings and individual meetings. Support the overall research mission of the lab by contributing to technology development, knowledge dissemination, and translational opportunities. Job Requirements: Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field. Research experience in battery materials, electrochemistry, or materials synthesis. Experience and knowledge with robotic systems, high-throughput experimentation, or autonomous laboratory development. Demonstrated scientific productivity (peer-reviewed publications). Strong hands-on experimental and problem-solving skills, with the ability to develop, integrate, and troubleshoot automated research workflows. Good communication and teamwork skills, with the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Learning-Strategist---Learning-Strategist--Centre-for-Innovation-in-Learning---NIE-_R00025558-1": {
      "title": "Senior Learning Strategist / Learning Strategist (Centre for Innovation in Learning) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . We are seeking a pedagogically minded and dedicated Senior Learning Strategist / Learning Strategist. Reporting to the Learning Strategist Manager, the appointee collaborates with faculties to design and develop cutting-edge blended learning experiences, providing strategic guidance for implementing innovative digital teaching and learning practices across NIE. Additionally, the appointee will work closely with fellow Learning Strategists and the other teams in the department to research, develop, and present innovative and pedagogically sound design solutions to stakeholders, in pursuit of enhanced practice and outcomes. The candidate should be familiar with the training and adult education landscape, be adept at facilitation and possess a commitment to staying up to date on higher education best practices. This is a 2-year contract position. Responsibilities Build Evidence-Based Innovation in Teaching & Learning within NIE Collaborate with fellow Learning Strategists to: Research adult learning theories, strategies, data, and appropriate educational technology tools to design, develop, and facilitate impactful face-to-face and online tech-enhanced workshops for faculty. Assess the learning needs of IN-Learning specialists in learning design and emerging technology. Design, develop, and facilitate engaging initiatives to support IN-Learning specialists in building their expertise in learning design and emerging technology. Collaborate with NIE faculty to: Identify learning needs for courses they teach. Propose frameworks, new/enhanced learning outcomes, tech-enabled teaching and learning strategies, and assessments as part of course redesigning. Propose appropriate educational technology to overcome gaps and enhance the learning outcomes of the courses.  Achieve constructive alignment of the learning outcomes with the learning activities and assessment in their courses. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to: Assess faculty capability development needs through qualitative and quantitative data analysis, to inform their work in designing, developing, and evaluating learner-centered blended learning experiences and fostering assessment literacy. Research, develop and present evidence-based and innovative design solutions with the project team to stakeholders.  Research and evaluate frameworks and educational technology tools for implementation to optimize and innovate teaching, learning and assessment practices in NIE. Research, write grant proposals and develop tech-enabled learning solutions. Work together on initiatives with IN-Learning's Engagement, Planning and Research team to share learning sciences knowledge and improve practices institute-wide. Carry out action research by: conceptualizing frameworks and methodologies  designing evaluation instruments  gathering and analyzing data (e.g. Learning Analytics) formulating decisions to improve the effectiveness of learning experiences and our Capability Development initiatives Contribute to special projects on teaching and learning, as required. Keep Up with Learning Sciences and Innovative Teaching and Learning Practices Stay current on learning sciences, innovative teaching and learning practices in higher education (e.g., personalized learning, adaptive learning, e-assessment, hybrid learning, learning analytics, and Artificial Intelligence).  Foster a culture of continuous learning within the team by providing opportunities for professional development and encouraging knowledge sharing. Requirements A University degree, preferably in Instructional Design, Education or Learning Sciences and Technologies. A minimum of 2 years of experience in instructional design, teaching and learning, within a higher educational setting or with adult learners. Proven ability to manage successful learning projects. To be considered for the Senior Learning Strategist position, candidates should possess at least 5 years of experience in instructional design, teaching, learning, and the adult education landscape. Possess a proven track record of managing complex learning projects. Demonstrate experience in a mentorship role and in leading complex projects. Expert knowledge of applying Adult Learning theories in the design of Blended Learning experiences. Possess strong research skills. Proven track record in designing and facilitating faculty development workshops for diverse audiences. Possess strong written, verbal, and presentation skills. Strong knowledge of emerging educational technologies for teaching and learning. Excellent time management skills to meet multiple deadlines simultaneously and consistently deliver high-quality results. Excellent organizational and project management skills. Experience in facilitating both face-to-face and online sessions. Familiarity with Learning Management System and a demonstrated ability to rapidly learn new tools and processes with minimal support. Demonstrate excellent interpersonal skills and strong problem-solving abilities. Highly motivated, able to work independently yet also a strong team player. A strong desire to learn, acquire, and share new knowledge. Maintain a positive attitude and work effectively under pressure to meet deadlines. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 3 Sep 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Senior-Executive--Alumni-Engagement_R00025554": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Senior Executive, Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. We invite suitable candidates to apply for Assistant Manager / Senior Executive, Alumni Engagement. The incumbent will support the Alumni Engagement Team at CCDS including furthering the relationship between CCDS and alumni, supporting initiatives that tap on the strength of our alumni to support our student body and ensuring the successful running of alumni events. Job Responsibilities: Alumni Engagement Activities Oversee, manage and support events together with the CCDS Alumni Association (CCDS AA) Facilitate meetings with relevant Alumni stakeholders Plan, organize and provide support for students and alumni activities and events Manage news write-ups and social media platforms to enhance CCDS Alumni Office’s engagement with existing students and alumni Serve as a point of contact to build enduring relationships with the CCDS AA and individual alumni to encourage ongoing involvement Address all alumni enquiries and coordinate engagement opportunities Alumni Strategies Design and implement comprehensive alumni engagement strategies that align with College’s interests and strengthen the alumni network Regularly assess alumni interests and motivations and create clear metrics that evaluate the success of events along with conducting continuous improvement proposals for future events Report and propose improvements to existing alumni strategies to the respective Alumni Leads Continuous Improvement Create clear metrics that evaluate the success of alumni events Conduct After Action Reviews (AARs) on all alumni events Establish SOPs for the running of events, budgeting and work responsibilities between CCDS AA and the College Improve existing SOPs to increase alumni engagement and efficacy of alumni programmes Maintain and update the Alumni SharePoint to ensure accurate documentation General Departmental Support Provide support across various departmental tasks and events within the College Coordinate logistics for departmental events and activities Address inquiries and assist the Deanery, faculty, students, and alumni   Alumni Finance Matters Monitor departmental budget, review allocated fund utilization and expenditure  Recommend purchases which align with the department’s needs Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree with at least 5 years of work experience in stakeholder management and partnership development. Working knowledge of event management, with experience in planning and executing large-scale events considered an advantage. Experience in stakeholder engagement and industry partnership management will be highly valued. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications and database management systems. Comfortable learning and working with new data and event management platforms. Able to work independently while contributing effectively in a team environment. Strong communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills. Willing to work weekends when required to support student and alumni events. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Corporate-Communications-Executive--RSIS-_R00025546": {
      "title": "Senior Corporate Communications Executive [RSIS]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe S. Rajaratnam School of International Studies (RSIS) , a Graduate School of Nanyang Technological University (NTU), is a leading professional school of international affairs and policy-oriented think tank. The School invites suitably qualified individuals for the position of: Senior Corporate Communications Executive The Senior Corporate Communications Executive reports to the Head of Corporate Communications, and is responsible for driving excellence in corporate communications for RSIS, in areas such as digital content and strategy, branding, and publicity, alongside other adjacent areas such as corporate merchandise, videography and photography. Applicants who possess additional necessary skillsets and longer relevant working experience may be considered for a higher appointment at Assistant Manager. This includes the following areas: Design and execute digital communications strategies across digital media, to build brand awareness/branding, which includes conceptualising short-term and long-haul plans to increase the branding and reputation of RSIS; Create, edit, and publish digital content (e.g. social media visuals and graphics, photos, videos, podcasts, etc.) across RSIS social media channels and website; Managing and working alongside external contracted vendors, and assist in corporate photography and videography on an as-needed basis; Manage the repository of photos and videos for archival purposes through documentation and categorisation, and assist in retrieval of material as and when required; Manage the inventory and sales of RSIS corporate merchandise, including the production of one-off merchandise for special occasions; Collaborate with other departments to manage RSIS branding; Assist in production of RSIS publications such as the annual review and newsletters. Requirements A relevant Bachelor’s degree in areas such as mass communications, journalism, art and design, digital marketing, etc.; Minimum 4-5 years of relevant experience in corporate communications, in areas such as social media, public relations, digital communications, and/or digital marketing. Prior experience in digital agencies and publication houses will be advantageous; Prior experience in strategic-level digital communications, such as storyboarding videos, designing communications campaigns for evergreen publicity and crisis management, and identifying emerging trends and new best practices for social media; Prior experience in event photography and videography, including the ability to conceptualise a storyboard and shoot and edit short-format reels for social media, is highly preferred; Strong application with popular social media platforms (Facebook, Twitter, YouTube, LinkedIn, etc.), including understanding social media metrics and being able to interpret analytics to increase effectiveness of RSIS digital strategy; Excellent analytical and time-management skills, with the ability to oversee and/or manage multiple projects Versatile team-player who is able to collaborate with other departments to achieve desired outcomes All applicants should submit the following: •       A cover letter specifying how your qualifications match the job description and why you will be a good fit for who we are looking for; •       A detailed CV, including any relevant portfolio of work (e.g. photography and videography work, social media posts done, etc.)  We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For further information about RSIS, please visit our website: www.rsis.edu.sg . Hiring Institution: RSIS"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--MSc-Programmes_R00024834": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, MSc Programmes",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) is seeking a Senior Executive to support the administration and operations of postgraduate coursework programmes. The role will be responsible for managing end-to-end programme operations, including academic services, admissions, examinations, and student engagement, while ensuring efficient processes, compliance with university policies, and a high-quality student experience. Key Responsibilities: Academic Services & Programme Delivery Manage programme lifecycle, including course registration, candidature, and graduation matters Support curriculum planning, OBTL submissions, and academic scheduling Coordinate internship and research project courses Maintain accurate documentation and records across academic and administrative functions Support data management, reporting, and administrative processes Admissions & Enrolment Administration Monitor admission cycle and track application, offer, and acceptance stages Verify applicant documentation and support admission processing Coordinate admission and/or scholarship interviews Maintain accurate admission records and track enrolment Examinations & Academic Governance Support examination processes, including marklists preparation and documentation Perform script checks, marks entry, and ensure accuracy Coordinate examination logistics and support invigilation Assist in handling academic misconduct cases Student Engagement, Outreach & Events Support planning and execution of student engagement activities and programme events Assist in outreach activities such as information sessions and networking events Coordinate event communications and logistics Requirements: Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in any discipline At least 2 to 3 years of relevant work experience in tertiary education preferred IT knowledge, proficient in MS office applications Familiarity with academic administration systems preferred Strong organisational, analytical, and coordination skills Meticulous, responsible, and able to work independently as well as in a team We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Assistant-Manager--Procurement_R00025290": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Procurement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU and the Role Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading global university known for its strong emphasis on education, research, and innovation. NTU is committed to excellence, sustainability, and creating positive impact for society through strong governance and responsible stewardship of resources. Why Join NTU At NTU, you will be part of a collaborative and professional work environment that values continuous learning. We are seeking a Senior Executive to join NSS Procurement. This role offers the opportunity to work closely with multiple Schools and Departments, drive meaningful procurement improvements, and contribute directly to the University’s operational excellence. Why this role is attractive: Exposure to a wide range of procurement categories and stakeholders Opportunity to drive process improvements and cost efficiencies A role that combines strategic thinking, stakeholder engagement, and hands‑on execution Job Description The Senior Executive is responsible for ensuring that procurement activities are carried out efficiently, cost‑effectively, and in full compliance with University policies and guidelines. The role supports partner Schools and Departments by managing end‑to‑end procurement activities across multiple spend categories. Key responsibilities include: Manage & lead the RFI/ RFQ/ RFP processes including development and spearhead of roadmap to meet NTU deliverables Reviewing and improving procurement processes to enhance efficiency, governance, and service delivery Managing supplier sourcing, evaluation, and contract negotiations to achieve value for money Providing procurement advice and guidance to internal stakeholders to ensure clear understanding of processes and requirements Conducting spend analysis to identify consolidation and cost‑saving opportunities Ensuring all procurement activities and contracts comply with institutional policies and regulatory requirements Building and maintaining strong working relationships with internal users and external suppliers Qualifications Must ‑ Have Requirements 4 to 7 years of relevant procurement experience in direct and/or indirect procurement Strong understanding of end‑to‑end procurement processes, including sourcing, tendering, and contract management Good knowledge of procurement governance, compliance, and policy requirements Strong analytical skills with the ability to perform spend analysis and develop practical recommendations Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently while collaborating effectively with others Good ‑ to ‑ Have Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Supply Chain Management, or a related discipline Experience with electronic procurement systems (for example, Ariba or similar platforms) Exposure to process improvement, automation, or data‑driven procurement initiatives Experience working in a large or complex organisation We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Strategic-Sourcing_R00022975": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Strategic Sourcing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nResponsibilities: Category Management / Strategic Sourcing Category strategy development: Developing and implementing strategic plans for various categories, aligning it with the NTU's overall goals and objectives. This involves analyzing market trends, identifying opportunities for growth, and setting performance targets. Supplier relationship management: Build strong and collaborative partnerships with suppliers to optimize value, reduce risks, and drive mutual success. This includes selecting and onboarding suppliers, negotiating contracts, managing performance, and fostering collaboration and innovation. Conduct market research and analysis to understand the dynamics of various categories, including pricing trends, supplier capabilities, emerging technologies, and competitive landscape. This information helps inform decision-making and identify opportunities for improvement. Collaborating with various internal stakeholders to ensure alignment and integration of category strategies with broader organizational objectives. This includes analysis of spending, regular communication, coordination, and joint decision-making in development of overall sourcing strategy/category management plan. Performance measurement and optimization: Developing and monitoring key performance indicators (KPIs) to assess the performance of various categories. This involves tracking metrics such as customer satisfaction, and supplier performance. Leveraging on the details to identify areas for improvement and takes actions to optimize category performance. Continuous improvement and innovation. This includes seeking new ways to enhance product/service offerings, exploring alternative sourcing strategies, and staying updated on industry trends and best practices. Identify and mitigate risks across the entire procurement process. Execute procurement tender process including development and spearhead of tender roadmap to meet NTU deliverables. Requirements: Qualifications/Skills Minimum Diploma / Degree Equivalent Qualification; with 4 - 6 years’ relevant work experience. Proficient in using Microsoft Office Suite of products to perform analytical tasks and quantitative modelling, to present and support recommendations. Functional Competencies Experience and sound knowledge in P2P process. Good to have Preferably with knowledge of financial systems, e.g., SAP and Ariba. Demonstrate project and time management skills and ability to deliver exceptional customer service. Organized, meticulous with excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to work well with multiple competing priorities, manage projects and meet deadlines. A good team player and able to work independently with minimum supervision. Proactive in pursuit of learning and are willing to put in the time and effort required to gain new skills and knowledge. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Purchasing_R00022041": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Purchasing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Senior / Executive is responsible to: Partner with the business and stakeholders to manage and administer all procurement activities. Responsible for quotation and tendering process which includes preparing specifications, calling, evaluation and award of quotations/tenders. Negotiate and coordinate with suppliers and cross-functional departments for best possible price purchase and delivery time with the quality required for the project. Cross-department collaboration to ensure procurement processes are done in adherence to NTU guidelines and policies. All tactical purchases and procurement administrative support includes but not limited to PO processing and contract management. Generate and analyze purchasing reports to identify areas for improvement. Any ad-hoc jobs required by the management. Build positive relationships with peers and supervisors to ensure process efficiency and effectiveness. Partner with the business to drive policy compliance and partner with internal stakeholders to improve efficiencies. Requirements: Minimum Diploma Equivalent Qualification; or Equivalent professional procurement experience with 1 year relevant experience. Demonstrate time management skills and ability to deliver exceptional customer service. Organised, meticulous with excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to work well with multiple competing priorities. A good team player and able to work independently with minimum supervision. Strategic thinking and willingness to go the extra mile to achieve desirable outcome. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive---Senior-Executive--One-stop_R00022043": {
      "title": "Executive / Senior Executive, One-stop",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin our dynamic team as an Executive / Senior Executive at NTU Shared Services, One-Stop. You will be responsible for various student-centric processes including student concession cards, NTU mailroom services, international student pass, student insurance, degree certificate & transcript, letter of certification and addressing diverse student queries received via our One Stop hotlines, counter and emails. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment and are passionate about providing exceptional service to students, we want you on our team! The key responsibilities are:   Handle diverse student enquiries received through One Stop hotlines, emails and counter, providing accurate and prompt assistance. Collaborate with relevant departments to address complex student-related queries and issues effectively. Handle international student pass, adhering to relevant regulations and guidelines. Support other portfolio including student insurance, degree certificate & transcript and letter of certification processes, student concession card, tuition grant and PSEA claim. Cover for NTU mailroom services, overseeing mail distribution and related logistical operations, when required. Draft standard operating procedures (SOPs) for various student services processes, ensuring clarity, consistency, and compliance with institutional policies and regulations. Review and propose updates to knowledge articles, aligned with changes in processes. Participate in ad hoc projects and initiatives aimed at improving student services, contributing expertise and insights to cross-functional teams as needed. Candidate with following experiences may be considered for Senior Executive role: Support the team in managing improvement projects within the department's scope, collaborating with IT and other relevant stakeholders/departments to share painpoints, identify requirements, implement changes, and ensure smooth integration with existing systems. Propose improvements in areas of work related to One-Stop scope, leveraging data analysis and stakeholder feedback to identify opportunities for optimization and efficiency gains. Experience or keen in automating processes using robotic process automation. The final offer will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and relevant experience. This position involves significant engagement with students, staff, and members of the public, and requires the incumbent to be based on campus. Requirements: Minimum Diploma in any discipline. Proficiency in Microsoft Office. Customer Focus: Demonstrated passion for delivering exceptional customer experiences, possessing empathy and a customer-centric mindset. Problem-Solving Aptitude: Strong analytical skills coupled with proactive problem-solving abilities and the capacity for quick decision-making. Interpersonal Skills: Excellent interpersonal abilities for fostering positive relationships, effective collaboration, and a dedication to teamwork. Adaptability: Flexibility to adapt to changing priorities, thrive in a dynamic environment, and manage multiple tasks simultaneously. Time Management: Efficient time management skills, adept at prioritization, and consistently meeting deadlines. Professionalism: Demonstrated professionalism, maintaining confidentiality, and adhering to company policies and procedures. Preferably with prior customer service experience and a genuine passion for assisting others. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Purchasing_R00022040": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Purchasing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Senior / Executive is responsible to: Partner with the business and stakeholders to manage and administer all procurement activities. Responsible for quotation and tendering process which includes preparing specifications, calling, evaluation and award of quotations/tenders. Negotiate and coordinate with suppliers and cross-functional departments for best possible price purchase and delivery time with the quality required for the project. Cross-department collaboration to ensure procurement processes are done in adherence to NTU guidelines and policies. All tactical purchases and procurement administrative support includes but not limited to PO processing and contract management. Generate and analyze purchasing reports to identify areas for improvement. Any ad-hoc jobs required by the management. Build positive relationships with peers and supervisors to ensure process efficiency and effectiveness. Partner with the business to drive policy compliance and partner with internal stakeholders to improve efficiencies. Requirements: Minimum Diploma Equivalent Qualification; or Equivalent professional procurement experience with 1 year relevant experience. Demonstrate time management skills and ability to deliver exceptional customer service. Organised, meticulous with excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to work well with multiple competing priorities. A good team player and able to work independently with minimum supervision. Strategic thinking and willingness to go the extra mile to achieve desirable outcome. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
