    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Lead--Finance--R2R-_R00024966": {
      "title": "Lead, Finance (R2R)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU Shared Services (NSS) Finance delivers end-to-end finance services across the University, supporting operational excellence, governance, and strategic decision-making. The Record-to-Report (R2R) function is a core pillar responsible for financial reporting, accounting integrity, and data governance. This role leads the R2R function covering General Ledger, Fixed Assets and Master Data Management, ensuring accurate and timely financial close and reporting. The position also drives process optimisation, automation, and transformation initiatives, positioning R2R as a strategic finance partner. Success in this role will be reflected in stronger close discipline, improved reporting quality, enhanced data governance, and measurable progress in process optimisation and digitalisation across the R2R function. Why Join This Role This role offers the opportunity to shape the future of R2R within a large, complex university environment, with exposure to enterprise-wide finance transformation, digitalisation and leadership-level decision support. The role combines operational leadership with the mandate to modernise processes, strengthen data and reporting capabilities, and contribute to the next phase of finance shared services at NTU. Key Responsibilities: Lead end-to-end R2R operations, including General Ledger, Fixed Assets and Master Data Management Oversee month-end, quarter-end and year-end financial close, ensuring accuracy, completeness and strong cut-off discipline Manage balance sheet integrity, including reconciliation governance and timely resolution of exceptions Support preparation of management, statutory and audit reports, ensuring reliability and compliance Ensure compliance with accounting standards, taxation requirements (including GST and Withholding Tax reporting validation) and NTU policies Drive review and validation of GST/WHT returns, ensuring alignment with GL and underlying financial data Strengthen financial controls, governance frameworks and audit readiness across R2R processes Drive process improvements, automation and digital initiatives (e.g. RPA, analytics, system enhancements) Oversee finance system governance and data integrity, including master data quality and controls Partner stakeholders (OFIN, Schools, Departments, CITS) to provide accounting advisory and resolve complex issues Lead and develop the R2R team, building strong technical accounting, systems and data capabilities Requirements: Degree in Accountancy or equivalent (CPA/CA preferred) Minimum 10 years of relevant experience in financial reporting / GL / R2R Strong knowledge of: - Financial close and reporting - General Ledger and balance sheet governance - Fixed assets accounting - Accounting standards and GST/WHT principles Experience in leading teams and managing stakeholders Experience as a digital finance change agents on AI-enabled finance processes We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Office-of-Commercial-and-Auxiliary-Services_R00024439": {
      "title": "Director, Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU is seeking an experienced and visionary leader to head its Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS). This senior leadership role is responsible for providing strategic leadership and oversight in the policies and operations relating to hospitality, commercial leasing, real estate management, and auxiliary services. In addition, the Director plays an active role and collaborates with stakeholders to cultivate a vibrant campus culture, involve both students and employees, and foster a strong sense of community. Key Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership for NTU’s hospitality, commercial leasing, real estate, and auxiliary services functions. Drive the transformation of NTU into a vibrant, welcoming, and sustainable environment for students, staff, and the wider community. Lead initiatives to enhance campus life, including F&B offerings, hospitality services, amenities, and community-facing activities. Oversee the University’s hospitality assets and ensure high standards of quality, service excellence, and financial sustainability. Provide strategic oversight of key auxiliary services such as campus transportation and car park operations, working closely with outsourced service providers. Lead the planning, development, and refurbishment of major campus hospitality and lifestyle assets. Develop and manage business strategies to optimise the use of leased assets and maximise revenue from commercial activities. Build strong partnerships with internal and external stakeholders to deliver innovative and value-driven solutions. Identify and manage strategic, financial, and operational risks across all areas under OCAS’s purview. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Hospitality Management, or a related discipline; a Master’s degree is an advantage. A minimum of 18 years of demonstrated experience in commercial leasing, hospitality, events management, community engagement, or university student life, along with a successful history in developing and implementing strategic initiatives and managing large-scale projects. Proven track record in leading transformation and implementing change management. Strong strategic and commercial acumen, with experience in business planning, stakeholder management, and change leadership. Ability to operate effectively in a complex, multi-stakeholder environment. Passion for enhancing campus life and community engagement, with an inclusive and collaborative leadership style. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Guest-Service-Officer--NEC-_R00025243": {
      "title": "Guest Service Officer (NEC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. Currently undergoing refurbishment, the NEC features 150 guestrooms and aims to offer a premier venue for corporate training, retreats and private events. We are looking for a proactive, service-oriented professional to join NEC as Guest Service Officer . As the welcoming face of NEC, you will be responsible for creating exceptional first impressions and delivering personalised service throughout each guest's stay. You will support front desk operations, orientate guests, anticipate their needs, and ensure every touchpoint reflects the NEC's commitment to hospitality excellence. Key Responsibilities Greet and provide a warm welcome to arriving guests to ensure a welcoming first impression. Assist with guest check-in and check-out procedures, coordinate VIP and special guest arrivals and departures, in accordance with established SOPs.   Provide room orientation to the guests and introduce NEC facilities. Manage and coordinate special requests from guests to ensure personalized service delivery (e.g. celebrating special occasions). Collate and document guest feedback into the Property Management System. Ensure the lobby and guest-facing areas are always neat and clean. Proactive in meeting guests requests and needs throughout their stay. Handle guests request and redirect the request to the appropriate department(s) if request is not within scope and capacity of Front Office. Listen to guest’s complaint or concerns and resolve their issue in a timely manner. Be familiar with NTU and NEC facilities and functions as well as major city attractions and events. Provide guests with accurate information as requested. Perform any other duties as may assigned by Duty Manager/Front Office Manager. Requirement Nitec/Higher Nitec/Diploma in Hotel Management or relevant discipline. Experience:  Experience in the hospitality industry with a minimum of 1 year in a similar capacity. Communication Skills:  Good spoken and written communication skills in order to interact well with guest. Professional disposition : Well-groomed, display a professional disposition with strong interpersonal skills. Proactive : Proactive and prompt in meeting guest’s requests and needs. Able to work rotating shifts, including weekends and Public Holidays. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Senior-Executive--Research-Grant-Administration_R00025539": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Senior Executive, Research Grant Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an “exciting place to learn and grow”. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities but are not limited to: To lead and manage a team of MSOs to support the operations of the Research Office. Oversee and manage the research grants administration (including RCAs), research finance, research staff hiring, and ensuring corporate governance of research projects and research integrity. Organise research events (research seminars/conferences/workshops), and handle research industry collaborations. To handle research data reporting (statistics/data required by various offices in NTU, external agencies, government organizations and P&T/contract renewals/faculty appraisals). Job Requirements: At least a bachelor’s degree Preferably with at least 5 years’ experience in research administration/ graduate program management in a tertiary education institution, with at least 3 years of supervisory experience leading a dynamic administrative team. Financial accounting knowledge preferred Strong leadership, stakeholder management and engagement skills Equipped with strong analytical skills with the ability to solve complex issues and work effectively under pressure. Possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills. High level of commitment and initiative. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Mechanical-Materials-Manufacturing-Engineering-_R00025538": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Mechanical/Materials/Manufacturing Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) is a research centre conducting fundamental and applied research in all aspects related to additive manufacturing. Our vision is to be the world leader in 3D Printing and a wellspring of knowledge, delivering state of the art and innovative solutions to the industry. SC3DP is at the forefront of developing advanced technologies and high-impact research in areas such biomedical, construction, aerospace, marine and offshore. It is one of the very few research centres globally with multi-sector 3D printing expertise. SC3DP’s research achievements, high-level industry collaboration, comprehensive facilities and resources have positioned it as a leading hub for 3D printing research and innovation globally. The Research Scientist is expected to help the principal investigator to carry out a research project on laser additive manufacturing in collaboration with an industrial partner. Key Responsibilities: Manage the project with the defined milestones and deliverables. Carry out hands-on experiments to meet deliverables and KPIs. Write and prepare communications content and interface with the industry and funding agency. Job Requirements: Bachelor qualification degree in mechanical, materials or manufacturing engineering or related field At least 8 years of relevant experience in engineering research / technical hands-on experience in additive manufacturing or related field Proficiency in experimental skills in microstructural characterization, including metallograph and EBSD. Proficiency in experimental skills in mechanical testing, such as hardness testing. Demonstrated experience in laser directed energy deposition additive manufacturing. Knowledge of the relationship between microstructures and mechanical properties of metallic materials. Good written and oral communication skills Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-the-School-of-Mechanical-and-Aerospace-Engineering--MAE-_R00025543": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are looking for part-time instructors in the areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering within the College of Engineering, School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering. Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a recognized MEng degree, preferably PhD, in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching Hours Classes are mainly conducted during the day/night on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). In view of the current COVID situation, online teaching and assessments are expected to be conducted where required. In addition, applicant must be prepared to act according to the situational changes in number of CAs, CA formats, etc. when required by the School.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/IT-Manager--NEC---Hospitality-Systems-_R00025002": {
      "title": "IT Manager (NEC - Hospitality Systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. It features 150 guestrooms and aims to offer a premier venue for corporate training, retreats and private events. We are looking for an experienced and service-oriented IT manager to oversee system operations, integrations, and technology enablement during NEC’s ongoing refurbishment and lead up to full opening. Key Responsibilities: 1. Systems Administration & Operation Partner with NEC’s Brand IT Team and NTU’s Centre for IT Services (CITS) to design, implement and maintain a resilient network architecture. Oversee daily operation of all NEC IT systems including PMS, POS, CRS, telecommunication, internet, and back-office systems. Ensure system uptime, reliability, and data integrity across all NEC functions. Manage server administration, data backups, and network configurations. Monitor system performance and proactively resolve issues to minimise downtime. 2. User Support & Training Develop and maintain functional documentation, SOPs and training materials for all NEC systems. Provide technical support to all NEC functions, troubleshooting hardware, software, and network issues in a timely manner. Coordinate user access rights, password controls, and compliance with IT policies. Provide staff training and systems onboarding to ensure smooth adoption of IT tools and cybersecurity awareness. 3. Cybersecurity & Data protection Implement and enforce data security protocols, antivirus measures, and system access controls. Ensure compliance with PDPA (Personal Data Protection Act) and required information security standards. Maintain regular updates and patch management for all systems and software. 4. Vendor & Contract Management Liaise with external vendors for system maintenance, upgrades, and technical support/troubleshooting. Review and manage IT-related service contracts, ensuring optimal service and cost efficiency. Evaluate new technology solutions and make recommendations to management. 5. Project Implementation Work closely with NEC team to analyse business needs to translate them into system requirements. Support NEC management team with technological insights to align IT strategies with overall business goals and objectives. Lead IT-related projects including system upgrades, new software implementation, and integration with third-party solutions. Coordinate with the brand IT team or corporate office on group initiatives and audits. Support technology requirements for events, conferences, and new operational setups. 6. Budgeting and Asset Management Prepare and manage the annual IT budget, ensuring cost control and resource optimisation. Maintain an accurate inventory of all IT hardware, software licenses, and related assets. Ensure preventive maintenance schedules and timely replacement of aging equipment. Requirem ents: A degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering or related disciplines. Minimum 6 years of relevant IT experience, with a significant portion dedicated to supporting PMS systems in the hospitality industry. Hands-on experience with Opera integrations. Expertise in hospitality system integrations, particularly Oracle Opera PMS and interface management. Proficiency in network administration (LAN/WAN, wireless setups, firewalls). Familiarity with hospitality IT standards and third-party hospitality solutions. Demonstrated ability to liaise effectively with user departments and vendors. Strong troubleshooting, issue-tracking, and documentation skills. The appointment title offered will be commensurate with candidate’s prior work experience. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Waveguide-Integrated-Superconducting-Nanowire-Single-Photon-Detectors-_R00025534": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Waveguide-Integrated Superconducting Nanowire Single-Photon Detectors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the Centre for Disruptive Photonic Technologies (CDPT) and the National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP), Nanyang Technological University, Singapore A Research Fellow / Research Engineer position is currently available across the Centre for Disruptive Photonic Technologies (CDPT) and the National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP), Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore. The Research Fellow (Project Leader) will integrate Superconducting Nanowire Single-Photon Detectors (SNSPDs) with state-of-the-art quantum Photonic Integrated Circuits (PICs). The role will scale and advance the fabrication, testing, and packaging workflows for waveguide-integrated SNSPDs, with the goal of developing a commercially-viable single-photon detection system prototype. The position combines device development with exploration of use cases and pathways to commercialization, and directly supports NTU’s mission to develop and commercialize emerging quantum computing and networking technologies. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to: Design PIC components and integrate SNSPDs with photonic integrated circuits. Scale and optimize fabrication and cryogenic testing workflows. Characterize detector and system performance, including detection efficiency, dark count rate, timing jitter, and yield. Develop packaging solutions compatible with the cryogenic environment, and manage and document process, design, and measurement data. Operate and maintain research laboratories, including cryostats and optical setups, in compliance with safety and laboratory protocols. Participate in the Venture Creation Program and pilot tests with research groups and industry partners, and explore potential use cases for the developed prototype. Contribute to progress reports, IP disclosures, grant proposals, and disseminate results through publications and at international conferences. Job Requirements: The applicant should: Hold a Ph.D. or Doctorate in Physics, Optical/Photonic Engineering, Electronic or Semiconductor Engineering, Information Science, or closely related disciplines. Have relevant research or industrial experience in one or more of the following: semiconductor/superconductor nanofabrication processes (thin-film deposition, photo- and electron-beam lithography, and etching); design and testing of cryogenic (< 10 K) electronic devices (e.g. superconducting devices, cryo-CMOS); or heterogeneous integration. Preferably be familiar with single-photon detection, heterogeneous integration, and quantum technologies concepts. Preferably have experience with photonic device/circuit design and simulation tools (e.g. Lumerical, Ansys, or similar). Have competence in data acquisition/analysis and scripting for instrument control (e.g. Python/MATLAB/LabVIEW). Demonstrate the ability to work both independently and within a collaborative research team, with strong communication and interpersonal skills. NTU seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Admin-Support_R00025193": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Admin Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) is seeking an experienced and highly motivated Senior Executive to join our team. The School is committed to developing programmes that offer cutting-edge lifelong learning solutions and globally recognized qualifications accessible by aspiring professionals and lifelong learners. This incumbent plays a critical role in supporting the school’s postgraduate office by providing administrative and operational support for the smooth running of master’s programmes. The role ensures that all processes related to student administration, academic operations, and postgraduate services are executed efficiently, in compliance with institutional policies and academic regulations. The position also supports continuous improvement initiatives to enhance service quality and operational effectiveness. This role reports to the Head of Graduate Office and Associate Chair (Graduate). Programme Operations: Academic Administration Administer postgraduate student life cycle activities including admission registration, enrolment, module registration, academic progression, examination, and graduation. Maintain accurate student records in university systems and ensure data integrity for reporting and audit purposes. Coordinate with academic departments, supervisors, and graduate committees to facilitate academic and administrative processes. Support the implementation of academic policies, guidelines, and quality assurance procedures for postgraduate programmes. Programme Operations: Operations & Process Management Manage day-to-day postgraduate office operations to ensure timely and accurate execution of academic and administrative tasks. Monitor key operational timelines such as course registration periods, examination schedules, and graduation deadlines. Prepare operational reports, statistics, and documentation for management review. Assist in process improvement and digitalisation initiatives to enhance efficiency and service delivery. Programme Operations: Outreach/Marketing Activities Organise outreach events for prospective students, current students, and alumni. Raise purchase requests for catering services via the Ariba system. Prepare ITQ documents for outreach/marketing-related activities. Prepare workshop/seminar announcements for posting in CCEB. Book venues for information sessions and seminars. Other Administrative Duties Manage the onboarding processes for part-time lecturers. Manage a role-based email account. Assist in the preparation and consolidation of data for reporting purposes where required. Assist the programme director in tracking the financial status of the programme and making accurate financial projections. Develop and maintain SOPs for the administration of the MSc programme. Liaise with University offices to ensure the smooth running of the programme. Attend meetings of College/University-level committees on MSc programmes. Assist in any ad hoc matters as delegated and required. Requirements Educational Qualification(s) Reputable Diploma or Bachelor’s degree. Specialisation in science or engineering disciplines is preferred but not essential. Knowledge Required Familiarity with admission cycles, matriculation processes, student records management, and academic progression tracking. Proficiency in basic productivity tools such as Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Microsoft Teams, and Adobe software. Ability to prepare, manage, and interpret administrative and academic data for operational and reporting purposes. Basic understanding of budget monitoring, cost tracking, and financial forecasting in an academic context. Relevant Experience 1–3 years of administrative experience, preferably in a higher education setting. Prior exposure to postgraduate or academic programme coordination is strongly preferred. Experience working with cross-functional stakeholders (faculty, students, and university departments). Skills & Competencies Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to convey important information clearly and effectively. Responsible and independent, with strong time management skills. Skilled in multitasking while maintaining attention to detail. Good situational awareness and the ability to assess and respond to dynamic conditions effectively. Other Personal Attributes Proactive and positive attitude towards work tasks. Strong service orientation. Eagerness to learn new skills and systems. Self-motivated, with a proactive approach to challenges. Analytical thinker with strong problem-solving capabilities. The School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Human-Resource_R00025533": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Human Resource",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs a key member of the HR team, you will play an essential role in supporting the HR Business Partner (HRBP) by managing a range of HR matters within the designated business unit(s). Your contributions will ensure the efficient and effective delivery of HR services, fostering a positive workplace environment. Key Responsibilities: You will support the HRBP in ensuring timely HR service delivery in the following key areas: Recruitment – collaborating with the Talent Acquisition and HR Shared Services team, you will support the administrative processes to ensure that the Business Unit is able to bring in the right talents in a timely manner Contract renewals of staff – you will work with key stakeholders to manage the administration of contract renewals of staff Performance management – you may also be expected to support the HRBP during the performance management cycle and this may include tracking timelines, helping People Managers to understand performance management tools and practices and consolidating data to facilitate discussions. HR Data – you will ensure that HR data is accurate and assist in preparation of HR reports/key updates to facilitate decision-making Provide HR advisory services regarding the university's policies and work processes Collaborate with the HRBP and HR Centres of Excellence on HR projects, including policy and process reviews. Qualifications: Degree with at least 3 years of experience in human resources administration or a related field. Candidates with prior experience of working in an educational / academic/ research environment would have an added advantage Highly attentive to details, possess the ability to multi-task and to manage deliverables under tight timelines Strong verbal and written communication skills; ability to interact effectively with diverse stakeholders Flexibility to adapt to changing priorities and evolving HR needs Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment while also being self-motivated Candidates with prior experience in using Workday system would have an advantage We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Public-Programmes_R00025528": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Public Programmes",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. The candidate will be leading Nanyang Executive Education’s Public Programmes. Key Responsibilities: To take ownership and lead business development efforts in the Public programmes To understand the executive education market, and perform analyses e.g. market research, competitor landscape, segmentation, growth trends, value proposition etc and make strategy recommendations To think strategically and to analyse and synthesize information into strategic actions as part of growing the NEE portfolio, in alignment with NBS/NEE overall business direction To service existing clients, in addition to adding new clients, as part of growing the pipeline and portfolio To work with closely with faculty to create learning proposals and programmes, through putting together information and persuasive ideas, that will meet manpower training needs and requirements To ensure high levels of client satisfaction as well as build trusted relationships with clients To grow strong relationship with key stakeholders, both internal and external, and find mutually beneficial ways of collaboration To identify and contextualize internal and external stakeholder issues and engage appropriately To assist in new corporate initiative development that will lead to better corporate processes and client experience Competencies and Qualification Requirements: A good bachelor’s degree, with at least 10 years’ working experience, preferably in the executive education, L&D department of an organization, or in consulting. A proven revenue-generation track record through business development, sales and bidding management Ability to work independently, as well as inter-dependently, within a team, and across teams Customer-oriented disposition, with excellent interpersonal skills, and to be able to work with all levels Good business acumen, with ability to develop proposals for clients in the areas of leadership and business management training Self-starter and problem-solver, who is adaptable to a changing environment, and is able to proactively address any challenges that may arise Excellent written, oral, presentation and facilitation skills Displays leadership skills and takes interest in nurturing and coaching junior members of the team We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Major-Gifts_R00022794": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Major Gifts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU University Advancement Office (UAO) supports the University’s giving mission by fostering meaningful relationships and strategic partnerships with philanthropists, alumni, business community partners, corporations, foundations and friends that result in goodwill and philanthropy towards education and research.   We are seeking a highly motivated and passionate individual to join the Major Gifts team. The key responsibilities are: To develop and manage relationships and activities related to the cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of donors and major gifts to maximise the University’s philanthropic outcomes. To take a strategic approach to fundraising which include major gifts, capital fundraising, corporate donations, grants and bequests. To leverage on the University leadership, faculty, and volunteers, in collaboration with other UAO colleagues, to advance relationships and gift discussions and ensure alumni, friends and corporate partners and foundations are best positioned to provide maximum levels of philanthropic support for NTU’s campaign priorities. To lead and facilitate gift structuring to optimise donor’s gift purpose and manage the process of closing the gift and work with the UAO Stewardship Team to cultivate and steer donors to the next level of giving.   Requirements: A Bachelor’s Degree in any discipline. Experience in Higher Education/Not-For-Profit fundraising with an ability to achieve monthly activity targets as a key metric of performance, is preferred. Candidates with appropriate business development/consultative sales experience may also be considered. Demonstrated experience managing complex and diverse relationships and the proven ability to collaborate effectively with multiple stakeholders. Exceptional interpersonal skills with proven ability to liaise, consult and negotiate confidently and professionally with donors, faculty, staff, and other stakeholders at all levels. Excellent written communication skills with extensive experience in developing business cases, proposals, and presentations. Well-developed planning and organisational skills with the ability to prioritise workload, meet deadlines and work under pressure in a fast-moving team environment. Sound acumen and strong professional presence as well as a collegial work style that promotes teamwork, creativity and open communication. Awareness of and sensitivity to a diverse range of stakeholders. A global, socially conscious mindset with an understanding and appreciation of cultural and intercultural sensitives. A proactive and solutions-oriented approach. Ability to influence without authority.   Appointment titles offered will commensurate with candidate’s prior work experiences.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Administrative-Support_R00025524": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) offers a full range of additive manufacturing services, from design and infrastructure to production and validation. With advanced technologies such as topology optimization, generative design, and bioinspired design, SC3DP creates optimized products using a variety of novel materials and printing processes, including hybrid printing, post-processing, and emerging technologies. Sustainability is a top priority for SC3DP, which offers material development and control services that combine artificial intelligence, big data, and other digital tools for process optimization, as well as non-destructive testing for AM parts. Backed by a team of experts and a state-of-the-art facility equipped with the latest equipment and technologies, SC3DP is committed to leading the way in sustainable additive manufacturing research and development.  The successful applicant will be responsible for providing operational and administrative support to the Centre, coordinating office activities, managing administrative processes, and ensuring effective support for faculty, research staff, and students. Job Responsibilities: Provide executive administrative support to the Executive Director, including managing schedules, coordination of meetings, and follow-up on operational matters. Support the overall administration and daily operations of the Centre, ensuring efficient coordination of activities and smooth workflow. Manage office IT and physical assets, including asset tracking, inventory management, and equipment allocation to support operational requirements. Plan, coordinate, and execute Centre events, ensuring effective organisation, timely implementation, and successful delivery of outcomes. Oversee event-related activities, including publicity and communications, preparation of presentation and event materials, logistical arrangements, and post-event follow-ups. Develop and coordinate corporate communications materials, including newsletters, annual reports, and ad-hoc announcements. Manage and maintain website content to ensure information is accurate, updated, and aligned with the Centre’s communication objectives. Requirements: Diploma/Degree in Business Administration or a related discipline with relevant experience in administrative and operational support, preferably in a higher education, research, or corporate environment. Proven experience in executive administrative support, office operations, asset management, and coordination of resources to support organisational needs. Strong organisational and coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, timelines, stakeholders, and operational activities effectively. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with experience in preparing reports, newsletters, presentations, corporate communications, and managing digital content platforms. Proactive, detail-oriented, and service-oriented individual with strong interpersonal skills, problem-solving abilities, and the ability to work independently while handling confidential information with discretion. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow---Senior-Research-Fellow--Wireless-Localization---Sensing-_R00025504": {
      "title": "Research Fellow / Senior Research Fellow (Wireless Localization & Sensing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow (Wireless Localization & Sensing) to conduct experimentally driven research on radio-based localization, tracking, and sensing for future 6G communication and Internet-of-Things systems. The Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow will develop localization and sensing algorithms, implement them on real hardware platforms, design and conduct measurement campaigns, and build demonstrable prototypes in realistic indoor environments. The Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow will work closely with the Principal Investigator and collaborators/students across NTU Singapore to deliver high-quality research, experimental testbeds, reusable datasets and software, peer-reviewed publications, intellectual property, and follow-on research proposals. Key Responsibilities: Conduct original research on wireless localization, tracking, and sensing techniques, with a strong emphasis on practical implementation and experimental validation. Identify potentially patentable research outcomes and fill in patent application forms. Write and publish high-quality research papers. Assist in the preparation and writing of research grant proposals. Co-supervise undergraduate and/or graduate students. Job Requirements: PhD in electrical and electronic engineering, communication engineering, signal processing, radar engineering, remote sensing, or related discipline. Strong publication record and hands-on experience in one of the following areas: wireless localization, wireless sensing, AI/machine learning for communications, or signal processing. Ability to conduct experimental research independently and collaboratively within a team. Good written and oral communication skills in English - essential for data analysis and communication with stakeholders We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/NIE-Overseas-Graduate-Scholarship--Mathematics---Mathematics-Education-_R00024927": {
      "title": "NIE Overseas Graduate Scholarship (Mathematics & Mathematics Education)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOBJECTIVE The National Institute of Education Overseas Graduate Scholarship (NIE OGS) will sponsor outstanding candidates to pursue full-time doctoral studies overseas. Upon completion of their doctoral studies, candidates will return to NIE to serve as educators and academics. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA The applicant must fulfill the following criteria: Be a Singapore Citizen. Has excellent academic records with very good Honours or Master’s degrees (or professional qualifications of equivalent standing), with relevant teaching and some research experience. Has the passion to pursue a challenging career in academia. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF SCHOLARSHIP The scholarship is tenable for a period of three years. The scholarship will provide: Two sets of economy class air tickets (one at commencement and completion of doctoral studies, and one to return to Singapore for data collection for doctoral thesis). Overseas maintenance allowance. Stipend. Pre-studies allowance (at commencement of doctoral studies). Thesis allowance (upon completion of doctoral studies). Tuition and other compulsory fees. Conference and fieldwork grants (by application). A scholar studying in the United States may be considered for a fourth year of sponsorship if the required minimum period of candidature is at least 4 years. The scholar may be required to serve a few months in the Ministry of Education (MOE) Headquarters before embarking on his/her doctoral studies (if applicable). The scholar will be required to enter into a bond to serve the National Institute of Education Nanyang Technological University (NIE NTU) as an employee for a period of five years upon obtaining the doctoral degree. NIE NTU reserves the right to revise the terms and conditions of the scholarship as it deems fit. AREA OF STUDY Mathematics or Mathematics Education The Mathematics & Mathematics Education (MME) Department at the NIE leads in academic and curriculum studies in Mathematics and Mathematics Education for pre-service teachers and in-service teachers. We are committed to exploring innovative methods of instruction aligned to the latest international trends in mathematics and mathematics education and seeking to develop excellent practices in our collaboration with our partners, both schools and other universities. We invite applicants who are interested to pursue a PhD in either Mathematics or Mathematics Education . For Mathematics Education, the research topic should be an area that is of direct relevance to the Singapore education. For Mathematics, the research topic could be one that can preferably be useful to the School Mathematics curriculum (e.g., an area in Discrete Mathematics). The applicant should be a Singapore school teacher with very good Honours degree or a Master’s degree. Applicants who demonstrate ongoing engagement in research prior to his/her PhD will be preferred. Applicants should meet the following criteria: Familiarity with the Singapore education system, with at least three years of teaching experience. For Mathematics Education, at least three years of K-12 teaching experience is required. At least a Second Class Honours (Upper Division) degree or a Master’s degree in Mathematics or Mathematics Education or a related field. Experience in either content research, education research, or related disciplines prior to PhD studies is highly preferred. Publications in international peer-reviewed academic journals will be an advantage. Demonstrated passion and commitment to serving as an academic staff member at NIE, particularly in teaching, research, and service in areas related to Mathematics or Mathematics Education. APPLICATION PROCESS The following supporting documents must be submitted together with the application form to NIE NTU, through Workday, by the closing date : a. Curriculum Vitae (which should include academic qualifications, employment history, scholarships & awards, a brief description of your research experience and publication list if available). b. A succinct write-up (2 pages) on the research topic which you intend to pursue. c. A succinct write-up (4 pages) on your commitment and interest in the area of study applied for and the expected contribution to NIE, schools and the Singapore education system. d. An abstract of any thesis previously written. e. Copies of two pieces of research work that you consider to be your most significant works (if available). f. All relevant educational certificates and transcripts including GCE ‘O’ Level, GCE ‘A’ Level, Polytechnic Diploma, University Degree(s). g. Letters for scholarships, prizes, other awards, memberships in academic & professional societies (if available). h. A copy of the letter(s) of offer from each university applied to for admission to doctoral studies (if available). i. A copy of the letter(s) of offer for other scholarships and/or awards applied for and the outcome of these applications (if available). j. A minimum of two confidential referees’ reports (preferably from academic referees) printed on the official letterhead, to be sent directly to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CONTACT INFORMATION For clarification or more information, please contact: Area of Study Head, MME for Mathematics or Mathematics Education here . Terms and Conditions of Scholarship NIE Human Resource Department - Email to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CLOSING DATE All applications, together with the required documents (a) to (j), must be submitted by 30 September 2026 . Please note that NIE reserves the right to consider only complete applications accompanied by all required documents. Each application will be assessed on its own merits. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/NIE-Overseas-Graduate-Scholarship--Visual---Performing-Arts-_R00024928-1": {
      "title": "NIE Overseas Graduate Scholarship (Visual & Performing Arts)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOBJECTIVE The National Institute of Education Overseas Graduate Scholarship (NIE OGS) will sponsor outstanding candidates to pursue full-time doctoral studies overseas. Upon completion of their doctoral studies, candidates will return to NIE to serve as educators and academics. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA The applicant must fulfill the following criteria: Be a Singapore Citizen. Has excellent academic records with very good Honours or Master’s degrees (or professional qualifications of equivalent standing), with relevant teaching and some research experience. Has the passion to pursue a challenging career in academia. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF SCHOLARSHIP The scholarship is tenable for a period of three years. The scholarship will provide: Two sets of economy class air tickets (one at commencement and completion of doctoral studies, and one to return to Singapore for data collection for doctoral thesis). Overseas maintenance allowance. Stipend. Pre-studies allowance (at commencement of doctoral studies). Thesis allowance (upon completion of doctoral studies). Tuition and other compulsory fees. Conference and fieldwork grants (by application). A scholar studying in the United States may be considered for a fourth year of sponsorship if the required minimum period of candidature is at least 4 years. The scholar may be required to serve a few months in the Ministry of Education (MOE) Headquarters before embarking on his/her doctoral studies (if applicable). The scholar will be required to enter into a bond to serve the National Institute of Education Nanyang Technological University (NIE NTU) as an employee for a period of five years upon obtaining the doctoral degree. NIE NTU reserves the right to revise the terms and conditions of the scholarship as it deems fit. Music The Visual & Performing Arts (VPA) Department at the NIE offers a vibrant and intellectually rich environment for the preparation of arts educators in drama, music and visual art. Deeply rooted in arts education and attentive to developments in contemporary artistic practice, the department values both strong practitioner expertise and rigorous theoretical grounding. Committed to Singapore’s context and internationally engaged in outlook, VPA prepares arts educators for both pre-service and in-service settings, while also offering graduate programmes in the arts and arts education. This call is open to applicants who wish to pursue a PhD in Music within a dynamic and forward-looking academic setting. Proposed research should be grounded in strong disciplinary foundations in music while engaging contemporary developments in a technology-pervasive world. Projects may span both musical art and sound arts, and should speak meaningfully to Singapore’s multicultural context while contributing to wider conversations in Music and Music Education. Applicants should meet the following criteria: Familiarity with the Singapore education system, with at least three years of teaching experience in a K-12 or pre-tertiary institution. At least a Second Class Honours (Upper Division) degree, or a Master’s degree, in Music or a related field. Experience in music-related research, academic publishing, and presenting at international and/or regional conferences is highly preferred. A strong record of artistic or professional practice, or creative works, including areas such as performance, composition, conducting, or music production, where relevant. Demonstrated passion and commitment to serving as an academic staff member at NIE, particularly in teaching, research, and service in areas related to Music and Music Education. APPLICATION PROCESS The following supporting documents must be submitted together with the application form to NIE NTU, through Workday, by the closing date : a. Curriculum Vitae (which should include academic qualifications, employment history, scholarships & awards, a brief description of your research experience and publication list if available). b. A succinct write-up (2 pages) on the research topic which you intend to pursue. c. A succinct write-up (4 pages) on your commitment and interest in the area of study applied for and the expected contribution to NIE, schools and the Singapore education system. d. An abstract of any thesis previously written. e. Copies of two pieces of research work that you consider to be your most significant works (if available). f. All relevant educational certificates and transcripts including GCE ‘O’ Level, GCE ‘A’ Level, Polytechnic Diploma, University Degree(s). g. Letters for scholarships, prizes, other awards, memberships in academic & professional societies (if available). h. A copy of the letter(s) of offer from each university applied to for admission to doctoral studies (if available). i. A copy of the letter(s) of offer for other scholarships and/or awards applied for and the outcome of these applications (if available). j. A minimum of two confidential referees’ reports (preferably from academic referees) printed on the official letterhead, to be sent directly to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CONTACT INFORMATION For clarification or more information, please contact: Area of Study Head, VPA for Music here . Terms and Conditions of Scholarship NIE Human Resource Department - Email to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CLOSING DATE All applications, together with the required documents (a) to (j), must be submitted by 30 September 2026 . Please note that NIE reserves the right to consider only complete applications accompanied by all required documents. Each application will be assessed on its own merits. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Affairs_R00022769": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering (CoE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is seeking a dynamic and detail-oriented Senior Assistant Manager to join our Faculty Affairs team. This strategic role works closely with the Head of Faculty Affairs to support the Associate Dean (Faculty) in managing critical faculty-related matters across all Engineering schools, ensuring operational excellence and supporting the College’s mission to attract, develop, and retain world-class faculty talent. Key Responsibilities: 1. Faculty Recruitment Coordinate faculty recruitment activities across CoE schools, including global faculty recruitment outreach events and campus visit programmes (e.g. Emerging Scholars Forum). Liaise with schools’ Faculty Administrators (FAs) and Human Resource Business Partners (HRBPs) to manage recruitment timelines and processes. Support the preparation of faculty appointment dossiers and documentation for the College committee’s review. Track schools’ search progress and recruitment metrics to prepare reports for the College leadership. 2. Faculty Appointments and Reappointments Manage the administrative processes for new faculty appointments, contract renewals, and reappointments. Coordinate with schools to ensure timely submission of appointment/reappointment documentation and compliance with University policies. Maintain accurate records of faculty appointments and contract terms across all CoE schools. 3. Faculty Performance Appraisal Oversee the annual faculty appraisal exercise across the College and CoE Schools to ensure adherence to timelines and processes. Coordinate with schools’ FAs and HRBPs to compile and track appraisal submissions. Prepare reports on appraisal outcomes for College leadership review. Support the implementation of performance management initiatives. 4. Faculty Development and Culture Assist in organising faculty development programmes, workshops, and engagement activities. Support initiatives to enhance faculty experience and foster a positive academic culture. Coordinate with schools on onboarding programmes for new faculty members. Facilitate communication of faculty-related policies and resources. 5. Faculty Promotion and Tenure Coordinate the promotion and tenure review processes across CoE schools. Work with school FAs to ensure complete and timely submission of promotion dossiers. Maintain documentation and tracking systems for promotion cases. Support the preparation of materials for College committees' review. 6. Strategic Support and Process Improvement Contribute to the review and streamlining of faculty-related processes to enhance efficiency. Prepare presentations, reports, and briefing materials for College committees and leadership. Maintain comprehensive databases and management information systems for faculty affairs. Support ad-hoc projects and initiatives related to faculty matters at the College level. Qualifications and Requirements: Education and Experience: A recognised university degree, preferably in engineering, business management, or a related field. At least 3-5 years of relevant experience in human resources, faculty academic administration, or related fields. Experience with faculty affairs is highly advantageous. Skills and Competencies: Strong organisational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to work effectively with diverse stakeholders, including faculty, administrators, and senior leadership. High attention to detail and commitment to accuracy in documentation and processes. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, M365 productivity tools, data analysis, and database management. Analytical mindset with the ability to prepare clear reports and presentations. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion. Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team. Personal Attributes: Proactive problem-solver with strong service orientation. Adaptable and resilient in a fast-paced academic environment. Strong work ethic with commitment to excellence. Cultural sensitivity and ability to work in an ‘international’ environment. Note: We recognise that not every candidate will fulfil every qualification listed. If you believe you have the relevant experience, transferable skills, and motivation to succeed in this role, we encourage you to apply. Why Join Us? NTU College of Engineering is consistently ranked among the world’s top engineering colleges. You will work at the strategic heart of the College, supporting critical decisions that impact faculty recruitment, development, and excellence across our diverse engineering disciplines. This role offers a unique opportunity to collaborate with distinguished academic leaders, engage with international faculty talent, and contribute to innovative initiatives that enhance faculty experience and organisational excellence. With exposure to high-level strategic planning and direct involvement in processes that shape the academic community, you’ll develop specialised expertise in faculty affairs within one of Singapore’s premier universities. How to Apply: Interested applicants are invited to submit their detailed resume and cover letter through NTU’s career portal. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Visiting-Associate-Professor_R00025518": {
      "title": "Visiting Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nVisiting Associate Professor Position in Nanophotonics Young and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore) is ranked 12th globally. It is also placed 1st among the world's best young universities. The Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP) at NTU invites applications for positions at the rank of Visiting Associate Professor in Photonics. We are looking for candidates holding a Ph.D. degree in physics, photonics, optoelectronics or a closely related area. The Visiting Associate Professor will collaborate with PAP colleagues to work in the area of quantum and topological photonic metamaterials and metasurfaces, time-crystal photonics, and nanoimaging. He/she will get involved in collaborative externally projects with PAP colleagues, as well as explore collaborations with colleagues from other Schools within NTU, with the aim of deepening institutional links between NTU and the candidate’s institution. The candidate should have more than 10 years of experience in cutting edge research in nanophotonics materials and devices, and deep knowledge in the latest research directions in metamaterials and metasurfaces. He/she should also be an expert in nanofabrication and nano-optics characterization techniques. He/she should have demonstrated an ability to obtain external grants, plus regularly publish in top-tier journals such as the Nature and Science family of journals. Enquiries about the position can be addressed to Professor LEW Wen Siang. Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Emoluments and General Terms & Conditions of Service The commencing salary will depend on the candidate's qualifications, experience and the level of appointment offered. Information on emoluments and general terms and conditions of service is available in the section on Terms and Conditions of Service for Academic Appointments. Application Procedure To apply, please refer to the Guidelines for Submitting an Application for Faculty Appointment at: http://www.ntu.edu.sg/ohr/career/submit-an- application/Pages/Faculty-Positions.aspx and send your application package and any enquiries to PAPrecruit@ntu.edu.sg. All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager---Assistant-Manager--Content-Creation_R00025522": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager / Assistant Manager, Content Creation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world's top universities. NTU's College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU's College of Computing and Data Science is an 'exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. We are seeking an experienced and dynamic Content Writer to be involved with the College’s branding campaigns and activities. What You Will Do: 1. Strategic Communications Develop and drive the College's integrated communications strategy to strengthen brand positioning, reputation, and stakeholder engagement locally. Collaborate closely with faculty members, researchers, and corporate stakeholders to drive communication initiatives. Lead the development of compelling thought content, executive communications, speeches, media features, strategic publications, and digital storytelling initiatives. 2. Content Creation Develop and implement internal and external communication strategies, ensuring alignment with the College’s branding and objectives. Create and manage high-quality communication materials, including press releases, presentations, website content, and corporate collaterals. Oversee and maintain the College’s websites, ensuring accuracy, relevance, and up-to-date content. Optimise the user experience (UX) and interface of the College’s websites to ensure they are visually appealing, accessible, and user-friendly. Monitor and analyse social media performance metrics, using data-driven insights to refine content and campaign strategies. Stay informed of emerging social media trends and best practices, continuously improving digital engagement strategies. 3. Branding and Promotion Support the development and execution of publicity campaigns to enhance the College’s visibility and brand awareness. Ensure that event publicity materials and marketing collaterals created by event organisers align with the College’s branding and communication guidelines. Oversee the planning and execution of College events, ensuring they are effectively promoted and successfully delivered. 4. Editing and Proofreading Review, edit, and refine content for clarity, accuracy, consistency, and adherence to brand style guidelines. Ensure all written materials maintain high editorial standards, with precise grammar, spelling, punctuation, and tone. 5. Performance Analytics and Reporting Establish communication effectiveness metrics and dashboards to evaluate campaign performance and stakeholder engagement. Analyse audience insights, website analytics, media coverage, and social media trends to inform strategic decision-making. Who You Are: Minimum a bachelor’s degree in mass communications, Literary Arts, New Media, Marketing, or a related field. At least 7 years of relevant experience in corporate communications and media, preferably within an educational institution. Tech-savvy and proficient in Microsoft Office and digital marketing tools, including Google Analytics and SEO. Well-versed in the digital economy, with experience managing digital public relations platforms and online engagement. Exceptional writing, editing, and proofreading skills, with strong attention to detail. Ability to craft clear, concise, and compelling narratives—from brand storytelling to impactful reports—demonstrating a strong sense of structure and storytelling techniques. A meticulous, dedicated, and proactive team player, who thrives on challenges and can multi-task effectively. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret data and optimise communication strategies. Strong interpersonal and communication skills (both verbal and written), with the ability to engage diverse stakeholders. Self-motivated, responsible, and proactive, with a positive work attitude and a commitment to excellence. Ability to manage high-pressure situations, demonstrating resilience and adaptability. Strong organisational skills, with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple projects simultaneously . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow-Senior-Research-Fellow--Healthy-Aging--LKCMedicine-_R00025509-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow, Healthy Aging [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are looking for a highly motivated Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow to join the LKCMedicine’s Centre for Geroscience and Geromedicine to focus on various aspects of translational bat immunology and aging research. The work will be conducted in a research group led by Nanyang Assistant Professor Matae Ahn who is a pioneer in bat immunology. The projects focus on learning from bats with exceptional healthy longevity to develop bat-inspired new targets and strategies to fight human diseases and aging, and have multiple national and international collaborations. Key Responsibilities: Conduct accurate monitoring, documenting and reporting of experimental results and/or research findings.  Drive research with proficient data analysis and literature review in various research projects.  Evaluate and interpret collected data and prepare oral presentations, written reports and scientific manuscripts for publication.  Contribute to project management including supervision of students and laboratory demonstrations where applicable.  Perform other related duties incidental to the work described therein.  Key Competencies and Requirements: PhD degree in Life Sciences, Biotechnology, Bioengineering, Veterinary Science or related field. Prior experience in animal work with tissue processing/histology or AI/bioinformatic analysis is highly preferred. Prior experience in the areas of immunology or aging is preferred but not compulsory for those with good academic and/or research track record. Equipped with effective organizational and interpersonal communications with excellent written, oral communication and computer skills. A team player who is able to prioritize, multi-task and work collaboratively in a diverse workforce.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Temporary-Senior-Executive--Learning-Technology--LKCMedicine-_R00025512": {
      "title": "Temporary Senior Executive, Learning Technology [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is seeking a reliable and detail-oriented Part-Time Learning Technologist to support the Education/Digital Learning team. The role offers practical experience in digital learning operations, educational technology and technology-enabled medical education. Responsibilities: Prepare and update learning activities, course sites and digital resources on approved platforms. Carry out pre-session checks, basic troubleshooting and timely escalation of unresolved issues. Support the formatting, uploading and quality checking of digital content. Execute assigned test cases and maintain guides, checklists, trackers and issue records. Respond to routine user enquiries and support scheduled digital learning sessions. Coordinate assigned follow-ups with faculty, colleagues and vendors. Requirements: Diploma, current studies or equivalent experience in information technology, educational technology, media, education or a related field. Comfortable using digital platforms, learning new tools and following documented procedures. Strong attention to detail, organisation and communication skills. Reliable, service-oriented and able to work independently with guidance and as part of a team. Experience with learning management systems, digital content or user support is advantageous. This is a 6 months temporary contract. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-II--Computer-Science-Computer-Engineering-Software-Engineering-Artificial-Intelligence-Data-Science-_R00025507": {
      "title": "Research Engineer II (Computer Science/Computer Engineering/Software Engineering/Artificial Intelligence/Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking a highly motivated and technically capable Research Engineer to support research work under the project “Sustainable Living”. Key Responsibilities: Collaborate closely with the Principal Investigator (PI) and research team to design, develop, and evaluate AI-driven solutions for sustainable living and green recommendation systems. Collect, organize, clean, and preprocess multimodal datasets, including textual, behavioral, contextual, and sustainability-related data, for AI modeling and analysis. Develop efficient data processing and experimentation workflows to support user modeling, preference understanding, behavior analysis, and personalized sustainability recommendations. Conduct experiments, evaluate model performance, analyze results, and iteratively improve AI models and systems. Collaborate with researchers from different disciplines and contribute to research publications, technical reports, project deliverables, and demonstrations. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or a related discipline. Candidates who are currently pursuing a Ph.D. are also welcome. Strong programming and software development skills, with the ability to implement and evaluate AI-based systems. Knowledge or practical experience in one or more of the following areas such as Natural Language Processing (NLP), Large Language Models (LLMs), Multimodal Artificial Intelligence,  Recommendation Systems, Intelligent/Agentic AI, etc. Research or project experience in data-driven AI, intelligent systems, recommendation systems, or related applications is preferred. Experience working with multimodal or domain-specific datasets is an advantage. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a proactive approach to addressing technical challenges. Good communication and teamwork skills, with the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Experience with academic research, publications, or participation in research projects is an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Programme-Director--Talent-Management-_R00025506": {
      "title": "Programme Director (Talent Management)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe CyberSG R&D Programme Office (CRPO) is a new national centre at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. CRPO will focus its efforts on three main thrusts to advance cybersecurity comprehensively: cutting-edge research and development, advancements in technology and translational development, and fostering ecosystem/industry growth and training. CRPO aspires to propel Singapore to the forefront of cybersecurity innovation and implementation, fueled by funding from the Cybersecurity Agency of Singapore (CSA). This financial backing empowers CRPO to finance visionary projects proposed by diverse entities, including research institutes (RIs), institutions of higher learning (IHLs), and industries. The scope of these initiatives spans the entire Technology Readiness Level (TRL) spectrum, from nascent concepts at TRL 1 to advanced, field-tested solutions at TRL 9, all within the dynamic realm of cybersecurity. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/crpo/crpo-verticals/translation-management . We are looking f or a Programme Director for Talent Management who will oversee a team of officers. The role will focus on i dentification of translational opportunities from cybersecurity research across IHLs in Singapore funded by the NRF. Key Responsibilities: Facilitate and matchmake stakeholders across startups, academia, and industry towards Talent Management. Oversee financial stewardship and budget allocation for all projects, ensuring efficient and accountable use of funds, adherence to cost guidelines, and alignment with institutional policies. Monitor Talent management events performance, including milestones, deliverables, risk management, and reporting, to ensure projects achieve high-impact outcomes in cybersecurity talents and events. Drive Talent Management team goals by identifying gaps, recommending enhancements, and integrating lessons learned from past projects to strengthen effectiveness. Provide leadership and guidance to Talent management team, ensuring clarity of roles, professional development, and effective coordination Ensure strategic alignment of matching talents within funded projects with CRPO’s mission to build Singapore’s national cybersecurity capabilities and foster innovation Collaborate and render support across verticals to ensure smooth operation and achieving KPI Job Requirements: Minimum requirement is bachelor’s degree qualification in talent management, entrepreneurship, business management or related field At least 10 years of relevant experience in Director’s role with hands-on experience in similar responsibilities and scope is necessary Familiarity with required scope in translation management is crucial Good written and oral communication skills (necessary) Proficiency in project performance management is crucial and acquired through minimum 10 years industry and practical training (on the job) Competent in talent management design and deployment is necessary Interpersonal skill as competent team leader with ability to work under tight timelines and develop solutions within Grantor’s criterion Ability to build rapport and influence stakeholders at all levels Possesses international experience, with a strong network of contacts in the region. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Research-Administration-and-Support-Services--LKCMedicine-_R00025446": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research Administration and Support Services [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are looking for a detail-oriented individual to join the Department of Research Administration and Support Services (RASS) at LKCMedicine. The role manages research grant administration across the full grant lifecycle, working with academic faculty members, University offices, external stakeholders and funders. Responsibilities: Manage assigned grant matters across the grant lifecycle from grant calls and proposal submissions to award set-up, variations, reporting and closure, in line with funder and University requirements. Review grant budgets, utilisation, expenditure and financial documentation to support compliance and audit readiness. Advise faculty members and research teams on funder guidelines, institutional processes, documentation requirements, approval routes and compliance expectations. Coordinate with University offices, funders and external stakeholders to resolve grant-related queries, submissions, operational issues and follow-up actions. Maintain accurate grant records, trackers and supporting documentation to support management reporting, monitoring, funder reporting and audit readiness. Contribute to broader grant operations and team priorities, including process improvement, reporting and cross-coverage of grant matters where required. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Science or a related discipline. Relevant experience in administration, research, grants, finance, compliance or stakeholder support would be advantageous. Strong organisational and analytical skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines, track deliverables and follow through on outstanding matters. Good communication skills and comfortable working with different stakeholders. Adaptable and willing to learn Proficient in using digital tools for tracking, documentation and collaboration; familiarity with grant management systems would be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Student-Engagement-and-Development--Undergraduate-Programmes-_R00024782-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Engagement and Development (Undergraduate Programmes)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA young and research-intensive university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities, NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) is the focal point of entrepreneurship education within the University, Singapore and the region. We are seeking an Assistant Manager (Student Engagement and Development). The incumbent will play a vital role in enhancing the undergraduate experience at NTUpreneur. Reporting to the Assistant Director/Lead, this position is central to promoting the Second Major in Entrepreneurship (SMiE) and Minor in Entrepreneurship (MiE) programmes, strengthening student engagement, and building a vibrant NTUpreneur community. A key performance indicator (KPI) is increasing enrolment for each programme cohort, making effective communication of the programmes’ value and offerings essential. Through targeted marketing efforts, outreach events, leadership programmes, and community-building initiatives, the role supports NTUpreneur’s mission to develop entrepreneurial-minded students and foster a dynamic and supportive environment within the Academy. The incumbent will plan and execute undergraduate outreach, student engagement, and community-building initiatives, while also owning the operational framework for sourcing and tracking high-potential entrepreneurial students and venture projects. Through integrated marketing, engagement strategies, and the development of a structured student and venture pipeline, the role contributes to enrolment outcomes and strengthens the NTUpreneur student ecosystem. Key Responsibilities: Plan, Develop and Organise Programme Marketing and Outreach Develop and implement marketing strategies for SMiE and MiE Oversee production of marketing materials (brochures, posters, social media) Manage social media channels and create engaging campaigns Collaborate with NTU Schools for cross-departmental Promotions Plan, Develop and Organise Outreach Events and Activities Plan and execute roadshows, Open House, info sessions, etc. Coordinate and support NTUpreneur’s participation in NTU/external events Organise visits for stakeholders Plan, Develop and Organise Student Engagement and Development Initiatives Implement onboarding sessions and community-building events Rebuild and manage Student Ambassador Programme and NTUpreneur Student Club Mentor student leaders and guide student club in event and programme execution Develop co-curricular initiatives that foster entrepreneurship Ensure Student Club follows NTU’s governance framework Own the sourcing and tracking framework for high-potential entrepreneurial students and venture projects, including procedures, systems and data governance Responsible for Data Management and Administration for the Undergraduate Team Responsible for data management and act as PDPA focal point Manage and maintain event calendar, reports, programme accounts Ensure updated programme content online (eg. Website and intranet) Responsible for Budgeting and Reporting on Student Engagement and Development functions Ensure proper tracking of budget and work with Lead on budget planning for student engagement activities Collect data, analyse trends and report on programme improvements Requirements: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised Institute of Higher Learning. 3–5 years of relevant experience in student engagement, student development, or programme/event management within a tertiary-education environment, with supervisory exposure. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, with familiarity in social-media tools, digital communications and basic design applications. Strong planning, organisational and multi-tasking abilities to manage student-related projects, events and outreach activities effectively. Excellent interpersonal and communication (oral and written) skills, with the ability to collaborate across teams, build rapport and engage a diverse range of stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to collect, analyse and report data for programme evaluation and improvement. Empathy and sensitivity in working with students, with the ability to foster inclusion, collaboration and a positive student experience. Strong social-media awareness and creativity in producing engaging digital content; experience in video editing or graphic-design tools will be an advantage. Proactive, resourceful and student-centred, demonstrating initiative, sound problem-solving and effective time-management skills. Team-oriented and adaptable, able to work independently and perform under pressure while maintaining professionalism and integrity. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager-Senior-Assistant-Manager--Academic-Learning_R00024778": {
      "title": "Manager/Senior Assistant Manager, Academic Learning (Undergraduate Programmes)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA young, research-intensive university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) is the focal point of entrepreneurship education within the University, Singapore and the region. We are seeking a Manager/Senior Assistant Manager, Academic Learning to lead the planning, governance, and delivery of NTUpreneur’s undergraduate programmes, ensuring the effective execution and continuous development of the Second Major in Entrepreneurship (SMiE) and Minor in Entrepreneurship (MiE). This role is accountable for maintaining academic quality, ensuring compliance with University policies, and driving programme enhancements through curriculum development, stakeholder alignment, and process optimisation to support NTU’s strategic educational objectives. K e y Responsibilities: 1. Oversee Academic Planning and Programme Management Develop and implement academic operational initiatives, policies, and guidelines to ensure good governance. Oversee planning, management, and coordination of SMiE and MiE Initiate inter-school collaborations and curriculum enhancements Oversee execution of university-wide academic initiatives and strategic plans 2. Manage Academic Programme Operations a. Oversee and monitor student enrolments, withdrawals, and academic progress b. Manage programme and course administration such as: Academic proposal submissions Timetable scheduling Instructor engagement and deployment Instructor appreciation Course registration Teaching facilities and logistics Results review and processing Ensure proper setup of course sites (NTULearn) Student Feedback in Teaching (SFT) and instructor evaluation student progression tracking Student Advisory (academic) c. Coordinate with Office of Academic Services (OAS) on candidature matters eg. verify SMiE and MiE awards for graduation d. Manage course approvals, submissions, and course mapping for outbound exchanges for students across the University e. Oversee inbound exchange students with course selections and approvals 3. Ensure Academic Governance & Policy Compliance Ensure adherence to NTU’s academic guidelines, practices, policies, and university-wide regulations. Review and implement academic policy updates periodically or when required, ensuring all curriculum changes and practices are aligned with NTU’s framework. Develop and maintain processes to track curriculum compliance, course approvals, and regulatory adherence. 4. Strengthen Stakeholder Engagement           Act as the liaison between faculty, NTU administration, and Joint Programme Partners. Manage relationships with academic partners, industry associations, and professional bodies to enhance programme offerings. Collaborate with faculty and external stakeholders to support cross-disciplinary entrepreneurship education. 5. Manage Process Improvement & Quality Assurance  Conduct regular curriculum reviews and teaching evaluations to maintain programme excellence. Review and optimise academic workflows and operational processes. Ensure adherence to academic integrity, governance, and quality standards. Implement best practices to improve efficiency in academic operations. 6. Plan and Oversee Publicity & Course Development   Initiate collaborations with the Student Engagement and Development (SED) arm to execute marketing strategies to increase enrolment for SMiE, MiE, and elective courses. Work with academic leadership to analyse student demand and design/develop new/enhanced credit-bearing courses. Oversee the process of recruitment and engagement of faculty and instructors. Collaborate with SED to implement outreach initiatives to promote NTUpreneur’s academic programmes. 7. Manage Sub-team & Budget Planning          Oversee and mentor the Academic Management and Operations team to ensure high performance. Develop and monitor budget allocations for academic operations. Prepare and present reports for management and key stakeholders. Ensure the team meets annual performance targets and strategic goals. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university with at least 6 years of experience in academic administration, programme management, or higher education operations Strong background in faculty coordination, curriculum development, and academic policy implementation Proven ability to manage teams, ensuring smooth academic operations and effective collaboration with faculty and instructors. Excellent organisational and problem-solving skills to handle multiple academic processes efficiently Strong analytical and critical thinking abilities to assess programme performance, policy implications, and operational improvements. Meticulous attention to detail to ensure accuracy in academic records, reporting, and policy implementation Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and academic management systems Effective interpersonal and communication (written and verbal) skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with students, faculty, University and external stakeholders Proactive, self-motivated, and adaptable, capable of working independently and within a team in a fast-paced academic environment We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Graduate-Career-Development_R00025115": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Graduate Career Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Business School competes with leading business schools globally to attract high-calibre professionals from diverse backgrounds to its graduate programmes. As part of Graduate Studies, the Career Development Office supports postgraduate students in their career development, leadership growth and employment outcomes throughout their learning journey. The position holder will provide leadership for the MBA Cluster within the Career Development Office, overseeing career development initiatives, leadership programmes, student engagement and employment outcomes across the MBA, Executive MBA (EMBA), Professional MBA (PMBA) and Nanyang Fellows (NF) programmes. Working closely with internal and external stakeholders, the role will drive strategic initiatives to enhance student success, strengthen industry partnerships and maintain the School's reputation for delivering outstanding graduate outcomes. What you will be working on: 1. Career Development strategy and implementation: Engage with leadership to identify and drive strategic initiatives to keep career services at the forefront of providing optimal and efficient services; Provide thought leadership to the team on initiatives to capitalise or respond to changes in environmental/ social/ economic factors impacting jobs for MBAs; Lead the careers team in providing multi-faceted career workshops, networking events and company presentations, to get students career-ready. Work closely with Graduate Studies leadership to develop and implement strategic initiatives that enhance student success and career outcomes. Analyse employment trends, student feedback and market intelligence to inform career development strategies and service enhancements. 2. Drive leadership and strategy for MBA Cluster: Develop and execute the strategic vision for the MBA Cluster, aligning career development offerings with student needs and market trends; Lead cross-functional initiatives to enhance the MBA career journey, from student onboarding through to post-graduation outcomes; Collaborate closely with Employer Engagement team to strengthen industry relationships and expand recruitment opportunities for MBA talent; Monitor industry shifts and student feedback to continuously refine the MBA career strategy and service delivery model. Lead initiatives to strengthen employment outcomes, student engagement and graduate employability across MBA programmes. Ensure career development initiatives support programme objectives, rankings performance and institutional priorities. 3. Lead and oversee Career Leads and Senior Career Fellows within the MBA Cluster: Lead, coach, and develop a team of Career Leads to deliver high-impact career advisory services to students; Set team goals, monitor performance metrics, and provide regular feedback to ensure alignment with office-wide objectives; Facilitate regular team meetings and one-on-one check-ins to drive collaboration, professional development, and knowledge sharing; Collaborate with other departments (e.g., academic programs, employer relations) to align career support with broader NBS goals; Oversee the recruitment, onboarding, deployment and performance of Senior Career Fellows to ensure high-quality coaching services. Establish quality standards and monitor the effectiveness of coaching interventions delivered by Senior Career Fellows. Facilitate collaboration and knowledge sharing among Career Leads and Senior Career Fellows to ensure a consistent student experience. 4. Lead career offerings for EMBAs, PMBAs and NFs Spearhead engagement with postgraduate students enrolled in these programmes, to deliver targeted leadership career offerings; Identify leadership needs of EMBAs and PMBAs, and recommend updates to content of career offerings by the team ; Manage the design and delivery of leadership development programmes, including identifying and engaging qualified instructors, industry leaders and Senior Career Fellows to deliver impactful learning experiences. 5. Provide guidance on all matters related to career development offerings for MBA students: Lead MBA team in delivering a suite of career offerings to MBA students, with view to helping students achieve their career aspirations; Work with NTU/NBS and external stakeholders in ensuring all relevant job and internship opportunities are availed to MBA students in a timely manner; Develop MBA engagement strategies to keep student satisfaction at a high level; Provide counselling to MBA students where required; Work with MBA team to identify skills required to help MBAs be career-ready; Ensure the integrity, accuracy and timely submission of employment outcomes data for MBA and NF programmes to support rankings, accreditation and institutional reporting requirements . 6. Partner employer engagement team to secure full-time jobs and internship opportunities for MBA students: Provide insights on job aspirations of MBAs to employer engagement team, and co-develop employer engagement strategies to help place MBA students in good jobs; Maintain understanding of market factors (national & global) relative to employer organisations, and build partnerships with companies providing jobs and internships/industry projects; Manage relationships with industry leaders with a view to having these leaders provide industry insights and career coaching to students. Analyse employment outcomes and hiring trends to identify opportunities to strengthen employer engagement strategies and student outcomes. Partner with Employer Engagement colleagues to develop targeted employer outreach strategies for MBA talent. What we are looking for in the person: Bachelor's degree from a recognised university is required. MBA or other relevant postgraduate qualification is preferred. At least 15 years of relevant professional experience, including leadership responsibility for teams, programmes, projects or stakeholder networks. Demonstrated track record in developing and executing strategic initiatives and managing complex stakeholder relationships. Strong understanding of talent markets, career development, leadership development and workforce trends. Experience engaging and influencing senior executives, industry leaders and postgraduate students. Proven coaching, facilitation and counselling experience, with the ability to support professionals at different career stages. Experience in career services and/or higher education, preferably within a business school environment, is advantageous. Excellent communication, presentation and stakeholder management skills. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate market insights into actionable strategies. A collaborative and proactive team player who demonstrates initiative, sound judgement and a commitment to excellence. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Head--Administration_R00024411": {
      "title": "Head, Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs the School Head of Administration, this role leads the development and implementation of organizational strategies, policies, standards, structures, systems and practices to achieve the overall goals of the School. Overseeing business operations, processes, initiatives and resources, the role provides integrated efficient and effective administrative services within the school, that are aligned with the School’s strategic goals and objectives and the University’s policies and processes. This role provides foremost support to the School Management on strategizing and setting up of new initiatives, such as Capital Campaigns, Continuing Education, Community Engagement and External Relations. Job Responsibilities: Strategic Planning and Implementation Work closely with the Chair in charting the strategic directions and roadmaps of the School in alignment with the University’s goals. Work with the central administrative offices and College to align and coordinate workflow processes between functions and departments within NTU. Drive administrative excellence as a potential strategic advantage for the University. Oversee strategic communications at the School Oversee and coordinate technical operations in the school including close collaboration with IT and pathway coordinators for Animation/Games, Visual Communication/Photography, Cinematic Arts and Transversal Design. Organization and Operations Excellence Accountable for all functional operations and administrative matters of the School. This includes (but is not limited to) areas in outreach and communications, specialized technical and technological laboratory support, international relations, research and grant administration, student care, facilities and general administration. Partner with respective functional business partners to address the school’s needs related to human resources, IT, finance and procurement. Oversee and optimize the use of resources and develop systems and processes to support the initiatives of the School with adherence to corporate policies and guidelines. Proactively develop, review and drive improvements in the School’s structure, systems, policies, processes and work to enhance organizational effectiveness. Analyze statistical data and make recommendations on report and proposal submissions to the Chair. Oversee planning and execution of student exchange programs and the School’s major events. Budget Planning and Allocation Oversee the overall financial operations of the school including financial reporting and analysis, budget planning and monitoring, as well as asset management, for financial effectiveness. Serve as an advisor to the Chair and Associate Chairs to ensure that the overall School’s operations are in accordance with the University’s policies and guidelines. Job Requirements: Degree from a recognized university with at least 15 years of relevant professional experience, including leadership responsibilities in administration or operations. Extensive relevant work experience, including leadership experience in operations, administration, or a related field. Experience in a Senior Managerial or Leadership role with a track record of effective performance will be advantageous. Experience in higher education or a related environment will be an advantage. Familiarity with technical operations or IT processes relevant to art, design, or media environments is beneficial. Strong stakeholder management, collaboration and conflict resolution skills . Strong operational experience, IT savvy and proven managerial experience in strategic and financial budgeting planning Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams and drive operational improvements Demonstrated strategic thinking and analytical capabilities with initiative, sound judgement and resourcefulness in problem solving. Highly adaptable, self-motivated and proactive in managing evolving priorities and new challenges Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to build a sense of community within the school. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Academic-Learning_R00017784": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Academic Learning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA young and research intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides entrepreneurship education within the University and the region. The Senior Assistant Manager is responsible for leading and executing the business development initiatives and overall operation of Master of Science in Technopreneurship and Innovation Programme (MSc TIP) and FlexiMasters in Technopreneurship and Innovation (FM TIP). The incumbent will work closely with the lead of the postgraduate team, Academic Director and Deputy Director of NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) for successful delivery of MSc TIP and FM TIP. The incumbent will be driving marketing and outreach, carrying out student recruitment and admission, student and alumni engagement, budgeting and financing, and ensuring all policy and procedures are adhered to. S/he will provide/present marketing strategy and analysis for information and decision, oversee and track follow up actions, work closely with lead, PG team to ensure quality, quantity and diversity of recruitment. S/he will also work with the various NTUpreneur teams and the various Offices in the university for cross programme promotion and inter-department joint activities. The incumbent will oversee various I&E activities and engagements to enhance the experiential learning. S/he will also support venture internship, expanding the industry network for placement of venture internship. The incumbent is expected to supervise executive / senior executive to ensure strong value proposition and to achieve excellence in administration.  Key Responsibilities 1. Lead and execute the business development Initiative of the Masters and FlexiMasters in Technopreneurship and Innovation Programme (MSc TIP and FM TIP) Conduct market researches, data analysis and organise information for marketing strategy for MSc TIP and FM TIP. Organise and coordinate programme outreach in a timely and cost-effective manner. Initiate and organise discussion with various partners and stake holders for program outreach. 2. Oversee marketing and recruitment.  Plan and organise programme info sessions and lead the content development for programme publicity. Organise and coordinate local and overseas roadshows and info sessions.  Prepare programme collaterals Oversee digital marketing campaign Create social media contents and consolidate alumni success stories 3. Track and follow up on effectiveness of outreach and adjust the marketing approach accordingly Follow up on various marketing efforts to track the effectiveness. Enhance programme branding. 4. Oversee student management, student wellbeing, alumni engagement and oversee administrative support  Attend to student queries, well being and integration. Plan and execute student engagement activities. Oversee administrative support required for sound implementation of the Programme 5. Oversee experiential learning Oversee the experiential learning such as company visit or ecosystem exposure. Oversee the Venture Internship elective module to ensure proper running and documentation. 6. Plan and oversee the operating budget and grant of the Programme Plan and oversee the operating budget for running both MSc TIP and FM TIP.. Process claims from grants, where available. Attend to audit query and exercise. Key Competencies & Qualification Bachelor degree in any discipline from a recognized university Preferably with 3 to 5 years relevant work experience in university environment  Knowledge in entrepreneurship and the start-up ecosystem Knowledge in marketing, branding and project management Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Experience in working with professors and students, government agencies and international organisations will be advantageous Good verbal and written communication skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Programme-Management-and-Student-Administration_R00024245": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Programme Management and Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position is part of the academic arm within the Undergraduate Programmes Office (UPO) and is required to lead and support the daily operations in UPO, enhancing the overall NBS student experience. Responsibilities: Oversee the proper planning, implementation and smooth delivery of the programme with Programme Director. Provide timely UAPP updates and reports to management. Oversee and manage the administration of undergraduate mid-term scholarships processes, University/College-level awards, and NBS Financial Aid applications. Oversee and manage with Academic Support Units to manage the Student Feedback on Teaching (SFT). Process students’ requests to manage appeals and provide recommendations. Reviewing and approving Students’ Leave of Absence applications. Review, provide advisory to all matters relating to candidature matters and assess any anomalies in progression pathways. Referral to respective support as and when necessary, such as UPO Student Care Team. Process Re-admission, withdrawal and termination student matters. Responsible for all freshmen credit transfer annually. Review, evaluate, update and provide advisory on course exemption matters. Provide academic advisory to students. Support ad hoc projects, events, and outreach activities. Requirements: A Bachelor’s degree from a recognized university. Possess minimum 6 years of relevant working experience, preferably in the education sector. Prior experience in a relevant administrative role in an institution of higher learning will be advantageous. Strong people management and leadership skills; Supervisory experience is required. Influencer with good interpersonal and communications skills to work well with people collaboratively. Self-motivated, resourceful, and flexible in adjusting and responding to changing priorities. Ability to work independently and as a team, personal initiative, and team spirit in the effective implementation of projects. Ability to lead the team by providing clear direction, supporting team members, and ensuring tasks are completed effectively and on time. Ability to manage multiple stakeholders, multi-task and deliver with quality and timeliness. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, planning and organizational abilities. Organised and meticulous with an eye for details. Proficient in Microsoft Office application. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Corporate-Services_R00024691": {
      "title": "Manager, Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Manager, Administration supports the Head of Corporate Services in strengthening operational governance, management reporting, and administrative coordination across the School. Acting as central liaison between senior leadership teams, administrative units, central university departments, the role supports the oversight of internal operations and coordination of across functional teams such as finance, HR, IT, planning, compliance and resource management. Additionally, the role focuses on improving visibility of operational and financial information, developing structured dashboards and reporting frameworks, and supporting cross-functional coordination among administrative units. The Manager will also contribute to process improvements, risk monitoring, and the consolidation of information relating to key school initiatives, including events and collaborations across units. Working closely with the Head of Corporate Services and in coordination with the Chief of Staff, the role supports leadership discussions by providing structured insights and improving the clarity and consistency of operational information to support implementation and execution. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Management, Finance, Public Administration, or a related discipline. At least 6–10 years of relevant experience in operations management, administration, consulting, or programme management roles. Strong analytical skills with the ability to consolidate and interpret operational or financial data. Experience in preparing management reports or dashboards to support leadership decision-making. Strong stakeholder management and communication skills. Ability to coordinate initiatives across multiple departments in a complex organisational environment. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Counsellor---Counsellor--BEACON-_R00025492": {
      "title": "Senior Counsellor / Counsellor (BEACON)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout the role Student wellbeing and support is a top priority and a key foundation for NTU Education 2025. It enables NTU students to thrive and flourish in their educational journey. As a Counsellor in NTU, you will play a crucial role to enable NTU to fulfil its mission for student wellbeing and support. As a team member of the University Counselling Centre, you will provide counselling for undergraduate and graduate students and engage with various internal and external stakeholders to promote a NTU campus community approach to mental health. BEACON is a satellite counselling service provided by the University Counselling Centre, designed to make professional counselling more accessible and convenient for students. The BEACON Counsellor provides short-term counselling support to students experiencing mild mental health issues, academic stress and interpersonal issues within the assigned colleges and/or schools. This includes provision of clinical services through different modes of counselling, i.e. face-to-face or online, developing strategies, planning and implementing counselling-related programmes, including referrals to relevant agencies. The Senior Counsellor / Counsellor will conduct practice-based research and facilitates outreach, trainings and programmes for the NTU community. A proactive, resourceful and compassionate professional, the BEACON Counsellor works under supervision as part of a collaborative team. The key responsibilities include: Counselling assessments and interventions Provide short-term professional counselling services, including conducting risk and need assessments and delivering intervention plans over a variety of modes and approaches such as in person or online, within the assigned colleges and/or schools Facilitate case formulation, including preparation of assessment reports, delivery of case presentations, and referrals to relevant organisations within social services ecosystem Provide guidance to less experienced BEACON counsellors in challenging cases in alignment with protocol for escalation of emergency cases Escalate and co-lead sensitive crisis cases with more experienced mental health practitioners Provide consultation to staff on concerns they have regarding students at-risk Identify gaps in counselling tools and frameworks for local contexts and propose recommendations for greater cultural contextualisation to supervisors Provide inputs for improvements in counselling programmes and services Design, develop and/or facilitate wellbeing training initiatives and wellbeing portfolio / project annually Maintain professional, legal and ethical standards Adhere to professional standards in clinical, legal and ethical practices, ensuring client consent and confidentiality and proper data privacy protocol in counselling Monitor staff adherence to professional standards in clinical, legal and ethical practices and assist in the development of clear data privacy protocol Assist in development of quality improvement projects to improve client care and services Document and maintain proper clinical records in accordance with policies and procedures of the University Counselling Centre. Use data-driven insights to identify gaps and drive improvements to counselling in line with the organisation's strategic direction Demonstrate expertise in counselling, pursuing additional trainings in specialised areas and developing a professional point of view Community approach to case intervention Work collaboratively with and make recommendations to schools, student service offices, Halls of Residence, Support and Care Team, etc. to facilitate a campus community approach towards managing students with mild to moderate mental health issues Work in inter-disciplinary teams (e.g. Educational/Clinical/ Counselling Psychologist, Counsellor) to provide evidence-based psychotherapeutic interventions/treatment to students with mild to moderate mental health issues and/or co-morbid issues (e.g. Special Education Needs and mental health issues) Leads NTU community, i.e. colleges and schools, outreach initiatives Liaise with other professionals (e.g. psychiatrists, doctors) and Social Service Agencies to mobilise community resources to provide care and support for the students Refer and/or recommend external service interventions (e.g. family therapy) as part of the student’s overall treatment plan Administrative support in University Counselling Centre (UCC) Support the daily operations of UCC, ensuring efficient and effective functioning Engage in data analysis and collation Perform additional duties as assigned by Head, UCC or Director, UWO The requirements include : Master’s degree in counselling Clinical member and registered counsellor with the Singapore Association for Counselling (SAC) At least five (5) years of professional counselling experience Proficiency in professional counselling approaches and tools to help clients with diverse issues and conditions Experience in working with young adults, preferably in an educational setting Experience in working in a multi-disciplinary team is advantageous Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining accuracy in all operational aspects Strong organisational and multitasking skills, with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple tasks and responsibilities Possess professional values that are in line with the Code of Ethics of SAC Possess good interpersonal and communication skills Proficiency in IT skills (e.g. Microsoft 365, use of Apps, appointment booking systems, case management systems) A good team player who is able to work independently We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Wireless-Power-Transfer-_R00025485": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Wireless Power Transfer)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Senior Research Fellow (SRF) who will develop, optimise, and validate wireless power transfer (WPT) systems for electric vehicle charging roadway applications. The SRF will contribute to Double-D coil-based WPT system design, electromagnetic simulation, magnetic coupling enhancement, electromagnetic shielding evaluation, and laboratory validation in a multidisciplinary research project involving civil and electrical engineering. Key Responsibilities: Developing and optimising Double-D coil-based WPT systems Simulating WPT efficiency, electromagnetic field distribution, impedance matching, and misalignment tolerance using electromagnetic simulation tools. Designing and evaluating surfaces and/or dielectric matching layers to improve magnetic coupling Evaluating electromagnetic shielding performance and electromagnetic field safety compliance Developing laboratory measurement setups to validate WPT efficiency, shielding effectiveness, lateral misalignment tolerance, and system robustness. Analysing simulation and experimental results, preparing technical reports, publishing research findings, and supporting project milestones. Working closely with PhD/MSc students, undergraduate students, and collaborators from civil and electrical engineering disciplines. Job Requirements: PhD in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Applied Electromagnetics, Power Electronics, Wireless Power Transfer, or closely related fields. More than 5 years of research experience in wireless power transfer, electromagnetic compatibility/interference, electromagnetic shielding, antenna/coil design, or related areas. Experience in electromagnetic simulation tools Experience in WPT coil design, resonant inductive coupling, impedance matching, magnetic-field analysis, and efficiency optimisation. Experience with laboratory measurements for WPT, electromagnetic shielding, or RF/low-frequency electromagnetic systems. Good publication record in relevant research areas. Proficiency in MATLAB, Python, C/C++, or equivalent tools for simulation, data analysis, and automation. Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to work in a multidisciplinary research team. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Power-System-Risk-_R00025490-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Power System Risk)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to work on a project in the area of power system risk modeling and assessment .  Key Responsibilities: Develop a probabilistic security assessment framework for heterogeneous operational uncertainties and contingencies Develop a comprehensive framework for evaluating the criticality of contingency events considering multiple impacts  Develop a coordinated and risk-averse optimization framework for interconnected power grid operation considering low-probability-high-impact contingency events Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering or related subjects. Expert knowledge in power system risk analysis We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Power-System-Stability-_R00025489-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Power System Stability)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to work on a project in the area of interconnected power system stability analysis and control .  Key Responsibilities: Develop a measurement-based approach to derive the static and dynamic equivalence of the external grids Establish a stochastic differential algebraic equation (SDAE) based analytic framework for interdependent electromechanical and electromagnetic dynamics modelling and analysis Design data-driven methods for power system stability assessment and control with stochastic resources Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering or related subjects. Expert knowledge in power system stability area We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Analog-in-memory-computing-macros-_R00025491": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Analog in-memory computing macros)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a  Research Fellow to conduct research in the area of analog/mixed-signal integrated circuit design . The role will focus on the development of analog in-memory computing macros for AI accelerators. Experience in tape-outs and industry will be highly appreciated for this role. Key Responsibilities: Leading analog in-memory-computing macro design Leading analog-to-digital converter development Leading test chip development Leading test chip testing Job Requirements: PhD qualification degree in integrated circuit design or related field At least 2~3 years of relevant experiences in industry / technical hands-on experience in analog/mixed-signal integrated circuit design Familiarity with research environment Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in industry-standard design tools and tape-out flows Competent in presentation skills We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Integrated-Polaritonic-Devices-_R00025479": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Integrated Polaritonic Devices)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Fellow at NTU’s National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP) will support the development of integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, focusing on long-range polariton propagation, low-energy switching, few-particle modulation of condensate nonlinearities, integrated polaritonic circuit functions, and coupling of polaritonic states with on-chip detection and readout architectures. The role will involve advanced optical spectroscopy and characterization techniques, including real-space and Fourier-space imaging, polarization- and time-resolved measurements, room-temperature and cryogenic testing, while working closely with device integration teams to advance integrated polaritonic systems. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to conduct research in integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, including the design, fabrication, optimization and experimental characterization of polaritonic waveguides, polariton lasers, cavity/waveguide networks, and polaritonic circuit elements. Design, fabricate, assemble, optimize and experimentally characterize integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides. Develop and operate optical spectroscopy setups involving real-space/Fourier-space imaging, polarization-resolved spectroscopy, time-resolved photoluminescence, electroluminescence, and room-temperature and/or cryogenic measurements. Investigate low-power and few-particle polaritonic effects, including condensate nonlinearities, low-energy switching, single- or few-polariton emission regimes, photon-correlation behaviour, and routes toward polaritonic logic or routing functions. Develop long-range polaritonic waveguiding platforms, polariton propagation measurements, electrical or optical routing schemes, and integration of polaritonic waveguides with single-photon detection where relevant. Collaborate with photonic device integration teams and CDPT partners to support device fabrication, assembly, testing and prototype demonstration. Operate and maintain research laboratories, including advanced microscopy and spectroscopy equipment, in compliance with safety and laboratory protocols. Perform data analysis and interpretation, prepare scientific publications, contribute to research reports and IP disclosures, and present findings at international conferences. Collaborate with internal and external partners on joint research projects and technology development. Contribute to progress reports, project meetings, day-to-day laboratory operations, future grant proposals, and the development and protection of intellectual property. Requirements: PhD in Physics, Optical/Photonic Engineering, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related discipline. Relevant research experience in experimental optics, optical spectroscopy, photonics, exciton-polariton physics, nonlinear optics, semiconductor optics, polaritonic waveguides, or related fields. Proven publication record in reputable international peer-reviewed journals. Hands-on experience in optical system design, alignment, operation, and advanced characterization techniques, including laser-based and imaging setups. Competent in scientific programming and data analysis (e.g., Python/Matlab), with strong communication skills and the ability to work independently and collaboratively within a research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Satellite-Communications-_R00025480": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Satellite Communications)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Temasek Laboratories@NTU, our mission is to undertake cutting-edge research in defence science and technology, driving new solutions and advancements across various research areas, including Microsystems Technology, Hardware Assurance, Signal Processing, Advanced Materials, Advanced Laser Technology, and Emerging Technologies. We take immense pride in our people, recognizing them as our greatest asset. Committed to nurturing professional development, we support personal aspirations and growth. Furthermore, we advocate for a healthy work-life balance, fostering yearly engagement and team bonding activities. We invite you to join our Centre for Communications and Signal Processing as a Research Scientist. This centre focus on developing advanced communications and signal processing capabilities for the Singapore defense community. The four key research areas are sensor array, signal processing systems, urban sensing and signal research. We are looking for a Research Scientist with a strong foundation in all aspects of Satellite communications. The researcher is expected to contribute towards addressing the detection, classification and localization of satellite communication terminal. Key Responsibilities:  The candidate will be expected to conduct research in passive detection, classification and geolocation of specifically the localization of unknown ground terminals from LEO NTN signals in harsh environments. The candidate will be responsible for both theoretical development and experimental design to validate the developed methods against real data. Supervise interns and students; review state-of-the-art literature; plan and execute R&D activities to meet project objectives and deadlines; generate and publish novel scientific contributions and support research proposals. Administrative duties may include safety management, asset management, and other assigned responsibilities. Job Requirements:  PhD in Electrical & Electronics Engineering, Communications, or a related field. Strong background in statistical signal processing, estimation theory, detection and classification, waveform-based geolocation, and machine learning/deep learning, with demonstrated research experience in passive localization and tracking using signals of opportunity from LEO NTN systems such as Starlink, Iridium, or similar satellite constellations. Proficiency with SDR platforms, particularly Ettus USRP devices and GNU Radio / UHD programming. Proficiency in Python and/or MATLAB; C++ is an advantage. Proficiency in satellite communications systems, NTN architectures, satellite ephemeris correction methods, and orbital simulation tools (STK, GMAT, Orekit, or equivalent) is desirable. Strong publication record commensurate with career stage. Strong communication skills, with the ability to convey complex technical concepts clearly and concisely. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Satellite-Communications-_R00025478": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Satellite Communications)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Temasek Laboratories@NTU, our mission is to undertake cutting-edge research in defence science and technology, driving new solutions and advancements across various research areas, including Microsystems Technology, Hardware Assurance, Signal Processing, Advanced Materials, Advanced Laser Technology, and Emerging Technologies. We take immense pride in our people, recognizing them as our greatest asset. Committed to nurturing professional development, we support personal aspirations and growth. Furthermore, we advocate for a healthy work-life balance, fostering yearly engagement and team bonding activities. We invite you to join our Centre for Communications and Signal Processing as a Research Scientist. This centre focus on developing advanced communications and signal processing capabilities for the Singapore defense community. The four key research areas are sensor array, signal processing systems, urban sensing and signal research. We are looking for a Research Scientist with a strong foundation in all aspects of Satellite communications. The researcher is expected to contribute towards addressing the detection, classification and localization of satellite communication terminal. Key Responsibilities:  The candidate will be expected to lead and conduct research in passive RF sensing, specifically the detection, characterization, and parameter estimation of NTN waveforms from LEO satellite systems in harsh environments. The candidate will be responsible for both theoretical development of waveform estimation methods and hands-on SDR experimental design to validate the developed methods. Additional responsibilities include supervise interns and students; review state-of-the-art literature; plan and execute R&D activities to meet project objectives and deadlines; generate and publish novel scientific contributions and support research proposals. Administrative responsibilities may include safety management, asset management, and other duties as required. Job Requirements:  PhD in Electrical & Electronics Engineering, Communication Engineering or a related field. Strong expertise in wireless communications, digital signal processing, physical-layer waveform analysis, and passive RF interception, with experience in LEO satellite communications and NTN systems (e.g., Starlink, Iridium). Proficiency in satellite link budget analysis, NTN architectures, orbital mechanics, and tools such as STK, GMAT, or Orekit for LEO pass and Doppler analysis. Experience in wireless channel modelling for LEO satellite links, including atmospheric propagation effects. Proficiency in Python and/or MATLAB; C++ is an added advantage. Knowledge of machine learning/deep learning for signal processing and receiver design is desirable. Experience with SDR platforms, particularly Ettus USRP devices, and GNU Radio/UHD development is an advantage. Strong publication record commensurate with career stage. Strong communication skills, with the ability to convey complex technical concepts clearly and concisely. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Wireless-Cellular-Security-_R00025477": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Wireless/Cellular Security)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe invite suitable candidate to join a strong research team in Temasek Laboratories@NTU with the following requisites: Key Responsibilities:  The candidate is expected to conduct and guide research in Wireless and Cellular Security, in particular the discovery of novel wireless attacks and their detection and mitigations. The candidate is expected to conduct both theoretical development of methods and experiment design to validate the developed methods. Other research responsibilities include supervising junior researchers/interns/students, carrying out detailed literature reviews and assessment of the state-of-the-art technologies. planning and executing detailed R&D activities to meet project objectives and deadlines, generating novel scientific or technological concepts for application of breakthrough nature and contributing to research proposals. Administrative responsibilities may include safety, asset management and other aspects related to being a member of Temasek Labs@NTU. Job Requirements:  PhD degree in Computer Science, Computer & Electronics Engineering or other related fields Strong background and knowledge in at least one or preferably more of the following fields: Cybersecurity, Deep Learning and software engineering with at least 3-5 years of research experience (including PhD training) in related fields. Proven track record in research and development of cybersecurity and/or Deep Learning technologies. Strong publication record in top cybersecurity or systems conferences/journals (e.g., USENIX Security, NDSS, ASE, TSE, TIFS, ICSE, FSE, ICST etc.) Strong programming skills in C/C++, python etc. Knowledge of Electrical or Software Engineering and Cybersecurity are plus. Good writing skills for writing proposals, reports and publications in good academic journals Completed application forms with detailed resumes may be submitted via email to Dr Sirajudeen Gulam Razul (esirajudeen@ntu.edu.sg) with the subject ‘Application for the Position of Research Scientist (Wireless / Cellular Security)’. Appointment grade and starting salary will depend on the candidates’ qualification and relevant experience. Qualified applicants are invited to send in their application on the prescribed form obtainable form: http://www.ntu.edu.sg/ohr/career/submit-an-application/Pages/Research-Positions.aspx Electronic submission of applications is highly encouraged. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Head--Strategic-Planning---Engagement--NIE-_R00025472": {
      "title": "Assistant Head, Strategic Planning & Engagement [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Assistant Head, Strategic Planning & Engagement in the department of Strategic Planning & Engagement (SPE), NIE Director’s Office. Responsibilities Assist the HOD in overseeing and executing NIE’s strategic planning and engagement processes through ─ Providing effective secretariat support and follow-through for key leadership and board meetings to drive effective executive-level decision-making.  Developing, monitoring, communicating and reporting on institutional strategic initiatives and success indicators. Conceptualising, organising and managing appropriate strategic engagement activities for the NIE senior leadership, appointment holders and senior staff – including leadership retreats, annual strategic reviews, annual addresses, etc. Supporting and facilitating specific cross-institutional project initiatives arising from the Strategic Plan such as Steering Committees / Taskforces / Programme Reviews / Strategic Projects. Support the HOD in the management of NIE-level intellectual property. Support the HOD in the management of the office, which may include the department’s budget, assets and physical spaces. Assist in special or ad-hoc projects / institutional events as assigned by the HOD / reporting officer. Requirements A University degree. Minimally 3 to 5 years of relevant working experience with a strong interest and/or track record in strategic planning, organisational development and/or copywriting and editing. Excellent conceptualisation and analytical skills. Excellent written communication and copywriting skills. Highly meticulous and able to analyse / make sense of large quantities of text and numerical information on a daily basis. Working knowledge of statistics and/or data analysis an advantage. Some working knowledge of corporate work planning and budgeting at the organisation level will be useful. High proficiency in MS Office with some working knowledge of document / information management systems. Strong team player with a pleasant disposition. Strong ability to work independently under pressure and to meet tight timelines. Willingness to learn and develop capabilities and to acquire and share new knowledge. Values and attributes demonstrating integrity, professionalism and a service mentality. Working experience in a public-funded educational institution would be advantageous. Application Closing Date 26 August 2026 Application We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other information NIE Staff can take chartered buses at their own expenses from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--HR-Partnering_R00023646": {
      "title": "Director, HR Partnering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nShape the future of HR at a leading university. Reporting to the Chief Human Resource Officer, the Director of Human Resource Business Partners (HRBP) will lead a dynamic team in driving strategic HR initiatives that empower people, strengthen culture, and advance the university’s mission. This is a high‑impact leadership role for someone passionate about building engaged HR Partnering teams and delivering exceptional HR experiences. Strategic Leadership Design and implement HR strategies aligned with the university’s vision and objectives. Partner with the Chief HR Officer to define HR priorities and lead enterprise-wide initiatives. Team Management Lead, mentor, and develop a team of HR Business Partners to deliver strategic HR guidance across all functions. Build a collaborative, high-performing, and results-oriented team environment. Business Partnering Establish strong relationships with university leadership and departments to understand and address HR needs. Serve as a trusted advisor, offering insights and recommendations on HR-related matters. Drive employee engagement and proactively manage employee relations throughout the employee lifecycle. Collaborate with the Talent Acquisition Centre of Excellence (COE) to ensure timely recruitment of talent with the right competencies. Champion organizational excellence, job redesign, and resource optimization through transformative HR initiatives. Promote business ownership of talent by coaching managers on career development and leadership growth. HR Policy Centre of Excellence Review and refine HR strategies, policies, and procedures specific to Faculty and Research Schemes. Recommend and implement changes to strengthen the delivery of professional HR services. What We’re Looking For Minimum 20 years of HR experience, including at least 10 years in a leadership role. Deep knowledge of the full HR spectrum, with proven ability to lead strategic initiatives. Strong leadership presence with the ability to inspire, coach, and influence without authority. Strategic thinker who thrives in ambiguity and can anticipate future needs. Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills, with a talent for building trust across diverse stakeholders. Resourceful, pragmatic, and solutions‑oriented mindset. Solid understanding of Employment Act and Labour Laws. Why Join Us Impact at scale: Shape HR strategy for one of the region’s leading universities. Leadership opportunity: Build and mentor various HRBP teams Transformative work: Drive initiatives that redefine how the university supports and develops its people. Collaborative culture: Work closely with senior leadership and influence decisions that matter We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/General-Manager--NEC_R00025475": {
      "title": "General Manager, NEC",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Hospitality Unit is part of the NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS), responsible for overseeing, enhancing and optimising the University's hospitality assets to deliver exceptional guest experiences and operational excellence. Through its hospitality assets, the Unit supports NTU's mission and strategic priorities by providing world-class venues for executive education, conferences, events, dining and accommodation, positioning NTU not only as a leading academic institution but also as a premier destination for industry engagement and hospitality. Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is one of the University's flagship hospitality assets managed by the Hospitality Unit. The General Manager (GM) is responsible for providing strategic leadership and overseeing NEC's overall performance, ensuring it delivers outstanding hospitality experiences while supporting the University's academic, commercial and engagement objectives. Key Responsibilities: Provide strategic leadership for NEC, setting its long-term direction and ensuring its hospitality, commercial and business objectives support the University's strategic priorities. Work closely with the appointed hotel operator, the incumbent shall lead the team in ensuring compliance with contractual obligations, agreed service standards and financial targets. Establish NEC's operating and service framework by working with appointed hotel operator to develop and implement Service Level Agreements (SLAs), Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), operational policies, guest service standards, reporting frameworks and performance measures that support the successful operation of NEC. Lead NEC's business and financial planning, including the review of annual business plans, operating budgets, capital expenditure proposals, forecasts and performance reports to ensure financial sustainability and achievement of commercial objectives. Responsible for operational performance through regular performance reviews, operational meetings and site inspections, ensuring agreed standards for guest satisfaction, operational efficiency, quality of service and financial performance are consistently achieved. Lead the planning and enhancement of NEC's hospitality and commercial assets, including maintenance, asset enhancement and lifecycle planning, ensuring the facilities remain safe, well maintained, attractive, fit for purpose and competitive. Lead and develop the NEC team, building a collaborative, stakeholder-centric and high-performing culture while fostering a strong working partnership with the hotel operator and other stakeholders. Identify opportunities to grow NEC's business, improve financial performance and maximise the use of its hospitality, meeting and commercial facilities through new programmes, partnerships and business opportunities. Collaborate closely with University leadership including internal departments, and external partners to ensure NEC supports executive education programmes, conferences, campus events, international engagements, research collaborations and other University priorities. Establish and maintain effective governance and risk management processes, ensuring compliance with legal, regulatory, safety, environmental and sustainability requirements, while overseeing business continuity planning and operational resilience. Monitor market trends, customer feedback and operational performance, using data and industry insights to improve services, strengthen NEC's competitiveness and support informed business decisions. Promote a culture of service excellence, continuous improvement and innovation, ensuring NEC continues to enhance its reputation as NTU's preferred executive hospitality, conference and event venue. Requirements: A Bachelor's/Master's Degree in Hospitality Management, Business Administration, or related field. Minimum 15 years in the hospitality industry with at least 6 years in a leadership role. Proven track record of managing hospitality assets, enhancing customer experiences, and driving profitability. Experience working with hotel management agreements, asset management or owner representation will be advantageous. Experience in managing various functions (eg. Sales & Revenue, Rooms etc) with a high drive for results and commercial acumen. Familiar with budget, P&L reports, revenue management, workforce planning/optimization, sales strategies & segmentation etc. Possess excellent organizational and interpersonal skills. Excellent communication and leadership skill, people-centric yet business-focused. Experience in managing high-value service contracts and strategic partnerships will be advantageous. Extensive experience in fostering and sustaining collaborations with diverse internal and external stakeholders. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow-Research-Fellow--Curatorial-Art-and-Cultural-Studies-Museum-Studies-Visual-Anthropology-Humanities-_R00025226": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Curatorial/Art and Cultural Studies/Museum Studies/Visual Anthropology/Humanities)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Max Planck–NTU Singapore Centre for Biocultural Worlding (CBCW) is seeking to is seeking to appoint one Research Fellow ( Curatorial Research and Practice ) for a two-year term (renewable), based at the NTU Centre for Contemporary Art Singapore. The fellow will be embedded in an interdisciplinary environment, hybrid in nature, with the Centre jointly operating across Singapore and Germany. As the CBCW functions as a research centre where curatorial and artistic research methods, legal inquiry, and diverse knowledge traditions converge to explore new forms of collaboration and stewardship of biocultural worlds, applications from candidates whose research interests align with CBCW’s concerns are welcomed. The focus is on biological, cultural, and epistemic diversity, with an approach that works relationally with, alongside, and across situated, grounded initiatives of novel research, experimentation in the fields of curatorial and artistic practices, and local and indigenous knowledge traditions. Key Responsibilities:  The fellow will conduct independent and collaborative curatorial and artistic research on relevant biocultural worlding topics and forge mutual connections with other CBCW projects. From within the CBCW to public platforms, institutional partnerships, and interventions beyond academic boundaries and museological frameworks, the fellow will advance curatorial and artistic research methods of inquiry to expand epistemic (and material) possibilities, developing new protocols and toolkits for conducting research. Job Requirements: PhD degree in fields of curatorial, art and cultural studies, museum studies, visual anthropology, or other related humanities fields. Knowledge of and practice in curatorial studies, contemporary art, visual culture and cultural anthropology, art history, or other relevant research methods. Outstanding publication achievements in relevant artistic journals, publications, exhibitions and proven visibility in creative projects, whether of international scope or locally specific. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines. Proven ability to work independently and collaboratively in an international, interdisciplinary team. Excellent academic writing skills with high literacy of artistic and scientific vocabularies that extends beyond text-based forms of knowledge. Critically attuned to current curatorial and museological discourse and landscape. Familiarity with how injustices result from imbalances among biological, cultural, and epistemic diversity. Familiarity with, and research experience in Singapore and/or the Asia-Pacific region would be an asset. Please submit your application on Workday, accompanied by the following supporting documents: Cover letter (one-page) and curriculum vitae, including list of publications, conference presentations, creative projects and exhibitions curated or participated in (in a single PDF). A two-page curatorial research proposal (excluding references and annexes) outlining: Proposed topic of the biocultural research. Methodology (specifying key collaborators and knowledge-holding communities) Description of activities and outcomes of the project. Elaboration on how the proposed research will augment the CBCW’s mission and vision. Scanned copies of qualifications (in a single PDF). Two letters of recommendation. For more information, visit the website www.bioculturalworlding.org . For any inquiries about the position, contact us at CBCW@ntu.edu.sg . The deadline for the call has been extended to 15 October 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Semester-Exchange-Programme--Inbound-_R00024218": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Semester Exchange Programme (Inbound)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. SASD works collaboratively with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey for all students. This position sits with the Office of Global Education and Mobility (OGEM), which is responsible for developing, managing and implementing exchange/ immersion programmes for NTU students and for incoming students from other Universities. The successful candidate will be part of the team that supports international students participating in the Semester & Short-Term Inbound Programmes. In addition to this, the incumbent will also support in generic administrative duties for the office.   Key responsibilities:  Ensure the processes for inbound programmes are delivered according to schedule. Process inbound applications for Global Education & Mobility (GEM) Trailblazer Programme.  Manage communication with inbound students’ and partner universities to address enquiries. Engage students for recruitment and provide assistance and support to students. Collate and ensure accuracy of inbound mobility data for reporting and analysis. Monitor the financial transactions and assist with budgeting, accrual, reporting, etc. Provide guidance to colleagues on purchasing procedures. Ensure office materials and resources are available for staff usage. Administrative duties for OGEM – sourcing and procurement of office supplies, finance/budget tracking, onboarding of new staff, manage Director’s calendar. Job Requirements: Degree in any discipline with at least 3 years of experience in administrative and/or student services related roles  Excellent organizational skills and detail-oriented to ensure accurate data is reported.  Customer-oriented mindset, with a commitment to delivering responsive, supportive, and high-quality service to students Strong command of written and verbal communication, with the ability to tailor messages to different audiences. Prior experience in student services, programme administration, or international education is an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Administrative-Support_R00025419": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU has over 32,000 students with close to half of whom reside in campus housing during the academic semester. The Vice Provost (Student Experience)(VP (SE) and AVP(SE) is responsible for ensuring an enriching, safe and meaningful student experience. This entails policy formulation, communication and coordinating the execution of campus wide initiatives with various Colleges, Schools and administrative departments across NTU. It is also important to engage students and other internal and external stakeholders to develop meaningful student experience initiatives and policies to enhance the NTU student experience. Role: Providing effective and efficient administrative and secretariat support to VP/AVPs, you will execute the full spectrum of programmes, tasks and activities, which include (but not limited to) appointment/meeting scheduling, documentation, minutes taking, report compilation and event management.   As an integral administrative member at the Student Experience team, you will also lead or be part of the taskforce in the planning, organization, and management of various meetings between VP/AVPs and other University leaders and department heads from Colleges, Schools and department.  You will also serve to assist the principal staff officer to VP/AVPs in the management of documentation and travel arrangement, prioritization of requests, handling of sensitive information, communication management, management reporting, and facilitation of inputs and recommendations for decision-making. Your key duties included but not limited to the following: Execute core administrative functions  to support VP/AVPs pertaining to student experience matters, information management and stakeholder reporting, ensuring confidentiality, speed and accuracy. Manage VP/AVPs  schedule, appointments, travel arrangements and submission of various claims, including VP/AVPs  role-based email account and calendar. Coordinate and provide logistic support to student experience-related events and visits. Assist with the preparation and collation management reports and presentation slides for VP/AVPs  and think of ways to best present these information concisely to support the intent of the presentation. Provide secretariat support to draft minutes of meeting and disseminate for review and circulation. Requirements: Degree qualification or equivalent, preferably with relevant working experience in IHL environment. At least 10 years of relevant work experience, supporting and working with senior management in a fast-paced and challenging environment. Good planning, organizational and problem-solving skills. Strong interpersonal skills and emotional intelligence. Good written and oral communication skills. Good time management skills. Flexibility and Adaptability in a fast-paced environment. IT savvy with good knowledge in Microsoft Office Applications. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Technical-Specialist--Laboratory-Management_R00025467": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist, Laboratory Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) offers a full range of additive manufacturing services, from design and infrastructure to production and validation. With advanced technologies such as topology optimization, generative design, and bioinspired design, SC3DP creates optimized products using a variety of novel materials and printing processes, including hybrid printing, post-processing, and emerging technologies. Sustainability is a top priority for SC3DP, which offers material development and control services that combine artificial intelligence, big data, and other digital tools for process optimization, as well as non-destructive testing for AM parts. Backed by a team of experts and a state-of-the-art facility equipped with the latest equipment and technologies, SC3DP is committed to leading the way in sustainable additive manufacturing research and development.  The successful applicant will play a critical role in providing operational-level technical expertise to faculty, research staff and students in the Centre while ensuring the safety of its laboratories. Job Responsibilities: Laboratory safety and management Take charge of regulated and unregulated material inventory. Verify the procurement and delivery of controlled items. Interact with equipment, material and chemical suppliers and ensure compliance with legal and safety requirements. Perform chemical verification and radiation safety in accordance with regulations and guidelines. Provide support for managing hazardous substances, which include metallic powders, chemicals, nanomaterials and other materials used in additive manufacturing and its associated secondary processes. Provide support for document control and facilitate the flow of information within the research community. Provide support for safety inspection and safety audit, ensuring all submitted documents are in order. Provide support for office and laboratory access. Ensure that laboratory operations follow relevant national/university safety regulations and occupational health and safety standards. Requirements: Diploma/Bachelor’s Degree in Engineering or related fields with 1 to 3 years of relevant working experience in a research environment. Good written and verbal communication skills . Knowledge of chemicals, radiation and hazardous materials management. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications. Meticulous, pro-active, diligent and able to work independently. Able to work in a dynamic environment. Service oriented team player. A positive attitude towards learning, a strong sense of accountability and a passion for continuous improvement We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Seismology-_R00025460": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Seismology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2008, the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) at Nanyang Technological is a leading research institute dedicated to understanding earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis, climate change, and other environmental challenges in Southeast Asia. Its key strengths include interdisciplinary expertise, advanced geophysical and remote-sensing capabilities, extensive regional field-observation networks, and strong collaborations with academic institutions and government agencies. For more details, please view https://earthobservatory.sg/research. The Earth Observatory of Singapore at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, invites applications for an outstanding Research Fellow with a strong background in earthquake monitoring. The successful candidate will lead and contribute to the development of advanced approaches for investigating earthquake nucleation and propagation mechanisms. The role involves both independent and collaborative research to achieve project objectives, as well as the publication of high-impact journal articles that enhance the international standing of the University. We are looking for a Research Fellow to develop and perform advanced seismic source analysis for both small earthquakes within the Singapore and moderate-large earthquakes in southeast Asia. Key Responsibilities: Apply and develop approaches for advanced earthquake source analysis Apply the developed system to the Singapore and its surrounding seismic data Publish high-impact research articles in leading international journals Assist in the preparation and development of competitive research proposals Support the supervision and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students Job Requirements: PhD degree in seismology and solid geophysics At least 2 years of relevant experience in earthquake monitoring Familiarity with related literature and software Good written and oral communication skills Entry level candidates are welcome to apply EOS seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Seismology-_R00025459": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Seismology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2008, the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) at Nanyang Technological is a leading research institute dedicated to understanding earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis, climate change, and other environmental challenges in Southeast Asia. Its key strengths include interdisciplinary expertise, advanced geophysical and remote-sensing capabilities, extensive regional field-observation networks, and strong collaborations with academic institutions and government agencies. For more details, please view https://earthobservatory.sg/research. The Earth Observatory of Singapore at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, invites applications for an outstanding Research Fellow with a strong background in earthquake monitoring. The successful candidate will lead and contribute to the development of advanced approaches for investigating earthquake nucleation and propagation mechanisms. The role involves both independent and collaborative research to achieve project objectives, as well as the publication of high-impact journal articles that enhance the international standing of the University. We are looking for a Research Fellow to develop and perform advanced seismic source analysis for both small earthquakes within the Singapore and moderate-large earthquakes in southeast Asia. Key Responsibilities: Apply and develop approaches for advanced earthquake source analysis Apply the developed system to the Singapore and its surrounding seismic data Publish high-impact research articles in leading international journals Assist in the preparation and development of competitive research proposals Support the supervision and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students Job Requirements: PhD degree in seismology and solid geophysics At least 2 years of relevant experience in earthquake monitoring Familiarity with related literature and software Good written and oral communication skills Entry level candidates are welcome to apply EOS seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Marketing--Recruitment---Admissions-_R00025458": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager (Marketing, Recruitment & Admissions)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. Nanyang Business School competes with top business schools from around the world to attract applicants from diverse backgrounds to join its graduate programmes. The key purpose of the role is to support student outreach, recruitment and admission functions in order to bring in the best students to join our graduate programmes. This role reports to the Assistant Director of Graduate Studies. Key Responsibilities include but not limited to the following: Coordinate monthly website and blog updates for the Graduate Studies Office Working with agencies on marketing outreach and campaigns Lead generation and nurturing activities with participants Represent programmes at events such as fairs, information sessions, webinars, and coffee chats (local and overseas) Consultation with prospects to advise on programme suitability Effective administration of programme admissions processes Provide a high level of service quality for applicants Key competencies and qualifications requirements: Degree in any field, Business or Marketing preferred. Minimum of 5 years relevant experience Process-oriented mindset Excellent eye for detail Strong marketing, communication and presentation skills Digital literacy in Microsoft Office and general cloud software These competencies are not compulsory, but any would be advantageous: Domain experience in education / graduate studies Experience in B2B, B2C and marketing to Asian countries Skills in visual design, copywriting, web, CMS, data visualization Familiarity in CRM systems, processes, and Marketing Automation Data-driven mindset and project management skills Relevant experience in the healthcare industry We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--R-R-Projects_R00025456": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, R&R Projects",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a strategic and results-driven Senior Assistant Director to lead renovation, upgrading, and development projects across the University campus. In this role, you will oversee a portfolio of multiple high-impact projects, provide leadership to the project team in project execution, and ensure that facilities meet the University’s academic, research, and operational objectives. You will play a pivotal role in shaping the campus developments, optimising utilisation, and establishing divisional project management frameworks, standards, and processes. This position offers exposure to lead complex projects and requires engagement with senior stakeholders across the University. Key Responsibilities: Provide strategic leadership in planning, directing, and delivering complex and high-impact renovation, upgrading, and development projects across the campus. Lead and mentor a team of project officers to efficiently carry out and complete assigned R&R projects ensuring alignment with the University’s operational, academic, and research objectives. Review and approve design proposals, project budgets, and high-value contracts within delegated authority, and resolve escalated project and operational issues. Ensure all project activities adhere to mandatory compliance regulations imposed by research activities. Provide custodial advice on user's requirements for project, encompassing their needs, preferences, desired timeline for completion, and the available funding sources. Lead the appointment and management of consultants, including architects, engineers, and other professionals, to guide the project design process as required. Lead the tender evaluation process, assess contractor submissions, and recommend contract awards. Assess, manage and recommend changes to the project scope or budget arising during project implementation. Regularly monitor the progress of the construction work to ensure timely delivery and proactively identify and mitigate project risks. Oversee site execution to ensure works are carried out safely, comply with quality standards and meet project specifications. Managing construction contracts, including progress payments, variation orders, claims, and contractual obligations.  Oversee compliance with safety, quality, and regulatory standards, and ensure projects are delivered on time and within budget. Requirements: Degree in Architecture, Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or related field. At least 12 years of relevant experience in managing commercial, institutional, or large-scale infrastructure projects, including leadership of multi-disciplinary project team. Strong knowledge in building construction and proficiency in reading construction drawings. Proven project management skills, including expertise in project planning, budgeting, scheduling, risk management, and stakeholder engagement. Knowledge of AutoCAD/REVIT for design purposes and ability to perform accurate measurements will be added advantage. Strong knowledge of procurement practices and construction contract administration, including PSSCOC. Excellent understanding of BCA Green mark requirements. Strong technical capability in reviewing design submissions and supervising consultants.  Experience in monitoring contractor’s performance through Works Order list, site inspection and monthly reports.  Knowledge of specialised research facilities such as cleanrooms, plant growth chambers, vibration-free laboratories, chemical laboratories and data centres, will be an added advantage. Strong understanding of building regulations, renovation practices, space planning principles and regulatory compliance. Demonstrated leadership and people management skills, with the ability to guide project teams and mentor junior staff. Excellent analytical, planning, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to make strategic decisions and drive results. Strong interpersonal and communication skills to effectively engage and influence senior stakeholders. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Psychology-_R00024589": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences at NTU is an interdisciplinary research and teaching hub covering psychology, economics, sociology, and public policy. It focuses on rigorous, high-impact research that informs policy and practice in Singapore and beyond. The School fosters collaboration across academia, government, and industry, supported by strong research infrastructure and a vibrant scholarly community. It is committed to developing future researchers through mentorship, training, and active involvement in research projects. Key Responsibilities: The Research Associate will support the implementation of research projects under the supervision of the Principal Investigator(s). The role involves coordinating participant recruitment and data collection across multiple settings (e.g. preschools, hospitals, and laboratories), while ensuring smooth day-to-day research operations. Key responsibilities include managing and executing studies, supervising and training research assistants and students, and supporting project timelines and administration. The Research Associate will also handle data management (including cleaning, coding, and analysis), ensure compliance with ethical and institutional requirements, and contribute to grant reporting. In addition, the role includes supporting research dissemination efforts, such as preparing manuscripts for peer-reviewed journals and assisting with conference presentations. Job Requirements: Degree in psychology or a related social science field (Master’s preferred) Experience in research with human participants, especially children or families Strong organisational, data management, and project coordination skills Ability to supervise and work collaboratively with students and research staff Good written and verbal communication skills Willingness to work flexibly across different settings and schedules We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Entrepreneurship-Development-Programme_R00025330": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Corporate Leadership and Innovation Programme",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nA young and research intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides education within the University and the region. The incumbent is responsible for developing, promoting and overseeing the business development and implementation of local and international executive programmes. This role will oversee and implement all marketing and promotional activities, to ensure learners’ objectives are met with quality executive programmes. The incumbent is also responsible for ensuring the profitability and sustainability executive programmes, through active seeking and initiating of collaboration opportunities with industry partners and key stakeholders, including Enterprise Singapore and others, and engagement of NTU Entrepreneurship Academy’s (NTUpreneur) Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) and alumni networks. The incumbent will report to the Senior Assistant Director of Corporate Leadership and Innovation Programme (CLIP)  to uphold and enhance the reputation of NTUpreneur, while supporting strategic initiatives of the I&E Office and NTU. Job Responsibilities: 1. Plan marketing strategies to increase business of NTUpreneur’s executive programmes Develop a viable marketing strategy for implementation and design marketing collaterals (digital for social media and global marketing platforms and print for roadshows). Seek potential corporate clients, global executive training platforms and seek business development opportunities. Prepare presentation deck to prospective corporate clients. 2. Facilitate and coordinate to design new and customised executive programmes Oversee the coordination between corporate clients, faculty/ Programme Director and Senior Assistant Director (SAD, CLIP ) to design customised courses for corporate clients. Identify and suggest trending topics, and potential markets for developing new executive programmes. 3. Oversee the implementation of processes to ensure smooth execution of key operations, policies and processes and efficiency in resource management Ensure relevance and quality of courses and quality of instructors hired to teach these courses. Coordinate with NTUpreneur’s Academic Director and NTU’s Professional and Continual Education (PaCE) to oversee the onboarding processes of instructors, mentors and industry partners Plan course schedule and ensure availability of faculty and instructors. Oversee the operation and logistical arrangements of classes to create positive learning experience and environment. Gather and analyse participants feedback, identify areas for improvement, design and implement solutions. 4. Engage stakeholders and develop professional partnerships opportunities Identify individual and corporate stakeholders for partnership. Leverage on their strengths and strong network for the benefit of NTU executive programme learners. Design and implement stakeholder and corporate engagement activities to retain interest, and increase awareness of NTUpreneur’s executive programmes. Identify training grant opportunities and secure collaborations leading to access of these grants for our learners. 5. Oversee Programme’s budget and expenditure plan Oversee annual budget and expenditures and track business performance to ensure a healthy stream of revenue and profits. Plan and deploy resources effectively according to the University’s guidelines. Prepare monthly financial reports and statistics for PaCE and the Director, NTUpreneur. Identify and facilitate the submission of grant application proposals to funding agencies. Oversee the submission of courses to SkillsFuture/ SSG to secure funding support for participants. Requirements: Degree in business or entrepreneurship with at least 3 years of experience in leading CET programme in Institute of Higher Learning or equivalent Experience in working with the government/ quasi-government agencies and administering grant processes and overseeing auditing processes Possess a good network consisting of entrepreneurs, intrapreneurs and industry partners Possess excellent writing and oral communication and presentation skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--CLIC-_R00025445": {
      "title": "Research Associate (CLIC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre for Lifelong Learning and Individualised Cognition CLIC is a research collaboration between the University of Cambridge and Nanyang Technological University (NTU) and hosted by the Cambridge Centre for Advanced Research and Education in Singapore (CARES) that aims to develop neuroscience-based interventions for lifelong flexible learning. Launched in October 2020 and funded by the National Research Foundation Singapore, CLIC brings together a multidisciplinary team of psychologists, neuroscientists, linguists and educators who conduct innovative research in the science of learning. The world of today is constantly evolving to keep pace with advances in technology and globalisation, requiring individuals to adapt and develop new skills to ensure resilience through a culture of lifelong flexible learning. Mental flexibility is required in order to adapt to change, problem-solve creatively in new situations and make the most of opportunities including emerging career opportunities. The capacity for cognitive flexibility is thus central to the modern digital age and our education system needs innovation to ensure citizens are equipped to develop these future skills. For example, major global challenges, including climate change, renewable energy, and food security, will require novel and creative approaches and solutions. CLIC researchers are developing a neuroscience-based model of flexible learning, including important social contextual factors, in order to inform the design of practical, real-life interventions for use in schools and the workplace. This will ensure that individuals are not only prepared for future career success, but also have a good quality of life and wellbeing, thus supporting a flourishing society. For more details, please view: https://www.cares.cam.ac.uk/research/clic/ We are looking for a  Research Associate to support research activities on cognitive flexibility and learning, and training-related brain changes among adults and adolescents . We anticipate the successful candidate to perform within a dynamic interdisciplinary research environment working collaboratively with project team members and take on opportunities for involvement in research activities related to science education, language and cognition, and cognition/learning and pedagogy. Key Responsibilities: Conducting literature review Conducting interviews Liaising with school personnel Survey construction, evaluation, and administration Familiarity with behavioral task data and experience in data management. Proven experience in data analysis, with proficiency in R for data wrangling and basic statistical analyses (e.g., ANOVA, regression, structural equation modelling, principal factor analysis). Understanding of online and offline psychological research tools, such as Qualtrics, Gorilla, and PsychoPy. Familiarity with standard formats for reporting data analysis, tables, figures and a solid understanding of APA 7th edition style guidelines. Strong communication skills and the ability to work efficiently. Able to collaborate well with others and deliver work on time. Assist in quantitative and qualitative processing and analysis Project and data management, maintain research records Collect primary data, responsible for data coding and entry Report preparation Assisting in the analysis of findings Other research related tasks as assigned by the Principal Investigator Job Requirements: Master’s degree in psychology with a background in cognition, education/learning, pedagogy, or related field. Experience in conducting, collecting data for and analysing surveys, psychological testing (computerised), behavioural testing and cognitive experiments Experience in conducting literature reviews and writing academic reports Experience with statistical analysis using SPSS and/or R language Good ICT skills Good communication skills and other interpersonal skills Excellent organizational skills and able to work effectively within deadlines Experience preparing reports, protocols, presentations and manuscripts with guidance Interest in research at the intersection of neuroscience, social science, education, and cognition We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Multi-Agent-Path-Planning-for-Autonomous-Drone-Operations-_R00025443": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Multi-Agent Path Planning for Autonomous Drone Operations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Fellow in Multi-Agent Path Planning for Autonomous Drone Operations to develop learning-based model predictive control (MPC) algorithms for multi-agent multirotor drone navigation around vessels in maritime environments. The role will focus on integrating multirotor crash predictions with vessel protected volume estimates to identify safety-buffer overlaps, developing multi-agent path-planning, and machine-learning methods for corridor allocation, airspace capacity optimisation, and defining safe air corridors and operational capacity limits under varying maritime traffic conditions. Key Responsibilities: Develop multi-agent path-planning frameworks for safe and efficient multirotor operations in maritime environments. Formulate multi-agent navigation problems, including state and action representation, safety constraints, vessel-protected volumes, route allocation, and trajectory optimisation. Develop model predictive control and multi-agent model predictive control algorithms for path planning under dynamic maritime conditions. Develop capacity optimisation algorithms that enable drones to respond to vessel movements, environmental disturbances, and changes in operational constraints. Integrate drone airspace-usage prediction, vessel protected volume estimation, navigation, decision-making, and control modules within a simulation-based validation framework. Develop methods to estimate the safe operational capacity for drone operations under different vessel traffic, airspace, and environmental scenarios. Design and conduct simulation experiments, sensitivity analyses, and validation studies to evaluate navigation safety, efficiency, robustness, scalability, and generalisation. Work with PhD students, research engineers, vessel operators, drone operators, and project collaborators to support system integration, testing, validation, and demonstration. Prepare technical reports, research publications, presentations, project deliverables, and documentation for stakeholder and expert review. Job Requirements: Education qualifications PhD degree in Robotics, Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related discipline. Strong research background in multi-agent reinforcement learning, multi-robot systems, autonomous systems, or learning-based navigation. A strong publication record in relevant journals or conferences would be an advantage. Soft skills Strong communication and problem-solving skills. Strong sense of ownership, responsibility, and initiative. Ability to mentor junior researchers, PhD students, or research engineers and collaborate with industry partners, and project stakeholders. Willingness to support project reporting and milestone reviews. Hard skills Strong programming skills in Python and deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Experience in autonomous navigation, path planning, trajectory optimisation, conflict detection, or collision avoidance. Experience in model predictive control and multi-agent model predictive control algorithms. Familiarity with optimisation techniques, machine-learning methods and data-driven modelling. Familiarity with robotics and autonomous-system simulation environments such as ROS/ROS2, Gazebo, AirSim, Unity, or equivalent platforms. Knowledge of vessel-motion prediction, dynamic obstacle avoidance, separation assurance, or traffic-aware navigation would be advantageous. Familiarity with geospatial data, maritime traffic data, Automatic Identification System data, or airspace-capacity modelling would be beneficial. Experience Experience in developing learning-based model predictive control algorithms in simulation. Experience in multi-agent robotic systems, drone swarms, or autonomous decision making. Experience in integrating prediction, planning, decision-making, and control modules within a simulation or experimental framework. Experience with control algorithms for embodied AI systems is desirable. Competencies Ability to formulate and solve navigation and optimisation problems under uncertainty, dynamic constraints, and changing operational conditions. Ability to work across AI, robotics, control, and UAV autonomy domains. Ability to deliver research outcomes within project timelines and contribute to high-quality publications We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer--Structural-Finite-Element-Analysis-for-Maritime-Drone-Operations-_R00025441": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Structural/Finite Element Analysis for Maritime Drone Operations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Engineer in Structural/Finite Element Analysis for Maritime Drone Operations to investigate the risk that multirotor drone collisions pose to vessels operating in maritime environments. The role will focus on developing and executing finite element analysis (FEA) simulations of drone-vessel impacts, estimating structural damage to critical vessel subsystems, and translating simulation outputs into damage severity classifications and risk matrices that feed into the project’s separation-assurance framework and the Maritime Digital Twin. The role will also be involved in developing data-driven or physics-informed surrogate models of the FEA simulations to enable fast, generalizable damage predictions across a range of drone and vessel scenarios. Key Responsibilities: Develop finite element analysis (FEA) frameworks to estimate structural damage from multirotor drone-vessel collisions in maritime environments. Formulate impact analysis problems, including drone impact trajectories, weight classes, vessel component geometry and material properties, and structural damage severity classification. Develop and execute nonlinear/explicit dynamic FEA simulations (e.g., ANSYS, Abaqus) covering mid-flight and landing-phase crash scenarios on different vessel types. Develop methods to translate structural damage severity into functional-impact and risk classifications for critical vessel subsystems. Develop data-driven or physics-informed surrogate models trained on FEA outputs to accelerate damage-severity prediction, reducing reliance on repeated simulations. Integrate damage estimation outputs with crash-area prediction and separation-assurance models within the project’s overall risk framework and the Maritime Digital Twin. Identify and prioritise critical versus non-critical vessel components and zones, working with vessel operators and the classification society to obtain relevant structural data. Design and conduct simulation experiments, sensitivity analyses, and validation studies to evaluate damage estimation accuracy, robustness, and generalisation across vessel types. Work with PhD students, research fellows, vessel operators, drone operators, and project collaborators to support system integration, testing, validation, and demonstration. Prepare technical reports, research publications, presentations, project deliverables, and documentation for stakeholder and expert review. Job Requirements: Education qualifications Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Material Science and Engineering, Civil/Structural Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong academic or project background in finite element analysis, structural mechanics, or impact/crash simulation. Research or project experience in maritime/naval structures, impact studies, or structural damage assessment would be advantageous. Soft skills Strong communication and problem-solving skills. Strong sense of ownership, responsibility, and initiative. Ability to work effectively with researchers, engineers, students, industry partners, and project stakeholders. Willingness to support project reporting and milestone reviews. Hard skills Demonstrated hands-on experience with FEA software, specifically nonlinear or explicit dynamic solvers used for impact/crash simulation (e.g., Abaqus Explicit, LS-DYNA, or ANSYS Explicit Dynamics). Competent in structural mechanics, material behaviour under dynamic/impact loading, and failure/damage modelling. Familiarity with drone dynamics or aerospace impact studies would be advantageous. Scripting ability (e.g., Python) for simulation automation, post-processing, or coupling FEA outputs with downstream risk models. Experience translating engineering simulation results into risk matrices or decision-support outputs for non-specialist stakeholders would be beneficial. Programming skills in Python or MATLAB for simulation data processing and analysis would be an advantage. Familiarity with surrogate modelling and physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) for generalising simulation-based predictions would be an advantage. Experience Experience integrating simulation, damage/risk assessment, and reporting workflows within a research or engineering project framework. Competencies Ability to scope, build, and validate simulation models independently from limited or partial input data. Ability to work across structural engineering, impact mechanics, and maritime domains. Ability to deliver research outcomes within project timelines and contribute to high-quality publications. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--AI-in-Medicine_R00025439-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate, AI in Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre of AI in Medicine is a university-level research centre with the mission to bridge the gap between cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies and practical applications in healthcare, The key objective is to spearheadresearch and development to revolutionise patient care and inform public health policies. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/c-aim We are seeking a Research Assistant / Research Associate to contribute towards the daily operational needs and strategic research priorities of the NTU Centre of AI in Medicine (C-AIM). The role will support the smooth running of C-AIM’s infrastructure, AVIT systems, administrative processes, procurement, audits, documentation, and coordination activities, ensuring that the Centre’s day-to-day functions are reliable, efficient, and responsive to project and stakeholder needs. In parallel, the candidate will provide behavioral, communications and social science research support for strategic healthcare AI implementation projects, including human-machine interactions, outcomes-based evidence, survey design and rollout, cohort recruitment, conversational analysis, simulation- and observation-based studies, data preparation, processing and analysis, project documentation, grant and proposal support, and coordination with internal and external collaborators. Through this dual operational and research-facing role, the candidate will help C-AIM translate AI innovations into practical healthcare applications that advance patient care, health system improvement, and responsible AI implementation in medicine. Primary responsibilities: Daily Operations, Infrastructure and AVIT Support Manage, operate and maintain C-AIM’s AVIT, computing and infrastructure resources, including microaccess laboratories and AI simulation rooms, to ensure readiness for meetings, events, demonstrations, teaching, research activities and stakeholder engagements; Provide day-to-day technical support, troubleshooting and liaison with institutional teams, vendors and service providers for equipment setup, servicing, procurement and upgrades; Maintain inventories, usage records, documentation and operational trackers to support efficient centre operations, audit readiness and continuity of services. Behavioural, Communication and Social Science Research Support Support healthcare AI implementation studies that examine human-machine interaction, communication practices, user behaviour, trust, acceptability, adoption, workflow fit and outcomes-based evidence in clinical, educational or organisational settings; Assist with the design, rollout and monitoring of surveys, interviews, focus groups, observational studies, simulation-based studies and conversational analysis protocols related to AI use in healthcare; Coordinate participant or cohort recruitment, consent-related documentation, scheduling, data collection logistics and follow-up activities for behavioural, communication and social science research components; Prepare, clean, organise and analyse qualitative, quantitative or mixed-methods data, including survey responses, observational notes, transcripts, interaction logs and implementation outcome measures. Healthcare AI Implementation and Project Support Support strategic healthcare AI implementation projects by assisting with needs assessment, workflow mapping, stakeholder documentation, user feedback collection and translation of research findings into practical implementation recommendations; Assist with data preparation, processing, analysis, evaluation and documentation for AI-enabled healthcare projects, ensuring that technical outputs are interpreted alongside behavioral, communication and organizational considerations; Contribute to the development, testing and evaluation of AI/ML workflows, prototypes, dashboards or tools that support responsible deployment, monitoring or evaluation of AI applications in healthcare settings; Support deployment, testing and maintenance of AI/ML applications on suitable institutional or cloud-based platforms, in coordination with relevant technical, governance and stakeholder teams. Research Coordination, Documentation and Communication Prepare and maintain research protocols, study materials, implementation notes, project reports, presentation materials and progress updates for C-AIM projects; Coordinate communication across research teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, external partners, vendors and administrative units to support timely project delivery and clear stakeholder engagement; Support the preparation of grant applications, research proposals, conference materials, posters, manuscripts, ethics submissions and other outputs arising from healthcare AI implementation and social science research work. Research Administration, Compliance and Centre Support Handle procurement, purchase requests, vendor coordination, asset tracking and resource planning for both routine centre operations and research project needs; Support audits, compliance checks, institutional reporting and documentation processes to ensure alignment with NTU, C-AIM and project governance requirements; Assist with research and legal agreements, project records, ethics or governance submissions where applicable, and coordination of administrative workflows required for collaborative healthcare AI projects; Coordinate with finance, procurement, human resources, estates, IT and other administrative departments to resolve operational matters and support smooth centre functioning. Required Competencies and Qualifications: Bachelor’s (for Assistant) or Master’s (for Associate) degree in Social Sciences, Communications, Psychology, Behavioral Science, Sociology, Economics, Econometrics, Public Health, Health Services Research, Implementation Science, Health Informatics, Data Science, or a closely related discipline relevant to behavioral, communication and healthcare AI implementation research. Training or experience in behavioral, communication, psychology, social science or econometric research methods, including survey design, interviews, focus groups, observational studies, simulation-based studies, conversational analysis, implementation evaluation or mixed-methods research. Ability to support healthcare AI implementation studies examining human-machine interaction, user behavior, trust, acceptability, adoption, communication practices, workflow fit and outcomes-based evidence in healthcare, education or organizational settings. Competence in preparing, cleaning, organizing and analysing qualitative, quantitative or mixed-methods data, including survey responses, interview or focus group transcripts, observational notes, interaction logs and implementation outcome measures. Familiarity with statistical, qualitative or econometric analysis tools such as R, Python, Stata, SPSS, NVivo, ATLAS.ti, Excel or equivalent platforms is advantageous; willingness to learn additional data analysis or healthcare AI tools is expected. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare research protocols, study materials, reports, grant or proposal inputs, presentations, ethics documents and stakeholder-facing updates clearly and accurately. Good interpersonal and coordination skills, with the ability to liaise professionally with research teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, study participants, vendors and administrative units across multidisciplinary healthcare AI projects. Practical ability or willingness to support daily centre operations, including AVIT setup, equipment readiness, infrastructure coordination, inventory tracking, procurement documentation, audit preparation and liaison with vendors or institutional service teams. Experience or willingness to learn research administration processes, including participant or cohort recruitment, consent-related documentation, ethics or governance submissions, project reporting, compliance documentation, grant support and research agreement coordination. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and interest in healthcare, AI in medicine, responsible AI implementation, digital health, health communication, behavioural science or health system improvement. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--AI-in-Medicine_R00025438-2": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate, AI in Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre of AI in Medicine is a university-level research centre with the mission to bridge the gap between cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies and practical applications in healthcare, The key objective is to spearheadresearch and development to revolutionise patient care and inform public health policies. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/c-aim We are seeking a Research Assistant / Research Associate to contribute towards the daily operational needs and strategic research priorities of the NTU Centre of AI in Medicine (C-AIM). The role will support the smooth running of C-AIM’s infrastructure, AVIT systems, administrative processes, procurement, audits, documentation, and coordination activities, ensuring that the Centre’s day-to-day functions are reliable, efficient, and responsive to project and stakeholder needs. In parallel, the candidate will provide data science and AI/ML modelling support for strategic healthcare AI projects, including clinical and biomedical data preparation, feature engineering, statistical modelling, machine learning model development, validation, performance evaluation, workflow prototyping, reproducible analysis, technical documentation, grant and proposal support, and coordination with internal and external collaborators. Through this dual operational and research-facing role, the candidate will help C-AIM translate AI innovations into practical healthcare applications that advance patient care, health system improvement, and responsible AI implementation in medicine. Primary Responsibilities: Daily Operations, Infrastructure and AVIT Support Manage, operate and maintain C-AIM’s AVIT, computing and infrastructure resources, including microaccess laboratories and AI simulation rooms, to ensure readiness for meetings, events, demonstrations, teaching, research activities and stakeholder engagements; Provide day-to-day technical support, troubleshooting and liaison with institutional teams, vendors and service providers for equipment setup, servicing, procurement and upgrades; Maintain inventories, usage records, documentation and operational trackers to support efficient centre operations, audit readiness and continuity of services. Data Science, AI/ML Modelling and Technical Research Support Support healthcare AI projects involving statistical modelling, machine learning, predictive analytics, natural language processing, multimodal data integration or other AI/ML approaches relevant to clinical, biomedical or health system applications; Assist with data extraction, cleaning, harmonisation, feature engineering, exploratory analysis, model training, validation, benchmarking, calibration and performance evaluation using appropriate statistical and machine learning methods; Develop, test and document reproducible analytical workflows, scripts, notebooks, pipelines, dashboards or prototypes to support AI/ML model development and evaluation in healthcare settings; Prepare technical summaries, model outputs, visualisations and interpretation notes to support research meetings, grant applications, project reports, manuscripts and stakeholder-facing communications. Healthcare AI Implementation and Project Support Support strategic healthcare AI implementation projects by assisting with needs assessment, workflow mapping, stakeholder documentation, user feedback collection and translation of research findings into practical implementation recommendations; Assist with data preparation, processing, statistical analysis, model development, validation, evaluation and documentation for AI-enabled healthcare projects, ensuring that technical outputs are robust, interpretable and aligned with clinical or implementation needs; Contribute to the development, testing and evaluation of AI/ML workflows, prototypes, dashboards or tools that support responsible deployment, monitoring or evaluation of AI applications in healthcare settings; Support deployment, testing and maintenance of AI/ML applications on suitable institutional or cloud-based platforms, in coordination with relevant technical, governance and stakeholder teams. Research Coordination, Documentation and Communication Prepare and maintain research protocols, study materials, implementation notes, project reports, presentation materials and progress updates for C-AIM projects; Coordinate communication across data science teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, technical partners, vendors and administrative units to support timely project delivery and clear stakeholder engagement; Support the preparation of grant applications, research proposals, conference materials, posters, manuscripts, ethics submissions and other outputs arising from healthcare AI, data science and AI/ML modelling work. Research Administration, Compliance and Centre Support Handle procurement, purchase requests, vendor coordination, asset tracking and resource planning for both routine centre operations and research project needs; Support audits, compliance checks, institutional reporting and documentation processes to ensure alignment with NTU, C-AIM and project governance requirements; Assist with research and legal agreements, project records, ethics or governance submissions where applicable, and coordination of administrative workflows required for collaborative healthcare AI projects; Coordinate with finance, procurement, human resources, estates, IT and other administrative departments to resolve operational matters and support smooth centre functioning. Required Competencies and Qualifications: Bachelor’s (for Research Assistant) or Master’s (for Research Associate) degree in Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Health Informatics, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, Applied Mathematics, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or a closely related quantitative discipline relevant to healthcare AI and AI/ML modelling. Training or experience in data science, statistical analysis, machine learning, predictive modelling, natural language processing, deep learning, biomedical data analysis, clinical data analytics or related AI/ML methods. Ability to support healthcare AI studies involving data preparation, feature engineering, model development, validation, benchmarking, calibration, performance evaluation, interpretability analysis and translation of technical outputs into actionable research insights. Competence in preparing, cleaning, organising and analysing structured or unstructured datasets, including clinical, biomedical, imaging, omics, text, survey, workflow, interaction-log or implementation outcome data where applicable. Proficiency or strong working familiarity with programming and data analysis tools such as Python, R, SQL, Git, Jupyter notebooks, machine learning libraries, statistical packages, visualisation tools or equivalent platforms is expected. Experience with reproducible analytical workflows, model documentation, experiment tracking, version control, data governance, privacy-aware analysis or deployment-oriented AI/ML workflows is advantageous. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical documentation, research protocols, analytical reports, grant or proposal inputs, presentations, ethics documents and stakeholder-facing updates clearly and accurately. Good interpersonal and coordination skills, with the ability to liaise professionally with research teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, technical partners, vendors and administrative units across multidisciplinary healthcare AI projects. Practical ability or willingness to support daily centre operations, including AVIT setup, equipment readiness, infrastructure coordination, inventory tracking, procurement documentation, audit preparation and liaison with vendors or institutional service teams. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and interest in healthcare, AI in medicine, responsible AI implementation, digital health, clinical data science, biomedical AI, machine learning or health system improvement. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Learning-Strategist---Learning-Strategist--Centre-for-Innovation-in-Learning---NIE-_R00017190": {
      "title": "Senior Learning Strategist / Learning Strategist (Centre for Innovation in Learning) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . We are seeking a pedagogically minded and dedicated Senior Learning Strategist / Learning Strategist. Reporting to the Learning Strategist Manager, the appointee collaborates with faculties to design and develop cutting-edge blended learning experiences, providing strategic guidance for implementing innovative digital teaching and learning practices across NIE. Additionally, the appointee will work closely with fellow Learning Strategists and the other teams in the department to research, develop, and present innovative and pedagogically sound design solutions to stakeholders, in pursuit of enhanced practice and outcomes. The candidate should be familiar with the training and adult education landscape, be adept at facilitation and possess a commitment to staying up to date on higher education best practices. This is a 2-year contract position. Responsibilities Build Evidence-Based Innovation in Teaching & Learning within NIE a) Collaborate with fellow Learning Strategists to: Research adult learning theories, strategies, data, and appropriate educational technology tools to design, develop, and facilitate impactful face-to-face and online tech-enhanced workshops for faculty. Assess the learning needs of IN-Learning specialists in learning design and emerging technology. Design, develop, and facilitate engaging initiatives to support IN-Learning specialists in building their expertise in learning design and emerging technology. b) Collaborate with NIE faculty to: Identify learning needs for courses they teach. Propose frameworks, new/enhanced learning outcomes, tech-enabled teaching and learning strategies, and assessments as part of course redesigning. Propose appropriate educational technology to overcome gaps and enhance the learning outcomes of the courses. Achieve constructive alignment of the learning outcomes with the learning activities and assessment in their courses. c) Collaborate with cross-functional teams to: Assess faculty capability development needs through qualitative and quantitative data analysis, to inform their work in designing, developing, and evaluating learner-centered blended learning experiences and fostering assessment literacy. Research, develop and present evidence-based and innovative design solutions with the project team to stakeholders. Research and evaluate frameworks and educational technology tools for implementation to optimize and innovate teaching, learning and assessment practices in NIE. Research, write grant proposals and develop tech-enabled learning solutions. Work together on initiatives with IN-Learning's Engagement, Planning and Research team to share learning sciences knowledge and improve practices institute-wide. Carry out action research by: conceptualizing frameworks and methodologies  designing evaluation instruments  gathering and analyzing data (e.g. Learning Analytics) formulating decisions to improve the effectiveness of learning experiences and our Capability Development initiatives Contribute to special projects on teaching and learning, as required. Keep Up with Learning Sciences and Innovative Teaching and Learning Practices Stay current on learning sciences, innovative teaching and learning practices in higher education (e.g., personalized learning, adaptive learning, e-assessment, hybrid learning, learning analytics, and Artificial Intelligence). Foster a culture of continuous learning within the team by providing opportunities for professional development and encouraging knowledge sharing. Requirements A University degree, preferably in Instructional Design, Education or Learning Sciences and Technologies. A master’s degree is preferred. A minimum of 2 years of experience in instructional design, teaching and learning, within a higher educational setting or with adult learners. Proven ability to manage successful learning projects. To be considered for the Senior Learning Strategist position, candidates should: Possess at least 5 years of experience in instructional design, teaching, learning, and the adult education landscape. Possess a proven track record of managing complex learning projects. Demonstrate experience in a mentorship role and in leading complex projects. Expert knowledge of applying Adult Learning theories in the design of Blended Learning experiences. Possess strong research skills. Proven track record in designing and facilitating faculty development workshops for diverse audiences. Possess strong written, verbal, and presentation skills. Strong knowledge of emerging educational technologies for teaching and learning. Excellent time management skills to meet multiple deadlines simultaneously and consistently deliver high-quality results. Excellent organizational and project management skills. Experience in facilitating both face-to-face and online sessions. Familiarity with Learning Management System and a demonstrated ability to rapidly learn new tools and processes with minimal support. Demonstrate excellent interpersonal skills and strong problem-solving abilities. Highly motivated, able to work independently yet also a strong team player. A strong desire to learn, acquire, and share new knowledge. Maintain a positive attitude and work effectively under pressure to meet deadlines. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 12 August 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Human-Factors-_R00025434": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Human Factors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAir Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) is a research institute at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, supported by the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). The key objective of ATMRI is to support research and innovation in air traffic management. ATMRI focuses on developing practical and data-driven solutions for complex aviation systems, in close collaboration with industry and international partners. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/atmri . We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems in air traffic management (ATM), with a focus on operator cognitive load, situational awareness, and decision-support interfaces for air traffic controllers. The role will involve designing and evaluating human-in-the-loop tools using methods such as eye-tracking, physiological sensing, and uncertainty visualization, contributing to the advancement of research and innovation at Nanyang Technological University. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems approaches to support air traffic management studies and applications. Design, develop, and evaluate decision-support interfaces and operator-facing tools using operational and simulated data. Support research activities on controller cognitive load, situational awareness, and resilience under current and future ATM concepts. Work collaboratively with researchers and engineers to develop prototype solutions and human-in-the-loop evaluation frameworks. Conduct user studies and analyse results (e.g. eye-tracking, physiological sensing) to assess the performance and usability of developed tools in realistic operational scenarios. Prepare technical reports, research papers, and project deliverables, and participate in project meetings and reviews. Publish research findings in top-tier journals and conferences in relevant fields (e.g. human-computer interaction, human factors, ATM). Contribute to research proposals, technical documentation, and other project-related activities as required. Job Requirements: PhD qualification in Human-Computer Interaction, Cognitive Science, Human Factors, Air Traffic Management, Transport, or other related fields. At least one (1) year of relevant research experience in human factors, cognitive systems, or related technical research roles, ideally within transport, aviation, or other safety-critical operational domains. Familiarity with research related to cognitive load assessment, decision-support interfaces, or human-in-the-loop systems for complex operational environments (e.g. air traffic management, control rooms). Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical reports and academic publications. Proficiency in job-specific technical skills, including programming for research and data analysis purposes (e.g. Python or similar languages), experience with eye-tracking or physiological sensing methods, as well as strong numerical and analytical skills. Competent in general research-related skills and professional attributes, including problem-solving and analytical thinking. Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively, develop solutions under defined timelines, and demonstrate good organisational and time management skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Linguistics--Singapore-Mandarin-Usage-Dictionary--_R00025431": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Linguistics (Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Humanities (SoH) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, brings together vibrant research and teaching across Chinese, English and literature, history, linguistics and multilingual studies, and philosophy. For more details, please visit https://www.ntu.edu.sg/soh . We are looking for a full-time Research Associate in Linguistics to support the MOE SSHR Thematic Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary. The Research Associate will be a core member of the project team and will independently conduct literature review, linguistic analysis, corpus-based research, and cross-varietal comparison. Key Responsibilities: The role will involve providing linguistic input for annotation and computational modelling, interpreting corpus and model outputs, and using these findings to design, draft, and refine dictionary entries. The Research Associate will also coordinate annotation and quality assurance, maintain research documentation, guide student assistants, and contribute to project reports, publications, presentations, and other research activities. The appointee will work independently while collaborating closely with the PI, Co-PIs, computational researchers, and project collaborators. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Linguistics, Chinese Linguistics, Applied Linguistics, Corpus Linguistics, Lexicography, or a related field Strong training in Chinese linguistic analysis, particularly in areas such as lexis, semantics, syntax, pragmatics, language variation, corpus linguistics, or lexicography High level of proficiency in written and spoken Chinese and English so as to support the technical components of the Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary Experience in corpus-based research, linguistic annotation, lexical analysis, dictionary compilation, or related language research Ability to independently analyze linguistic data, interpret corpus and computational findings, and produce clear research outputs Strong analytical, writing, organizational, and quality assurance skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively and to guide student assistants Familiarity with Singapore Mandarin, other Mandarin varieties, Chinese dialects, multilingualism, corpus tools, or annotation platforms would be an advantage to support the technical components of the Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Natural-Language-Processing--Singapore-Mandarin-Usage-Dictionary--_R00025430-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Natural Language Processing (Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Humanities (SoH) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, brings together vibrant research and teaching across Chinese, English and literature, history, linguistics and multilingual studies, and philosophy. For more details, please visit https://www.ntu.edu.sg/soh. We are looking for a full-time Research Assistant with a background in Natural Language Processing (NLP) to support the technical components of the MOE SSHR Thematic Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary. The role will focus on corpus construction, including speech-to-text processing and transcription of spoken corpora, and on the training, fine-tuning, and evaluation of computational models (e.g., Word2Vec, BERT) for identifying lexical variation and region-specific features in Singapore Mandarin. The Research Assistant will be based in Singapore and work closely with the Principal Investigator, Co-PI, and collaborators. The position is offered on an initial contract of 18 to 24 months. Key Responsibilities: Support corpus construction, including speech-to-text processing and transcription of spoken corpora Perform data preprocessing, cleaning, and quality checks on written and spoken corpus data Contribute to the training, fine-tuning, and evaluation of computational models (e.g., Word2Vec, BERT) Implement models and carry out systematic performance evaluation Prepare model outputs for linguistic validation and dictionary integration Contribute to the technical development of the online dictionary platform, including database integration and search functions Document code, workflows, and datasets, and support other project-related tasks as assigned Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computational Linguistics, Natural Language Processing, or a related field Technical hands-on experience in NLP or machine learning, including model training, fine-tuning, and evaluation Familiarity with NLP models and toolkits (e.g., Word2Vec, BERT) and with speech-to-text workflows Proficiency in Python and common machine learning / NLP libraries (e.g., PyTorch, scikit-learn) Good written and oral communication skills; proficiency in Mandarin Chinese so as to support the technical components of the Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary Ability to work independently and collaboratively, meticulous with an eye for detail, and excellent organizational skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Robotics-_R00025422": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Robotics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee The project aims to develop robust, intelligent and efficient navigation systems for inspection robots, enabling autonomous localization, decision-making, motion planning and safe navigation in complex, dynamic real-world environments. The Research Associate will support research on robot navigation, focusing on the integration of visual perception, localization, planning and navigation. The role will also investigate learning-based approaches, including diffusion models and reinforcement learning, for navigation decision-making, trajectory generation and adaptive robot behavior. Key Responsibilities: Design and develop navigation algorithms for inspection robots in complex and dynamic environments. Work on global and local motion planning, obstacle avoidance, trajectory generation and trajectory tracking for humanoid robots. Investigate diffusion models and diffusion-based policies for navigation planning, trajectory generation and action prediction. Apply reinforcement learning and/or imitation learning methods to improve navigation performance and adaptive robot behavior. Integrate visual navigation and planning modules with humanoid locomotion and whole-body control systems. Build and evaluate algorithms in simulation environments and on real-world humanoid robotic platforms. Contribute to publications and technical reports Assist in mentoring students and supporting research activities Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Robotics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, or related fields Strong background in at least one of the following: robot motion planning and control; autonomous decision-making; robot localization and navigation. Experience in one or more of the following: path planning, motion planning, trajectory optimization or model predictive control; reinforcement learning, imitation learning or learning-based control; diffusion policies or generative decision-making; robotics physics simulators (e.g., Isaac Gym, MuJoCo, Gazebo) Proficiency in Python and/or C++ Experience with PyTorch or similar deep learning frameworks Strong problem-solving ability and hands-on implementation skills We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Dean-s-Office-and-Global-Engagement--Office-for-Research---NIE-_R00025368": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Dean’s Office and Global Engagement (Office for Research) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Assistant Manager, Dean’s Office and Global Engagement with the Office for Research. The Dean's Office plays an integral role in the strategic communications and engagement efforts of OfR, effectively conveying its strategic positioning and policies to MOE, NIE, and other stakeholders. The office also advances NIE’s global leadership and reputation in education research by fostering strategic international partnerships, facilitating high-impact collaborations and strengthening NIE’s contributions to global educational knowledge and practice. As the Assistant Manager, Dean’s Office and Global Engagement, you will play a key support role in NIE’s global research engagement strategy, building sustainable partnerships with leading universities and research institutions, and supporting initiatives that position NIE as a global thought leader in education research, policy, and practice. You will also support in strategic communications and engagement efforts of OfR. This is a contract post till 31 Mar 2028. Responsibilities Support the Dean’s Office in advancing NIE’s global engagement objectives and strategic priorities. Provide support in strategic research matters, including collation of reports, requests and secretarial support for OfR management and other strategic meetings. Support in organising Programme Office Meetings and OfR events including strategic retreats, townhalls and outreach to Academic Departments. Assist in the implementation of NIE’s global research engagement plans, including coordination, partnership activities, and collaboration initiatives. Help identify productive relationships with universities, research institutes, governments, and international organisations. Support the preparation, review, and coordination of institutional agreements, such as MOUs and Research Collaboration Agreements, in consultation with relevant stakeholders. Assist NIE faculty in identifying international research opportunities and developing collaborations. Coordinate international research outreach activities, including symposia, conferences, visiting scholar programmes, and research dialogues. Coordinate and arrrange international research consultancies, capacity-building programmes, and strategic research partnerships. Track and monitor the progress and outcomes of international research partnerships, and maintain records and dashboards for reporting purposes. Provide administrative and operational support on governance, compliance, and cultural protocol matters in international engagements. Work closely Associate Dean, Global & Strategic Engagement, OfR and internal stakeholders to ensure smooth execution of global engagement activities and alignment with NIE goals. Collaborate with NIE Research Centres, Academic Departments, and administrative units to strengthen international research engagement and raise NIE’s global visibility. Any other duties as assigned by the reporting officer. Requirements       A University degree. Preferably with 3 years of working experience in an educational institution. Good understanding of global trends, and quick ability to understand research environments. Excellent interpersonal, negotiation and communication skills. Strong analytical, planning and organizational abilities, with experience in project and stakeholder management. Good writing skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced and dynamic environment often with tight timelines. Able to communicate professionally and work with faculty and staff across various administrative units. Able to monitor compliance in policies and uphold governance of policies. High level of professionalism, adaptability and discretion when handling sensitive or confidential information. Proficiency in MS office applications or project management tools is an advantage. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 12 August 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Advanced-Diamond-Synthesis-_R00023571": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Diamond Synthesis and Device Fabrication)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nTemasek Laboratories@NTU (TL@NTU) is a premier research institute at Nanyang Technological University specializing in advanced defense and security technologies. The institute collaborates with external partners and stakeholders on cutting-edge research in strategic defense systems, advanced materials, power electronics, and semiconductor technologies. TL@NTU houses state-of-the-art cleanroom facilities, thermal evaporation systems, and electrical characterization equipment supporting mission-critical research initiatives. We are seeking a Research Scientist to lead device fabrication and electrical characterization for developing diamond-based semiconductor devices for next-generation defense electronics. Key Responsibilities: Lead cleanroom fabrication of diamond-based electronic devices, including photolithography, thin film deposition, etching, metallization, and device patterning Develop and optimize surface charge transfer doping of hydrogen-terminated diamond through thermal evaporation of transition metal oxide (TMO) films, including in-situ annealing protocols for formation of 2-dimensional hole gas (2DHG) channels Fabricate low-resistance ohmic contacts and develop process flows for integration of diamond into radiofrequency (RF) field effect transistors (FETs) and high-power electronic devices Conduct comprehensive electrical characterization, including sheet resistance, I-V and C-V measurements, Hall effect, contact resistance, and transport property analysis, and extract device parameters Verify and optimize the surface transfer doping mechanism and characterize diamond post-deposition to confirm that surface conductivity is maintained Operate, and where required install and commission, the Microwave Plasma Chemical Vapour Deposition (MPCVD) reactor and hydrogenation system, and optimize iterative growth protocols for electronic-grade single-crystal diamond Execute plasma hydrogen termination of grown crystals and verify hydrogenation effectiveness, including crystal face specificity Perform materials characterization using Raman spectroscopy, Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM), X-ray diffraction (XRD), and scanning electron microscopy (SEM) to establish quality feedback loops between synthesis, fabrication, and device performance Coordinate safe handling and transport of diamond wafers between synthesis and fabrication facilities and ensure adherence to project timelines Maintain detailed fabrication protocols, process and equipment documentation, and device characterization records Prepare technical reports and presentations for project deliverables and review meetings, and collaborate with external partners and collaborating institutions Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Physics, Applied Physics, or related field with specialization in semiconductor device fabrication and characterization Minimum 2-3 years of relevant experience in cleanroom device fabrication, preferably with wide-bandgap semiconductors or novel electronic materials Extensive hands-on experience with cleanroom processes including photolithography, thin film deposition (thermal evaporation, sputtering), etching, and metallization Strong expertise in electrical characterization techniques including I-V measurements, C-V profiling, Hall effect measurements, and device parameter extraction Knowledge of metal oxide thin film deposition and surface functionalization of semiconductors Experience with ohmic contact formation and contact resistance measurement techniques Understanding of semiconductor device physics, particularly field-effect transistors, surface conductivity mechanisms, and charge transfer processes Proficiency in device simulation tools and electrical measurement equipment (probe stations, parameter analyzers, etc.) Experience with diamond, SiC, GaN, or other wide-bandgap semiconductor devices is highly desirable Excellent written and oral communication skills with proven publication record in device physics or semiconductor technology Strong project management and organizational skills with demonstrated ability to meet strict deadlines Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively across multidisciplinary teams and multiple institutions Rigorous adherence to cleanroom protocols, safety procedures, and contamination control practices Prior experience with RF devices, power electronics, or high-voltage devices is an advantage We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Infrastructure-Planning---Upgrading--M-E-_R00025086": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Infrastructure Planning & Upgrading (M&E)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading research-intensive university in Singapore, committed to excellence in education, research and innovation. We are inviting experienced and motivated individuals to join our Office of Development and Facilities Management (ODFM), which oversees the development, operation and maintenance of all University buildings and grounds in support of NTU’s academic, research and administrative functions. We are seeking a dynamic and experienced Assistant Director, Infrastructure Planning & Upgrading (M&E) to lead mechanical and electrical (M&E) infrastructure upgrading initiatives across the campus. This role offers the opportunity to drive large-scale projects, modernize critical systems, and contribute to the development of a future-ready and sustainable university environment. Key Responsibilities Plan and oversee multi-year M&E upgrading roadmap and budget aligned with asset lifecycle and campus master plan. Conduct asset condition assessments and establish renewal priorities based on risk, criticality and lifecycle considerations. Drive infrastructure planning initiatives that support sustainability and digital transformation goals. Lead the end-to-end implementation of M&E infrastructure projects, including design, procurement, construction and commissioning. Manage consultants and contractors to ensure projects are delivered safely, on time, within budget and in accordance with quality standards. Implement effective project governance, risk management and quality assurance practices throughout the project lifecycle. Integrate energy-efficient technologies and sustainable solutions into infrastructure upgrading projects. Identify opportunities to optimize energy performance and improve the operational efficiency of campus infrastructure. Requirements Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Building Services, Facilities Management or related discipline. At least 10 years of relevant experience in mechanical & electrical (M&E) engineering, facilities/infrastructure management, or building services. Proven experience in managing infrastructure upgrading or asset renewal projects in a large and complex environment. Good knowledge of M&E systems, including HVAC, electrical distribution, fire protection systems, lifts and building management systems. Strong understanding of infrastructure lifecycle management, asset renewal strategies and maintenance practices. Good knowledge of project management, budgeting, risk management and contract administration. Strong stakeholder management, communication and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deliver results in a dynamic environment. Familiarity with energy-efficient technologies, smart building solutions and sustainability initiatives will be advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Partnerships---Engagement_R00024089": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Partnerships & Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nResearch Centre for Residue and Toxic Industrial Waste Management (TREASURES) at NTU is seeking a dynamic, highly organized, and resourceful Assistant Manager, Partnerships & Engagement to join the team. This position plays a pivotal role in bridging the gap between cutting-edge academic research and real-world industrial application. As the Assistant Manager, you will have the exciting opportunity to drive strategic corporate partnerships, manage high-impact engagement events, coordinate collaborative grant funding initiatives, and shape the digital public face of the centre. If you are passionate about science communication, stakeholder engagement, and research administration, we invite you to apply. Key Responsibilities: Event & Workshop Management: Spearhead the end-to-end planning and execution of industrial engagement events, including large-scale workshops, seminars, and targeted industry visits.  Digital Communications: Manage, maintain, and continuously update the research centre’s website, ensuring that news, upcoming events, and key research milestones are communicated effectively to an external audience. Stakeholder & Grant Coordination: Act as the primary administrative liaison for industrial partners and corporate stakeholders. Liaise with external Institutes of Higher Learning (IHLs) and industrial partners on grant funding-related matters to facilitate joint research collaborations.  Secretariat & Administrative Support: Provide vital day-to-day support for industry-focused meetings and advisory boards, including minute-taking, data gathering, and the preparation of management reports and presentation slides. Information Management: Handle confidential and sensitive industrial data or collaboration agreements with the highest level of discretion. Requirements: A Bachelor’s degree from a recognized institution in Business, Communications, STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics), or a related discipline. At least 3 to 4 years of relevant work experience in event management, corporate communications, or industrial liaison roles, ideally within a fast-paced or complex organization. Experience working within an Institute of Higher Learning (IHL) or a research institute is highly advantageous. Strong organizational and time management skills, with a proven track record of managing logistics for diverse audiences. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, specifically the ability to translate complex research or technical concepts into accessible language for industrial partners. Proficiency in website content management and Microsoft Office applications. A proactive, resourceful, and adaptable approach to work, with strong interpersonal skills to liaise effectively with academics and corporate executives. Relevant work experience in Building and Environment Sector is preferred. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Centre-for-African-Studies_R00025418": {
      "title": "Director, Centre for African Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNTU-SBF Centre for African Studies (CAS), which is overseen by CAS Advisory Board, is a trilateral platform with government, business and academia to promote knowledge and expertise on Africa among Asian businesses and policymakers, to accelerate the creation of deeper economic and policy links between Africa and Asia. The Director, CAS jointly reports to the Chairman of the Advisory Board, CAS and Dean, Nanyang Business School (NBS), with a matrix reporting to Associate Dean, Research, Nanyang Business School As the Centre Director, this role oversees all activities for CAS, ensures the alignment of CAS’ development to its mission, drives the strategic vision for the centre and assists in establishing CAS’s presence locally, as well as internationally. The incumbent will develop and implement strategies to drive deeper collaborations between African and Singaporean companies, as well as to work closely with NBS faculty members to develop thought leadership in the area. Responsibilities: Centre Strategy Planning and Strategic Collaborations Work closely with the Advisory Board and NBS Senior Management to define and execute CAS’ strategic vision. Develop and deliver strategic road map to strengthen collaborations between African and Singaporean companies. Identify opportunities, assess risks and implement mitigation strategies to support sustainable growth and impact. Outreach & Industry Engagement Lead outreach and industry engagement initiatives in line with the Centre’s strategy. Build and maintain a strong network of corporate, government and ecosystem partners. Create and curate platforms to deepen relationships and mutual understanding between African and Singaporean businesses. Thought Leadership Partner with NBS faculty to drive practice-oriented thought leadership relevant to Africa-Singapore business collaboration. Lead end-to-end thought leadership delivery, including but not limited to content development, stakeholder engagement, copyright management and distribution. Expand visibility and impact of the Centre’s thought leadership through relevant platforms and channels. Governance Provide day-to-day leadership of the Centre, ensuring delivery against strategic and operational plans. Oversee resource allocation, financial management, budgeting and performance monitoring. Ensure full compliance with governance and reporting requirements Establish and maintain effective governance processes and workflows. Be accountable for achieving KPIs set by the Advisory Board, NBS Senior Management Revenue Generation & Fundraising Develop and execute a clear roadmap toward financial sustainability and self-funding. Leverage partnerships and other monetization avenues Lead business development efforts, engaging a multitude of stakeholder Operational Excellence Oversee planning, budgeting and delivery of CAS initiatives and events. Ensure operational excellence and efficiency in the Centre’s overall functioning. Maintain an up-to-date Centre activities calendar aligned with Centre’s mission and vision . Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree PhD or DBA qualifications would be viewed favorably A minimum of 10 years of relevant experience Demonstrated experience in driving successful partnerships and/or industry engagement Demonstrated experience and working knowledge of companies from Africa Established networks and contacts in this area would be a distinct advantage Experience in outreach and running engagement events Familiarity and working experience with faculty members and/or an institution of higher learning would be an advantage Experience working on industry white papers and projects would be preferred Strategic thinking capabilities Self-driven and yet able to work in a team Good organisational skills Strong interpersonal and communication skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Math-Foundation-of-AI-_R00025397": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Math Foundation of AI)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. The group of Wang Zhongjian is looking for postdocs working on scientific computing and machine learning related topics. The funding is currently under a MOE grant entitled: Towards Infinite Dimensional Generative Models. The contract period of the position is up to three years subject to funding availability. Applicants should be familiar with and have track records in at least one of the following fields: approximation of neural networks, convergence of Langevin/MC sampling, analysis and algorithm design of interacting particle systems, operator learning, regularity theories in inverse/scattering problems. Once successful, the candidate is expected to transfer their expertise to machine learning/scientific computing in collaborations with other group members (phd students, exchange graduate students, etc). When projects are required, the group will provide reasonable GPGPU computing resources from the NSCC. The review of candidates will be conducted monthly until all the positions are filled. Once applied on Workday, the candidate may drop an email with application packages for faster screening. Key Responsibilities: Research Paper/proposal writing Teaching assisting Graduate student mentoring Job Requirements: A PhD degree in Mathematics or related areas, with focus on numerical analysis or machine learning. Experience in computational math. Proficient in coding languages, such as C, C++, Fortran, and Python. Strong written and verbal communication skills Strong publication record We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--LKCMedicine-_R00025399-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Hwei-Ee Tan lab studies the fundamental biological basis of “gut-feelings”, how bacteria in the gut signals to the host to influence physiology and behaviour. Using mice as a mammalian model, the lab investigates how diet and microbiome factors modulates host phenotypes (e.g. food reward, anxiety behaviours, etc). Besides supporting curiosity-driven basic research on the gut-brain axis, his lab is also studying the brain-gut axis, to uncover host-microbe interactions. His lab’s work is multidisciplinary, the research scope covers diverse skills from molecular biology to systems neuroscience, physiology and behaviour. With top-tier research support from National Research Foundation Singapore, Brain & Behavior Research Foundation (NARSAD), etc, his lab at NTU LKCMedicine is actively recruiting talented postdoctoral research fellows, research assistants, and interns, and also open to sponsoring motivated PhD/Masters students. A short-term or part-time research assistantship may also be arranged for motivated trainees. Key Responsibilities: Develop and conduct high quality research independently, as a candidate is expected to have relevant experience in one or more of these areas (e.g. mice/rodent handling, optogenetics and behaviours, animal surgery and dissection, calcium imaging, gnotobiotic studies and microbiome analysis, etc). Lead, assist or learn in a dynamic range of projects and lab duties, including but not limited to molecular biology and histology procedures, microscopy, rodent behavioural assays, neuroscience optogenetic and chemogenetic techniques, functional recording and calcium imaging, mice surgery, data analysis and presentation, lab maintenance and office, academic and administrative tasks Mentor and collaborate with group members and other research teams Demonstrate him/herself exceptionally self-motivated, a team player Any other responsibilities as advised by the PI based on the evolving needs in the lab The applicant should at least: Hold a Diploma or Bachelor degree in Biology or relevant disciplines Have a keen interest in the lab’s research theme on the microbiome gut brain neuroscience Be proficient in relevant techniques described above Be highly motivated and conscientious Demonstrate her/his competencies and qualifications satisfactorily Work independently, and also have the ability to work effectively in a team Have good organisational, verbal and interpersonal skills Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Programme-Director--Techno-commercial-Marketing--NTUitive-_R00025375": {
      "title": "Programme Director, Techno-commercial/Marketing [NTUitive]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University – NTUitive Pte Ltd (NTUitive), Nanyang Technological University's innovation and enterprise company, hosts the Separation Technologies Applied Research and Translation (START) Centre. START Centre, a national facility, was launched in June 2016 to develop and de-risk the commercialisation of innovative separation and filtration technologies. START bridges a critical gap in the ecosystem, between lab-scale R&D carried out in local as well as overseas research entities, and eventual market adoption, by focusing on translation, technology scale-up and piloting to accelerate the commercialisation process. START collaborates with leading local and global Institutes of Higher Learning (IHLs) and various industrial partners to achieve this goal.  Industry projects have been an important part of START’s portfolio, and will gain increasing importance in the coming years. START has also been focused on addressing Singapore’s National Priorities. Seawater desalination, one of our national taps, will be critical towards increasing the availability of water for Singapore’s industrial and commercial growth, as will the ability to drive Industrial Wastewater reuse and Resource Recovery. Starting October 1, 2026 (RIE 2030), START Centre will host SG MEM, Singapore Membrane Consortium, which is an industry-facing national entity with paid participation from 30 industrial members, in addition to experts from translational centres and IHLs.  SG MEM is the umbrella organization, coordinating and facilitating collaborations between industry partners, and also with translational centres and academia. The Programme Director, Techno-commercial/Marketing will report to the Managing Director, START and work closely with the Managing Director and senior technical leaders on growing the organization.  Some of the key responsibilities include the following: Working closely with the Managing Director on Strategic Planning, towards increasing financial self-reliance for START. Actively seeking out opportunities for new industry projects and collaborations. Developing and implementing a competitive pricing model for industry projects. Analysing and valuing START’s Intellectual Property. Acting as back-up to the Managing Director during the MD’s absence. Mentoring technology leaders in writing funding proposals, including for projects and collaborations and vetting the same for costing and timelines. Leading the operations of SG MEM, which will be hosted by START from October 1, 2026.  Leverage the strong relationship with our 30 paid industry members and develop new opportunities for growing SG MEM and START. Co-ordinating outreach activities for START and SG MEM. The candidate needs to have a Degree in Business Management (added knowledge of engineering would be a plus), Engineering or Science and a proven record of customer engagement and relationship management, techno-commercial skills, industry project costing, outreach and marketing, budget management, and personnel leadership.  The role requires at least 10 years of industry experience (techno-commercial sales and/or marketing), with at least 5 years in managerial roles. The skillsets for the role include the following: Managing customer base and developing new customers. Developing project and sales proposals, including costing and timelines. Strategic thinking and growth mindset. Team leadership and management. Appointment may vary and will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTUitive"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/HR-Executive--Human-Resource-Department---NIE-_R00025374": {
      "title": "HR Executive (Human Resource Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout the National Institute of Education (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore's national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation's education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . About the Role NIE HR partners the Institute across the full range of its people’s decisions, from day-to-day operations through to workforce planning and capability building. How we work reflects that. We use AI and digital tools to take the effort out of routine work, sharpen our insights and raise the quality of advice we give to staff and stakeholders. We are looking for an HR Executive who is comfortable working this way. You do not need a technical background. You do need good judgement, a bias for improving how things are done, and the discipline to verify what a tool gives you before it reaches a stakeholder. Responsibilities Assist in providing support for HR systems, including requirements gathering, user acceptance testing and post-implementation adoption. Support the full spectrum of HR functions such as appointment, contract renewal, leave, benefits and exit. Prepare HR reports and dashboards and help turn workforce data into clear observations that leaders can act on. Use approved AI and digital tools to draft, summarise and analyse — for example, first-cut correspondence and FAQs, thematic analysis of exit interview and survey feedback, and drafting of process documentation — always with human review before release. Review HR processes and procedures with an automation and simplification lens, and propose improvements where a workflow, template or tool would remove manual effort. Manage queries and provide advice to stakeholders such as line managers and employees, using our knowledge base and tools to respond accurately and quickly. Help maintain the quality of our HR knowledge base and templates so that our digital tools draw on current and correct information. Apply data protection, confidentiality and responsible-use standards in all use of AI tools, including on the handling of personal and sensitive employee data. Provide support in HR projects and initiatives. ​ Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma, preferably in Business Studies with specialisation in Human Resource Management. Preferably 2-3 years of relevant working experience in an HR role. Familiar with the Employment Act, local immigration rules and work pass application procedures. Meticulous, detail-oriented and comfortable working with numbers and data. Strong digital skills, including high proficiency in Microsoft Office. Comfort with spreadsheets beyond basic use (lookups, pivot tables) will be an advantage. Demonstrated practical use of AI tools in a work or study setting, with an understanding of their limits. You should be able to describe how you have used one, what you checked, and where you would not rely on it. Sound judgement on confidentiality and data handling. Able to take initiative, work independently and collaboratively in teams. Good written and spoken communication skills. Experience using Workday will be advantageous. Interest in pursuing IHRP certification will be viewed favourably. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 13 August 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--LKCMedicine-_R00025353-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Molecular and Cellular Dysfunction in Diabetes Laboratory, led by Associate Professor Yusuf Ali, combines in vitro systems biology, advanced imaging, in vivo models and multi-omics technologies to elucidate pathways critical to type 2 diabetes mellitus pathogenesis, with focus on pancreatic and immune function. The team is moving into molecular nutrition, harnessing the power of novel ingredients and prebiotics to mitigate the rise of persons living with diabetes. A laboratory under the Nutrition, Metabolism and Health programme, our work seeks for causality so that we can translate mechanistic insights into therapeutic strategies for mitigating type 2 diabetes and related metabolic conditions.   For more details, please view: https://dr.ntu.edu.sg/cris/rp/rp00609 We are seeking a passionate and motivated Research Fellow to contribute to a high-impact project exploring how intracellular lipid regulation is altered under different diets and how the endocrine pancreas can be better protected under obesity and metabolically dysregulated conditions. As type 2 diabetes is also a condition of low grade chronic inflammation, expertise on studying how circulating immune cells interact with tissue-specific immune cells will be a plus. The project investigates molecular mechanisms underpinning cell stress and resilience, integrating in vitro and in vivo studies using genetically modified mouse models, human islets, and multi-omics approaches. This position is ideal for researchers with a strong interest in lipid metabolism, autophagy/lipophagy, and diabetes pathophysiology. Key Responsibilities: Conduct various in vitro assays/experiments, including histology, western blotting, immunofluorescence microscopy, etc. Perform in vivo experiments, animal studies Computational biology to integrate results and generate list of perturbed pathways Contribute to research grant proposal applications, including literature review and preliminary data Contribute to research deliverables, such as manuscript writing, attending local and/or international conferences Mentor and supervision of undergraduate/PhD students and junior research staff Collaborate effectively with the research teams to achieve overall research goals and objectives Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies: PhD in Life Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, or related field At least 2-3 years of relevant experience in molecular biology, cell culture, imaging, or metabolic disease models Strong technical proficiency in laboratory techniques such as immunoblotting, immunofluorescence microscopy, qPCR, and animal handling Familiarity with regulatory standards, good laboratory practices and experience with IACUC protocols Excellent written and oral communication skills, with demonstrated ability to draft scientific manuscripts and presentations Strong organizational, motivational and self-driven skills, with a team-plater attitude (Entry-level candidates with strong experimental skills and interest in metabolic disease research are welcome to apply) Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Battery-Research---Electrolytes-_R00025362": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Battery Research – Electrolytes)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . The School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is seeking to hire a Research Fellow (Battery Research – Electrolytes) . We are seeking to hire a Research Fellow to drive cutting-edge research in advanced batteries. The incumbent will develop new electrolytes, interphases, and electrode materials , advancing fundamental understanding and practical performance of high-energy cell chemistries for energy storage systems. This role directly supports NTU’s mission to lead sustainable energy solutions for global impact. Key Responsibilities: Conduct independent and collaborative research on battery materials, electrolytes, and interphase engineering. Design and perform advanced electrochemical testing. Synthesize novel molecules and materials for battery electrolyte and interphase designs. Develop AI/ML methods to accelerate materials discovery for battery applications. Utilize and develop sophisticated characterization techniques to probe electrode interphase evolutions. Publish research outcomes in leading journals and present at international conferences. Collaborate with internal/external partners, including industry and international research groups. Contribute to grant proposals, project reports, and lab safety/management operations. Job Requirements: Education qualifications: PhD in Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Chemistry, Materials Science, Physics, or related fields. Soft skills: Independent thinker, excellent communicator, collaborative team player, and mentor Hard skills: Expertise in electrochemistry, spectroscopy, microscopy, and/or computational modeling. Experience: Strong track record in battery research, evidenced by publications in reputable journals. Competencies: Strong problem solving, creativity in research design, and commitment to academic excellence We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Resident-Relations_R00025354": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Resident Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Campus Housing (OCH) serves to make NTU the hub and destination to deliver best-in-class campus for learning, working, and living. OCH is a critical department responsible for student and faculty housing on campus, the sports and recreational facilities, and its related services. We are looking for an individual who has a strong passion for delivering exceptional service to residents of the University’s student and faculty housing, and athletes and users of sports & recreation facilities on campus.   The role provides the successful candidate with the opportunity to develop and contribute holistically across areas of excellence in customer relationship management, facilities & contracts management and/or quality and corporate functions (e.g. finance / billing, quality management, etc.) within the Department. If you are a diploma holder with at least 3 years of relevant working experience in residential management / services, customer service / resident relations management, or housing operation support and contract management, quality, and corporate service (finance / billing), you may be the one whom we are looking for. Having experience in student hostels, staff housing or hospitality services would be a plus for this role!  The incumbent is required to: Hostel application processing and the assignment of rooms / housing units, including the management of waitlist and students’ appeal for on-campus accommodation. Ensure the high quality of rooms / housing units for students’ check-in through comprehensive inspections. Ensure accurate billing of hall fees and other payable items as well as timely collection and follow-up where necessary. This includes accurate and timely refunds to students where applicable. Collaborate with colleagues and external vendors / contractors to get update on the status of maintenance / repairs to student hostels. Proactively engage student residents in understanding and addressing residents’ needs and contributing to problem-solving and resolution of concerns. This includes addressing and resolving student residents’ requests, feedback, and complaints promptly to meet SLA requirements. Communicate and inform student residents in advance on scheduled maintenance, adhoc repairs and other matters that may cause inconvenience to residents. Conduct routine walkthroughs of OCH managed premises to evaluate safety and security measures. This includes follow-up actions for enhancement and refinements of measures. Conduct investigations and compile supporting documentation for incident reports. This includes proposal of suitable sanctions for rule violations based on the severity and frequency of infractions, and prompt escalation of persistent and / or severe breaches for further enforcement measures, as well as implementation of approved sanctions. Maintenance of up-to-date and precise records, including resident details, occupancy status, and availability, to facilitate billing processes and management reporting. Ensure that facilities reservations are made through established booking channels, and all pre-event and post-event arrangements are properly managed. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Finance--AISG-_R00023794": {
      "title": "Manager, Finance (AISG)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis role is deployed to AISG and is a 2-year full time contract. Key Responsibilities include: Monitor all grants managed by AISG to ensure availability and grant compliance Ensure all financial procedures align with university policies and support year-end audit/tax filing processes Ensure SOPs are properly documented Manage research project financial data and system to ensure timely and accurate grant submission in accordance with the NTU policies and processes, grant T&C and harmonised guidelines Prepare periodic grant expense claim reports and management reports for Senior Management Coordinate with research teams for budgeting and financial reporting purposes Liaise with internal and external auditors on the grant certification audit & year end audit Mentor, guide and motivate staff Identify training needs and opportunities for staff Requirements Degree in Accounting, Finance, or related discipline; CA/CPA/ACCA preferred 8–10 years of finance experience, with at least 5 years in research grant finance (university / research institute / public sector) Strong experience managing high‑volume research grants, including budgeting, utilisation monitoring, claims, and compliance with grant T&Cs and harmonised guidelines Proven ability to support grant certification audits and year‑end audits, and liaise with internal and external auditors Hands‑on experience with finance and research grant systems and strong financial reporting skills Experience supervising and mentoring staff, and working closely with researchers and senior management Detail‑oriented, organised, and able to manage multiple deadlines in a fast‑paced research environment We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Earth-Science-Geophysics-_R00025342": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Earth Science/Geophysics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Asian School of the Environment (ASE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is an interdisciplinary school focusing on the connections between geosciences, ecology, society and Earth systems. Our approach integrates these disciplines to examine big hazards and environmental challenges both in Southeast Asia and globally. We conduct cutting-edge research on topics that include geohazards, climate change, sea-level rise, environmental sustainability, conservation of environment and biodiversity, and interactions between environment and society. We seek a Research Fellow to work on using dense seismic arrays, particularly distributed acoustic sensing (DAS), for hazards and coastal monitoring. The candidate will work under the supervision of Asst Prof Voon Hui Lai. The successful candidate should demonstrate expertise in seismic data processing and modelling, dense array analysis, distributed acoustic sensing, and seismoacoustics, and a strong track record of publishing impactful research in areas relevant to the position. Key Responsibilities: Develop methodologies to detect, characterize, and model seismic, coastal hazards and other environmental signals recorded on dense seismic and fibre-optic sensing data Plan and conduct field deployments using seismic and distributed acoustic sensing systems Publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals and present results at national and international conferences Provide scientific leadership and mentorship to undergraduate students, Research Assistants, and Research Associates, supporting their research development while fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing research environment. Build and maintain effective collaborations with project team members, researchers, and external partners, contributing to research planning, scientific discussions, and the successful achievement of project objectives and deliverables. Job Requirements: PhD in Earth science, geophysics, or a related field. Demonstrated expertise in seismic source detection, seismoacoustics, signal processing, waveform modelling, and/or environmental seismology. Proven experience in the analysis and interpretation of dense seismic array data and/or distributed acoustic sensing. Proven experience planning and conducting geophysical field deployments. Strong programming skills in Python or MATLAB. Strong track record of publishing research relevant to the position in leading Tier 1 journals Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, as the position requires engagement with stakeholders in an international research environment. Proven ability to prepare scientific manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at international conferences. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research while working effectively in a multidisciplinary and collaborative team environment. Interested applicants should submit a CV, research statement, list of referees, and list of publications and their relevance to position. For additional information, please email Asst. Prof. Voon Hui Lai at voonhui.lai@ntu.edu.sg . Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Quantum-Sensing-_R00024727": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Quantum Sensing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTemasek Laboratories@NTU TL@NTU explores the frontiers in science and develops strategic technologies to enhance the defence and security of Singapore. TL@NTU forms part of the defence technology community in Singapore alongside DSO National Laboratories, Defence Science and Technology Agency (DSTA), Temasek Laboratories @ NUS and @SUTD and the local defence industry. The Centre for Quantum Sensing Technology (CQST) advances the science and engineering of next‑generation quantum sensors, with core programmes in cold‑atom sensing, quantum photonics, quantum materials, and superconducting sensor technologies. Key Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be involved in experimental work related to quantum sensing materials development and characterization, device fabrication and instrumentation work as needed. The job scope includes To assist in research operations (procurement of lab supplies, experimental setup, checking of literature and product specifications, establish safe work processes, etc.) To ensure conduct and proper documentations of experiments in consultation with project leader To assist in monitoring, repair and maintenance of equipment and process tools To support events, publications, proposals, planning, monitoring, reporting related to the project as relevant.  Job Requirements:  Minimally BSc/BEng in physics, engineering, materials engineering with 1-2 years of industry work experience would be advantageous Relevant prior experience in quantum related work would be advantageous We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Stakeholder-Engagement_R00024427": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Stakeholder Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nRanked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides education within the University and the region. The Assistant Director, Stakeholder Engagement is responsible for leading and implementing the existing and new initiatives to drive, facilitate and execute new opportunities for students’ I&E growth journeys as part of a holistic entrepreneurship education. The incumbent is responsible for identifying and facilitating collaboration between NTU community and external stakeholders, such as ESG, ACE, SGInnovate, Social Impact Catalyst, raiSE etc and government or government funded institutions. The incumbent will facilitate to connect NTU students to available resources (for example, equipment) and facilities (Innovation Ports and Makers’ Labs) on campus. This role will work with the relevant managers of these resources to provide the necessary support and accelerate students’ I&E journeys. The incumbent will play a strategic role in designing and curating high-impact Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) initiatives that bridge students with industry, ecosystem partners, and global opportunities. This role focuses on expanding and strengthening students’ I&E pathways, through curated activities and collaborations with strategic partners to enhance relevant industry knowledge, expertise, and real-world experience to enrich learning and venture-building outcomes. Working across institutions of the NTU I&E and NTU schools, the role focuses on enabling students across disciplines to translate ideas into viable startups through structured, outcome-based initiatives, as well as strengthening NTUpreneur’s position within the local and global entrepreneurship ecosystem through strategic partnerships and stakeholder engagement. The successful candidate can look forward to a rewarding career at NTU with ample opportunities for growth and development. Job Responsibilities: Drive, design, strengthen, and promote NTU Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) Pathway for Students Provide leadership to strengthen existing I&E Pathway for NTU students.  Conceptualise, and organise impactful and outcome-driven co-curricular I&E programmes, to increase entrepreneurial skillsets and experience in real-world situations and exposure to industry, Grow student leadership in I&E activities through targeted strategy, for example, proactive engagement with relevant students’ Clubs and Societies, and other student networks to lead I&E activities on campus. Lead Stakeholder Engagement and Industry Partnership Development Identify, build, and sustain strong relationships with alumni, local and international industry partners, startups, venture capitalists, accelerators, and ecosystem players. Through partnerships, create meaningful opportunities to increase knowledge on venture creation, opportunities for venture incubation, increase local and global exposure to the I&E ecosystem. Increase NTU I&E visibility and reputation locally and internationally, through active participation and by organising representatives in events organised by high-profile institutions/ organisations. Drive internal collaboration towards NTU I&E Alignment Identify opportunities and drive collaborations with faculty, Leads of the undergraduate, postgraduate teams, and experiential learning (student venture support) teams to align programmes and their objectives for stronger outcomes. Support cross-functional initiatives within NTUpreneur and the broader NTU I&E ecosystem. Oversee the design and implementation of major University I&E events to ensure effective outcomes and implement effective outreach strategies to reach the targeted audience Conceptualise I&E engagement activities with strong value proposition to attract students to pursue entrepreneurship education and entrepreneurship in major university-level events such as the annual Open House, Freshmen Orientation, and NTUpreneur Day, the annual Chua Thian Poh Pinnacle Prize and Distinguished Speakers Series. Engage strategic partners of other NTU’s departments such as NTUitive, International Engagement Office, Alumni Engagement Office to organise I&E activities etc. Drive, and oversee the implementation of  effective outreach and marketing materials to promote NTUpreneur’s activities Conceptualise effective and targeted marketing and outreach strategies to promote our academic, experiential learning (I&E Pathways) programmes. Oversee and coordinate with academic programme teams to ensure that NTUpreneur’s website is updated promptly and check on compliance of NTU I&E Corporate Guidelines for all EDMs and brochures. Manage by creating or coordinating content creation of NTUpreneur’s social media. Report engagement results on a monthly basis. Requirements : Bachelor’s (Hons) Degree (Preferably in Entrepreneurship or Business) At least 5 years relevant work experience in a university and multi-disciplinary environment. Experience in the startup ecosystem is a plus. Experience in fact-finding and analysing data to ensure effective outcomes Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Experience in working with professors, I&E government funding agencies, MNCs with innovation arm. Good communication skills Knowledge in entrepreneurship, start-up development and ecosystem Knowledge of best practices in venture support in world-class universities as part of a holistic entrepreneurship education Knowledge in government grants, and other available support from related agencies for startups in Singapore Experience in budget planning, managing and processing claims in grants Enjoy working with students, empowering and helping them to accelerate their I&E journeys Capability to work independently to drive the execution of projects, but with strong attributes of a team player Demonstrated resourcefulness, strong problem-solving skills, and the ability to multitask efficiently, even under tight deadlines Meticulous and eye for details in organising information and tracking work progress Creative and refreshing ideas and demonstrated experience in organising large-scale events We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--AI--Technology--Medicine-_R00025329": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (AI, Technology, Medicine)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Division of Information Technology and Operations Management at Nanyang Business School is inviting applications for a Research Assistant position. Job Responsibilities: The RA is expected to plan, organize and implement research projects, in collaboration with the principal investigators. The successful candidate will work closely with professionals in the field of AI, technology and medicine. Conduct literature reviews, coordinate schedules for data collection with survey and interview participants Assist in data collection, data transcription and analysis Contribute to the dissemination of research findings Job requirements: Minimally a bachelor’s degree in a related field (i.e. Business, AI, Technology or Medicine) Excellent oral and written communication skills are required Able to work independently and meet deadlines Experience with qualitative methods and data analysis We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Science---Computer-Engineering---Cybersecurity---Artificial-Intelligence-_R00025324": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Science / Computer Engineering / Cybersecurity / Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Associate to contribute to the design and implementation of simulation environments, intelligent testing and traffic analysis frameworks, automated security evaluation tools, experimental studies and technical documentation Job Responsibilities: Develop and maintain the simulation and testing environment for drone communication protocols. Design and implement intelligent frameworks for protocol fuzz testing and security evaluation. Develop traffic analysis methods for anomaly detection, behaviour classification and attack inference. Conduct experiments to assess protocol robustness, security and resilience under abnormal and adversarial conditions. Develop automated methods for validating identified vulnerabilities and evaluating potential attack scenarios. Analyse experimental results and contribute to the improvement of the developed frameworks and methodologies. Develop LLM-based agentic frameworks for generating intelligent and diverse fuzzing inputs. Prepare technical documentation, project reports, research publications and presentations, and work with the research team to achieve project milestones and deliverables. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline. Relevant experience in software development, cybersecurity, network protocols, artificial intelligence or related research areas. Good programming skills in languages such as Python, C or C++. Familiarity with Linux-based development environments, software debugging and testing tools. Knowledge of network communication, protocol analysis, vulnerability assessment or traffic analysis. Experience with machine learning, large language models, automated testing or security research would be advantageous. Strong analytical, problem-solving and technical documentation skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team, with good written and verbal communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Science---Software-Engineering---Artificial-Intelligence-_R00025323": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Science / Software Engineering / Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to conduct research in formal verification, machine learning and artificial intelligence system assurance. The successful candidate will develop new techniques and tools for analysing, verifying and improving the correctness, robustness and reliability of deep neural networks and AI-enabled software systems.   Job Responsibilities: Develop novel methods and algorithms for the verification, testing and robustness analysis of deep neural networks and AI-enabled systems. Explore techniques such as abstraction, invariant learning, convex approximation, symbolic analysis and high-dimensional geometric analysis to improve the scalability and precision of AI verification. Evaluate the developed techniques through experiments, benchmark datasets and real-world AI applications. Publish research findings in reputable conferences and journals, and prepare project reports and technical deliverables. Collaborate with the Principal Investigator, research team and external partners, while mentoring junior researchers and students. Job Requirements: PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research and develop novel research methods. Proven research track record with publications in reputable conferences or journals. Ability to work independently and collaboratively, with good analytical, communication and mentoring skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTUGillman-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Social-Science-Arts-Humanities-_R00025249": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Social Science/Arts/Humanities)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Climate Transformation Programme (CTP) is spearheaded by the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS). It aims to develop, inspire and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just, and sustainable Southeast Asian societies. The Climate Transformation Programme–Sustainable Societies Cluster works collaboratively across the CTP themes from Climate and Biodiversity, Mitigation, to Climate Processes and Extremes, to develop a suite of programmes that form a synergistic relay of interdisciplinary research and external outreach. The initiatives aim to cultivate a critical multiplicity of voices, perspectives, and knowledges from both within and outside academic realms in the formation of ‘Sustainable Societies’ that engage with questions of climate change. The position supports the Sustainable Societies (Arts Sub-Group) Cross-Cutting Cluster under the MOE Tier 3c Climate Transformation Programme (CTP). The CTP is spearheaded by the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS). The Sustainable Societies (Arts Sub-Group) Cluster is co-led by Principal Investigator (PI) Professor Laura Miotto. Under the supervision of Professor Miotto, the position serves as a key contact in coordinating projects and initiatives led by the cluster, from the administration and preparation of materials for reporting to the coordination of internal and external stakeholders. The role will assist in general administration and coordinate with various NTU departments as required, from the Finance department to the Administrative Office of EOS. The role will also contribute to content development and the organization of research and educational public programmes such as the Climate Transformation: Sustainable Societies Lecture Series and adjacent gatherings. This position is for an 8-month contract. The candidate will be based at the NTU Centre for Contemporary Art Singapore at Gillman Barracks. For more information, visit the website https://ntu.ccasingapore.org/ . Key Responsibilities: Key administrative contact for various project stakeholders such as co-investigators, local and international collaborators, research fellows and other internal and external parties, including vendors. Provide general administrative support, day to day management, and organisational logistics of the research project. Prepare all project materials for all reporting obligations (both grantor and NTU) and ensure timely completion and submission. Assist in the preparation of field trips in all matters, ranging from visa to travel and accommodation arrangements. Assist Research Associate/Research Fellow/PI in data management and executions of any meetings, conference and exhibitions where necessary. Undertake any other duties relevant to the research project such as corresponding with stakeholders and working with other departments (e.g. Finance and event management) Support the PI, as well as the Co-I in all grant administration matters. Job Requirements: Possess at minimum a Bachelor’s degree in a relevant social science, arts or humanities discipline. Demonstrated professional experience in academic, research or educational institutions. Strong skills in organisation/administration, project and time management in order to meet competing deadlines. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to liaise with internal and external stakeholders and collaborators. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Excel, Adobe CS, social media programmes Demonstrated writing skills for grant applications. Experience with A/V equipment assisting with video and audio recording. Highly motivated and able to work independently with minimal supervision. The closing date of the advertisement is 14th August 2026 . We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Integrated-Polaritonic-Devices-_R00025314": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Integrated Polaritonic Devices)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Fellow at National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP) will contribute to the development of integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, with emphasis on long-range polariton propagation, low-energy switching concepts, few-particle modulation of condensate nonlinearities, integrated polaritonic circuit functions, and coupling of polaritonic states to on-chip detection/readout architectures. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to conduct research in integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, including the design, fabrication, optimization and experimental characterization of polaritonic waveguides, polariton lasers, cavity/waveguide networks, and polaritonic circuit elements. The role includes developing and operating advanced optical spectroscopy setups; measuring propagation, emission, nonlinear response, switching behaviour, photon-correlation behaviour, and coupling to detection/readout platforms; and supporting the development of long-range polaritonic waveguiding platforms and polaritonic logic or routing functions. The Research Fellow is expected to work, generate ideas and experimentally prove them both independently and within team-working efforts with other researchers working on the project to deliver state‑of‑the‑art single‑photon imaging capabilities, and to disseminate results through publications, reports, and IP contributions. Requirements: PhD in Physics, Photonics, Optical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, or a related field. Strong research background in experimental optics, photonics, optical spectroscopy, exciton-polariton physics, nonlinear optics, semiconductor optics, or related areas. Proven publication record in internationally recognized peer-reviewed journals. Experience in designing, aligning, and operating advanced optical setups involving lasers, microscopy, spectroscopy, and imaging systems is preferred. Experience in polariton devices, photonic waveguides, topological photonics, photonic crystals, or single-photon measurement techniques is advantageous. Proficiency in scientific programming and data analysis tools such as Python or MATLAB. Strong analytical, communication, teamwork, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently in a research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Integrated-SNSPD-Detectors-_R00025315": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Integrated SNSPD Detectors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Fellow at National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP) will contribute to the development of integrated superconducting nanowire single-photon detector (SNSPD) technologies for on-chip quantum photonic and sensing platforms. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to conduct research in integrated SNSPD detectors and readout technologies, including the development and experimental validation of waveguide-integrated SNSPD devices; process integration; optical coupling optimization; on-chip detection-efficiency measurement; timing-jitter characterization; photon-number-resolving operation; and detector integration with quantum photonic circuits. The role also includes nanofabrication and process development for integrated photonic and detector structures, including thin-film deposition, lithography, etching, wafer- or chip-scale process flow optimization, and materials/device characterization. The Research Fellow will also develop SNSPD integration in MWIR topological waveguides and waveguide-integrated MWIR detector platforms, including device fabrication/assembly, coupling to MWIR waveguides, and optimization of detector performance. The role further includes development of SNSPD detector arrays and readout architectures, including multi-pixel detector arrays, space- or time-multiplexed effective-pixel arrays, photon-number-resolving detection, integrated electronic boards for control/readout, hybrid cryogenic electronics, biasing, amplification, thresholding, digitization, and detector-array performance benchmarking. The Research Fellow is expected to support cryogenic packaging and system-level integration, including fiber-array coupling, electrical interconnects, compact packaging of detector chips, low-noise readout interfaces, and reliability/yield/stability assessment of integrated detector prototypes. The Research Fellow is expected to work, generate ideas and experimentally prove them both independently and within team-working efforts with other researchers working on the project to deliver state‑of‑the‑art single‑photon imaging capabilities, and to disseminate results through publications, reports, and IP contributions. Requirements: PhD in Physics, Photonics, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Nanotechnology, or a related discipline. Strong research background in integrated photonics, nanophotonics, nanofabrication, photonic device fabrication, superconducting detectors, or related fields. Proven publication record in reputable peer-reviewed journals. Experience in cleanroom fabrication processes and advanced materials/device characterization techniques is preferred. Familiarity with photonic waveguide platforms and detector integration technologies is advantageous. Experience with SNSPDs, superconducting materials, cryogenic measurements, MWIR photonics, detector arrays, readout electronics, or cryogenic packaging will be an added advantage. Proficiency in scientific programming, data analysis, simulation, and modeling tools (e.g., Python, MATLAB, TCAD, photonic simulation software). Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication, and teamwork skills, with the ability to work independently in a research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Human-Factors-_R00025308": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Human Factors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAir Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) is a research institute at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, supported by the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). The key objective of ATMRI is to support research and innovation in air traffic management. ATMRI focuses on developing practical and data-driven solutions for complex aviation systems, in close collaboration with industry and international partners. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/atmri . We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems in air traffic management (ATM), with a focus on operator cognitive load, situational awareness, and decision-support interfaces for air traffic controllers. The role will involve designing and evaluating human-in-the-loop tools using methods such as eye-tracking, physiological sensing, and uncertainty visualization, contributing to the advancement of research and innovation at Nanyang Technological University. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems approaches to support air traffic management studies and applications. Design, develop, and evaluate decision-support interfaces and operator-facing tools using operational and simulated data. Support research activities on controller cognitive load, situational awareness, and resilience under current and future ATM concepts. Work collaboratively with researchers and engineers to develop prototype solutions and human-in-the-loop evaluation frameworks. Conduct user studies and analyse results (e.g. eye-tracking, physiological sensing) to assess the performance and usability of developed tools in realistic operational scenarios. Prepare technical reports, research papers, and project deliverables, and participate in project meetings and reviews. Publish research findings in top-tier journals and conferences in relevant fields (e.g. human-computer interaction, human factors, ATM). Contribute to research proposals, technical documentation, and other project-related activities as required. Job Requirements: PhD qualification in Human-Computer Interaction, Cognitive Science, Human Factors, Air Traffic Management, Transport, or other related fields. At least three (3) years of relevant research experience in human factors, cognitive systems, or related technical research roles, ideally within transport, aviation, or other safety-critical operational domains. Familiarity with research related to cognitive load assessment, decision-support interfaces, or human-in-the-loop systems for complex operational environments (e.g. air traffic management, control rooms). Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical reports and academic publications. Proficiency in job-specific technical skills, including programming for research and data analysis purposes (e.g. Python or similar languages), experience with eye-tracking or physiological sensing methods, as well as strong numerical and analytical skills. Competent in general research-related skills and professional attributes, including problem-solving and analytical thinking. Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively, develop solutions under defined timelines, and demonstrate good organisational and time management skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Materials-Physics-_R00025309": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum Materials Physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. The Belopolski Research Group (QuantumX Labs) is hiring ambitious & creative Research Fellows to explore topological quantum materials. Our group aims to discover new topological quantum phases of matter, explore their physics and apply them to address challenges in electronics, photonics, quantum computing, catalysis and biology. We use molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) to synthesize atomically precise crystals, we integrate them with two-dimensional exfoliated materials, and we characterize them using transport and angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES). We have immediate need for enthusiastic postdocs to synthesize novel quantum anomalous Hall phases by MBE, characterize altermagnets and p -wave magnets by ARPES, pursue scalable wafer-scale moiré epitaxy, develop epitaxial superconductors for quantum computing and integrate machine learning for automated high-throughput MBE. We are particularly excited to recruit postdocs with experience in optics, two-dimensional materials and a strong theoretical background. Applicants should have a Ph.D. in quantum physics, electrical engineering or a related field. Key Responsibilities The Research Fellow will pursue scientific research broadly on topological quantum materials at QuantumX Labs, the research group of Prof. Ilya Belopolski, https://www.quantumx.science . Researchers will have the opportunity to, Synthesize atomically precise thin films of new topological materials using molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) Develop innovative approaches to accelerate MBE materials development using in situ characterization & machine learning Integrate epitaxial synthesis with exfoliated two-dimensional materials & devices Characterize resistivity, Hall response, non-linear transport and magnetization Explore electronic structure with angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES) at synchrotrons such as Diamond Light Source in the UK or the Advanced Light Source in the USA Develop theoretical models of topological materials to understand & interpret experimental data Leverage nanofabrication facilities & collaborate with other leading research groups at the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) and the School of Physical & Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Collaborate worldwide to identify new candidate materials, perform ab initio calculations and complement our results with additional experimental techniques Build out additional in-house experimental capabilities in optics, microwaves and quantum sensing The researcher is also encouraged to bring in physics & techniques from their Ph.D. which augment or resonate with the interests of our group & the community at NTU. Job Requirement Ph.D. in quantum physics, electrical engineering or a related discipline; familiarity with superconductivity, magnetic skyrmions, topological insulators, Mott insulators and/or quantum spin liquids Technical experience with experimental synthesis, transport & optics techniques, such as: Low-temperature transport & characterization by PPMS, MPMS and/or dilution fridge Second harmonic generation, photoluminescence, Raman spectroscopy & other optical techniques Materials synthesis by molecular beam epitaxy (MBE), pulsed laser deposition (PLD) etc. Exfoliation & device fabrication of two-dimensional materials such as graphene & chalcogenides Strong theoretical & mathematical background Interest in leading scientific breakthroughs, as well as working closely with a team, to deepen our understanding of emergent phenomena in quantum physics and pioneer applications to electronics, photonics, quantum computing, catalysis and biology We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Business-Systems-Specialist-Analyst--Digital-Solutions-Department---NIE-_R00023948": {
      "title": "Business Systems Specialist/Analyst (Digital Solutions Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . The National Institute of Education (NIE) invites suitable candidates to join the Division of Academic Computing & Information Services (ACIS) as a Business Systems Specialist/Analyst (19-month contract). This role is instrumental in supporting various project management initiatives within the organization, with a strong emphasis on stakeholder management. We are seeking a dynamic IT professional who excels in project management and is an effective team player. If you are looking for an exciting opportunity to contribute to the advancement of educational systems in the academic domain, we encourage you to apply. Join us in shaping the future of education at NIE! Job Description As a member of the Digital Solutions department responsible for project management initiatives for Academic’s Domain , your responsibilities will include: Strategic Visibility & Stakeholder Management : Act as the primary advocate for the user community, ensuring all stakeholders are engaged regarding their system concerns and feel heard by the Digital Solutions department. Proactively communicate project roadmaps and keep the university and institution informed about the progress of institute strategic initiatives. Manage change effectively by ensuring users are well-informed of enterprise-level changes, system updates, and ongoing technology refresh of legacy applications. Establish real-time dashboards to enhance performance transparency, making project health and support metrics visible to Digital Solutions leaders and the wider division. Collaborate closely with the Development Team to provide visibility on project plans, stakeholder feedback, and institutional changes. Support Strategy & Triage Governance : Oversee the classification of support requests by domain to protect project timelines and ensure effective resource allocation. Define and monitor Service Level Agreements (SLAs) for all user-facing requests to maintain high institutional satisfaction through timely responses. Innovation Delivery & Data Integrity : Continuously seek to implement innovations driven by AI, data, and automation across institutional applications. Lead initiatives to ensure data integrity and accuracy, addressing any discrepancies proactively. Collaborate with the Development team to enhance the efficiency of processes and implement automated solutions where feasible. Utilize AI-driven insights to monitor project performance and identify areas for improvement before they impact the user community. Requirements A University degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field. At least 2 years of experience in a project management or related role, with specific exposure to stakeholder management and support. Proven expertise in project management methodologies and techniques. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to engage with a diverse range of stakeholders. Familiarity with data governance and compliance principles. Quick learner who is passionate and willing to learn new languages and technologies. Experience in the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) framework and Agile project management methodologies. Knowledge of cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure) is a plus. Fresh graduates with a keen interest in AI-assisted development and project management are welcome to apply. Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail. Self-motivated team player with a positive attitude, capable of adapting to changes. Ability to work under tight deadlines and manage fluid requirements. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 6 August 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Gesture-Sign-Linguistics--Computational-Linguistics-_R00025303": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Gesture—Sign Linguistics, Computational Linguistics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are looking for a Research Fellow to support the Principal Investigator in advancing research on gesture, sign language, and computational linguistics. The role will focus on designing and conducting experiments, analysing gesture and sign language data, and collaborating with the PI and project partners on related publications and deliverables. Key Responsibilities: Design and conduct experiments on gesture and sign language; Annotate and analyse video/motion-capture data; Apply statistical methods to linguistic data Collaborate with the PI and partners on findings and publications; Supervise junior student assistants; Prepare reports and contribute to publications; Ensure compliance with ethical guidelines and project timelines. Job Requirements: PhD in Linguistics, Sign Language Studies, Cognitive Science, or a related field; Relevant experience in gesture studies, sign language research, or experimental linguistics; Proficiency in video/motion-capture annotation tools and statistical/computational analysis (e.g. R, Python, ELAN); Strong written and oral communication skills; Ability to work independently and collaboratively across disciplines. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--AI-in-Medicine_R00025293-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow, AI in Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre of AI in Medicine is a university-level research centre with the mission to bridge the gap between cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies and practical applications in healthcare, The key objective is to spearheadresearch and development to revolutionise patient care and inform public health policies. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/c-aim We are looking for a Postdoctoral Fellow to play a central role in galvanising and advancing the Centre’s efforts in research collaboration and grant applications. The Postdoctoral Fellow will provide critical leadership and support across C-AIM’s portfolio of AIML projects strategic planning, grant writing, review of research agreements, and ensuring the smooth operation of the Centre’s flagship projects. The role will focus on: Developing strategic plans to advance research capability of the Centre: Formulate and implement short-, medium-, and long-term research strategies that strengthen the Centre’s research capacity, competitiveness, and impact. Monitor research performance indicators and recommend initiatives to enhance research productivity, quality, and sustainability. Building and extending research collaboration efforts with key partners within a dynamic multidisciplinary environment Cultivate and strengthen strategic partnerships with academic institutions, healthcare organisations, industry partners, government agencies, and community stakeholders. Initiate, coordinate, and manage collaborative research projects that leverage expertise across multiple disciplines and sectors. Identify opportunities for national and international collaborations that enhance the Centre’s research profile and expand its research ecosystem. Designing and conducting research aligned with the Centre’s research pillars, including literature reviews, data collection, and data analysis. Lead the conceptualisation, design, and execution of research studies that align with the Centre’s strategic research themes and priorities. Conduct comprehensive literature reviews and environmental scans to identify evidence gaps, inform study design, and support the development of research proposals. Develop robust research methodologies, protocols, and data collection instruments using qualitative, quantitative, or mixed-methods approaches as appropriate. Oversee data collection activities, ensuring compliance with ethical, regulatory, and institutional requirements. Perform rigorous data management, statistical analysis, and interpretation of findings using appropriate analytical tools and methodologies. Prepare research reports, policy briefs, presentations, and manuscripts that effectively communicate findings to academic, professional, and stakeholder audiences. Advancing Centre’s performance in publications and grant applications Drive the development and submission of high-quality grant proposals to secure competitive research funding from local and international funding bodies. Identify funding opportunities and coordinate multidisciplinary teams in the preparation of grant applications, budgets, and supporting documentation. Lead and contribute to the publication of research findings in high-impact peer-reviewed journals and other scholarly outlets. Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies: PhD graduates, in medical AI, healthcare informatics, bioinformatics, computer science, AI implementation science, or related disciplines, Have graduated within four years from their respective PhD programs at the time of application. Received at least two years of graduate training (including the PhD duration) Demonstratable familiarity in ideally two or more of the following disciplines: biomedical informatics, clinical research, medicine, public health, implementation science and data science Excellent track record of research accomplishments Keen to embark on exciting and innovative projects involving the development of medical AI technologies, working with stakeholders in education and implementation, healthcare AI governance and regulation, and other topics pertaining to the successful deployment of AI into healthcare systems, especially in Singapore. Keen to embark on exciting and innovative projects in AI in Medicine Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Climate-Transformation-Programme--CTP--_R00025287-1": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Climate Transformation Programme (CTP))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) at Nanyang Technological University in Singapore invites applications for the position of Project Officer to support the Climate Transformation Program (CTP). The CTP is an interdisciplinary research program with the mission to develop, inspire and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just and sustainable SEA societies. The incumbent will provide comprehensive administrative, financial, and operational support for research programmes and projects, with a strong focus on ensuring compliance with funding agency and University policies governing grant management and fund utilization. This includes but not limited to tracking of grant-related documentation and handling of procurement and logistics needs. The role will also contribute to various type of report preparation, project management and  research-related activities to support the successful delivery of project objectives. Key Responsibilities: Provide support for the day-to-day management of research projects, including finance, procurement, and project coordination. Process procurement transactions (Purchase Requisitions, Purchase Orders, Goods Receipts), reimbursement claims, and financial documentation in accordance with University and funding agency policies. Monitor project budgets and expenditures, maintain accurate financial records, and support budget tracking and reporting. Coordinate project meetings, workshops, seminars, travel arrangements, and other programme activities, including logistical support for local and overseas collaborators. Liaise with Principal Investigators (PIs), researchers, funding agencies, NTU Shared Services, and other internal and external stakeholders to facilitate the smooth implementation of research projects. Monitor project progress, maintain project records and databases, and track key deliverables, milestones, and performance indicators. Prepare and compile progress reports, financial reports, and supporting documentation for funding agencies, audits, and management reporting. Ensure compliance with University policies, funding agency requirements, and governance procedures, while providing general support to research teams. Perform other project-related and ad hoc administrative duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Project Management, Science, Finance or a related discipline, with at least 3 years of relevant working experience in project administration, finance or grant management. A strong finance background is preferred. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multi-cultural team environment. Excellent interpersonal, planning and coordination skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills, able to interact professionally with stakeholders at all levels Excellent organizational, analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to multitask and prioritize tasks in a fast-paced environment. Experience in managing government-funded research grants and familiarity with Singapore’s research grant management guidelines will be an advantage. Interested applicants should submit a CV, and a statement of interest. Incomplete applications will not be considered. NTU seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Electronic-Engineering--Computer-Science--Mechanical-Engineering--_R00025278": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Electronic Engineering/ Computer Science/ Mechanical Engineering )",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a talented and responsible researcher to support the scientific research and the engineering practice in perception and embodied intelligence. Key Responsibilities: The Research Fellow will work on a project to conduct research on learning from human demonstrations for robot manipulation used in household service and manufacturing. The roles of this position include: Develop robotic foundation models for general manipulation based on vision-language-action models Develop learning from human demonstration (LfD) framework for vision-language-action models Develop multi-embodiment retargeting framework with safety constraints Develop a mobile bimanual manipulation system to complete diverse tasks in household environment and in manufacturing deployment scenarios Job Requirement PhD in Electronic Engineering, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering or related field 3-year research experience in related area Expertise in robotic manipulation systems Knowledge in robotic foundation models  Publication track record is an advantage Proficiency in basics of programming languages such as ROS and Python Excellent communication skills, written and verbal – able to communicate complex concepts clearly and accurately We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be informed. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Postgraduate---Continuing-Education-Programmes--LKCMedicine-_R00025273": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Postgraduate & Continuing Education Programmes [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is seeking a detail-oriented and organised Senior Executive to join the Graduate Programmes team. The successful candidate will provide essential administrative support for our CET programmes, ensuring smooth operations, seamless digital course delivery, and a positive learner experience. The Senior Executive will be a primary point of contact for learners and adjunct faculty, ensuring a smooth and positive experience for all stakeholders. This role is central to the successful delivery of our programmes, involving the coordination of programme logistics, management of learner support, and assistance with financial administration. Responsibilities: Programme Administration & Logistics Coordinate the end-to-end logistics for all CET programmes, including scheduling, booking of venues or virtual platforms, and managing catering. Provide administrative support to Course Directors, including scheduling programme meetings, preparing minutes, and assisting with programme reviews. Manage digital dissemination of course content; set up courses on the Learning Management System (LMS) and ensure all online learning materials are current and accessible. Provide on-site or online administrative support during programme sessions to assist faculty and learners, and to manage attendance. Administer pre and post-programme activities, including the collection of feedback, collation of results, and generation of reports. Learner & Stakeholder Support Serve as the primary front-line support for CET programmes, handling all enquiries from prospective learners, current participants, and the public via email and phone. Manage the full learner registration and enrolment process, from application processing and matriculation to fee collection and issuance of confirmations. Maintain accurate learner records and manage the issuance of course certificates, transcripts, and other relevant documentation. Liaise with adjunct faculty and instructors to coordinate schedules, gather teaching materials, and process administrative and payment-related requests. Finance & Administrative Support Assist the Manager with financial administration for the CET portfolio. Coordinate with the Office of Faculty Affairs to facilitate the appointment, renewal, and onboarding of trainers and adjunct faculty. Process procurement requests, including raising purchase orders and ensuring compliance with university procurement policies. Handle the processing of invoices and claims for payment from external vendors, part-time lecturers, and adjunct faculty. Perform data entry and maintain accurate records for programme finance and learner enrolment. Requirements: A recognised diploma in any discipline. A degree in Business, Communications, or a related field is an advantage. Minimum 2–3 years of hands-on experience in an administrative, operational, or customer service role. Excellent organisational and multitasking skills, with a proven ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Meticulous with a keen eye for detail, particularly in record-keeping and processing information. Strong interpersonal and communication (both written and verbal) skills, with a customer-centric mindset. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook). A proactive and collaborative team player who is also able to work independently. This is a 3 years contract appointment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Advanced-power-electronics-and-energy-systems-_R00025268": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Advanced power electronics and energy systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to support research and development activities in advanced power electronics and energy systems. The role involves the design, development, control, and experimental validation of high-efficiency power electronic converters, including solid-state transformers and advanced power-delivery architectures for data centres. The technologies developed may also support renewable energy integration, energy storage, DC distribution, and smart-grid applications. The Research Fellow will contribute to project execution, research proposal preparation, industry collaboration, and the dissemination of research outcomes through technical reports, publications, and presentations. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research and development in power electronic converters, solid-state transformers, data-centre power-delivery systems, converter control, and energy systems. Design, model, simulate, and develop advanced power electronic converter topologies and associated control algorithms. Investigate high-efficiency and high-power-density power-conversion architectures for data-centre power delivery, DC distribution, renewable energy integration, energy storage, and grid-connected applications. Support the development of solid-state transformer technologies, including converter topology design, control, protection, system integration, and performance evaluation. Design and build laboratory-scale power converter prototypes, control platforms, and associated hardware systems. Perform experimental testing, data acquisition, data analysis, and evaluation of system efficiency, power density, reliability, and dynamic performance. Develop simulation and system-level models using tools such as MATLAB/Simulink, PLECS, PSCAD, or equivalent software. Support the integration and testing of power electronic converters, magnetic components, sensors, control systems, and laboratory hardware. Contribute to research proposal preparation, including literature reviews, technical writing, development of research concepts, and preparation of work plans. Prepare technical reports, project documentation, research publications, and conference presentations. Collaborate with faculty members, research staff, graduate students, external collaborators, and industry partners. Support the supervision and technical guidance of graduate students, undergraduate students, and research assistants when required. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety procedures and support the proper operation and maintenance of laboratory equipment. Job Requirements PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Power Electronics, Power Engineering, or a closely related field. Strong background in power electronic converter design, modelling, modulation, and control. Knowledge or experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: Solid-state transformers; Data-centre power-delivery architectures; High-frequency and high-power-density power conversion; DC distribution systems; Wide-bandgap semiconductor-based converters; Renewable energy and energy storage systems. Experience with simulation tools such as MATLAB/Simulink, PLECS, PSCAD, or equivalent software. Experience in power converter hardware design, prototyping, control implementation, laboratory testing, and experimental validation is preferred. Familiarity with digital control platforms, power semiconductor devices, magnetic components, protection systems, or thermal management would be advantageous. A good research publication record in power electronics or a related area is preferred. Prior experience in research proposal writing, technical grant preparation, or industry-funded research projects would be advantageous. Competencies Strong analytical, technical, and problem-solving capabilities. Ability to independently develop and execute research activities. Ability to work effectively within a multidisciplinary research team and collaborate with academic and industry partners. Good technical writing, presentation, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple research activities, project deliverables, and deadlines. Strong interest in high-efficiency power conversion, solid-state transformers, data-centre power delivery, and sustainable energy technologies. Commitment to high-quality research, experimental rigour, and laboratory safety. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Embodied-AI-_R00025271": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Embodied AI)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . Our team is seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to contribute to cutting-edge research in embodied AI and robotic manipulation. This role will support our mission to advance AI-driven robotic systems for real-world applications, including human-robot interaction, robotic perception, and intelligent control. The successful candidate will assist in developing novel algorithms and integrating them into robotic platforms, helping to push the boundaries of embodied intelligence in both research and practical deployment. Key Responsibilities: Develop and implement perception and control algorithms for robotic arms and embodied AI systems. Assist in integrating multimodal AI models (vision, language, force sensors) with robotic systems. Conduct experiments in both simulated and real-world environments, testing AI-driven robotic behavior. Work with hardware platforms, including robotic manipulators and mobile robots. Support the preparation of research publications, reports, and presentations. Collaborate with faculty, postdocs, and industry partners on AI and robotics research projects. Assist in the maintenance and operation of research lab equipment and robotic systems. Job Requirements: PhD degree with at least 3 first-author papers in Computer Science, Robotics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. Experience in robotic perception, control, or learning-based methods. Proficiency in Python and C++ for AI and robotics applications. Familiarity with robotic middleware (e.g., ROS, MoveIt) and hardware integration. Knowledge of machine learning, reinforcement learning, or vision-language models for robotics is a plus. Hands-on experience with robotic arms (e.g., UR5, Franka Emika, or similar) is desirable. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate-Research-Fellow--Plant-Biology-and-Molecular-Biology-_R00023891-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Plant Biology and Molecular Biology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) at NTU Singapore, in collaboration with Wageningen University & Research (WUR), is part of Singapore Indoor Farming System (SingFarm)—a CREATE-NRF programme focused on building a sustainable, data-driven food production model with strong industry relevance to contribute Singapore’s ambition in achieving 20 per cent local production of its fiber (vegetables, mushrooms etc.) by 2035. The candidate would be working in a multinational team at the forefront of Singapore’s agricultural innovation and food security. The position of Research Associate/Research Fellow will focus investigating the metabolic basis of agronomic and nutritional traits in Brassica crops through advanced metabolomics and multi-omics integration. The candidate will apply high-resolution metabolic profiling and data-driven approaches to uncover phytochemical diversity, identify metabolite–gene associations, and elucidate pathways underlying traits such as disease resistance, quality, and nutritional value. The role will contribute to linking metabolite composition with genetic variation and gene expression, enabling the discovery of key regulatory mechanisms and supporting targeted metabolic engineering strategies to enhance crop performance and nutritional quality. Key Responsibilities:  Perform metabolite profiling of segregating plant populations to identify compounds associated with traits such as disease resistance, quality, and shelf life Integrate metabolomic and genetic datasets to uncover metabolite–gene relationships Identify candidate metabolic pathways and underlying genes associated with target traits Conduct functional characterization and validation of candidate genes to elucidate their biological roles Research Associate (Master’s level) Master’s degree in Plant Biology, Biotechnology, Molecular Biology, Genetics, or a related field Strong biochemistry and plant genetics background Experience with plant molecular biology techniques Strong analytical skills and ability to work independently and as part of a team Independent and proactive working attitude Open and clear communication Research Fellow (PhD level) PhD degree in Plant Biotechnology, Molecular Genetics, Plant Physiology, or a closely related discipline Demonstrated experience with biochemistry, plant genetics and plant molecular biology techniques Strong analytical skills and ability to work independently and as part of a team Independent and proactive working attitude Open and clear communication Proven ability to lead experiments, analyze data, and publish research We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Assistant-Manager--Content-Development---Writer--Science-Engineering-Tech-_R00025266": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, Content Development & Writer (Science/Engineering/Tech)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis role supports the College of Engineering’s communications function through development of research-based content and supporting the coordination and administrative processes required for content delivery. Working closely with the Head of Communications, the role contributes to translating scientific and engineering concepts into accessible content, while supporting content pipelines, stakeholder coordination, and operational tasks across multiple schools. The position complements digital and design functions by supporting content development, organisation, and workflow management to enable consistent and timely communications outputs. Key Responsibilities: Scientific Content Development, Research Translation, & Writing Pitch, research, write, and edit technical stories, features, and profiles on faculty, students, research projects, and publications Conduct interviews with researchers and translate complex scientific concepts into clear, structured narratives Ensure scientific accuracy, clarity, and alignment with editorial standards Provide scientific, research and academic insight for team members and copy/content reviews as assigned Content Pipeline & Stakeholder Engagement Assist in the development of content pipeline system and campaigns Proactively identify and track potential content opportunities Maintain and update a centralised content pipeline tracker (stories in progress, upcoming opportunities, deadlines) Follow up with stakeholders to gather inputs, materials, and approvals Stakeholder Coordination & Administrative Support Coordinate interviews with faculty and researchers (scheduling, preparation, follow-ups) Manage communication with stakeholders to collect drafts, images, and approvals Support organisation of meetings, editorial calendars, and content planning sessions Publication Support Support preparation of content for website, newsletter, and publications Assist with proofreading, fact-checking, and editorial refinement Contribute to development of longer-form outputs (e.g. Annual Magazine, features) Ad Hoc Duties May Include: Communications calendar and scheduling support, including coordination of timelines, deadlines, and content planning Content intake and documentation, ensuring materials received from stakeholders are complete, organised, and ready for use Preparation of analytics inputs and basic reporting, including data gathering from digital platforms Assist in website maintenance and update General, digital and design function support as needed IDEAL PROFILE A background in science, engineering, or research combined with a strong interest in science communication or journalism; OR a background in science communication or journalism with a strong interest in science, engineering, or research; OR a combined background in both areas Ability to understand and interpret technical material Strong writing skills with attention to clarity and accuracy Understanding of what makes a good narrative Charismatic and comfortable engaging with academic stakeholders Organised and detail-oriented, with ability to manage multiple inputs We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Research-Achievements--Impact-and-Strategic-Enhancement--LKCMedicine-_R00025256": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager,  Research Achievements, Impact and Strategic Enhancement [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Research Achievements, Impact and Strategic Enhancement (RAISE) Office is established to develop strategies to enhance the research impact, visibility, and reputation of the school institutionally, nationally and internationally. It sits within the ambit of the LKCMedicine Research Administration and Support Services Department under the Vice Dean of Research Office. Reporting to the Head of RAISE, you will be part of a dynamic team at the vanguard of highlighting and reporting on the school’s research impact and achievements. You will also work with other departments including the School Faculty, Finance, Office of Innovation and Enterprise (OIE) and Office of Patient Engagement (OPEN). Responsibilities: Research Impact metrics, Data Analytics & AI Automation Evaluate and leverage platforms such as Altmetrics to capture non-traditional research impact metrics, including policy influence, societal engagement, and economic contributions etc Establish systematic frameworks to monitor, analyse, and report research impact metrics, incorporating AI-enabled analytics to identify trends, correlations, and emerging impact signals Compute and deliver reports on grant income of the School, incorporating automations to derive reporting needs such as breakdown of annualised grant quantum, update of grant end date etc  Perform multi-level data analyses related to research grants, including external grant return ratios at the school, programme, and individual faculty levels Design and implement AI-driven automation solutions (e.g., scripting, machine learning models, or workflow automation tools) to streamline data extraction, integration, validation, and reporting processes, reducing manual effort and enhancing scalability Consolidate, clean, and harmonise data from various sources (e.g., internal databases, research systems) to ensure consistency and reliability across datasets Develop and maintain interactive dashboards and data visualisations (e.g., using Power BI, Tableau, Programming or similar tools) to support research performance monitoring  Collaborate with internal stakeholders (e.g., IT, research systems teams) to strengthen data infrastructure, integrate AI-enabled tools, and develop solutions for real-time tracking of research impact and performance  Track and analyse research-related metrics that contribute to university rankings, and identify opportunities to strengthen the school’s research performance and ranking outcomes Research Communications & Visibility Build and maintain strong working relationships with faculty members to identify and track high-impact research publications for dissemination across appropriate publicity platforms, including the school website, social media channels, press releases, magazines, and other communication channels Organise and support events and activities that enhance the school’s research impact, reputation, and visibility Work closely with the Communications and Outreach Department to profile and publicise the achievements of research faculty Collaborate with programme and centre directors to coordinate and deliver the school’s annual publication on research impact and achievements Management Reporting Track, collate and synthesize updates from faculty and the wider research community, including media coverage, publication highlights, awards, and other key milestones Assist the team in preparing the Dean’s Management Report (quarterly), reporting to Governing Board and Board of Trustees, ensuring data accuracy and consistency Organise and support internal team and research programme meetings, including scheduling, preparing agendas, documenting minutes, and following up on action items Undertake ad-hoc tasks where required Requirements: Any Bachelor Degree / Diploma Some background or experience in data analytics / academic / healthcare industry / research communications would be preferred. More than 5 years of experience in data analytics, designing infographics, creating professional and attractive powerpoint slides for management.   Proficient in Microsoft Office especially MS Excel, MS Powerpoint Meticulous and good at designing dashboards, data visualizations, infographics Self-starter and ability to explore and evaluate new impact metrics with minimal supervision Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Positive attitude, able to multi-task, and work under pressure and tight deadlines Resourceful, strong analytical and problem-solving skills and ability to develop new ideas and provide conceptual solutions Added advantage if candidate has some knowledge in Programming, R, Python, RPA or related languages We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow-Senior-Research-Fellow--Systems-Neuroscience-or-NeuroAI--LKCMedicine-_R00025238-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow, Systems Neuroscience or NeuroAI [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are seeking Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow to join the Neuroscience and AI Research (Nair) group, led by Nanyang Assistant Professor Aditya Nair, to study how machine learning models and neural circuits in the brain process states of emotion. The Nair group combines cutting-edge systems neuroscience tools with the development of new AI methods to understand and model complex brain data. Key Responsibilities: For systems neuroscience focus: Perform in-vivo neural recordings in rodent models of social behavior and decision making. For NeuroAI focus: Analyze high-dimensional brain data, document results and carry out an independent research project. For NeuroAI focus: Develop and apply new machine learning and computer vision methods such as large-language models and vision-language models for high-throughput analysis of video data. For NeuroAI focus: Apply data-driven dynamical system modeling tools using specialized software packages to elucidate neural computations involved in emotion. Prepare and contribute to grant applications and conference presentations. The candidate is also expected to write and draft research publications in top neuroscience and AI journals.   Attend a weekly lab meeting and journal club and present data and/or papers as necessary. Key Competencies and Requirements: Doctoral degree (PhD) in systems neuroscience or computational neuroscience/AI/ML or relevant fields. We also invite candidates with interdisciplinary backgrounds to apply. For systems neuroscience focus: Experience with stereotaxic surgery in rodents, optogenetics and in-vivo microendoscopic imaging. For systems neuroscience focus: Experience with large-scale electrophysiology recordings with silicon probes or Neuropixel probes is highly advantageous.   For NeuroAI focus: Strong programming skills in Python and Matlab. For NeuroAI focus: Familiarity with analyzing large-scale neural data (such as imaging datasets, electrophysiology datasets or video data) is highly desirable. For NeuroAI focus: Proficiency in popular deep learning, computer vision and/or user-interface software frameworks (such as Pytorch, TensorFlow, OpenCV, PyQt, Gradio etc). The candidate is expected is have a strong numeric and analytical background. Competent in information visualization. A working knowledge of Adobe Illustrator is a strong advantage . Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary environment. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--Artificial-Intelligence-Neuroscience--LKCMedicine-_R00025241-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate, Artificial Intelligence/Neuroscience [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are seeking Research Assistant/Associate to join the Neuroscience and AI Research (Nair) group, led by Nanyang Assistant Professor Aditya Nair, to study how machine learning models and neural circuits in the brain process states of emotion. The Nair group combines cutting-edge experimental tools with the development of new AI methods to understand and model complex brain data. Key Responsibilities: Analyze high-dimensional brain data, document results and carry out an independent research project. Develop and apply new machine learning and computer vision methods such as large-language models and vision-language models for high-throughput analysis of video data. Apply data-driven dynamical system modeling tools using specialized software packages to elucidate neural computations involved in emotion. Assist in maintaining specialized software repositories created by the lab. Prepare and contribute to grant applications and conference presentations. The candidate is also expected to write and draft research publications in top neuroscience and AI journals.  Attend a weekly lab meeting and journal club and present data and/or papers as necessary. Key Competencies and Requirements: Bachelor’s degree (for Research Assistant) and Master’s degree (for Research Associate) in computer science, neuroscience, computational biology, psychology, life science or relevant fields. We also invite candidates with interdisciplinary backgrounds to apply. Strong programming skills in Python and Matlab. Familiarity with analyzing large-scale neural data (such as imaging datasets, electrophysiology datasets or video data) is highly desirable. Proficiency in popular deep learning, computer vision and/or user-interface software frameworks (such as Pytorch, TensorFlow, OpenCV, PyQt, Gradio etc). The candidate is expected is have a strong numeric and analytical background. Competent in information visualization. A working knowledge of Adobe Illustrator is a strong advantage . Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary environment. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
