      "title": "Research Assistant (Environmental Microbiology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a motivated and capable Research Assistant to support research activities involving quantitative microbial analysis using multi-omics approaches. The successful candidate will contribute to laboratory and computational research workflows, including microbial cultivation, multi-omics data generation and analysis, and modelling of microbial systems. This role offers the opportunity to work within a multidisciplinary research environment and contribute to projects involving microbial ecology, systems biology, biotechnology, and related fields. Key Responsibilities Conduct quantitative microbial research using genomic, transcriptomic, metabolomic, fluxomic, and other multi-omics approaches. Perform laboratory-based molecular microbiology experiments, including microbial cultivation and sample preparation. Analyse and interpret complex biological datasets using computational and bioinformatics tools. Develop and apply metabolic, ecological, statistical, or related computational models to address research objectives. Support the operation, maintenance, and optimisation of microbial culture systems, including bioreactors and defined culture platforms where applicable. Prepare research reports, technical documentation, manuscripts, presentations, and other project-related materials. Collaborate effectively with researchers, technical staff, and external stakeholders across multidisciplinary teams. Maintain accurate experimental records and ensure compliance with laboratory safety and research governance requirements. Contribute to grant applications, project reporting, and dissemination of research findings where required. Qualifications and Requirements Bachelor's degree in Microbiology, Molecular Biology, Biotechnology, Bioengineering, Bioinformatics, Life Sciences, or a related discipline. Advanced qualifications such as a PhD are advantageous. Demonstrated experience in molecular microbiology and multi-omics research methodologies. Experience in the analysis of genomic, transcriptomic, metabolomic, fluxomic, or related biological datasets using laboratory and/or computational approaches. Knowledge of bioinformatics tools and workflows for amplicon sequencing, metagenomics, or related sequencing platforms. Experience with microbial culture systems; exposure to bioreactor operations or defined culture systems would be an advantage. Familiarity with metabolic, ecological, statistical, or related modelling approaches. Strong scientific writing, data interpretation, and communication skills. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within multidisciplinary research teams. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks and timelines effectively. Preferred Attributes Experience integrating multiple omics datasets for biological interpretation. Proficiency in scientific programming or data analysis tools commonly used in bioinformatics and computational biology. Experience contributing to scientific publications, technical reports, or research proposals. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Photonics-_R00025225": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum Photonics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a research fellow to carry out the research project and be responsible for administrative and logistical upkeep pertaining to laboratory operations. The project is for product design and engineering for quantum photonics. Experience in Quantum photonics is preferred. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research activities related to product design and engineering for quantum technologies. Apply optics and electronics design knowledge in the development and optimization of quantum technology and quantum photonics systems. Job Requirements: PhD in Electrical Engineering or Quantum Engineering. Familiarity with quantum technologies Good written and oral communication skills Highly motivated in multidisciplinary research Proven experience in product design, project leading and optics alignment. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--MOF---6th-_R00025206": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (MOF – 6th)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . Key Responsibilities: We are looking for a Research Fellow to advance MOF‑based electrochemical and CO2 removal research. Electrochemical process on interface phenomena MOF synthesis, testing under different conditions Simulation of scaled up process. Interface with machine learning group on database set up CO2 removal process Job Requirements: Candidates with strong background in Materials chemistry/Physical chemistry Experience with MOF synthesis, energy storage system or electrochemical system PhD in Chemistry/Materials Science/Physics Encourage initiating activities on MOF development, devising, and analytical process Experience in machine learning will be preferred Good oral and written communication skills Candidates with strong publication/patent records will be preferred We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Photocatalysis-_R00025197": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Photocatalysis)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research studied in an NTU lab . The role will focus on development of semiconductor nanostructures for photocatalytic reactions. Key Responsibilities: Participate in the conduct of research project with research team members to ensure completion of deliverables Maintenance of lab equipment and supplies that include procurement and liaison with suppliers Mentor junior PhD student and undergraduate students for their research studies Assist in grant writing and reports that consolidate research findings Job Requirements: PhD degree in engineering or science with first-author journal publications on solution-based synthesis of semiconductor nanostructures (Entry level candidates are welcome to apply) Proficiency in photocatalytic tests and operating gas chromatography equipment Good written and oral communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Administrative-Support--NTUitive-_R00025190": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Administrative Support [NTUitive]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) advances cohesive and collaborative relationships across various innovation drivers within the NTU community. It seeks to accelerate the University’s efforts in translating scientific discoveries, innovation and creative work into technological and social entrepreneurship activities that benefit industry and society. NTUitive - the University’s innovation and enterprise company - plays a pivotal role in translating research breakthroughs into solutions that benefit society. We support innovators, entrepreneurs and industry partners in translating promising ideas and deep tech into ventures and real-world solutions with commercial and societal impact. As a wholly-owned subsidiary of NTU and a key innovation driver under NTU I&E, NTUitive oversees the cultivation of startups and spin-offs, as well as the related investments. The Assistant Manager, Administrative Support provides executive, operational and programme management support to the Associate Vice President (Technology Transfer) and the NTU I&E Technology Transfer team. The role is responsible for ensuring the effective coordination of executive engagements, stakeholder interactions, office operations and programme activities, while maintaining high standards of governance, compliance and service delivery. Working closely with internal and external stakeholders, he/she supports the administration and implementation of strategic programmes, and contributes to process optimisation, digitalisation and continuous improvement initiatives. Through effective coordination, stakeholder engagement and operational support, the role contributes to the smooth functioning of office operations and the successful planning and implementation of new programmes and initiatives in NTU I&E. Successful candidate can look forward to a rewarding career at NTUitive with ample opportunities for growth and development. Responsibilities: Executive and Stakeholder Support Manage the calendar, appointments, meetings and official engagements of the Associate Vice President (Technology Transfer). Coordinate meeting logistics, prepare agendas and meeting materials. Facilitate communication and correspondence on behalf of the AVP. Monitor and track follow-up actions arising from meetings and engagements. Provide administrative and coordination support for strategic initiatives, projects and activities led by the AVP. Serve as a key coordination point between the AVP and internal/external stakeholders. Coordinate stakeholder engagements, workshops and visits involving industry, government and academic partners, ensuring effective communication and follow-up of agreed actions. Operational Excellence, Governance and Transformation Oversee day-to-day office administration and operational support functions, including facilities, office resources and administrative records. Manage office resources, procurement, IT assets and inventory records. Liaise with corporate departments and vendors on facilities, IT and operational matters. Review operational workflows and administrative procedures, identify opportunities for process optimisation and digitalisation, and support the implementation of improvement initiatives. Ensure proper maintenance of administrative records and assets in compliance with organisational policies, audit requirements and data governance standards. Support internal audits, compliance reviews and reporting exercises by coordinating documentation, records and follow-up actions. Participate in departmental transformation initiatives, including the implementation and adoption of digital systems, automation solutions and process enhancement projects. Programme Administration and Management Support Coordinate end-to-end programme administration, including application processing, proposal evaluation, award administration and related stakeholder communications. Monitor programme milestones, progress reporting, compliance requirements and administrative deliverables to support effective programme implementation. Process fund disbursements in accordance with approved guidelines, financial controls and organisational policies. Maintain complete, accurate and up-to-date programme and financial records in accordance with organisational, funding and audit requirements. Prepare programme statistics, management reports, dashboards and performance updates to support programme monitoring and decision-making. Support programme governance and compliance activities, including record management, audit preparation, risk monitoring and adherence to organisational and funding requirements. Coordinate and manage programme-related events, briefing sessions, outreach activities, workshops and stakeholder engagement initiatives to support programme objectives and outreach efforts. Serve as a key contact point and engage internal and external stakeholders, including applicants, award recipients, reviewers and partners, to facilitate programme delivery, address operational issues and ensure a positive stakeholder experience. Support the review and enhancement of programme administration processes, including the implementation of new systems, process automation initiatives and digital solutions to improve operational efficiency, service quality and user experience. Any other ad-hoc initiatives and projects undertaken by the Office. Requirements: Bachelor's Degree from a recognised university. Good understanding of office administration, records management, procurement and operational support processes. Knowledge of project coordination, process improvement and change management principles. Knowledge of higher education, research, innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystems will be an advantage. Minimum 4-6 years of relevant working experience in administration, programme administration, executive support, operations management or a related function. Experience supporting senior management and coordinating meetings, events and stakeholder engagements will be an advantage. Experience managing administrative processes, records and reporting requirements. Experience coordinating programmes, projects or initiatives involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. Strong organisational and coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines concurrently. Good analytical skills and proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, for data management, tracking and reporting. Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare correspondence, reports and meeting materials. Strong interpersonal and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at different organisational levels. Ability to exercise sound judgement in prioritising requests, managing competing demands and handling confidential information appropriately. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a team environment. Project coordination skills, including the ability to manage timelines, monitor deliverables and coordinate stakeholders effectively. Meticulous, organised and detail-oriented, with a strong commitment to accuracy and quality. Proactive, resourceful and responsive in addressing issues and following through on tasks. Adaptable and able to work effectively in a dynamic environment with evolving priorities and requirements. Professional and tactful in handling sensitive information and interactions with senior stakeholders. Positive team player with a collaborative mindset and willingness to support departmental initiatives beyond assigned responsibilities. Demonstrates initiative and ownership in driving tasks to completion with minimal supervision. Resilient and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities and processes may evolve over time. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTUitive"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Communication-Media-Studies-Computational-Social-Science-Information-Science-Computer-Science-Data-Science-_R00025189-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Communication/Media Studies/Computational Social Science/Information Science/Computer Science/Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI), together with the Earth Observatory of Singapore, is looking for a Research Fellow to make an important contribution to the research project: “Climate Transformation Program (CTP): Cross Cutting Theme 1 – Sustainable Societies” funded by the MOE Tier 3C Grant. CTP aims to develop, inspire, and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just, and sustainable Southeast Asian societies. CTP will generate knowledge and innovation across disciplines including climate and Earth science, ecology, materials science, artificial intelligence, humanities, social sciences and the arts, finance, health, and engineering. It will also translate state-of-the-art scientific results into real world solutions for Singapore, and it will transfer these solutions to Southeast Asia (SEA) and beyond. As part of this programme, “Cross-cutting theme 1: Sustainable Societies”, this theme will leverage climate research in communication, public opinion and psychology, and artistic impressions to shape public attitudes and behaviours towards climate change issues. The Research Fellow will work directly with the PI of the Sustainable Societies theme, Professor Shirley Ho, based in the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information at NTU. Key Responsibilities: The successful candidate will contribute to an interdisciplinary research program by: Conducting literature reviews and supporting manuscript development Collecting and analysing online public discourse data using sentiment and content analysis methods Applying statistical and computational techniques to analyse large-scale textual datasets Contributing to peer-reviewed journal articles and conference presentations Preparing progress reports and final research outputs Supporting dissemination of findings to academic and public audiences Assisting with general project coordination and administrative tasks as required Job Requirements: We are seeking a highly motivated researcher with: PhD in Communication, Media Studies, Computational Social Science, Information Science, Computer Science, Data Science, or a related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in sentiment analysis, opinion mining, or computational analysis of media and public discourse. Candidates should be able to connect computational analysis with communication theories and research questions. Strong quantitative research skills and proficiency in Python or R. Experience with large-scale textual data, natural language processing, machine learning, transformer-based models, or large language models is required. Additional strengths that would be beneficial include: Experience with fine-tuning or prompting large language models for sentiment, emotion, stance, or framing analysis. Experience analysing large-scale textual data from sources such as social media, news, or online communities. Experience collecting data through APIs or web scraping. Experience preparing grant proposals and contributing to funded research projects. Knowledge of open-science practices, including reproducible workflows, preregistration, and research-data management. Ability to lead collaborative projects with third-party data companies, coordinate internal and external stakeholders, and manage project timelines, deliverables, and quality. Prior experience in project management or industry–academia collaboration is preferred. A strong publication record or demonstrated potential to publish in reputable communication, computational social science, or interdisciplinary venues. Candidates should be able to independently develop research questions, conduct analysis, prepare manuscripts, and deliver project milestones. Strong academic writing and presentation skills, with the ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary team. Experience supervising research assistants, contributing to grant proposals, or managing research projects is advantageous. Why Join Us This position offers the opportunity to: Contribute to an interdisciplinary research programme addressing climate change and sustainable societies in Southeast Asia. Collaborate with researchers from diverse disciplines across NTU and partner institutions. Conduct research with the potential to inform public understanding and societal responses to climate change. Develop a strong research profile through publications, conference presentations, and collaborative projects. Interested applicants are invited to submit a cover letter, full CV and names and contact details of three referees in one document. Enquiries about this position can be made to TSYHo@ntu.edu.sg. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Financial-Planning---Analysis_R00024755": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Financial Planning & Analysis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Finance (OFIN) supports the University in planning and executing sound financial management in fulfillment of the University’s mission; implementing and maintaining a robust financial framework that supports management in effective decision-making; providing fiscal stewardship of University’s resources; and ensuring financial governance and compliance with regulatory requirements. The Deputy Director will report to the Director, FP&A. Responsibilities Lead a team of finance professionals to coordinate and consolidate the University‑wide budget, including departmental budgets managed through department cluster leads and finance partners. Develop deep functional expertise and leadership capabilities amongst finance leads/partners so that they can support the operational finance strategy and performance standards for their respective areas of responsibility. Has overall accountability for translating the University and Finance function’s long‑term objectives into coherent, actionable financial plans across departments, in partnership with finance leads and partners. Plan and allocate resources to areas where they will most effectively contribute to long term goals. Possess deep understanding of various internal operational processes related to finance within the University, benchmark best practices amongst higher educational institutions and drive continuous improvements. Support capital / strategic initiatives with financial modelling. The candidate will collaborate with other university corporate functions (including the Office of Human Resources to analyse manpower planning outcomes) and provide financial insights that support the University’s objectives. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Finance or Accountancy with minimum 15 years of relevant experience in financial planning & analysis and budgeting CA is a pre-requisite Relevant work experience in a supervisory position. Solid knowledge and experience in Audit Administration Strong senior stakeholder management skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strong analytical and problem solving abilities Experience working in SAP HANA and Workday environments, including reporting or diagnostics, is advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-IT-Security-Analyst--Information-Security-Department---NIE-_R00024901": {
      "title": "Senior IT Security Analyst (Information Security Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable candidates to apply for the position of Senior IT Security Analyst within the Division of Academic Computing & Information Services (ACIS). This is a 3-year contract position. Key Responsibilities   Incident Response Leadership : Oversee the entire Incident Response lifecycle from detection to resolution. Lead investigations of IT security incidents and ensure thorough root cause analysis and remediation. Develop and maintain Incident Response playbooks and procedures. Coordinate with internal, external stakeholders, and vendors during incidents. Conduct post-incident reviews and report findings to management. Manage and coordinate incident response efforts across hybrid IT environments, including on-premises and cloud systems. Monitoring and Detection Develop and implement advanced threat detection and monitoring strategies. Utilize SIEM, EDR, and other security tools for timely incident detection. Perform threat hunting and proactive security assessments. Collaborate with IT teams to deploy and optimize security solutions. Threat Statistics and Reporting Analyze and compile statistics on threats relevant to the Institute. Prepare and present detailed reports on threat statistics to stakeholders. Use data visualization tools to communicate threat trends and insights. Innovation and Continuous Improvement Evaluate and integrate new technologies to enhance security operations. Foster a culture of continuous improvement within the team. Encourage continuous learning and professional development. Security Project Management Support and coordinate cybersecurity projects and initiatives across the Institute. Work with internal stakeholders and vendors to track project deliverables, timelines, risks, and action items. Assist in the implementation, enhancement, and operationalization of security technologies and solutions. Facilitate meetings, prepare project updates, and maintain documentation related to cybersecurity initiatives. Support process improvement and automation initiatives within the Security Operations function. Requirements A University degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or a related field. Professional Certification(s) in incident handling and security analysis preferred. GCIH or its equivalent is preferred. Minimum of 4 years of progressive experience in IT security, with a focus on Incident Response. Minimum of 4 years of experience in a Security Operations Center (SOC), with proven leadership capabilities. Intermediate knowledge of security operations, incident analysis, incident handling, threat hunting, vulnerability management/testing, system patching, log analysis, intrusion detection, firewall administration, and network security assessment tools. Proficiency in Security Information and Event Management (SIEM), Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR), traffic and packet analysis, digital forensics, cloud security, and host-based intrusion detection systems. Experience in Blue/Purple teaming, firewall administration, Intrusion Prevention Systems (IPS), Web Application Firewalls (WAF), virtualization, and cloud technologies. Knowledge and experience in Linux, Windows, and Database technologies preferred. Strong knowledge of industry standards and information security policy frameworks. Ability to conduct gap analysis, improve security monitoring and alerting processes, and identify opportunities for operational improvement. Ability to evaluate Information Security threats, provide response guidance, and ensure appropriate controls and mitigation measures are implemented. Excellent leadership, communication, stakeholder management, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively under pressure and coordinate with stakeholders at all levels, including University administration. Demonstrated ability to manage security initiatives/projects, coordinate with vendors and stakeholders, and document business requirements. Passionate about cybersecurity, continuous learning, and emerging technologies. Open-minded and adaptable towards adopting new technologies, including Artificial Intelligence (AI), Agentic AI, and security automation. Demonstrates curiosity, innovation, and a forward-thinking mindset in enhancing security operations capabilities. Strong interest in contributing towards the development of an AI-enabled and automation-driven SOC environment. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 24 July 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Science-_R00025148": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. The College of Computing & Data Science (CCDS) invites applications for the position of Research Associate.   The Research Associate (RA) will play a key role in advancing the research mission of NTU by supporting cutting-edge projects in computer vision, machine learning, physical AI, and spatial AI. The RA will contribute to the development of innovative algorithms, data preparation pipelines, and experimental evaluations that are central to the Physical Vision Group’s long-term goal of building general-purpose physical simulators and spatial intelligent systems.    Reporting to the Principal Investigator, the RA will help ensure a healthy and vibrant research environment within the Physical Vision Group (PVG, https://physicalvision.github.io/  ). This will involve closely collaborating with faculty, postdoctoral researchers, and PhD students, bridging foundational research with real-world applications in robotics, VR/AR, and embodied AI. Key Responsibilities: Conduct individual research within the designed project: process data, develop research methods, build and evaluate computer vision and machine learning algorithms empirically. Author research articles at an international level for peer-reviewed conferences. Engineer software based on the research outcomes of the project and distribute this on the group’s web. Manage own academic research and administrative activities. Adapt existing and develop new scientific techniques and experimental protocols. Test hypotheses and analyse scientific data from a variety of sources. Contribute ideas for new research projects. Develop ideas for generating research income, and present detailed research proposals to senior researchers. Any other duties appropriate with the role. Job Requirements: Hold a relevant Master degree in Computer Science. Sufficient theoretical and practical knowledge of methodologies such as deep and statistical learning. Excellent communication skills, including the ability to write for publication, present research proposals and results, and present the research output at meetings. Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Strong publication record at the principal international computer vision and machine learning conferences will be better. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--AI-for-Medicine--LKCMedicine-_R00025063": {
      "title": "Research Associate, AI for Medicine [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The MVAIT Lab at LKCMed seeks to hire a Research Associate (RA) who will play a role in pioneering research on medical image processing, medical visual technology and LLM, and the interface of AI algorithms with surgical robotics. The RA will design and implement cutting-edge algorithms and also be actively involved in the development AI tools tailored for different medical domains. These are efforts to bridge the gap between advanced computational framework and practical medical use cases. The tools and framework developed by the RA will be meticulously adapted to meet the needs of clinicians, radiologists, and biologists, assisting them in their daily tasks and pioneering research. Ultimately, this position plays a pivotal role in LKCMed's overarching mission to leverage technology to enhance healthcare outcomes and propel the institution to the forefront of medical advancements. Key Responsibilities: Design and implement AI algorithm models to analyze multimodal medical datasets (including MRI, CT, X-ray, OCT, and ultrasound images) for high-precision medical organ segmentation, 3D modeling research, and intelligent diagnosis. Explore and develop the application of large-scale pre-trained models in medical scenarios, including but not limited to intelligent consultation systems based on large language models and disease management systems utilizing multi-modal large model technologies. Develop, test, and optimize AI software systems for various medical tasks, ensuring their applicability and accuracy in real-world medical environments. Utilize data storage technologies to manage multimodal medical data securely and efficiently, ensuring data privacy while providing high storage capacity to accelerate AI model training and inference. Enhance the visualization capabilities of AI software system outputs using VR/AR equipment and 3D visualization technologies, aiding clinical observations and assisting interns in training and rapid learning. Collaborate with the team to systematically complete research and development tasks, assisting in the development of AI-assisted robotic solutions for surgical procedures, including pre-operative planning and intra-operative guidance. Ensure that all research activities adhere to ethical guidelines and patient data privacy regulations. Stay updated on the latest advancements in medical imaging, image processing, robotics, and large language models, ensuring that the research remains at the forefront of the field. Collaborate with external researchers and interdisciplinary teams (including medical professionals, AI experts, and research professors) to ensure the necessity, professionalism, rationality, and practicality of the research. Write research proposals, grant applications, and contribute to the team's strategic research direction. Mentor and train junior researchers, students, and interns, ensuring they possess the necessary skills and knowledge to contribute effectively to the research. Competencies and Qualification Requirements: Master degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field from a prestigious institution. Extensive experience in deep learning, AI, computer vision, 3D reconstruction algorithms, and large-scale Pre-trained Models. A solid research foundation and engineering experience in the AI medical field, proficient in programming languages and frameworks such as Python, C++, Pytorch, Tensorflow, Opencv, and COLMAP. Experience in software system engineering, capable of designing a well-structured system architecture to support the implementation of AI medical software. Proficiency in SQL and other data storage technologies, able to apply them flexibly and effectively in the AI medical field, ensuring data storage performance and security. Experience analyzing and interpreting medical imaging datasets, particularly ophthalmic imaging data, with an understanding of the nuances and peculiarities of such datasets. A deep understanding of ethical considerations, patient data privacy regulations, and other compliance-related aspects of medical research. Ability to collaborate with interdisciplinary teams, including medical professionals, AI experts, and research professors. Proactive and self-driven, capable of developing and managing multiple tasks and projects simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English; proficiency in additional languages is a plus. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Civil-Engineering-_R00025158": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Civil Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU, CEE is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. The job is aimed at developing smart connectors for modular floating breakwaters. Key Responsibilities: Design and fabricate self-sensing concrete. Lab test and analysis of self-sensing concrete. Optimize and evaluate the performance for field trials. Publish several papers in top journals. Write proposals for further development. Mentor students. Job Requirements: PhD degree in civil engineering or related field At least 1 year of relevant experience in structural materials and signal processing. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in ABAQUS , and lab test skill Ability to work independently and develop solutions under strict timelines We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Spinal-Cord-Injury-Experiments-for--Neural-Tissue-Engineering-Research-_R00023404": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Spinal Cord Injury Experiments for  Neural Tissue Engineering Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Research Fellow/ Post-doctoral position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Sing Yian CHEW (Nanyang Technological University, NTU) and Prof. Shawn JE (Duke-NUS) in Singapore, to a highly motivated candidate who has a passion for in vivo Spinal Cord Injury cell/scaffold implantation treatment and neural tissue engineering research.   The focus of this project is to evaluate cell transplantation and tissue engineered scaffolds for in vivo neural tissue regeneration. We are seeking an individual who is experienced in spinal cord injury microsurgery with rats and interested in conducting animal implantation studies, as well as carrying out behavioral tests; and characterizing/evaluating scaffold-cell/tissue interactions through immunofluorescent and histochemical staining and imaging.   The candidate will be jointly supervised by Prof. Sing Yian CHEW and Prof. Shawn JE. This position offers a unique opportunity to apply in vivo experimentation skills to neural tissue engineering, through strong collaborative efforts with scientists and engineers across different local and overseas institutions (SMART/MIT, University of Osaka, Nagoya University, NUS).   Key Responsibilities:    The candidate will be given opportunities and is expected to design and execute experiments independently. He/she is also expected to interpret experimental results, and author papers in high-quality journals in areas that are related to the research. The candidate should demonstrate excellent communication skills and should have a strong passion and commitment to science. He/she will also work closely with the Principal Investigators to help supervise and train students and junior lab members and to ensure smooth functioning of an active research program. The candidate will have the opportunity to explore his/her own interests across functions. Job Requirements: Ph.D. level scientist proficient in animal experiments, particularly in spinal cord injury microsurgery and neural tissue engineering. Expertise in rodent models, immunofluorescent and histochemical staining of tissues, evaluation of tissue response/interactions using fluorescent microscopy (confocal) imaging. Expertise in western blotting, quantitative RT-PCR is a plus. Strong ability to communicate effectively orally and in written form, and experienced in writing manuscripts. Strong ability to perform self-directed work. Strong organizational skills and proactive personality with outstanding motivation, creativity, critical and analytical thinking skills, strong scientific commitment and ability to work as a team. Starting salaries will depend on candidate’s qualification and experience. Candidates are expected to start March 2026. Review of applicants will continue until positions are filled. Applicants should submit a cover letter indicating their area of interest and how they intend to participate and contribute to the research, complete curriculum vitae and addresses of three references in a single PDF document to Dr. Sing Yian CHEW ( sychew@ntu.edu.sg ) and Prof. Shawn Je ( shawn.je@duke-nus.edu.sg ).   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Industry_R00025123": {
      "title": "Director, Industry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Director (Industry) plays a pivotal role in driving strategic partnerships with industry, public agencies and international universities / institutions to enhance research, innovation, and commercialization efforts. This role oversees engagement initiatives, secures industry funding and aligns academic expertise with industry needs to enhance the university’s impact and reputation. Responsibilities Strategic Planning and Partnership Development Develop and implement a comprehensive strategic plan to identify opportunities for cultivating and building a robust pipeline of partnerships with key industry stakeholders. Formulate and execute strategies to strengthen and expand partnerships with industry leaders, advancing the university’s strategic objectives. Identify and capitalize on university-wide opportunities to collaborate with industry leaders, ensuring alignment with institutional goals. Foster strong partnerships with industry sectors and public agencies, promoting engagement across a dynamic cross-industry ecosystem. Curriculum Innovation and Industry Integration Design strategies to integrate academic curricula with global and industry trends, ensuring relevance and future-readiness of educational programs. Promote greater involvement of industry professionals in curriculum design, teaching, and mentorship programs to bridge the gap between academia and the workforce. Encourage the integration of interdisciplinary and experiential learning opportunities, such as internships, industry-led projects, and hands-on training. Leadership and Oversight Lead and oversee key university-industry partnership initiatives at the university level, ensuring alignment with institutional goals and priorities. Champion innovative university-industry initiatives in research and education, enhancing the university’s competitive edge in global and regional contexts. Work closely with stakeholders across colleges, schools, and research centers to facilitate cross-functional synergies and streamline initiatives for greater impact. Governance and Performance Monitoring Oversee central governance and data management processes to ensure alignment with institutional objectives, track progress, and measure performance effectively. Establish policies for research funding, publication standards, and collaborations with industry to support high-impact initiatives and maintain compliance with global standards. Promote success stories of university-industry collaborations to attract additional partnerships and funding opportunities. Stakeholder Engagement and Communication Organize industry-academia conferences, networking events, and expos to showcase collaborative achievements and strengthen ties with industry stakeholders. Address resistance to change by engaging stakeholders in co-creation processes and maintaining transparent communication throughout all initiatives. Build trust and buy-in among faculty, staff, and external partners through clear and consistent messaging. Capacity Building and Change Management Train faculty and staff to adapt to new collaboration models and evolving industry expectations, fostering a culture of continuous improvement and adaptability. Promote professional development opportunities to equip academic and administrative teams with the skills needed to sustain and grow partnerships. Requirements Minimum Bachelor’s degree with strong administration management experience in a Research & Development environment. Significant experience in a leadership role involving university-industry collaborations, strategic planning or organization development.  Proven track record of successfully managing and expanding large-scale partnerships and initiatives. Proven leadership experience in managing strategic partnerships and collaborations, preferably within an academic or industry setting. Strong understanding of global and industry trends in education, research, and technology. Exceptional communication, negotiation and stakeholder engagement skills. Ability to drive cross-functional initiatives and manage complex projects with multiple stakeholders. Expertise in governance, data management and performance measurement. A visionary mindset with a demonstrated ability to innovate and lead change effectively. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Materials-Science---Engineering-Materials-Science-Polymer-Chemistry-Chemical-Engineering-Nanotechnology-Physics-Electrochemistry-_R00025126": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Materials Science & Engineering/Materials Science/Polymer Chemistry/Chemical Engineering/Nanotechnology/Physics/Electrochemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. ERI@N has multiple Interdisciplinary Research Programmes which focus on translational Research, Development & Deployment which focus on specific area of the energy value chain, and a number of Living labs and Testbeds which facilitate large scale technology deployment enabling validation and demonstration of real-world applications. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/erian Key job purpose : The successful candidate will support the characterisation and evaluation of carbonaceous materials for lithium-ion and next-generation battery applications. The role will involve assisting in materials analysis, electrochemical testing, and data collection to support ongoing research and development activities related to battery materials and electrode performance. The candidate will work closely with the research team to study the structure, morphology, and electrochemical behaviour of carbon materials such as graphite, hard carbon, and conductive additives used in battery systems Key Responsibilities: The candidate’s scope of work will include the following: Assist in the characterisation of carbonaceous materials (e.g., graphite, hard carbon, soft carbon, graphene, carbon nanotubes) used in lithium-ion batteries. Support routine material characterisation and analysis using techniques such as: a. X-ray diffraction (XRD) b. Raman spectroscopy c. BET surface area analysis d. Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) e. Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) Assist with battery electrode preparation and coin cell assembly. Conduct basic electrochemical testing, including: a. Cyclic voltammetry (CV) b. Galvanostatic charge–discharge testing c. Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) Collect, organise, and maintain experimental data and laboratory records. Prepare summaries, technical slides, and reports for internal discussions. Support general laboratory operations, equipment maintenance, and safety procedures. Work collaboratively with team members on battery materials research projects Job Requirements: Possess a Bachelor’s Degree in Materials Science & Engineering. in Materials Science, Polymer Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, or a related discipline (e.g., Nanotechnology, Physics, or Electrochemistry). Basic knowledge in the characterisation of carbonaceous materials or battery electrode materials. Hands-on experience will be advantageous. Basic or prior knowledge in solid-state characterisation techniques, particularly Raman spectroscopy, XRD, SEM/TEM, and BET surface analysis. Experience with Li-ion battery fabrication and electrochemical testing (e.g., coin cells, pouch cells, or prototype assemblies) is strongly preferred. Familiarity with surface functionalisation, defect engineering, and doping strategies for carbon materials is an advantage. Demonstrated ability to support the team and contribute creatively to multidisciplinary R&D projects. Evidence of scientific contribution in relevant research areas is strongly preferred (FYP, URECA). Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to support, prepare technical reports and presentations effectively. A collaborative team player with strong interpersonal skills and a proactive, willingness to learn mindset. Ability to work under pressure, manage multiple tasks, and meet tight project deadlines. Demonstrated sense of responsibility, attention to detail, and commitment to high-quality work We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Physical-Sciences-Engineering-_R00025119": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Physical Sciences/Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. Join the laboratory of Prof Lew Wen Siang at SPMS. We are seeking a Research Fellow to contribute to a project focused on the Development of Advanced MRAM Technology for Artificial Intelligence Memory and Smart Sensing .   Key Responsibilities: Design and develop high-performance MRAM devices for advanced computing memory applications. Manage project activities by liaising with international semiconductor companies, research institutes, and foundry partners. Lead the preparation of technical write-ups for quarterly industry press releases related to the joint development programme. Perform physical vapour deposition (PVD) of MRAM structures on 300 mm wafers using the ULVAC Entron system. Coordinate with circuit designers and semiconductor foundries on CMOS front-end wafer development and back-end-of-line integration processes. Conduct MRAM electrical transport measurements using probe stations and bonded memory chips, including device-level reliability testing such as endurance and retention measurements. Fabricate MRAM devices using advanced lithography techniques, including optical lithography and/or electron-beam lithography. Perform device processing using ICP-RIE and/or ion milling techniques. Analyse structural, electrical, and materials characterisation results, including scanning electron microscopy, X-ray diffraction, transmission electron microscopy, and related techniques. Job Requirements: PhD degree in a relevant field of physical sciences or engineering. At least 6 years of relevant experience in a similar role or technical discipline, including PhD research experience in non-volatile memory or a closely related area. Strong experience in semiconductor wafer-level device development. Proficiency in semiconductor processing techniques, particularly those relevant to advanced memory device fabrication. Good programming skills; experience in device modelling or simulation would be an advantage. Strong analytical and data visualisation skills, with the ability to interpret and present complex technical results clearly. Ability to work independently, develop practical solutions under tight timelines, and maintain a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent organisational and time management skills. Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to prepare project reports and deliver technical presentations to academic and industry stakeholders. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Postgraduate---Continuing-Education-Programmes--LKCMedicine-_R00025117": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Postgraduate & Continuing Education Programmes [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is seeking a proactive and meticulous Senior Assistant Manager to join the Graduate Programmes team. The successful candidate will be responsible for the end-to-end management of Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes and will oversee all finance-related operations for the CET portfolio. This pivotal role requires strong organisational skills, financial acumen, and the ability to manage multiple complex projects in a fast-paced environment. The Senior Assistant Manager will work closely with faculty, internal stakeholders (e.g., Finance, Legal), and external partners to ensure the successful delivery and financial sustainability of programmes targeted at healthcare professionals. Responsibilities: CET Programme Management & Operations Oversee the end-to-end operational planning and execution of CET programmes, from setup and scheduling to final delivery and feedback collection. Manage the full learner lifecycle, including admissions processing, enrolment, matriculation, learner communications, and post-programme support. Serve as the primary point of contact for CET learners, providing high-quality support and managing all enquiries. Collaborate with faculty, adjuncts, and internal departments to ensure smooth programme delivery. Provide administrative support to Course Directors and assist with programme-related tasks to ensure smooth and efficient operations. Manage all programme logistics, including scheduling, venue/platform booking, and the preparation and distribution of course materials. Continuously review and improve administrative processes to enhance programme efficiency, scalability, and the overall learner experience. Ensure all programmes are compliant with university policies and external requirements. CET Financial Management & Analysis Lead the annual CET budgeting cycle, working with programme leads to develop realistic financial targets. Develop, manage, and monitor individual programme budgets, ensuring alignment with the School's strategic goals and financial targets. Monitor revenue and expenditures closely; conduct regular variance analysis and financial reconciliations for the entire CET portfolio. Develop and maintain financial dashboards and reports to provide management with real-time visibility into programme performance, profitability, and key financial metrics. Prepare and present accurate and timely financial reports, summaries, and insights to senior management to support strategic decision-making. Manage procurement, invoicing, and billing processes, serving as the key liaison with the university's central finance office. Oversee the timely and accurate processing of payments for adjunct faculty, supervisors, and external vendors. Strategic, Contract & Stakeholder Management Manage the financial administration of external funding, including SSG grant claims, reporting, and supporting any related audit requirements. Support the Senior Assistant Director in developing business proposals and detailed financial models for new programme initiatives. Serve as the primary financial and administrative liaison for external partners (e.g., healthcare groups) regarding programme costs, billing, and financial reporting. Contribute to cross-functional projects related to education innovation, system implementation, and operational efficiency. Undertake other duties as required to support the School’s strategic goals. Requirements: A recognised degree in Business, Finance, Accounting or related discipline. Minimum 7–8 years of relevant working experience, preferably in programme management, finance, or administration. Strong financial acumen with hands-on experience in budgeting, financial reporting, and analysis. Excellent project management, organisational, and multitasking skills with a keen eye for detail. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (especially Excel for financial management) and PowerBI (for dashboard creation and management). A proactive and collaborative team player with strong interpersonal and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently, manage competing priorities, and meet tight deadlines. Prior experience in the education or healthcare sectors is highly desirable. Experience working in a higher education or training institute environment. Familiarity with SkillsFuture Singapore (SSG) funding schemes, claims processes, and compliance requirements. This is a 3 years contract appointment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Communication-Psychology-Public-Health-Behavioral-Sciences-Social-Science-_R00025096-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Communication/Psychology/Public Health/Behavioral Sciences/Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is looking for a Research Associate under the project Transforming Health Behaviour Insights through AI Driven Segmentation Models. The advertised position will be based in the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) and work under the supervision of Principal Investigator Prof Shirley S. Ho. Focusing on the social science components of the project, the Research Associate will work with the PI and research team to drive the operationalisation of a large-scale lifestyle and values survey aimed at a psychosocial segmentation of the population cohort across Singapore’s adult population. This research will identify attitudinal and socio-cultural variables that underpin trust, risk perception, and receptiveness to health messaging. The scope includes surveys on health behaviours, lifestyle practices, and psychological traits, forming the empirical basis for the AI-driven population segmentation models. The Research Associate is expected to support a range of research and administrative works within the project, from data collection, data analysis, to research presentation, manuscript preparation, and administrative tasks associated with the project and within the team. This job contributes to the overall mission and objectives of NTU by nurturing leaders through research, attracting the right talent that the University needs to sustain organizational growth, and retaining employees to perform and sustain a performance culture. Key Responsibilities: To engage in literature searches and manuscript preparation. To work with vendors to implement and oversee large-scale surveys (approx. 5,000 participants across Singapore). To conduct data cleaning, uploading, and management. To conduct statistical analysis of data. To coordinate with participants and stakeholders. To contribute to research publications, presentations, and progress reports. To engage in the dissemination of research findings with the support of and under the supervision of the Principal Investigator. To carry out administrative work and other research work associated with the project. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in communication, psychology, public health, behavioral sciences or a related social science discipline. Fundamentals of survey research and quantitative data analytical skills (e.g., SPSS, MPLUS, or R). Preference with be given to candidates who meet the following requirements: A team player in a project setting, also with ability to work independently. Experience in a multi-cultural team environment. Initiative and good interpersonal skills. Knowledge of quantitative methodology and (or) computational data analytics. Prior experience in communication, psychology, public health, or behavioural science research. Interested applicants are invited to submit a cover letter, full CV and names and contact details of three referees in one document. Enquiries about this position can be made to Prof. Shirley Ho at tsyho@ntu.edu.sg Kindly note that only short-listed candidates will be contacted for interview. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Resilient-Urbanisation---Natural-Ecosystems-_R00024870": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Resilient Urbanisation & Natural Ecosystems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. The School plays an integral role in spearheading tertiary education, advancing research innovations and providing professional services in a number of key disciplines in Civil and Environmental Engineering and Maritime Studies fields, with the objective of contributing to the technological and economic advancement of Singapore and beyond. The School’s mission in research is to achieve excellence by providing a conducive and intellectually stimulating environment to enable high quality work in strategic directions that are of significant impact to industry, science and technology. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/cee We are looking for a Research Engineer I to join a CITIES OF TOMORROW (CoT) R&D project for VERTICAL 5: CITY IN NATURE. The project plays a pivotal role in ensuring a resilient urban environment against climate change and contributes to NTU strategic research in Resilient Urbanisation & Natural Ecosystems that is aligned with Singapore’s national Research, Innovation and Enterprise 2025 plan. Key Responsibilities: Assist in field and laboratory tests Develop test protocols Compile test data and maintain database Conduct analysis and evaluation Assist to prepare budgets, reports and papers Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in relevant discipline or related field Ability to work both indoors and outdoors Good written and oral communication skills for report writing Knowledge of software like Python and 3D modelling software will be an advantage. Class 3 driving license (Singapore) will be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Clinical-Research-Officer--Operations---LKCMedicine-_R00025081-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Operations) [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is looking for a Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Operations) who is self-motivated, proactive in problem solving and a strong team player. The candidate will enjoy staff benefits and be part of the Health for Life in Singapore (HELIOS) Study team, a flagship Singapore population health study jointly conducted by LKCMedicine, National Healthcare Group and Imperial College of London. We aim to profile the health and behavior of up to 100,000 people from the general Singapore population over the next few years. We are conducting (1) surveys on health, lifestyle and dietary habits, (2) physical and functional measurements (e.g. anthropometry, hand grip strength, treadmill walking test, spirometry, ECG, retinal imaging, arterial stiffness and skin physiology assessments and (3) biomarkers for chronic diseases.  The candidate will play a key role mainly in, but not limited to, the following roles: Maintain clear and professional communication with study participants. Able to guide participants through the study, ensuring they complete all required assessments. Administer questionnaires and perform sample and physiological data collection accurately and efficiently. Eager to develop skills and gain exposure to all aspects of study processes and tasks. Ensures minimal disruption to study operations by troubleshooting and addressing equipment failures promptly. Monitor consumables and study supplies, flagging needs for replenishment. Ensure strict adherence to study protocols, including familiarity with the Code Blue Response SOP. Adhere to Good Clinical Practice standards and HBRA requirements throughout the conduct of the study. Assist and work well with the Team Leads and colleagues. Key Competencies and Requirements: Bachelor degree in Allied Health Sciences / Biomedical Sciences or other related fields. Diploma holders with relevant experience may also apply. Ability to work independently with high levels of motivation. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. A team player, able to work well in a team to deliver good research participant care. Must pay attention to detail. Fluent in spoken and written English. Fluent in Tamil, Malay, Chinese or dialects would be of advantage. Phlebotomy skills is an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Clinical-Research-Officer--Recruitment---LKCMedicine-_R00025077-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Recruitment) [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is looking for a Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Recruitment ) who is self-motivated, proactive in problem solving and a strong team player. The candidate will enjoy staff benefits and be part of the Health for Life in Singapore (HELIOS) Study team, a flagship Singapore population health study jointly conducted by LKCMedicine, National Healthcare Group and Imperial College of London. We aim to profile the health and behavior of up to 100,000 people from the general Singapore population over the next few years. We are conducting (1) surveys on health, lifestyle and dietary habits, (2) physical and functional measurements (e.g. anthropometry, hand grip strength, treadmill walking test, spirometry, ECG, retinal imaging, arterial stiffness and skin physiology assessments and (3) biomarkers for chronic diseases.  The candidate will play a key role mainly in, but not limited to, the following roles: Maintain clear and professional communication with study participants. Screen volunteers for their eligibility to participate in the study. Schedule and send reminders to participants for research session. Maintain the study’s recruitment database. Manage appointment booking system and participant registration properly. Provide weekly recruitment reports to the study investigators. Maintains the confidentiality of personal information acquired pertaining to the study participants. Implement strategies to improve participant recruitment. Preparing and distributing outreach materials. Lead the social media strategy and provide continuous updates on the study progress via social media, as well as to other media channels. Key Competencies and Requirements: Diploma / basic degree in business management and marketing, communication or social sciences. Ability to work independently with high levels of motivation. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Able to work well in a team to deliver good research participant care. Must pay attention to detail. Fluent in spoken and written English. Fluent in Tamil, Malay, Chinese or dialects would be of advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoctoral-Fellow--Chinese-Political-Thought-_R00025046": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow (Chinese Political Thought)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences at NTU Singapore is part of the College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS), which promotes interdisciplinary research and teaching across the full range of social science disciplines. Ranked among the world's top universities, NTU combines rigorous scholarship with an orientation toward addressing major societal challenges. The Postdoctoral Fellow will join the research project 1980: The Global Electoral Moment — China and Beyond , hosted at the Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme (PPGA) and led by Nanyang Assistant Professor Simon Sihang Luo. The project examines the lived experience of electoral founding moments in China and beyond, with attention to the political sentiments, institutional visions, and ideological contests they generated. The Fellow will conduct original archival and textual research on modern and contemporary Chinese political thought, develop an independent research agenda within the project's broader themes, and contribute to collaborative publications and working papers. The role also involves participation in project-related academic events and the broader intellectual life of the PPGA. Key Responsibilities Conduct original archival and textual research on modern and contemporary Chinese political thought, with particular attention to Chinese-language primary sources Develop and advance an independent research agenda aligned with the project's themes of electoral politics, institutional imagination, and intellectual history Contribute to collaborative research outputs, including peer-reviewed publications, working papers, and project reports Assist in the organisation of project-related academic events, including workshops, conferences, and invited speaker series Participate actively in the intellectual life of the Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme (PPGA) at NTU Support grant-related administrative tasks and research documentation as required Job Requirements PhD in Political Theory, Intellectual History, or a relevant field, with a focus on Chinese political thought Strong research record commensurate with career stage Native or full professional proficiency in Chinese - essential for data analysis and communication with stakeholders Demonstrated expertise in archival research, including facility with handwritten Chinese-language primary sources Ability to engage with comparative and global frameworks in the study of Chinese political institutions Interested applicants are to apply online with your CV and Cover Letter. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--LKCMedicine-_R00025064": {
      "title": "Research Fellow [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Pavesi Lab at Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine), Nanyang Technological University, develops advanced human microphysiological systems (MPS) and vascularized organoid platforms to model solid-tumour biology and therapy response. This position will support a project to develop and validate a colon cancer model, a kit-ready vascularized patient-derived organoid platform enabling intravascular dosing, real-time imaging, and downstream tissue retrieval for flow cytometry and single-cell/spatial profiling. The Lab works at the interface of bioengineering and translational cancer biology, with a focus on standardizing workflows (SOPs and QC criteria) to enable robust cross-sample comparisons and future scale-out. We are looking for a Research Fellow (Vascularized Organoids & Microphysiological Systems) to lead the day-to-day execution of a platform development project focused on patient-derived colorectal cancer organoid culture integrated with perfused microvascular networks. The role will focus on optimizing and standardizing vascularized organoid workflows, executing drug-response and combination-therapy assays, coordinating single-cell and spatial profiling readouts, and delivering validated SOPs/QC metrics and project milestones. Key Responsibilities: Establish, maintain, and quality-control patient-derived colorectal cancer organoids (PDOs), including expansion, organoid formation, and experimental scheduling. Set up and optimize vascularized organoid cultures. Execute intravascular dosing assays (e.g., 5-FU and rational combinations), including experimental design, controls, replicate planning, and documentation. Perform and/or coordinate readouts including live/dead imaging, confocal microscopy quantification, and sample retrieval for downstream analyses. Conduct tissue dissociation and immune/phenotypic profiling workflows as needed (e.g., flow cytometry, immunofluorescence marker validation, basic biomarker assays). Coordinate external core services and pipelines for single-cell RNA-seq (and, where applicable, spatial profiling), including sample preparation, submission logistics, and data organization.  Perform first-pass data handling and interpretation (with lab bioinformatics support), including QC tracking, summary plots, and integration of multimodal results into clear conclusions. Manage project operations: procurement of consumables, inventory tracking, coordination with collaborators/industry partners where relevant, and monthly progress reporting to the PI. Contribute to outputs: figures, internal reports, conference abstracts, manuscripts, and invention/patent-supporting documentation when appropriate. Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies: PhD in Bioengineering, Biomedical Engineering, Cell/Molecular Biology, Biotechnology, Immunology, Cancer Biology, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated hands-on experience with 3D culture systems, preferably patient-derived organoids/tumoroids and/or primary cell co-cultures. Experience with one or more of the following: microfluidics or organ-on-chip systems, perfusable/vascular co-culture models, ECM hydrogel handling (e.g., collagen/fibrin), confocal microscopy, image quantification, flow cytometry. Familiarity with sample preparation and coordination for single-cell workflows (e.g., viability handling, dissociation, logistics with sequencing cores); basic literacy in interpreting scRNA-seq outputs is an advantage. Strong organizational skills, meticulous record-keeping, and ability to execute under project timelines; ability to work independently while coordinating with a multidisciplinary team. Good written and oral communication skills for reporting progress, documenting SOPs/QC, and contributing to manuscripts/presentations. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Digital-Transformation--Academic-Services-_R00025065": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Digital Transformation (Academic Services)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Academic Services (OAS) plays a key role in advancing the University’s educational goals and supporting the provision and governance of academic learning in NTU. We provide the end-to-end academic services from the time of their matriculation to their graduation, creating positive impacts on the academic journey of all 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate (coursework and research) students during their study in NTU.  This position supports digital transformation and data governance in Academic Services through the management and coordination of key student academic systems, with primary responsibility for the academic core of the Student Management System (SMS), as well as other academic SaaS systems. The job holder coordinates system enhancements, supports stakeholder engagement and user adoption, and helps deliver system improvements aligned with operational needs and university priorities. Working closely with the Director and relevant stakeholders, the job holder serves as a key point of contact for requests relating to academic systems and data, supports compliance with data governance guidelines, and contributes to data stewardship and quality assurance efforts. The role also drives the development and adoption of data visualisation dashboards and reporting solutions, and supports selected cross-functional and system-related projects that strengthen academic services across Schools and Colleges, from matriculation to graduation. Key Responsibilities: 1.    Academic Services Systems Implementation and Management Manage and coordinate key student academic systems within Academic Services, with primary responsibility for the implementation and management of the Academic Core of the Student Management System (SMS), as well as other academic SaaS systems. Coordinate system changes, enhancement requests, and follow-up actions with Academic Services teams, IT, the Project Management Office, SMS teams, and other relevant stakeholders to ensure timely delivery aligned with functional requirements, governance standards, and project timelines. Support user adoption by gathering feedback, refining requirements, coordinating training and post-implementation support, and promoting continuous improvement in system use. 2.    Data Governance, Request Management and Stewardship Serve as the key point of contact for requests relating to academic systems and data within Academic Services, including the assessment of requests before escalation for approval. Evaluate and coordinate responses to complex requests, including those involving sensitive student information, by identifying relevant data from undergraduate and postgraduate systems, interpreting applicable business rules, and ensuring compliance with the University’s data governance guidelines, access controls, and privacy requirements. Support data stewardship and quality assurance efforts by working with data owners and relevant stakeholders to define standards, monitor data quality, resolve inconsistencies, and uphold the accuracy, consistency, and proper use of academic data. 3.    Data Analytics and Dashboard Development Drive the development and adoption of data visualisation dashboards and reporting solutions for Academic Services. Work with stakeholders to identify user needs, translate business requirements into dashboard functionality, refine usability, and support rollout and continuous enhancement. Where feasible, develop dashboards for Academic Services and support the effective use of data analytics to strengthen academic and administrative decision-making. 4.    Cross-functional Projects and Digital Transformation Support the Director in coordinating selected cross-functional and system-related projects that contribute to digital transformation and academic operations. Responsibilities include stakeholder coordination, progress tracking, issue follow-up, and support for the timely implementation of project outcomes across Academic Services, Schools, and Colleges. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Information Systems, Data Analytics, Education, or a related field. At least 3 to 5 years of relevant work experience in academic services, student academic systems, system implementation, or digital transformation, with experience in coordinating cross-functional projects and system enhancements. Proven experience in coordinating system change and enhancement requests for student academic systems, Student Management System (SMS) or equivalent enterprise systems. Experience in dashboard development, reporting, process automation, or digitisation initiatives is advantageous. Familiarity with tools such as Power BI, Power Automate, low-code platforms, or other data analytics tools will be an advantage. Strong understanding of academic operations and student lifecycle processes, with the ability to interpret business requirements, business rules, system flows, and academic data structures. Strong stakeholder management, interpersonal, and communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with internal teams, IT partners, data stakeholders, and end users, support user onboarding and training, and translate technical, operational, or policy requirements into clear and user-friendly guidance. Strong analytical and critical thinking abilities, with a detail-oriented mindset, sound judgement, and the ability to assess data- and system-related requests, including matters involving sensitive information, in accordance with governance and privacy requirements. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--In-Vivo-Neural-Tissue-Engineering-_R00023827": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (In Vivo Neural Tissue Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe invite applications for a  Research Fellow to join an interdisciplinary research team led by  Dr. Sing Yian Chew (NTU) . The successful candidate will contribute to an ongoing research program focused on  neural tissue engineering ,  in vivo spinal cord injury (SCI) models , and  regenerative biomaterials . Responsibilities: Plan and conduct in vivo experiments using rat SCI models Conduct microsurgical procedures, cell/scaffold implantation, and animal behavioral / functional evaluations Carry out analyses to understand mechanisms of action: e.g. tract tracing, immunofluorescent and histochemical staining and confocal imaging, RNA-seq. Data analysis, interpretation of experimental outcomes, and preparation of manuscripts for publication Supervise and train junior researchers and contribute to laboratory management Participate in multidisciplinary collaborations within and beyond NTU Requirements: Ph.D. and/or M.D. in Biomedical Engineering, Neuroscience, or a related discipline Published and demonstrated expertise in handling rodents as well as functional and behavioral assessments. Published expertise in animal surgery , preferably  SCI microsurgery in rodents Hands-on experience with tract tracing, tissue sectioning, immunofluorescence, histology, and confocal microscopy Experience with western blotting and qRT-PCR is advantageous Strong written and oral communication skills for research work Highly motivated, well-organized, and capable of independent work and teamwork We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Optics-and-Nanophotonics-_R00025060-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum Optics and Nanophotonics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee The role is for a research fellow to conduct experimental research in quantum optics, nanophotonics, and light-matter interaction at EEE/NTU. The researcher will study and control collective and single-emitter light-matter interactions in advanced photonic structures, contributing to fundamental quantum science and future quantum technologies. Key Responsibilities: Design, set up, conduct, and analyse experiments in quantum optics, nanophotonics, and light-matter interaction. Develop and operate single-photon spectroscopy, Hanbury Brown-Twiss (HBT), Hong-Ou-Mandel (HOM), and related optical spectroscopy measurements. Investigate collective quantum optical effects enabled by nanophotonic platforms, including superradiance, superfluorescence, and quantum imaging. Study strong light-matter interaction in the single-emitter regime and optical spectroscopy of nanoscale systems with embedded quantum emitters. Characterise photonic structures and quantum-emitter systems, maintain rigorous experimental records, and ensure safe laboratory practice. Collaborate with EEE/NTU researchers and project partners; contribute to publications, presentations, reports, and research proposals. Support mentoring and training of students and junior researchers in relevant experimental techniques. Requirements PhD in Physics, Applied Physics, Photonics, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Materials Science, or a related field. Strong experimental experience in quantum optics, single-photon spectroscopy, HBT, HOM, and optical spectroscopy of nanoscale quantum-emitter systems. Experience with nanophotonic platforms, quantum emitters, and light-matter interaction is desirable. Strong analytical, troubleshooting, documentation, and scientific communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary research environment. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Adjunct-Associate-Professor-in-Wine--Environment-and-Society_R00025047": {
      "title": "Adjunct Associate Professor in Wine, Environment and Society",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAsian School of the Environment Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Adjunct Associate Professor ASE, in collaboration with CoHASS, invites applications for an Adjunct Associate Professor position at NTU. The appointee will develop and deliver an innovative interdisciplinary undergraduate elective course using wine as an integrative case study to demonstrate the interconnectedness of Earth systems, agricultural and viticultural landscapes, human society, history, culture, and commerce. The course will draw on faculty expertise and students from across NTU's colleges, including CoS, CoHASS, and NBS. In addition to the undergraduate course, the appointee will contribute to executive education programmes and engagement activities that communicate our research to non-specialist audiences and external stakeholders. Key Responsibilities Design and deliver an interdisciplinary undergraduate elective course drawing on connections between environmental science, climate change, land use, cultural geography, economics, and society, using viticulture and the global wine industry as a sustained integrative case study. Develop curriculum and teaching materials that make ASE research — including work on climate variability, soil science, landscape change, and natural hazards — accessible and relevant to students from diverse academic backgrounds. Develop curriculum and teaching materials that draw on CoHASS disciplines — including cultural geography, history, anthropology, and the social study of food and consumption — to illuminate wine as a lens for understanding human societies and their relationship with the natural world. Contribute to executive education programmes addressing the intersection of environmental change, land use, culture and fine wine, with a focus on the Asia-Pacific region. Support engagement activities with external stakeholders, including prospective donors and industry partners, through curated events, masterclasses, and dinners that communicate ASE and CoHASS science in compelling and accessible formats. Collaborate with faculty across ASE, CoHASS, NBS, and other NTU schools to strengthen interdisciplinary educational programming in this topic and build cross-school academic relationships. Requirements Essential: Bachelor’s degree in a discipline relevant to ASE or CoHASS, together with significant professional experience in the wine industry and demonstrated advanced expertise in wine at a senior level. Candidates should hold a recognised international industry credential (e.g., Master of Wine or equivalent) or possess an equivalent combination of professional standing, industry achievements, and domain expertise that reflects comparable mastery in the field. Minimum 15 years of professional experience spanning the commercial, communications, and educational dimensions of the wine industry, including substantial direct experience in the Asia-Pacific market. Demonstrated track record as a wine educator, including design and delivery of formal accredited courses at professional or institutional levels (e.g. WSET Level 3+ or equivalent). Substantial experience as a communicator and writer for both specialist and non-specialist audiences, including a published portfolio of articles, reports, or books in high-quality trade or general media outlets. Proven experience designing and hosting high-level events, masterclasses, and educational programmes for senior professional and membership audiences. Established professional network within the regional and international wine industry, including active ties to wine-producing regions and industry bodies across Asia, Australasia, and Europe. Preferred: Demonstrated intellectual engagement with wine as a cultural, environmental, and economic phenomenon, evidenced through published books, industry research, or extended analytical writing. Experience operating within or alongside academic or research institutions, including guest lecturing, mentorship of emerging professionals, or collaboration with scientific communities. Experience within key Asian wine markets, particularly Singapore, Hong Kong, Japan, and Greater China. Experience translating complex scientific or technical content for lay audiences in formal and informal settings. Application Procedure Application package should include: Cover Letter (what you have to offer and why you chose NTU) Full Curriculum Vitae (CV) including evidence of teaching and publication. Writing samples or evidence of communications work (e.g., published articles or books) All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence.  The Search Committee will begin reviewing applications on  31 Jul 2026,  and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be processed, and only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For further enquiries, please contact  Chair-ASE@ntu.edu.sg   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Human-Resources_R00022385": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Human Resources",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs a key member of the HR team, you will play an essential role in supporting the HR Business Partner (HRBP) by managing a range of HR matters within the designated business unit(s). The successful candidate may have a focus in supporting HR operations under either the faculty or research portfolio. Key Responsibilities HR Operations Support Respond to employee inquiries and provide advisory support on HR policies and procedures Coordinate onboarding, offboarding, and HR administrative processes for faculty and research staff Manage administrative processes for contract renewals in coordination with stakeholders Ensure accuracy of HR data and support preparation of reports for decision-making Ensure compliance with employment laws, labor regulations, and institutional policies 2. Recruitment Administration Support end-to-end recruitment processes for full-time and contingent roles Collaborate with Talent Acquisition and HR Shared Services to ensure timely hiring Liaise with external recruitment agencies and manage vendor coordination 3. Performance Management Assist HRBPs during performance management cycles by tracking timelines and consolidating data Guide People Managers on performance tools and practices Ensure smooth execution of appraisal processes across designated business unit(s) 4. HR Projects & Engagement Collaborate with HRBPs and Centres of Excellence on HR initiatives, including policy reviews and process improvements Qualifications Degree with at least 3 years of experience in human resources administration field. Candidates with prior experience of working in an educational / academic/ research environment would have an added advantage Highly attentive to details, possess the ability to multi-task and to manage deliverables under tight timelines Strong verbal and written communication skills with demonstrated ability to interact effectively with diverse stakeholders Flexibility to adapt to changing priorities and evolving HR needs Proactive in resolving conflicts, answering queries, and addressing challenges faced by employees in a dynamic academic setting. Candidates with prior experience in using Workday system would have an advantage We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified . Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Human-Resource-Business-Partner_R00021496": {
      "title": "Human Resource Business Partner",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Description In this role, you will be a strategic HR advisor who builds strong partnerships with the senior leaders and the HR Centres of Excellence (COE) teams to develop and execute the People Strategies. Our HR Business Partnering team is structured to offer our stakeholders close support in three clusters – namely the Schools/Colleges, Administrative and Research clusters. All HR Business Partners report to Cluster Head of the HR Business Partnering Team and depending on the cluster which you are assessed suitable for, you may have a secondary reporting line to the School Chair/ Pan-University Research Centres. Responsibilities: Establish strong partnership with the business units to drive organizational effectiveness while implementing HR programmes and initiatives Actively identify gaps and opportunities where people-related risks can be minimized and influence solutions/outcomes Provide advice on HR policies and procedures including but not limited to the following areas - employment legislation, talent management, performance management, recruitment, manpower planning, rewards strategies and employee engagement; Establish clear understanding of the hiring requirements of the Business Units and work closely with NTU’s Shared Services team on the hiring of talents and appointment/re-appointment of staff on a timely basis. Be a facilitator and HR advisor to senior leaders in managing matters pertaining to industrial relations, employee grievances, conduct and discipline. Provide advice to stakeholders on policy changes, collaborate with senior leaders and functional HR Centre of Excellence to drive all HR initiatives such as manpower planning and projection, budget planning, employee engagement surveys, people development programs, change management plans, performance management etc. Depending on the eventual deployment of units which the HR Business Partner will support, he/she may be required to supervise a small team of HR professionals. Requirements: Degree with at least 5 years of relevant working experience in the Human Resources function, preferably in a HR Business Partnering role. Good Knowledge of Employment Act and Labour Laws Excellent communications and interpersonal skills with strong ability to engage and influence stakeholders at various levels Demonstrates flexibility and adaptability according to changing needs and priorities Collaborative and is comfortable working in a matrix structure with multiple priorities Resourceful and possess strong initiative to drive changes Ability to work independently as well as be active team members within and across the HR team.  Please note that successful candidates will be offered a 3-year contract with full benefits at the first instance. You can look forward conversion into a permanent appointment, subject to candidate’s good work performance and the University’s prevailing guidelines. Appointment titles (i.e. Assistant Manager/ Manager/ Assistant Director etc) offered will commensurate with candidate’s prior work experiences. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Semiconductor-Advanced-Packaging-_R00024649": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Semiconductor Advanced Packaging)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We seek a Research Fellow to advance low-temperature Cu/dielectric hybrid bonding for fine-pitch, high-density interconnects by developing and validating a new flow with reliable dielectric sealing under ≤ 200 ° C. The role integrates materials selection, wafer-level process development, and reliability demonstration to deliver a manufacturable 3D-integration solution that supports NTU’s leadership in industry-relevant advanced packaging research. Key Responsibilities: Develop and run a Cu–Cu hybrid bonding flow for fine-pitch 3D integration. Optimize process windows (pressure/temperature/anneal/surface activation) to minimize contact resistance and voids; maintain cleanroom/tool best practices. Characterize materials and interfaces using optical/profilometry, SEM/TEM, surface chemistry, and electrical IV; translate data into process improvements. Validate reliability and scalability via thermal cycling/HTS/electrical stress on test vehicles; build prototype stacks (e.g., interposer/test-chip) to evidence manufacturability. Report and collaborate: produce clear technical reports/presentations, coordinate with partners, and maintain rigorous documentation, version control, and safety compliance. Job Requirements: PhD in Materials/ Microelectronics/ EEE/ or related. Hands-on semiconductor process development in cleanroom (Cu interconnect/wafer or hybrid bonding; litho/etch/CMP/plasma/anneal). Characterization: optical/profilometry, SEM/TEM, XPS/AFM, electrical probing; DoE/statistics (Python/Matlab a plus). Strong documentation, safety discipline, and clear communication in English. Process integration & optimization; root-cause/failure analysis. Reliability mindset (design/interpret thermal & electrical stress tests). Collaboration with tool vendors/industry partners; concise reporting; ownership. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Research-Engineer-II--Computer-Science---Robotics---Automation-_R00025015": {
      "title": "Research Engineer II (Computer Science / Robotics / Automation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. ERI@N has multiple Interdisciplinary Research Programmes which focus on translational Research, Development & Deployment which focus on specific area of the energy value chain, and a number of Living labs and Testbeds which facilitate large scale technology deployment enabling validation and demonstration of real-world applications. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/erian Our department is seeking to hire a software engineer with experience in C++, Python, and Linux systems to join the Future Mobility Solutions research program. The successful candidate will work on the development, testing, and fine-tuning of self-driving vehicles, ranging from utility vehicles like buggies and road sweepers to public road vehicles. This role will contribute to advancing the autonomous driving technologies and robotics by supporting software development, vehicle trials and data processing. The role will also support the development of assessment methodologies for AV safety across various operational domains and preparation of technical reports, white papers, and presentations. Key Responsibilities: Work on C++ and Python codes for software development in linux systems Familiar with ROS & ROS2 for building autonomous or robotics systems Beneficial if familiar with open-source platforms like Autoware or Apollo for self-driving systems Develop, test, and fine-tune software for autonomous robots and vehicles across different platforms. Process and analyze sensor data, including LIDAR and camera inputs, for robotics and automation applications. Conduct outdoor vehicle trials for testing and validation of perception, navigation algorithms, and self-driving systems. Collaborate with team on improving and optimizing the performance of the autonomous vehicle system for real-world conditions. Participate in vehicle data collection activities and help refine software to meet project deliverables. Engage in software development and troubleshooting using ROS/ROS2 frameworks. Work on implementing object recognition and tracking models, such as YOLO, including optimizing model performance with tools like TensorRT Implement object recognition and tracking models, such as YOLO or similar frameworks, and integrate them into the existing autonomous software stack to enhance path planning and navigation, ensuring improved decision-making and obstacle avoidance. Job Requirements: Background in robotics and automation. Education: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Robotics, Automation, or a related field. Minimum Knowledge and Skills: Proficient in C++, Python, and Linux systems Familiar with ROS or ROS2 environments Strong understanding of LIDAR and camera sensor data processing for robotics and automation (and other sensors such as INS (GNSS-IMU), RADARs and Ultra-sonic sensors). Experience with outdoor testing, data collection, and validation of algorithms used in self-driving applications such as perception and navigation algorithms. Beneficial Experience: Prior work on open-source autonomous driving platforms such as Autoware or Apollo. Familiarity with computer vision and experience implementing image / object recognition systems, such as YOLO, for real-time object detection and classification. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Operations--Business-Development-_R00024997": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Operations (Business Development)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nReporting to the Centre Manager at the NTU Centre in Computational Technologies for Finance (CCTF), the Senior Assistant Manager will lead and manage the full spectrum of operational, financial, and administrative functions related to the Centre’s professional training programmes. The incumbent will play a key role in ensuring seamless programme delivery, stakeholder engagement, and regulatory compliance, while contributing to the strategic development and long-term sustainability of the Centre’s training portfolio. This role requires a proactive and resourceful individual with strong coordination, analytical, and project management skills, capable of driving operational excellence and continuous improvement. •    Programme Development & Strategic Execution Lead the design and development of training programmes aligned with industry needs and organisational goals. Conduct in-depth market analysis and stakeholder engagement to identify emerging trends and learning gaps. Drive the end-to-end programme lifecycle – from conceptualisation to evaluation – working closely with academic and industry experts. Propose new training initiatives and strategic partnerships to expand the Centre’s outreach and impact. •    Business Development & Stakeholder Management Develop and implement strategic outreach plans to grow and diversify the Centre’s customer base (corporate partners, government agencies, and professionals). Build and maintain high-trust relationships with key stakeholders, including C-suite clients, faculty, and external collaborators. Represent the Centre in internal and external engagements to promote the value and impact of our training programmes. Drive customer satisfaction and retention through proactive communication and after-programme engagement. •    Programme Operations & Team Coordination Oversee the full operational management of training delivery – including scheduling, logistics, resource planning, and on-site execution. Supervise junior officers and interns, providing guidance and performance feedback to ensure operational excellence. Lead cross-functional coordination with trainers, vendors, and internal departments to ensure smooth programme delivery. Manage crisis resolution and troubleshooting during programme execution. •    Financial Planning & Budget Oversight Prepare and oversee detailed programme budgets, ensuring optimal resource allocation and cost-efficiency. Track revenue targets and perform variance analysis to support Centre’s financial sustainability goals. Liaise with Finance on invoicing, vendor payments, and grants or fund utilisation, ensuring compliance with audit requirements. •    Governance, Compliance & Quality Assurance Ensure all training activities comply with NTU’s policies, funding requirements, and relevant legal/regulatory frameworks. Champion data protection and uphold PDPA and privacy regulations in all programme operations. Implement and continually refine Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for quality consistency. Use data analytics and participant feedback to drive continuous improvement in programme design and delivery.  Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline, with substantial experience in programme management, business development, or related fields. Relevant work experience in similar environments will be an advantage. A self-starter, adaptable and able to multi-task in a fast-paced environment. Excellent administrative skills. Good interpersonal and communication skills.  Detail-oriented and strong organisational skills. Motivated self-starter who is comfortable working with a team, as well as independently, under tight deadlines. Strong conceptual and analytical skills. Experience or interest in Blockchain and distributed ledger technologies for applications in diverse domains will be advantageous but not mandatory.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Visiting-Associate-Professor-in-Visual-Communication_R00024418": {
      "title": "Visiting Associate Professor in Visual Communication",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nVisiting Associate Professor Position in Visual Communication The School of Art, Design and Media (ADM) at Nanyang Technological University Singapore (NTU) invites applications for a one-year Visiting Associate Professor position in Visual Communication. ADM is part of the College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (COHASS). This position is intended for eminent overseas academics such as international prize recipients or distinguished scholars whose presence will enhance the academic standing of the faculty. The primary responsibility of this role is teaching. However, there are opportunities for candidates to incorporate their research interest(s) in the course syllabi as well as collaborations with other faculty within ADM. Therefore, candidates should be able to demonstrate a strong teaching track record in a current or previous Associate Professor academic level position. We seek candidates with expertise in one or more areas of Visual Communication, including fields such as, but not limited to, graphic design, editorial design, typography and typeface design, illustration, visual identity, production, concept development, design criticism, motion graphic, curatorial design, and exhibition design. The successful candidate will be responsible for the delivery of undergraduate courses in Visual Communication. There are opportunities to advise on curricular direction and to develop courses, and to provide technical review and feedback on facilities and equipment for pedagogical needs. The candidate is expected to bring international visibility to the school through continued high quality academic scholarship and/or impactful creative activity. The school expects a variety of service duties, including school and university committee service, and coordination of courses. Responsibilities include but are not limited to 1. Deliver 2 courses a semester in Visual Communication 2. Provide advice and expertise to identify and expand areas of curricular development 3. Provide up-to-date technical expertise to review and advise on technologies for teaching needs 4. Take on pathway coordination role and attending academic meetings Successful candidates should have a terminal degree (MFA, PhD or Practice PhD) in Visual Communication/Graphic Design, or equivalent area of expertise. In exceptional cases, an MA supported by significant professional experience can also be considered. The candidate should have a strong track record of teaching experience at the university level. Preference will be given to the candidate with substantial industry experience and good collaborations at the international level. Applicants are invited to submit their applications through the NTU career portal by clicking on the “Apply” button above. Please provide the following in your application: 1. Cover letter; 2. Curriculum vitae (including records of competitive grants and graduate supervision, if applicable); 3. Teaching statement; 4. Teaching evaluation; 5. Research statement; 6. Writing samples or creative portfolio; The closing date for applications is 31 July 2026. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified via email. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Hwa-Chong-International-School---Tooh-Fee-San-Distinguished-Professorship-in-Education-and-Artificial-Intelligence--NIE-NTU-_R00024911": {
      "title": "Hwa Chong International School – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professorship in Education and Artificial Intelligence (NIE/NTU)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHwa Chong International School – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professorship in Education and Artificial Intelligence National Institute of Education (NIE), Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore Overview The National Institute of Education (NIE) is among the world’s top education institutes, recognised for its excellence in teacher education and educational research.  NIE has played a key and pivotal role in shaping and developing Singapore’s teaching profession and landscape through evidence-informed, practice-focused and values-based programmes and initiatives. An autonomous institute situated within the research-intensive Nanyang Technological University (NTU), NIE is consistently ranked within the top 10 in the world for research impact in the field of Education. The Opportunity NIE invites applications for the Hwa Chong International School (HCIS) – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professorship in Education and Artificial Intelligence . The distinguished professorship will champion transformative research and innovation at the intersection of artificial intelligence (AI) and education. The HCIS – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professor in Education and Artificial Intelligence will Lead cutting-edge interdisciplinary research in AI and education Drive innovation in the design, implementation, and evaluation of AI-enabled pedagogies, curricula, and assessment Translate research into real-world educational impact, including collaboration with schools as testbeds for innovation Foster international collaborations with leading academics, industry partners, and educational institutions Contribute to strengthening Singapore’s position as a global hub for AI-enabled education Provide intellectual leadership through teaching, mentorship, and capacity building within NIE and NTU Requirements The ideal candidate should: Be an internationally recognised scholar with a distinguished track record of research and leadership in AI and education or related fields Demonstrate outstanding scholarly achievements, including high-impact publications and sustained research funding Exhibit strong commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and innovation Have a proven record of academic leadership, mentorship, and global engagement Show the ability to translate research into practice and policy impact in education Application Process Interested candidates should submit their Cover letter and Curriculum Vitae through Workday. For enquiries, interested applicants may write to Ms Yilian Wu . Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Cryptography-and-or-machine-learning-interpretability-_R00024939": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Cryptography and/or machine learning interpretability)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore   The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers.  In order to complete the NRF Investigatorship research project “Interpretable and Automated Cryptanalysis for Tailor-Made Cryptographic Design”, the school is looking to recruit one research fellow on cryptography and/or machine learning. Key Responsibilities The candidate will conduct research on cryptography and/or machine learning The candidate will help preparing reports and presentations for the project The candidate will publish relevant results to cryptography and/or machine learning conferences/journals Job Requirement PhD in Mathematics and/or Electronics and/or Computer Science Ability to work independently and as part of a team with strong initiatives. Good communication and interpersonal skills. Expertise in symmetric cryptanalysis/design or in state-of-the-art explainable AI solutions is a strong plus We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
