    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Multi-Sensor-Fusion-_R00018676": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Multi-Sensor Fusion)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-10-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre for Advanced Robotics Technology Innovation (CARTIN) is looking for a candidate to join them as a Research Associate. Key Responsibilities: Development of robust and reliable sensor fusion algorithms for localization and navigation algorithms of AGV in repetitive and dynamic environments AGV platform and sensor system hardware and software integration Algorithms and systems verification and validation Report writing and presentations Job Requirements: MEng degree in electrical engineering, computer science, robotic or related fields Extensive experiences in AGV and sensor fusion Extensive research and practical experiences in developing visual and radio-based SLAM Experience in system integration and flight control Strong coding capability Excellent communication and writing skills A ble to communicate complex concepts clearly and accurately Good interpersonal skill Excellent teamwork awareness We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-for-Translation-and-Localisation_R00018675": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer for Translation and Localisation",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-10-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nMaster of Arts in Translation and Interpretation Programme (MTI) at NTU is seeking experienced part-time instructors who excel at teaching courses on translation, localisation, project and data management. A proven track record of practical experience in handling corporations and clients at multinational, regional and local levels, with the knowledge of applying cutting edge project management tools and software are preferred. The instructor’s responsibilities include designing the course syllabus, conducting lectures and student consultation, designing assignments, administering assessment and grading, and providing constructive feedback to support student learning. Requirements: Demonstrable experience in teaching and curriculum development in higher education. Candidates should have a master level of T&I (Translation and Interpreting) degree and/or postgraduate level degree of project & data management. Preference will be given to candidates who have strong industry experience in translation projects management. We are also looking for candidates who possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a strong commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive learning environment. The successful candidate is expected to use both Chinese and English as the medium of instruction and to commence duty as soon as possible. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
