    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-the-School-of-Mechanical-and-Aerospace-Engineering_R00018530": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for part time teaching positions. We are looking for part-time instructors in the areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering within the College of Engineering, School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering. Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a recognized MEng degree, preferably PhD, in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching Hours Classes are mainly conducted during the day/night on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). In view of the current COVID situation, online teaching and assessments are expected to be conducted where required. In addition, applicant must be prepared to act according to the situational changes in number of CAs, CA formats, etc. when required by the school. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Psychology-Cognitive-Neuroscience-Education-_R00018516": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Psychology/Cognitive Neuroscience/Education)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Centre for Research and Development in Learning at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (CRADLE@NTU)  supports multidisciplinary and interdisciplinary research across NTU devoted to transforming learning in higher education. Leveraging on knowledge and methods from education, psychology, organizational behavior, neuroscience, and technology design, CRADLE aims to develop and test theories to explain learning processes. CRADLE seeks applications for the position of Research Fellow for a 1-year term (with renewable opportunities). Our current search is for candidate(s) interested in cognitive neuroscience of learning, and/or bridging findings from educational neuroscience to educational strategies. Suitable candidates will play a crucial role in developing and managing research projects conducted to contribute towards CRADLE’s research thrust of Science of Learning. Key Responsibilities: Conducting independent research Handling grant proposal documentation and associated administrative tasks Conducting literature search and writing reviews Supervising and leading team of researchers Coordinating between and liaising with faculty from different disciplines Some involvement with centre’s administrative duties Job Requirements: D octorate (PhD) degree and publication record in psychology, cognitive neuroscience, education, or related fields Experience in teaching or conducting research related to education settings are preferred.  Have good interpersonal skills Have demonstrated record of excellent scientific writing skills. Independence in developing programmatic research is encouraged Experience with systematic reviews and meta-analysis Experience in producing research reports Good statistical knowledge and skills, including familiarity with statistical analysis software such as R and SPSS. Knowledge and experience in social science research methodologies Experience in using graphical-user interfaced software e.g. Qualtrics, Google forms Supervisory and leadership skills for teams Person-oriented communication and coordination skills Experience with conducting and coordinating behavioral experiments in neuropsychology or cognitive psychology. Experience with neuroimaging techniques (functional and diffusion MRI/EEG/fNIRS and/or TMS). Familiarity with image data analysis tools such as SPM, FSL, AFNI, Matlab, DSIstudio etc. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00018487": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPart-Time Lecturer for EE6510 Power System Operation & Planning The School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, invites qualified candidates to apply as Part-Time Lecturer for EE6510 Power System Operation & Planning. The Part-Time Lecturer is expected to teach this postgraduate course commencing in October 2024. This 13-week course will be offered to students taking NTU EEE MSc Power Engineering Programme with the objective to impart to the students the knowledge relevant to power system planning and operations. The course will provide in-depth coverage of all essential aspects of power system operation and planning including load forecasting, generation scheduling, network operation, probability and reliability, generation planning and transmission planning. The successful candidate should have extensive relevant industry experience and/or at least a PhD degree in Electrical & Electronic Engineering (with Power Engineering research background) and a passion for teaching. Past teaching experience in a similar subject at Postgraduate Level (for EE6510) is preferred. Further information about the School can be viewed at the following website: EEE : https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee/home The successful candidate is expected to assume duty in October 2024 and is able to commit at least 5 months (1 semester) to this position. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00018480": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting tutorials and assessment) in our School on Ethics and Civics. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach the following topics: • Human rights, justice, and equality • Meritocracy • Political systems (Singapore, Southeast Asia) • Multiculturalism • Freedom of speech and responsibility • Gender and diversity Key Responsibilities: • Attend lectures (online). • Conduct tutorials and assessments for the assigned course. • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts). • Work closely with the course coordinator to handle students’ queries on course related matter. Qualification and requirement: • A degree in the social sciences, specialization in political science and sociology and good knowledge of Singapore will be an advantage. • Demonstrable ability to teach the proposed topics on Ethics and Civics at the undergraduate level will be an advantage. • Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, research and/or teaching experience on the course topics) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Electroplating-_R00018430": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Electroplating)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Project Officer. Our group is having open positions (research staffs) who are motivated to develop chemical process for surface finishing (electroless plating, electroplating, electrochemical etching)   Key Responsibilities:  To develop chemical surface finishing (electroless plating, electroplating, electrochemical etching) Job Requirements:  BS degree in chemistry, chemical engineering, material science, material engineering, or relative field Knowledge and experience in electrochemical processes We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Electroplating-_R00018431": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Electroplating)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Project Officer. Our group is having open positions (research staffs) who are motivated to develop chemical process for surface finishing (electroless plating, electroplating, electrochemical etching)   Key Responsibilities:  To develop chemical surface finishing (electroless plating, electroplating, electrochemical etching) Job Requirements:  BS degree in chemistry, chemical engineering, material science, material engineering, or relative field Knowledge and experience in electrochemical processes We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow---Research-Associate---Project-Officer--Fiber-Reinforced-Composites-_R00018395": {
      "title": "Research Fellow / Research Associate / Project Officer (Fiber Reinforced Composites)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) at NTU is seeking a highly skilled and motivated research staff to join our team. We are looking for a researcher with experience in working with carbon and glass fiber composite materials, epoxies, fire resistance and/or mechanical behavior of composites. Key Responsibilities: Work within the framework of the project to achieve and go beyond the project objectives. The candidate’s primary responsibility is to understand and improve the thermal insulation characteristics of epoxy based composites that are used for construction applications. The candidate is expected to interact and closely work within a multi-disciplinary and multi-cultural team.  Expected to display a very high degree of professional ethics Understand the safety issues while working with composites and fire protection materials. Job Requirements: Minimally Bachelor’s degree in relevant engineering or science disciplines is required Applicants with PhD preferred. The candidate is expected to be an expert in the handling/processing of epoxy composites and/or fire retardancy. The candidate is required to understand insulation mechanisms, and work towards project goals within the timeframe of the project. Relevant experience (flame retardant materials, manufacturing of epoxy composites, testing of fire resistance, etc.) is significant advantage. Flame retardancy background is considered as a huge positive. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Blockchain-_R00018380": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Blockchain)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCollege of Engineering (CoE) is looking for a candidate to join them as a Research Fellow. The NTU Centre in Computational Technologies for Finance is a newly created pan-university centre in NTU to coordinate and support NTU’s initiatives, activities and programs in Blockchain. The centre is co-managed by CoE and NBS. Key Responsibilities: Conduct fundamental and applied blockchain research with the focus on blockchain with sharding to reduce complexity and resource consumption Develop generative and advanced AI algorithms to optimize blockchain and data management platform for industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) Publish findings in top-tier journals such as IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing and top-tier conferences such as IEEE INFOCOM Support major research grant proposals for Blockchain initiatives Job Requirements: PhD in Computer Science/Engineering, Mathematics, Information Systems, or related fields Strong publication record in top journals and conferences Demonstrate high proficiency of communications skill We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Nonlinear-Optics-and-Metrology-_R00018314": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Nonlinear Optics and Metrology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-08-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Research Fellow.  The Research Fellow will be working on optics, nonlinear optics, spectroscopy and metrology projects at the centre Key Responsibilities:  Expected to work with the PI and other team members for doing R & D and take key role for the development of the systems for bioimaging and metrology Conduct and coordinate research within NTU and collaborating partners in line with its research strategy under the supervision of the PIs and collaborators Publish research outcomes in journals of international standing; Attend and present research findings and papers at academic meetings, and contribute to the external visibility of the centre. Draft research reports for PIs and undertake specific roles and management functions as may be reasonably required by the PIs. Job Requirements:  PhD in Optical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Precision Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Physics or a similar discipline with optics, spectroscopy and instrumentation background Previous experience in optics, nonlinear optics, optical measurement technologies, spectroscopy, metrology, and machine vision are desirable Expertise in handling and maintenance of high power CW and pulsed laser systems, spectrometers, high-resolution cameras, and delicate optical components are desirable Possess good programming, optical instrumentation, automation and dataprocessing skills (e.g. C++, LabVIEW, Zemax, OSLO, TracePro, MATLAB, Python, ImageJ) Proven publication track record would be an advantage ​ We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer--Minor-in-Geography-and-Urban-Studies-_R00018018-1": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer (Minor in Geography and Urban Studies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-08-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences is looking for Part-time Lecturers (PTL) who will be responsible for teaching undergraduate courses under the Minor in Geography and Urban Studies (GUS). We invite applications for part-time lecturers to conduct tutorials for Minor in GUS courses in, but not limited to, the following areas: •  Introduction to Human Geography •  Urban Geography •  Postcolonial approaches to space •  Spaces of exclusion and differentiation •  Changing nature of work •  Gender, sexuality and space •  Southeast Asia and Singapore •  Bordering, securitization and threats in a changing world Key Responsibilities: •  Propose a new course or teach an existing course. •  Conduct lectures or seminars. •  Conduct tutorials and assessments for a course. •  Conduct grading of course assessments/exam scripts. •  Other responsibilities related to undergraduate teaching. Qualifications: 1.  At least a PhD Degree in social sciences 2.  At least 1-2 years teaching experience at a tertiary level with excellent teaching evaluation. Singaporeans and Singapore Permanent Residents are preferred. To apply Applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include cover letter, detailed CV listing their teaching and industry experience as well as student feedback on teaching from previous institutions, if available). Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Mission-decomposition-and-Real-time-mission-planning-replanning-_R00018007": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Mission decomposition and Real-time mission planning/replanning)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre for Advanced Robotics Technology Innovation (CARTIN) is looking for a candidate to join them as a Research Fellow. Key Responsibilities: Carry out literature research on STOA of mission decomposition. Develop an efficient modeling framework that can capture a variety of operational requirements and uncertain operational environment. Develop an efficient mission analysis and decomposition method. Apply the developed modeling and decomposition methods in a simulation testbed. Publish research results in reputable journals and conferences (in particular, ICRA). Assist project PI to coach research students. Job Requirements: PhD degree in relevant fields with past research foci on formal methods, modeling and analysis of complex operations under uncertain environment. Strong publication record in relevant fields. Knowledge in modeling, simulation, and analysis of sea operations is a plus. Proficiency in English is essential to conduct research. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer--Psychology-_R00017363": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer (Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-06-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences invites applications for part-time lecturer (PTL). We are looking for PTL who will serve as primary instructor of core and elective courses in the Psychology major curriculum. Key Responsibilities: Preparation and delivery of lectures, tutorials, and discussion sections. Supervision and coordination of teaching assistants and tutors. Setting of assessment components and marking of examinations. Qualification and requirement: The successful candidate will hold a doctorate-level or a masters-level qualification in an appropriate Psychological field, be able to demonstrate effective teaching and training of undergraduate students.  Candidates with specializations in one or more of these fields are particularly welcome: Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and Clinical Psychology. Evidence of excellence in teaching and/or clinical supervision is highly desirable. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute significantly to teaching and development of multiple courses at the undergraduate level, including introductory level survey-type courses, laboratory and methods courses, and seminar courses. Essential selection criteria: The attainment of a higher degree (PhD/DPhil/Masters) in Psychology or a related discipline Experience and interest in teaching undergraduate psychology students, with a strong and demonstrable commitment to the organization and delivery of teaching, particularly in one or more areas of Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and/or Clinical Psychology Excellent communication and interpersonal skills relevant to teaching and pastoral care Willingness and ability to contribute to the overall objectives of the Programme and School, working collaboratively with others Desirable selection criteria: A developing track record of research (e.g. peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations) in Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and/or Clinical Psychology Experience of academic administration For further information about the School, and Psychology, at NTU, please refer to the following website: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sss/psychology To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience, preferred course) CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) Student feedback on teaching (if available) Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Science-_R00017311": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Computing & Data Science (CCDS) invites applications for the position of Research Fellow.  The successful applicant will be responsible for the development of a software platform to support Smart Nation applications.   Key Responsibilities:  Design and implement natural language processing (NLP) algorithms and models for semantic analysis, e.g., topic modeling, embedding, named-entity recognition, coreference resolution and parsing, and Multilingual translation. Application of NLP in knowledge and information extraction Conduct “translational” research to apply state-of-the-art solutions at scale for real-world challenges Documentation and scientific reporting Mentoring junior staff Job Requirements:  PhD in Computer Science Minimum 5 years software development experience (Entry Level Candidates with relevant project experience will also be considered) Experience and excellent research background in NLP Passionate about NLP and AI-related research, innovations, and their applications Proficient in one or more programming languages (e.g., Python, etc.) and research packages/modules Experience in large-scale text processing and analytics Good track records in publication Experience in Multilingual Translation is an added advantage. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Finance-Business-Partnering_R00011001": {
      "title": "Manager, Finance Business Partnering",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-05-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Finance Business Partner (FBP) plays an instrumental role in establishing finance business partnership with stakeholders in University’s unit or group of University’s units. The partnership is vital to enable and ensure effective finance planning, reporting and operations in alignment with University’s policies and guidelines. This role is responsible for planning and executing the implementation of finance initiatives and targets to help achieve the goals of the University’s unit. It includes financial planning, budget monitoring and reporting, ensuring governance and compliance and coordinating operational activities related to specific objectives of the University’s unit. The role has a primary reporting line into the Office of Finance and a secondary reporting line into the University’s unit. Responsibilities: Understands School’s strategy, priorities and aligns the financial activities to enable School to enable School to achieve the priorities. Provides relevant financial insights that value-add to the overall School performance. Performs pro-active partnering role and acts as a trusted financial advisor to the senior management in the School to resolve strategic and operational changes. Conducts decision-support analyses that provides real-time and accurate financial information (endowment report, expenditure report, budget utilization report) and draws insights from such analyses to make recommendations to the School Management, as well as relevant finance stakeholders (e.g. finance partner @ college or finance leadership team). Drives effective end-to-end financial and/or budget planning and variance analyses and monitors external changes that would have impact on School financial position, supports any change initiatives or project / process improvements that will improve the depth and efficiency of forecasting, budgeting, monitoring and reporting of financial performance of the School. Recommends ideas and solutions with the aim of enhancing operational processes within the School by incorporating finance expertise (such as risks exposure) and best practices; Drives continuous improvements and identifies key areas of potential cost savings in the School. Provides required financial expertise and advisory to stakeholders (e.g. faculty, principal investigators, managers) so as to protect assets and ensures compliance with existing policies and regulation. Uses organizational acumen and knowledge of School to advise finance office holders on implications to financial reporting, statutory and regulatory reporting. Engage with internal and external stakeholders. Supports all audit reviews and execute any audit remedial actions. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Finance or Accountancy CPA preferred Candidate should have a minimum of 8 years of relevant experience Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-lecturer-for-Multimodal-and-Theatre-Translation_R00016491": {
      "title": "Part-time lecturer for Multimodal and Theatre Translation",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-03-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPart-time lecturer for Multimodal and Theatre Translation Master of Arts in Translation and Interpretation Programme (MTI) at NTU is seeking experienced part-time instructors who excel at teaching courses on theatre translation. A proven track record of practical translation experience for drama, theatre, play and other forms of stage performance are preferred. The instructor’s responsibilities include designing the course syllabus, conducting lectures and student consultation, designing assignments, administering assessment and grading, and providing constructive feedback to support student learning. Requirements: Demonstrable experience in teaching and curriculum development in higher education. Candidates should have a postgraduate level degree level of T&I (Translation and Interpreting) degree and/or PhD degree for theatre studies. We are also looking for candidates who possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a strong commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive learning environment. The successful candidate is expected to use both Chinese and English as the medium of instruction and to commence duty as soon as possible. Please click “APPLY” button to submit your application. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Engineer-I--Satellite-System-Hardware-_R00016505": {
      "title": "Senior Research Engineer I (Satellite System Hardware)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-03-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of EEE invites applications for the position of Senior Research Engineer I (Satellite System Hardware).   The Research Engineer will work on a project to conduct the research on development of energy harvesting systems used in low power smart sensors for monitoring of buildings and bridges, as well as the integration of energy harvesters, power management circuit and monitoring sensors.   Key Responsibilities: Design and develop MCU/MPU/SOC platform. Analyze system requirements and generate modular specifications. Identify and qualify components for spacecraft operation. Build, test and modify prototypes. Circuit validation and system operational validation. Test and characterize circuits. Code and debug in embedded C. FPGA programming. Guide/design printed circuits to comply to EMC/EMI requirements. Work with team members to ensure smooth integration of various subsystems. Document all process and implementation. Manage tasks according to project schedule. Support the centre and project operation, such as satellite mission operation, satellite testing and student activities. Work on a project to conduct the research on development of energy harvesting systems used in low power smart sensors for monitoring of buildings and bridges. Work on integration of energy harvesters, power management circuit and monitoring sensors.   Job Requirements: Bachelor‘s degree and above in Electronic Engineering or related field from a reputable university. Diploma with good industry experience may also be considered. Experience in MCU/MPU/SOC embedded system platform design and programming. Good understanding and ability in analog and digital circuit design Proficient and good skill in pcb artwork such as Altium or Orcad. Knowledge of various embedded hardware and application systems. Experience in generation of design specification documentation, schematic capture, and circuit analysis and simulation. Experience with debugging tools such as bus and spectrum analyzer. Experience in CAN, SPI, I2C bus protocols. Able to multi-task and work in a dynamic environment. Fluent verbal and written communications in English. Complete full product life cycle knowledge is preferred. Experiences in FPGA, Analog or RF design is preferred.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Communication--Science-Communication--Psychology-_R00016459": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Communication/ Science Communication/ Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-03-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information is looking for a Research Assistant to join the research project, titled “ATTAIN*SG: Achieving public TrusT in AI in autoNomous vehicles in SinGapore”. The Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information is a world-class full-fledged communication school in Singapore, with an international faculty and state-of-the-art research centers. We provide a wide range of opportunities for self-conducted, mentored, and collaborative research in a vibrant and supportive environment. More information can be found here: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/wkwsci Key Responsibilities: Conduct literature search Assist in development and conceptualization of a survey Assist in analysis of survey data Contribute to research publications and presentations Assist in writing progress report and final research report Engage in the dissemination of the results of the research with the support of and under the supervision of the Principal Investigator Organize a conference related to the theme of the project Carry out administrative work associated with the program of research as necessary Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in fields including communication, psychology, sociology, or a social science related discipline Prior experience in survey methodology for social science research Good quantitative data management and analytical skills (e.g., being able to analyze data using SPSS, MPLUS, R, and/or Python) Good communication and organizational skills Ability to work in a highly collaborative and multi-cultural team environment Team player in a project setting, also with ability to work independently in a multi-cultural team environment Must demonstrate initiative and good interpersonal communication skills Prior experience in autonomous vehicles research Internationally recognized research track record as evidenced by journal publications and conference presentations We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Mechanical-Engineering-Robotics-Mechatronics-Automation---Control-Engineering-Artificial-Intelligence--AI--_R00015865-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Mechanical Engineering/Robotics/Mechatronics/Automation & Control Engineering/Artificial Intelligence (AI))",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Research Associate.   Key Responsibilities:  Work on human-like traffic simulation, with the focus of modeling traffic behaviors from large-scale real-world datasets. ​ The work will involve traffic scene representation, behavior modeling with common sense and prediction, generating road layouts, initializing states of traffic agents, rendering in physical simulators, and experimental validation. Job Requirements:  At least have a Masters Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, Mechatronics, Automation and Control Engineering, Artificial Intelligence (AI), etc. Relevant working experience will be preferred. Strong background in autonomous driving, simulator, AI, and automation. Good communication skills and the ability to work independently and facilitate projects with minimal supervisiont Able to contribute to Journal/Conference papers with good presentation skills Able to plan and organize well and adhere to deadlines. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00015379": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-11-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are looking for part-time lecturers in the following areas of business specialisations within the College of Business, Nanyang Business School: •    Accounting •    Banking & Finance •    Business Law •    Information Technology & Operations Management •    Leadership, Management & Organisation •    Marketing •    Strategy, International Business and Entrepreneurship •    Sustainability Classes are mainly conducted on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a degree in Business or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Only shortlisted applicants will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
