    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00015259": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-10-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting tutorials and assessment) in our School on Ethics and Civics. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach the following topics: • Human rights, justice, and equality • Meritocracy • Political systems (Singapore, Southeast Asia) • Multiculturalism • Freedom of speech and responsibility • Gender and diversity Key Responsibilities: • Attend lectures (online). • Conduct tutorials and assessments for the assigned course. • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts). • Work closely with the course coordinator to handle students’ queries on course related matter. Qualification and requirement: • A degree in the social sciences, specialization in political science and sociology and good knowledge of Singapore will be an advantage. • Demonstrable ability to teach the proposed topics on Ethics and Civics at the undergraduate level will be an advantage. • Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, research and/or teaching experience on the course topics) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer--Evergreen---Open-_R00015131": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer (Evergreen) (Open)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-10-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are looking for part-time lecturers in the following areas of business specialisations within the College of Business, Nanyang Business School: •    Accounting •    Banking & Finance •    Business Law •    Information Technology & Operations Management •    Leadership, Management & Organisation •    Marketing •    Strategy, International Business and Entrepreneurship •    Sustainability Classes are mainly conducted on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a degree in Business or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Only shortlisted applicants will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00015143": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-10-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nTeaching a portion of MSE Major Prescribed Elective Course: MS4630 Photovoltaic Devices and Energy Storage (Lecture and Tutorial). The teaching assignment will also include setting up exam questions, marking exam scripts and invigilation. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer--Psychology-_R00014909": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer (Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-09-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences invites applications for part-time lecturer (PTL). We are looking for PTL who will serve as primary instructor of core and elective courses in the Psychology major curriculum. Key Responsibilities: Preparation and delivery of lectures, tutorials, and discussion sections. Supervision and coordination of teaching assistants and tutors. Setting of assessment components and marking of examinations. Qualification and requirement: The successful candidate will hold a doctorate-level or a masters-level qualification in an appropriate Psychological field, be able to demonstrate effective teaching and training of undergraduate students.  Candidates with specializations in one or more of these fields are particularly welcome: Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and Clinical Psychology. Evidence of excellence in teaching and/or clinical supervision is highly desirable. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute significantly to teaching and development of multiple courses at the undergraduate level, including introductory level survey-type courses, laboratory and methods courses, and seminar courses. Essential selection criteria: The attainment of a higher degree (PhD/DPhil/Masters) in Psychology or a related discipline Experience and interest in teaching undergraduate psychology students, with a strong and demonstrable commitment to the organization and delivery of teaching, particularly in one or more areas of Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and/or Clinical Psychology Excellent communication and interpersonal skills relevant to teaching and pastoral care Willingness and ability to contribute to the overall objectives of the Programme and School, working collaboratively with others Desirable selection criteria: A developing track record of research (e.g. peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations) in Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and/or Clinical Psychology Experience of academic administration For further information about the School, and Psychology, at NTU, please refer to the following website: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sss/psychology To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience, preferred course) CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) Student feedback on teaching (if available) Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Occupational-Therapy-Physio-Therapy-_R00014742": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Occupational Therapy/Physio Therapy)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-08-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Research Assistant. A Research Assistant is sought to develop raining materials and facilitate specialised clinical and medical educational sessions.   Key Responsibilities:  Provide clinical input for risk assessments for medical robotic products. Lead the training of clinicians during the installation/ implementation process Perform/oversee clinical trial site management duties (e.g. site selection, monitoring). Job Requirements:  A degree in Occupational Therapy/Physio Therapy or related areas. Comfortable & skilled with public speaking and training PC literate and have excellent organizational skills Teaching or research experience (preferred) We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-for-EE6506-Power-Semiconductor-Based-Converter-in-Renewable-Energy-Systems_R00014511": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer for EE6506 Power Semiconductor Based Converter in Renewable Energy Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-08-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, invites qualified candidates to apply as Part-Time Lecturer for EE6506 Power Semiconductor Based Converter in Renewable Energy Systems. The Part-Time Lecturer is expected to teach this postgraduate course commencing in August 2023. This 13-week course will be offered to students taking NTU EEE MSc Power Engineering (PE) Programme with the objective to create a background on theoretical, practical and design aspects of power semiconductor devices and passive components, including their applications in various power converter systems essential in all Renewable Energy Systems, and this will be illustrated through examples, problem solutions & applications. The techniques of device selection, their control and protection of power semiconductor devices would be covered. This will be illustrated through examples, problem solutions, applications and case study. The successful candidate should have extensive relevant industry experience and/or at least a PhD degree in Electrical & Electronic Engineering (with relevant research background) and a passion for teaching. Past teaching experience in a similar subject at Postgraduate Level (for EE6506) is preferred. Further information about the School can be viewed at the following website: EEE : https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee/home For enquiries about the job scope of this position, please contact the Hiring Manager: Dr Foo Yi Shyh Eddy, Telephone: +65 67904519, Email:  eddyfoo@ntu.edu.sg The successful candidate is expected to assume duty in August 2023 and is able to commit at least 5 months (1 semester) to this position. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-the-School-of-Mechanical-and-Aerospace-Engineering_R00014255": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-07-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for part time teaching positions. We are looking for part-time instructors in the areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering within the College of Engineering, School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering. Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a recognized MEng degree, preferably PhD, in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering  or  a  closely  related  field,  have  extensive  industry  and/or  academic  experience  with  a  passion  for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching Hours Classes are mainly conducted during the day/night on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). In  view  of  the  current  COVID  situation,  online  teaching  and  assessments  are  expected  to  be  conducted  where required. In addition, applicant must be prepared to act according to the situational changes in number of CAs, CA formats, etc. when required by the School. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer_R00014211": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-07-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are looking for part-time lecturers in the following areas of business specialisations within the College of Business, Nanyang Business School: Accounting Banking & Finance Business Law Information Technology & Operations Management Leadership, Management & Organisation​​ Marketing Strategy, International Business and Entrepreneurship​​ Sustainability Classes are mainly conducted on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a degree in Business or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. For enquiries, please email to Mr Tang Kai Han ( kaihan.tang@ntu.edu.sg ) (NBS HR) . Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Communication-Psychology-Sociology-Social-Science-_R00013705": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Communication/Psychology/Sociology/Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-06-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) is looking for a Research Assistant to make an important contribution to a project on public opinion and communication towards science, environmental, and health issues, funded by NTU. Key Responsibilities: To engage in conducting literature searches and manuscript preparation. To engage in survey and experiment conceptualization and design. To conduct statistical analyses with survey and experimental data. To conduct qualitative data analyses. To contribute in research publications and presentations. To write progress report and final research report To engage in the dissemination of the results of the research with the support of and under the supervision of the Principal Investigator. To carry out administrative work associated with the program of research as necessary. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in communication, psychology, sociology, or a social science related discipline. Strong foundation in survey and experimental research and analytical skills (e.g., SPSS, MPLUS, or R). A team player in a project setting, also with ability to work independently in a multi-cultural team environment. Must demonstrate initiative and good interpersonal communication skills. Prior experience in survey and experimental research. An internationally recognized research track record as evidenced by journal publications and conference presentations. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer_R00013850": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are looking for part-time lecturers in the following areas of business specialisations within the College of Business, Nanyang Business School: Accounting Banking & Finance Business Law Information Technology & Operations Management Leadership, Management & Organisation​​ Marketing Strategy, International Business and Entrepreneurship​​ Sustainability Classes are mainly conducted on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a degree in Business or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. For enquiries, please email to Mr Tang Kai Han ( kaihan.tang@ntu.edu.sg ) (NBS HR) . Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Nanyang-Business-School-International-PhD---Postdoctoral-Scholarship--NBSIPS--2023_R00011768": {
      "title": "Nanyang Business School International PhD / Postdoctoral Scholarship (NBSIPS) 2023",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-02-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Nanyang Business School (NBS) International PhD Scholarship (IPS)/Postdoctoral Fellowship (IPF) 2023 is now open for application. NBSIPS/IPF aims to encourage outstanding Singapore citizens to pursue an academic career in NBS by supporting their doctoral or postdoctoral studies abroad. Under this scheme, the successful candidates will be employed as University staff. They will be granted paid leave to pursue a sponsored PhD/Postdoctoral programme in an approved overseas university. Upon successful completion of the programme, they will be appointed as tenure-track Assistant Professors of the University. The successful applicant should be a Singapore citizen and have a First Class Honours Bachelor’s degree in Accountancy, Business, Social Sciences, Mathematics or Engineering. A detailed study plan and interviews by the School and University panels will form an important part of the selection process. Full information on the programme, including the application form, eligibility, programme structure, mentorship, service obligations and application procedures, can be downloaded at the end of this page. The application deadline is 28 February 2023 . Applications will be reviewed after the closing date. Do submit all applications via NTU Workday by clicking the “Apply” button. All late or incomplete applications will not be considered. For queries, please write to evd-nbs@ntu.edu.sg . Documents   Information Booklet Application Procedures Application Form for PhD Programme Application Form for Postdoctoral Programme Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Project-Engineer--E-IC---Separation-Technologies-Applied-Research-and-Translation-Centre--NTUitive-_R00007822-1": {
      "title": "Project Engineer, Separation Technologies Applied Research and Translation Centre [NTUitive]",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-02-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Project Engineer is responsible for executing whole or assigned parts of translation projects related to membrane fabrication, module fabrication and system level validation of locally and globally sourced novel membrane technologies using in-house pilot test equipment and large-scale external pilot validation platforms. Responsibilities: Assist project in-charge to execute assigned tasks in membrane translation operations, maintenance of membrane fabrication equipment and membrane module design and fabrication from small scale 2-inch modules up to 8 -inch industrial scale modules. Operation of in-house pilot system to evaluate the performance of membrane modules of new technologies including test protocol preparation and process parameter optimization before integration into large scale external pilots. Transfer in-house pilot’s operation, data collection and reporting method to on-field pilot systems leading to technology evaluation on the integrated demonstration plant. Assist project in-charge and engineering manager in sourcing components for scaling up of selected membrane technologies to pilot systems. Support and contribute to discussions leading to engineering design and system process flow finalization for pilot operations. Stay abreast with state-of-art developments in water treatment technologies. Prepare, operationalize, and maintain SOP’s pertaining to membrane processes. Train and educate junior staff in matters related to membrane technology and water treatment operations. Ensure strict compliance with Health, Safety, Environment (HSE) Regulations. Present regular project progress review to senior management. Requirements: Bachelor’s in Engineering (Materials/Mechanical/Chemical/Environmental) Fresh graduates are welcome to apply. At least 2 years of experience in membrane technology, process operations and optimization is an advantage. Experience in membrane fabrication processes e.g., flat sheet and hollow fiber and/or other types of membranes is an advantage) Good knowledge of water treatment systems based on polymeric and ceramic membrane technologies. Experience in processing and communicating P&ID’s for pilot systems related to water treatment and other separation process applications. Hands on experience in using design software including but not limited to AutoCAD is a plus. Appointment may vary and will commensurate with candidate's years of working experience. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTUitive"
    },
