    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00011370": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs) who can contribute to teaching Singapore: Imagining the next 50 years.   Key Responsibilities: • Conduct lectures / tutorials in the related discipline (both face-to-face and online) • Handle administrative work concerning the grading of students • Give inputs regarding the course curriculum Qualification and requirement: • A least a Master’s Degree. • At least 2-3 years teaching experience at a tertiary level with excellent teaching evaluation. • Teaching experience in Singapore-related topics is preferred. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • Detailed CV listing teaching and industry experience • Student feedback on teaching from previous institutions, where applicable Only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00011229": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPart Time Teaching Positions Young and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore) is the fastest-rising university in the world’s Top 20 and ranked 11th globally. NTU is also placed 1st amongst the world’s best young universities. The School of Social Sciences at NTU offers a stimulating and multidisciplinary education and research in the social sciences, and is home to four major disciplines for undergraduate and postgraduate degrees (Economics, Psychology, Sociology and Public Policy and Global Affairs). Part-Time teaching position(s)  is available to cater to the short-term teaching needs of School of Social Sciences for the following: Subject Area: Principles in Economics International Finance               Job Responsibilities: Conduct lectures / tutorials in the related discipline (both face-to-face and online) Course Curriculum Planning and Coordination. Handle administrative work and examination matters concerning the grading of students Requirements: A least a Master’s Degree. At least 2-3 years teaching experience at a tertiary level with excellent teaching evaluation. Teaching experience in Microeconomics/Macroeconomics/Finance-related topics is preferred. It should include the reference  “Application for Part-time Teaching Position”  in the subject line with attached detailed CV listing teaching and industry experience, as well as student feedback on teaching from previous institutions, where applicable. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Bahasa-Indonesia_R00010560": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Bahasa Indonesia",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNTU invites applications for part-time teaching of the Bahasa Indonesia  language electives at the beginner and intermediate levels. Requirements: A postgraduate qualification, preferably in a humanities subject or relevant field. A degree in Bahasa Indonesia would be considered an advantage. Experience in teaching and learning, preferably at tertiary level. Skills and knowledge in IT and multi-media course development. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Language-and-Communication-Centre_R00011043": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Language and Communication Centre",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are seeking experienced candidates capable of teaching academic writing and communication skills. Instructors will be responsible for teaching 2-hour tutorials in addition to class preparation, assessing student assignments according to guidelines, being available for student consultations, working with curriculum writers on curriculum matters, and working with coordinators on administrative matters. Requirements: Master’s degree or higher in Linguistics, Education or Literature At least 2-3 years relevant teaching at a tertiary level   Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Malay_R00011408-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Malay",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNTU invites applications for part-time teaching of the Malay  language electives at the beginner and intermediate levels. Requirements: Master’s degree in Malay language or equivalent. A native speaker with high proficiency of the Malay language. Effectively bilingual in both Malay and English Language. Knowledge in the application of IT in language teaching and experience with multimedia course materials Experienced in various genres of the Malay language. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Publishing_R00010595": {
      "title": "Part‐time Lecturer in Publishing",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNTU invites applications for part‐time teaching of various humanities related courses as one of our offerings in the Continuing Education program within the School of Humanities. Candidates should have a proven track‐record in teaching. Lecturers will be responsible for leading workshops and seminars for 12 hours in addition to syllabus planning, class preparation, marking for assessment and student consultation. We seek to fill several part‐time lecturer positions, subject to candidates with the following credentials: - MA/PhD degree or extensive industry experience  - Ability to teach at least one of the following: Practical Ethics Culture and history that are relevant to the Singapore context Digital humanities Environmental humanities Editing, Publishing, and Branding Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Engineer--Algorithm-and-Operation-Researcher-_R00010743-1": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Engineer, Hardware Developer)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Project Officer.  Key Responsibilities:  The Project Officer will j oin the team to develop insect-computer hybrid robots control system: Design and fabrication of wirelessly controlled sensor-backpack mounting on living insects to (i) electronically stimulate their neurons and muscles to navigate them on demands and (ii) report environmental conditions Develop firmware, algorithm, data structure and user interface for sensor-backpack remote control Integrate customized algorithm in insect computer hybrid robot operation and test the operation of sensor-backpack on living insect Technical write up and presentation Job Requirements: Degree in Mechatronics/ Robotics/ Electrical and Electronics/ Computer Engineering Experience in PCB design and fabrication Experience in C/C++ programming for embedded system Experience in real time operating system development Experience in wireless communication (BLE, Sub-Ghz, UWB, etc …) is advantageous Experience in C#, Java, JavaScript, Python is advantageous Knowledge and experience in insect anatomy and physiology is advantageous A team player and technically motivated to solve problems. Good interpersonal and communication skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Electrical---Electronic-Engineering-Mechatronics-Robotics-Engineering-Mechanical-Engineering-_R00011214-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Electrical & Electronic Engineering/Mechatronics/Robotics Engineering/Mechanical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Research Fellow. Key Responsibilities:  Work is related to development and demonstration of a prototype for Mobile robot combination coupling and decoupling device/platform. Excellent prototyping and problem solving skills. Capable of working independently and within a team, while supervising other Final year students working on their final year projects on related area. Can communicate and present technically complex issues to multidisciplinary/multinational teams (local and international) Job Requirements:  Ph.D degree in Electrical/Electronics/Robotics, mechanical or mechatronics engineering Experience in related area of cobot or related technologies (Plus). Familiar with control systems of cobot and robotic systems (Plus) Working knowledge of software (Python, C++, Matlab or similar). Practical and hands-on, active self-learner and able to pay close attention to technical details Proficiency in English and verbal communication, have strong work ethic and can work independently and comfortably in a multidisciplinary environment. Good working knowledge in ROS (Robot Operating System). We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--High-Frequency-Active-Circuit-Design-_R00010582-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (High Frequency Active Circuit Design)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Research Fellow position is available in the Centre for Integrated Circuits and Systems, School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. Job Description: Support the research for the project titled:Terahertz Transmitter and Receiver Antennas for Wireless Communications. The project investigates the On-chip Hybrid Electronic and Photonics Transceiver design for high data-rate wireless communication at the sub-THz band. The CMOS/SiGe technologies will be used for the design of electronic circuits Work on the design and characterization of sub-THz electronic circuits (Oscillators, Mixers) Work closely with the Photonics team for hybrid integration of photonics devices Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical and Electronic Engineering and related study area Strong background in RFIC components design (mmWave will be advantageous) Good Experienced in EDA tools (Cadence, ADS) and EM modelling tools (HFSS, CST) RF characterization measurements Able to make active IC design of phased array antenna systems and on chip antenna including fabrication and characterization measurement Capable and broad experience in: (i) Active circuit design (ii) Work in group (iii) Post-fabrication measurement We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Engineer-I--Computer-Science-_R00010614-1": {
      "title": "Senior Research Engineer I (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Senior Research Engineer I position is available in the Centre for Smart Platform Infrastructure Research on Integrative Technology (SPIRIT), Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. SPIRIT is a translational R&D institute funded by National Research Foundation and supported by Smart Nation Programme Office and GovTech, to develop the Smart Platform Infrastructure to enable applications in Video Analytics, Wireless Sensors Network and other areas required by Singapore as a Smart Nation. Through cutting-edge systems research, SPIRIT Centre aims to enable translational efforts in data science and analytics for solving public sector challenges through innovative solutions. Job Description: The Senior Research Engineer I will be responsible for the AI/NLP research and development in designing smart nation platforms. The key responsibilities include: Gather system requirements by defining and analyzing system problems Design and implement natural language processing (NLP) algorithms and models for semantic analysis, e.g., word embedding, named-entity recognition, coreference resolution and parsing, and ontology and knowledge graph constructions Application of NLP in knowledge and information retrieval, and relevancy ranking with spatiotemporal consideration Conduct “translational” research to apply the state-of-the-art solutions at scale for real world challenges Documentation and scientific reporting Job Requirements: PhD in computer science Some experience and research background in AI and NLP Passionate about NLP and AI related research, innovations and their applications Proficient in one or more programming languages (e.g., Python, C/C++, etc.) and research packages/modules Experience in large-scale text processing and analytics Good track records in publication We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Engineer-I--Computer-Science-_R00010619-2": {
      "title": "Senior Research Engineer I (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Senior Research Engineer I position is available in the Centre for Smart Platform Infrastructure Research on Integrative Technology (SPIRIT), Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. SPIRIT is a translational R&D institute funded by National Research Foundation and supported by Smart Nation Programme Office and GovTech, to develop the Smart Platform Infrastructure to enable applications in Video Analytics, Wireless Sensors Network and other areas required by Singapore as a Smart Nation. Through cutting-edge systems research, SPIRIT Centre aims to enable translational efforts in data science and analytics for solving public sector challenges through innovative solutions. Job Description: The successful applicant will be responsible for the AI/NLP research and development in designing smart nation platforms. The key responsibilities include: Gather system requirements by defining and analyzing system problems Design and implement natural language processing (NLP) algorithms and models for semantic analysis, e.g., word embedding, named-entity recognition, coreference resolution and parsing, and ontology and knowledge graph constructions Application of NLP in knowledge and information retrieval, and relevancy ranking with spatiotemporal consideration Conduct “translational” research to apply the state-of-the-art solutions at scale for real world challenges Documentation and scientific reporting Job Requirements: PhD in computer science Some experience and research background in AI and NLP Passionate about NLP and AI related research, innovations and their applications Proficient in one or more programming languages (e.g., Python, C/C++, etc.) and research packages/modules Experience in large-scale text processing and analytics Good track records in publication We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer---Public-Policy-and-Global-Affairs_R00008473": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - Public Policy and Global Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme, School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting seminars, lectures, tutorials and assessment) in our Programme, particularly in these areas: • Political Theory (including but not limited to the history of political thought, contemporary political theory, non-Western political theory, analytic political thought) • Public Policy or Public Administration (including but not limited to public policy and administration in Singapore and Asia, policy implementation, AI and governance, sustainability) • Environmental governance • Civil society • Gender and development • Ethics and Civics • Comparative politics Key Responsibilities: • Develop course materials and syllabus • Conduct seminars/lectures/tutorials • Develop assessments for the course • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts) • Invigilate the final examination. • Handle all student queries on course related matter • Work with the Head of Division to ensure smooth and timely course delivery Qualification and requirement: • A least a PhD in social sciences, specialisation in a political science subfield will be an advantage • Prior tutoring/lecturing experience will be an advantage • Able to teach and invigilate during office hours To apply Interested applicants should email their application to UG-PPGA@ntu.edu.sg. Application package (one file) should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience) • Sample syllabi of proposed course to be taught • CV (highlight teaching experience) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer--Public-Policy-and-Global-Affairs-_R00006003": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer (Public Policy and Global Affairs)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme, School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting tutorials and assessment) the core courses in the Programme, specifically: • Fundamentals of Politics • Politics of Singapore • Introduction to International Relations and Foreign Policy • Introduction to Political Theory • Introduction to Public Administration and Policy Key Responsibilities: • Attend lectures (to be discussed and agreed with course coordinator). • Conduct tutorials and assessments for the assigned course. • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts). • Invigilate the final examination. • Work closely with the course coordinator to handle students’ queries on course related matter. Qualification and requirement: • A least a Master Degree in social sciences, specialisation in a political science subfield will be an advantage. • Some prior tutoring/lecturing experience will be an advantage. • Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience, preferred course) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00006159": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting tutorials and assessment) in our School on Ethics and Civics. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach the following topics: • Human rights, justice, and equality • Meritocracy • Political systems (Singapore, Southeast Asia) • Multiculturalism • Freedom of speech and responsibility • Gender and diversity Key Responsibilities: • Attend lectures (online). • Conduct tutorials and assessments for the assigned course. • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts). • Work closely with the course coordinator to handle students’ queries on course related matter. Qualification and requirement: • A degree in the social sciences, specialization in political science and sociology and good knowledge of Singapore will be an advantage. • Demonstrable ability to teach the proposed topics on Ethics and Civics at the undergraduate level will be an advantage. • Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, research and/or teaching experience on the course topics) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-Screenwriting--Creative-Writing-_R00001319": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in Screenwriting (Creative Writing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPart-time Lecturer in Screenwriting (Creative Writing) -School of Humanities We are seeking an experienced screenwriter capable of teaching HZ9205 Screenwriting as one of our offerings in Creative Writing within the School of Humanities. Candidates should have a proven track-record in writing and developing projects for the screen. Instructor will be responsible for leading workshops and seminars for three class hours per week in addition to syllabus planning, class preparation, marking for assessment and student consultation. Requirements: Master’s degree or higher At least 2-3 years teaching screenwriting at a tertiary level   For further information about the current Creative Writing Electives, please refer to the following website: http://www.soh.ntu.edu.sg/Programmes/english/undergraduate/Pages/Minorcreativewriting.aspx   Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Tutors--Linguistics-and-Multilingual-Studies-_R00000625-1": {
      "title": "Part-Time Tutors (Linguistics and Multilingual Studies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nSchool of Humanities The Linguistics and Multilingual Studies (LMS) programme invites applications for part-time tutors. We are in particular looking for candidates who can teach the core courses in the Programme, namely, Introductory Linguistics, Phonetics and Phonology, Structure of English, Morphology and Syntax, Semantics and Pragmatics, Sociolinguistics, Bilingualism and Multilingualism. Criteria: Candidates must possess at least an Masters of Arts in Linguistics. Some prior tutoring experience will be an advantage. Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Community-Immersion-Programme---Data-Coordinator_R00025758": {
      "title": "Community Immersion Programme & Data Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is seeking a Programme Coordinator to support the development of the Community Immersion Programme (CIP), supported by the NBS30 Fund. The role will take ownership of assigned programme workstreams across local and overseas projects, working closely with students, faculty, alumni mentors, community partners, host universities and relevant NTU teams. The role combines  programme coordination, stakeholder engagement, data management and process improvement , with opportunities to contribute to the development and scaling of a new programme. The successful candidate will also leverage data, digital tools, automation and appropriate AI applications to enhance mentor matching, programme tracking, reporting and operational efficiency. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate and oversee assigned local and overseas CIP projects and programme workstreams, from planning and onboarding through implementation, tracking and post-project follow-up. Manage multiple project timelines, milestones and stakeholder deliverables, ensuring timely follow-up and resolution of operational issues. Develop effective working relationships with students, faculty, alumni mentors, NGOs, social enterprises, host universities and relevant NTU teams to align requirements and support programme coordination and delivery. Support the identification and assessment of suitable community partners and alumni mentors, and recommend appropriate matches based on project requirements and established programme criteria. Analyse alumni and programme data to support mentor matching, stakeholder engagement, programme tracking and reporting. Identify and implement approved process improvements, including the use of digital tools, automation and appropriate AI applications to improve operational efficiency and data quality. Plan and coordinate logistics for CIP launches, briefings, mentor sessions, student presentations and other programme activities. Track programme participation, project progress and outcomes, and prepare dashboards, reports and updates for management, donors and relevant stakeholders. Analyse programme feedback and data to identify trends, operational gaps and opportunities to enhance programme effectiveness and participant experience. Support the continuous development and scaling of CIP processes and workflows as the programme grows. Requirements: Recognised Bachelor’s degree or Diploma with 3-4 years work experiences . Entry-level candidates with relevant experiences and interest are welcome to apply. Good working knowledge of programme/project planning, stakeholder engagement and operational processes, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, timelines and stakeholders concurrently. Strong stakeholder engagement and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build effective working relationships and work collaboratively with diverse internal and external stakeholders. Good analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret data, identify issues, evaluate options and recommend practical solutions. Ability to take ownership of assigned workstreams from planning through implementation, monitoring and follow-up. Comfortable working with spreadsheets, databases and reporting tools, with the ability to use data to support programme tracking, analysis and reporting. Ability and interest in using digital, automation and/or AI-enabled tools to improve programme processes, data management and operational efficiency. Ability to identify opportunities for process improvement and implement approved enhancements. Good written and verbal communication skills, with strong attention to detail and the ability to prepare clear programme updates, reports and other materials. Proactive, resourceful and adaptable, with a strong sense of ownership and accountability and the ability to work independently in a developing programme environment. Experience or knowledge in community engagement, student development, alumni relations, social impact programmes, events or education-related programmes would be advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Coral-Microbial-Ecology-_R00025757": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Coral Microbial Ecology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Case Research Team in SCELSE is seeking a research fellow with established field techniques, ability to use molecular protocols for DNA and RNA isolation from marine bacteria and seagrasses for molecular community analysis, genome sequencing and metagenomics. The candidate should be a talented marine microbiologist with experience working with marine microbes and field experience. Responsibilities: Perform manipulative experiments with corals and bacteria to determine their thermal and disease tolerance To sample, manipulate and experiment with corals using physiological and molecular analysis Work with a group of marine scientists to identify beneficial microbes for coral resilience. Requirements: PhD in marine microbiology or marine microbial ecology Competent in molecular microbiology and bioinformatics Ability to culture bacteria and corals to manipulate them in laboratory and field station settings. Ability to perform DNA manipulation (e.g., extraction, purification, QC) for molecular community analysis. Ability to perform PAM-fluorometry, flow cytometry, microscopy. Marine field experience Confidence in swimming, working in intertidal zone and boat travel for field sampling. Ability to handle microbes competently and safely up to Biological Safety Level 2 (BSL2) Ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Excellent interpersonal skills Possess a sense of initiative and proactiveness We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Enhanced-Learning--Agents-and-Algorithms-_R00025754": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum-Enhanced Learning, Agents and Algorithms)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Centre for Quantum Technologies at NTU invites applications for a Research Fellow position in Quantum-Enhanced Learning, Agents and Algorithms. The successful candidate will conduct independent and collaborative research at the intersection of quantum information science, machine learning, statistical learning theory, quantum thermodynamics, and complexity science. The Research Fellow will develop novel theoretical frameworks and algorithms for quantum-enhanced learning and intelligent agents, with research directions including quantum advantages in data-sparse learning, quantum algorithms for learning and sampling, temporal quantum information processing, non-Markovian dynamics, and quantum resource theories. The role also involves contributing to interdisciplinary research initiatives, publishing high-impact scientific findings, preparing research proposals, and presenting research outcomes at conferences and seminars. The successful candidate will work closely with faculty members, researchers, and students within the international research network, while supporting the supervision and mentoring of postgraduate students. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to cutting-edge research with both fundamental scientific significance and potential real-world applications. Key Responsibilities Conduct high-quality research in quantum-enhanced learning, quantum information science, and related areas. Develop new theoretical models, methodologies, and algorithms. Publish research outcomes in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Prepare grant applications, technical reports, and research presentations. Collaborate with internal and external researchers across multiple disciplines. Contribute to the supervision and development of graduate students. Support the achievement of research milestones and project objectives. Job Requirements PhD in Quantum Information, Theoretical Physics, Computer Science, Mathematics, Machine Learning, or a closely related discipline. Candidates nearing completion of their PhD may also be considered. Demonstrated research excellence through publications, conference presentations, or related scholarly achievements. Knowledge and experience in one or more of the following areas: Quantum algorithms Quantum stochastic processes and quantum combs Machine learning and statistical learning theory Reinforcement learning Differential privacy Model reduction and distillation Quantum reservoir computing Variational quantum circuits Quantum resource theories and quantum thermodynamics Strong analytical, problem-solving, and quantitative research skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary research teams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Enhanced-Learning--Agents-and-Algorithms-_R00025755": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum-Enhanced Learning, Agents and Algorithms)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Centre for Quantum Technologies at NTU invites applications for a Research Fellow position in Quantum-Enhanced Learning, Agents and Algorithms. The successful candidate will conduct independent and collaborative research at the intersection of quantum information science, machine learning, statistical learning theory, quantum thermodynamics, and complexity science. The Research Fellow will develop novel theoretical frameworks and algorithms for quantum-enhanced learning and intelligent agents, with research directions including quantum advantages in data-sparse learning, quantum algorithms for learning and sampling, temporal quantum information processing, non-Markovian dynamics, and quantum resource theories. The role also involves contributing to interdisciplinary research initiatives, publishing high-impact scientific findings, preparing research proposals, and presenting research outcomes at conferences and seminars. The successful candidate will work closely with faculty members, researchers, and students within the international research network, while supporting the supervision and mentoring of postgraduate students. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to cutting-edge research with both fundamental scientific significance and potential real-world applications. Key Responsibilities Conduct high-quality research in quantum-enhanced learning, quantum information science, and related areas. Develop new theoretical models, methodologies, and algorithms. Publish research outcomes in leading peer-reviewed journals and conferences. Prepare grant applications, technical reports, and research presentations. Collaborate with internal and external researchers across multiple disciplines. Contribute to the supervision and development of graduate students. Support the achievement of research milestones and project objectives. Job Requirements PhD in Quantum Information, Theoretical Physics, Computer Science, Mathematics, Machine Learning, or a closely related discipline. Candidates nearing completion of their PhD may also be considered. Demonstrated research excellence through publications, conference presentations, or related scholarly achievements. Knowledge and experience in one or more of the following areas: Quantum algorithms Quantum stochastic processes and quantum combs Machine learning and statistical learning theory Reinforcement learning Differential privacy Model reduction and distillation Quantum reservoir computing Variational quantum circuits Quantum resource theories and quantum thermodynamics Strong analytical, problem-solving, and quantitative research skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary research teams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--LKCMedicine-_R00025756": {
      "title": "Senior/Research Fellow [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Hwei-Ee Tan lab studies the fundamental biological basis of “gut-feelings”, how bacteria in the gut signals to the host to influence physiology and behaviour. Using mice as a mammalian model, the lab investigates how diet and microbiome factors modulates host phenotypes (e.g. food reward, anxiety behaviours, etc). Besides supporting curiosity-driven basic research on the gut-brain axis, his lab is also studying the brain-gut axis, to uncover host-microbe interactions. His lab’s work is multidisciplinary, the research scope covers diverse skills from molecular biology to systems neuroscience, physiology and behaviour. With top-tier research support from National Research Foundation Singapore, Brain & Behavior Research Foundation (NARSAD), etc, his lab at NTU LKCMedicine is actively recruiting talented postdoctoral research fellows, research assistants, and interns, and also open to sponsoring motivated PhD/Masters students. Prior to submitting their application, postdoctoral applicants are strongly encouraged to also look up the lab’s website and email the PI with a CV/resume and a cover letter articulating their scientific ambition.   Key Responsibilities : The postdoctoral applicant must demonstrate commitment to co-create impactful discoveries in the microbiome gut-brain neuroscience field with us. In addition to being exceptionally motivated, having core skills for animal and lab work, and willing to work in our team and help with essential lab duties. The candidate must have experience and specialized expertise in multiphoton/ 2-photon in vivo calcium imaging and data analysis, or in gnotobiotic studies and microbiome analysis/bioinformatics. Key Competencies/Requirements : Hold a doctoral (PhD) degree in neuroscience or relevant disciplines with strong publication track record Lead impactful work within the lab’s research theme on the microbiome gut brain neuroscience Exhibit proficiency in mice/rodent handling, optogenetics and behaviours, animal surgery and dissection Demonstrate experience and specialized expertise in multiphoton/ 2-photon in vivo calcium imaging and data analysis, or in gnotobiotic studies and microbiome analysis/bioinformatics Be highly motivated and conscientious, able to work independently and with a team, and willing to teach, learn, and assist with essential lab duties Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Learning-Governance---Process-Excellence_R00025753": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Learning Governance & Process Excellence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU PACE is the continuing education and training arm of Nanyang Technological University (NTU), supporting lifelong learning and workforce development through industry-relevant programmes for professionals and organisations. The Senior Assistant Manager, Learning Governance & Process Excellence is responsible for establishing, maintaining and strengthening robust governance frameworks and systems for Adult Educators management, curriculum and assessment practices, courseware quality assurance, assessment governance and continuous improvement across NTU PACE's lifelong learning portfolio. The role ensures compliance with institutional quality standards, Skills & Workforce Development Agency (SWDA) requirements through development of governance frameworks, documented processes, evidence management practices and audit-ready quality assurance systems while balancing the practical needs of a higher education institution. The role also supports business process improvement and digital transformation initiatives, identifying opportunities to leverage AI and workflow automation to improve operational efficiency, quality assurance, scalability and stakeholder experience. The role works closely with Programme Directors, Adult Educators, Value Streams leads and industry stakeholders to support Adult Educator governance, courseware review, assessment quality assurance, industry validation and continuous improvement activities. The role also supports the digitalisation and standardisation of governance processes to improve efficiency, evidence traceability and stakeholder accountability. Key Responsibilities Support Adult Educator governance processes, including Adult Educator onboarding, qualification verification, capability development and quality monitoring. Coordinate curriculum and assessment reviews with industry practitioners, subject matter experts and advisory committees. Maintain quality assurance processes, governance documentation and standard operating procedures to support institutional and regulatory requirements. Facilitate continuous improvement initiatives arising from programme reviews, stakeholder feedback and quality assurance activities. Identify opportunities to improve efficiency through process improvement, digital solutions and workflow automation. Requirements Must Have Bachelor's Degree from a recognised university. Diploma in Adult and Continuing Education (DACE) or Diploma in Design and Development of Learning for Performance (DDDLP). At least 8 years of relevant experience in adult education, training management, curriculum development, learning quality assurance or related fields. Experience in trainer governance, curriculum review, assessment processes or quality assurance. Strong stakeholder engagement, communication and project coordination skills. Good to Have Experience working with SkillsFuture Singapore (SSG), WSQ, TPQA or similar quality assurance frameworks. Experience in process improvement, digitalisation or workflow automation initiatives. Familiarity with AI-enabled productivity tools and learning technologies. Why Join Us This role offers the opportunity to contribute to the quality, relevance and continuous improvement of NTU PACE's lifelong learning programmes while working closely with academic, industry and government stakeholders to support workforce development and lifelong learning initiatives. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-engineering-Computer-Science-Electronics-Engineering-_R00025752": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: The development of new algorithms, Their efficient numerical implementation and evaluation, Their theoretical analysis, Writing a paper on the work performed in collaboration with the PI and possibly other group members. Job Requirements: Preferably Master in Computer engineering, Computer Science, Electronics Engineering or equivalent. Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills In-depth knowledge relevant to the project domain. Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research. The ability and willingness to adapt and incorporate novel ideas and approaches in scientific industry. Demonstrated ability to formulate hypothesis and design effective numerical experimental plans. Ability to design and implement new numerical experimental methods. High-level expertise in the required experiment or modelling methods. Ability to initiate collaboration research in multidisciplinary team. Oversee and report project progress. Ability and willingness to work some flexible hours. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--HR-Operations_R00025751-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, HR Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager supports the University’s operations by ensuring the timely and compliant onboarding of staff across all employment schemes, work pass administration as well as the timely and accurate charging of recruitment cost to the respective cost centres. As a specialist in work pass matters, the role provides subject‑matter expertise to support regulatory compliance and smooth onboarding processes. The role also supports the team’s automation and digitalisation efforts by working with internal stakeholders to streamline workflows, standardise processes, and improve candidate and staff experience. In addition, the Assistant Manager contributes to the review and improvement of operational processes, SOPs, and service controls to support efficiency, consistency, and compliance. Key Responsibilities: Manage end‑to‑end pre‑employment and onboarding processes, including scheduling and conducting Day 1 orientation, to ensure timely, accurate, and compliant onboarding. Prepare and issue onboarding documentation and access requirements, including related employment materials. Verify employment and statutory documents to ensure completeness, accuracy, and compliance prior to commencement. Administer work pass applications, renewals, issuance, and cancellations in accordance with regulatory requirements and timelines. Provide timely and accurate advice to hiring units, employees, and stakeholders on work pass and onboarding‑related matters. Reconciliation of work pass and pre employment billing Drive automation, digitalisation, and continuous review of onboarding and work pass processes, SOPs, and service controls to improve efficiency, consistency, and service quality . Requirements: Degree in Administration or Human Resources areas Good knowledge of employment‑related regulations and work passes is advantageous.   Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at different levels. Proven ability to manage high‑volume transactions with accuracy, attention to detail and sound judgement. Proficiency in HR systems (e.g. Workday) and Microsoft Office applications is an advantage. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoc-Research-Fellow--Electrolyte-and-materials-interfaces-for-batteries-_R00025748": {
      "title": "Postdoc/Research Fellow (Electrolyte and materials interfaces for batteries)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt EI2 Lab www.wrzhanglab.com , we focus on advancing electrochemistry, materials, and engineering as an integrated platform to build technologies for a sustainable and resilient future. We focus on the ion conductor and its interface with other materials. We aim to understand the ion/electron transportation in the conductor, and the chemo-electro-mechanics behavior at these materials interface. By understanding and ultimately controlling these interfaces, we will enable the development of advanced energy systems and electronic devices, including high energy Li/Na batteries, all-solid-state batteries, sensors, switch, electrochemical transistors, with scalable architectures for real-world applications. The School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a highly motivated Postdoctoral or Research Fellow to drive independent research in next-generation electrochemical energy systems ; support interdisciplinary collaborations across materials science, electrochemistry, and mechanics; mentor graduate and undergraduate students in the lab. The role will contribute to cutting-edge research in electrochemical energy storage and conversion , with a focus on solid-state batteries, interfacial chemistry, electro-chemo-mechanics, and novel energy materials. Key Responsibilities: Conduct advanced research on solid-state batteries ; high energy batteries; materials synthesis; Develop materials for electronic devices like sensors, semiconductors, switch, transistors . Design and perform electrochemical, mechanical, and advanced materials characterizations. Collaborate with internal and external academic/industrial partners on joint projects. Prepare manuscripts for high-impact journal publications and present at international conferences. Contribute to grant proposal writing and new project development. Mentor and supervise PhD, Master’s, and undergraduate students in the laboratory. Job Requirements: PhD or conferring PhD degree in Materials Science, Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or related field At least 3 years of relevant experience in a similar role / technical hands-on experience in materials synthesis, electrochemical testing, and advanced characterization techniques. Proven track record of high-quality research publications in high-impact journals. Good written and oral communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary team. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoc-Research-Fellow--New-electrochemistry-and-electrode-materials-for-next-gen-batteries-_R00025747": {
      "title": "Postdoc/Research Fellow (New electrochemistry and electrode materials for next-gen batteries)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt EI2 Lab www.wrzhanglab.com , we focus on advancing electrochemistry, materials, and engineering as an integrated platform to build technologies for a sustainable and resilient future. We focus on the ion conductor and its interface with other materials. We aim to understand the ion/electron transportation in the conductor, and the chemo-electro-mechanics behavior at these materials interface. By understanding and ultimately controlling these interfaces, we will enable the development of advanced energy systems and electronic devices, including high energy Li/Na batteries, all-solid-state batteries, sensors, switch, electrochemical transistors, with scalable architectures for real-world applications. The School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a highly motivated Postdoctoral or Research Fellow to drive independent research in next-generation electrochemical energy systems ; support interdisciplinary collaborations across materials science, electrochemistry, and mechanics; mentor graduate and undergraduate students in the lab. The role will contribute to cutting-edge research in electrochemical energy storage and conversion , with a focus on solid-state batteries, interfacial chemistry, electro-chemo-mechanics, and novel energy materials. Key Responsibilities: Conduct advanced research on solid-state batteries ; high energy batteries; materials synthesis; Develop materials for electronic devices like sensors, semiconductors, switch, transistors . Design and perform electrochemical, mechanical, and advanced materials characterizations. Collaborate with internal and external academic/industrial partners on joint projects. Prepare manuscripts for high-impact journal publications and present at international conferences. Contribute to grant proposal writing and new project development. Mentor and supervise PhD, Master’s, and undergraduate students in the laboratory. Job Requirements: PhD or conferring PhD degree in Materials Science, Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or related field At least 3 years of relevant experience in a similar role / technical hands-on experience in materials synthesis, electrochemical testing, and advanced characterization techniques. Proven track record of high-quality research publications in high-impact journals. Good written and oral communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary team. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Materials-Science---Engineering---Mechanical-Engineering---Chemical-Engineering-_R00025740": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Materials Science & Engineering / Mechanical Engineering / Chemical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) is a research centre conducting fundamental and applied research in all aspects related to additive manufacturing. Our vision is to be the world leader in 3D Printing and a wellspring of knowledge, delivering state of the art and innovative solutions to the industry. SC3DP is at the forefront of developing advanced technologies and high-impact research in areas such biomedical, construction, aerospace, marine and offshore. It is one of the very few research centres globally with multi-sector 3D printing expertise. SC3DP’s research achievements, high-level industry collaboration, comprehensive facilities and resources have positioned it as a leading hub for 3D printing research and innovation globally. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Associate with a strong engineering background to advance an industry-collaborative research project on metal additive manufacturing. This role is mainly focused on the advanced characterization, microstructural analysis, and mechanical property evaluation of 3D printed samples. The objective of this role is to assist in solving practical engineering challenges in industrial applications and facilitate the industrial translation of our research outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Material Characterizations: Conduct microstructural analysis using Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM), Electron Backscatter Diffraction (EBSD), X-ray Diffraction (XRD), and optical microscopy etc. Mechanical Testing: Perform tensile, fatigue, hardness, and impact testing to evaluate the performance of the printed components. Data Analysis & Reporting: Analyze testing data, visualize data, prepare detailed technical reports, and present research findings to the industrial partners. Quality Assessment: Evaluate the impact of post-processing on material properties, and identify defects (e.g., porosity, lack of fusion). Job Requirements: A master’s degree in Materials Science & Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Chemical Engineering or a closely related technical field. Extensive hands-on experience with advanced material characterization techniques (e.g., SEM, EBSD, XRD, optical microscopy) and mechanical testing equipment (e.g., tensile, fatigue, and hardness testers). Deep understanding of material science and structure-property relationships in metallic systems. Strong analytical capabilities with a proven ability to interpret complex testing data and independently prepare comprehensive technical reports. Familiarity with materials commonly used in additive manufacturing is highly desirable. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Vision-and-Artificial-Intelligence-_R00025739": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Vision and Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHyundai-NTU-A*STAR Corporate Lab offers an excellent R&D environment to create novel technologies with the world leading automotive company, Hyundai by translating the research into the dark factory directly with implementing and validating the research using AI, Robotics, 3D Printing and Digital Twins. We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct the research for the project entitled “Manual Assembly Job Quality Inspection”. The role will focus on research and development of AI algorithms for defect detection, image/video analysis and understanding Key Responsibilities: Develop artificial intelligence (AI) technologies for defect detection, image/video analysis and understanding. Perform system integration of the developed algorithms Oversee project budget and coordinate the procurement and maintenance of equipment Provide mentorship and academic guidance to students Prepare and compile reports pertaining to the project. Job Requirements: PhD degree in Computer Science, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, or related field. At least 3 years of relevant experience in computer vision, artificial intelligence, etc. Proficiency in programming languages such as C and Python Proficiency in deep learning frameworks such as Pytorch and Tensorflow Knowledge in imaging and computing devices and equipment Good written and oral communication skills Ability to work independently and as a team Excellent organizational / time management skills Good publication records We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Civil-Engineering-Ocean-Engineering-_R00025743": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Civil Engineering/Ocean Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Research Fellow position (equivalent to Postdoctoral Fellow in many countries/regions) is available in the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE), Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore. The successful candidate will work on research related to the hydrodynamic behavior of floating structures. Key Responsibilities: Conduct wave flume tests and develop numerical/analytical models of floating structures. Prepare project reports and publish scientific papers in peer-reviewed journals. Assist the PI in preparing research proposals and supervising research students. Job Requirements : PhD degree in Civil Engineering, Ocean Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline. Research experience in hydrodynamics and structural dynamics. Strong publication record in relevant research areas. Effective writing and communication skills. Experience in supervising research students and preparing research proposals will be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Flexible-Electronics-_R00025737": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Flexible Electronics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . We are seeking a highly motivated and interdisciplinary Research Fellow to develop soft, stretchable interconnect technologies for next-generation stretchable and flexible electronic devices. The role focuses on the design, fabrication, and reliability of conductive interconnects and bonded interfaces on soft, deformable substrates, with emphasis on printable conductive materials, low-temperature and photonic sintering/bonding processes, interfacial reaction and diffusion mechanisms, and electromechanical reliability under repeated deformation. The successful candidate will contribute to NTU’s research in advanced materials and soft/flexible device platforms by bridging materials science, interfacial and interconnect engineering, and printed/flexible electronics. Key Responsibilities: Design, fabricate, and characterize stretchable and flexible interconnects and bonded joints on soft, deformable substrates using printable conductive materials and low-temperature/photonic bonding and sintering methods. Develop conductive inks, nanoparticle and composite material systems, and interlayer/interface designs for reliable soft interconnection and device integration. Conduct microstructural, chemical, mechanical, and electromechanical characterization, including electrical and reliability evaluation under bending, stretching, and cyclic deformation. Collaborate with interdisciplinary researchers to integrate soft-interconnect solutions into stretchable electronic devices, sensors, and system-level platforms where relevant. Assist in manuscript preparation, conference presentations, grant development, and reporting to funding agencies and collaborators. Mentor junior researchers and students where required, and support general laboratory management, procurement and equipment coordination where required. Job Requirements: PhD in Materials Science, Electronic/Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Microelectronics, Chemistry, or a related discipline. Demonstrated research experience in flexible/stretchable electronics interconnection, printed electronics, conductive inks, soldering, interfacial joining, or low-temperature bonding of advanced materials. Strong background in interfacial and interconnect engineering, joint/interface design, and characterization of bonded and printed interfaces on rigid or soft substrates. Experience in one or more of the following areas is highly desirable: conductive ink formulation and printing, photonic/pulsed-light or low-temperature sintering, nanoparticle/nanocomposite conductive materials, flexible/stretchable device fabrication, electronic/advanced packaging, interfacial reaction and diffusion, or microstructure-property-reliability relationships in interconnects. Familiarity with microstructural, chemical, mechanical, and electrical/electromechanical characterization methods for materials and interfaces. Strong publication record in reputable journals and the ability to independently drive research tasks to completion. Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary and collaborative research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Curriculum--LKCMedicine-_R00025736": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Curriculum [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Senior Executive, Curriculum will work closely with the School Leads, different teams within the department and the various education offices in the healthcare training institutions to ensure seamless coordination in curriculum delivery on campus and in clinical posting training sites. Responsibilities: Provide logistical and administrative support for sessions scheduled in the Year 3 Enhanced Campus Based Learning (ECBL) weeks for Medicine, Surgery and Short Postings clinical blocks, Year 3 Campus Teaching Week (CTW) and Wrap-up Week (WuW) Coordinate simulation-based learning experiences by working closely with session Leads to finalise Simulated Patient (SP) scenarios, coordinate SP recruitment and ensure all supporting arrangements are delivered to a high standard. Collaborate with Leads, the Office of Medical Education and Science & Anatomy Laboratories teams to ensure learning spaces, equipment and resources are prepared prior to the session. Facilitate the development and deployment of curriculum resources by collaborating with content experts to coordinate, quality-check, format and publish preparation materials across relevant digital learning platforms. Coordinate clinical education placements and postings by partnering closely with hospital Education Offices (EDOs) to plan and arrange Medicine and Surgery clinical postings for students, ensuring placements are well-coordinated and aligned with curriculum requirements. Drive the effective administration of the digital curriculum by creating and maintaining learning events across the full academic year in Elentra, including attendance-taking activities, to support accurate scheduling and communication. Coordinate logistics for integrated and combined teaching sessions within the Medicine and Surgery clinical postings, working across relevant stakeholders to ensure teaching spaces, resources and operational arrangements are in place for smooth and effective session delivery. Oversee room booking for teaching spaces in the Eco Book Assist in events organised by the team and department Requirements: A good University degree in any discipline Candidates with prior experience in the education and/or healthcare sector are preferred Experience in scheduling/timetabling will be an advantage Excellent interpersonal and communication (written and verbal) skills Able to work independently under time pressure and changing deadlines/priorities in a dynamic environment Able to multi-task and work on different portfolios and projects simultaneously Analytical, Meticulous and enjoy solving problems We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--M-E-Facilities-Management_R00025735": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, M&E Facilities Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU is a world-class research-intensive university located in Singapore, consistently ranked among the top universities in Asia and the world. We are home to over 36,000 students and 10,000 staff, offering a vibrant and dynamic work environment for individuals seeking to advance their careers. NTU is seeking an experienced and motivated Senior Assistant Manager to join our dynamic team in Office of Development and Facilities Management. The department oversees the physical development and maintenance of all university buildings and grounds in support of the academic, research, continuing education and training, and administrative functions of the University. As a Senior Assistant Manager, your role encompasses comprehensive operations and maintenance of the designated M&E services and steering their upgrading works to ensure long-term reliability. Responsibilities: Oversee the operation and maintenance of Fire Protection, Plumbing, Sanitary & Gas, Lift, and ELV systems. Monitor preventive and corrective maintenance works carried out by term contractors to ensure system reliability and uninterrupted operation. Review maintenance reports, breakdown trends and system performance to identify recurring issues and recommend improvement actions. Oversee term contractors to ensure maintenance works are carried out in accordance with contract requirements, safety standards and service levels. Responsible for asset management through proper tracking of asset condition, maintenance history and lifecycle information. Oversee upgrading and improvement projects to enhance safety, reliability, accessibility and operational effectiveness of systems. Manage internal stakeholders, consultants and contractors during project implementation. Ensure M&E systems and works comply with statutory requirements, codes of practice, and internal governance frameworks. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering or Facilities Management. At least 5 years’ experience in facilities management or M&E related field. Strong technical understanding of building services M&E systems, particularly Fire Protection, Plumbing & Sanitary, and Lift related infrastructure, enabling detailed design review, system interfacing, fault diagnosis, and optimization of system performance, reliability and maintainability. Hands-on experience in facilities management including supervising term contractors on-site, verifying maintenance and rectification works, ensuring compliance with statutory and safety requirements, and maintaining dependable day-to-day operations. Strong project management and organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities. Effective communication skills, able to work with stakeholders and contractors to resolve issues. Good problem-solving and analytical skills, with a hands-on approach to fault diagnosis and resolution. Proactive and take ownership of assignments and challenges. Able to work independently. Continuous improvement mindset, with an interest in improving work processes and system performance. NTU offers a supportive and dynamic work environment that provides employees with opportunities for personal and professional growth. Our employees have access to a range of learning and development opportunities, including training programs, workshops and seminars. NTU values the well-being of its employees and has in place several staff welfare initiatives such as health and wellness programs, free access to on-campus fitness facilities and discounted health screening. Joining NTU as a Senior Assistant Manager is an excellent opportunity for an individual looking to further their career in a challenging and dynamic environment. If you have the required skills and experience and are excited about this opportunity, we invite you to submit your application today!   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Intelligent-Manufacturing-_R00025734": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Intelligent Manufacturing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . Perform research on Industrial AI, develop novel AI methods, prepare Project and Project requirements. Represent Research and support positive outcomes for the project and research group. Key Responsibilities: Project performance AI method development Gathering of domain knowledge and formalization Writing of research documentation/ideas/publication Mentoring of students/other researchers (potentially) as well as long-term research agenda development and implementation Job Requirements: Education & Experience: Master’s degree in a relevant field (Information Systems and Engineering) or equivalent advanced research experience with a proven track record of research in the specified domain. Bachelor's degree will be considered with relevant work experience. Domain Expertise: Practical experience and deep domain knowledge in relevant Industrial AI sectors. Work Location: Position is based physically in Singapore. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoctoral-Fellow--Mechanics-_R00025733": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow (Mechanics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. We are seeking a Postdoctoral Research Fellow to contribute to collaborative projects on shape-morphing materials and applications to adaptive aeronautics. Key Responsibilities: Development of novel designs and mechanisms for shape-morphing structures Development of models for sensing and control in shape-morphing systems Experimental implementation of designs Engaging in scientific exchange with collaboration partners of the project Preparing reports, scientific papers, and presentations Job Requirements: PhD in mechanical engineering, physics, or a related field Research experience on shape-morphing structures, mechanical metamaterials, or computational mechanics Evidence of potential for excellence in research Excellent written and oral communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Atomic-catalysts-and-Machine-Learning-_R00025731": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Atomic catalysts and Machine Learning)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. Join the laboratory of Fan Hongjin at SPMS. We are seeking a Research Fellow to contribute to a project focused on focused on data-driven discovery of atomic catalysts. Key Responsibilities: Theoretical predictions using DFT and machine learning, and mechanistic understanding of atomic catalysts Investigation of mechanism by in-situ and/or operando techniques and theoretical calculations Coordinate the collaboration with other researchers in this project to maintain steady progress, and provide support to the research group on related experiments Provide support to the project management and lab infrastructure, including procurement, setting up battery fabrication line, set up equipment for in-situ and/or operando characterizations, annual and final project reports Make regular progress reports to PI Write one proposal based on results obtained from this project for external grant Job Requirements: A PhD degree in material sciences or applied physics, with focus on renewable energy Evidenced experience in DFT and machine learning especially its application in atomic catalysts Strong publication record on the topic of renewable energy materials especially electrocatalysis Entry level candidates are welcome to apply Strong motivation to undertake grand challenges in multidisciplinary subjects Excellent team player who is capable and willing to provide supports in a dynamic and interdisciplinary environment The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Wireless-Cellular-Security-_R00025729": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Wireless/Cellular Security)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe invite suitable candidate to join a strong research team in Temasek Laboratories@NTU with the following requisites: Key Responsibilities:  The candidate is expected to conduct and guide research in Wireless and Cellular Security, in particular the discovery of novel wireless attacks and their detection and mitigations. The candidate is expected to conduct both theoretical development of methods and experiment design to validate the developed methods. Other research responsibilities include supervising junior researchers/interns/students, carrying out detailed literature reviews and assessment of the state-of-the-art technologies. planning and executing detailed R&D activities to meet project objectives and deadlines, generating novel scientific or technological concepts for application of breakthrough nature and contributing to research proposals. Administrative responsibilities may include safety, asset management and other aspects related to being a member of Temasek Labs@NTU. Job Requirements:  PhD degree in Computer Science, Computer & Electronics Engineering or other related fields Strong background and knowledge in at least one or preferably more of the following fields: Cybersecurity, Deep Learning and software engineering with at least 3-5 years of research experience (including PhD training) in related fields. Proven track record in research and development of cybersecurity and/or Deep Learning technologies. Strong publication record in top cybersecurity or systems conferences/journals (e.g., USENIX Security, NDSS, ASE, TSE, TIFS, ICSE, FSE, ICST etc. Strong programming skills in C/C++, python etc. Knowledge of Electrical or Software Engineering and Cybersecurity are plus. Good writing skills for writing proposals, reports and publications in good academic journals We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Administrative-Support_R00025728": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Renaissance Engineering Programme is NTU’s signature programme that aims to nurture engineering leaders with an entrepreneurial spirit to serve society. The programme covers a broad spectrum of multidisciplinary subjects bridging engineering, business and humanities. This position plays a key role in managing the undergraduate academic and examination matters under REP. It will also play a pivotal role in providing administrative support for overseas exchange to students including pre-departure matters and professional attachment matters. The position is also required to support the annual admission interview exercise, participate in major outreach events and activities and work closely with the student club in social media publicity. 1.   Provide Academic Support for Undergraduate Degree Provide quality administrative services to both REP faculty and students to ensure a smooth delivery of the undergraduate programme including handling class scheduling. Manage the administration of course registration activities, class time-tabling including liaison with students. Work closely with the Engineering Schools and College of Computing and Data Science on the timetabling for the core and electives. Organise town halls and prepare notes of meetings and provide support for department meetings. Assist in the examination scheduling and provide support where necessary. Assist in the updating of students’ records. 2.   Provide Administrative Support for Students on Overseas Exchange Assist with the administrative support for overseas exchange programme related to pre-departure. Assist with post exchange support including queries and surveys. Provide academic and administrative support including assigning supervisors for students’ professional attachment. Track and update student records related to professional attachment. 3.    Provide Administrative Support for Annual Admissions Exercise and Outreach Activities Provide administrative support for the annual admissions exercise such as interviews scheduling and engaging applicants post admission interviews and attend to their queries. Provide administrative support for external student outreach events and internal student engagement activities. Work closely with the student club in social media publicity. Requirements: Bachelor degree in Business Administration or equivalent. Prior experience in managing undergraduate programme in an institute of higher learning. Good knowledge and shows some interest in engineering subjects. 3-5 years of relevant working experience preferably in a tertiary institution. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with cultural sensitivity towards staff and students of different cultural backgrounds. Meticulous, resourceful and possess excellent organisational and project management skills and be able to thrive and multi-task in a fast-paced environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--GNSS-Processing-and-Analysis-_R00025722": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (GNSS Processing and Analysis)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) is a University Research Institute at Nanyang Technological University Singapore that conducts fundamental research on earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis, and climate change in and around Southeast Asia, towards safer and more sustainable societies. EOS maintains a regional network of geophysical observation stations in collaboration with neighboring countries in Southeast Asia, that are supported by the EOS Centre for Geohazard Observations, as well as a Remote Sensing Lab (EOS-RS). Computational resources are available through a dedicated cluster and collaboration with the High-Performance Computing Centre of NTU. In addition, EOS hosts state-of-the-art analytical facilities for petrological and geochemical analysis, and a Community Engagement office that co-creates learning opportunities for a range of audiences to promote a safer and more sustainable future. EOS seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We are looking for a Research Fellow (RF) to join EOS. The successful candidate will work under the supervision of Asst Prof Lujia FENG and focus on GNSS data processing and analysis for tectonic deformation studies. The primary purpose of this position is to conduct high-quality research using geodetic observations to quantify crustal deformation, characterize fault-slip processes, and improve our understanding of earthquake hazards. The candidate will develop and maintain GNSS processing workflows, contribute to the interpretation of geodetic observations, and support ongoing research projects within the tectonics and geodesy research programme. The RF is also expected to contribute actively to other research activities within EOS . Key Responsibilities: Develop and implement an automated post-processing workflow for GNSS data analysis using multiple software packages, including PRIDE PPP-AR, GAMIT/GLOBK, and GipsyX Process raw GNSS data, analyze position time series, and estimate station velocities and associated uncertainties Compile and assess published GNSS velocity fields for Southeast Asia Contribute to the integration of InSAR and GNSS observations and the development of deformation fields, strain-rate maps, and geodetic models Present scientific results at local and international meetings and conferences Write up research results for publication in reputable international journals Assist with data management, documentation, and the preparation of technical reports Participate actively in research meetings, project discussions, and progress reporting Job Requirements: PhD in geodesy or related field At least 3 years of relevant experiences in GNSS data processing Strong computation skills with experience using MATLAB and/or Python Excellent written and verbal communications skills Evidence of being able to work both independently and collaboratively, with a strong team spirit We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Safety---Governance-Engineer--SAGE-_R00025725": {
      "title": "AI Safety & Governance Engineer (SAGE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. The AI Safety and Governance Engineering (SAGE) function ensures LLM/GenAI systems deployed through AI Singapore's 100 Experiments (100E) programme are safe, secure, and compliant before delivery to project sponsors. We are seeking an AI Safety & Governance Engineer to join the SAGE team. In this role, you will execute safety testing, conduct red teaming exercises, review system architectures for vulnerabilities, and support governance practices. You will also mentor AIAP apprentices on responsible AI practices. The incumbent will work across diverse industry projects while contributing to Singapore's AI safety standards and practices. Duties & Responsibilities: Execute automated LLM safety testing pipelines integrated with GitLab CI/CD as mandatory gate before project delivery. Conduct red teaming and adversarial testing: prompt injection, jailbreaking, data leakage, RAG poisoning, multi-turn attacks. Review LLM system architectures (agentic, multimodal, RAG) for security vulnerabilities and provide design recommendations. Document vulnerabilities with severity ratings, reproduction steps, and remediation guidance. Support compliance with AI safety standards: ISO 42001, NIST AI RMF, OWASP LLM Top 10, MITRE ATLAS, Singapore Model AI Governance Framework. Train and mentor AIAP apprentices on responsible AI engineering during deep-skilling and project phases. Contribute to AI Singapore's community-building activities through talks, workshops, and documentation. Requirements: Degree with at least 2-4 years of work experience. Appointment at senior level may be considered based on relevant experience. We welcome applicants from all disciplines who can demonstrate the following skills: LLM/GenAI Systems: Working knowledge of LLM architectures, prompt engineering, RAG implementations, and API integration. Security Testing: Experience with vulnerability assessment, adversarial testing, or penetration testing. Understanding of LLM-specific vulnerabilities (prompt injection, jailbreaking, data leakage). Systems Design: Ability to review system architectures for security vulnerabilities and recommend secure design patterns for agentic, multimodal, and RAG applications. Software Engineering: Proficient Python skills with commitment to clean, maintainable code. Experience with testing frameworks (pytest, unittest). DevOps & Automation: Familiarity with Git, Docker, and CI/CD pipelines (GitLab or GitHub). Documentation: Strong technical writing skills for vulnerability reports and compliance evidence. Collaborative Mentor: Eager to guide AIAP apprentices and contribute to SAGE's supportive team culture. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Librarian---Senior-Assistant-Manager--Service-Innovation---Excellence--User-Experience---Space-Transformation-_R00025723": {
      "title": "Librarian / Senior Assistant Manager, Service Innovation & Excellence (User Experience & Space Transformation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a leading research-intensive university known for its strong focus on innovation, interdisciplinary learning, and creating meaningful impact through education and research.   The Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) plays an important role in supporting students across their academic journey, from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. Working closely with schools, colleges, and other partners across the University, SASD helps to create a seamless, enriching, and student-centred experience at NTU.   Within this broader mission, NTU Libraries , under the Office of Information, Knowledge and Library Services (OIKLS) , provide essential learning, research, and collaborative environments that support the University community. We are seeking an experienced and forward-looking Librarian / Senior Assistant Manager to shape user-centred library services, drive service innovation, and enhance physical and hybrid library environments across NTU.   This is an exciting opportunity to make visible impact on how students, faculty, and researchers experience library spaces and services. The role combines leadership in operations, user experience, space transformation, and continuous improvement, offering the chance to contribute meaningfully to NTU’s teaching, learning, and research mission.   Key responsibilities Lead and enhance library operations and service delivery across key user touchpoints, driving improvements in service quality, consistency, and user experience. Shape and deliver space transformation and user experience initiatives that support evolving patterns of learning, collaboration, discovery, and wellbeing. Lead service innovation and continuous improvement efforts informed by user feedback, operational insights, and emerging trends. Develop and guide staff and student assistants to support operational readiness, service excellence, and the effective implementation of change. Requirements A bachelor’s degree in any discipline; a postgraduate qualification in library and information studies or a related field will be preferred. At least 5 years of relevant experience in academic, research, public, or other service-oriented environments, including supervisory experience. Experience in operations, user-facing services, service improvement, project leadership, or change implementation. Strong communication, stakeholder engagement, analytical, and people management skills. At NTU, you will join a collaborative and forward-looking university environment committed to continuous learning, innovation, and service excellence. This role offers the opportunity to work across diverse library settings, partner stakeholders across the University, and contribute to improvements that have meaningful and visible impact on the campus community. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Robotics-_R00025716": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Robotics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a talented and responsible researcher to support the scientific research and the engineering practice in perception and embodied intelligence. Key Responsibilities: The Research Associate will work on a project to conduct research on development of mobile and bimanual robotic manipulation system used in household service and manufacturing. The roles of this position include: Develop robotic foundation models for general mobile manipulation based on vision-language-action models Develop efficient manipulation learning framework from human instructional videos and reduce the data demand for policy learning Develop a mobile bimanual manipulation system to complete diverse tasks in household environment and in manufacturing deployment scenarios Job Requirements Master’s in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Computer Science or related field 1-year research experience in related area Expertise in robotic manipulation systems Knowledge in robotic foundation models  Publication track record is an advantage Proficiency in basics of programming languages such as ROS and Python Excellent communication skills, written and verbal – able to communicate complex concepts clearly and accurately We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Career-Coach_R00025718": {
      "title": "Career Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTo support NTU Education 2025 and beyond, this role is critical as part of the (Career & Attachment Office) CAO’s strategy to develop NTU students into future-ready graduates.  This strategic role of a Career Coach (with a dual role as a Career Business Partner to Schools and Colleges) guides, coaches and empowers NTU undergraduate and postgraduate students in their personal self-discovery, career exploration and professional development, thereby enhancing their employability and employment aligned to their career interests and goals. Responsibilities: Provide 1:1 personalised career coaching and small group coaching. Guide students in exploring their career preferences, strengths, values and interests. Administer self-assessment and career profiling tools, where necessary, to enable students to understand themselves better. Coach students in their early career exploration and planning over the 4 years at NTU. Provide students with information and resources on career-related topics (job search strategies, resume writing, interview skills, industry skills frameworks, career workshops etc). Conduct Mandatory ML0004 Small Group resume critique and mock interview coaching sessions. Coach students in strategies for internship and job search. Engage students, student groups, and faculty members in career awareness and preparation matters. Customize and design school-specific career initiatives and programmes to increase students' employability (e.g., career and industry talks, alumni-sharing sessions, and bespoke workshops). Collaborator and Point of Contact (POC) to respective School’s leadership on career-related matters. Involve in Schools’ outreach programmes (e.g. Career Day). Job Requirements: A recognised degree with 9 to 10 years of experience, including at least 5 years’ experience in career coaching/counselling/career services/graduate recruitment/human resources/executive search/learning and development. Change agent and constantly initiating new ideas within the College-level team of Career Coaches to increase awareness and CAO’s services to the students. Relevant career coaching certification(s). Possess qualifications/certification in self-assessment and career profiling tools. Experienced coach with excellent coaching skills and ability to engage young adults. Knowledgeable in traditional and technology/AI-enabled career coaching tools. Knowledgeable of industries, workplace and employer expectations.   Strong initiative, self-motivated, and focused on helping students achieve career success. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Competent in conducting/presenting career-related workshops. Active listener with strong critical thinking and decision-making skills. Meticulous with strong organisation and administration skills. Excellent team player with strong interpersonal skills. Proficient in MS Office tools. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Support-and-Care_R00025715": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Support and Care",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe ideal candidate for this position will play a key role in ensuring that the highest level of care and support is provided to members in the OneNTU community. The incumbent will coordinate efforts for care and support, and ensure the relevant processes and operations are conducted in accordance with the University’s policies and protocols. Job Responsibilities: Ensure efficiency and quality of care and support for the NTU Community. Manage critical incidents within a team to ensure that emergency interventions provided to employees, students, and NOK are well-coordinated.  Put in place specialised case management and safety plans and implement them to ensure timely management of the cases and quick resolution. Coordinate follow-up care and support with internal and external stakeholders to ensure continuity of care. Capture and maintain care and support information, data, and records for analysis and reporting. Monitor support and care channels and respond promptly to queries. Develop/enhance support and care networks to ensure needs of the NTU community are met. Facilitate communications between schools/halls and University-level offices in the management of cases. Assist in implementing regular communications with NTU stakeholders and external resources to facilitate case management and ensure seamless workflows, and to improve awareness and understanding of issues and concerns within the NTU caregiver network. Assist in the implementation of specialist training and development to enhance the community’s competencies for care and support. Assist in the development and implementation of wellbeing services, volunteer programmes, and training programmes to enhance wellbeing capacity and capabilities in NTU.   Ensure that Effective Levels of Care for students and employees are met and standardised across NTU. Provide guidance to stakeholders in policies, procedures, guidelines, and templates to facilitate support and care processes.  Assist in the dissemination of relevant data and data analysis to NTU stakeholders to ensure the caregiving network in NTU can make informed decisions for support and care programmes and services for their own employee and student population.   Requirements: Educational Qualification(s) Minimally a bachelor’s degree in any related field from a recognised University, preferably in psychology, counselling, or social work. Knowledge Required Fluent with data collection and management. Knowledge of analytic methods, approaches, tools, and implementation will be advantageous. Proficient with Microsoft 365 and technological tools and information systems relevant in a university setting. Strong proficiency (spoken and written) in Mandarin will be advantageous as t his role involves frequent communication and engagement with Mandarin-speaking students and members of the public Prior training in critical incident management and/or prevention will be advantageous. Relevant Experience At least 4 to 6 years of experience working directly in care and support services, preferably in the tertiary education sector. Proven track record in care and support, case management and crisis management will be highly advantageous. Skills & Competencies Successful experience with stakeholder management, able to work with colleagues from different backgrounds and departments, as well as stakeholders external to NTU. Other Personal Attributes A strong commitment and passion towards wellbeing and support. Excellent team player with strong verbal and written communication skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Laboratory-Services_R00025713": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Laboratory Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the school is renowned for its high academic standards and research. It is one of the largest EEE schools in the world, with over 120 faculty members and more than 5,000 students, including around 2,000 graduate students. We invite applications for the position of Senior Assistant Manager. The incumbent shall provide teaching technical excellence across teaching laboratories in the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering. Key Responsibilities:  Provide administrative and technical support for all laboratory users. Manage Procurement for teaching labs. Asset management and maintaining proper records for inventory auditing. Support all assigned laboratory teaching classes. Familiar with Python and Linux is a plus. Experience in risk management, workplace safety and health (i.e. ISO 45001) is a plus. Assist the Safety Committee on laboratory safety matters. Perform any other duties assigned by the school. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Electrical and Electronic Engineering is preferred. Minimum 3 years of relevant experience in an educational institution is preferred. Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Highly motivated, initiative, and proactive. IT savvy, proficient in MS Office applications. Meticulous and organized, with the ability to multi-task. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-Masters-of-Science-in-Psychology--SSS-_R00025499": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in Masters of Science in Psychology (SSS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences invites applications for Part-Time Lecturers (PTLs) to teach in the Master of Science in Psychology (MScP) programme. We are looking for PTLs to serve as primary instructors for both foundational and specialisation courses within the MScP curriculum. Successful candidates will be responsible for course and curriculum development, course delivery, student consultation and marking duties. Qualification and requirement: Successful candidates will hold a doctorate-level or a masters-level qualification in an appropriate Psychological field or other related fields, be able to demonstrate effective teaching and training of postgraduate students. Candidates with specialisations in one or more of these fields are particularly welcome: Community Health Psychology, Forensic Psychology, Neuropsychology and Thanatology. Evidence of excellence in teaching and/or clinical supervision is highly desirable. Successful candidates will be expected to contribute significantly to teaching and development of multiple courses at the postgraduate level, including foundational and specialisation courses. Essential selection criteria: The attainment of a higher degree (PhD/DPhil/Masters) in Psychology or a related discipline Experience and interest in teaching postgraduate psychology students, with a strong and demonstrable commitment to the organisation and delivery of teaching, particularly in one or more areas of Community Health Psychology, Forensic Psychology, Neuropsychology and Thanatology Excellent communication and interpersonal skills relevant to teaching and pastoral care • Willingness and ability to contribute to the overall objectives of the Programme and School, working collaboratively with others Desirable selection criteria: Experience of academic administration For further information about the School, and MSc in Psychology, at NTU, please refer to the following website: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sss/graduate-education/MScP To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience, preferred course) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--3D-Reconstruction-_R00025701": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (3D Reconstruction)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Assistant to conduct research on 3D reconstruction, with a particular focus on developing advanced 3D Gaussian Splatting techniques for dynamic and streaming scenarios. The role will involve designing and implementing novel algorithms for efficient, high-fidelity 3D scene reconstruction and representation, including applications in embodied environments where an agent must continuously perceive, update, and reason about its surrounding world. Key Responsibilities: The research assistant will focus on the following tasks Data collection and processing Conducting experiments and analyzing results Providing general support for the lab Job Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, or related field Knowledge and experience in world model, computer vision and deep learning Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in basics of programming languages such as Python Self-Motivated and takes initiative We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--IC-Design-and-academic-_R00025699": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (IC Design and academic)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are hiring a Research Fellow in IC design to design and realize high speed high efficiency analog/RF ICs. The Research Fellow is also expected to support teaching activities as required by the school. Key Responsibilities: This role involves working on innovative solutions in the field of RF power management IC. The key responsibilities of this position include: Design, implement and test RF power management ICs or other analog/mixed signal/RF ICs. Development cycle including circuit design, simulation, modeling, layout, verification and measurements. Develop scripts and algorithms for analog IC design Prepare research papers/reports/technology disclosures, etc Assist the school in various teaching activities, including instructing or supervision of labs and tutorials Job Requirements: Ph.D./M.Eng/MSc in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Statistics, or other related fields.  Entry Level candidates are welcome to apply At least 2 years of relevant experiences in IC design/Electronics  Familiar with Analog/Power Management/RF/ADC/DAC IC design Proficiency in Cadence Proficiency in Python and Matlab Experience in implementing algorithms for machine learning Good written and oral communication skills We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Research-Associate--Computer-Science-_R00025707": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Research Associate (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow’. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. We are seeking a motivated Research Assistant or Research Associate to join the Parallel Systems Lab ( https://psl-ntu.github.io ) at NTU’s CCDS. The role focuses on designing, developing, and evaluating efficient, scalable systems for modern multi-agent HPC-AI workflows. Responsibilities include workload analysis, system prototyping, benchmarking, and experimental validation on local and national supercomputing platforms. The RA will collaborate with faculty and domain scientists to address real-world application needs and contribute to cutting-edge research at the intersection of AI and HPC. This position offers hands-on experience with advanced HPC technologies and large-scale computing environments. Key Responsibilities: Analyze and characterize emerging multi-agent AI and HPC workloads to identify performance, scalability, and system-level challenges. Design, implement, and prototype efficient systems and infrastructure for large-scale AI/HPC workflows. Conduct benchmarking and experimental evaluation on local and national supercomputing platforms, analyzing performance and scalability. Contribute to research papers, technical reports, and presentations for internal reviews and external conferences or journals. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s or master’s degree in Computer Science or a related discipline. Good knowledge of agentic AI/AI workflows, parallel computing, algorithms, and system performance analysis and optimization. Proficiency in programming languages such as C/C++ and Python. Demonstrated ability to conduct research, solve complex technical problems, and develop innovative solutions. Experience with parallel systems, machine learning/AI, or performance benchmarking is highly desirable. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in multidisciplinary research teams. Strong analytical, problem-solving, teamwork, and written and verbal communication skills. Proactive, self-motivated, and willing to learn new technologies and research areas. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoctoral-Researcher-Fellow--Chemistry-_R00025705": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher/Fellow (Chemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) is an interdisciplinary joint school under College of Engineering and College of Science at NTU Singapore The Nicewicz group at CCEB is seeking to hire a Postdoctoral Researcher/Fellow to facilitate research in the development of novel and broadly useful sustainable molecular transformations for the synthesis of complex molecules using single electron redox processes. Key Responsibilities: Daily experiments and analysis of the collected data To supervise junior graduate students and undergraduate researchers To submit weekly reports on the experimental results  Prepare manuscript(s) as a result of the research J ob Requirements: Bachelor’s / Master’s degree and Conferring PhD student in Chemistry or related field At least 5 years of relevant experiences in organic chemistry / technical hands-on experience in reaction development Good written and oral communication skills Competent in management of projects/teams of students and presentation of data. Interpersonal skills: ability to work independently, to lead teams, develop solutions under strict timelines, meticulous and excellent organizational/time management skills Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Computer-Engineering-Computer-Science-Electronics-Engineering-_R00025702": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research and development in computer vision, multimodal learning, medical/industrial imaging, and related AI4X topics. Design, implement, train, and evaluate deep learning models and research prototypes using Python/PyTorch and related tools. Prepare and curate research datasets, conduct quantitative and qualitative experiments, and perform rigorous result analysis. Review relevant literature and identify suitable baselines, datasets, evaluation protocols, and research opportunities. Contribute to technical reports, project deliverables, research papers, code repositories, and presentations. Work closely with the PI and collaborators, participate in research meetings, and support collaborative research activities. Perform other research-related duties as assigned by the PI in support of the project objectives. Job Requirements: Preferably Bachelor’s degree in computer engineering, Computer Science, Electronics Engineering or equivalent. Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills In-depth knowledge relevant to the project domain. Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research. The ability and willingness to adapt and incorporate novel ideas and approaches in scientific industry. Demonstrated ability to formulate hypothesis and design effective experimental plans. Ability to design and implement new experimental methods. High-level expertise in the required experiment or modelling methods. Ability to initiate collaboration research in multidisciplinary team. Oversee and report project progress. Ability and willingness to work some flexible hours. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Lipid-Nanoparticle-Delivery-Advanced-Imaging---Membrane-Biophysics-_R00025704": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Lipid Nanoparticle Delivery/Advanced Imaging & Membrane Biophysics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) invites applications for the position of Research Fellow in Lipid Nanoparticle Delivery, Advanced Imaging and Membrane Biophysics . The Nano-Bio Interface Lab led by Assoc. Prof. Wenting Zhao at the School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology, Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore), investigates how nanoscale membrane organization, geometry, and biophysical properties regulate cellular and biomolecular processes in disease and therapeutic delivery. The laboratory has established strong capabilities in nanofabrication, advanced fluorescence and super-resolution microscopy, quantitative cell imaging, and biomimetic membrane systems. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to contribute to an interdisciplinary research programme focused on understanding the cellular entry, intracellular trafficking, membrane interaction, and endosomal escape of lipid nanoparticles (LNPs) for next-generation RNA and nucleic-acid therapeutics. The project will integrate advanced live-cell imaging, super-resolution microscopy, single-particle tracking, supported lipid bilayers (SLBs) and other artificial membrane systems, together with LNP engineering and characterization, to elucidate how nanoscale membrane properties regulate LNP–membrane interactions and intracellular delivery. The work will provide mechanistic insights for the rational design of more effective delivery systems, particularly for challenging therapeutic cell types. The Research Fellow will take a significant role in leading research projects, developing new experimental approaches, training junior researchers, preparing scientific publications and research grants, and coordinating interdisciplinary collaborations. Key Responsibilities: Develop and lead research projects investigating LNP–membrane interactions, intracellular trafficking, and endosomal escape. Establish and apply advanced fluorescence imaging approaches, including super-resolution microscopy, live-cell imaging, and single-particle tracking. Develop and utilize supported lipid bilayers, lipid vesicles, and other artificial or biomimetic membrane systems to study nanoparticle–membrane interactions. Perform LNP preparation, characterization, cellular delivery, and quantitative evaluation of intracellular trafficking and cargo release. Develop quantitative image-analysis approaches for particle tracking, membrane dynamics, and intracellular transport. Analyse experimental data, review relevant literature, and prepare manuscripts for publication in scientific journals. Contribute to research grant applications, scientific presentations, and project reports. Collaborate closely with researchers from engineering, cell biology, biophysics, imaging, and therapeutic-delivery backgrounds. Supervise and train junior researchers, students, and visiting scientists. Assist with laboratory operations, equipment maintenance, research coordination, and compliance with laboratory safety requirements. Job Requirements: A Ph.D. in bioengineering, biomedical engineering, biophysics, cell biology, chemical engineering, materials science, nanotechnology, pharmaceutical sciences, or a closely related discipline. Strong research experience in advanced fluorescence microscopy and quantitative imaging is highly preferred. Hands-on experience with super-resolution microscopy, such as STED, SIM, PALM/STORM, expansion microscopy, or related techniques, is highly desirable. Experience in single-particle tracking, live-cell particle trafficking, or quantitative image analysis is highly preferred. Experience with supported lipid bilayers, lipid vesicles, artificial membranes, membrane reconstitution, or other biomimetic membrane systems is highly desirable. Experience with lipid nanoparticles, liposomes, RNA/nucleic-acid delivery, nanoparticle formulation, or drug-delivery technologies is strongly preferred. Research experience in membrane biophysics, intracellular trafficking, endocytosis, endosomal biology, or nanoparticle–cell interactions would be advantageous. Experience in mammalian cell culture, molecular/cell biology, and biochemical assays is desirable. Programming or quantitative data-analysis experience, including particle tracking or microscopy image analysis, would be advantageous. Candidates should demonstrate strong scientific independence, problem-solving ability, communication skills, and the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary team. A strong publication record, including first-author publications in reputable peer-reviewed journals, is preferred. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTUOne-North-Campus-Singapore/Portfolio-Manager_R00025703": {
      "title": "Portfolio Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Investment Office, who manages the University’s global investment fund, is looking to expand its existing investment team. The successful candidate(s) will be responsible for managing or co-managing the investment fund’s multi-asset portfolio, which spans both public and private markets across credit, equities and hedge funds. Depending on the asset class assigned, the Portfolio Manager/Analyst may invest directly or via external managers. The role involves developing a structured investment framework to generate excess returns over benchmark while managing risks, conducting research/due diligence on potential investments, guiding asset allocation decisions, trade execution as well as monitoring investment performance. This position offers opportunities for the successful candidate to interact actively with and learn from global/local top tier managers including their portfolio managers, CIOs and CEOs. The right candidate should be decisive, enjoy navigating complex environments and relish the challenge of building conviction in investment themes and translating them into investment plans or action.         Requirements At least 5-10 years in Fixed Income, Hedge Funds, Equities, Private Markets or investment banking. Demonstrates knowledge and understanding of business fundamentals, financial analysis and asset valuations. Proficient in economics, financial modelling, statistical analysis and investment research tools. Excellent oral and written skills are required for communicating investment proposals. Possesses at least a bachelor’s degree in sciences, mathematics, finance or economics. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Associate-Assistant-Professor-of-Microbiome_R00025698-1": {
      "title": "Associate/Assistant Professor of Microbiome",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-05\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nACADEMIC FACULTY APPOINTMENT: The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine A tenure-track Associate/Assistant Professor of Microbiome at Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine is expected to contribute to the development of research and teaching at the School. He/She is expected to undertake high quality internationally leading research in the area of microbiology pertaining to either microbiome or microbial bioinformatics within the Microbiome Medicine Research Programme, in line with the overarching research strategy of Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine, in addition to any other duties as assigned by the Vice Dean, Research and Dean.   Key Responsibilities   Job Purpose: The appointee will be expected to undertake high quality research in the area of microbiology pertaining to either microbiome or microbial bioinformatics, in line with the research strategy of the School and in conjunction with other recent appointments, obtain research funding and supervise research staff and students. The appointee is expected to undertake teaching and educational responsibilities for the training of medical students and postgraduate research students. Teaching methods will include extensive use of team-based learning and e-learning. The appointee is expected to contribute to integration of science relating to microbiology into the MBBS curriculum and to ensure the delivery of excellence in these areas, including the team-based delivery of the curriculum. Primary Activities: Undertake high quality research activities by sustaining a personal research plan, developing innovative research proposals and funding bids, managing and undertaking research activities, publishing in international peer-reviewed journals, reviewing manuscripts and grant applications when appropriate. Seek competitive grant and collaborative industry funding to develop a sustainable research programme. Contribute to, support and develop teaching and educational activity at undergraduate level and supervise undergraduate students. Contribute to, support and develop teaching and educational activity at undergraduate and graduate level and supervise undergraduate and graduate students. Develop and support research projects (including interdisciplinary) with other faculty in the field of Microbiome Medicine at LKCMedicine and across the wider NTU community. These may include research that pertains to all health aspects relating to microbiology, especially those directed at unravelling the mechanisms of microbial pathogenesis, host-microbiome interactions, nutritional or environmental interaction, bacterial and non-bacterial microbiome, clinical trials or bioinformatics related to microbiome. Supervise and mentor junior faculty members and research staff. Participate in academic committees and meet other administrative requirements as appropriate. Job Descriptions cannot be exhaustive, and the appointee may be required to undertake other duties which are broadly in line with the above key responsibilities as assigned by the Vice-Dean, Research and Dean. Requirements: Qualifications, Knowledge and Experience: MBBS/MD and/or PhD degree(s) Relevant postdoctoral or clinical experience Significant experience and outstanding record of translational clinical research and teaching with a high level of scientific achievement, productivity and impact in the field of Microbiology or Microbiome Medicine Experience in working with human microbiome and metagenomic data would be an advantage Management and Teamwork: Ability to lead and work as part of a multidisciplinary team Ability to work co-operatively with medical and non-medical staff Ability to supervise research staff and students Communicating and Influencing: Ability to communicate effectively with staff and students Ability to motivate others Strong presentation skills Ability to work in a team Desirable Attributes: Experience and desire to participate in undergraduate and postgraduate medical education and training. Demonstrated ability to develop teams and to create networks. Fully conversant with patient-centred approach to modern medicine and the use of new technologies in both education and patient care. Understanding of the academic and administrative needs of internationally recognized universitites. Ability to work in and develop teams and to create networks at both a national and international level. Track record of having supervised graduate students to successful completion of PhDs. Time Commitment The level of effort for this appointment is at 1.0 full time equivalent (FTE) employment. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Executive---Senior-Executive--Ecosystem-Operations---Engagement--co11ab--LKCMedicine-_R00025686-1": {
      "title": "Executive / Senior Executive, Ecosystem Operations & Engagement, co11ab [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nco11ab is Singapore's first biomedtech incubator located within Novena Health City. Established through a tripartite partnership between NTU, A*STAR and NHG, co11ab accelerates the translation of biomedical and healthcare innovations by connecting startups with clinicians, researchers, investors, industry partners and healthcare institutions. As a collaborative innovation hub, co11ab provides access to laboratories, makerspaces, clinical expertise, strategic partnerships and commercialisation opportunities, enabling startups to progress from concept and prototype development through clinical validation and market adoption. Joining co11ab means becoming part of a dynamic ecosystem dedicated to advancing healthcare innovation and improving patient outcomes. Reporting to the Deputy Director, the Executive / Senior Executive (Ecosystem Operations & Engagement) is responsible for supporting community operations, member engagement and the delivery of ecosystem activities. The role coordinates programmes, outreach initiatives, marketing communications and day-to-day operational activities to deliver a seamless experience for members, partners and visitors. Key Responsibilities: Community & Member Engagement Manage member onboarding, engagement and community-building activities. Support the administration of the co11ab membership programme and member communications. Build positive relationships with members, startups and ecosystem partners while gathering feedback to enhance member experience. Ecosystem Operations Coordinate ecosystem visits, delegations, stakeholder meetings and visitor management. Maintain CRM, membership and engagement records. Ensure operational readiness for meetings, programmes and community activities. Programmes, Events & Outreach Coordinate the delivery of programmes, workshops, networking events and outreach activities. Liaise with internal teams, speakers, vendors and partners to ensure successful execution. Support conferences, exhibitions, roadshows and other ecosystem engagement initiatives. Marketing & Communications Coordinate updates to the co11ab website, digital platforms and marketing collateral. Support LinkedIn, newsletters and community communications using approved content. Coordinate promotional materials and publicity for programmes and outreach activities. Operational Excellence Coordinate administrative and operational support for co11ab activities. Maintain accurate records, documentation and operational processes. Identify opportunities to improve operational efficiency, community engagement and member experience. Undertake other duties assigned by the Deputy Director. Success Indicators High member and stakeholder satisfaction. Successful delivery of programmes and outreach activities. Timely marketing communications and website updates. Accurate membership and operational records. Continuous improvements to community engagement and operational efficiency. Qualifications & Experience Diploma or degree in Business Administration, Communications, Marketing, Events Management or a related discipline. 2–4 years of relevant experience in community engagement, stakeholder management, programme coordination, events or operations. Experience in an innovation hub, incubator, accelerator, healthcare, research or higher education environment is an advantage. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the confidence to engage professionally with startups, industry partners, government agencies and senior management. Strong communication skills are essential. Strong interpersonal, organizational and stakeholder management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities. Proactive, service-oriented and able to work independently as well as collaboratively across teams. Proficient in Microsoft Office; familiarity with CRM, website content management or event management platforms is advantageous. Core Competencies includes Communication & Stakeholder Engagement, Community & Member Experience, Programme & Event Coordination, Marketing & Communications Coordination, Planning, Organization & Problem Solving and Customer Service & Teamwork Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Faculty-Engagement---Value-Propositions_R00025696-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Faculty Engagement & Value Propositions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU University Advancement Office (UAO) supports the University’s giving mission by fostering meaningful relationships and strategic partnerships with philanthropists, alumni, business community partners, corporations, foundations and friends that result in goodwill and philanthropy towards education and research that underpin a shared sustainable future. The position is responsible for building compelling donor centric propositions and enhancing the fundraising competency of faculty and units to advance the philanthropic cause for the Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU). Key Responsibilities include the following: Build strong working relationships with faculty colleagues to develop new funding propositions of the Colleges & Schools. Aligning funding needs or offerings from the faculty to the giving interests of prospective donors, to drive new gift opportunities. Support faculties in managing conversations on new gift opportunities between stakeholders within the University, as well as prospective donors. Create articulate and compelling proposals and donor centric collaterals for donor engagement. Supporting Senior Leadership for gift cases. Provide administrative and operational support for advancing gift purposes where required. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in any discipline. Proficient in relationship management, editorial writing, presentation and product packaging capabilities. At least 8 years’ progressive career track record in business development and/or marketing role demonstrating engagement with senior stakeholders. Ability to position technical innovations into go-to-market messages. Experience in Higher Education or Business Development will be an added advantage. Values philanthropy for higher education and is self-motivated to contribute for community building. Team-oriented with a positive “can-do” attitude. Demonstrates discretion in preparing, disclosing and handling information of a confidential and sensitive nature. Ability to perform duties with tact, maturity and independent judgment. A strong track record of independently managing complex stakeholder engagements and advancing strategic opportunities. Candidates with less experience may be considered for the Manager level. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Mechanical-Engineering---Nanotechnology-_R00025695": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Mechanical Engineering / Nanotechnology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) is a research centre conducting fundamental and applied research in all aspects related to additive manufacturing. Our vision is to be the world leader in 3D Printing and a wellspring of knowledge, delivering state of the art and innovative solutions to the industry. SC3DP is at the forefront of developing advanced technologies and high-impact research in areas such biomedical, construction, aerospace, marine and offshore. It is one of the very few research centres globally with multi-sector 3D printing expertise. SC3DP’s research achievements, high-level industry collaboration, comprehensive facilities and resources have positioned it as a leading hub for 3D printing research and innovation globally. We are looking for a highly motivated Research Fellow to join our multidisciplinary team aiming to develop the next generation of metal multimaterial additive manufacturing. The successful candidate will work on the development of a novel laser powder bed fusion system, focusing on automation and control aspects of this novel machine and the implementation of an in-process monitoring system. This role is central to our efforts to push the boundaries of AM material innovation and supports NTU’s commitment to sustainable and impactful technological development. Key Responsibilities: Conduct systematic experimental campaigns in multimaterial LPBF, generating process, material, and structural data to support model development, validation, and process consolidation. Develop and apply physics-based and data-driven modeling frameworks to describe, predict, and optimize multimaterial LPBF processes, integrating in-situ monitoring, process parameters, material combinations, and resulting microstructural and structural outcomes. Design and optimize multimaterial and functionally graded LPBF components, including lightweight lattice and architected structures, incorporating DfAM guidelines and performance-driven criteria. Perform experimental studies to evaluate powder bed behaviour, melt pool dynamics, and inter-material transition zones, assessing their impact on process stability, densification, and component performance. Analyse experimental and modeling results to establish robust process–material–structure relationships and support informed optimization strategies. Support automation, control, and in-process monitoring development for a novel multimaterial LPBF platform. Document research findings, prepare technical reports, and contribute to publications and presentations for internal and external stakeholders. Support project planning, timelines, and delivery, ensuring milestones are met and solutions meet industrial standards for quality and safety. Requirements: PhD in Mechanical Engineering, Nanotechnology, or a closely related discipline. Strong background in the mathematical modeling of multiscale and multiphysics phenomena, including proven application of dimensional analysis, fractal analysis, and hybrid physics–AI approaches. Demonstrated ability to interpret complex process behaviour through fractal descriptors across additive manufacturing technologies. Proficiency in advanced mechanical design, including DfAM and topological optimization of lattice structures, supported by practical experience with CAD platforms such as Fusion 360, SolidWorks, and nTop. Experience in the implementation of artificial intelligence and data-driven methods for additive manufacturing applications, including ANNs and evolutionary genetic algorithms for process optimization supported by programming knowledge (e.g. Matlab, Python). Hands-on experience with advanced additive manufacturing workflows, including LPBF, FDM, SLA/DLP, and electrohydrodynamic-based processes (e-jet printing, electrospray, electrospinning). Experience in materials characterization, encompassing microstructural, mechanical, thermal, surface, and electrical property assessment. Ability to lead complex research tasks, manage multiple workstreams, and communicate technical results effectively to multidisciplinary academic and industrial stakeholders. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Mechanical-Engineering---Biomedical-Engineering---Materials-Science-_R00025693-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Mechanical Engineering / Biomedical Engineering / Materials Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) is a research centre conducting fundamental and applied research in all aspects related to additive manufacturing. Our vision is to be the world leader in 3D Printing and a wellspring of knowledge, delivering state of the art and innovative solutions to the industry. SC3DP is at the forefront of developing advanced technologies and high-impact research in areas such biomedical, construction, aerospace, marine and offshore. It is one of the very few research centres globally with multi-sector 3D printing expertise. SC3DP’s research achievements, high-level industry collaboration, comprehensive facilities and resources have positioned it as a leading hub for 3D printing research and innovation globally. We are seeking to hire a highly motivated Research Associate to support research activities in additive manufacturing, computational design, biomaterials, and biomedical engineering. The role will focus on the design, fabrication, optimization, and experimental validation of advanced three-dimensional printed structures and biomedical devices, including porous scaffolds, bioactive composite materials, and patient-specific solutions. The successful candidate will contribute to ongoing research and innovation in advanced manufacturing technologies by developing novel bio fabrication strategies, computational design approaches, and multifunctional biomaterials for tissue engineering and regenerative medicine. The position will also support collaborative research activities with academic and industrial partners, contributing to NTU’s mission of advancing cutting-edge research and translational biomedical engineering. Key Responsibilities: Conduct independent and collaborative research in additive manufacturing, computational design, biomaterials, and biomedical engineering. Design and optimize three-dimensional printed structures using computer-aided design, numerical modelling, data-driven optimization, and artificial intelligence-assisted methods. Develop and characterize bioactive polymeric, ceramic, or composite materials for tissue engineering and regenerative medicine applications. Plan and perform additive manufacturing experiments, including process optimization, mechanical testing, structural characterization, and biological evaluation. Analyze experimental data and prepare technical reports, journal publications, and research presentations. Collaborate closely with researchers, students, clinicians, and industrial partners to support interdisciplinary research activities. Maintain laboratory equipment and ensure compliance with laboratory safety procedures. Job Requirements: Master's degree in mechanical engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Materials Science, or a related discipline. Experience in additive manufacturing and computational design. Experience in biomaterials, tissue engineering, or biomedical applications. Experience in materials characterization, mechanical testing, microscopy, and image analysis. Experience with CAD, numerical modelling, optimization, or artificial intelligence-assisted design is desirable. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within an interdisciplinary research environment. Good publication record in relevant research areas. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Lab-Technician--Cleanroom---Nanofabrication-Facilities-_R00025694": {
      "title": "Lab Technician (Cleanroom & Nanofabrication Facilities)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lab Technician at NTU’s National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP) will support the daily operation, maintenance, and safe use of CDPT cleanroom facilities. The role involves maintaining and troubleshooting fabrication equipment (e.g., FIB, EBL, RIE, ALD, deposition systems), managing consumables and inventory, and ensuring high equipment uptime and safety compliance. The successful candidate will administer booking systems, coordinate facility usage, support fabrication processes, train users on equipment operation and work on cleanroom operational and safety protocols in collaboration with superusers. Responsibilities: Operate, maintain, and troubleshoot nanofabrication equipment Manage cleanroom consumables and ensure facility readiness Train and certify users; enforce SOPs and safety compliance Administer booking systems and coordinate equipment usage Support fabrication processes and research activities Job Requirements: Diploma with at least 3 years of experience or a Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Physics, Materials Science, Nanotechnology, or a related field. Hands on experience in cleanroom or nanofabrication environments. Familiarity with tools such as FIB, EBL, RIE, lithography, or thin film deposition systems. Strong safety awareness and good documentation and record-keeping practices. Responsible, methodical, and able to support multiple users in a shared facility. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--AI-based-Process-Monitoring-_R00025688": {
      "title": "Research Associate (AI-based Process Monitoring)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Associate to develop novel AI methods for process monitoring in laser-based metal additive manufacturing . The role will focus on thermal field modelling, multi-physics numerical simulations, machine learning and process parameter optimization. We expect the candidate to use data-efficient AI methods to accurately predict process anomalies and material defects during the printing process, to further achieve superior part quality and process stability and sustainability. Key Responsibilities: The Research Associate will work on a cross-disciplinary project at the intersection of fluid mechanics, numerical simulation, design optimization and machine learning. The key responsibilities of this position include: Collect thermal data from metal additive manufacturing process Develop cost-efficient and data-efficient AI models Perform process anomaly and material defects detection   Implement real-time process monitoring for layer-wise printing   Collaborate with internal and external stakeholder on energy systems Maintenance of lab or equipment or supplies that include procurement and liaison with suppliers Assist or produce high-quality reports and documents that consolidate research findings Mentoring thesis-based undergraduate and master students Assist in proposal writings Job Requirements: Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies for this position: Master's degree or above in Mechanical Engineering, Structural Engineering, Energy Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Machine Learning, or related fields. Expertise in laser-based metal additive manufacturing process Expertise in data-driven and AI/machine learning research Proficiency in basics of programming languages such as C++, Python, and/or Matlab Strong understanding of research methodologies, data analysis, and statistical techniques Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team Effective written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to convey information, collaborate and build relationship Ability to produce technical content for publications and deliver informative presentations to diverse audience including students Strong analytical and problem-solving skills to analyze and interpret research data Attention to details and a commitment to upholding ethical standards in all research activities Passion in the field of research and a desire to contribute to meaningful projects Excellent verbal and written communication skills Publication track record is an advantage for this position We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Immunology-_R00025687": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Immunology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science at Nanyang Technological University, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance excellence in biological and biomedical sciences. Our research spans diverse and impactful areas including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative disorders, telomere biology, and genome function. SBS is home to a vibrant, international community of scientific leaders, researchers, and professionals dedicated to innovation, discovery, and education. Join the laboratory of Asst Prof Loh Jia Tong at the School of Biological Sciences. We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Fellow to join our immunology research laboratory investigating early-life innate immune mechanisms in health and disease. Our research focuses on understanding how innate immune cells shape host defence, tissue development, and repair during early life and how these processes influence susceptibility to infectious and inflammatory diseases. We integrate state-of-the-art mouse models, high-dimensional immune profiling, single-cell genomics, and functional immunology approaches to uncover fundamental mechanisms driving development and disease pathogenesis. Job Description Design and conduct independent research projects in immunology. Perform and analyze high-dimensional flow cytometry experiments. Utilize and develop murine models of infection and immune-mediated disease. Perform primary immune cell isolation, culture, and functional assays. Analyze and interpret single-cell RNA sequencing datasets. Contribute to manuscript preparation, grant applications, and presentation of research findings. Mentor junior researchers and contribute to a collaborative laboratory environment Requirements PhD in Immunology, Cell Biology, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Sciences, or a related field Entry level candidates with strong technical expertise and enthusiasm for immunology research are particularly encouraged to apply. Strong experimental background in immunology research Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in: High-dimensional flow cytometry and data analysis Mouse experimentation and in vivo disease models Primary cell isolation and culture Single-cell RNA sequencing data analysis Prior experience in innate immunity, neutrophils, and myeloid cells is an advantage A publication record in peer-reviewed journals. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary team. Interested candidates should submit: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Brief statement of research interests At least two referee letters The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager---Deputy-Cluster-Lead--cum-Hall-Office-Lead-_R00025689-1": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager / Deputy Cluster Lead (cum Hall Office Lead)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Campus Housing (OCH) serves to make NTU, the university with the best-in-class campus for learning, working, and living. OCH has a mission to provide optimal on-campus living environment for students and faculty to excel in learning, research, teaching and other NTU related work. It is responsible for student and faculty housing on campus, the sports and recreational facilities, and its related services. We are looking for individuals who have a strong passion for delivering exceptional service to residents of the University’s student and faculty housing, and athletes and users of sports & recreation facilities on campus.   The role, serving as a Deputy Cluster Lead of the student hostel, offers the successful candidate a chance to enhance, contribute, and expand their skills comprehensively in areas such as customer relationship management and other leadership roles within the Department. If you have a degree with more than 5 years of managerial working experience in residential management/services, customer service/relationship management, hospitality management, central administration function, you may be the one whom we are looking for.  Having an experience in student hostels, staff housing or hospitality services would be advantageous for this role.  The incumbent is required to: Plan, manage, and oversee the hostel application processing and the assignment of rooms, including the management of waitlist and students’ appeal for on-campus accommodation. Ensure the high quality of rooms for students’ check-in through comprehensive inspections. Ensure accurate billing of hall fees and other payable items as well as timely collection and follow-up where necessary. This includes accurate and timely refunds to students where applicable. Collaborate with other departments and external vendors / contractors to get update on the status of maintenance / repairs to student hostels. Proactively engage student residents in understanding and addressing residents’ needs, and contributing to problem-solving and resolution of concerns. This includes addressing and resolving student residents’ requests, feedback, and complaints promptly to meet SLA requirements. Plan, curate communications and inform student residents in advance on scheduled maintenance, adhoc repairs and other matters that may cause inconvenience to residents. Plan, organize, and conduct routine walkthroughs of OCH managed premises to evaluate safety and security measures. This includes follow-up actions for enhancement and refinements of measures. Lead and take charge of investigations and compile supporting documentation for incident reports. This includes proposal of suitable sanctions for rule violations based on the severity and frequency of infractions, and prompt escalation of persistent and / or severe breaches for further enforcement measures, as well as implementation of approved sanctions. Ensure the maintenance of up-to-date and precise records, including resident details, occupancy status, and availability, to facilitate billing processes and management reporting. Ensure that facilities reservations are made through established booking channels, and all pre-event and post-event arrangements are properly managed. Oversee regular stock-taking exercises and the disposal of managed inventory and assets within the cluster. Define requirements for procuring necessary goods and services, including prepartion of quotations and tenders, their evaluation, and making recommendations for award of business. Plan, deploy, supervise and manage staff within the Hall Office to deliver optimal outcomes. This includes ensuring that newly joined staff are properly integrated into the team and familiarised with hostel policies, procedures and their work responsibilities. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Light-Detection-and-Ranging--LiDAR--with-Single-Photon-Detector-_R00025029": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Light Detection and Ranging (LiDAR) with Single-Photon Detector)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at Centre for Disruptive Photonic Technologies, School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore A Research Fellow position is currently available at the Centre for Disruptive Photonic Technologies (CDPT), School of Physical & Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore. The Research Fellow (Project Leader) will be required to develop and demonstrate single-photon light detection and ranging (LiDAR) systems by integrating in‑house single‑photon detectors. The role will assess various LiDAR configurations, optimize the optical, timing, and control subsystems, validate performance in laboratory settings, and help chart a pathway toward field-deployable prototypes with superior sensitivity, timing, and resolution. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to conduct research in low-photon regime LiDAR; integrate light sources, trigger/reference detection, time-tagging, synchronization, and control electronics; establish measurement workflows, benchmark detection range, depth resolution, field of view, frame rate, robustness under background light; perform optical/system simulations and develop control and data pipelines for acquisition, reconstruction, and visualization; provide measurement-driven feedback to the detector team; contribute to advanced processing strategies for single-photon sensing, including real-time or event-driven approaches for improved performance and efficient information extraction. The Research Fellow is expected to work, generate ideas and experimentally prove them both independently and within team-working efforts with other researchers working on the project to deliver state‑of‑the‑art single‑photon imaging capabilities, and to disseminate results through publications, reports, and IP contributions. The Research Fellow will be required to: Design, assemble, and align a single‑photon‑enabled scanning microscope; integrate detector modules, synchronization electronics, and time‑tagging workflows. Develop imaging protocols and benchmark sensitivity, contrast, resolution, and acquisition strategies on calibrated samples. Develop advanced signal and data-processing workflows for single-photon LiDAR and time-resolved imaging, including event-based or neural-network-assisted approaches for efficient extraction of information from sparse photon measurements, low-latency operation, and improved robustness under photon-limited conditions. Develop hardware-software co-design for intelligent sensing, including implementation and evaluation of real-time or near-sensor processing pipelines, and exploration of algorithmic approaches that can be integrated with detector readout and acquisition architectures for enhanced system-level performance. Operating and maintaining research laboratories, including advanced microscopy and spectroscopy equipment, in compliance with safety and laboratory protocols. Analyze data, prepare scientific publications, and present findings at international conferences. Collaborate with internal and external partners on joint research projects and technology development. Contribute to progress reports, project meetings, and support day-to-day laboratory operations. Job Requirements: Must have a Ph.D. or Doctorate in Physics, Optical/Photonic Engineering, Information Science or closely related disciplines Applicants must have relevant research experience in optical/laser setups and scanning systems (eg, galvo or similar) including alignment and throughput optimization. Applicants must have a good track record of scientific publications in international peer reviewed journals Applicants preferably should demonstrate extensive research experience in optical imaging setups such as low photon detectors/ timing/synchronization, data acquisition, and execution of light detection and ranging protocols. Applicants preferably should be familiar with single-photon detection concepts and time-of-flight or equivalent timing measurements, awareness of noise, efficiency, and timing trade-offs in low-light imaging. Applicants should have competence in data acquisition/analysis and scripting for instrument control (e.g., Python/Matlab/LabVIEW) Applicants preferably should have experience in real-time processing or FPGA-based prototyping or embedded sensing architectures, or machine-learning-driven analysis for photon-limited measurements. Exposure to event-driven sensing or hardware-algorithm co-design for single-photon systems will be an added advantage. Applicants should show ability to work both independently and within a collaborative research team. Applicants should show strong communication and interpersonal skills; ability to work both independently and within an institution. NTU seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Student-Community-Engagement_R00025775": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Community Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNTU Student Affairs Office (SAO) seeks to achieve its mission of collaborating and co-creating a meaningful and enriching student life experience with its partners by promoting students' personal growth through co-curricular learning arising from student-led activities, leadership development initiatives, residential hall programmes, inclusion and integration efforts, community engagement initiatives and sports. This job calls for a dynamic and passionate individual to serve as the Assistant Director, Student Community Engagement to improve the development and delivery of programmes and holistic educational needs of students under NTU's Community Engagement Framework, to promote an enriching and vibrant student life among the university's 34,000 student body. The Assistant Director, Student Community Engagement supports the Deputy Director in the planning, execution, and continuous enhancement of student life initiatives across campus. This role is instrumental in driving strategic efforts related to student community engagement and student organisations.  The Assistant Director leads the development and delivery of a university-wide community collaboration framework to strengthen student engagement and vibrancy across Arts, Sports, Residential Life, Leadership, and Academic Clubs. The Assistant Director will also spearhead the operationalisation of the community engagement framework and provide strategic direction and operational oversight for a portfolio of 60+ Community and interest-based clubs, driving measurable learning outcomes, sustainable partnerships, and strong governance. Key Responsibilities Management of community and interest-based student clubs Implement the strategic plans and programmes of the Student Engagement and Campus Vibrancy Division.  Lead and oversee the year-round planning and delivery of  activities of 60+ community and interest-based student clubs. Lead, oversee and implement the operationalisation of the NTU Community Engagement Framework towards established desired outcomes. Lead and drive innovation in co-curricular programming across Student Organisations such as the Welfare Services Club and Special Interests Clubs to enhance student vibrancy and engagement. Work closely with student leaders, partners and other stakeholders to keep various programmes on schedule and within budget. Mentor and guide student leaders in their development and competencies building.  Community Engagment Framework Oversee and lead the portfolio strategy, set annual priorities, and establish an annual plan for community and interest-based clubs, aligned to NTU/SAO Student Development outcomes. Establish new partnerships  and manage complex stakeholder engagement, including close collaboration with external partners such as the People’s Association, grassroots leaders, etc. to ensure that student-led initiatives are both impactful and sustainable. By overseeing the guidance provided to clubs to design and deliver services for the wider community, the role advances a larger intent of character development – helping students grow as responsible, empathetic leaders who contribute meaningfully to society. Oversee the design, implementation and continuous refinement students’ community engagement participation strategy, success metrics, and governance. Oversee the establishment and implementation of capacity-building approach for clubs (leadership development, community impact design, collaboration readiness). Stakeholder Partnerships and Collaboration Enablement Actively cultivate and manage relationships with internal stakeholders (NTU Offices, faculty/staff advisors, student organisations) and external partners (social service agencies, community organisations, corporate/public sector partners where relevant). Lead the team in effective inter-club and cross-office collaborations. Governance, Funding & Impact Reporting Oversee governance and compliance across programmes and funding, including budget stewardship and grant utilisation (e.g. Social Impact Internship Stipend). Establish and oversee portfolio-wide KPIs and reporting standards (participation, volunteer contributions, learning outcomes, partnership depth and social impact indicators). Consolidate insights to meet MOE/NTU reporting requirements and lead in driving continuous improvement. People Leadership & Team Management Supervise, coach and lead a team, ensuring clear KPIs and workload allocation. Develop the team’s skills, knowledge and competencies continuously to close skills gaps. Develop tools, methods and standard procedures for capability building. Build an environment and a culture of continuous learning. Job Requirements Degree in any discipline with at least 10 years of relevant experience in student development, community engagement, programme management, stakeholder partnerships, and/or public/education sector work, with minimum 3 years in supervisory role. Demonstrate experience leading teams and delivering multi-stakeholder initiatives at scale. Strong programme design capability with proven ability to deliver measurable outcomes. Excellent communication, facilitation, negotiation and influencing skills, especially in working collaboratively with diverse stakeholders from different cultural and disciplinary backgrounds. Strong governance mindset; comfortable with budgeting, compliance, and grant stewardship. Resourceful, good analytical skills, operationally strong and detail-oriented with good problem-solving capabilities. Proficient in all Microsoft Office application software and comfortable with digital systems and workflows. A passion for youth development. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-Senior-Research-Engineer--Computer-Science---Data-Science---Information-Science---Digital-Humanities-_R00025774": {
      "title": "Research Engineer/Senior Research Engineer (Computer Science / Data Science / Information Science / Digital Humanities)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Asian Centre for Digital Cultures (ACDC) at CoHASS, NTU, invites applications for two Research Engineer/ Senior Research Engineer positions. Working at the intersection of computation and the humanities, arts, and social sciences, the successful candidates will enable innovative research by providing technical support, methodological expertise, and collaborative capacity across the Centre’s research initiatives. Key Responsibilities:  Support CoHASS researchers in exploring and applying digital methods and tools, including coding, empowering principal investigators to integrate digital tools into their projects, in partnership with other technical groups across NTU and Singapore Assist “ACDC methods lab” lead and co-lead in conducting regular academic events Provide training in selected digital methods and tools Support researchers in developing Web and mobile applications Support researchers in using cloud services for research and development Help with the ethical scraping, collection, cleaning, and structuring of diverse qualitative and quantitative datasets Develop and maintain the ACDC website and portal to effectively showcase ongoing projects and outputs Support researchers in writing the methods and technical sections of research proposals and publications Define and manage guidelines for best-practice software design and development and the effective management of risks and issues that affect scope, schedule and quality Maintain currency of contemporary and relevant sector-wide developments in software development relevant to ACDC and share with other members of the team Other duties, appropriate to this classification, as directed Job Requirements:  A Master’s degree in computer science, data science, information science, digital humanities Experience with social science/humanities/arts research methods Python coding skills including Pandas package, statistical or machine learning packages, access to cloud AI services Experience with cloud services and environments Experience with developing Web or mobile applications Demonstrated experience in supporting a high-quality service to users, including analysing problems and resolving problems related to research requirements, monitoring the status of services, proactively seeking service improvements to meet emerging areas of need Ability to pick up new methods and software packages by reading manuals and following online tutorials Open source development and management is highly valued, along with experience working in an agile software development environment Enthusiasm in exploring and learning new digital methods The closing date for application is 15 October 2026. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
