    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Geotechnics-Geophysics-_R00025769": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Geotechnics/Geophysics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) at Nanyang Technological University is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. It has over 60 faculty members and more than 1,500 students and is rapidly expanding its range of education and research activities. We are looking for a Research Fellow to 1) curate and integrate available geotechnical, geological, and geophysical datasets; 2) develop 3D models for the characterization of near-surface geological formations; 3) develop geophysical methods for imaging and characterizing subsurface structures. Key Responsibilities: Develop novel 3D modeling algorithms for near-surface characterization using curated geo-data. Contribute to the development of intelligent geophysical imaging algorithms. Publish high-impact research articles in leading international journals Assist in the preparation and development of competitive research proposals Support the supervision and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students Job Requirements: PhD’s degree in geotechnics, geophysics, or related field At least 2 years of relevant experiences in geological modeling Familiarity with related literature and software Good written and oral communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Social-Sciences---Digital-Humanities---Media-and-Communication-Studies---Cultural-Studies---Sociology-_R00025771": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Social Sciences / Digital Humanities / Media and Communication Studies / Cultural Studies / Sociology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Asian Centre for Digital Cultures (ACDC) at CoHASS, NTU, invites applications for a Research Associate to contribute to interdisciplinary research on digital cultures, platforms, technology, and social transformation in Asia. The successful candidate will contribute to the development, delivery, and dissemination of research projects, while supporting the Centre’s academic programmes. Key Responsibilities:  Support the centre director, deputy directors, and admin coordinator with daily operations including scheduling meetings, managing project timelines, and organising academic events Assist principal investigators in conducting literature reviews, gathering qualitative / quantitative / computational data, and drafting academic outputs  Collect, clean, and organise primary and secondary datasets, performing preliminary data analysis to support centre projects Prepare research reports, policy briefs, presentation materials, and draft manuscripts for academic journal submissions Assist in preparing research grant proposals, tracking project deliverables, and drafting progress reports for funding agencies Serve as a point of contact for internal NTU stakeholders, external international collaborators, visiting scholars, and research partners Other duties, appropriate to this classification, as directed Job Requirements:  A Master’s degree in social sciences, digital humanities, media and communication studies, cultural studies, sociology, or a closely related field Track record in conducting academic research with proficiency in research methods, data analysis, and digital research Strong project management, time management, and multi-tasking skills with attention to detail in handling administrative procedures Excellent written and oral communication skills, with experience drafting academic report or administrative documentation Good ability to work both independently with minimal supervision and collaboratively within a multi-disciplinary team environment Research interest in Asian digital cultures, technology and social transformation, platform economies, or heritage cultures in Asia. The closing date for application is 15 October 2026. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Research-and-Partnership_R00025770": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research and Partnership",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) hosts world-class education and research programmes in organic and inorganic chemistry, physical chemistry, chemical engineering, bioengineering and process engineering and synthetic chemistry. We aim to nurture future-ready graduates with the ability to tackle new challenges in chemicals manufacturing, healthcare, energy, food, and other important sectors. We are seeking a dedicated and dynamic professional to join us as Assistant Manager, Research & Partnership . You will assist the Head of Research & Partnership within the school, in building and nurturing collaborations with academia, industry, and government agencies, while strengthening existing alliances and seeking new opportunities for research, education, and industrial engagement. You will also support faculty in research-related matters, ensure compliance with institutional and national requirements, and drive initiatives that elevate the school’s research reputation and impact. You will also serve as the unit manpower officer (UMO) of the school, overseeing manpower budget planning, hiring and salary allocations for research projects. Key Responsibilities Support the Associate Chair (Research) and Head of Research & Partnership in the effective administration and day-to-day operations of the School’s Research and Partnership Office. Serve as the Unit Manpower Officer of the School in managing researchers’ manpower budget allocations across multiple research grants to ensure optimal resource utilisation and compliance. Review and manage the manpower payroll projections for research grant, including salaries, bonuses, SDL, employment pass fees, and insurance costs. Approve and process manpower-related variation requests including new hiring, contract renewals, transfers, position upgrades, ensuring sufficient funding and complies with the guidelines. Ensure research manpower budgets and expenditures are aligned with funding agency guidelines. Plan and coordinate seminars, industry engagements and other research related events, covering end-to-end event management including logistics, stakeholder coordination, budgeting and on-site execution. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to ensure events and activities are delivered effectively and in alignment with school’s objectives. Coordinate institutional grant calls and nomination exercises, including announcement dissemination, collation and timely submission to the relevant offices. Provide support to faculty members throughout the research grant lifecycle. Manage the research data management to ensure institutional alignment and maintaining appropriate documentation for audit readiness. Undertake other administrative projects or responsibilities as assigned. Requirements A recognised Bachelor Degree. No prior working experience is required, though experience in research grant and/or project management, or prior experience in a higher education setting, will be an added advantage. Good understanding of the research ecosystem. Excellent analytical, problem solving and stakeholder management skills. Able to work effectively under pressure. Resourceful and independent. Proactive and positive attitude towards work tasks. Assertive and meticulous. The School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.  Appointment titles offered will commensurate with candidate’s prior work experiences. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow-Senior-Research-Fellow--Polymeric-Precursors-Towards-Ceramic-and-Porous-Ceramics-_R00025763": {
      "title": "Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow (Polymeric Precursors Towards Ceramic and Porous Ceramics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. Our research group focuses on research areas including macromolecular and hybrid materials, including topics in the fields of polymer science and engineering, composite materials, high temperature resistant materials, ceramic precursor materials, environmental chemistry and materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . We are looking for a research fellow to carry out R&D activities on the research directions of developing precursors to be converted into ceramic materials in different formfactors such as solid films and porous materials. The role will focus on developing the precursor formulation, conversion process into porous ceramic materials, characterizations of relevant precursors and ceramic composite, and explore various possible applications. Key Responsibilities: Develop precursor formulations to be converted into porous ceramic materials for suitable applications Conduct research and development activities on preparation of porous ceramic materials, including formulation of problem statement, execution of lab-scale and pilot-scale experiments/operations, sample characterizations, data analysis, and so on. Prepare technical reports, intellectual properties documents, safety documents, and academic publications Job Requirements: PhD degree in Materials Science, Polymer Science, Chemical Engineering, or Environmental Engineering. Strong research experience on relevant topics on material science, chemical engineering, and green technologies preferred for this relatively short-team project Proficiency in hands-on and characterization techniques such as DSC, FTIR, DMA, rheology, mechanical testing etc. Industrial-relevant experience in scalability and productization is favorable. Knowledge on LCA and TEA is an advantage. Good team-player, good communication skills, problem solver, thinker and doer, able to exhibit leadership when needed Good wet laboratory practice and familiar with considerations on laboratory safety. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--LKCMedicine-_R00023476-2": {
      "title": "Research Associate [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Liu Lab (Principal Investigator: Dr. Yi Liu) of the Cancer Discovery and Regenerative Medicine Programme at the Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) is a collaborative, forwarding-thinking, and innovative cell biology research laboratory. The lab aims to conduct impactful and creative cancer and stem cell research by leveraging 3D cell models including organoids and spheroids. For more details, please view the Liu lab website https://liulab.myportfolio.com/ & the programme website https://www.ntu.edu.sg/medicine/research/research-programmes/cancer-discovery-regenerative-medicine . We are seeking a motivated Research Assistant to join our team in advancing cancer and stem cell biology research. The role will independently executing experimental protocols, collecting and analyzing data, and contributing to our understanding of cancer mechanisms and stem cell behavior. Key Responsibilities: Maintain and develop complex cellular models, including organoids, 3D spheroids, and 2D cell cultures. Independently conduct and analyze a range of molecular and cellular biology experiments, utilizing techniques such as qRT-PCR, CRISPR-based genetic manipulation, advanced live-cell imaging, and biochemical assays. Collaborate directly with the Principal Investigator (PI) and PhD students to execute outlined research plans and optimize experimental protocols. Support laboratory compliance and safety by assisting and contributing to the creation of Risk Assessments (RAs) and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies: Master's degree (for Research Associate) in cell biology, biochemistry, or molecular biology Candidate must have Minimum of 1 year of hands-on laboratory experience with organoid culture and stem cell maintenance Good written and oral communication skills Demonstrated ability to develop, manage, and execute research plans Competent in observance, patience, resilience, and determination Excellent interpersonal skills, including the ability to work independently and collaboratively to develop solutions and troubleshoot under strict timelines Highly meticulous with a strong attention to detail, excellent organizational, and time management skills Entry level candidates are welcome to apply Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Mechanical-Engineering-_R00025788": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Mechanical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is seeking to hire a Research Fellow to work on the design, manufacturing, team building, and industrial promotion of an electrical generating system using the sea wave energy as the power source. Key Responsibilities: Design, Research, and solution demonstration of wave energy equipment components. Procurement of experimental consumables, prototype manufacturing and assembly of wave energy equipment. Liaison and organization of large-scale indoor tests of wave energy equipment. Channel expansion and industry exhibition promotion of wave energy equipment. Job Requirements: Education qualifications: PhD (Mechanical Engineering) or above Soft skills: Organization management and project progress control ability, channel development and industry exhibition promotion ability, Adaptability to high-intensity R&D and industry-application settings abilities. Hard skills: Communication and written skills, design software use and manufacturing processing ability, Hands-on abilities in operating advanced characterization and testing instruments (TEM, Cs-correctedTEM, cryo-EM, XRD, universal tester, etc.). Experience: More than 3 years of management experience in energy and aerospace sectors. More than 1 year of research and development experience in aerospace and defense industrial R&D fields, through a national elite engineer program at a top-tier aerospace enterprise. Competencies: Scheme demonstration and organizer management of wave power generation experimental device, excellent communication and negotiation skills, can implement the contact and arrangement of large-scale experiments, can ensure the safety of experimental construction and solve technical problems. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Science-_R00025787": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: Conduct independent research in deep learning and Generative AI. Produce publications in top conferences and journals. Offer guidance and assistance to students involved in the project. Collaborate with industrial and academic partners. Perform other duties related to the research program. Job Requirements: A PhD in Computer Science or a relevant field. Strong background in deep learning, Generative AI, and multimodal learning. Strong publication record in top conferences and journals, such as CVPR, NeurIPS, AAAI, IJCAI, IEEE TPAMI, and IJCV. Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Lead--Academic_R00025786": {
      "title": "Lead, Academic",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Lead, Academic is a key leadership role responsible for ensuring the effective delivery and continuous improvement of postgraduate (PG) academic programmes. The role supports the university’s mission to provide high-quality, research-driven education by managing academic processes, coordinating curriculum development, and driving innovation in programme administration. Acting as a bridge between academic leadership, faculty, and administrative systems, the jobholder ensures excellence, compliance, and responsiveness to evolving academic needs. Key Responsibilities: PhD Programme & Examination Management & Research Exchange partnerships Oversee PhD-specific academic processes: Qualifying Examinations (QE), thesis, reviewer coordination. Coordinate QE logistics, reports, and reviewer assignments. Attend to academic matters for PhD programme partnerships and joint PhDs. Oversee research exchange programmes (e.g., China Scholarship Council (CSC), non-degree). Oversee PhD Admissions and Scholarships. Academic Partnerships & Research Exchange Support academic matters for joint PhD programmes and institutional partnerships. Oversee research exchange programmes (e.g., CSC, non-degree), ensuring smooth processing and tracking. Faculty & Teaching Support Provide teaching support insights and coordinate faculty engagement initiatives. Post Work Study Scheme (WSS) assignments as requested by professors and GS Office and assign shortlisted students. Financial Administration & Billing for Students Check on prepared billing for MSc students for  each Semester. Follow up on Monthly Aging Report for MSc students with outstanding tuition fees. Oversee fee waiver appeals process. Process WSS students’ claim submission. Data-driven Planning and Process Improvement Manage Data analysis of postgraduate student demographics for Graduate Intake and Enrolment Planning (GIEP) projections. Improve workflows and implement policies for process automation and digitalization of administrative workflows to improve efficiency. Educational Qualification(s) Bachelor’s degree or diploma with minimum 5 years of relevant experience in student services. Knowledge Required Strong background in academic administration, curriculum development, or programme management. Familiarity with postgraduate education frameworks and regulatory requirements. Big picture of how graduate programmes are derived and the administration to run it smoothly. Relevant Experience Minimum 5 years of experience in Student services, with 2 years of supervisory experience. Skills & Competencies MS Office. Multi-tasking. Ability to lead a team. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Effective communication and organisational skills. Excellent organizational, analytical, and stakeholder engagement skills. Ability to manage complex processes and drive continuous improvement. Event planning and management. Other Personal Attributes Flexible. Approachable. Helpful. Meticulous Team player. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Embodied-AI-for-Intelligent-System-_R00025785": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Embodied AI for Intelligent System)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to support the research on Integrated Sensing and Communications (ISAC) with Reconfigurable Intelligent Metasurfaces (RIS). Key Responsibilities: Design the algorithm on Embodied AI for Intelligent System. Conduct simulation and perform experiment in some scenarios. Document research outcome to publish at top international conference / journal. Write report for the project progress. Work with other research fellow and PhD students for the system development. Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, or related field. Good publication record. Have prior experience in conducting experiments is a plus. A thorough knowledge of the AI is highly preferred. Excellent interpersonal communication and presentation skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Digital-Health---Full-Stack-Developer--LKCMedicine-_R00025780": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, Digital Health - Full-Stack Developer [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Dementia Research Centre (Singapore) (DRCS) conducts human research in neuropsychology, neuroimaging and biomarkers to advance understanding of Alzheimer’s disease, vascular dementia and related conditions, and integrates digital platforms and artificial intelligence in translational research for cognitive disorders. The Centre offers a dynamic and supportive research environment, access to state-of-the-art core facilities, and valuable opportunities for hands-on experience in dementia research. We are looking for a  motivated and enthusiastic Research Assistant to join our team, focusing on building digital solutions targeted at cognitive and mental healthcare. Key Responsibilities: Full-stack application development Design, develop, test, and maintain web and mobile applications supporting digital health and cognitive healthcare initiatives. Build responsive, user-friendly front-end interfaces using React and React Native. Develop and maintain backend services, APIs, and application logic using Node.js and TypeScript. Implement scalable, secure, and maintainable software solutions following established development practices. Troubleshoot, debug, and optimise application performance across web and mobile platforms. Participate in software testing, deployment, and release activities. Cloud infrastructure and system operations Deploy, manage, and maintain cloud-based applications and services on AWS. Support application monitoring, performance tuning, security, and reliability improvements. Assist in implementing development workflows, version control, and deployment pipelines. Contribute to system documentation, technical specifications, and operational procedures. Product development and collaboration Work closely with researchers, clinicians, UI/UX designers, and other developers to translate research requirements into digital solutions. Participate in product ideation, prototyping, and iterative development activities. Contribute to the development of digital cognitive assessment tools, healthcare applications, and related technologies. Support the integration of research-driven features, analytics, and data-driven functionalities into user-facing applications. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders on research and innovation projects. Key Competencies and Requirements: Essential qualifications Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related discipline; candidates with a Diploma and relevant industry experience are also encouraged to apply. Essential skills and experience Strong hands-on experience in full-stack application development. Proficiency in JavaScript and/or TypeScript. Experience in developing backend services using Node.js. Experience in developing web applications using React. Experience in developing mobile or cross-platform applications using React Native. Familiarity with AWS cloud services and deployment environments. Experience building responsive and mobile-compatible web applications. Strong problem-solving and analytical skills. Good verbal and written communication skills. Able to work independently while collaborating effectively within a multidisciplinary team. Strong attention to detail and commitment to producing high-quality software. Preferred Experience in participating in digital product development projects, hackathons, or innovative technical initiatives. Experience with cloud architecture, CI/CD pipelines, and DevOps practices. Familiarity with UI/UX principles and implementation of user-centred design. Experience in working with healthcare, digital health, research, startup, or product development environments. Experience integrating analytics, AI, machine learning, or data-driven features into applications. Active GitHub portfolio or examples of deployed applications. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--AI-Modelling-_R00025784": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (AI Modelling)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nGlobally recognized as a leading research and technology organization, the Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI) addresses national priorities through its diverse expertise in Biotechnology and Bioprocesses, Membrane Technology, Chemicals and Materials, Resource Recovery, and Modelling & Artificial Intelligence. By harnessing its cross-cutting, interdisciplinary, and transformative capabilities, NEWRI drives innovation in water circularity and sustainability, next-generation solid waste solutions, circular economy resource recovery, climate resilience and digitalization. We are looking for an Research Fellow to conduct high-quality research and propose cutting-edge solutions to nearshore seawater level monitoring and wave height monitoring. Key Responsibilities: Conduct high-quality research and experiments on nearshore seawater monitoring Prepare grant proposals and project reports Program using Python and test theoretical findings via computer simulations Test the methods via lab experiments Publish results in top-tier journals in related field s Assist in mentoring PhD students Job Requirements: PhD degree in mathematics, systems engineering, or machine learning Expertise in monitoring of sea Strong programming skills An outstanding track record of research in the corresponding field demonstrated by an excellent publication record (e.g., coastal engineering, water research, top ML conferences) Advanced written and communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Lab-Operations_R00025783-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Lab Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering is seeking an Assistant Manager to manage the Computer Aided Design laboratory operations and activities. The candidate would be responsible for providing efficient technical and administrative support for all laboratory teachings and research activities and to oversee the safety standards in the lab in compliance with ISO 45001 standard. Key Responsibilities: Provide technical and administrative support for all undergraduate and research activities. Carry out all planned teaching supports of laboratory classes, experiments and projects. Maintain and configure computer hardware to ensure that they are in good working condition. Manage and troubleshoot hardware and software issues in computers and Windows servers. Procure laboratory software, equipment, and consumables in a timely manner and in accordance with school/university purchasing guidelines. Laboratory asset management and maintaining proper records for inventory auditing. Ensure safety practices in the laboratory. Carry out housekeeping of the laboratory. Conduct safety risk assessments for all equipment and processes. Ensure laboratory equipment is properly maintained, safe to operate and in good working condition. To ensure that lab’s resources are sufficient to function as a teaching/ research laboratory. Requirements: A recognized degree in Mechanical/ Mechatronics/ Manufacturing Engineering. Minimum 2-3 years in Computer Aided Design/Computer Aided Manufacturing environment. Preferably 1-2 years of experience in administering and configuring computer systems (IT knowledge). Knowledge of Computer Aided Design and Engineering software such as SolidWorks, SolidCAM, Ansys, Autodesk Fusion. Good computer hardware and software troubleshooting skills. Knowledge of workplace safety practices. Able to support and assist students in teaching classes. Demonstrates initiative, willingness to learn, and interest in continuous improvement. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Assistant-Manager--MSc-Programme_R00025779": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, MSc Programme",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAs a Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, you will be responsible for the administrative and operational management of the MSc in Precision Scientific Instrumentation (MSPSI). You will oversee admissions processing, curriculum coordination, timetabling, candidature matters, internship administration, and examination support to ensure smooth programme delivery in compliance with University policies. Responsibilities: Manage end-to-end programme administration from admissions to graduation. Coordinate internship processes and documentation across relevant MSc programmes. Oversee curriculum documentation, timetabling, and course registration processes. Support examination operations and mark entry processes. Process PTL claims and support faculty administrative matters. Coordinate closely with faculty, students, and internal stakeholders to ensure operational continuity. Requirements: A degree holder from a recognised university. Around 3–5 years of relevant experience in programme administration or higher education operations. Strong organisational skills and attention to detail. Familiarity with academic administrative processes and institutional systems. Ability to work independently within defined operational frameworks. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--BSL3-Facility--LKCMedicine-_R00025760-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, BSL3 Facility [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The LKCMedicine BSL‑3 Facility is a research‑focused biocontainment unit at the Experimental Medicine Building (EMB), NTU. The facility supports research and diagnostic work involving Risk Group 3 pathogens. The Senior Executive plays a critical role in supporting laboratory operations, ensuring biosafety and biosecurity compliance, and enabling safe, efficient research activities within the BSL‑3 environment. Key Responsibilities: Support the operations of the NTU LKCMedicine BSL‑3 Facility by providing operational, administrative, and biosafety compliance support for research involving RG3 pathogens Assist with experimental activities Maintain facility inventory and documentation Coordinate facility users and supporting procurement Key Competencies and Requirements: Diploma/Bachelor’s degree in Biomedical Sciences / Life Sciences or equivalent. Strong understanding of Singapore biosafety regulations and infectious agents. Minimum 6 months in BSL‑2 lab; animal handling experience is advantageous. Knowledge of disinfectants/sterilants, aerosol exposure risks; excellent written/verbal communication. Good team player, motivated, willing to learn, strong work ethic. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/XMLNAME--Early-Advert--Research-Fellow--Experimental-free-electron-driven-X-ray-nanophotonics-_R00025797": {
      "title": "[Early Advert] Research Fellow (Experimental free-electron-driven X-ray nanophotonics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding schools of Nanyang Technological University, ranking 1st in the world in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering according to the U.S. News & World Report Best Global Universities (2025/2026); and 4th globally according to QS World University Rankings by Subject (2026). The L. J. Wong Group on X-ray & Free Electron Quantum Nanophotonics is one of the leading research groups in the world on X-ray photonics, having been recognized as a 2024 Falling Walls Winner in Physical Sciences for “Breaking the Wall of Quantum X-ray Tech” by the Falling Walls Foundation. [Group website: https://sites.google.com/view/ljwgroup ] We are seeking a Research Fellow to spearhead cutting-edge research in the experimental study of free-electron-driven X-ray photonics, with the goal of using such a source to achieve X-ray phase-contrast imaging on a table-top scale. Key Responsibilities: Perform experiments on free-electron-driven X-ray nanophotonics and phase-contrast imaging in customized scanning electron microscope (SEM) and transmission electron microscope (TEM) setups Lead papers and publish in high-impact journals Present at top-tier international conferences Job Requirements: PhD degree in physics, engineering or related field Familiarity with vacuum electronics and free-electron-based devices We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/XMLNAME--Early-Advert--Research-Fellow--Computational-and-theoretical-modeling-of-free-electron-driven-X-ray-nanophotonics-_R00025796": {
      "title": "[Early Advert] Research Fellow (Computational and theoretical modeling of free-electron-driven X-ray nanophotonics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding schools of Nanyang Technological University, ranking 1st in the world in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering according to the U.S. News & World Report Best Global Universities (2025/2026); and 4th globally according to QS World University Rankings by Subject (2026). The L. J. Wong Group on X-ray & Free Electron Quantum Nanophotonics is one of the leading research groups in the world on X-ray photonics, having been recognized as a 2024 Falling Walls Winner in Physical Sciences for “Breaking the Wall of Quantum X-ray Tech” by the Falling Walls Foundation. [Group website: https://sites.google.com/view/ljwgroup ] We are seeking a Research Fellow to spearhead cutting-edge research in the computational and theoretical modeling of free-electron-driven X-ray photonics. Working closely with experimentalists, the research fellow will lead the study of coherent X-ray emission from free-electron-driven van der Waals materials, and the use of this platform for realizing X-ray phase-contrast imaging on a table-top scale. Key Responsibilities: Develop theoretical and numerical frameworks for free-electron-driven X-ray nanophotonics – i.e., model the physics of free electrons impinging on nanomaterials like van der Waals crystals, and subsequent coherent X-ray emission processes. Lead papers and publish in high-impact journals Present at top-tier international conferences Job Requirements: PhD degree in physics, engineering or related field Familiarity with electrodynamics and electromagnetism; quantum physics/quantum electrodynamics is a plus We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Appointments_R00025795": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Faculty Appointments",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) http://www.eee.ntu.edu.sg is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. It is one of the largest EEE schools in the world, with more than 120 faculty members and an enrollment of more than 5,000, of which about 2,000 are graduate students. We invite applications for the position of Assistant Manager, Faculty Appointments. This position is responsible for providing administrative support to School Chair and faculty. This can include providing secretariat support for School Search Committee, School Re-appointment Committee, School Review Committee for Promotion and Tenure, Appraisal Committee, etc. Key Responsibilities: Handle sensitive and confidential matters and provide support to ensure necessary flow of information to relevant stakeholders. Support School Search Committee (SSC), School Reappointment Committee (SREC) and School Review Committee for Promotion and Tenure (SRCPT) and Appraisal Committee for appointment, reappointment, promotion and appraisal respectively. Plan, coordinate and support for faculty matters like contract renewal, re-employment and promotion. Identify, plan, implement and enhance operational processes. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree preferably in a Business or its equivalent discipline. At least 3 years of experience in a similar role. Demonstrated ability in supporting C Suite executives. Proficient with standard MS office software (Power BI, MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint). Possess strong written and communication skills. Able to write and correspond professionally. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Assessment-Operations-and-Partnerships_R00025789": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Assessment Operations and Partnerships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Academic Services (OAS) plays a vital role in enabling student success across the entire academic journey by implementing and administering academic policies established by the University's academic bodies. OAS delivers comprehensive academic services from matriculation to graduation, empowering students, upholding excellence, and partnering stakeholders to provide a seamless, student-centred experience while maintaining the highest standards of integrity, governance, and professionalism. Within OAS, the Examinations team is responsible for the planning, administration, and continuous enhancement of the University's assessment ecosystem. The team ensures that assessments are conducted securely, fairly, and efficiently while safeguarding academic standards and upholding the principles of academic integrity. As the University expands its digital assessment capabilities, the team also plays a key role in supporting digital transformation initiatives and driving the adoption of technology-enabled assessment practices. Key Responsibilities: Assessment Operations: Plan and administer centralised and decentralised assessments in compliance with University assessment regulations, policies, and procedures. This includes the delivery of large-scale face-to-face centralised assessments, assessment scheduling, venue allocation, seating arrangements, logistics coordination, invigilator deployment, assessment material management, and the administration of assessment-related student cases such as medical certificate submissions and special consideration requests. Digital Assessment Operations & Adoption: Oversee the operations, readiness, and utilisation of the University's digital assessment halls, ensuring seamless assessment delivery, efficient turnaround between bookings, and consistently high facility utilisation. Partner with Schools and faculty members to support the implementation and adoption of digital assessment practices by providing operational guidance, assessment planning support, and expertise on assessment technologies and processes. Assessment Partnerships, Engagement & Communications: Build trusted partnerships with stakeholders to support OAS' strategic and operational objectives. Design and deliver engagement, communications, and outreach initiatives that strengthen stakeholder understanding, readiness, and confidence in OAS’ services. Gather insights and feedback to enhance experiences, improve service delivery, and support the successful adoption of OAS initiatives. Governance, Experience Design & Continuous Improvement: Support academic integrity initiatives and drive process improvements, automation, and digital transformation efforts to improve operational efficiency, governance, and service quality. Apply user-centred and service design principles to enhance the assessment experience for students, faculty members, and operational partners. Gather stakeholder feedback, identify pain points and opportunities, and translate insights into practical improvements that strengthen engagement, service delivery, and effectiveness. Resource Management & Projects: Manage procurement and vendor coordination activities and analyse operational data and performance indicators to support informed decision-making. Participate in and support cross-functional projects and institutional initiatives related to digital transformation, stakeholder engagement, and service excellence initiatives that advance OAS' strategic and operational objectives. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Information Systems, Data Analytics, Education, Communications or a related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant experience, preferably in academic services within a higher education institution. Experience in assessment administration and operations, digital assessments, event management, communications, customer experience, service design or large-scale operational environments. Experience supporting high-stakes, mission-critical operations involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and tight timelines will be highly advantageous. Strong stakeholder engagement and relationship management skills, with the ability to build trusted partnerships across diverse stakeholder groups.  Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to develop and deliver both strategic and tactical communications.  Ability to translate complex operational and technical information into clear, audience-appropriate communications and actionable guidance. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and data management tools. Collaborative and stakeholder-focused, with a passion for building relationships and delivering positive stakeholder experiences. Innovative and improvement-minded, with an interest in driving service improvements and assessment transformation initiatives. Demonstrates high integrity, professionalism, and a commitment to upholding governance, service excellence, and academic integrity. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Embodied-AI---Dex-Hands-_R00025791": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Embodied AI & Dex Hands)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . Position Overview We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to join our research team focusing on integrating multimodal large language models (LLMs) with embodied AI. This position will involve the development and deployment of Vision-Language-Action models for real-world robotic applications, such as autonomous task execution and human-robot interaction. The successful candidate will work on cutting-edge research at the intersection of AI, robotics, and multimodal learning. Key Responsibilities Design and implement VLA models and world models. Develop and optimize deep learning algorithms to enable robotic arms to perform complex tasks guided by natural language instructions. Utilize PyTorch to train and fine-tune models on multimodal datasets. Experiment with and deploy vision-language-action models on robotic platforms. Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to advance the field of embodied intelligence. Publish high-quality research in top-tier conferences and journals. Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science, Robotics, AI, or a related field. At least 4 top-tier 1st author papers on AI and robotics. Expertise in deep learning, multimodal LLMs, and Vision-Language-Action models. Strong programming skills in Python, with significant experience in PyTorch. Hands-on experience with robotic systems, particularly robotic arms. Familiarity with human-robot interaction and reinforcement learning is a plus. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research and contribute to collaborative projects. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Forest---Urban-Ecology-_R00025790": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Forest & Urban Ecology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nASE is an interdisciplinary school that will be a world leader in environmental research focused on Asian environmental challenges. The ASE integrates earth and environmental life science, ecology, engineering and technology, human ecology, humanities, and the social sciences to address key issues of the environment and sustainability. We are hiring a laboratory manager to support the operation and management of research laboratories in the Asian School of the Environment. The laboratory manager will coordinate procurement of chemicals, consumables and scientific equipment; maintain chemical and equipment inventories; and oversee equipment servicing and maintenance. The role will provide training and technical support to students and researchers in the operation and troubleshooting of analytical instruments. The laboratory manager will also support laboratory safety, regulatory compliance, inspections and risk assessments, and contribute to the efficient day-to-day operation of research facilities. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate procurement of chemicals, lab consumables, field equipment, and scientific instrumentation to support research activities and operational requirements Provide training and technical support to undergraduate students, postgrad researchers, and lab users on the operation, maintenance and troubleshooting of analytical instruments including iSEAL, TOC/TN analyzer, ICP-OES, CHN analyzer and GC-MS. Maintain and manage comprehensive chemical inventories across multiple laboratories, ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements, and laboratory safety standards. Oversee equipment maintenance schedules, service records to ensure operational reliability and data quality Support asset tracking, inventory control, and lifecycle management of laboratory equipment Ensure laboratories meet health, safety and environmental requirements through regular inspections and risk assessments Serve as a member of the lab safety committee and chemical spill response team Provide operational and administrative support for lab management, ensuring efficient day-to-say functioning of research facilities Job Requirements: Bachelor Degree in chemistry, biology, environmental science, or equivalent. Experience working in a chemical and/or biological laboratory. Experience or familiarity with laboratory equipment, chemical management and laboratory safety. Familiarity with analytical instruments such as TOC/TN analyzers, ICP-OES, CHN analyzers and GC-MS is advantageous. Good organizational, troubleshooting and record-keeping skills. Good communication skills and ability to provide technical support and training. Able to work independently and as a good team player. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Analyst---Senior-Analyst---Associate-Research-Fellow--Centre-of-Excellence-for-National-Security---RSIS-_R00025792": {
      "title": "Research Analyst / Senior Analyst / Associate Research Fellow (Centre of Excellence for National Security) [RSIS]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nResearch Analyst / Senior Analyst / Associate Research Fellow (Centre of Excellence for National Security)   The S. Rajaratnam School of International Studies (RSIS) , a Graduate School of Nanyang Technological University (NTU), is a leading research-intensive and teaching institution on security research in the Asia-Pacific region. RSIS invites applications for the position of Associate Research Fellow / Senior Analyst / Research Analyst in the Centre of Excellence for National Security (CENS). The applicant is expected to: Contribute significantly to the policy-research agenda of CENS, specifically, AI-enabled Disinformation, Rumours, Untruths, Misinformation, Smears and strategic communications in relation to Singapore. Carry out administrative work. Assist in fostering a collegial environment within CENS and beyond – one that is conducive to high research productivity and good institutional citizenship. Specifically, they must demonstrate the ability to connect research objectives and findings to the interests, needs and strategic outcomes of CENS and RSIS. They must think and act beyond immediate/personal interests and possess a bigger picture view. They must collaborate effectively across and within CENS and RSIS to value-add to both entities. Other advantageous traits include: Self-starter, resourceful. Able to work both independently and collaboratively. Strong analytical, communication and facilitation skills.   In terms of qualifications/work experience, the candidate should: Possess a Masters degree in a relevant field or have working experience in a related domain for at least three years. Have a good understanding of the issues above and an ability to conduct policy-relevant research. Possess good command of the English language, as well as, good writing and research skills with an aptitude and interest for in-depth research on the policy-research agenda mentioned above. Preferably have some knowledge of AI such as vibe-coding skills and/or how to use AI for research, media and/or improve efficiency. All applicants should submit the following: A cover letter specifying how your qualifications match the job description. A detailed curriculum vitae. 2 published articles or writing samples. 3 reference letters. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For further information about RSIS, please visit our website: www.rsis.edu.sg Hiring Institution: RSIS"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Research-Programme-Management-_R00025812": {
      "title": "Manager (Research Programme Management)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Manager (Research Programme Management) is responsible for overseeing and driving NTU's research programmes and strategic initiatives in healthy longevity. The role supports the University's research and innovation objectives by developing and coordinating a shared scientific roadmap across NTU's academic units, implementing internal funding programmes to catalyse interdisciplinary collaborations, and strengthening NTU's competitiveness for external funding opportunities. The incumbent will work closely with Colleges, Schools, researchers, funding agencies, healthcare institutions, industry partners and other stakeholders to facilitate research translation, foster strategic partnerships, and support the successful delivery of healthy longevity research initiatives. The role also oversees the governance and administration of programme funding, ensuring effective, compliant and efficient management of resources to maximise research impact and outcomes. Key Responsibilities Develop and coordinate a shared scientific roadmap for healthy longevity across NTU's academic units. Implement internal funding initiatives and coordinate research programmes to foster interdisciplinary collaboration and maximise research impact. Build and manage strategic partnerships with academic, clinical, government, industry, and international stakeholders. Monitor programme performance, funding utilisation, and key deliverables to ensure successful implementation of research initiatives. Facilitate stakeholder engagement activities, workshops, symposia, and committee support related to healthy longevity initiatives. Job Requirements Bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline (e.g. Business Administration, Engineering, Science, Healthcare, Life Sciences, or related fields). At least 7 years of relevant experience in research programme management, research management, strategic planning, stakeholder engagement, partnership development, or related fields. Strong stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across diverse stakeholder groups. Strong analytical, organisational, and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deliver outcomes in a dynamic environment. Experience in the higher education, healthcare, research, public sector, or innovation ecosystem would be advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--R-R-Projects_R00025811": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, R&R Projects",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYou will be in the Projects team under the Office of Development & Facilities Management Department which oversees physical development, and maintenance of all University buildings and grounds in support of the academic, research and administrative functions of the University. In this role, you will be part of the Projects team to carry out renovation and upgrading of campus buildings and facilities.  Responsibilities: Lead a team of project officers to efficiently carry out and complete assigned R&R projects. Oversee project completion within the allocated budget and ensure the realization of design intents as provided by stakeholders. Fulfil all necessary project operational requirements and adhere to mandatory compliance regulations imposed by research activities. Provide custodial advice on user's requirements for project, encompassing their needs, preferences, desired timeline for completion, and the available funding sources. Lead in appointing and managing a team of consultants, including architects, engineers, and other professionals, to guide the project design process as required. Appointment of consultants to ensure accurate cost estimates and preparation of necessary documentation for tender procurement. Assume lead role in the tender process by soliciting and evaluating contractor bids, ultimately providing a recommendation for the contract award. Assess, manage and recommend changes to the project's scope or budget that may arise during construction. Regularly monitor the progress of the construction work to ensure the project stays on schedule and proactively identify any potential issues that may arise. Supervise the work being done on-site with team members to ensure the work is being carried out safely and to a high level of quality. Managing the construction contract, which entails managing payments, change orders, and other contractual obligations between the project team and the contractor. Requirements: Degree in Architecture / Building / Engineering / Project management or related field with at least 10 years of relevant working experience in Consultancy, Construction Management, Project Management, Facilities Management or equivalent. Demonstrate knowledge in building construction and proficiency in reading construction drawings. Good project management skills, including expertise in project planning, budgeting, scheduling, risk management, and stakeholder engagement. Ability to use AutoCAD/REVIT for design purposes and ability to perform accurate measurements will be added advantage. Adequate knowledge of procurement and construction contract administration. Good understanding of BCA Green mark requirements. Strong technical skills for checking and supervising professional consultants. Ability to monitor contractor’s performance by tracing Works Order list, site inspection and monthly reports. Strong problem-solving abilities in handling technical issues. Possess good interpersonal, communication and organization skills. Proactive, self-motivated and have sense of urgency toward work. Have a strong focus on customer satisfaction. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Technical-Specialist--Natural-Sciences-and-Science-Education-Department---NIE-_R00025810": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist (Natural Sciences and Science Education Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applications for a Technical Specialist position in the Natural Sciences and Science Education (NSSE) Department. This is a 2-year contract position. The key role of the Technical Specialist is to take care of different aspects of the teaching laboratories and ensuring the smooth and efficient running of the laboratory operations, including the safety of laboratory users. Key responsibilities Provide technical support for pre-service, in-service and post-graduate lab classes. Maintain and conduct troubleshooting for lab instruments/equipment in teaching and research labs. Willingness to learn the operation and safety protocols of the various scientific instruments to be assigned by the Head of Department. Ensure laboratory sessions are properly set up, i.e., equipment and consumables are properly prepared and cleaned after use. Plan and budget for the assigned Primary Science instrument maintenance, equipment upgrading, spare accessories, and consumables. Ensure laboratory instruments are in good working condition and maximize their lifetime.  Ensure adherence of safety procedures in the laboratories. Perform any other duties, e.g. in other science laboratories, as assigned by the reporting officer and Management team of NSSE Department. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma in Physics/Biology/Chemistry. Minimum 1-year related working experience in a science or related environment. Experience in providing technical support to students in higher education will be an added advantage. High level of safety awareness. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both written and oral. Ability to multitask, work independently, and effectively in a team. Hard-working, self-disciplined, responsible, and committed. Application The closing date of the advertisement is 2 October 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other information NIE Staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Engineering-and-Materials-Science-_R00025806": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Engineering and Materials Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is a collaboration between Nanofilm Technologies International Limited (“Nanofilm”, “NTI”), Nanyang Technological University (“NTU”) and supported by Singapore under RIE2025. The Laboratory’s objective is to propel Innovation and Technologies commercialisation through NTU’s innovation and NTI’s deep technology. NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory aligns with Singapore’s RIE2025 handbook – which emphasises the nation’s commitment to research and innovation, aiming to drive economic growth and address national challenges. The Nanyang Technological University NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is looking for a Research Engineer to oversee equipment operations, processes and maintenance for a safe, efficient environment. Responsible for coordinating equipment, ensuring compliance with safety standards, and leading a team towards successful research and development outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Oversee research equipment operations, ensuring safety and efficiency of research activities in Corp Lab. Uphold all relevant health and safety regulations from university within the laboratory. Running of equipment processes and maintenance of equipment to keep it in optimal conditions. Coordinate equipment scheduling, delivery, and maintenance together with researchers and project PIs Lead and train laboratory research staff and students, fostering a collaborative environment. Stay updated on technological advancements and implement quality controls. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a scientific, engineering, or related field. Research and development knowledge in nanotechnologies and thin film technologies are highly sought. Proven experience as a Equipment Engineer/Process Engineer or in a similar role, with a strong focus on equipment management. In-depth understanding of research laboratory equipment, operations, and principles. Effective communication and interpersonal skills, capable of maintaining robust working relationships. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Engineering-and-Materials-Science-_R00025807-1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Engineering and Materials Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is a collaboration between Nanofilm Technologies International Limited (“Nanofilm”, “NTI”), Nanyang Technological University (“NTU”) and supported by Singapore under RIE2025. The Laboratory’s objective is to propel Innovation and Technologies commercialisation through NTU’s innovation and NTI’s deep technology. NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory aligns with Singapore’s RIE2025 handbook – which emphasises the nation’s commitment to research and innovation, aiming to drive economic growth and address national challenges. The Nanyang Technological University NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is looking for a Research Engineer to oversee equipment operations, processes and maintenance for a safe, efficient environment. Responsible for coordinating equipment, ensuring compliance with safety standards, and leading a team towards successful research and development outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Oversee research equipment operations, ensuring safety and efficiency of research activities in Corp Lab. Uphold all relevant health and safety regulations from university within the laboratory. Running of equipment processes and maintenance of equipment to keep it in optimal conditions. Coordinate equipment scheduling, delivery, and maintenance together with researchers and project PIs Lead and train laboratory research staff and students, fostering a collaborative environment. Stay updated on technological advancements and implement quality controls. Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a scientific, engineering, or related field. Research and development knowledge in nanotechnologies and thin film technologies are highly sought. Proven experience as a Equipment Engineer/Process Engineer or in a similar role, with a strong focus on equipment management. In-depth understanding of research laboratory equipment, operations, and principles. Effective communication and interpersonal skills, capable of maintaining robust working relationships. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Manager--Engineering-and-Material-Science-_R00025805": {
      "title": "Project Manager (Engineering and Material Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is a collaboration between Nanofilm Technologies International Limited (“Nanofilm”, “NTI”), Nanyang Technological University (“NTU”) and supported by Singapore under RIE2025. The Laboratory’s objective is to propel Innovation and Technologies commercialisation through NTU’s innovation and NTI’s deep technology. NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory aligns with Singapore’s RIE2025 handbook – which emphasises the nation’s commitment to research and innovation, aiming to drive economic growth and address national challenges. The Nanyang Technological University NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is looking for a Project Manager to support the delivery of co-funded multidisciplinary research projects across the laboratory. Key Responsibilities: Lead the full project lifecycle from initiation and planning through execution, monitoring and closeout. Develop and maintain project plans, Gantt charts, milestones, resource schedules and reporting timelines. Monitor project progress and expenditure, including planned-versus-actual analysis, and coordinate corrective actions where necessary. Coordinate with funding agencies, industry partners, University administration, principal investigators, researchers, engineers, suppliers and collaborators. Prepare project status reports, progress updates and financial summaries for different stakeholder and governance requirements. Identify and mitigate project risks, manage issues proactively and escalate significant matters appropriately. Support grant administration and ensure compliance with funding agreements, funding agency guidelines and University policies. Job Requirements: MSc and/or Degree in Engineering or Materials Science; a relevant postgraduate qualification would be advantageous. At least 6-8 years of project management experience, preferably in a research, academic or multi-stakeholder environment. CAPM or PMP training or certification, with active certification preferred. Proficiency in Microsoft Project or equivalent tools such as Smartsheet, Primavera P6 or ProjectLibre, as well as Microsoft Office. Experience applying waterfall, agile or hybrid project management methodologies to research-driven projects. Strong stakeholder management, analytical, reporting and problem-solving capabilities. Proficiency in written and spoken English and Mandarin to communicate with suppliers, partners and stakeholders. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Manager--Engineering-and-Material-Science-_R00025804": {
      "title": "Project Manager (Engineering and Material Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is a collaboration between Nanofilm Technologies International Limited (“Nanofilm”, “NTI”), Nanyang Technological University (“NTU”) and supported by Singapore under RIE2025. The Laboratory’s objective is to propel Innovation and Technologies commercialisation through NTU’s innovation and NTI’s deep technology. NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory aligns with Singapore’s RIE2025 handbook – which emphasises the nation’s commitment to research and innovation, aiming to drive economic growth and address national challenges. The Nanyang Technological University NTI-NTU Corporate Laboratory is looking for a Project Manager to support the delivery of co-funded multidisciplinary research projects across the laboratory. Key Responsibilities: Lead the full project lifecycle from initiation and planning through execution, monitoring and closeout. Develop and maintain project plans, Gantt charts, milestones, resource schedules and reporting timelines. Monitor project progress and expenditure, including planned-versus-actual analysis, and coordinate corrective actions where necessary. Coordinate with funding agencies, industry partners, University administration, principal investigators, researchers, engineers, suppliers and collaborators. Prepare project status reports, progress updates and financial summaries for different stakeholder and governance requirements. Identify and mitigate project risks, manage issues proactively and escalate significant matters appropriately. Support grant administration and ensure compliance with funding agreements, funding agency guidelines and University policies. Job Requirements: MSc and/or Degree in Engineering or Materials Science; a relevant postgraduate qualification would be advantageous. At least 6-8 years of project management experience, preferably in a research, academic or multi-stakeholder environment. CAPM or PMP training or certification, with active certification preferred. Proficiency in Microsoft Project or equivalent tools such as Smartsheet, Primavera P6 or ProjectLibre, as well as Microsoft Office. Experience applying waterfall, agile or hybrid project management methodologies to research-driven projects. Strong stakeholder management, analytical, reporting and problem-solving capabilities. Proficiency in written and spoken English and Mandarin to communicate with suppliers, partners and stakeholders. ​ We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Science-_R00025803-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow’. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: The candidate will work on the project to conduct research and literature review on AI for quantitative trading and financial investment. Develop a new AI solution to find the optimal strategy Conduct experiment to verify the efficiency of the designed solution Analyze data acquired from the field survey and make comparison Writing research papers to report the results Job Requirements: Preferably Master’s degree in Computer Science and related discipline. Sufficient experience and knowledge in finance. Expertise in computer programming Good knowledge and experience on Software Engineering is a plus. Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Communication-Studies-Psychology-Social-Sciences-Education-_R00025799": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Communication Studies/Psychology/Social Sciences/Education)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished as a partnership between Nanyang Technological University (NTU) and the National Healthcare Group (NHG), the Asian Centre for Health Behavioural Insights & Interventions (HABITS) aims to improve population health through multidisciplinary and translational research to support interventions, policy and programmes; strengthen national capabilities through the integration of translational research into health intervention processes; and increase Singapore’s regional and international profile as a centre of excellence for health behavioural sciences. We are looking for a Research Associate to work closely with the Centre's Pillar Leads and Directors to support the management of research projects and the development of competitive research grant applications. The Research Associate will contribute to the end-to-end execution of research projects, from study planning and implementation through to data analysis and dissemination. Responsibilities include coordinating participant recruitment and data collection, managing day-to-day research operations, maintaining research databases and study documentation, overseeing project budgets, procurement, assets, and ethics submissions, ensuring compliance with institutional and regulatory requirements, conducting quantitative and qualitative data analyses, preparing research reports and manuscripts for publication, and research translation activities. Key Responsibilities: Support the planning, coordination, and day-to-day management of research projects to ensure timely delivery of project milestones and deliverables. Assist with the preparation and development of competitive research grant applications, including literature reviews, proposal writing, budgeting, and supporting documentation. Coordinate end-to-end research activities, including participant recruitment, scheduling, data collection, and study implementation across multiple projects. Prepare and manage ethics applications, regulatory submissions, and study documentation, ensuring compliance with institutional, ethical, and data governance requirements. Manage research databases, maintain accurate study records, and oversee the secure storage and handling of research data in accordance with institutional policies. Conduct quantitative and/or qualitative data analysis using appropriate research methods and statistical software. Prepare research reports, manuscripts, conference abstracts, presentations, and other scholarly outputs for dissemination. Coordinate project logistics, including procurement, budgeting, financial tracking, research assets, and vendor management where required. Liaise with internal and external stakeholders, including collaborators, funding agencies, schools, community partners, and government agencies, to facilitate project implementation. Undertake other relevant research, administrative, and operational duties as assigned by the Centre's Pillar Leads and Directors. Job Requirements: Master's degree in Communication Studies, Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, or a related discipline. Knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methodologies, including experimental and survey design, focus group discussions, and associated data collection and analysis. Prior experience in coordinating or managing academic or applied research projects. Familiarity with research involving adolescents, digital wellbeing, health, schools, or community-based interventions would be an advantage. Possesses strong interpersonal and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively with schools, government agencies, healthcare organisations, community partners, and other collaborators. ​ We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Communication-Studies--Psychology--Social-Sciences-Education-_R00025798": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Communication Studies/ Psychology/ Social Sciences/Education)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished as a partnership between Nanyang Technological University (NTU) and the National Healthcare Group (NHG), the Asian Centre for Health Behavioural Insights & Interventions (HABITS) aims to improve population health through multidisciplinary and translational research to support interventions, policy and programmes; strengthen national capabilities through the integration of translational research into health intervention processes; and increase Singapore’s regional and international profile as a centre of excellence for health behavioural sciences. We are looking for a Research Fellow to work closely with the Centre's Pillar Leads and Directors to support the management of research projects and the development of competitive research grant applications. The Research fellow will contribute to the end-to-end execution of research projects, from study planning and implementation through to data analysis and dissemination. Responsibilities include coordinating participant recruitment and data collection, managing day-to-day research operations, maintaining research databases and study documentation, overseeing project budgets, procurement, assets, and ethics submissions, ensuring compliance with institutional and regulatory requirements, conducting quantitative and qualitative data analyses, preparing research reports and manuscripts for publication, and research translation activities. Key Responsibilities: Lead the planning, coordination, and day-to-day management of research projects to ensure timely delivery of project milestones and deliverables. Assist with the preparation and development of competitive research grant applications, including literature reviews, proposal writing, budgeting, and supporting documentation. Coordinate end-to-end research activities, including participant recruitment, scheduling, data collection, and study implementation across multiple projects. Prepare and manage ethics applications, regulatory submissions, and study documentation, ensuring compliance with institutional, ethical, and data governance requirements. Manage research databases, maintain accurate study records, and oversee the secure storage and handling of research data in accordance with institutional policies. Conduct quantitative and/or qualitative data analysis using appropriate research methods and statistical software. Prepare research reports, manuscripts, conference abstracts, presentations, and other scholarly outputs for dissemination. Coordinate project logistics, including procurement, budgeting, financial tracking, research assets, and vendor management where required. Liaise with internal and external stakeholders, including collaborators, funding agencies, schools, community partners, and government agencies, to facilitate project implementation. Undertake other relevant research, administrative, and operational duties as assigned by the Centre's Pillar Leads and Directors. Job Requirements: PhD in Communication Studies, Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, or a related discipline. Knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methodologies, including experimental and survey design, focus group discussions, and associated data collection and analysis. Prior experience in coordinating or managing academic or applied research projects. Familiarity with research involving adolescents, digital wellbeing, health, schools, or community-based interventions would be an advantage. Possesses strong interpersonal and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively with schools, government agencies, healthcare organisations, community partners, and other collaborators. ​ We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Web-Projects-and-Digital-Experience_R00025828": {
      "title": "Manager, Web Projects and Digital Experience",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNTU’s corporate web estate spans more than 150 site instances and over 50,000 pages and content items. As a key inbound communications channel, it is where prospective students, researchers, partners, donors, media and the public discover NTU, understand what the University has to offer and, ultimately, choose to engage. Its effectiveness therefore depends not only on robust technology and disciplined delivery, but also on sound digital communications and editorial judgement. We are looking for a Manager, Web Projects and Digital Experience to drive the delivery and continuous improvement of NTU’s web and digital communications initiatives. Sitting at the intersection of project management, digital communications, user experience and web technology, the role will independently manage multiple projects of varying scale – from major website revamps, replatforming and content migration exercises to targeted enhancements and optimisation initiatives. Beyond ensuring that projects are delivered effectively, the successful candidate will help translate the University’s communications and marketing objectives into digital experiences that are discoverable, intuitive and effective in moving audiences towards meaningful action. Working closely with internal stakeholders, vendors and delivery partners, the role will bring together project management discipline with a strong understanding of audience journeys, search optimisation, content, conversion, analytics and user experience to improve the performance of NTU’s web estate over time.   Main Responsibilities Lead end-to-end web and digital projects from planning and requirements gathering through development, UAT, deployment, go-live and post-implementation support, ensuring delivery to agreed scope, timeline and budget. Manage project governance and delivery, including project plans, milestones, dependencies, risks, issues, change requests, budgets and management reporting, with timely escalation and resolution of key matters. Translate business, communications and marketing objectives into clear requirements, user stories, functional specifications and acceptance criteria, ensuring alignment among stakeholders throughout the project lifecycle. Manage internal and external delivery partners, including appointed vendors and agencies, to ensure deliverables, solution designs, service levels and contractual commitments are met. Drive digital experience and audience journey optimisation, applying user experience, information architecture, content structure, audience segmentation and conversion principles to improve how audiences discover and engage with NTU. Strengthen NTU’s inbound digital performance, including SEO, AEO and GEO, search visibility, landing-page effectiveness, conversion optimisation, lead generation and web analytics. Uphold web quality, accessibility and experience standards across the corporate web estate, including design consistency, WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility, performance, content quality, navigation and information architecture. Use data and user insights to inform improvements, leveraging web analytics, search data, user research and usability testing to identify opportunities and prioritise enhancements. Strengthen web governance and operational readiness, including publishing workflows, roles and permissions, quality assurance, content review cycles, documentation, training and transition of projects into business-as-usual operations. Coordinate multiple concurrent projects and priorities, maintaining a forward view of the web project pipeline and sequencing initiatives according to strategic priorities, resources, budgets and stakeholder readiness. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Business, Communications, Digital Media, Marketing or a related discipline, with 5–8 years of relevant project management experience. Proven track record in independently managing end-to-end website and digital projects, including website redesigns, replatforming, content migration and digital enhancements. Strong experience in vendor, agency and stakeholder management, with the ability to manage multiple projects, competing priorities, budgets, timelines and risks in a complex organisation. Strong understanding of digital experience and inbound marketing, including SEO, AEO, GEO, audience journeys, conversion optimisation, information architecture and web analytics. Working knowledge of web technologies and CMS platforms such as Sitefinity, Sitecore, Drupal, WordPress or Adobe Experience Manager, with sufficient technical literacy to engage effectively with developers and vendors. Good understanding of UX, accessibility and web quality standards, with experience using analytics, search data and user insights to drive continuous improvement. Excellent communication, project management and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate business and marketing objectives into clear requirements and communicate effectively with both technical and senior stakeholders. Project management certification (e.g. PMP, PRINCE2, Scrum Master) or relevant digital marketing, SEO, analytics or UX certification would be an advantage. Experience in higher education, public sector or other large organisations is preferred. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-MSAE-Programme--SSS-_R00025818": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in MSAE Programme (SSS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences is looking for Part-time Lecturers (PTL) who will be responsible for conducting lecturers, tutorials and assessments so as to impart practical knowledge to students of the Master of Science in Applied Economics. Key Responsibilities: 1. Teaching Duties: • Conduct lecturers and/or tutorials 2. Course Assignment Duties: • Assess project • Set exam questions, • Conduct invigilation, • Mark exam scripts • Enter exam marks in online system • Board of Examiners meeting – to discuss on the student’s examination marks for his course and general issues on examination matters • PhD degree in Economics/Finance or related fields • Extensive industry and/or academic experience • Effective communication skills (written and verbal) • Strong ability in facilitating classroom-based and online learning Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Wearable-Robotics-and-Biomechanics-_R00025823-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Wearable Robotics and Biomechanics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research .   We are looking for a  Research Fellow, Wearable robotics and Biomechanics to conduct research and develop innovative robotic technologies for understanding, enhancing, and restoring human movement. The role will focus on wearable robotics, human biomechanics, intelligent sensing and control, and assistive technologies, including exoskeletons, powered prostheses, and balance augmentation systems. The Research Fellow will contribute to high-impact research, lead independent research activities, publish research findings, develop new research directions, and support the growth of the research group.   Key Responsibilities: Lead independent research in wearable robotics, biomechanics, human movement, and assistive technologies, including developing new research directions and research proposals. Develop and validate robotic systems such as wearable exoskeletons, powered prostheses, and balance augmentation systems through computational modelling, system development, and experimental studies. Publish and disseminate research findings through high-quality journal and conference publications, presentations, and other scholarly activities. Mentor and supervise students and contribute to research collaborations and a productive research environment within the group.     Job Requirements: Education qualifications: PhD in Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, Biomedical Engineering, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Control Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Candidates who are nearing completion of their PhD may also be considered, subject to completion before the appointment.   Soft skills: Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary research environment.  Strong problem-solving skills and initiative in developing new research ideas.   Hard skills: Strong background in one or more of the following areas: robotics, control, biomechanics, wearable robotics, human movement, sensing, or artificial intelligence. Experience with robotic system development, computational modelling, experimental design, or human-subject experiments. Proficiency in programming and data analysis using MATLAB, Python, C/C++, or equivalent tools.   Experience: Demonstrated research experience through peer-reviewed publications in relevant fields. Experience in developing and experimentally validating robotic or wearable systems is preferred. Experience in supervising or mentoring students and/or contributing to research proposals is an advantage.   Competencies: Ability to independently formulate research questions, develop methodologies, and execute research projects. Ability to integrate knowledge across robotics, biomechanics, sensing, control, and AI. Ability to analyze experimental data and communicate research findings effectively.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Molecular-Microbiology-and-Biotechnology-_R00025821": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Molecular Microbiology and Biotechnology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nGlobally recognized as a leading research and technology organization, the Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI) addresses national priorities through its diverse expertise in Biotechnology and Bioprocesses, Membrane Technology, Chemicals and Materials, Resource Recovery, and Modeling & Artificial Intelligence. By harnessing its cross-cutting, interdisciplinary, and transformative capabilities, NEWRI drives innovation in water circularity and sustainability, next-generation solid waste solutions, circular economy resource recovery, climate resilience and digitalization.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/newri .   We are seeking a Research Fellow to join an academic research project on antimicrobial resistance (AMR). The successful candidate will conduct molecular microbiology and biotechnology research to investigate AMR mechanisms and the mobility of resistance genes. The work will combine microbiological and molecular experiments with data analysis to understand resistance phenotypes, genetic determinants, and gene transfer. Candidates with bioinformatics expertise are particularly encouraged to apply.   Key Responsibilities: Conduct molecular microbiology and biotechnology experiments related to AMR and gene mobility. Perform microbial cultivation, molecular biology, genetic, and antimicrobial susceptibility analyses. Analyze experimental results and, where applicable, genomic or other omics datasets. Integrate laboratory and computational findings and contribute to manuscripts, reports, and presentations. Collaborate with project members and support student mentoring and good research practices.   Job Requirements: PhD in microbiology, molecular microbiology, biotechnology, molecular biology, environmental engineering, bioengineering, or a related field. Strong hands-on experience in microbiology and molecular biology research techniques. Experience in antimicrobial resistance, microbial genetics, gene mobility, or microbial genomics is preferred. Bioinformatics skills, including analysis of genomic/metagenomic/transcriptomic data, would be an advantage. Experience with R, Python, Linux/Unix, sequence-analysis tools, or biological databases is an advantage. Good analytical, scientific writing, communication, organizational, and teamwork skills. Entry level candidates with a relevant PhD are welcome to apply.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Centre-for-Health--Culture--and-Society-_R00025817": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Centre for Health, Culture, and Society)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Centre for Health, Culture, and Society (CHCS) at NTU CoHASS is a new interdisciplinary and cross-sector research hub dedicated to understanding health and sickness through the concept of the lifeworld — the social, cultural, and historical horizons within which patients, practitioners, and caregivers make sense of their experiences. Working with faculty across all four CoHASS Schools and established partnerships with major Singapore hospitals and arts organisations, the Centre advances research across five thematic strands: Digital Health, Medical Pluralism, Arts for Health, Healthcare Systems, and Disability Studies. We are seeking a Research Fellow to conduct interdisciplinary research within one or more of the Centre's thematic strands, engage with cross-sector partners, assist with grant development, contribute to our undergraduate and postgraduate teaching programmes, and support the Centre's wider activities. Key Responsibilities: Conduct and publish interdisciplinary research within the Centre's thematic strands. Engage with hospital, arts, and community partners on cross-sector research projects. Assist with grant applications to various funding bodies. Contribute to teaching on the MA in Health, Culture, and Society. Mentor student researchers and support the Centre's PPI initiatives. Contribute to the Centre's seminars, events, publications programme, and outreach activities. Job Requirements: PhD's degree in a relevant humanities or social sciences discipline. Academic expertise in health, culture, and/or society; commitment to the lifeworld approach. Track record of independent research and scholarly outputs. Experience or aptitude for interdisciplinary and cross-sector collaboration. Strong communication skills and ability to engage academic and non-academic audiences. Entry-level candidates are welcome to apply. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Events-Officer--RSIS-_R00025794": {
      "title": "Senior Events Officer [RSIS]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe S. Rajaratnam School of International Studies (RSIS) , a Graduate School of Nanyang Technological University (NTU), is a leading professional school of international affairs and policy-oriented think tank. The School invites suitably qualified individuals for the position of: SENIOR EVENTS OFFICER The successful candidate will report to the Head, Events and assume the following responsibilities: Provide administrative support for RSIS’ Events Unit Assume the role of Event Lead for events Assist the Event Supervisor to organise and manage events with responsibilities for all administrative and logistical tasks including, where necessary, liaison with speakers and guests, flight and accommodation arrangements, vendors liaison, budget management, conducting of rehearsals and virtual test calls Monitor the progress of event planning and execution Ensure the event administrative and operational requirements are met Ensure compliance with RSIS and NTU policies and regulations   Requirements: Diploma with 1-2 years’ relevant experience Strong communication, organisational and interpersonal skills Proficiency in MS Office applications Proficiency in virtual events software is preferred Knowledge of ITQ/ITT process for procurement of goods and services is preferred All applicants should submit the following: A cover letter specifying how your qualifications match the job description; and A detailed curriculum vitae. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For further information about RSIS, please visit our website: www.rsis.edu.sg . Hiring Institution: RSIS"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Student-Development_R00025845": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Student Affairs Office (SAO) plays a key role in fostering the holistic development of students, co-creating a vibrant, meaningful and enriching student life experience through student-led activities, leadership development, transition and integration efforts, residential programmes, and community engagement. The Assistant Director, Student Development provides overall leadership and integration across the following portfolios: Transition, Undergraduate Student Development, Postgraduate Student Development, and Governance. The role leads the portfolio leads and their teams, sets collective priorities and operating direction, and is accountable for coherence of student development outcomes across the student lifecycle. Key Responsibilities Lead for Transition Experience (Undergraduate and Postgraduate) Set the strategic direction and desired outcomes for the university-level Transition portfolio, and hold the portfolio lead accountable for translating the year-long Transition framework into plans and delivery aligned with the University's student development priorities. Advise and staff the Vice Provost and Director in leading the University Orientation Coordinating Committee, synthesising issues across Schools, residential halls and student bodies, recommending institution-level priorities and trade-offs, and ensuring portfolio leads follow through on committee decisions. Provide executive oversight of the Transition and Orientation Programme (TOP), setting outcomes, governance parameters and cross-University priorities. Hold the Transition portfolio lead accountable for operational delivery and intervene on material cross-unit issues, risks and decisions that require Assistant Director-level resolution. Lead for Undergraduate and Postgraduate Student Development Student Development Programmes: Strategise and drive, in partnership with Associate Deans and Associate Chairs and through the portfolio lead, student development programmes to advance undergraduate and postgraduate student development, engagement, well-being and overall satisfaction, while promoting Inter-School collaboration and UG-PG collaboration within Schools. Strategic Oversight of the School Constituent Clubs and Scholar Clubs: Provide oversight, through the portfolio lead, for Schools Constituent Clubs, both undergraduate and postgraduate, and NTU Honours College in developing student leaders through experiential participation in student club activities. Strategic Oversight of the NTU Students’ Union and the Graduate Students’ Association: Provide senior oversight for portfolio lead's advisory relationship with NTUSU and GSA in aligning their activities and policies with NTU’s broader mission. Act as a bridge between NTUSU/GSA, university administration, and external partners, fostering strong relationships and ensuring constructive dialogue and actionable outcomes on topics such as academic options, campus facilities, and student welfare. Lead for Policy and Governance for all Student Organisations Lead the team in charge of the formulation, review, and operationalisation of Policy and Governance for all Student Organisations across constituition, activities, finance, safety to ensure coherence and consistent implementation. Determine the stakeholder and escalation approach for significant policy changes; lead engagement where issues have University-wide implications or require alignment among senior academic and administrative stakeholders. Serve as the policy subject matter expert consultant to stakeholders. Requirements: Degree in any discipline At least 10–12 years of relevant working experience involving considerable interaction with students or youth, with a minimum of 3 years in a supervisory role. Experience in the tertiary education sector is advantageous. Deep understanding of student development practices and co-curricular programme design, with a strong grasp of pedagogical skills and direct experience in designing and facilitating learning experiences. Proven track record in stakeholder management, with excellent communication, negotiation and influencing skills across organisational hierarchy. A strong passion for nurturing and developing students, combined with demonstrated ability to lead multiple portfolio leads and teams, establish clear accountabilities, coach managers, manage performance and capability, and align resources and priorities across interdependent workstreams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Centre-Administration---Centre-for-Health--Culture--and-Society_R00025847": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (Centre Administration), Centre for Health, Culture, and Society",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAbout us Nanyang Technological University is a research-intensive university known for connecting technology with human-centred design. The Centre for Health, Culture, and Society is a new interdisciplinary research centre in the College of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences, dedicated to advancing research and creative practice at the intersection of health, culture, and society. We bring together researchers from across four Schools with doctors, artists, writers, caregivers, and patients to understand how culture, communication, and creativity shape the way people live with health and illness. We work in partnership with major Singapore hospitals, arts organisations, and patient advocacy groups, and we run a seminar series, annual conferences, practitioner workshops, and a taught Masters programme. The role We are looking for a Centre Administrator to run the administrative, financial, and operational side of the Centre. Reporting to the Director, you will be our sole dedicated administrator, and you will have unusual scope to shape how a new centre works. This is a varied role for someone who enjoys owning processes end to end. You will: Manage and monitor the Centre's budgets across several funding streams, process financial transactions, and prepare financial reports for the Director and funders. Support grant applications and manage post-award reporting, milestone tracking, and audit documentation. Plan and deliver our events programme, including conferences, a seminar series, and workshops for healthcare professionals. Act as the administrative point of contact for our hospital, arts, and community partners, and maintain partnership records and agreements. Provide secretariat support to the Centre's Steering Committee and advisory boards. Maintain our website, newsletters, and mailing lists, and support public engagement. Coordinate recruitment, onboarding, and visitor arrangements with NTU Human Resources, and support our Masters and undergraduate programmes. Why join us You will be joining at the founding stage, with real influence over how the Centre operates and a broad portfolio spanning research administration, events, partnerships, and communications. We are committed to the career development of everyone in the Centre and you will have access to NTU's learning and development programmes, staff welfare initiatives, and flexible working arrangements. You will work alongside researchers, clinicians, and artists on questions that matter to people's lives. What we are looking for — essential A good Bachelor's degree in any discipline. At least three to five years of experience in an administrative, project coordination, or operations role, ideally in a university, research institute, hospital, arts organisation, or non-profit. Demonstrated experience of managing budgets and financial administration independently, with meticulous attention to detail. Experience of organising events from planning through to delivery and reporting. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing deadlines with limited supervision. Proficiency in Microsoft Office. Good to have Experience of research grant administration, pre-award or post-award. A background in the humanities, social sciences, public administration, or business administration. Familiarity with NTU or comparable university finance, procurement, and HR systems. Experience of working with hospitals, arts organisations, or community partners. Website content management and newsletter or social media experience. An interest in health, culture, and society. This is a three-year fixed-term appointment, renewable. Based at NTU's Nanyang Avenue campus. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Science-_R00025846": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty.   A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow’. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing.   Job Responsibilities: The candidate will work on the project to conduct research and literature review on AI for smart manufacturing. Develop a new AI solution to find the optimal strategy Conduct experiment to verify the efficiency of the designed solution Analyze data acquired from the field survey and make comparison Writing research papers to report the results   Job Requirements: Preferably Master’s degree in Computer Science and related discipline. Sufficient experience and knowledge in manufacturing. Expertise in computer programming Good knowledge and experience on Software Engineering is a plus. Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.     Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/NIE-Overseas-Graduate-Scholarship--Policy--Curriculum---Leadership-_R00025827-1": {
      "title": "NIE Overseas Graduate Scholarship (Policy, Curriculum & Leadership)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nOBJECTIVE   The National Institute of Education Overseas Graduate Scholarship (NIE OGS) will sponsor outstanding candidates to pursue full-time doctoral studies overseas. Upon completion of their doctoral studies, candidates will return to NIE to serve as educators and academics.     ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA   The applicant must fulfill the following criteria:   Be a Singapore Citizen. Has excellent academic records with very good Honours or Master’s degrees (or professional qualifications of equivalent standing), with relevant teaching and some research experience. Has the passion to pursue a challenging career in academia.     TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF SCHOLARSHIP   The scholarship is tenable for a period of three years. The scholarship will provide:   Two sets of economy class air tickets (one at commencement and completion of doctoral studies, and one to return to Singapore for data collection for doctoral thesis). Overseas maintenance allowance. Stipend. Pre-studies allowance (at commencement of doctoral studies). Thesis allowance (upon completion of doctoral studies). Tuition and other compulsory fees. Conference and fieldwork grants (by application).   A scholar studying in the United States may be considered for a fourth year of sponsorship if the required minimum period of candidature is at least 4 years.   The scholar may be required to serve a few months in the Ministry of Education (MOE) Headquarters before embarking on his/her doctoral studies (if applicable).   The scholar will be required to enter into a bond to serve the National Institute of Education Nanyang Technological University (NIE NTU) as an employee for a period of five years upon obtaining the doctoral degree.   NIE NTU reserves the right to revise the terms and conditions of the scholarship as it deems fit.     AREA OF STUDY Educational Policy   The Policy, Curriculum & Leadership (PCL) Department at NIE leads in educational policy, curriculum, and leadership studies that contribute to both theory and practice. We believe education is central to improving lives and societies, and seek to develop wisdom in policy-making, discernment in curriculum, and foresight in leadership. Our work examines complex educational challenges and the ways in which policies, institutions, and systems respond to changing social, economic, technological, and political conditions, while advancing research, teaching, and societal impact in Singapore and internationally.   This call invites applicants who share our mission and wish to pursue a PhD in Educational Policy . Educational policy is concerned with how educational problems are defined, how policies are formulated and implemented, how decisions are shaped by institutions and different actors, and how policies influence educational systems, organisations, practices, and outcomes. It encompasses areas such as policy formation and implementation, governance, educational reform, equity and inclusion, accountability, regulation, financing, data and evidence use, and the relationships between education and wider social, economic, political, and technological change. Applicants may pursue a wide range of policy questions, including how policies emerge and evolve, how they are interpreted and enacted across different levels of the education system, why reforms produce particular intended or unintended consequences, and how educational systems respond to major contemporary challenges.     Applicants should meet the following criteria:   At least a Second Class Honours (Upper Division) degree, or a Master’s degree from a recognised institution, with a strong academic record. Candidates may come from education or from other relevant disciplines, including but not limited to public policy, sociology, political science, economics, statistics, management, history, or the humanities. Demonstrate a strong interest in educational policy and an understanding of significant issues and challenges facing education systems. This may be developed through academic study, research, professional experience, work in education or the public sector, or other relevant experiences. Prior teaching experience is not required.   Demonstrate strong potential for doctoral-level research in educational policy, evidenced through academic achievement and/or relevant research, analytical, professional, or intellectual work. Candidates with interdisciplinary backgrounds and methodological strengths that can be applied to the study of educational policy are particularly welcome.   Demonstrate intellectual curiosity, commitment to developing expertise in educational policy, and the potential to contribute to NIE through research, teaching, and service following completion of the PhD. Prior experience in educational policy research or teaching is not required.     APPLICATION PROCESS   The following supporting documents must be submitted together with the application form to NIE NTU, through Workday, by the closing date :   Curriculum Vitae (which should include academic qualifications, employment history, scholarships & awards, a brief description of your research experience and publication list if available).   A succinct write-up (2 pages) on the research topic which you intend to pursue.   A succinct write-up (4 pages) on your commitment and interest in the area of study applied for and the expected contribution to NIE, schools and the Singapore education system.   An abstract of any thesis previously written.   Copies of two pieces of research work that you consider to be your most significant works (if available).   All relevant educational certificates and transcripts including GCE ‘O’ Level, GCE ‘A’ Level, Polytechnic Diploma, University Degree(s).   Letters for scholarships, prizes, other awards, memberships in academic & professional societies (if available).   A copy of the letter(s) of offer from each university applied to for admission to doctoral studies (if available).   A copy of the letter(s) of offer for other scholarships and/or awards applied for and the outcome of these applications (if available).   A minimum of two confidential referees’ reports (preferably from academic referees) printed on the official letterhead, to be sent directly to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CONTACT INFORMATION   For clarification or more information, please contact:   Area of Study   Head, PCL for Educational Policy here .   Terms and Conditions of Scholarship   NIE Human Resource Department - Email to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg .     CLOSING DATE   All applications, together with the required documents (a) to (j), must be submitted by 30 November 2026 .   Please note that NIE reserves the right to consider only complete applications accompanied by all required documents.   Each application will be assessed on its own merits. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Nanomaterials-_R00025836": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Nanomaterials)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Institute for Digital Molecular Analytics and Science (IDMxS), officially launched on 1 December 2022, is a Research Centre of Excellence (RCE) supported by a total investment of around S$160 million over 10 years. The key objective is to support efforts on interfacing the biological and living world with the world of information technology and data science. For more details, please view https://idmxs.org/.   We are looking for a Project Officer (PO) to support the development of machine learning-driven, array-based nanosensors for detecting and differentiating complex, multi-component mixtures. The role will focus on the design and fabrication of receptor-functionalized nanoparticles, the collection and analysis of spectroscopic data across multiple receptor-analyte pairs, the investigation of underlying receptor-analyte interactions, and the development of suitable machine learning frameworks for the selection and optimization of receptor combinations for different analytical tasks.   Key Responsibilities: Design and functionalize nanoparticles with different molecular receptors for array-based nanosensing. Perform spectroscopic measurements, including surface-enhanced Raman scattering (SERS), to investigate receptor-analyte interactions. Establish a spectroscopic database comprising measurements across multiple receptor-analyte pairs. Perform data processing, analysis, and interpretation of spectroscopic measurements. Investigate underlying receptor-analyte interactions with the aid of in silico calculations, including density functional theory (DFT) simulations. Apply machine learning approaches to evaluate, select, and optimize receptor combinations for different analytical tasks. Assist the Principal Investigator with the preparation of research papers and other scientific outputs.   Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in chemistry, materials science, or a related discipline. Min 3 years of relevant research experience in nanomaterial synthesis, characterization, surface functionalization, and/or applications in molecular sensing. Experience with spectroscopic techniques, particularly surface-enhanced Raman spectroscopy, including the analysis and interpretation of spectroscopic data. Familiarity with computational approaches for investigating molecular interactions, such as density functional theory (DFT) simulations. Familiarity with machine learning approaches applied to spectroscopic datasets. Good communication skills, with the ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Laboratory-_R00025835": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Laboratory)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Institute for Digital Molecular Analytics and Science (IDMxS), officially launched on 1 December 2022, is a Research Centre of Excellence (RCE) supported by a total investment of around S$160 million over 10 years. IDMxS’ overarching approach is to go beyond the neat simplicity of intermolecular interactions in dilute media and embrace the inherent complexity of biological interactions and dense heterogeneity of their environments.  For more details, please view https://idmxs.org/ .   Key Responsibilities: Laboratory Setup, Operations & Resource Management  Lead the setup, commissioning, and operational readiness of the new lab at IDMxS Level 7, including space planning, equipment installation, and workflow design.  Oversee day-to-day laboratory operations to ensure effective utilization of resources (equipment, chemicals, gases, and consumables) in alignment with research priorities.  Establish and maintain laboratory-level management systems (e.g., inventory tracking, equipment coordination, SOP frameworks), in alignment with IDMxS institutional policies and shared service structures.  Identify opportunities to enhance laboratory workflows and operational efficiency, and implement improvements in coordination with relevant institutional teams.   Research Project & Operational Support Provide operational and coordination support to Prof. Bazan’s research programs, including tracking project timelines, facilitating resource planning, and supporting milestone delivery. Support grant-related activities at the laboratory level, including budget tracking, documentation preparation, and coordination with institutional offices. Contribute to the preparation of research proposals and progress reports, supporting effective communication of research direction and outcomes.   Procurement Coordination & Resource Planning Strategize and oversee laboratory-specific procurement requirements, including equipment, chemicals, gases, and consumables, and work closely with IDMxS procurement and finance teams to ensure timely and compliant acquisition. Support vendor engagement, technical evaluation, and planning of major equipment purchases in alignment with research requirements. Facilitate efficient procurement workflows at the laboratory level while adhering to institutional processes.   Laboratory Safety & Compliance Support the implementation of laboratory safety practices in alignment with IDMxS safety policies and regulatory requirements. Coordinate risk assessments, safety training, and onboarding processes for laboratory personnel in collaboration with institutional safety teams. Mentor and oversee the operational conduct of research staff and students within the laboratory to maintain high standards of professional practice. Promote a strong culture of safety and compliance within the synthesis laboratory environment.   Laboratory Coordination, Engagement & Representation Coordinate laboratory access, visits, and collaborations, ensuring operational readiness and effective communication of laboratory capabilities. Serve as a key interface between Prof. Bazan’s laboratory and IDMxS administrative and technical units, facilitating smooth coordination and information flow. Support engagement with external collaborators and partners through coordination of laboratory-related activities.   Requirements: PhD in a relevant discipline with 8 years postdoctoral or research experience in a laboratory setting. Experience in lab setup, operations, resource planning, and implementation of SOPs and systems. Ability to support research programmes, track timelines, and contribute to grant and reporting activities. Experience in procurement planning, vendor coordination, and working with finance/procurement processes. Understanding of lab safety practices, risk assessments, and regulatory requirements. Coordination and communication skills with faculty, researchers, and support units. Ability to manage multiple priorities and drive operational improvements independently. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Coral-Reef-Ecosystems-_R00025837": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Coral Reef Ecosystems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) at Nanyang Technological University is seeking a Research Fellow (Post-doctoral) in Coral Reef Ecosystems for an initial 12-month appointment, with potential for extension subject to project needs and funding. The Fellow will work under Assistant Professor Kyle Morgan to integrate existing and newly collected photoquadrat, multiscale photogrammetry and environmental datasets to identify regional spatial patterns and temporal trends in ecological processes and carbonate budgets across South and Southeast Asia. The ideal candidate will have strong research interests in fundamental field-based coral reef science, carbonate budgets, and analysis of large, complex ecological datasets. Experience in coral bleaching research, reef resilience, and/or climate-driven ecological change would be highly desirable. The Research Fellow will develop ambitious, frontier research questions and lead high-quality peer-reviewed publications. They will contribute to regional field campaigns, collaborative research, and capacity building, while independently developing and delivering a coherent research programme within the group.   Key Responsibilities: Lead research, analysis and publications on coral reef ecology, coral bleaching and carbonate budgets. Analyse large regional photoquadrat, photogrammetry, benthic and environmental datasets to identify spatial patterns and temporal trends. Develop frontier research questions and robust quantitative approaches. Plan and conduct regional scientific-diving field campaigns and build productive relationships with a diverse range of collaborators. Provide expert coral and benthic community identification and contribute to data quality control. Lead manuscripts, reports, presentations and other research outputs; support junior researchers and group activities. Job Requirements: PhD in marine science, marine ecology or related discipline. Strong publication record for career stage in coral reef ecology or related fields. Expert coral and benthic community identification skills, with coral reef field and scientific-diving experience. Advanced Open Water or Rescue Diver certification. Strong statistical and data-analysis skills, including R/Python and large ecological or environmental datasets. Experience with photoquadrat, photogrammetry and/or Agisoft Metashape is highly desirable. Excellent scientific writing, communication, collaboration and independent research skills; familiarity with Southeast Asian reef systems is advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Stack-development-and-scaling-Senior-Research-Fellow--Vanadium-Redox-Flow-Battery--VRFB--_R00025842": {
      "title": "Stack development and scaling Senior Research Fellow (Vanadium Redox Flow Battery (VRFB))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. ERI@N has multiple Interdisciplinary Research Programmes which focus on translational Research, Development & Deployment which focus on specific area of the energy value chain, and a number of Living labs and Testbeds which facilitate large scale technology deployment enabling validation and demonstration of real-world applications.    We are looking for a Senior Research Fellow to develop a VRFB stacks from pilot scale to commercial systems, ensuring performance, reliability, and manufacturability. The role bridges R&D, testing, and production to enable smooth transition into large-scale deployment.   Key Responsibilities Lead of vanadium redox flow battery stacks development from prototype to commercial scale while ensuring performance and reliability. Develop, assemble, and validate stack designs through structured testing, durability studies, and failure analysis. Work closely with manufacturing and supply chain teams to ensure designs are production-ready and cost-effective. Establish test rigs, SOPs, and quality benchmarks, and use performance data to drive continuous design improvement. Job Requirements Master’s or PhD in Mechanical engineering/chemical/electrochemical/material, or a related discipline. Minimum 2-5 years of hands-on experience in electrochemical stack development, preferably in vanadium redox flow batteries, fuel cells, or similar systems. Strong practical knowledge of stack scaling, assembly, and performance testing. Experience with durability testing, failure analysis, and data-driven design improvement. Ability to work across R&D, manufacturing, and testing teams in a scale-up or pilot-to-commercial environment.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Academic-Matters_R00025843": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Academic Matters",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Undergraduate Programmes Office at Nanyang Business School is seeking an experienced and collaborative Assistant Director to lead academic matters within the Undergraduate Programmes Office. The role is central to ensuring effective academic programme planning, curriculum administration, stakeholder engagement and continuous improvement in support of a high-quality student experience.   The successful candidate will work closely with school leadership, faculty, academic divisions, university offices, students and external partners to support the delivery and enhancement of NBS undergraduate programmes and related academic initiatives.   Key Responsibilities: Curriculum Planning, Forecasting, Programme Management and Development Oversee course planning, forecasting, coordination and execution for NBS undergraduate programmes, the University Accelerated Pre-University Programme, inter-school collaborations and new academic initiatives. Manage key academic administration matters, including Business major selection, Change of Programme and Change of Major processes. Oversee the provision of curriculum planning advice to students, including matters relating to Broadening and Deepening Electives, MOOCs, minors and second major offerings. Oversee student administration matters, including mid-term scholarships, awards and related academic processes.   Stakeholder Engagement and Partnership Development Build and maintain effective working relationships with academic divisions, faculty, students, university offices, industry partners, professional bodies and external stakeholders. Support collaborations with internal and external partners, including the development of work-study degree programmes, internships and industry-linked academic opportunities. Serve as a key liaison on academic matters, facilitating communication, feedback and alignment across students, faculty, school leadership and university administration.   Academic Governance, Operations and Continuous Improvement Work closely with the Associate Dean, Assistant Deans and Deputy Director to drive academic initiatives and operational priorities for the Undergraduate Programmes Office. Contribute to the conceptualisation, development and implementation of academic initiatives, policies and guidelines to support sound governance and effective programme delivery. Support the implementation and monitoring of university academic initiatives, strategic plans and unit-level work plans. Review, recommend and drive improvements to academic operations, including structures, systems, policies and procedures that support efficient and consistent programme delivery. Provide supervision, guidance and development support to team members within the academic arm of the Undergraduate Programmes Office.   Requirements: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university, with at least 10 years of relevant working experience; experience in the education or higher education sector would be an advantage. Relevant experience in academic administration, programme management, curriculum planning, student administration or governance within an institution of higher learning would be advantageous. Proven supervisory experience, with strong people management, mentoring and team leadership capabilities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage senior stakeholders and present information clearly and professionally. Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trust, influence outcomes and collaborate effectively across diverse stakeholder groups. Strong analytical, planning, organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deliver quality outcomes within timelines. Self-motivated, adaptable and resourceful, with the initiative to improve processes and respond effectively to changing priorities. Meticulous and attentive to detail, with proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturers--PCL---NIE-_R00025800": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturers (PCL) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nNational Institute of Education - Part-time Lecturers (PCL) The National Institute of Education (NIE) invites applications for the position of Part-time Lecturer in the Policy, Curriculum & Leadership (PCL) Department. Job Description Part-Time Lecturers are engaged for teaching duties such as conducting lectures, tutorials and practicum supervision . Please refer to https://www.ntu.edu.sg/nie/ for more information on NIE courses/programmes. Requirements   A Master’s degree. Experience in teaching NIE courses/programmes.     Candidates who do not possess the above qualifications but have proven skills/industry experience are also invited to apply.   Other Information Part-time Lecturers will be paid on an hourly basis at the rates prescribed for the various courses/programmes. The engagement will be on a semester basis (January to June, July to December).   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Stack-Scaling-Engineer--Vanadium-Redox-Flow-Battery--VRFB--_R00025832": {
      "title": "Stack Scaling Engineer (Vanadium Redox Flow Battery (VRFB))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. ERI@N has multiple Interdisciplinary Research Programmes which focus on translational Research, Development & Deployment which focus on specific area of the energy value chain, and a number of Living labs and Testbeds which facilitate large scale technology deployment enabling validation and demonstration of real-world applications.   We are looking for an Engineer to lead the scale-up of VRFB stack designs from lab and pilot scale to commercial systems, ensuring performance, reliability, and manufacturability. The role bridges R&D, testing, and production to enable smooth transition into large-scale deployment.   Key Responsibilities: Lead the scale-up of vanadium redox flow battery stacks from prototype to commercial scale while ensuring performance and reliability. Develop, assemble, and validate stack designs through structured testing, durability studies, and failure analysis. Work closely with manufacturing and supply chain teams to ensure designs are production-ready and cost-effective. Establish test rigs, SOPs, and quality benchmarks, and use performance data to drive continuous design improvement.   Job Requirements: Bachelor/master’s or PhD in Mechanical engineering, or a related discipline. Minimum 5 years of hands-on experience in electrochemical stack development, preferably in vanadium redox flow batteries, fuel cells, or similar systems. Hands-on experience in manufacturing, assembly, performance testing and process development of VRFB stacks, including flow frames, bipolar plates, membranes, gaskets, electrodes, and end plates. Strong understanding of Design for Manufacturing (DFM), stack assembly, compression/torque control, sealing, leak prevention, flow distribution, quality inspection, and performance testing, with experience in production scaling and troubleshooting. Ability to manage engineering design changes and Engineering Change Requests (ECRs), including manufacturability assessment, design review, BOM/drawing updates, change implementation, validation, and cross-functional coordination. Experience with durability testing, failure analysis, and data-driven design improvement. Ability to work across R&D, manufacturing, and testing teams in a scale-up or pilot to commercial environment.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Student-Administration_R00025834": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Undergraduate Programmes Office (UPO) at Nanyang Business School (NBS) is seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented individual to support the administration of Professional Exposure Programmes and Global Exchange initiatives. The role involves managing student mobility and experiential learning programmes, coordinating with internal and external stakeholders, and providing administrative and advisory support to students throughout their academic journey.   Key Responsibilities: Administer the end-to-end operations of Professional Exposure Programmes, including Professional Attachment (PA), Experiential Semester Programme (ESP), Work-Study Degree (WSDeg), and Overseas Entrepreneurship Programme (OEP). Coordinate inbound and outbound student mobility programmes, including exchange applications, nominations, course registration, course matching, credit transfer, and exchange-related administration. Liaise with faculty members, academic divisions, university offices, partner institutions, and industry stakeholders to facilitate programme delivery and student participation. Advise students on programme eligibility, academic requirements, university policies, and administrative procedures related to internships and student exchanges. Manage student records, programme databases, course registration matters, and related communications to ensure operational accuracy and compliance. Support the administration of BU5643 Cultural Intelligence and other overseas exposure initiatives, including enrolment, training coordination, and stakeholder engagement. Prepare reports, analyse programme data, and support process improvement initiatives to enhance operational efficiency and student experience. Handle student enquiries and appeals professionally, providing timely and accurate advice in accordance with university policies and guidelines. Support any other projects and responsibilities assigned by the management. Requirements: A Bachelor's degree from a recognised university, preferably with 1-3 years of relevant work experience. Prior experience in higher education administration or programme management will be advantageous. Strong interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Meticulous, analytical, and solution-oriented, with a strong attention to detail. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word, and PowerPoint. Demonstrated commitment to service excellence and student-centric administration.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Linguistics-_R00025833": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Linguistics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Linguistics and Multilingual Studies programme at the NTU School of Humanities explores language in all its dimensions: structural, social, cognitive, and technological. We have a strong focus on multilingualism, especially in linguistic ecologies of Asia and Southeast Asia, and produce globally significant research on linguistic diversity, human communication, and the evolving relationship between language and technology.   We are looking for a full-time Research Assistant to support the grant-funded project Bridging history and structure: Formal approaches to family-internal contact morphosyntax across Austronesian , a detailed investigation of the Malayo-Polynesian languages of Maritime Southeast Asia. This project focuses on understudied and underdescribed Austronesian languages in Singapore, Indonesia, East Timor and beyond, and the interactions between speaker communities thereof (including but not limited to Singapore Colloquial Malay, Baweanese, Helong, Meto, Amarasi, Hawu, and Kupang Malay). This role will play a key role in collecting and analysing qualitative data, interfacing with collaborators and community members, and managing and preparing project outputs for archiving and dissemination.   Key Responsibilities: Coordinate interview scheduling and administer consent procedures in compliance with ethics requirements. Transcribe, annotate, and otherwise process audio-recorded interviews using language documentation software for analysis and archiving. Organise, maintain and manage project data (including recordings, metadata, transcriptions, and fieldnotes) in a manner which is both secure and in line with established archival standards. Support literature review tasks including establishing baseline grammatical descriptions for various Malayo-Polynesian languages from published sources. Supervise junior student assistants. Support the preparation of project reports or documentation, materials for the dissemination of project findings, and other community-facing project outputs.   Job Requirements: A Bachelor’s degree in Linguistics or related field. Proficiency in English and Malay or Indonesian (both written and spoken, in colloquial as well as standardized registers), including oral communication skills so as to support the research project which focuses on understudied and underdescribed Austronesian languages in Singapore, Indonesia, East Timor and beyond, and the interactions between speaker communities thereof (including but not limited to Singapore Colloquial Malay, Baweanese, Helong, Meto, Amarasi, Hawu, and Kupang Malay). Prior experience in linguistic annotation, transcription, analysis, or related language research and software (e.g. FLEx, ELAN) is an advantage. Familiarity with qualitative data collection (including interviews) and basic data management practices is preferred. Strong understanding of research ethics and/or prior experience with community-oriented research work are desirable. Ability to work independently and collaboratively, with meticulous attention to detail and excellent organisational skills Entry level candidates are welcome to apply. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Cytoskeletal-Biochemistry-and-Biophysics-_R00025831": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Cytoskeletal Biochemistry and Biophysics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance biological and biomedical sciences. At SBS, our research spans various areas, including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative diseases, telomere biology, and genome function. Over the years, SBS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sbs . We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled researcher to join our team in advancing cytoskeleton technology. The successful candidate will apply interdisciplinary approaches to investigate cellular processes and develop innovative tools in cell biology. Key Responsibilities: Conduct experimental research using quantitative biochemistry, biophysics, and cell biology. Develop and optimize advanced technologies targeting cytoskeletal dynamics. Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams within SBS and external partners. Analyze, interpret, and present research findings in written reports and publications. Contribute to the preparation of grant applications and scientific manuscripts.   Job Requirements: A PhD degree in Biological Sciences, Biochemistry, Biophysics, or a related discipline. Hands-on experience in quantitative biochemical and biophysical techniques. Strong background in cell biology, particularly in cytoskeleton-related research. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research and work collaboratively. Excellent analytical, organizational, and communication skills. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Senior-Assistant-Manager--Alumni-Engagement_R00025830": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager/ Senior Assistant Manager, Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University's College of Engineering brings together five Schools under a single College Office that sets standards and directs delivery across the College.   The Assistant Manager/ Senior Assistant Manager, Alumni Engagement supports the planning and delivery of alumni engagement initiatives for the College. Reporting to the Assistant Director, Advancement, the role focuses on strengthening alumni connections through events, communications and engagement programmes that foster lifelong relationships between alumni and the College.   Working closely with the five Schools, the Office of Alumni Engagement (OAE) and other University stakeholders, the incumbent serves as a key coordinator for College alumni activities and engagement efforts, contributing to the College's alumni engagement priorities within the University's alumni engagement framework.   Key Responsibilities:   1. Support Alumni Engagement Programmes and Activities Plan, coordinate and deliver alumni engagement programmes, networking sessions and community-building activities that strengthen alumni affinity with the College. Support initiatives that encourage alumni participation in mentoring, student engagement and other College activities. Identify opportunities to enhance alumni engagement across different alumni segments.   2. Build and Maintain Alumni Relationships Develop and maintain positive relationships with alumni, alumni volunteers and alumni leaders. Serve as a key point of contact for alumni enquiries and engagement opportunities. Support alumni involvement in College programmes and initiatives through regular outreach and engagement.   3. Partner with Schools and Stakeholders Work closely with the five Schools, the Office of Alumni Engagement (OAE) and other University stakeholders to coordinate and deliver alumni engagement initiatives. Support Schools in the implementation of alumni activities and events. Facilitate collaboration between alumni, faculty, students and industry partners where appropriate. 4. Manage Alumni Communications and Outreach Support the development and dissemination of alumni communications through email, social media and digital platforms. Maintain alumni communication calendars and engagement campaigns. Promote alumni programmes, events and success stories to enhance outreach, participation and alumni awareness.   5. Coordinate Alumni Events Support the planning and execution of the College's alumni event portfolio, including reunions, homecoming activities, networking events, speaker sessions and alumni gatherings. Manage event administration, registration, vendor coordination and post-event follow-up. Monitor event participation and support efforts to enhance attendee experience and satisfaction.   6. Maintain Alumni Records, Reporting and Continuous Improvement Maintain accurate alumni records and engagement data within the University's alumni systems. Monitor participation trends and prepare reports on alumni activities and outcomes. Collect and analyse feedback from alumni programmes and events, and recommend improvements to enhance future engagement initiatives.   7. Support Administration and Governance Support procurement, budgeting, payment processing and record-keeping for alumni engagement activities. Ensure compliance with University policies, processes and documentation requirements. Assist with reporting and administrative matters to support the effective delivery of alumni engagement activities.   Requirements:   A bachelor's degree from a recognised university. At least 3 to 5 years of relevant experience in alumni relations, stakeholder engagement, events management, partnerships, marketing, communications or related fields. Strong stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build positive relationships with alumni and internal stakeholders. Excellent organisational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple activities and deadlines. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Experience in event management, alumni engagement or higher education would be an advantage. Proficiency in both English and Chinese is required as the role regularly communicates with English-speaking and Chinese-speaking stakeholders We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Neuroscience---Biology---Biomedical-Sciences-_R00025851": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Neuroscience / Biology / Biomedical Sciences)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. We are seeking a Research Fellow to investigate sensory processing and neural circuit mechanisms.   Job Responsibilities Conduct research on mechanosensory and somatosensory circuits and sensory coding. Develop and apply behavioural assays, calcium imaging and genetic manipulations to study sensory processing and motor sequence generation. Analyse experimental data, maintain reproducible research records and interpret findings in relation to neural circuit mechanisms. Prepare publications and project reports, collaborate with the research team and guide students.   Job Requirements PhD in Neuroscience, Biology, Biomedical Sciences or a related discipline. Research experience in sensory neuroscience, neural circuits or neurodevelopmental disorders. Experience with animal models, electrophysiology, behavioural assays and genetic techniques. Proven ability to design experiments, analyse data and publish research findings. Strong scientific writing, communication and teamwork skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Cybersecurity---Computer-Science---Information-Security---Electronic-or-Communication-Engineering-_R00025852": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Cybersecurity / Computer Science / Information Security / Electronic or Communication Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. We are seeking s seeking a Research Fellow to conduct research on LLM agent safety and secure authentication. The role involves developing runtime monitoring and behavioural evaluation techniques for LLM agents, and investigating secure and usable authentication for intelligent devices.   Job Responsibilities   Develop monitoring methods to detect malicious skill execution and unsafe or misaligned agent behaviour. Design experiments and prototypes to evaluate agent safety, task performance and monitoring overhead. Investigate biometric authentication for smartphones and wearable devices and evaluate security and usability. Analyse findings, prepare publications and project reports, as well as, collaborate with the research team. Job Requirements PhD in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Information Security, Electronic or Communication Engineering, or a related discipline. Research background in LLM agent safety, runtime monitoring, biometric authentication or intelligent-device security. Familiarity with LLM agents and ability to implement prototypes and conduct rigorous experiments. Experience in biometric sensing or acoustic signal analysis would be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--CO2-capture-_R00024445": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (CO2 capture)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nGlobally recognized as a leading research and technology organization, the Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI) addresses national priorities through its diverse expertise in Biotechnology and Bioprocesses, Membrane Technology, Chemicals and Materials, Resource Recovery, and Modeling & Artificial Intelligence. By harnessing its cross-cutting, interdisciplinary, and transformative capabilities, NEWRI drives innovation in water circularity and sustainability, next-generation solid waste solutions, circular economy resource recovery, climate resilience and digitalization. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/newri . Key Responsibilities: The candidate will be undertaking full research work and administrative duties during the term of employment: Coordinate the project execution and communication among the collaborating parties. Work synergistically with PI and Co-I in experimental designs, conducting experiments, troubleshooting and data analysis. Develop sorbent materials for CO2 capture from real combustion flue gas. Scale up the production of sorbent materials for CO2 capture from real combustion flue gas. Manage the day-to-day operation of the reactor apparatus. Procure raw materials, consumables and research equipment. Write and publish research papers. Effectively communicate research findings to collaborators, funding agencies and the scientific community. Provide training to research associate/assistant on the relevant skills for the proposed project. Summarise the findings in this project and produce the progress reports, final report and scientific recommendations. Job Requirements: Bachelor degree in Chemical Engineering, Environmental Engineering, Materials Science, or a relevant field. Experience in developing CO2 sorbents, especially in developing calcium-based CO2 sorbents to be used in circulating fluidized beds. Extensive knowledge in treatment and reutilisation of incineration ashes is highly desired. Good record of peer-reviewed papers is advantageous. Scientific articles, proposals and reports writing skill is required. Good interpersonal skills. Good writing and communication skills. Excellent teamwork awareness. Productive, hard-working and dedicated to the completion of any task assigned. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
