      "title": "Project Lead (CO2 capture)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nGlobally recognized as a leading research and technology organization, the Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI) addresses national priorities through its diverse expertise in Biotechnology and Bioprocesses, Membrane Technology, Chemicals and Materials, Resource Recovery, and Modeling & Artificial Intelligence. By harnessing its cross-cutting, interdisciplinary, and transformative capabilities, NEWRI drives innovation in water circularity and sustainability, next-generation solid waste solutions, circular economy resource recovery, climate resilience and digitalization. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/newri . Key Responsibilities: The candidate will be undertaking full research work and administrative duties during the term of employment: Coordinate the project execution and communication among the collaborating parties. Work synergistically with PI and Co-I in experimental designs, conducting experiments, troubleshooting and data analysis. Upgrading and operating a pilot-scale circulating fluidized bed system. Procure and commission a pilot-scale system to produce CO2 sorbents. Procure consumables and research equipment. Liaise with industry partners, vendors, contractors, university departments and government agencies. Job Requirements: The candidate must have a Bachelor degree or equivalent qualifications specialising in Chemical Engineering or a closely related discipline from an internationally reputable university. Extensive experience in managing pilot-scale research projects is required. Good interpersonal skills and excellent teamwork awareness. Good writing and communication skills. Productive, hard-working and dedicated to the completion of any task assigned. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Robot-Learning---Manipulation-_R00025850-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Robot Learning & Manipulation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nSHARE@NTU Corporate Laboratory focuses on the development of key technologies for humanoid robotics, aimed at enabling intelligent services, industrial assistance, and human-centric applications. The research areas include multimodal sensing, artificial intelligence, environmental perception and situational awareness, as well as real-time motion planning and decision-making, allowing humanoid robots to operate safely and efficiently in complex and dynamic environments. Through the development of advanced humanoid robotic platforms, SHARE@NTU Lab seeks to address the growing global demand for automation while cultivating the next generation of local talent in robotics, artificial intelligence, and intelligent sensing technologies.   Our Lab aims to hire a Research Fellow with strong robotics learning background to help develop and improve our visuomotor manipulation policies, with a heavy emphasis on real-robot deployment.   Key Responsibilities: Lead the research and development of learning-based visuomotor policies for humanoid robot manipulation, from problem formulation to real-world validation Define research directions and technical roadmaps for manipulation capabilities such as grasping, object reorientation, bimanual manipulation, and assembly Advance techniques including behavior cloning, reinforcement learning, and VLA-based reasoning, with a focus on novel contributions and publishable outcomes Develop principled approaches to robustness challenges such as sensor noise, partial observability, contact dynamics, and environment variability Oversee the research pipeline from data collection strategy and model training to evaluation methodology and deployment Manage project milestones, deliverables, and timelines; coordinate with collaborators and stakeholders, and report progress to the PI Supervise and mentor research associates, engineers, and PhD students working on the project Collaborate with perception, controls, systems, and hardware teams to guide integration of learned policies into the full autonomy stack Evaluate tradeoffs between learning-based and classical approaches and make principled architectural and design decisions Lead the preparation of publications, technical reports, and grant/project documentation   Job Requirements: PhD in Robotics, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field Strong publication record in robot learning, manipulation, embodied AI, or related areas (e.g., CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, NeurIPS, CVPR) Demonstrated experience developing and deploying robot learning systems on real robots Deep expertise in robot manipulation and visuomotor control Strong command of behavior cloning, reinforcement learning, or related learning-based manipulation methods Proficiency in Python and modern deep learning frameworks (e.g., PyTorch) Proven ability to independently define research problems, design experiments, and drive projects to completion Experience supervising or mentoring junior researchers or students   Bonus Qualifications Prior work on humanoids or highly dexterous robotic platforms Experience transitioning research prototypes into commercial or production robotic systems Track record of successful collaboration with industry partners Passion for building autonomous humanoid robots that operate in the real world We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Simulation---BioMEMS-_R00025869": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Simulation & BioMEMS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated Research Assistant to join our advanced sensors research team at NTU MAE. The successful candidate will support multidisciplinary research activities in biomechanics, robotics, and advanced materials within the laboratory.   Responsibilities:   Support the team towards comprehensive literature reviews on injury biomechanics, physiological effects, computational modelling and related research topics. Develop, implement and validate computational simulation models for impact and injury prediction using appropriate numerical methods and software tools. Design and conduct experimental studies using instrumented human manikins and other test platforms to evaluate biomechanical responses and validate simulation results. Assist in the design, fabrication, and characterization of tissue simulants and non-Newtonian materials, including support for 3D printing and additive manufacturing processes. Develop and optimize experimental setups, testing protocols and data acquisition systems for biomechanical and robotics-related research. Analyse experimental and simulation data, prepare technical reports, and document research findings. Support the integration of advanced materials and sensing technologies into robotics and other interdisciplinary research initiatives. Inline sensor system developmental work for 3D printing of non-newtonian materials.  Optimization of hardware configurations to maintain a food-grade environment, including development of testing protocols and validation procedures. Collaborate with faculty members, researchers, students and external partners to achieve project objectives and milestones. Assist in the preparation of research publications, presentations, grant reports, and project deliverables. Maintain laboratory equipment and ensure compliance with laboratory safety procedures and research best practices. Liaise with external vendors on custom sensors and related mechanical system development.  Manage technical specifications and acceptance testing.  Coordinate technical discussions with collaborators and project stakeholders.  Track project milestones, risks, and technical deliverables.   Requirements:   Bachelor degrees in Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Robotics, or related discipline. Knowledge of multi-physics modelling for non-newtonian materials. Experience with 3D printing technologies, sensors, system integration, experimental testing, or measurement systems will be advantageous. Familiarity with signal processing and analysis, control systems, Python, MATLAB, C++, LabVIEW, or equivalent tools is preferred. Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication, and project coordination skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary teams.    We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--NBS-Global-Leaders_R00025874": {
      "title": "Manager, NBS Global Leaders",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAs a leading business school in Singapore and globally, Nanyang Business School competes with top business schools from around the world to attract top applicants from diverse backgrounds to join its undergraduate programmes. The Manager will report to the Assistant Director of NBS Global Leaders (NGL) programme and will have a dotted reporting line to Assistant Director of UPO Marketing, Outreach, Admissions. The NBS Global Leaders (NGL) programme is a signature scholars programme offered by NBS. Working closely in partnership with the Marketing, Outreach & Admissions (MOA) pillar, the incumbent shall play an important role in the entire recruitment process for the NGL programme, from marketing to outreach and admissions.    The manager will also oversee one NGL staff member responsible for UPO-related activities that impact NGL students, e.g., enrolment, curriculum planning, overseas exchange, and other programme components.   Key Responsibilities include but not limited to the following: Formulation and drive execution of the marketing plan for the NGL programme Drive analysis of market trends, candidates’ insights, programme trends and competitors’ analysis to build programme strategy Spearhead social media marketing for the NGL programmes to boost engagement with potential applicants, current UG students, and related stakeholder groups. Initiate, organize and run information sessions/webinars/experience days locally as well as internationally (as and when required) Plan and execute admissions processes for applicants to the NGL programme Perform other tasks assigned by the Assistant Director, including the support of student management and curriculum matters Key competencies and qualifications requirements: Degree in any field; Business or Marketing preferred. Minimum of 5 years relevant experience Possess a creative and innovative mind for the development of engaging and targeted campaigns An analytical thinker who can interpret campaign data to drive decisions Keen knowledge of various digital marketing platforms and performance tracking Keen knowledge of marketing automation tools such as HubSpot and SendGrid Strong content marketing skills such as long and short-form content creation, copywriting Strong project management skills with the ability to coordinate and manage multiple projects concurrently Proficient in Microsoft Excel and visualization of dataset Able to work after-office hours/ weekend when required (This is due to outreach and marketing events which will typically be held over weekends such as open houses for Poly/JC students etc.) Enjoy meeting and connecting with new people   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Senior-Executive---Lab-Operations_R00025858": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Senior Executive – Lab Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty.   A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow’. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing.   We invite suitable candidates to apply for the Assistant Manager / Senior Executive, Laboratory Operations.   Responsibilities: Support the operations, infrastructure and technical environments of CCDS Graduate Research Laboratories and centralised research computing facilities, including GPU, server and specialised research equipment. Ensure the operational readiness, reliability and effective functioning of laboratory and research computing infrastructure, including the configuration, deployment, maintenance and troubleshooting of workstations, servers and GPU-enabled systems. Coordinate procurement, vendor management and asset lifecycle activities, ensuring research infrastructure and equipment are appropriately maintained and available to meet faculty, researcher and student needs. Administer laboratory access, safety, compliance and audit requirements, ensuring that research environments operate in accordance with relevant policies and standards. Work with faculty, researchers, students and other stakeholders to coordinate infrastructure requirements and continuously improve the efficiency and effectiveness of research laboratory and computing operations. Leverage Generative AI and AI-enabled tools, where appropriate, to enhance information analysis, technical documentation, workflow automation, troubleshooting and operational productivity   Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree or Diploma in Information Technology, Computer Science, Computing, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Engineering, or a related discipline. Relevant professional certification(s) in Artificial Intelligence (AI), Generative AI, Machine Learning, Data Analytics, Cloud Computing, IT Infrastructure, or related technologies would be advantageous. Experience in technical support, infrastructure administration, laboratory operations, or research computing environments. Linux knowledge is required; scripting or programming knowledge such as Python, Bash, or PowerShell is advantageous. Experience with servers, GPU systems, workstations, virtualization, cloud platforms, scientific computing, or AI/ML research infrastructure is advantageous. Good working knowledge of Generative AI and modern AI productivity tools, with the ability to apply them effectively to technical, operational, analytical, and administrative work. Strong organisational, troubleshooting, analytical, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Able to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic research and technology-driven environment. Proactive and adaptable, with a willingness to continuously learn and adopt emerging AI and computing technologies.    We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--EdTech-Enablement_R00025863": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, EdTech Enablement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nChange How NTU Teaches with AI: Senior Assistant Manager, AI Enablement (Teaching & Learning) Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a world-class, research-intensive public university dedicated to providing a transformative education, advancing research, and nurturing global leaders. Driven by innovation, excellence, and a commitment to positive global impact, NTU fosters an inclusive and vibrant ecosystem where cutting-edge technology meets education. At the Institute for Pedagogical Innovation, Research & Excellence (InsPIRE) – Educational Services, we implement, integrate and optimise the University’s digital learning ecosystem to deliver a seamless, user-centric and high-impact teaching and learning experience. Our Edtech Enablement team is where that work meets faculty: we help academics put EdTech to work in their teaching, and we tell the story of what they achieve with it. The Opportunity We are looking for someone who can build with AI and teach others to do the same, as Senior Assistant Manager, EdTech Enablement . Around 80% of your time goes to EdTech and AI enablement – training and coaching faculty, consulting on course and assessment design, and creating AI-built learning assets you can put in front of a room. The remaining 20% is change management and communications: making sure your programmes and the University’s wider teaching and learning initiatives land with the people who need to act on them. You will not just talk about AI; you will build with it and show your work. Key Highlights of the Role: Enable Faculty to Teach with AI: Design and run the workshops, clinics and onboarding that take academics from curiosity to confident, compliant practice. Shape How Courses Are Designed: Consult with faculty and course teams on applying AI to course design, assessment and learning content – and on where it does not belong. Build and Showcase AI Exemplars: Create your own AI-built learning assets, prompt workflows and use cases, and present them at showcases, communities of practice and leadership briefings. As a Senior Assistant Manager, you will work hands-on across faculty enablement, AI-enhanced learning design, AI content creation and supporting communications. Primary Duties: Faculty EdTech Enablement & Training: Design and deliver a recurring programme of hands-on workshops, clinics and onboarding sessions, plus the guides, prompt libraries and recorded demonstrations that let faculty keep learning on their own. AI-Enhanced Learning Design Consultancy: Advise faculty and course teams on applying AI to course design, assessment design and learning content, within University academic integrity and data protection guidelines. AI Creation & Showcase: Build demonstrable AI-generated and AI-assisted learning assets, prompt workflows and use cases, and curate them into a library of exemplars and success stories you present across the University. Tool Evaluation & Governance-Aligned Adoption: Evaluate and pilot emerging EdTech and AI tools, translate University policy into practical guardrails faculty can follow, and feed needs back to platform owners and vendors. Communications & Engagement: Plan and execute communications that build awareness and uptake of your programmes and of university-wide teaching and learning initiatives, working with Corporate Communications and school-level leads. Measurement & Continuous Improvement: Track participation, adoption, capability uplift and sentiment; report on impact; and use what you learn to sharpen the next cycle of enablement. Candidate Qualifications & Requirements Must-Have Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Education, Educational Technology, Instructional Design, Communications, or a related discipline. Tertiary-level teaching experience EdTech & Enablement Experience: At least 5 years in educational technology, learning design, digital learning or staff capability development, including hands-on work with generative AI applied to teaching, learning or content creation. AI Fluency & Portfolio: Demonstrated practical use of generative AI tools (e.g. Google Gemini, Microsoft Copilot, ChatGPT, Claude) to create learning content, media or workflows, with work you can show and explain. Shortlisted candidates will be asked to walk us through something they have built with AI. Training & Facilitation: Proven experience designing and delivering training, workshops or onboarding to academic or professional audiences, with confident presentation and demonstration skills. Consultancy & Learning Design: Experience advising educators or subject matter experts on course, assessment or content design, and translating pedagogical needs into practical technology solutions. Communications & Core Competencies: Strong writing and editing for internal audiences with experience across email, web, social and event channels; excellent stakeholder engagement and influencing skills; adaptable thinking; and high integrity. Good-to-Have Skills (Preferred): Experience in higher education, an Institute of Higher Learning (IHL), or the public sector, and a postgraduate qualification in education or learning design. Familiarity with learning management systems and digital learning tools. Experience building lightweight AI solutions such as custom assistants, GPTs, agents or no-code automations, and hands-on design, video or e-learning authoring skills. Why Join NTU? At NTU, we value our people as our greatest strength. Joining InsPIRE – Educational Services means becoming part of an inspiring, supportive, and growth-oriented work environment. Continuous Learning & Professional Growth: Access extensive learning and development opportunities, certification programmes and workshops to keep your skills sharp in fast-evolving fields such as generative AI, learning design and educational technology. Career Progression: Enjoy structured career development opportunities within a leading global university system. Staff Welfare & Hybrid Work Initiatives: Benefit from flexible work arrangements (including Work-From-Home options), comprehensive medical coverage, and regular university-wide employee engagement and team-building activities. Vibrant Campus Community: Experience a diverse, inclusive, and collaborative campus atmosphere equipped with world-class facilities. How to Apply If you are excited about changing how a university teaches – and you can show us what you have already built with AI, we would love to hear from you. Please submit your updated CV and cover letter through the NTU Careers Portal. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Organic-Chemistry-_R00025861": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Organic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) conducts interdisciplinary education and research across chemistry, chemical engineering and biotechnology, with research strengths that include synthetic, biological and medicinal chemistry. We are looking for a Research Fellow in Organic Chemistry to develop sustainable synthetic methods for high-value glycosides through traceless activation and radical coupling. The role will focus on selective modification of carbohydrates and glycosides, radical reaction development, synthesis and purification of complex products, mechanistic studies and rigorous analytical characterization under the project “Sustainable Chemistry for High-Value Glycoside Products via Traceless Activation.”   Key Responsibilities:   Design and execute multi-step syntheses of carbohydrates, glycosides, glycomimetics and related high-value products. Develop selective sugar-modification and functionalization methods using traceless activation strategies. Develop and optimize radical coupling reactions, including reaction design, selectivity, efficiency and substrate-scope evaluation. Plan protecting-group strategies and control chemoselectivity, regioselectivity and stereoselectivity in complex carbohydrate substrates. Purify products and intermediates using flash chromatography, preparative HPLC, recrystallization and other suitable methods.   Job Requirements:   PhD in Chemistry, Organic Chemistry, Chemical Biology, Biochemistry or a related discipline. Hands-on experience in carbohydrate chemistry, sugar modification, and the synthesis of glycosides, glycomimetics or related compounds. Demonstrated experience in designing and optimizing radical coupling reactions, including photochemical or electrochemical approaches where applicable. Strong organic synthesis and reaction-development skills, including protecting-group strategies and control of chemoselectivity, regioselectivity and stereoselectivity. Proficiency in product purification and structure characterization using flash chromatography, preparative HPLC, 1D/2D NMR, LC-MS/HRMS and HPLC/UPLC.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Organic-Chemistry-_R00025860-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Organic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) conducts interdisciplinary education and research across chemistry, chemical engineering and biotechnology, with research strengths that include synthetic, biological and medicinal chemistry.   We are looking for a Research Fellow in Organic Chemistry to develop, synthesize, characterize and purify antibody-drug conjugates (ADCs), peptides and related linker-payload components. The role will focus on solution-phase synthesis, solid-phase peptide synthesis (SPPS), conjugation and purification workflows, analytical characterization, and the delivery of reproducible research results.   Key Responsibilities:   Design and execute multi-step solution-phase organic synthesis and solid-phase peptide synthesis (SPPS) of peptides, linkers, payloads, linker-payloads and other ADC-related molecules. Develop and optimize amide-bond formation and conjugation reactions, including coupling-reagent selection, protecting-group strategies, chemoselectivity, conversion and yield. Develop and optimize ADC conjugation and purification workflows to produce material that meets project specifications. Purify peptides, small molecules, intermediates, linker-payloads and ADCs using flash chromatography, preparative HPLC, SEC/FPLC and other suitable methods. Characterize products and assess identity, purity, drug-to-antibody ratio and aggregation using NMR, LC-MS, HPLC/UPLC, UV-Vis, SEC and HIC. Troubleshoot amide coupling, SPPS, conjugation, purification and analytical issues, and recommend practical solutions. Maintain accurate experimental records and prepare technical reports, presentations and manuscripts. Maintain good research and laboratory safety practices and perform related duties assigned by the Principal Investigator.   Job Requirements:   PhD in Chemistry, Chemical Biology or Biochemistry. Demonstrated hands-on experience in synthetic organic chemistry and in the synthesis and purification of antibody-drug conjugates; linker-payload chemistry and bioconjugation experience is required. Hands-on experience with SPPS, including resin handling, coupling cycles, cleavage, deprotection, preparative HPLC purification and LC-MS analysis. Experience developing amide-bond formation and conjugation methods, including coupling-reagent selection, protecting-group strategies, reaction optimization and chemoselectivity. Experience with ADC purification and characterization using SEC/FPLC, HIC, LC-MS, analytical HPLC/UPLC and UV-Vis, including assessment of purity, drug-to-antibody ratio and aggregation. Good experimental documentation, problem-solving, scientific writing and oral communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaborate effectively in a multidisciplinary research team.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Organic-Chemistry-_R00025859": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Organic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) conducts interdisciplinary education and research across chemistry, chemical engineering and biotechnology, with research strengths that include synthetic, biological and medicinal chemistry.   We are looking for a Research Fellow in Organic Chemistry to develop, synthesize, characterize and purify antibody-drug conjugates (ADCs), peptides and related linker-payload components. The role will focus on solution-phase synthesis, solid-phase peptide synthesis (SPPS), conjugation and purification workflows, analytical characterization, and the delivery of reproducible research results.   Key Responsibilities:   Design and execute multi-step solution-phase organic synthesis and solid-phase peptide synthesis (SPPS) of peptides, linkers, payloads, linker-payloads and other ADC-related molecules. Develop and optimize amide-bond formation and conjugation reactions, including coupling-reagent selection, protecting-group strategies, chemoselectivity, conversion and yield. Develop and optimize ADC conjugation and purification workflows to produce material that meets project specifications. Purify peptides, small molecules, intermediates, linker-payloads and ADCs using flash chromatography, preparative HPLC, SEC/FPLC and other suitable methods. Characterize products and assess identity, purity, drug-to-antibody ratio and aggregation using NMR, LC-MS, HPLC/UPLC, UV-Vis, SEC and HIC. Troubleshoot amide coupling, SPPS, conjugation, purification and analytical issues, and recommend practical solutions. Maintain accurate experimental records and prepare technical reports, presentations and manuscripts. Maintain good research and laboratory safety practices and perform related duties assigned by the Principal Investigator.   Job Requirements:   PhD in Chemistry, Chemical Biology or Biochemistry. Demonstrated hands-on experience in synthetic organic chemistry and in the synthesis and purification of antibody-drug conjugates; linker-payload chemistry and bioconjugation experience is required. Hands-on experience with SPPS, including resin handling, coupling cycles, cleavage, deprotection, preparative HPLC purification and LC-MS analysis. Experience developing amide-bond formation and conjugation methods, including coupling-reagent selection, protecting-group strategies, reaction optimization and chemoselectivity. Experience with ADC purification and characterization using SEC/FPLC, HIC, LC-MS, analytical HPLC/UPLC and UV-Vis, including assessment of purity, drug-to-antibody ratio and aggregation. Good experimental documentation, problem-solving, scientific writing and oral communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaborate effectively in a multidisciplinary research team.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director-Senior-Assistant-Director--Procurement-Operations_R00025854": {
      "title": "Assistant Director/Senior Assistant Director, Procurement Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a seasoned procurement leader who combines strong operational discipline with strategic thinking. The ideal candidate is hands-on, commercially astute, customer-focused and capable of leading diverse procurement teams while partnering effectively with senior stakeholders. The candidate should possess a broad procurement background across multiple categories and be comfortable operating in a dynamic and complex higher education environment.   The incumbent is responsible for leading and overseeing the University's day-to-day procurement operations across all procurement categories particularly in Lab equipment and Consumables.   As a Procurement Lead, the incumbent will provide strategic and operational leadership to procurement teams, ensuring the efficient, compliant, and cost-effective acquisition of goods and services. The role is accountable for procurement governance, category management, stakeholder engagement, supplier relationship management, staff development, and continuous process improvement.   The incumbent will lead teams supporting academic, research and administrative units, drive procurement excellence, and ensure procurement activities are conducted in accordance with policies, regulatory requirements, and best practices.   Processes Perform thorough analysis of spending and partnership with stakeholders, and development of overall sourcing strategy/category management plan. Leading and embedding transformation projects, developing & deploying processes & systems, and proactively managing governance & compliance. Supplier Relationship Management: Pro-actively develops and manages key stakeholders and suppliers, develops relationships, establishes KPIs/SLAs and classification of vendors, performance tracking, and communicates feedback. Conduct market research, analyze industry trends and evolving technology to proactively identify supply base issues to minimize risk, protect continuity of supply, utilize emerging opportunities, and ensure appropriate goods/ services are being acquired at competitive prices. Manage complex Request for Proposals (RFPs), Requests for Quotation (RFQs), Requests for Information (RFIs) and drive the supplier negotiation process using lowest bid, lowest cost per quality point or best value analyses. Execute procurement tender process including development and spearhead of tender roadmap to meet NTU deliverables. Delivering regular updates to the management with detailed status reporting. People Work collaboratively with suppliers and customers to identify and execute continuous cost and performance improvement strategies. Lead, oversee and manage the purchasing and strategic sourcing function in NTU including but not limited to daily management, leadership and support to team. Driving effective teamwork, collaboration, and close dialogue with all interfacing functions to ensure a seamless efficient approach to information exchange and process flows to other areas within the procurement function.  System Use purchasing tools such as spend analytics, e-sourcing, auctions and contract management while adhering to strategic sourcing standards/ policies.  Qualifications/Skills Minimum 10-12 years of relevant procurement experience. At least 5 years in a leadership role managing procurement teams. Experience in public sector, higher education, research institutions, healthcare, statutory boards or large complex organisations is preferred. Demonstrated experience in strategic sourcing, contract management and procurement governance.     We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Maintenance-Operations_R00025901": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Maintenance Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNTU is seeking experienced and motivated individuals to join our dynamic team in Office of Development & Facilities Management. The department oversees the physical development and maintenance of all University buildings and grounds in support of the academic, research and administrative functions of the University. As a Senior Executive, Maintenance Operations, you are responsible to oversee the repair and maintenance of external infrastructure in the Campus to ensure they are safe to use and functional at all times. Key Responsibilities: Supervise and check the maintenance activities to ensure inspection programs and preventive maintenance works for Campus’s external infrastructure and grounds are carried out as planned and in accordance with standards expected. Follow up promptly on corrective maintenance works to minimize downtime and maintain a safe environment. Supervise and check planned and corrective maintenance programs for electronic speed advisory signs to ensure systems are in good working condition. Supervise and check planned slope inspection programs and screen service report to pick up potential slope failure tell-tale sign and take quick remedial actions to mitigate. Process user’s request, understand the requirements, develop work proposals and estimate associated costs. Oversee procurement of services, supervise work progress and ensure materials and workmanship meet standards. Review and track site progress through meetings and inspections to meet user’s project completion timeline. Identify improvement works, maintenance needs and cyclical maintenance programs and derive budget required for new Financial Year. Undertake any other duties assigned. Requirements: Degree in Civil Engineering, Building Services, Facilities Management or equivalent with at least 3 years of relevant experience. Good understanding of the design, construction and maintenance of drains, roads, culverts, linkways, slopes, and related civil infrastructure will have added advantage. Basic proficiency in AutoCAD and ability to interpret engineering and construction drawings. Proficient with Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Word and PowerPoint. Self-motivated with a positive work attitude and good customer-oriented mindset. Good oral and written communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with stakeholders at all levels. Joining NTU as a Senior Executive, Maintenance Operations is an excellent opportunity for an individual looking to further their career in a challenging and dynamic environment. If you have the required skills and experience and are excited about this opportunity, we invite you to submit your application today! We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Microbiology--Bioinformatics--Computational-Biology-_R00025894": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Microbiology/ Bioinformatics/ Computational Biology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. The school plays an integral role in spearheading tertiary education, advancing research innovations and providing professional services in a number of key disciplines in Civil and Environmental Engineering and Maritime Studies fields, with the objective of contributing to the technological and economic advancement of Singapore and beyond. The school’s mission in research is to achieve excellence by providing a conducive and intellectually stimulating environment to enable high-quality work in strategic directions that are of significant impact to industry, science and technology.   For more details, please view School of Civil and Environmental Engineering | NTU Singapore   The research group focuses on understanding the environment-microbe-human complex interactions. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow (RF) with an interest in antimicrobial resistance and bioinformatics.   The RF will work on a project aiming to profile antimicrobial resistance and bacterial communities. Key Responsibilities : Conduct rigorous study design. Perform in-depth, critical data analyses. Effectively communicate research findings through presentations and high-quality journal publications. Assist in supervising research students within the group.   Job Requirements: PhD in microbiology, bioinformatics, computational biology or a related field. Experience on python, linux and HPC. A strong interest in interdisciplinary research. Excellent interpersonal skills to work effectively with group members and collaborators. Good oral and written communication skills in English. Demonstrated ability to work efficiently and with minimum supervision We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Civil-Engineering-_R00025888": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Civil Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nSchool of Civil and Environmental Engineering is a school under College of Engineering and is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. The key objective of this position is to support the development of simulation models for coastal infrastructure, such as seawalls and dikes. Key Responsibilities: Develop simulation models. Conduct laboratory-scale tests. Validate the models using field test data. Publish research findings/papers in high-quality top journals. Prepare proposals for further research and development. Mentor and supervise students. Job Requirements: PhD in Civil Engineering or a related field. At least 1 year of relevant experience in machine learning and structural health monitoring. Good written and oral communication skills. Proficiency in ABAQUS and laboratory testing. Ability to work independently and develop solutions within strict timelines. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--AI-for-Nature-Based-Climate-Solutions-_R00025899": {
      "title": "Research Associate (AI for Nature Based Climate Solutions)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nASE is a diverse school focusing on the connections between geosciences, ecology, society and Earth systems. Our approach integrates these disciplines to examine big environmental challenges both in Southeast Asia and globally. We conduct cutting-edge research on topics that include ecology, geohazards, climate change, sea-level rise, environmental sustainability, conservation of environment and biodiversity, and interactions between environment and society. For more information on ASE please visit https://www.ntu.edu.sg/ase .   The Yanyan Cheng research group is seeking a Research Associate. This position is part of a Singapore MOE funded research project hosted by ASE. The Research Associate will help advance research in integrated assessment modeling and understand interactions among land, water, carbon, energy, climate, ecosystems, and human systems.   This is a one-year appointment and potentially renewable based on performance and funding availability.   Key Responsibilities:   Collect, curate, validate, and document large-scale multimodal ecohydrological remote sensing datasets. Train and evaluate models on large datasets and high-performance computing systems; establish reproducible baselines, ablation studies, and evaluation suites. Apply the developed datasets and models to the monitoring and analysis of tropical ecohydrological processes.   Job Requirements:   The candidate should hold a master's degree in information and communication engineering, with research experience in 3D point-cloud or point-cloud sequence processing, is highly desirable. The candidate should posse extensive relevant experience in model design and development, programming implementation, experimental design and evaluation, and peer-reviewed scientific writing. The candidate should have demonstrated research expertise in both remote sensing and computer vision. The candidate should have a strong publication record. Preference will be given to candidates with first- or co-first-author papers in CCF Rank A computer science venues (e.g., CVPR) and leading peer-reviewed remote sensing journals (e.g., IEEE TGRS). The candidate should have strong programming skills in Python and MATLAB, together with practical experience in deep-learning frameworks such as PyTorch, remote sensing data processing, Linux environments, and high-performance computing. The candidate must be able to communicate fluently and demonstrate strong academic writing skills for papers, reports, and presentations. The candidate should be able to work independently and collaboratively, manage large datasets and research codebases, meet project deadlines, and produce reproducible research outputs. Interpersonal skill (e.g. Ability to work independently / develop solutions under strict timelines, meticulous and eye for details / excellent organizational / time management skills).   ASE seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate-Research-Fellow--Research-Institute-for-Cancer-Prevention--Screening-and-Early-Detection--LKCMedicine-_R00025889-2": {
      "title": "Research Associate/Research Fellow, Research Institute for Cancer Prevention, Screening and Early Detection [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Research Institute for Cancer Prevention, Screening and Early Detection has recently been established at the Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine. It aims to be a leading Asian institution in clinical translational research and education for cancer prevention and early detection. The initial areas of research focus relate to precision cancer prevention including the development and validation of risk prediction models; and clinical implementation research of targeted screening and behavioural interventions to increase cancer screening relevant to an individual’s cancer risk profile.  The Institute works closely with Primary Care and Family Medicine at LKC Medicine, given the Institute’s focus on the role of primary care in cancer prevention and detection. We are looking for a Research Associate/Research Fellow with a background and strong interest in cancer screening and detection within primary care settings. The successful candidate will contribute to an interdisciplinary project developing and evaluating targeted screening methods for common cancers among at-risk individuals. The role will involve generating and supporting clinical and population-based research activities, including research plan generation, study implementation, data collection and analysis, ethics applications, and stakeholder engagement. Working closely with clinicians, behavioural scientists, patient partners, and industry collaborators, the candidate will contribute to research that informs the delivery of effective and equitable cancer screening and detection programmes. Key Responsibilities: Working as part of a research team, support the conduct of a feasibility study in primary care to tailor multi-cancer screening according to cancer risks.   Research, data analysis and interpretation Support the development of trial specific materials including cancer risk communication reports Support patient recruitment, delivery of interventions and follow-up of study participants Data collection, analysis and interpretation of quantitative and qualitative data Project management, ensuring study deliverables, reports and publications are completed punctually according to study and grant timelines Support the preparation of reports, presentation and manuscripts for publication in peer reviewed publication and lay statement   Administration Ensure all work processes met the ethical standards of the University, Singapore Good Clinical Practice Guidelines and other applicable regulatory and ethical requirements   Collaboration and communication Work effectively with key stakeholder groups, including patients, clinicians and clinic staff to achieve project and program outcomes Contribute to grants, manuscripts, reports, reviews, abstracts, posters and oral presentations with collaborators Assist in communications with institutional review board staff regarding ethics applications, amendments and reports Work collaboratively with Theme PI and other members of the research team to develop and achieve research outputs Key Competencies and Requirements: Masters/PhD degree in health services research, precision medicine, implementation science or a related discipline e.g. medicine, nursing, allied health, genetic counselling, public health, social sciences. Experience in health services, population health or implementation research Design and conduct of research projects using a range of methods Proficiency in using software packages including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, statistical packages, NVivo Familiarity with primary care settings in Singapore and/or internationally Leadership competencies: Ability to build rapport and influence stakeholders at all levels Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer--Psychology---Neuropsychology---Cognitive-Neuroscience-_R00025882": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Psychology / Neuropsychology / Cognitive Neuroscience)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCentre for Lifelong Learning and Individualised Cognition CLIC is a research collaboration between the University of Cambridge and Nanyang Technological University (NTU) and hosted by the Cambridge Centre for Advanced Research and Education in Singapore (CARES) that aims to develop neuroscience-based interventions for lifelong flexible learning. Launched in October 2020 and funded by the National Research Foundation Singapore, CLIC brings together a multidisciplinary team of psychologists, neuroscientists, linguists and educators who conduct innovative research in the science of learning.   The world of today is constantly evolving to keep pace with advances in technology and globalisation, requiring individuals to adapt and develop new skills to ensure resilience through a culture of lifelong flexible learning. Mental flexibility is required in order to adapt to change, problem-solve creatively in new situations and make the most of opportunities including emerging career opportunities. The capacity for cognitive flexibility is thus central to the modern digital age and our education system needs innovation to ensure citizens are equipped to develop these future skills. For example, major global challenges, including climate change, renewable energy, and food security, will require novel and creative approaches and solutions.   CLIC researchers are developing a neuroscience-based model of flexible learning, including important social contextual factors, in order to inform the design of practical, real-life interventions for use in schools and the workplace. This will ensure that individuals are not only prepared for future career success, but also have a good quality of life and wellbeing, thus supporting a flourishing society.   The CLIC program is seeking one full-time Research Engineer (with potential opportunities for reappointment). The Research Engineer will support research activities focusing on cognitive flexibility and learning, and training-related brain changes among adults and adolescents. Given the highly inter-disciplinary nature of the project, the research Research Engineer will be expected to take on opportunities for involvement in research activities related to human neuroimaging, language, infant cognition/learning and pedagogy.   Key Responsibilities: Support the recruitment of approximately young adults (18 – 30 years) from vocational institutions (e.g. ITE, polytechnics and universities) as well as from the general working population via community sampling (e.g. community centres, clinics, via social media platforms). Organize the collection of datasets Overview and standardize protocols for data coding, data entry and data analysis for the datasets Assist with the preparation of conference presentations journal papers Other administrative duties   Job Requirements: Master's degree in Psychology, Neuropsychology, Cognitive Neuroscience or a related discipline Prior experience in conducting adult cognitive testing and neuroimaging (fMRI, EEG) Prior experience with participant recruitment processes Prior experience and familiarity with data management protocols and ethical regulatory frameworks in Singapore Experience in performing general administration tasks for research projects Experience in producing research reports Good statistical knowledge and skills, including familiarity with statistical analysis software such as R and SPSS Good IT skills (Office®) Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills Excellent organizational skills and able to work within given deadlines Excellent time management and organizational skills.  We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Please apply by uploading your CV and academic transcript to NTU job portal link. If you have any questions, please feel free to reach out to us at clic@ntu.edu.sg . Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Psychology---Neuropsychology---Cognitive-Neuroscience-_R00025881": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Psychology / Neuropsychology / Cognitive Neuroscience)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCentre for Lifelong Learning and Individualised Cognition CLIC is a research collaboration between the University of Cambridge and Nanyang Technological University (NTU) and hosted by the Cambridge Centre for Advanced Research and Education in Singapore (CARES) that aims to develop neuroscience-based interventions for lifelong flexible learning. Launched in October 2020 and funded by the National Research Foundation Singapore, CLIC brings together a multidisciplinary team of psychologists, neuroscientists, linguists and educators who conduct innovative research in the science of learning.   The world of today is constantly evolving to keep pace with advances in technology and globalisation, requiring individuals to adapt and develop new skills to ensure resilience through a culture of lifelong flexible learning. Mental flexibility is required in order to adapt to change, problem-solve creatively in new situations and make the most of opportunities including emerging career opportunities. The capacity for cognitive flexibility is thus central to the modern digital age and our education system needs innovation to ensure citizens are equipped to develop these future skills. For example, major global challenges, including climate change, renewable energy, and food security, will require novel and creative approaches and solutions.   CLIC researchers are developing a neuroscience-based model of flexible learning, including important social contextual factors, in order to inform the design of practical, real-life interventions for use in schools and the workplace. This will ensure that individuals are not only prepared for future career success, but also have a good quality of life and wellbeing, thus supporting a flourishing society.   The CLIC program is seeking one full-time Research Assistant (with potential opportunities for reappointment). The research assistant will support research activities focusing on cognitive flexibility and learning, and training-related brain changes among adults and adolescents. Given the highly inter-disciplinary nature of the project, the research assistant will be expected to take on opportunities for involvement in research activities related to human neuroimaging, language, infant cognition/learning and pedagogy. Key Responsibilities: Support the recruitment of approximately young adults (18 – 30 years) from vocational institutions (e.g. ITE, polytechnics and universities) as well as from the general working population via community sampling (e.g. community centres, clinics, via social media platforms). Organize the collection of datasets Overview and standardize protocols for data coding, data entry and data analysis for the datasets Assist with the preparation of conference presentations journal papers Other administrative duties   Job Requirements: Bachelor and/or Master's degree in Psychology, Neuropsychology, Cognitive Neuroscience or a related discipline Prior experience in conducting adult cognitive testing and neuroimaging (fMRI, EEG) Prior experience with participant recruitment processes Prior experience and familiarity with data management protocols and ethical regulatory frameworks in Singapore Experience in performing general administration tasks for research projects Experience in producing research reports Good statistical knowledge and skills, including familiarity with statistical analysis software such as R and SPSS Good IT skills (Office®) Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills Excellent organizational skills and able to work within given deadlines Excellent time management and organizational skills.  We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Please apply by uploading your CV and academic transcript to NTU job portal link. If you have any questions, please feel free to reach out to us at clic@ntu.edu.sg . Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Education-Research-Scientist--Science-of-Learning-in-Education-Centre--SoLEC---NIE-_R00025887": {
      "title": "Education Research Scientist, Science of Learning in Education Centre (SoLEC) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nOverview The National Institute of Education (NIE) is among the world’s top education institutes, recognised for its excellence in teacher education and educational research. NIE has played a key and pivotal role in shaping and developing Singapore’s teaching profession and landscape through evidence-informed, practice-focused and values-based programmes and initiatives. An autonomous institute situated within the research-intensive Nanyang Technological University, NIE is consistently ranked within the top 10 in the world for research impact in the field of Education. The Science of Learning in Education Centre (SoLEC) is a dynamic young research center with the ambition to become an international leader in Science of Learning in Education. Hosted at the National Institute of Education (NIE), SoLEC advances cutting- edge research by integrating insights from neuroscience, cognitive science, psychology, physiology, education, technology and AI in Education. We welcome exceptional candidates who thrive at the intersection of learning and data sciences. The ideal candidate brings a proven track record of impactful, interdisciplinary research. We especially encourage applications from scholars and researchers with expertise at the intersection of cognitive science, psychology, statistics and data analytics. Candidates with appropriate qualifications and relevant research experience are encouraged to apply. We invite applications for the position of Education Research Scientist to join SoLEC. Requirements PhD in a relevant discipline (e.g. Cognitive Science, Psychology, Statistics, Data Analytics or a closely related field) Up to 2 years of post-PhD experience Ability to lead and collaborate within research teams Strong track record in the following are as: - Publishing in high quality, peer-reviewed journals - Securing competitive, peer-reviewed research funding - Conducting independent, innovative research - Applying appropriate data analytics and research methods to learning and educational data Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (spoken and written English) Responsibilities   Design and implement SoLEC’s research programmes in collaboration with colleagues Lead the development of research projects and secure external funding opportu-nities Publish internationally in peer-reviewed journals and disseminate impactful findings Translate research into practice and policy impact within education systems Manage administrative and programme‑related tasks to ensure smooth operations Contribute to strategic research initiatives of SoLEC, OfR and NIE Participate actively in the wider research and service community of NIE   Application Interested applicants should complete and submit the following documents: Cover letter addressing how you meet each of the requirements of this position Curriculum vitae (including qualification, publications, records of competitive grants and graduate supervision, if applicable); Research statement indicating your research areas and accomplishments, highlight best research papers with Tier 1 publications, and research plans Any other documents that demonstrate your qualifications   Closing Date The closing date for applications is 30 October 2026 .   Other Information Queries regarding the position should be directed to sandra.chua@nie.edu.sg   Note to applicants: We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified via email. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Natural-Sciences---Science-Education-Department---NIE-_R00025826": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Natural Sciences & Science Education Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Research Assistant on a 6-month contract at the Natural Sciences & Science Education Department .   Project Title: Multiplexed fluorescent nanosensor array for AI-enabled rapid gut health biomarker detection   Project Introduction: We are seeking a highly motivated Research Assistant to join our team on a medical technology translation project. Our work focuses on the technical and commercial advancement of a breakthrough optical nanosensor platform, moving it from the laboratory into a practical clinical, AI-enabled diagnostic tool. By developing and deploying multiplexed sensor arrays that rapidly screen for critical gut health and inflammatory biomarkers simultaneously, we aim to achieve functional assessment of gut health. This role offers a unique opportunity to work at the cutting edge of deep tech nano-biotechnology, while actively participating in real-world commercialization pathways and venture design. Strong performance opens future pathways ahead including potential contract renewal, direct involvement in spin-off venture conversion, or mentorship towards PhD graduate study in chemical biology and biosensing.   Requirements: Essential Bachelor’s degree in Chemical Biology, Biochemistry, Biological Sciences, Chemistry, Chemical Engineering or a related field. Careful and systematic in conducting laboratory work. Reliable and able to adhere closely to established experimental protocols. Proactive and willing to learn, with the ability to work independently after appropriate training. Demonstrates a strong interest in and passion for deep-tech commercialization and venture design.   Preferred Hands-on experience working in a Biosafety Level 2 (BSL-2) laboratory environment, including the operation and maintenance of Class II Biological Safety Cabinets (BSC). Prior experience with biological assays, biofluids, or metabolite biosensing. Proficiency in data analysis tools (e.g., Excel, Origin, Python, etc.). Familiarity with spectroscopic techniques (e.g., fluorescence, Raman spectrophotometry, and UV-Vis spectrophotometry). Prior experience or exposure to deep-tech commercialization and translation, such as participation in entrepreneurial bootcamps, technology transfer projects, or startup environments.   Responsibilities:   Assay & Nanosensor Testing : Conduct systematic optical assays, including fluorescence and absorbance measurements, to evaluate nanosensor array responses to target gut health biomarkers and metabolites. BSL-2 Laboratory Operations: Perform biofluid and chemical preparation, routine biological sample assays, while maintaining strict BSL-2 biosafety protocols and proper use of Biosafety Cabinets (BSC). Data Analysis & Protocol Optimization: Record, analyze, and document experimental dataset reproducibility to support device optimization and translational milestones. Venture & Clinical Integration: Assist with translating bench data for venture design workshops, startup commercialization activities, and clinical partner updates. Lab Maintenance: Assist with baseline equipment setup, reagent inventory, and biosafety compliance in the laboratory. Any other administrative duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator.   Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Mechanical-Engineering-_R00023282": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Mechanical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Fellow. The role will focus on helping to build thermal-flow engineering and bioengineering expertise in the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Research domain to establish itself as a World Class Centre and well recognized in Singapore and beyond, enhancing the academic excellence of NTU and attracting interest of more industrial collaborators. Key Responsibilities: Develop a new and robust numerical model with lattice Boltzmann method to simulate flow and heat transfer with phase change processes. Carry out thorough a numerical investigation of the phase change characterizations. Examine underlying physical mechanisms and propose relevant physical scaling laws. Plan and carry out experiments. Be responsible for conducting high quality research, writing journal/conference papers, and assisting in student supervision and writing the project report. Job Requirements: A PhD’s degree in mechanical engineering or related engineering field. Know multiple-scale and multi-phase numerical modeling and familiar with lattice Boltzmann simulations Having rich skills in coding in Fortran/C/C++ and high-performance computing Good knowledge in fluid mechanics, heat and mass transfer as well as surface phenomena. With good record in publishing research papers. Preferably with expertise in deep learning approaches and also experimental experience. Good communication and writing skills & team player. Strong interest in research work. Highly motivated, independent and resourceful. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager--Grant-Administration_R00025886": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, Grant Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Institute for Digital Molecular Analytics and Science (IDMxS) is a new, unique interdisciplinary Research Centre of Excellence (RCE), funded by Ministry of Education (Singapore), Nanyang Technological University and National University of Singapore.   The Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, Grant Administration supports the effective administration and financial management of research grants at IDMxS, ensuring compliance with funding guidelines, regulatory requirements, and reporting deadlines. The role works closely with researchers, funding agencies, and internal stakeholders to support research activities and facilitate the smooth execution of grant-related processes. Responsibilities Grant Administration Manage the full grant lifecycle, including application submission, award creation, variations, and grant closure. Review grant proposals, communicate approved budgets, and ensure compliance with funding guidelines and requirements. Provide financial and grant advisory support to Principal Investigators (PIs), researchers, funding agencies, and internal stakeholders. Monitor grant budgets, verify expenses, prepare forecasts and reports, and follow up on funding disbursements. Coordinate with internal and external stakeholders on grant administration matters and identify new grant opportunities for the Centre.   Research Support Administration Support research operations through purchase requisition approvals, finance coding, invoice processing, journal postings, and claims submissions. Administer and track purchase requisitions through the ARIBA system. Coordinate manpower administration activities, including funding checks and maintenance of related documentation. Create and maintain project structures (WBS/PID) to support research grants and manpower funding requirements. Provide administrative support to Centre leadership, including meeting coordination, travel arrangements, expense claims, and other ad hoc operational duties. Maintain annual Grant Calls Calendar and effectively prompts PIs 3 months ahead of time and thereafter, to facilitate the application of grant calls.   Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Business Administration, or a related field. Minimum 3+ years of experience in grant administration, preferably in a research, higher education environment. Must have knowledge of and experience in all administrative functions associated with end-to-end grant management. Experience in research benchmarking (e.g., calculating H-index, FWCI-index) will be advantageous. Strong communication, organisational, analytical, and problem-solving skills, with a keen attention to detail. Ability to collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders, including researchers, funding agencies, and senior leadership, while ensuring compliance with governance requirements. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Principal-Research-Fellow--4D-Printing-Technology-_R00025880": {
      "title": "Principal Research Fellow (4D Printing Technology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) is a research centre conducting fundamental and applied research in all aspects related to additive manufacturing. Our vision is to be the world leader in 3D Printing and a wellspring of knowledge, delivering state of the art and innovative solutions to the industry. SC3DP is at the forefront of developing advanced technologies and high-impact research in areas such biomedical, construction, aerospace, marine and offshore. It is one of the very few research centres globally with multi-sector 3D printing expertise. SC3DP’s research achievements, high-level industry collaboration, comprehensive facilities and resources have positioned it as a leading hub for 3D printing research and innovation globally. The Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) at Nanyang Technological University is seeking a Principal Research Fellow to lead the research and commercialization activities of the 4D printing technology. The role will translate the project’s research and clinical progress into various commercial applications, while integrating market validation, business-model development, strategic partnerships, IP and licensing strategy, regulatory-commercial planning, manufacturing strategy, fundraising readiness and spin-off formation. Key Responsibilities Direct research activities that translate 4D Printing research into applications with commercial potentials Secure major external funding by writing competitive research grants and partnering with industry or government bodies Direct cross-functional alignment with the technical and clinical teams to translate customer, partner and regulatory feedback into product-development priorities, validation requirements and commercially relevant specifications. Lead commercialisation strategy, venture development and execution against government grant fund objectives. Develop and validate the business model, value proposition, market-entry strategy and customer requirements. Build OEM, distributor, clinical, manufacturing, investor and strategic partner pipelines and progress commercial agreements. Coordinate commercial aspects of HSA/FDA, QMS, manufacturing and legal-manufacturer strategy with relevant specialists. Lead spin-off, IP/licensing, financial model, fundraising and investment-readiness activities. Establish commercial KPIs, governance, risk management and stakeholder reporting. Job Requirements Master’s degree or equivalent postgraduate qualification in engineering, science, technology, business or a related field. At least 15 years of relevant experience, including senior responsibility for deep-tech commercialisation, venture creation, technology transfer or technology-based businesses. Strong track record in research translation, competitive translational funding, industry partnerships, licensing/spin-offs and venture readiness. Demonstrated capability in business-model development, market validation, IP strategy, fundraising and strategic negotiation. Excellent stakeholder-management and communication skills across academia, government, industry, clinical partners and investors. International experience and strong networks in Singapore’s innovation ecosystem and global industry are advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Bioinformatics-and-Cancer-Genomics---LKCMedicine_R00025883-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Bioinformatics and Cancer Genomics), LKCMedicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are looking for a Research Associate to support bioinformatics research, with particular focus on cancer genomics and cancer screening at the Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine. The role will focus on analysing genomic and clinical data and supporting the development of cancer survival prediction models. Key Responsibilities:   • Analyse and interpret cancer genomic and associated clinical data using bioinformatics and statistical methods. • Perform data cleaning, quality control and integration, and maintain reproducible analysis scripts and records. • Assist in developing and evaluating survival prediction models for breast cancer research. • Provide day-to-day bioinformatics support to the PhD student, including analyses and figures for thesis completion and defence. • Work with the research team to prepare grant proposals, figures, reports and manuscripts, and communicate findings. Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies:   Masters or equivalent qualification degree in Bioinformatics, Data Science, Computational Biology, Genomics, Biostatistics or related field Experience in bioinformatics or genomic data analysis through coursework, research projects or employment. Familiarity with cancer genomics and statistical methods Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in in R or Python for data analysis and visualisation Competent in analytical and problem-solving skills, with attention to detail. Ability to work independently and collaboratively, with good organisational and time management skills. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Trust-Technologies-_R00025885": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for its people and businesses by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize. We are looking for a Research Engineer to develop, implement, deploy, and maintain backend systems and platform infrastructure for Trust Technology and related areas such as privacy and security, which are important components of digital trust platforms. The role will focus on developing secure and scalable backend services, managing data storage and user information, and supporting the deployment and operation of web-based applications. Key Responsibilities:   Design, develop, deploy, and maintain backend services and platform infrastructure to support research prototypes and digital trust applications. Work closely with Centre’s researchers to translate research outputs into scalable and deployable system implementations. Set up and manage databases, storage systems, and backend services, including platforms such as Supabase, with appropriate security controls for protecting user information and sensitive data. Deploy and maintain web applications, including authentication, authorisation, access control, and related application security mechanisms. Support platform deployment, system integration, monitoring, maintenance, and scaling to ensure reliable and secure system operation. Job Requirements: Minimum Bachelor’s degree in computer science/ engineering or related fields. Proficiency in programming languages such as Java, Python, Go, C/C++ or other backend development languages is required. Experience with backend development frameworks will be an advantage. Proficiency with working with common Linux distributions such as Ubuntu, CentOS, RHEL etc. (including shell scripting) is required. Proficiency and experience in backend system development, API development, and deployment of web-based applications is required. Proficiency in installing, configuring, and using SQL databases is required. Experience with backend and database platforms such as PostgreSQL, Supabase, or other cloud-based data services will be an advantage. Experience in deploying and maintaining applications in cloud-based or containerised environments, and supporting system scalability and availability, will be advantageous. Experience in implementing authentication, authorisation, access control, and security mechanisms for web applications and backend services will be advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Trust-Technologies-_R00025878": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for its people and businesses by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize. We are looking for Research Engineers to design and develop secure web applications and platforms in Trust Technology and related areas such as privacy, security, and digital payments. The roles will focus on full-stack web development, secure authentication and authorisation, and the implementation of user workflows and payment-related protocols to support trusted digital transactions. Key Responsibilities:   Design and develop secure full-stack web applications using JavaScript, Node.js, and related frameworks. Implement authentication, authorisation, and security mechanisms, including JWT, OAuth, and relevant cryptographic protocols. Develop end-to-end user workflows, including registration, onboarding, and payment-related processes. Integrate APIs, payment services, and emerging payment protocols to support secure digital transactions. Work with researchers and industry partners on system development, UI design, testing, and deployment. Job Requirements:  Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or related fields. Proficiency in JavaScript, Node.js, and frontend and backend web development. Good understanding of authentication, authorisation, JWT, OAuth, and web application security. Experience in API development, database integration, and implementing end-to-end user workflows. Knowledge of payment rails, merchant payment processing, or emerging protocols such as A2P and Verified Intent is advantageous. Good problem-solving, communication, and teamwork skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Finance--LKCMedicine-_R00025877-1": {
      "title": "Senior/Assistant Manager, Finance [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. This position plays a key role in supporting the Finance Business Partner and works closely with respective stakeholders on forecasting, budgeting, analysis and reporting activities, manages the school’s financial closure activities leading to the completion of annual audited financial statements, manages the Endowment Fund reporting; and collaborates with NTU/LKCMedicine Advancement Office on Donors’ reporting. Responsibilities: Periodic financial and management reporting. Liaise with external auditors and manage auditors’ request for audit schedules / samples / documentation during audit fieldwork. Analyse and review of Fund Centre Reports and highlight any irregularity / inconsistency with the FP&A Team. Provide adhoc/periodic fund activities report to Donors. Support the coordination of revised estimates and budget inputs from respective stakeholders to develop annual operating budgets and evaluate short-term and long-term funding requirements. Monitor budget to actual results and provide insightful variance analysis of significant deviations to identify any financial risk and opportunity. Provide guidance and support to stakeholders in budgetary control and expenditure management. Continuous process improvement on financial and management reporting. Requirements: A degree from a recognized university in Accountancy or Professional accounting qualifications. Understanding of accounting principles and clear knowledge of Financial Reporting Standards. Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel (including V-lookup, Pivot Table etc.) and knowledge of SAP financial system will be an added advantage. Strong organizational and administrative skills, particularly in the areas of compliance and customer engagement skills. Numerically inclined, meticulous, proactive, with good analytical, communication and interpersonal skills. Good time management, able to multi-task and meet tight reporting deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Able to work independently, perform under pressure and work effectively as a team. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. This is a contract position till 31 March 2029. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Veterinarian--Animal-Research-Facility--LKCMedicine-_R00025879": {
      "title": "Veterinarian, Animal Research Facility [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Veterinarian will be responsible for providing high-quality medical care to a range of laboratory animal species, ensuring their health and well-being through preventative care, diagnostics, treatment, and surgical procedures. This role requires a dedicated professional committed to upholding the highest standards of veterinary medicine and animal welfare. Responsibilities: Prevention, Diagnosis, Control and Treatment of Disease Assessment of sick and dead animals, including necropsy of dead animals if needed. Prescribing and administration of treatment/euthanasia of sick animals. Implement, manage and continuously refine the sentinel animal health monitoring system. Review all incoming and outgoing animal health review and approval.  Addressing nutritional requirements when required. Oversee quarantine protocols, species-specific nutritional requirements, and bio-exclusion controls. Pain and distress- prevention, minimization and alleviation Advising staff and researchers about the use of analgesics and anaesthetics in animals, including dispensing of above-mentioned drugs/agents. Keeping records of all drugs provided to researchers/staff. Procurement of drugs or agents used in veterinary medicine. Keeping records of veterinary drugs provided to staff and researchers. Maintain procurement, inventory, and strict controlled drug logbooks in compliance with university and statutory standards. Oversee environmental enrichment and husbandry programs that reduce stress and enhance physiological stability. Ensure that all welfare concerns regarding the use of animals within the facility meets regulatory guidelines. Pain and distress must be minimised or eliminated when possible. Assisting the researchers on procedures and general equipment usage Train the researchers regarding the safe use of euthanasia chambers and anaesthetic equipment. Ensuring that all anaesthetic equipment are maintained and calibrated on a regular basis. Ensure that all physical means of euthanasia are carried out appropriately without any welfare concerns. Advise the researchers and staff on the aseptic surgical methodologies, fluid administration and withdrawal volumes and breeding colony maintenance. Conduct Responsible Care and Use of Animals (RCULAC) and Responsible Care and Use of Fish (RCUF) Practical courses for new users. Review RCULAC online theory course to ensure that information provided is accurate and up to date. Provide expert consultation on complex surgical procedures, aseptic techniques, post-operative management, and emergency critical care. Design, coordinate, and deliver theoretical and practical training modules, including RCULAC and RCUF practical courses for research personnel. IACUC Address all regulatory requirements of a veterinarian as defined by the NACLAR Guidelines. This includes sitting on the IACUC committee and reviewing animal use protocol, facility and program evaluations, monitoring of IACUC compliance and advising researchers regarding sick/moribund animal, humane endpoints and treatment plans/euthanasia. In cases of non-compliance with IACUC protocols, to work with the IACUC secretariat on addressing such concerns. Implement researcher/staff training sessions to enhance ongoing training and development of researchers and facility staff. Requirements: A degree in veterinary medicine AVS licensed veterinarian with 2-3 years working experience, preferably with experience in laboratory animals veterinary care in research setting in academia Restricted license veterinarian or veterinarian eligible for restricted license and with at least 2-3 years working experience in laboratory animals may be considered. This is a 3 years contract appointment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-the-School-of-Mechanical-and-Aerospace-Engineering--MAE-_R00025884": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for part time teaching positions.   We are looking for part-time instructors in the areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering within the College of Engineering, School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering.   Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a recognized MEng degree, preferably PhD, in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels.   Teaching Hours Classes are mainly conducted during the day/night on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). In view of the current COVID situation, online teaching and assessments are expected to be conducted where required. In addition, applicant must be prepared to act according to the situational changes in number of CAs, CA formats, etc. when required by the School. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Flexible-Bioelectronics-_R00025876": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Flexible Bioelectronics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research .   We are seeking a highly motivated and interdisciplinary Research Fellow to support the development and integration of soft, flexible, and stretchable electronic materials and devices. The role centres on the design, fabrication, and characterisation of soft functional materials, films, and device interfaces for flexible and bio-integrated electronics, with emphasis on mechanical/strain engineering, adhesion and interface design, and reliable device performance under deformation. Application areas include soft bioelectronics and wearable sensing, plant biointerfaces, and electrophysiological signal monitoring. The successful candidate will contribute to NTU’s research in advanced materials and soft/flexible device platforms by bridging materials science, interfacial engineering, and soft/stretchable electronics.   Key Responsibilities: Design, fabricate, and characterise soft functional materials, films, and device interfaces for flexible, stretchable, and bio-integrated electronic devices, including biointerfaces for electrophysiological and environmental sensing. Develop soft and bio-derived functional materials, adhesive and interface designs, and mechanical/strain-engineering strategies that enable strong adhesion, strain isolation, and reliable device function under deformation. Conduct microstructural, chemical, mechanical, and electromechanical characterization, including electrical and reliability evaluation under bending, stretching, and cyclic deformation. Collaborate with interdisciplinary researchers to integrate soft-material and device solutions into flexible and stretchable electronic systems, sensors, and platforms where relevant. Assist in manuscript preparation, conference presentations, grant development, and reporting to funding agencies and collaborators. Mentor junior researchers and students, and support general laboratory management, procurement and equipment coordination where required.   Job Requirements: PhD in Materials Science, Chemistry, Bioengineering, Electronic/Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline. Demonstrated research experience in flexible/stretchable electronics, soft or bio-derived functional materials, or soft device interfaces. Strong background in the design and characterisation of soft materials and/or device interfaces, including adhesion, mechanical/strain engineering, and electromechanical behaviour on soft or deformable substrates. Experience in one or more of the following areas is highly desirable: soft and stretchable hybrid electronics, biomaterials for bioelectronics, plant biointerfaces and electrophysiological sensing, adhesive and interface materials, flexible/stretchable device fabrication, and reliability of devices under repeated mechanical deformation. Familiarity with microstructural, chemical, mechanical, and electrical/electromechanical characterisation methods for materials and interfaces; data-analysis skills (e.g., MATLAB) an advantage. Publication record in reputable journals and the ability to independently drive research tasks to completion. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
