    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Engineering-Computer-Science-Electronics-Engineering-_R00025892": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering)",
      "description": "Research Associate (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering) Skip to main content Sign In Search for Jobs Research Associate (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering) page is loaded Research Associate (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering) Apply locations NTU Main Campus, Singapore time type Full time posted on Posted Yesterday job requisition id R00025892 Young and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: Designing and developing scalable algorithms for building Spatial Data Systems. Wring research papers of high quality based on research results Building deployable systems based on the research results. Job Requirements: Preferably Master degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Electronics Engineering or equivalent. Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills In-depth knowledge relevant to the project domain. Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research. The ability and willingness to adapt and incorporate novel ideas and approaches in scientific industry. Demonstrated ability to formulate hypothesis and design effective experimental plans. Ability to design and implement new experimental methods. High-level expertise in the required experiment or modelling methods. Ability to initiate collaboration research in multidisciplinary team. Oversee and report project progress. Ability and willingness to work some flexible hours. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU Similar Jobs (5) Research Associate (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering) locations NTU Main Campus, Singapore time type Full time posted on Posted Yesterday Research Associate (Computer engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering) locations NTU Main Campus, Singapore time type Full time posted on Posted 20 Days Ago Research Associate (Computer Science/Electronics Engineering) locations NTU Main Campus, Singapore time type Full time posted on Posted Yesterday View All 5 Jobs About Us A research-intensive public university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in the Engineering, Business, Science, Humanities, Arts, & Social Sciences, and Graduate colleges. It also has a medical school, the Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine, established jointly with Imperial College London. NTU is also home to world-class autonomous institutes – the National Institute of Education, S Rajaratnam School of International Studies, Earth Observatory of Singapore, and Singapore Centre for Environmental Life Sciences Engineering – and various leading research centres such as the Nanyang Environment & Water Research Institute (NEWRI) and Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N). Ranked amongst the world’s top universities by QS, NTU has also been named the world’s top young university for the past seven years. The University’s main campus is frequently listed among the Top 15 most beautiful university campuses in the world and has 57 Green Mark-certified (equivalent to LEED-certified) buildings, of which 95% are certified Green Mark Platinum. Apart from its main campus, NTU also has a campus in Novena, Singapore’s healthcare district. Under the NTU Smart Campus vision, the University harnesses the power of digital technology and tech-enabled solutions to support better learning and living experiences, the discovery of new knowledge, and the sustainability of resources. For more information, visit www.ntu.edu.sg About NIE About RSIS About LKCMedicine About NTUItive Read More © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Engineering-Computer-Science-Electronics-Engineering-_R00025891": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty.   A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing.   Key Responsibilities: Designing and developing scalable algorithms for building Spatial Data Systems. Wring research papers of high quality based on research results Building deployable systems based on the research results.   Job Requirements: Preferably Master degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Electronics Engineering or equivalent. Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills In-depth knowledge relevant to the project domain. Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research. The ability and willingness to adapt and incorporate novel ideas and approaches in scientific industry. Demonstrated ability to formulate hypothesis and design effective experimental plans. Ability to design and implement new experimental methods. High-level expertise in the required experiment or modelling methods. Ability to initiate collaboration research in multidisciplinary team. Oversee and report project progress. Ability and willingness to work some flexible hours.     We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.       Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Paleoseismology---Neotectonics----Levelling-Data-Investigation-_R00025914": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Paleoseismology & Neotectonics)/ (Levelling Data Investigation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Multidisciplinary Team at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore These cluster hires will contribute to an integrated programme spanning fault assessment, seismic and geodetic monitoring, earthquake physics, ground-motion modelling, site response, exposure and vulnerability, and probabilistic seismic hazard and risk assessment, working to strengthen Singapore’s national capabilities. New hires will join a multidisciplinary research team spanning Nanyang Technological University’s Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS), Asian School of the Environment (ASE), and School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE). For more information, please visit: https://earthobservatory.sg , https://ntu.edu.sg/ase , and https://ntu.edu.sg/cee .   We are looking to fill a total of 5 Research Assistant positions:   (1–4) Research Assistant (Paleoseismology & Neotectonics) We are looking for a Research Assistant to support geological field, laboratory, and analytical activities associated with paleoseismic trench investigations. The role will focus on trench preparation and documentation, surveying, sample collection and processing, sedimentological analysis, data management, and other technical support needed to complete rigorous investigations of past fault movement.   Key Responsibilities: Analyse existing geological data and digital terrain models to refine fault locations ahead of trenching Assist with preliminary geophysical field investigations at candidate trench sites Support paleoseismic field investigations, including trench excavation, wall cleaning, gridding, surveying, field documentation, and site permitting and logistics Assist experienced trench loggers with trench-wall logging and photographic documentation Assist with sedimentological and stratigraphic observations and preliminary data analysis Collect, label, and catalogue geological samples in the field for subsequent laboratory analysis and dating Process samples and prepare materials for geochronological dating and sedimentological analysis Support data management, including field records, photographs, and sample registers Mentor undergraduate interns who will be contributing mostly to desk-based analysis of geological data   Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in geology, geoscience, Earth science, geotechnical engineering, or a related field Basic knowledge of geology, sedimentology, stratigraphy, and geomorphology, with considerable prior geological field experience strongly preferred Familiarity with field documentation practice, including note keeping, photography, and sample labelling Proficiency with relevant mapping, drafting, GIS, and/or structure-from-motion software is strongly preferred Good written and oral communication skills, including the ability to contribute to technical reports for review by external experts Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team under demanding field conditions and strict timelines Excellent organisational and time-management skills, with meticulous attention to field documentation Careful and systematic approach to field documentation, sample handling, and data management, with a demonstrated ability to follow documentation protocols consistently Willingness and ability to perform demanding physical fieldwork, including extended periods in trenches in warm tropical regions, and to travel for fieldwork in the region. Entry-level candidates are welcome to apply where they can demonstrate the required technical background and relevant experience   (5) Research Assistant (Levelling Data Investigation) We are looking for a Research Assistant to join EOS. The successful candidate will work under the supervision of Asst Prof Lujia FENG and focus on the analysis of levelling data for tectonic deformation studies. The primary purpose of this position is to conduct high-quality research using historical and contemporary levelling observations to quantify crustal deformation, investigate long-term tectonic processes, and improve our understanding of earthquake hazards. The RA will support the compilation, digitization, analysis, and interpretation of geodetic datasets and contribute to the development of integrated geodetic models of deformation. The RA is also expected to contribute actively to other research activities within EOS.   Key Responsibilities: Compile, review, and evaluate levelling datasets to assess their suitability for constraining long-term vertical crustal deformation Digitize, quality control, analyze, and interpret historical levelling records Contribute to the integration of levelling, InSAR, and GNSS observations for the development of deformation fields, strain-rate maps, and geodetic models Assist with data management, documentation, and the preparation of technical reports Participate actively in research meetings, project discussions, and progress reporting Support other research activities within EOS as required   Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Earth science, Geophysics, Geodesy or a closely related field Proficiency in computational methods, with experience in programming using MATLAB, and/or Python Meticulous with a keen eye for detail and high level of accuracy Excellent written and verbal communications skills Proven ability to work both independently and collaboratively, with a strong sense of team spirit Entry level candidates are welcome to apply   Interested candidates should submit the following documents: A current curriculum vitae (CV) A succinct cover letter (not more than one page) detailing research interests and relevant experience The name and contact information for 2–3 references; institutional e-mail addresses are preferred, but other addresses will be accepted with suitable explanation If the candidate has relevant publications, they may include web links (URLs) in the CV or as an annex to the cover letter (this will not count toward the one-page limit)   We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and are committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.   We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Paleoseismology---Neotectonics----GNSS-Processing-and-Analysis----Seismic-Source-Characterisation----Ground-Motion-Characterisation----Geotechnics---Geophysics-_R00025911": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Paleoseismology & Neotectonics)/ (GNSS Processing and Analysis)/ (Seismic Source Characterisation)/ (Ground Motion Characterisation)/ (Geotechnics & Geophysics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Multidisciplinary Team at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore These cluster hires will contribute to an integrated programme spanning fault assessment, seismic and geodetic monitoring, earthquake physics, ground-motion modelling, site response, exposure and vulnerability, and probabilistic seismic hazard and risk assessment, working to strengthen Singapore’s national capabilities. New hires will join a multidisciplinary research team spanning Nanyang Technological University’s Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS), Asian School of the Environment (ASE), and School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE). For more information, please visit: https://earthobservatory.sg , https://ntu.edu.sg/ase , and https://ntu.edu.sg/cee .   We are looking to fill a total of 5 Research Fellow (postdoctoral scholar) positions:   (1) Research Fellow (Paleoseismology & Neotectonics) We are looking for a Research Fellow to lead paleoseismic trench investigations to reconstruct past fault activity. The role will focus on mapping potentially active faults, planning trench geometry, directing excavation, leading trench logging in the field, and interpreting stratigraphic and structural evidence for past earthquakes, then synthesising trench, dating, and sedimentological results into site reports suitable for technical review and possible publication.   Key Responsibilities: Analyse existing geological data and digital terrain models to refine fault locations ahead of trenching Collaborate with in-house experts in geophysical and CPT techniques to conduct preliminary surveys of candidate trench sites Lead planning and execution of paleoseismic trench investigations at multiple sites Design trench geometry and excavation strategies in consultation with the project leadership team Direct field activities, including trench excavation, wall preparation, gridding, logging, surveying, and sampling Lead interpretation of stratigraphic and structural relationships and assess evidence for past faulting and earthquake deformation Develop sampling strategies and coordinate geochronological, sedimentological, and other laboratory analyses Integrate field, borehole, geomorphic, geophysical, and laboratory evidence to develop histories of faulting Prepare trench logs, datasets, technical reports, conference abstracts, presentations, scientific manuscripts Mentor and supervise Research Associates and Research Assistants working within the trenching team Contribute to site prioritisation, subsequent field planning, and broader project synthesis   Job Requirements: PhD in geology, geoscience, Earth science, geotechnical engineering, or a related field At least 4 years of paleoseismic trenching experience, including a leading role in trench investigations at multiple sites and experience in different sedimentary and tectonic environments (experience gained during Master’s or PhD research may be counted towards this requirement) Demonstrated ability to map faults based on topographic and geomorphic expression, plan trench geometry, direct excavation, lead trench logging, and interpret stratigraphic and structural relationships in the field Familiarity with paleoseismic documentation standards appropriate for independent technical review, and with geochronological methods used to date past earthquakes Proficiency with relevant mapping, drafting, GIS, and structure-from-motion software Good written and oral communication skills, including the ability to prepare technical reports for review by external experts Ability to lead a small field team, work collaboratively across disciplines, and deliver results under fieldwork and permitting constraints Excellent organisational and time-management skills, with meticulous attention to field documentation Willingness and ability to perform demanding physical fieldwork, including extended periods in trenches in warm tropical regions, and to travel for fieldwork in the region.   (2) Research Fellow (GNSS Processing and Analysis) We are looking for a Research Fellow to join EOS. The successful candidate will work under the supervision of Asst Prof Lujia FENG and focus on GNSS data processing and analysis for tectonic deformation studies. The primary purpose of this position is to conduct high-quality research using geodetic observations to quantify crustal deformation, characterize fault-slip processes, and improve our understanding of earthquake hazards. The candidate will develop and maintain GNSS processing workflows, contribute to the interpretation of geodetic observations, and support ongoing research projects within the tectonics and geodesy research programme. The RF is also expected to contribute actively to other research activities within EOS.   Key Responsibilities: Develop and implement an automated post-processing workflow for GNSS data analysis using multiple software packages, including PRIDE PPP-AR, GAMIT/GLOBK, and GipsyX Process raw GNSS data, analyze position time series, and estimate station velocities and associated uncertainties Compile and assess published GNSS velocity fields for Southeast Asia Contribute to the integration of InSAR and GNSS observations and the development of deformation fields, strain-rate maps, and geodetic models Present scientific results at local and international meetings and conferences Write up research results for publication in reputable international journals Assist with data management, documentation, and the preparation of technical reports Participate actively in research meetings, project discussions, and progress reporting   Job Requirements: PhD in geodesy or related field At least 3 years of relevant experiences in GNSS data processing Strong computation skills with experience using MATLAB and/or Python Excellent written and verbal communications skills Evidence of being able to work both independently and collaboratively, with a strong team spirit   (3) Research Fellow (Seismic Source Characterisation) We are looking for a Research Fellow to develop the seismic-source component of Singapore’s national seismic hazard model. The role will focus on compiling and evaluating earthquake and fault datasets, modelling source geometry and earthquake occurrence, quantifying epistemic uncertainty, and building auditable logic-tree inputs for probabilistic seismic hazard assessments (PSHA).   Key Responsibilities: Compile, reconcile, and quality-assure earthquake catalogues and waveform datasets from Singapore, regional agencies, and international sources; undertake magnitude harmonisation, declustering, completeness analysis, and reanalysis of historical nearby events Evaluate geological, seismological, and geodetic evidence from other teams and external partners to identify and characterise relevant seismic sources Develop PSHA seismic-source models covering source geometries, distributed-seismicity zones, smoothed seismicity, three-dimensional shallow-crustal and subduction-interface structures, magnitude-frequency distributions, recurrence parameters, and maximum magnitudes Quantify epistemic uncertainty in alternative source interpretations and implement well-documented branches and weights in the seismic-source logic tree Integrate seismic-source models with ground-motion characterisation in version-controlled PSHA workflows; perform exploratory hazard calculations, sensitivity and disaggregation analyses Prepare reproducible datasets, code, technical reports, peer-reviewed publications, and presentations   Job Requirements: PhD in Earthquake Engineering, Civil Engineering, Seismology, Geophysics, Earth Sciences, Engineering Seismology, or a closely related field Strong research record in seismic-source characterisation, earthquake-catalogue analysis, statistical seismology, earthquake-occurrence modelling, fault-source modelling, or probabilistic seismic hazard assessment Demonstrated experience in earthquake-catalogue processing, including declustering, completeness analysis, magnitude harmonisation, recurrence modelling, magnitude-frequency distributions, or maximum-magnitude assessment Sound knowledge of distributed and fault-based source models, spatial seismicity modelling, logic trees, and the treatment of epistemic uncertainty in PSHA Proficiency in Python or a comparable scientific programming language, together with experience in geospatial analysis, reproducible computational workflows, and version control; familiarity with the OpenQuake Engine and the OpenQuake Model Building Toolkit is advantageous Ability to manage and quality-assure large, heterogeneous datasets and to produce transparent, traceable technical documentation suitable for scientific review Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to work independently, publish high-quality research, collaborate across multidisciplinary and international teams, and manage multiple research tasks   (4) Research Fellow (Ground Motion Characterisation) We are looking for a Research Fellow to develop the ground-motion component of Singapore’s national seismic hazard model. The role will focus on evaluating regional and global strong-motion data, selecting and adjusting ground-motion models, characterising site response and uncertainty, and building auditable logic-tree inputs for probabilistic seismic hazard assessments (PSHA).   Key Responsibilities: Compile, review, and quality-assure regional and global strong-motion databases, waveform records, and associated metadata, assessing their completeness and applicability to Singapore’s tectonic and geological setting Analyse regional recordings and model residuals and select candidate ground-motion models for relevant tectonic regimes, including shallow-crustal, subduction-interface, and intraslab earthquakes Apply stochastic ground-motion simulations to augment limited empirical data, particularly for nearby sources, and evaluate model performance through sensitivity and validation studies Develop and test host-to-target adjustments accounting for regional differences in stress drop, anelastic attenuation, kappa, source, path, and site effects Characterise site response and amplification, including the suitability of Vs30-based classifications, nonlinear soil behaviour, and other parameters relevant to Singapore’s geological conditions and built environment Characterise aleatory variability and quantify epistemic uncertainty through documented branches and weights in the ground-motion logic tree Integrate ground-motion characterisation with seismic-source models in version-controlled PSHA workflows   Job Requirements: PhD in Earthquake Engineering, Civil Engineering, Seismology, Geophysics, Earth Sciences, Engineering Seismology, or a closely related field Strong research record in ground-motion modelling, strong-motion data analysis, ground-motion models or prediction equations, stochastic simulation, site-response analysis, or probabilistic seismic hazard assessment Demonstrated experience in processing and quality-assuring strong-motion datasets and conducting residual analysis, model selection, model calibration, sensitivity testing, or validation Sound knowledge of earthquake source, path, and site effects, including stress drop, attenuation, kappa, site amplification, nonlinear soil behaviour, and aleatory and epistemic uncertainty Proficiency in Python, MATLAB, Julia, or a comparable scientific programming language, with experience in numerical analysis, reproducible workflows, and version control; familiarity with the OpenQuake Engine, the OpenQuake Model Building Toolkit, and strong-motion databases is advantageous Ability to manage large datasets, develop transparent and auditable modelling workflows, and produce clear technical documentation suitable for expert review Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to work independently, publish high-quality research, collaborate across multidisciplinary and international teams, and manage multiple research tasks   (5) Research Fellow (Geotechnics & Geophysics) We are looking for a Research Fellow to 1) curate and integrate available geotechnical, geological, and geophysical datasets; 2) develop 3D models for the characterization of near-surface geological formations; 3) develop geophysical methods for imaging and characterizing subsurface structures.   Key Responsibilities: Develop novel 3D modelling algorithms for near-surface characterization using curated geo-data Contribute to the development of intelligent geophysical imaging algorithms Publish high-impact research articles in leading international journals Assist in the preparation and development of competitive research proposals Support the supervision and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students   Job Requirements: PhD in Geotechnics, Geophysics, or a related field At least 2 years of relevant experience in geological modelling and/or geophysical imaging Familiarity with site investigation, borehole logging, and geophysical approaches Experience with machine learning or deep learning is preferred Good written and oral communication skills Interested candidates should submit the following documents: A current curriculum vitae (CV) A succinct cover letter (not more than one page) detailing research interests and relevant experience The name and contact information for 3 references; institutional e-mail addresses are preferred, but other addresses will be accepted with suitable explanation If the candidate has relevant publications, they may include web links (URLs) in the CV or as an annex to the cover letter (this will not count toward the one-page limit) We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and are committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.   We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Principal-Scientific-Data-Officer--Quality-Assurance---Quality-Control--Audit-_R00025910": {
      "title": "Principal Scientific Data Officer (Quality Assurance / Quality Control /Audit)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Multidisciplinary Team at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore These cluster hires will contribute to an integrated programme spanning fault assessment, seismic and geodetic monitoring, earthquake physics, ground-motion modelling, site response, exposure and vulnerability, and probabilistic seismic hazard and risk assessment, working to strengthen Singapore’s national capabilities. New hires will join a multidisciplinary research team spanning Nanyang Technological University’s Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS), Asian School of the Environment (ASE), and School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE). For more information, please visit: https://earthobservatory.sg , https://ntu.edu.sg/ase , and https://ntu.edu.sg/cee .   Principal Scientific Data Officer (Quality Assurance, Quality Control, and Audit)   We are looking for a Principal Scientific Data Officer (PDO) specialising in data QA/QC & data auditing. The PDO will be responsible for developing and implementing programme-wide data quality standards objectives with comprehensive data tracking and auditability. The objective is to establish an auditable database of all finalised information and data created by the research programme across its research teams in seismic monitoring, earthquake-hazard assessment, and seismic-risk analysis. The PDO will work closely with the research teams comprising some 40 research staff to develop database protocols and procedures for the documentation covering information acquisition and processing, and for models including their underlying model components and assumptions. The PDO will also conduct periodic internal data auditing to ensure data protocols and database are maintained to readily meet external data auditing requirements of ISO9001 or higher ISO/IEC27001. Key Responsibilities: Establish programme-wide data protocols and procedures for creating a comprehensive database of all finalized research information including data, models and associated documentation Develop and maintain an auditable database of all programme research information with appropriate data tracking, documentation and version control that can support future ISO certification such as ISO9001 or higher ISO/IEC27001. Working collaboratively with individual research teams as the data providers of the programme, populate and maintain the database as new research results are obtained, analyzed and finalized Perform regular internal data auditing to ensure established protocols and procedure are fully met on a continuing basis Prepare reproducible data subsets in support of technical reporting, peer-reviewed publications, and submissions to funding and regulatory agencies. Job Requirements: A Master’s degree or higher in a relevant scientific or engineering discipline (e.g. Data Science, Computer Science, Information Systems/Informatics, Geophysics, Earth Sciences, Civil/Earthquake Engineering), or a closely related field Formal training in data management, statistics, informatics, data science or closely related field Demonstrated capability in understanding of scientific workflows and research methodologies with the ability to translate research processes into robust data management and quality assurance practices Advanced qualifications or professional training in research quality management, information systems and/or regulatory compliance More than 8 years of relevant experience in scientific data management, research data governance, QA/QC, or data auditing with the last 5 years in progressively senior or leadership-level responsibilities Demonstrated leadership experience with responsibility in developing and implementing quality systems, governance frameworks, or audit programme for large, complex, multidisciplinary research programmes Strong interpersonal and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively and independently with research teams to resolve data discrepancies and conflicts, and manage competing priorities in a collaborative manner Experience working independently with funding agencies, external auditors and/or reviewers on matters relating to data management, data quality, governance and compliance Interested candidates should submit the following documents: A current CV, including name and contact information for two references A succinct cover letter (not more than one page) detailing relevant experience in scientific data management and research data governance If the candidate has relevant publications, they may include web links (URLs) as an annex to the cover letter We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and are committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.   We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Paleoseismology---Neotectonics---Fault-Zone-Analysis-in-Bedrock--and-Research-Engineer-II--Seismology-_R00025913": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Paleoseismology & Neotectonics)/ Fault-Zone Analysis in Bedrock) and Research Engineer II (Seismology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Multidisciplinary Team at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore These cluster hires will contribute to an integrated programme spanning fault assessment, seismic and geodetic monitoring, earthquake physics, ground-motion modelling, site response, exposure and vulnerability, and probabilistic seismic hazard and risk assessment, working to strengthen Singapore’s national capabilities. New hires will join a multidisciplinary research team spanning Nanyang Technological University’s Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS), Asian School of the Environment (ASE), and School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE). For more information, please visit: https://earthobservatory.sg , https://ntu.edu.sg/ase , and https://ntu.edu.sg/cee .   We are looking to fill a total of 4 Research Associate / Research Engineer II positions:   (1&2) Research Associate (Paleoseismology & Neotectonics) We are looking for a Research Associate to provide senior field and analytical support for paleoseismic trench investigations. The role will focus on mapping potentially active faults, trench-wall logging, stratigraphic and structural interpretation, sample collection and processing, sedimentological analysis, and integration of field and laboratory results under the direction of the lead trenching scientist.   Key Responsibilities: Analyse existing geological data and digital terrain models to refine fault locations ahead of trenching Collaborate with in-house experts in geophysical and CPT techniques to conduct preliminary surveys of candidate trench sites Lead documentation and interpretation of trench-wall exposures under the direction of the Research Fellow Recognise and record key stratigraphic and structural relationships in the field, including evidence for past surface rupture Support trench-log compilation, drafting, and integration of paired wall logs Support sample collection, processing, and preparation of materials for geochronological and sedimentological analysis Assist with integration of dating results and contribute to site interpretation Contribute to the preparation of site reports and technical documentation Guide and check the work of Research Assistants during logging, sampling, and field documentation Support wall preparation, gridding, surveying, and site logistics during trenching   Job Requirements: Master’s degree in geology, geoscience, Earth science, geotechnical engineering, or a related field At least 1 full year of paleoseismic trenching experience (experience gained during Master’s research may be counted towards this requirement) Demonstrated experience with sedimentology, structural geology, tectonic geomorphology, and Quaternary mapping, or comparable work Ability to recognize and document stratigraphic and structural relationships in the field Proficiency with relevant mapping, drafting, GIS, and structure-from-motion software Good written and oral communication skills, including the ability to prepare technical reports for review by external experts Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team under demanding field conditions and strict timelines Excellent organisational and time-management skills, with meticulous attention to field documentation Willingness and ability to perform demanding physical fieldwork, including extended periods in trenches in warm tropical regions, and to travel for fieldwork in the region. Entry-level candidates are welcome to apply where they can demonstrate the required technical background and relevant experience   (3) Research Associate (Fault-Zone Analysis in Bedrock) We are looking for a Research Associate to support a multidisciplinary geoscience research programme focused on the characterization of geological materials and the investigation of fault-zone processes in the subsurface, with the end goal of assessing fault behaviour and geological evidence of past deformation. The role will contribute to sample characterization; laboratory investigations including geochemical, mineralogical, microstructural, geomechanical, and/or geochronological testing; and integrating the results into fault-zone interpretation.   Key Responsibilities: Conduct routine geological logging, sample screening, and preliminary characterization of rock materials Support inventory, prioritisation, preparation, scanning, and digital archiving of priority bedrock cores Assist in identifying and selecting core intervals for follow-up detailed analysis Prepare samples of fault-zone materials and fractured bedrock for geochemical, mineralogical, microstructural, geomechanical, and geochronological testing, and support laboratory analyses Coordinate logistics related to sample handling, transportation, storage, and laboratory activities Support structural and mineralogical interpretation of faulted and fractured core intervals Assist with data collection, quality control, processing, visualization, and management of scientific datasets Maintain research databases, metadata records, and project documentation Support preparation of technical reports, conference abstracts, presentations, and scientific manuscripts Work closely with research staff, collaborators, and laboratory personnel to ensure timely delivery of project objectives   Job Requirements: Master’s degree in geology, geoscience, Earth science, geological engineering, or a related field is required; a Master’s thesis focused on petrology, mineral characterization, geochemistry, geochronology, structural geology, or related geoscience topics would be advantageous Experience in geochronological, geochemical, mineralogical, microstructural, or geomechanical laboratory work, and/or familiarity with identifying minerals suitable for geochemical or geochronological investigations Academic background in petrology, mineralogy, geochemistry, geochronology, structural geology, or closely related fields would be advantageous Experience with scientific data management and analysis is required; experience with core handling, sample preparation, scanning, laboratory workflows, or geological data management would be advantageous Good written and oral communication skills, including the ability to prepare technical reports for review by external experts Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary collaborative team, and to manage multiple concurrent laboratory workflows Excellent organisational and time-management skills, with meticulous attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate sample and data records Entry-level candidates are welcome to apply where they can demonstrate the required technical background and relevant experience   (4) Research Engineer II (Seismology) We are looking for a Research Engineer II to join a multidisciplinary team of seismologists and engineers working on AI-assisted earthquake monitoring and seismic data processing. The role will focus on developing an operational software package by integrating, optimizing, and validating existing workflows for routine seismic data processing. Beyond software development, the candidate will have opportunities to contribute to advanced AI algorithms and intelligent systems for agentic earthquake detection, processing, early warning, and interpretation.   Key Responsibilities: Integrate and optimize existing seismic data-processing workflows into robust operational software Test, validate, document, and maintain software packages for research and operational applications Contribute to the development of AI-assisted workflows for agentic earthquake monitoring, detection, warning, and interpretation Publish high-impact research outcomes in leading international journals or conferences Support student mentoring and technical training   Job Requirements: Master’s degree in computer science, data science, machine learning, engineering, geophysics, or related field Strong programming skills in Python and at least one compiled language, such as C, C++, or Fortran Experience in scientific software development, data processing, workflow integration, or system deployment Familiarity with artificial intelligence, machine learning, and AI-assisted coding tools is preferred Experience with seismic data, signal processing, scientific computing, or operational monitoring systems would be advantageous Strong problem-solving, communication, and teamwork skills   Interested candidates should submit the following documents: A current curriculum vitae (CV) A succinct cover letter (not more than one page) detailing research interests and relevant experience The name and contact information for 2–3 references; institutional e-mail addresses are preferred, but other addresses will be accepted with suitable explanation If the candidate has relevant publications, they may include web links (URLs) in the CV or as an annex to the cover letter (this will not count toward the one-page limit)   We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and are committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.   We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Electrocatalysis-_R00025917": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Electrocatalysis)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research .   We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research in advanced electrocatalysis and electrochemical synthesis. The role will focus on catalyst design, reaction mechanisms, and process development for selective electrochemical conversion of organic molecules and related energy-conversion reactions. The candidate will independently design and conduct experiments, establish structure-activity/selectivity relationships, develop scalable electrochemical systems and prepare publications. Depending on experience, the candidate may pursue independent research projects aligned with the team’s research directions.   Key Responsibilities: Design, synthesize, and characterize electrocatalysts and electrode systems for selective electrochemical transformations of organic molecules and related energy-conversion reactions. Conduct electrochemical measurements and reaction optimization to evaluate activity, selectivity, Faradaic efficiency, stability, and kinetics under relevant operating conditions. Investigate reaction pathways and interfacial mechanisms using electrochemical analysis, product analysis, and appropriate materials characterization, and establish structure-activity/selectivity relationships. Develop and optimize electrochemical reactors and scale-up strategies, including high-current-density operation and evaluation of process and techno-economic feasibility where relevant. Analyze data independently, maintain clear research records, prepare manuscripts, patents, reports and presentations, mentor junior researchers, collaborate across projects, and support laboratory safety and operations.   Job Requirements: A PhD in Chemistry, Materials Science and Engineering, Chemical Engineering, or a related field Strong background in electrochemistry and electrocatalysis, with research experience in electrocatalytic organic transformations, electrosynthesis, hydrogen/oxygen electrocatalysis, fuel cells, or related reactions Hands-on experience in catalyst or materials synthesis, electrochemical testing, reaction optimization, quantitative product analysis, and/or mechanistic investigation Experience in reaction pathway analysis, electrocatalytic kinetics, and structure-activity/selectivity relationships; experience in reactor engineering, scale-up, or techno-economic analysis would be an advantage Strong research track record demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications, with the ability to plan and conduct research independently and solve problems systematically Good teamwork, mentoring, organizational, and written and spoken communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Mechanical-Engineering---Bioengineering-_R00025915": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Mechanical Engineering / Bioengineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) is a research centre conducting fundamental and applied research in all aspects related to additive manufacturing. Our vision is to be the world leader in 3D Printing and a wellspring of knowledge, delivering state of the art and innovative solutions to the industry. SC3DP is at the forefront of developing advanced technologies and high-impact research in areas such biomedical, construction, aerospace, marine and offshore. It is one of the very few research centres globally with multi-sector 3D printing expertise. SC3DP’s research achievements, high-level industry collaboration, comprehensive facilities and resources have positioned it as a leading hub for 3D printing research and innovation globally. We are looking for a Research Associate to support the development of in vitro bioelectronic tissue models through biofabrication and biomaterials engineering. The role will focus on the design and fabrication of cell-laden hydrogel constructs, conductive biomaterials, and engineered tissue platforms, as well as their biological, structural, and functional characterization. The Research Associate will contribute to interdisciplinary research at the interface of tissue engineering, biofabrication, biomaterials, and bioelectronics, supporting the development of physiologically relevant in vitro models for fundamental research and translational applications.   Key Responsibilities: Develop and optimize biofabrication workflows for in vitro tissue models Prepare and characterize hydrogels, conductive inks, and bioinks Perform 3D bioprinting and post-fabrication processing of tissue constructs Conduct mammalian cell culture, maintenance, and biological assays Perform electrical stimulation and functional characterization experiments Carry out microscopy imaging and quantitative analysis of biological samples Support electrochemical and materials characterization experiments where required Maintain accurate experimental records and assist with manuscript/report preparation Contribute to laboratory operations, procurement, and equipment maintenance Collaborate with interdisciplinary research teams and external collaborators   Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Bioengineering or related field At least 3 years of relevant experience in tissue engineering, biomaterials, biofabrication, cell culture, or related experimental work Familiarity with mammalian cell culture practices, sterile techniques, hydrogel preparation, and biofabrication workflows Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in experimental laboratory techniques, microscopy imaging, data analysis, quantitative characterization, and scientific reporting Competent in soft skills including problem-solving, adaptability, interdisciplinary collaboration, and scientific communication Ability to work independently, develop solutions under strict timelines, and maintain meticulous experimental records with strong organizational and time management skills Candidates with strong hands-on laboratory experience are welcome to apply We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Centre-for-Research-in-Pedagogy-and-Practice---NIE-_R00025916": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Centre for Research in Pedagogy and Practice) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Research Assistant on a 2-year contract at the Centre for Research in Pedagogy and Practice (CRPP) .   Project Title: Main Study of CORE 4 Research Programme: Education Trend Studies of Designated Subject Domain (DSD) Pedagogies in Singapore’s Primary and Secondary Classrooms (C4MS).   Project Introduction: The Core Research Programme aims to provide a systemic measurement and modelling of curriculum and reform initiatives and pedagogical practices in a representative sample of Primary and Secondary schools in Singapore. Core has undergone three iterations and the Core 4 Main Study will continue the central objective of conducting empirical investigations into the nature of the “instructional core” of teaching and learning in Singapore classrooms. Research will focus on a series of Designated Subject Domains, which include English Language, English Literature, History, Humanities, Geography, Mathematics and Mother Tongue.   Requirements:   Essential: Bachelor’s degree, preferably in psychology, social sciences, education, or statistics. Ability to work independently and in a team Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills Good time management and organisational skills Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications   Preferred: Experience in using Statistical Package for the Social Sciences (SPSS) and/or NVivo qualitative data analysis software. Experience in classroom observations and video data coding. Experience of collating and organising large amounts of data (video/audio) Skills in or knowledge of managing/using a Network Attached Systems (NAS) to store data. Skills in or knowledge of setting up/managing a website.   Responsibilities: Perform literature review and report writing Conduct data collection (survey, student artefacts, classroom observations, focus group discussions, interviews), transcription, qualitative and quantitative data analysis Perform project administration tasks such as scheduling and liaising with teachers and preparation of materials Manage research data and assist with managing the Network Attached System Assisting the Principal Investigator in writing papers/publications and creating presentation materials Perform other assignments as determined by the Principal Investigator and co-Principal Investigators   Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Office-for-Research---NIE-_R00025918": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Office for Research) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Research Assistant on a 12-month contract at the Office for Research .   Project Title: RaDiX: Building flexibility and creativity to support lifelong learning through Physical Education   Project Introduction: This project intends to rely on Science of Learning and Movement Science to investigate the development of creativity in children and young adults. More precisely it looks at how to identify creative behavior and what is the long-term effect of practicing in a creative environment on the development of fundamental movement skills. The experimental protocol will involve participants performing different motor tasks, while the researchers will collect multimodal data (i.e., movement, brain imaging) to dive into what is a creative behavior, how to identify more creative persons and how to quantify motor creativity at the individual level.   Requirements:   Bachelor’s degree in sport science or related scientific discipline (e.g. neuroscience, computer science) Good knowledge in movement analysis techniques and brain imaging data acquisition (e.g., fNIRS, EEG) Experience in conducting experimental research on human participants Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing Excellent computer competency, strong knowledge of coding Excellent ability to manage large multi-source data set   Responsibilities:   Recruit participants and schedule data collection Assist with data collection using video camera and 3D motion capture system Enter and organize data Perform data analysis using specialized software (R, JASP, Python, Matlab) Prepare reports, conference presentations and draft for journal publications Support general maintenance and activities of NIE Motor Behavior Lab Other related duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator   Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--L-OD-Operations_R00025912-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, L&OD Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager supports the effective delivery of the University’s Learning and Organisational Development (L&OD) operations by ensuring accurate, timely and compliant administration of key people development programmes. This includes administering bond deeds and scholarships, providing end‑to‑end administrative support for training and development activities, managing absentee payroll matters, and overseeing invoicing, claims and charging to Colleges & Schools.   In addition, the role plays a key part in driving automation and digitalisation efforts, working closely with internal stakeholders to streamline learning workflows, standardise processes. The Assistant Manager contributes to the review and improvement of L&OD processes, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and service controls to ensure consistency, scalability, and compliance.   Through the consistent execution of these operational processes, the role enables the smooth functioning as well as improvement of staff development initiatives, supports financial and governance requirements, and ensures accountability in the use of development resources. The role contributes to the University’s broader mission by providing reliable operational infrastructure that supports staff capability building, workforce sustainability and institutional excellence.   Key Responsibilities: Provide end‑to‑end operational support for Learning & Organisational Development (L&OD) activities, including administration of bond deeds and scholarships, training and development coordination, absentee payroll support, and management of invoicing, claims and charging to Schools. Ensure accurate, timely and compliant execution of L&OD operational processes in accordance with University policies, service standards and governance requirements, supporting effective utilisation of development resources. Drive L&OD automation and digitalisation efforts by partnering with internal stakeholders to streamline learning workflows, reduce manual processing and improve data accuracy and operational efficiency. Review, standardise and maintain L&OD processes, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and service controls to ensure consistency, scalability, audit readiness and compliance.   Serve as a key operational point of contact for Schools, OHR, Finance and Payroll teams, facilitating coordination, resolving operational issues and supporting continuous improvement in L&OD service delivery.   Requirements: Degree in Administration or Human Resources areas Good knowledge of HR recruitment processes and employment‑related regulations is advantageous.   Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at different levels. Proven ability to manage high‑volume transactions with accuracy, attention to detail and sound judgement. Proficiency in HR systems (e.g. Workday) and Microsoft Office applications is an advantage. Entry level candidates are welcome. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Project-Coordination-Event-Management-Administration-_R00025909": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Project Coordination/Event Management/Administration)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. The University combines technological strength with human creativity to address the significant challenges facing society, and draws its faculty and students from across the world. The College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS) aims to be Asia’s leading centre for innovative, interdisciplinary humanities, arts and social science teaching and research. Its research priorities are Digital Culture and Society; Health, Culture and Society; Global Asia; and Art, Science and Ecology. The Global Asia Research Centre (GARC) is a research centre within the College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS), Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. The Centre serves as a platform for interdisciplinary research and scholarly exchange on Asia and its global connections, bringing together academics, researchers, policymakers, and industry partners through research initiatives, conferences, workshops, seminars, and public engagement activities.   Through its research programmes and events, GARC facilitates dialogue on issues of regional and global significance, supports the dissemination of research findings, and fosters collaborations across institutions and disciplines.   For more information, please visit: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/hass/research/global-asia-research-centre ---- Globally ranked among top research and technology organizations in the environment and water domain, the NTU’s Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI) ecosystem interacts across a multi- and inter- disciplinary platform of Research – engineering – Development (RED) activities in its approach to developing innovative solutions.   With leading edge technology and robust engineering, NEWRI strives to take its fundamental research from novel lab-scale innovation to industry-level translation and derisking activities - from field applications to piloting and development at full scale in real life settings. Through industrial and community- philanthropic projects for commercial and societal impact, NEWRI continuously strives to make a difference towards developing a circular economy for global sustainability.   For more details, please view   https://www.ntu.edu.sg/newri   This is a joint appointment between the Global Asia Research Centre and the Mining Mineral Life project, housed at the Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI). The Project Officer will contribute to the management and delivery of programs in the Global Asia Research Centre and the Mining Mineral Life: Extracting the Energy Transition in Southeast Asia research project. The role will be divided 60% on the Global Asia Research Centre and 40% on Mining Mineral Life. The role will be essential to the delivery of world class research programs and impact activities including organizing international conferences, seminars, fieldwork logistics.   At GARC, the candidate will join a team of the Director, the Deputy Director, and multiple Early Career Fellows. The centre also hosts Visiting Fellows and Visiting Professors.   On the Mining Mineral Life side, the candidate will join a team including the PI, two Research Fellows, and one PhD student. The team will also collaborate with artists and graphic designers on a program of scholarly and public facing artistic impact projects.    Key Responsibilities: Coordinate the planning and execution of conferences, workshops, seminars, lectures, and other Centre-related events. Liaise with internal and external stakeholders to confirm event requirements, budgets, timelines, and deliverables. Manage venue bookings, travel arrangements, accommodation, transportation, catering, and other logistical requirements. Administer event registration platforms and maintain participant databases. Coordinate the preparation and dissemination of invitations, publicity materials, event websites, and email communications. Monitor project and event budgets, process procurement requests, and support financial administration activities. Liaise with vendors and service providers, including caterers, transport providers, photographers, and accommodation providers. Coordinate event setup, onsite operations, attendee registration, and troubleshoot operational issues during events. Manage photography, videography, and event recording arrangements where required. Prepare post-event reports, maintain project documentation, and support reimbursement and claims processing. Support website content updates and post-event publicity activities. Undertake other administrative and project-related duties as assigned. Assist in the delivery of international conferences at NTU and elsewhere by liaising with participants, facilitating travel arrangements, booking of rooms and spaces at NTU and beyond. Helping to facilitate during events, manage and arrange catering and other essential bookings. Assist with hiring and onboarding of new research staff and PhD students. Assist with fieldwork logistics for research team, including flights, accommodation, visa applications, budgeting, monitoring project accounts, facilitate local and overseas payments.   Job Requirements: Educational Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Communications, Event Management, Project Management, Public Administration, Social Sciences, Humanities, or a related discipline.   Experience Experience in project coordination, event management, programme administration, or a related field is preferred. Experience in higher education, research administration, or academic environments would be advantageous.   Skills and Competencies Strong organisational and project coordination skills. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines simultaneously. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Excellent stakeholder management and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Outlook. Strong attention to detail and problem-solving abilities. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Experience with event management systems, website content management, or procurement platforms would be advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.  Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Trust-Technologies-_R00025908": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for its people and businesses by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize. We are looking for a Research Engineer   to design, development and deployment of LLM-powered AI agents that transform core insurance workflows, including underwriting, claims, policy servicing, risk assessment and customer engagement. The role will build autonomous and multi-agent systems capable of interpreting insurance documents, applying policy rules, supporting decision-making and executing end-to-end processes, while ensuring reliability, compliance and human oversight. By combining large language models, agentic AI frameworks and insuranc domain knowledge, this position will help the business improve operational efficiency, decision quality, customer experience and responsible AI adoption across the insurance value chain. Key Responsibilities:   Ability to code-switch effortlessly between talking business and talking tech, and can help stakeholders, engineers, and businesses easily understand complex AI and LLM research concepts Conduct research into LLM-powered AI agents and multi-agent systems – translating algorithms, tools, and frameworks into working prototypes that can explain how research outputs can be productised into new insurance capabilities. Work closely with Centre's researchers to design and develop system implementation work from research into the product, supporting key insurance workflows such as underwriting, claims, policy servicing and risk assessment. Design and build working agent tools and evaluation frameworks that can support the technology transfer of new AI capabilities to research partners and can be used to showcase the value of LLM-based agentic AI in insurance. Write and maintain technical documentation, presentations, and papers on AI agent design, evaluation, guardrails and trust mechanisms, helping to educate and raise the overall competency in responsible AI and trust technologies for insurance applications. Engage global partners and researchers to understand latest trends in LLMs, agentic AI and insurance technology, and advance Singapore's mindshare in trustworthy AI agent systems for the insurance sector. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Software Engineering or a related discipline; Relevant LLM or AI agent research experience is preferred. Ability to code-switch effortlessly between talking business and talking tech, and can help stakeholders, engineers, and businesses easily understand complex AI and LLM research concepts Strong hands-on experience with large language models, prompt engineering, retrieval-augmented generation, agent frameworks and multi-agent system design Proficiency in Python and common AI/ML tools and frameworks, with experience building production-grade AI applications, APIs, evaluation pipelines or agent orchestration systems Solid understanding of AI safety, guardrails, model evaluation, monitoring, data privacy, explainability and responsible AI practices in regulated environments Good knowledge of system platform development, database technologies, and software engineering best practices Experience in insurance, financial services or other regulated domains is preferred, including familiarity with underwriting, claims, policy servicing, risk assessment or customer engagement workflows We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Trust-Technologies-_R00025907": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for its people and businesses by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize. We are looking for a Research Engineer   to design, development and deployment of LLM-powered AI agents that transform core insurance workflows, including underwriting, claims, policy servicing, risk assessment and customer engagement. The role will build autonomous and multi-agent systems capable of interpreting insurance documents, applying policy rules, supporting decision-making and executing end-to-end processes, while ensuring reliability, compliance and human oversight. By combining large language models, agentic AI frameworks and insuranc domain knowledge, this position will help the business improve operational efficiency, decision quality, customer experience and responsible AI adoption across the insurance value chain. Key Responsibilities:   Ability to code-switch effortlessly between talking business and talking tech, and can help stakeholders, engineers, and businesses easily understand complex AI and LLM research concepts Conduct research into LLM-powered AI agents and multi-agent systems – translating algorithms, tools, and frameworks into working prototypes that can explain how research outputs can be productised into new insurance capabilities. Work closely with Centre's researchers to design and develop system implementation work from research into the product, supporting key insurance workflows such as underwriting, claims, policy servicing and risk assessment. Design and build working agent tools and evaluation frameworks that can support the technology transfer of new AI capabilities to research partners and can be used to showcase the value of LLM-based agentic AI in insurance. Write and maintain technical documentation, presentations, and papers on AI agent design, evaluation, guardrails and trust mechanisms, helping to educate and raise the overall competency in responsible AI and trust technologies for insurance applications. Engage global partners and researchers to understand latest trends in LLMs, agentic AI and insurance technology, and advance Singapore's mindshare in trustworthy AI agent systems for the insurance sector. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Software Engineering or a related discipline; Relevant LLM or AI agent research experience is preferred. Ability to code-switch effortlessly between talking business and talking tech, and can help stakeholders, engineers, and businesses easily understand complex AI and LLM research concepts Strong hands-on experience with large language models, prompt engineering, retrieval-augmented generation, agent frameworks and multi-agent system design Proficiency in Python and common AI/ML tools and frameworks, with experience building production-grade AI applications, APIs, evaluation pipelines or agent orchestration systems Solid understanding of AI safety, guardrails, model evaluation, monitoring, data privacy, explainability and responsible AI practices in regulated environments Good knowledge of system platform development, database technologies, and software engineering best practices Experience in insurance, financial services or other regulated domains is preferred, including familiarity with underwriting, claims, policy servicing, risk assessment or customer engagement workflows We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Lead--Student-Care_R00025906": {
      "title": "Lead, Student Care",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe EEE Undergraduate Office is seeking a Lead, Student Care to serve as the School’s Student Care Manager. The role leads individual pastoral care and complex student cases, academic intervention and at-risk follow-up, student discipline coordination and student-care governance, working closely with faculty, academic administrators and relevant University professional services. Key Responsibilities Lead individual student pastoral-care cases, including complex, sensitive and high-risk matters, and ensure appropriate assessment, follow-up, referral and escalation. Own academic intervention and at-risk student follow-up, coordinating actions with faculty, programme coordinators and academic administration colleagues. Coordinate School-level student discipline and conduct cases, including documentation, fact-finding, communication and management escalation. Support care-related Leave of Absence, withdrawal, reinstatement and financial/well-being referrals without duplicating process ownership held by other teams. Maintain clear crisis and escalation pathways and work closely with the University Wellbeing Office and other relevant professional services. Develop and maintain student-care SOPs, case-management practices, confidential records, reporting and trend analysis. Supervise the Assistant Manager, SEN & Student Support Programmes and maintain clear interfaces with SEN/support programmes, Student Life and Academic Operations. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Counselling, Psychology, Social Sciences, Social Work, Education, Student Affairs or a related discipline; candidates with substantial relevant experience from other disciplines may also be considered. At least 5 years of relevant experience in higher education, student affairs, student support, social services, counselling-related administration, case management or a related field. Demonstrated ability to manage sensitive or complex cases, exercise sound judgement and work effectively with multiple stakeholders. Strong interpersonal, communication, organisation and documentation skills, with high standards of confidentiality and discretion. Experience supervising or coaching staff and improving student-support processes is preferred. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Space-Planning_R00025905": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Space Planning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager, Space Planning supports the University's planning, allocation, utilisation and optimisation of its campus space portfolio. The role applies space data, analytics, forecasting and digital planning capabilities to support evidence-based decisions. The incumbent coordinates assigned planning workstreams, engages stakeholders across the University, and translates analysis into practical recommendations that improve space utilisation and planning outcomes.   Main Responsibilities: Support campus-wide space planning, allocation, utilisation and optimisation across assigned portfolios and planning initiatives. Conduct space demand assessments, utilisation analysis, capacity planning and scenario modelling to support current and future space requirements. Maintain reliable space inventory and planning data, apply data governance standards, and develop dashboards, analytics and management reports. Support digital space planning capabilities, including data models, visualisation tools, planning analytics and space information systems. Identify opportunities to improve the utilisation and efficiency of existing campus assets and support strategies to address space constraints and emerging needs. Develop and monitor key performance indicators, dashboards, and management reports to provide timely insights into space utilisation, capacity, demand, and portfolio performance.   Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Urban Planning, Real Estate, Facilities Management, Data Analytics, Engineering, Business, or a related discipline. At least 5 years experience in strategic space planning, campus planning, real estate portfolio management or a related field, preferably within a large and complex organisation. Track record in space demand assessment, utilisation analysis, capacity planning, planning analytics or optimisation of physical assets. Strong analytical and data capabilities, with experience using space information systems, dashboards, business intelligence tools, data visualisation or planning analytics. Strong problem-solving, project management, communication, presentation and stakeholder engagement skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Topological-Polaritons-_R00025904": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Topological Polaritons)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers.   Join the laboratory of Su Rui at SPMS. We are seeking a Research Fellow to contribute to a project focused on Topological polaritons.   Key Responsibilities:   Fabrication of topological exciton polariton lattices based on novel seminconductors Use electron beam lithographic techniques to etch novel lattice patterns Perform optical characterizations of structures using various optical spectroscopy Collaborate with theoretical researchers in the design and optimization for new fundamental effects and the creation of polaritonic topological lattices Perform nonlinear optical measurements, using interferometric, angle-resolved, and correlation type techniques Record, manage, and store collected data in line with NTUs data management policies Disseminate results in the form of peer-reviewed publications and presentations at international conferences Writing grant proposals and mentor PhD students   Job Requirements:   PhD in Physics, Optics, Material sciences, Engineering from a reputable University Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in microcavity sample fabrication and optical spectroscopy measurements. Track record of peer-reviewed papers in international journals   The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Lead--Lifelong-Learning--Academic-_R00025903": {
      "title": "Lead, Lifelong Learning (Academic)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) is one of the founding Schools of Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. The school is renowned for its academic and research excellence and has more than 120 faculty members and over 6,000 students, including approximately 3,000 graduate students. We invite applications for the position of Lead, Lifelong Learning (Academic) in the Associate Chair, Graduate (Lifelong Learning), MSc Programme Office. Reporting to the Head, Strategy and Lifelong Learning, the incumbent will work closely with the Head, Strategy and Lifelong Learning, Associate Chair, Graduate (Lifelong Learning), and Assistant Chair (Lifelong Learning) to support the strategic development, administration and effective delivery of its MSc programmes. Key Responsibilities Contribute to strategic initiatives to support the growth, development and positioning of the School’s MSc programmes. Lead and coordinate curriculum reviews, examinations and academic governance matters, including Memoranda of Agreement (MOAs) and related agreements with partner universities. Oversee and coordinate key administrative, financial and operational functions across the MSc programmes to ensure effective programme delivery. Drive process improvement and operational excellence through streamlining, automation and continuous improvement initiatives. Strengthen student experience by overseeing academic and wellbeing support, and ensuring enquiries and appeals are managed in a timely, consistent and equitable manner. Leverage data and insights to support programme planning, performance monitoring and management decision-making. Lead and support other strategic and cross-functional initiatives as assigned by the school. Requirements Bachelor’s degree with at least 10 years of relevant experience, or a postgraduate degree with at least 6 years of relevant experience, preferably in higher education, programme administration, operations, student services, recruitment, or admissions. Strong strategic, operational, project management and analytical capabilities. Good organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a service-oriented mindset. Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel, with demonstrated ability to perform data analysis, reporting and data-driven insights. Experience with Power BI, Microsoft Power Automate and other data visualization or process automation tools would be an advantage. Self-motivated, resourceful and able to work independently as well as collaboratively. Knowledge of the higher education landscape and university administration would be an advantage. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate---Research-Engineer-II--Robotics-and-Machine-Learning-_R00025927": {
      "title": "Research Associate / Research Engineer II (Robotics and Machine Learning)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research .   We are looking for a Research Associate / Research Engineer II to conduct cutting-edge research and software/hardware development in robotic systems operating under uncertainty. The role will focus on designing, implementing, and experimentally validating advanced algorithms in uncertainty-aware robot perception and robust robotic manipulation, directly supporting NTU's commitment to advancing world-class robotics research and industrial innovation.   Key Responsibilities:   Key responsibilities of the research engineer is to contribute to the following areas. Design, implement, and benchmark algorithms in probabilistic robotics, uncertainty-aware perception, and robust robotic manipulation under real-world uncertainties. Lead the development, maintenance, and public release of clean, well-documented open-source software repositories (e.g., ROS/ROS2 packages, Python/C++ libraries). Execute software-hardware integration for robotic manipulators, sensors, and actuators to build reliable, high-performance experimental setups. Plan and execute experimental validation in laboratory and field settings; evaluate perception-action loops using multi-modal sensor data. Draft invention disclosures for patents/IP protection and write research manuscripts for top-tier robotics publications (e.g., ICRA, IROS, RSS, T-RO). Manage laboratory infrastructure, ensure compliance with workplace safety standards, and co-guide student researchers.   Job Requirements: Master's degree in Robotics, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related discipline. Strong programming proficiency in C++ and Python, with hands-on experience in ROS/ROS2 and Linux environments. Solid theoretical foundation or practical experience in robot perception, state estimation, computer vision, or robotic manipulation under uncertainty. Experience with open-source software contributions, code versioning (Git), or patent disclosures is highly desirable. Excellent technical writing skills, proactive problem-solving mindset, and the ability to work effectively in a collaborative research team. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Professor-of-Viral-Immunity--LKCMedicine-_R00025930-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Viral Immunity [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nACADEMIC FACULTY APPOINTMENT:  The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine A Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Viral Immunity at Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine is expected to contribute to the development of research and teaching at the School. He/She is expected to undertake high quality internationally leading research in the area of Viral Immunity, in line with the overarching research strategy of Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine, in addition to any other duties as assigned by the Vice Dean, Research and Dean. Key Responsibilities Job Purpose: The appointee will be expected to undertake high quality research in the area of Viral Immunity, in line with the research strategy of the School and in conjunction with other recent appointments, obtain research funding and supervise research staff and students. The appointee is expected to undertake teaching and educational responsibilities for the training of medical students and postgraduate research students. Teaching methods will include extensive use of team-based learning and e-learning. The appointee is expected to contribute to integration of the science relating to Viral Immunity into the MBBS curriculum and to ensure the delivery of excellence in these areas, including the team-based delivery of the curriculum. Primary Activities: Undertake high quality research activities by sustaining a personal research plan, developing innovative research proposals and funding bids, managing and undertaking research activities, publishing in international peer reviewed journals, reviewing manuscripts and grant applications when appropriate. Seek competitive grant and collaborative industry funding to develop a sustainable research programme. Contribute to, support and develop teaching and educational activity at undergraduate level and supervise undergraduate students. Contribute to, support and develop teaching and educational activity at undergraduate and graduate level and supervise undergraduate and graduate students. Develop and support research projects (including interdisciplinary) with other faculty in the field of Respiratory & Infectious Diseases at LKCMedicine and across the wider NTU community. Supervise and mentor junior faculty members and research staff. Participate in academic committees and meet other administrative requirements as appropriate. Job descriptions cannot be exhaustive and the appointee may be required to undertake other duties which are broadly in line with the above key responsibilities as assigned by the Vice Dean, Research and Dean. Person Specification Qualifications, Knowledge and Experience: MBBS/MD and/or PhD degree(s) Relevant postdoctoral or clinical experience Significant experience and outstanding record of translational clinical research and teaching with a high level of scientific achievement, productivity and impact in the field of Viral Immunity. Management and Teamwork: Ability to lead and work as part of a multidisciplinary team Ability to work co-operatively with medical and non-medical staff Ability to supervise research staff and students Communicating and Influencing: Ability to communicate effectively with staff and students Ability to motivate others Strong presentation skills Ability to work in a team Desirable attributes: Experience and desire to participate in undergraduate and postgraduate medical education and training. Demonstrated ability to develop teams and to create networks. Fully conversant with patient-centred approach to modern medicine and the use of new technologies in both education and patient care. Understanding of the academic and administrative needs of internationally recognised universities. Ability to work in and develop teams and to create networks at both a national and international level. Track record of having supervised graduate students to successful completion of PhDs. Time Commitment The level of effort for this appointment is at 1.0 full time equivalent (FTE) employment. The closing date for applications is 15 November 2026. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Sales-Executive--Nanyang-Executive-Centre--Hospitality-_R00025929": {
      "title": "Sales Executive, Nanyang Executive Centre (Hospitality)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north.   The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. NEC features 150 refurbished guestrooms and refreshed event spaces that aims to offer a premier venue for high-level conferences, workshops, executive programmes, and industry engagements.    We are seeking a proactive Sales Executive to drive business growth for NEC. Reporting to the General Manager, you will be responsible for selling NEC accommodation, event and function spaces while delivering exceptional customer service. You will identify target audiences, cultivate client relationships, and maximise revenue through strategic sales initiatives.   KEY RESPONSIBILITES Business Development   Promote NEC's accommodation and event spaces to NTU audience, suitable clients, and individual guests. Implement upselling and cross-selling strategies to maximise revenue per booking. Identify and pursue new business opportunities through lead generation, networking, and market research. Build good rapport with existing and prospective clients to develop business leads and secure repeat business. Monitor market trends, industry development and activities to maintain competitive positioning. Achieve individual KPI and revenue targets as set out in the yearly business plan. Upsell hotel services (e.g., AV equipment, catering, upgraded rooms). Review the sales strategy with the Sales Manager and General Manager to ensure NEC remains on track in establishing the short‑ and long‑term goals set by NEC Management. This will be done through weekly or bi‑weekly sales meetings and account review processes. Client Relations & Administration   Maintain comprehensive records of all client interactions, proposals, and follow-ups. Provide regular sales progress reports and booking updates to management. Propose ways to improve sales processes, standards and policy. Conduct site inspections and familiarization tours for prospective clients. Negotiate rates, terms, and contracts with clients to achieve mutually beneficial agreements. Ensure all billing information, special requests, and guest preferences are captured at the point of booking. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of room inventory, rates, packages, promotions, and special offers.   Internal Collaboration Communicate group details effectively to the Operations, Front Office, and Banquet teams. Coordinate with the Revenue Manager to ensure pricing strategies align with demand. Work with the Marketing team to promote special offers and packages.   Requirements:   Diploma in Sales & Marketing, Hotel Management or relevant discipline. Minimum of 1 year working experience in hospitality industry. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Proven ability to build rapport, foster and maintain long-term relationships with clients. Skilled in negotiating prices and terms to reach a mutually beneficial agreement with potential clients. Professional in demeanour and service-oriented with a commitment to exceeding client expectations. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Humanoid-Locomotion-_R00025922-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Humanoid Locomotion)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking to hire a research fellow to lead advancements in humanoid robots and embodied AI. This role will contribute to NTU’s mission of driving transformative research in artificial intelligence and robotics by developing Vision-Language-Action models that enable seamless human-robot interaction and autonomous task execution. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in enhancing NTU’s global reputation for excellence in robotics and AI. Key Responsibilities Design and implement VLA models and world models. Develop and optimize deep learning algorithms to enable robotic arms to perform complex tasks guided by natural language instructions. Utilize PyTorch to train and fine-tune models on multimodal datasets. Experiment with and deploy vision-language-action models on robotic platforms. Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to advance the field of embodied intelligence. Publish high-quality research in top-tier conferences and journals. Job Requirements Ph.D. in Computer Science, Robotics, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated research experience in AI, robotics, machine learning, computer vision, or related fields. Strong knowledge of deep learning, multimodal AI models, Vision-Language-Action models, or related technologies. Proficiency in Python programming and experience with deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch. Experience working with robotic systems, automation platforms, or robotic manipulation technologies is advantageous. Familiarity with reinforcement learning, human-robot interaction, or embodied AI is an advantage. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager-Senior-Executive--Shared-Services-HR-Faculty_R00025925": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager/Senior Executive, Shared Services HR Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThis position provides end-to-end HR operational and administrative support to assigned Schools for the University’s faculty population, with a focus on Reappointment, Re-employment, and Promotion & Tenure (PT) as part of the NSS HR Faculty Performance Team. It ensures that faculty-related processes are delivered accurately, efficiently, and in accordance with established Service Level Agreements (SLAs) and University requirements. Key responsibilities include coordinating faculty-related matters with Schools, Faculty Affairs Office, HR Business Partners, and other stakeholders; preparing and verifying documentation; maintaining accurate HR records and systems data; and providing secretarial and administrative support throughout the faculty lifecycle.   The incumbent is also responsible for establishing and maintaining the annual Reappointment database and coordinating the reappointment cycle, including proactive engagement with Schools, monitoring case progress, and issuing timely reminders and follow-ups to ensure cases are appropriately tabled and submitted to the FAR Secretariat within prescribed timelines.   In addition, the incumbent supports University-level meetings by coordinating schedules, managing logistics, preparing meeting materials, taking minutes, and working closely with team members to ensure effective execution.   Key Responsibilities Manage advance planning, preparation and maintenance of the annual Faculty Reappointment and Re‑employment database across all appointment schemes, ensuring alignment with University governance timelines. Coordinate with Colleges and Schools to disseminate cases, track reviews, and ensure timely tabling and submission for university-level meetings, including follow‑ups and reminders to prevent delays. Proactively monitor contract expiry and renewal timelines to enhance stakeholder readiness, minimise last‑minute escalations, and support smooth monthly university-level meeting planning. Provide HR operational and secretariat support to School‑level committees involved in faculty appointment, reappointments, promotion and tenure deliberations. Support university‑level meetings by preparing logistics, taking minutes, and working jointly with team members to ensure smooth coordination. Contribute to HR‑related projects, process improvement initiatives, and workflow enhancements. Requirements Diploma or Degree in Business Administration, or a related discipline ie. Human Resources Good knowledge of the Employment Act and Labour laws of Singapore Comfortable to handle/review a high volume of administrative transactions Strong written and verbal communication skills Good interpersonal and organisational abilities. Meticulous, with a strong service‑oriented mindset. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications and PowerPDF Working knowledge of Workday is advantageous We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-English--SOH-_R00025920-1": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in English (SOH)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking an experienced lecturer capable of teaching Contemporary Literature and Culture as one of our graduate class offerings in English programme within the School of Humanities. Candidates should have a proven track-record in graduate teaching.   Instructor will be responsible for leading workshops and seminars for three class hours per week in addition to syllabus planning, class preparation, marking for assessment and student consultation.   Requirements: PhD degree   Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Adjunct-Associate-Professor_R00025919-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Adjunct Associate Professor will be responsible for teaching in the suite of graduate programmes under the Graduate Studies Office. Primarily, he will be responsible for teaching in the Master in Healthcare Management (MHEAL) programme on Health Service Management. The role contributes directly to NTU's lifelong learning strategy, healthcare workforce development agenda and postgraduate education growth. The key responsibility is to teach in the MHEAL programme. Course: Global Health Service Management. Be a guest speaker for workshops and seminars. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Faculty-Ops-and-Support_R00025941": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Faculty Ops and Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) is seeking an experienced and highly motivated Senior Executive to join our team. The School is committed to developing programmes that offer cutting-edge lifelong learning solutions and globally recognized qualifications accessible by aspiring professionals and lifelong learners.     The Senior Executive will support the Assistant Manager, Faculty Ops and Support in coordinating and administering day-to-day faculty operational and administrative matters, ensuring the Faculty Affairs Office delivers accurate, timely, and efficient services in these areas: faculty secretarial support, recruitment, appointment, reappointment, performance appraisal, promotion and tenure as well as faculty development and culture.   Key Responsibilities:   Executive & Secretarial Support   Provide administrative support to Associate Chair (Faculty) including procurement, claims, travel arrangements, and document submissions. Provide secretariat support for committees and meetings, including booking of meeting rooms, agenda preparation, minute-taking, and follow-up actions. Maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive documentation with accuracy and discretion. Support digitalisation initiatives led by the Assistant Manager, and suggest improvements to workflows. Maintain up-to-date records and assist in the preparation of reports, presentations, and internal communication materials. Liaise with internal departments (e.g., Finance, HR, Research Office) and external vendors to follow up on administrative, compliance and process-related matters, and escalate complex issues to the Assistant Manager. Perform any other duties as assigned to support the team’s and school’s objectives.   Faculty Recruitment, Appointment, Reappointment and Promotion Administration Support   Gather and compile information on potential international candidates. Liaise with School’s HR and Shared Services team to follow up on Faculty appointment, re-appointment, promotion and tenure and related processes and support smooth execution of administrative process. Provide end to end support on faculty recruitment such as (but not limited to) interview / meeting scheduling, travel arrangement, campus visit and claims. Prepare and compile faculty dossier in appointment, re-appointment, promotion for Committee’s review and check that documents are complete before submission. Support annual faculty appraisal exercise to ensure adherence to timelines and processes. Maintain up-to-date records and assist in the preparation of reports, presentations, and internal communication materials. Perform any other faculty-related duties as assigned to support the team’s and school’s objectives. Assist in preparing faculty recruitment-related publicity materials.   Requirements: Bachelor’s degree preferably in a Business Administration, Education, Human Resource or any related field. At least 2 years of administrative experience, preferably in higher education or a research-intensive setting. Candidates with less experience but strong organisational skills are welcome to apply. Experience supporting senior staff or committees is an advantage. Calm under pressure and able to juggle competing priorities. Proficient with standard MS office software (MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint). Possess strong written and communication skills. Ability to work independently on routine matters and as part of a team. Able to source for information and liaise with various stakeholders to get work done.   The School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Artificial-Intelligence-_R00025938-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nHyundai-NTU-A*STAR Corp Lab serves to drive research development and industry adoption of AI, Robotics, 3D Printing technologies, and Digital Twins through collaborative projects with HMGICS, and with schools and research centres within and beyond the University. To support the research for the project titled: LLM Based Smart Assistant System.   The project aims to research and develop technologies in the following technically challenging areas to deliver an LLM-based smart assistant system for automative equipment maintenance. The base application should handle multi-query strategy and fusion of Information sources (original equipment manual, internet forums, databases, knowledge graphs). The Search module must enable direct searches and fusion of information across various data sources and knowledge graphs, using LLM-generated for merge / prioritise information from different streams.   We are looking for a Research Fellow to lead the research on the LLM-based smart assistant system for automative equipment maintenance. The role will focus on lead the team of researchers to propose novel ideas and develop the novel solutions to the challenging problems.   Key Responsibilities: Lead the research on an LLM-based smart assistant system for automotive equipment maintenance, Lead a team of researchers to propose novel ideas and develop innovative solutions to challenging technical problems. Conduct literature reviews on AI and machine learning for decision-making and recommendation. Design new AI solutions and search modules that enable direct search and information fusion across various data sources. Evaluate and compare the proposed systems against existing models to measure their effectiveness in merging and prioritizing information. Write research papers to report findings and results.   Job Requirements: Preferably PhD in computer science or related field. Expertise in computer programming Knowledge in machine learning and data science     Proven research ability as evidenced through a portfolio of publications and/or conference papers and/or patents. Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player In-depth knowledge relevant to the project domain. Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research. The ability and willingness to adapt and incorporate novel ideas and approaches in scientific industry. Demonstrated ability to formulate hypothesis and design effective experimental plans. Ability to design and implement new experimental methods. Ability to initiate collaboration research in multidisciplinary team. Oversee and report project progress. Ability and willingness to work some flexible hours. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Research-Administration-and-Support-Services--LKCMedicine-_R00025935": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research Administration and Support Services [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are looking for a detail-oriented individual to join the Department of Research Administration and Support Services (RASS) at LKCMedicine. The role manages research grants across the full grant lifecycle and administers Research Scholarships funded by external grants, working with faculty members, University offices, external stakeholders and funders.   Responsibilities:   Manage assigned grant matters across the full grant lifecycle, from grant calls and proposal submissions to award set-up, variations and reporting, in line with funder and University requirements. Manage and track externally grant-funded Research Scholarships, including student numbers, scholarship periods, funding availability, cost commitments and supporting documentation. Coordinate with the Graduate Office, Grants Team and relevant stakeholders on scholarship funding arrangements, timelines, documentation, changes and follow-up matters. Review grant budgets, expenditure, manpower details and supporting documentation to support compliance and audit readiness. Advise faculty members and research teams on grant guidelines, institutional processes and documentation requirements, and coordinate with relevant stakeholders on follow-up matters. Maintain accurate grant and scholarship records, trackers and supporting documentation for monitoring, reporting and audit readiness. Contribute to broader grant and research scholarship operations, team priorities and process improvement, including cross-coverage where required.   Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Science or a related discipline. Relevant experience in administration, research, grants or finance would be advantageous. Strong organisational and analytical skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines, track deliverables and follow through on outstanding matters. Good communication skills and comfortable working with different stakeholders. Adaptable and willing to learn Proficient in using digital tools for tracking, documentation and collaboration; familiarity with grant management systems would be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Librarian--Academic-Engagement_R00025942": {
      "title": "Senior Librarian, Academic Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a leading research-intensive university known for its strong focus on innovation, interdisciplinary learning, and creating meaningful impact through education and research. The Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) plays an important role in supporting students across their academic journey, from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. Working closely with schools, colleges, and other partners across the University, SASD helps to create a seamless, enriching, and student-centred experience at NTU. Within this broader mission, NTU Library , under the Office of Information, Knowledge and Library Services (OIKLS) , provides essential learning, research, and collaborative environments that support the University community. We are looking for a Senior Librarian, Academic Engagement to strengthen academic engagement, research support, and curriculum services by building strong partnerships with faculty, researchers, postgraduate students, and academic departments. The successful candidate will deliver high-value reference, literature, and research support services; promote the effective use of social media metrics and outreach analytics; apply emerging technologies such as Generative AI to improve service delivery; and oversee course reserves and curriculum support services to ensure timely, compliant access to course readings. Key Responsibilities Lead NTU Course Reserves and curriculum support services, including faculty engagement, reading-list workflows, service standards, copyright compliance and platform enhancements. Lead and enhance Social Media Impact Metrics services, overseeing platforms, researcher profiles and engagement data, and advising faculty and research staff on their interpretation and use. Plan and administer reference, literature and research support services, including access to specialised databases, datasets, statistics and market intelligence resources. Evaluate and implement Generative AI solutions and digital workflows to strengthen team capabilities and improve reference and research support services. Build sustained partnerships with faculty, researchers, Schools and Colleges through targeted engagement, consultation, training and scholarly outreach initiatives. Assess teaching, research and resource needs to recommend relevant library services, programmes and acquisitions aligned with curriculum and research priorities. Deliver systematic search and review consultations, training and outreach, applying agreed quality standards to search strategies and service outputs. Requirements Degree in any discipline; MSc in Information Studies, MLIS, or equivalent qualification is preferred. At least 7 years of professional working experience in academic, research, or special libraries. Good subject knowledge across disciplines and familiarity with research resources, external data services, research databases, and literature review methodologies. Knowledge of social media impact metrics, data analytics, AI literacy, digital fluency, and copyright requirements in library or educational settings. Strong communication, interpersonal, collaboration, time management, and project management skills. Service-oriented, curious, adaptable, and able to work independently and collaboratively in a changing environment. Why Join Us This role offers the opportunity to contribute to a dynamic academic library environment, work closely with faculty and researchers, and shape services that support teaching, learning, research, and scholarly impact across the University. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-II--Trust-Technologies-_R00025936": {
      "title": "Research Engineer II (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for its people and businesses by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize. We are looking for a hands-on Research Engineer to build and implement the AI components of Project. The role is execution-focused and covers end-to-end development of local large language model (LLM) systems, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), model fine-tuning and adaptation, NLP analytics, data pipelines, backend integration, evaluation, and trustworthy AI controls. The engineer will translate defined project requirements into working prototypes and deployable technical components, with emphasis on reliable operation in controlled or on-premise environments. Key Responsibilities: The National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) at NTU is seeking a hands-on Research Engineer to build AI components for Projectx. The role focuses on implementation of local LLM systems, RAG, model fine-tuning, NLP analytics, trustworthy AI controls, and deployment tooling. Build end-to-end local LLM/RAG pipelines for conversational analysis of large unstructured datasets. Fine-tune and adapt LLM/NLP models using techniques such as supervised fine-tuning and LoRA/PEFT, and benchmark them against RAG/prompting baselines. Implement NLP capabilities such as entity extraction, entity resolution, relationship analysis, and other project-specific analytics. Develop backend APIs, database/vector-store integration, local model serving, GPU inference and containerized deployment. Implement access control, audit logging, traceable retrieval/output provenance, model isolation, and human-review workflows. Conduct systematic evaluation, security/robustness testing, error analysis, performance optimization, and regression testing. Maintain reproducible code, model/configuration versions, experiment records, technical documentation, and deployment instructions. Communicate results clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences. Report drafting   Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in computer science, AI, engineering, data science, software engineering, or a related field with 4 years of relevant working experience. Strong Python skills with hands-on experience in LLM/NLP development. Practical experience with RAG and model fine-tuning/PEFT; PyTorch and/or Hugging Face experience preferred. Working knowledge of Linux, Git, Docker, SQL, APIs, and modern data/model-serving workflows. Experience with local GPU deployment, vector databases, NLP analytics, or trustworthy AI/security controls is an advantage. Independent, execution-oriented, methodical, and able to deliver working technical components under tight timelines. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Econometrics-and-Machine-Learning-_R00025939": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Econometrics and Machine Learning)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Economics Programme in NTU’s School of Social Sciences seeks a Research Fellow. The research develops reliable instrumental variable (IV) estimation/inference method and machine learning algorithm with weak instruments, high-dimensional instruments or controls, and clustered data.   Key Responsibilities: Develop econometric theory for weak-identification-robust tests, bootstrap methods, estimator combinations, and leave-cluster-out bias correction and inference methods. Implement simulations and empirical analyses of import competition, education, and pretrial decisions using IV regressions. Prepare reproducible code, research papers, technical appendices, and presentations in collaboration with the project team.   Job Requirements: PhD in Economics, Econometrics, Statistics, or a closely related field by the appointment start date. Strong econometric theory, probability, statistics, and research skills in IV methods, causal inference, and machine learning. Proficiency in R, Python, MATLAB, or Julia; ability to implement simulations and analyse data. Strong communication and collaboration skills; specialist experience in weak identification, bootstrap methods, or cluster-robust inference is desirable. Entry level PhD candidates who meet the qualification requirement by the start date are welcome; prior postdoctoral experience is desirable.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--AI-Evaluation--Trust-Technologies-_R00025937": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (AI Evaluation, Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for its people and businesses by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize. We are looking for a Research Engineer to support the evaluation and validation of AI systems developed at the Centre. The role focuses on assessing how reliably these systems perform in real-world conditions — designing evaluation methods, building test datasets, analysing where and why models succeed or fail, and contributing to the development of prototypes and tooling. This work underpins the Centre's mission of ensuring that emerging technologies are trustworthy, fair, and safe in practice. Key Responsibilities: The National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) at NTU is seeking a Research Engineer to support the evaluation and validation of AI systems. This role combines hands-on technical work with regular engagement with external partners. You will: Work directly with project partners and clients — participating in requirement discussions and technical meetings, preparing materials, and following up on action items. Design evaluation frameworks, test datasets, and scoring methodology for AI and ML systems. Develop annotation guidelines and monitor labelling quality. Conduct error analysis and translate findings into clear recommendations for improvement. Run structured experiments with large language models, and build supporting prototypes and tooling. Communicate results clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in computer science, engineering, data science, or a related field. Confidence to engage directly with external partners and clients, and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to non-technical audiences. Proficiency in Python, with practical experience in ML workflows including model evaluation and error analysis. Working knowledge of NLP and hands-on experience with large language models. Experience in evaluation methodology or data annotation will be a strong advantage. Careful, methodical, and able to work independently under tight timelines. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Micro-Electromechanical-Systems--MEMS--Development-_R00025940": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Micro-Electromechanical Systems (MEMS) Development)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research.   We are looking for a Research Associate to conduct interdisciplinary research at the interface of microfabrication, functional soft materials, and bioactive delivery systems. The role will focus on developing micro/nanostructured material platforms for controlled release, biological screening, microbial culture, and food or biomedical applications.   Key Responsibilities: Conduct independent and collaborative research aligned with the objectives of the project and laboratory. Design and perform experiments, analyze data, and interpret research findings. Prepare manuscripts, reports, presentations, and other research outputs. Contribute to grant proposal preparation and project documentation. Collaborate with researchers, students, and external partners. Mentor and support junior researchers and students. Maintain accurate research records and ensure compliance with laboratory, safety, and institutional requirements. Ensure compliance with relevant safety, ethical, regulatory, and institutional guidelines.   Job Requirements: Education qualifications: The candidate should have a Masters degree in a relevant discipline. Soft skills: The candidate should have strong communication skills, organizational, and problem-solving skills, and be able to work independently as well as collaboratively in a research team. Hard skills: The candidate should be able to conduct research, analyze data, interpret results, and prepare research outputs such as reports, presentations, and manuscripts. Experience: The candidate should have relevant research experience through doctoral training or equivalent research activities. Experience in manuscript preparation, research presentation, or collaborative research would be an advantage. Competencies: The candidate should be self-motivated, responsible, and capable of contributing to research projects, publications, project deliverables, and compliance with institutional and research guidelines. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Communication--Psychology--Sociology--Social-Science-_R00025933": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Communication/ Psychology/ Sociology/ Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI), together with the Earth Observatory of Singapore, is looking for a Research Fellow to make an important contribution to the research project: “Climate Transformation Program (CTP): Cross Cutting Theme 1 – Sustainable Societies” funded by the MOE Tier 3C Grant. CTP aims to develop, inspire, and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just, and sustainable Southeast Asian societies. CTP will generate knowledge and innovation across disciplines including climate and Earth science, ecology, materials science, artificial intelligence, humanities, social sciences and the arts, finance, health, and engineering. It will also translate state-of-the-art scientific results into real world solutions for Singapore, and it will transfer these solutions to Southeast Asia (SEA) and beyond. As part of this programme, “Cross-cutting theme 1: Sustainable Societies”, this theme will leverage climate research in communication, public opinion and psychology, and artistic impressions to shape public attitudes and behaviours towards climate change issues. The Research Fellow will work directly with the PI of the Sustainable Societies theme, Professor Shirley Ho, based in the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information at NTU.     Key Responsibilities: Conducting literature reviews and supporting theory development Designing immersive VR experiences for research purposes Engage with external vendors to develop VR experiences Designing and conducting experimental studies Performing statistical analyses of experimental data (e.g., SPSS, R, or Mplus) Contributing to peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations Preparing progress reports and final research outputs Supporting dissemination of research findings to academic and public audiences Assisting with project coordination and administrative tasks   Job Requirements: A PhD degree in communication, psychology, sociology, or a related social science discipline. Strong foundation in experimental research Demonstrated or hands-on experience in VR development or immersive media research Proficiency in statistical tools (e.g., SPSS, R, or Mplus) A strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals and conferences Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary, multicultural team Strong initiative, communication skills, and research ownership Experience collaborating with external vendors to translate research designs into functional systems   Why Join Us: Contribute to an interdisciplinary research programme addressing climate change and sustainable societies in Southeast Asia. Collaborate with researchers from diverse disciplines across NTU and partner institutions. Conduct research with the potential to inform public understanding and societal responses to climate change. Develop a strong research profile through publications, conference presentations, and collaborative projects.   Interested applicants are invited to submit a cover letter, full CV and names and contact details of three referees in one document. Enquiries about this position can be made to TSYHo@ntu.edu.sg .   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Tropical-Ecosystem-Monitoring-and-Simulations-_R00025934": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Tropical Ecosystem Monitoring and Simulations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nASE is a diverse school focusing on the connections between geosciences, ecology, society and Earth systems. Our approach integrates these disciplines to examine big environmental challenges both in Southeast Asia and globally. We conduct cutting-edge research on topics that include ecology, geohazards, climate change, sea-level rise, environmental sustainability, conservation of environment and biodiversity, and interactions between environment and society. For more information on ASE please visit https://www.ntu.edu.sg/ase .   The Yanyan Cheng research group is seeking a Research Fellow. This position is part of a Singapore NRF funded research project hosted by ASE. The Research Fellow will help advance research in Earth system modeling and understand interactions among land, water, carbon, energy, atmosphere, ecosystems, and human systems .   This is a one-year appointment and potentially renewable based on performance and funding availability.   Key Responsibilities:   Collect, validate, and harmonize field and remote sensing imagery for ecosystem monitoring. Develop machine/deep learning-based workflows to interpret ecosystem disturbance. Synthesize model simulations and multi-source observations to diagnose how the atmosphere responds to changes in land surface properties and the associated land–atmosphere feedback. properties and the associated land–atmosphere feedback. Participate in mentoring RAs and students at ASE.   Job Requirements:   A PhD in physical geography, remote sensing, and ecology. Preferably with several years of relevant experience in ecosystem monitoring, and the design of manipulation experiments, development of diagnosis frameworks (e.g., knowledge-guided machine learning, casual inference, and Bayesian neural networks), evaluation of simulation results (e.g., climate extremes and precipitation patterns, land-atmospheric interactions), analysis of the mechanisms behind model improvements and climate projections. Should be familiar with remote sensing data processing from multiple platforms (satellite, airborne, and ground) and sensors (optical, radar, and lidar). Should be familiar with tropical climate and environmental studies. Should have advanced programming skills in Python, as well as proficiency in other programming languages such as R, NCL, and MATLAB. Should have proficiency in scientific computing, high-performance computing (HPC), and scripting (e.g., Bash, CDO/NCO). Should have strong quantitative and analytical skills in working with climate model datasets and observational datasets. As the position requires stakeholder engagement in English, candidate should have good written and oral communication skills in English. Candidate should have published scientific papers in high-quality research journals. Should be enthusiastic in research, and have good spirit in teamwork and collaboration.   ASE seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Pre-Doctoral-Research-Assistant---Research-Associate_R00025931": {
      "title": "Pre-Doctoral Research Assistant / Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Nanyang Business School is seeking a Pre-Doctoral Researcher to support faculty-led research projects across various business and management disciplines. This position provides a unique opportunity for individuals considering future doctoral studies to gain hands-on experience in academic research.   Key responsibilities: Support faculty members in the execution of ongoing research projects. Conduct literature reviews and synthesise academic findings from relevant research publications. Collect, clean, validate, and manage research datasets from various sources. Perform quantitative and/or qualitative data analyses using appropriate research tools and methodologies. Assist in the development of research reports, working papers, journal manuscripts, conference presentations, and grant proposals. Support survey development, experimental studies, field research, and data collection activities where applicable. Prepare research documentation, data dictionaries, research protocols, and project records. Assist with ethics review applications and regulatory compliance requirements where necessary. Participate in research seminars, workshops, and scholarly activities organised by the School. Collaborate with faculty, doctoral students, and research teams on assigned projects. Perform other research-related duties as assigned.   Requirements Bachelor's or Master's degree in any discipline; candidates from diverse academic backgrounds are encouraged to apply. Strong interest in academic research and research-oriented careers. Strong quantitative and analytical skills; proficiency in R, Python, Stata, SQL, or equivalent is preferred. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organisational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a research-intensive environment. Self-motivated, intellectually curious, and committed to continuous learning. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Administrative-Support_R00025932": {
      "title": "Manager, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNTU-WeBank Joint Research Centre on FinTech (WeBank) is Singapore’s 1st Joint Research Centre in Fintech. By employing “state-of-the-art” research, such as data science and analytics, Internet of Things (IoT) and blockchain technologies, the centre aims to enable and realise Banking 4.0, where banking can be personalised and done anytime, anywhere.     Key Responsibilities: Manage the Centre/Lab’s day-to-day administrative and operational functions, ensuring effective, efficient and compliant service delivery. Develop, review and implement administrative policies, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), workflows and tracking mechanisms to strengthen governance and operational efficiency. Manage financial administration, including travel requests, expense claims, event-related expenditure and other financial transactions, ensuring appropriate funding, approvals, documentation and compliance with NTU policies. Manage the procurement and vendor management activities, including procurement planning, purchase processes, vendor registration, delivery coordination, invoice processing and resolution of procurement-related issues. Plan and oversee event arrangements for meetings, workshops, seminars, visits and other activities, including venue, catering, logistics, registration, audio-visual and on-site arrangements. Oversee staff onboarding and offboarding, access administration, seating and space allocation, staff records and other related administrative matters in coordination with HR and relevant University units. Manage fixed and inventory asset management, including asset records, tagging, loan documentation, asset verification and return of assets during staff offboarding. Oversee the Work Study Scheme and other research/student administrative processes, providing guidance to PIs, supervisors, researchers and students and ensuring timely and accurate processing. Act as a key liaison between Centre/Lab’s leadership, researchers, PIs, Finance, Admin, Procurement, IT/access teams, vendors and other University stakeholders to resolve operational matters and facilitate effective collaboration. Monitor workload, priorities, service standards and operational risks across the administrative function, escalating significant issues and recommending appropriate solutions to management. Identify opportunities to streamline administrative processes, improve service delivery and strengthen governance through better workflows, documentation, systems and practices. Provide guidance and support to the administrative team, where applicable, and promote a collaborative, accountable and service-oriented working environment.   Job Requirements: A good degree in any discipline from a recognized university with at least 5 years of relevant experience in administration, operations, research administration or a similar role, preferably within a university. Excellent communication, interpersonal and stakeholder-management skills. Strong analytical, problem-solving and decision-making abilities, particularly when dealing with complex or non-standard situations. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures and guidelines and translate them into practical operational solutions. Strong attention to detail, accuracy and follow-through. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgement within delegated authority and escalate issues appropriately. Demonstrated ability to improve processes and introduce practical solutions to enhance operational efficiency and service quality. Service-oriented and collaborative, with the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at different levels. Committed to integrity, compliance and high standards of professional conduct.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Chinese-Executive-Education-Partnerships_R00026000": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Chinese Executive Education Partnerships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nNanyang Business School (NBS), Nanyang Technological University (NTU), is seeking a Senior Assistant Director (Business Development – Joint Executive Education) to support the growth of its executive education portfolio through collaborative programmes with partner universities. Based within the ASEAN & China Programmes Office, this role focuses on co‑developing and delivering joint executive education programmes with selected partner institutions, primarily in China and selected international markets. The role complements existing open‑enrolment executive education activities by strengthening NBS’ institution‑to‑institution partnerships. Key responsibilities include, but not limited to the following: Joint Executive Education Programme Development (Partner Universities) Drive the origination, assessment, and development of joint executive education programme opportunities with partner universities, primarily in China. Lead collaboration with academic directors and faculty from NTU and partner institutions to define joint programme themes, target audiences, and delivery formats that align academic excellence with market demand. Lead engagement with partner universities on programme structuring, positioning, branding, and delivery arrangements to ensure alignment of academic, commercial, and institutional objectives.   Partner University Relationship Management Serve as the primary working‑level contact for designated partner universities on joint EE initiatives. Maintain regular engagement to ensure alignment on programme objectives, timelines, and expectations. Facilitate resolution of operational or coordination issues during programme development and delivery. Commercial Structuring and Financial Viability of Joint Programmes Lead the commercial structuring of joint executive education programmes, including pricing strategy, cost-sharing models, and revenue frameworks, in alignment with ACP leadership and institutional objectives. Drive financial viability assessments for joint programmes, working with finance and operations teams to ensure sustainable and scalable programme delivery models that meet revenue targets. Oversee financial and participation performance of joint programmes, identifying optimisation opportunities and recommending strategic adjustments to improve commercial outcomes.  Programme Design Input and Market Relevance Shape the design and positioning of joint executive education programmes by translating market intelligence, client needs, and industry trends into strategic curriculum direction. Lead engagement with academic directors to ensure joint executive education programmes reflect emerging global themes, including internationalisation, leadership development, and geopolitical dynamics. Drive continuous curriculum refinement by synthesising participant and partner feedback into actionable programme enhancements that strengthen market relevance and differentiation. Internal Collaboration and Team Contribution Lead cross-functional coordination across academic directors, marketing, finance, operations, and programme teams to ensure effective development and delivery of joint executive education programmes. Provide strategic pipeline analysis and partner intelligence to ACP leadership to inform portfolio planning, prioritisation, and growth strategy. Lead capability development by codifying and disseminating best practices in partnership-based executive education programme development across teams.  Key competencies and qualification requirements:  Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Minimum 10 years of relevant professional experience in business development, executive education, programme development, partnerships, stakeholder engagement, or professional services roles. Strong understanding of executive education and senior leadership development, with the ability to translate market and client needs into programme and partnership strategies. Proven experience in university-to-university partnerships, including the development and management of joint or co-branded executive education programmes. Strong knowledge of China’s business environment and cross-border executive contexts, with demonstrated ability to apply this understanding to partnership development and programme positioning. Strong commercial acumen, including experience in pricing strategy, cost structure evaluation, and assessment of financial viability for executive education programmes. Demonstrated track record in developing and managing strategic partnerships, engaging senior external stakeholders, and coordinating complex multi-party initiatives. Strong analytical, organisational, and programme management capability, with experience managing multiple concurrent strategic initiatives in complex environments. Excellent stakeholder management, influencing, and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with senior executives and institutional partners. Bilingual proficiency in English and Chinese (spoken and written) due to need to liaise frequently with international partners and handle Chinese business documents Proficient in business productivity and collaboration tools (e.g. Word, Excel, presentation software, email, and digital collaboration platforms), applied in a complex stakeholder environment. Demonstrates strong professional maturity, adaptability, and sound judgement, with the ability to operate independently across diverse institutional and cultural contexts. Willingness to undertake domestic and international travel as required. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Science-of-Learning-in-Education-Centre---NIE-_R00025997-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Science of Learning in Education Centre) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Research Assistant on a 6-month contract (renewable) at the Science of Learning in Education Centre (SoLEC) .   Project Title: Cerebrovascular Health, Adult Learning, Resilience and Mechanisms: CHARM Study   Project Introduction: As part of CHARM study, we will develop learning pedagogy for middle aged adults based on the principles of neuropsychological pedagogy and life-style interventions. Two learning packages will be designed with each package comprising a pre-course, course, and post-course components. The course components will include lectures, group-activities, and homework. The content will be developed by our team, in close collaboration with adult learners, through interviews and focus group sessions comprising learners of various age groups and occupational-types.   Requirements Academic qualification: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Education Technology, or a related field   Work experience: Prior experience serving as a platform administrator (Moodle, WordPress LMS, etc.), including managing user accounts, roles, permissions, and system configuration. Prior experience of integrating LMS with xAPI and LRS is preferred. Prior experience supporting online learning or digital learning environments Prior experience working in educational, research, or training contexts Prior experience with basic data handling, analytics, or reporting Prior experience supporting research or educational projects   Desirable interests, skills, and attributes: Strong interest in educational technology and digital learning innovation Interest in improving learning experiences in higher education settings Good technical problem-solving skills Strong communication and organisational skills Good interpersonal skills and service-oriented mindset Ability to work independently, proactively, and collaboratively within a research team   Responsibilities Set up, configure, and maintain e-learning platforms (e.g., Moodle, WordPress LMS, or similar systems) Take ownership of LMS platform (e.g., installation, plugin setup, course structure), in addition to ongoing maintenance. Support the design, implementation, and maintenance of online learning environments for the program Troubleshoot technical issues and provide timely support to users and project members Support integration of learning tools, plugins, and third-party applications as needed Monitor system performance and ensure platform stability, security, and updates Support the delivery of online learning activities and related program operations Assist in organising and managing digital learning content and resources Contribute to data extraction, usage tracking, and reporting when required Track platform usage and generate reports/analytics Support research and program-related activities as assigned by the Principal Investigators Perform other tasks as required by the project team   Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Environmental-Sciences-_R00025991": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Environmental Sciences)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Asian School of the Environment (ASE) at Nanyang Technological University is an interdisciplinary school that aims to be a world leader in environmental research focused on Asian environmental challenges. The ASE integrates earth and environmental life science, ecology, engineering and technology, human ecology, humanities, and the social sciences to address key issues of the environment and sustainability. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/ase . The Wetland Carbon Lab at NTU’s Asian School of the Environment (ASE) focuses on understanding the role of wetlands and aquatic ecosystems, including mangroves peatlands, and streams, as natural climate solutions. The lab integrates field-based experiments, high-frequency sensor networks, stable isotope approaches, and modelling to study water, carbon, nitrogen, and energy fluxes and greenhouse gas emissions across ecosystems and watersheds.   We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to lead eddy covariance data analysis for our greenhouse gas flux research in Southeast Asian wetlands. The position supports NTU’s mission to advance solution-oriented environmental research and contributes to climate change mitigation and adaptation strategies.   Key Responsibilities: Responsible for regular quality assurance and quality control (QA/QC) of eddy covariance and supporting meteorological data, and for producing monthly data reports. Improve, standardize, and automate EC pre- and post-processing workflows (e.g. flux calculation, filtering, gap-filling, flux partitioning, uncertainty estimation), ensuring rigorous documentation and reproducibility. Prepare and contribute to peer-reviewed publications, research proposals, technical reports, and internal technical notes, and present findings at scientific meetings. Contribute to the development of a Southeast Asian flux tower network, including data harmonization and partner engagement.   Job Requirements: PhD in Environmental Science, Atmospheric Science, Micrometeorology, Biogeochemistry, Ecology, or a closely related field Strong experience in eddy covariance measurements of greenhouse gas (CO2, CH4) and energy fluxes. In-depth knowledge of eddy covariance theory and instrumentation, and of standard processing software. Analytical and modelling skills with R or Python; experience building automated, reproducible data pipelines. Excellent scientific communication and interpersonal skills Proactive, independent, and team-oriented ASE seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit based on merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--IT-Applications-Support_R00025992": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, IT Applications Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated Senior Assistant Director, IT Applications Support to oversee the support of Finance related applications and integration. The ideal candidate will ensure the stability, reliability, and performance of these applications.   In this role, you will collaborate with diverse stakeholders, including business users from Finance Department, as well as in-house teams and external vendors. Your work will contribute to delivering high-quality IT systems and services that meet the University’s strategic objectives.   Responsibilities   Oversee the entire incident management process, ensuring incidents are resolved within established SLA, acting as a key escalation point for critical issues. Conduct root cause analysis to resolve and prevent recurring application problems. Lead a support team, managing their schedules and performance. Communicate effectively with business users, management, and other technical teams on system status, issues, risks. Manage third-party vendors for support, oversee change requests, and ensure service quality and contract compliance. Lead AMS support and end-to-end project execution for SAP, SAP Ariba and finance application, covering service management, requirements, solution design, integration, testing, deployment, post-go-live stabilization, and transition to operations. Explore latest technologies to improve support processes; and contribute to strategic planning. Lead Finance applications, with particular focus on AI solution design, secure system and data integration, and end-to-end solutions that connect processes across both functions. Manage audit queries / requests and ensure supported systems adhere to audit and compliance requirements.   Requirements   Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering or related discipline. At least 12 years of IT experience which consists of: 10 years of applications support with at least 5 years in a lead or supervisory role 5 years of internal/external audit support 3 years of project management experience Strong foundation of IT – this includes project management methodologies, system design, web application development, and IT security/audit controls. Experience working in an ITIL-based framework (Incident, Problem, Change Management) and systems such as ServiceNow, Jira. Proficient in web technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, APIs, RESTful services), middleware, API integrations, and low-code development platforms (e.g. OutSystems). Proficient in troubleshooting complex technical & integration issues; and supporting enterprise-level SaaS based applications. Demonstrated experience leading Finance application solutions, including AI design, integration architecture, and end-to-end delivery across functional boundaries. Knowledge of enterprise platforms such as SAP, CPI, BTP, SAP Ariba, Bank interfaces, Payment Gateway. Experience with Workday and payroll systems would be an advantage. Effective communicator with diverse stakeholders, vendors, and colleagues, capable of explaining technical concepts in non-technical terms. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, customer-centric mindset with a focus on providing high-quality service. Strong interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively under pressure and manage multiple priorities. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Physical-Education---Sports-Science-Department---NIE-_R00024836": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Physical Education & Sports Science Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Research Fellow on a 32-month contract at the Physical Education and Sport Science (PESS) Department . Project Title: Research Centre for Sport, Physical Activity, and Health Project Introduction: The newly established research centre in PESS aims to be an internationally recognized centre of excellence for research, knowledge exchange and impact in the field of sport, physical activity and health. Requirements: Essential PhD in Sports Science, Physical Education or Health Sciences, or closely related areas. Demonstrated proficiency in both quantitative and qualitative research methodologies (mixed-methods experience is highly valued). A robust portfolio of research achievements, evidenced by high-quality peer-reviewed publications. Proven ability to independently conduct comprehensive literature reviews, conceptualize research gaps, and write competitive, successful grant proposals. Highly self-motivated with the capacity to drive research projects forward independently and with minimal supervision. Proficiency in written and verbal English skills, capable of articulating complex scientific concepts to both academic and non-academic stakeholders. A strong collaborative ethos with a proven ability to work effectively within multidisciplinary research teams. Preferred A demonstrated commitment to continuous professional development, with a proactive interest in mastering advanced or emerging research methodologies. Demonstrated commitment to building a long-term career in academic research. Responsibilities: Research Design & Execution Lead the conceptualization, design, and execution of research projects within sports science, physical education, or health-related domains. Apply both quantitative and qualitative research methodologies to collect, manage, and rigorously analyze complex datasets. Conduct systematic and comprehensive literature reviews to identify research gaps, inform study designs, and support theoretical frameworks. Prepare and manage Institutional Review Board (IRB) or ethics committee applications, ensuring all research adheres strictly to ethical guidelines and data protection protocols. Grant Acquisition & Funding Take a lead role in identifying relevant funding opportunities and drafting highly competitive research grant proposals. Collaborate with the Principal Investigator (PI) to develop long-term funding strategies to sustain and expand the lab’s research portfolio. Publication & Dissemination Author and co-author high-quality manuscripts for submission to top-tier, peer-reviewed academic journals. Represent the research team by presenting findings at national and international academic conferences and symposiums. Translate complex research findings into accessible reports or presentations for practitioners, policymakers, or the general public. Leadership & Collaboration Provide guidance, training, and mentorship to junior research staff, research assistants, and graduate/undergraduate students. Independently manage day-to-day research operations, ensuring project milestones and deliverables are met on time. Foster and maintain strong collaborative networks with internal departments, external academic institutions, and industry or clinical partners. Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Research-Fellow--Solid-Waste-Valorization-_R00025981": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Solid Waste Valorization)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nGlobally recognized as a leading research and technology organization, the Nanyang Environment and Water Research Institute (NEWRI) addresses national priorities through its diverse expertise in Biotechnology and Bioprocesses, Membrane Technology, Chemicals and Materials, Resource Recovery, and Modeling & Artificial Intelligence. By harnessing its cross-cutting, interdisciplinary, and transformative capabilities, NEWRI drives innovation in water circularity and sustainability, next-generation solid waste solutions, circular economy resource recovery, climate resilience and digitalization.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/newri .   We are looking for a Research Fellow to work on the development and testing of thermal technologies for solid waste valorization. The role will focus on experimental work in laboratory and will be related to the application of heterogeneous catalysis, pyrolysis and carbon capture for solid waste treatment. Key Responsibilities: Conduct experimental work on thermal waste treatment technologies (pyrolysis, carbon capture, solid carbon and hydrogen generation). Design, procure, install and operate experimental prototypes; Investigate performance of catalysts, system configuration and process conditions that influence the yield and quality of outputs from waste; Develop improvements in catalyst formulation and system design to mitigate the factors decreasing quality and yield of outputs; Characterize samples and interpret the results (N2 adsorption, Raman, FESEM, TEM, XPS, XRD, TGA, TPO, TPR, GC-MS, etc.); Liaise with project collaborators; Publish research papers and document developed intellectual property. Report the progress to stakeholders (internal and external).   Job Requirements: PhD qualification degree in Chemical Engineering, Material Science, Environmental Engineering/Science or related field. At least 1 year of relevant experiences in relevant role / technical hands-on experience in pyrolysis, carbon capture, solid carbon and hydrogen generation. Familiarity with analytical techniques for solid/liquid characterization. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in design of experiments, interpretation of experimental results, writing papers/reports. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Energy-Storage-for-SG-Grid-_R00025990": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Energy Storage for SG Grid)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defense Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research .   Meng Research Group is seeking a Research Fellow to investigates how sodium-ion batteries can be engineered and operated to deliver grid ancillary services in Singapore, as the first step toward a sodium-ion virtual power plant. Ancillary services impose a distinctive duty cycle on storage batteries: frequent, short, high-power events, partial state-of-charge operation, and stringent response-time requirements, operating under the constraints of local weather conditions which tend to be hot and humid.     The successful candidate will work closely with senior researchers, engineers, software developers, and collaborators to address this task through three linked aims: first, characterizing the electrochemical and thermal behavior of candidate sodium-ion chemistries under realistic ancillary-service duty cycles; second, developing degradation-aware control and bidding strategies that balance market revenue against battery lifetime; and third, validating these models on existing platforms in NTU's test facilities. Key Responsibilities: Support the development and operation of deployable grid assets for Singapore, beginning with a battery energy storage system (BESS) designed to participate in the National Electricity Market's ancillary services, before scaling into a full virtual power plant (VPP) in the long term. Conduct automated materials synthesis, characterization, electrochemical testing, and data analysis for battery systems. Participate in project planning, data collection and analysis to generate high-quality, reproducible research outcomes. Prepare manuscripts for publication in high-impact journals and contribute to grant proposals and research reports. Report on research progress and/or literature update in scheduled group meetings and individual meetings. Support the overall research mission of the lab by contributing to technology development, knowledge dissemination, and translational opportunities. Job Requirements: Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field. Research experience in battery materials, electrochemistry, or materials synthesis. Experience and knowledge with robotic systems, high-throughput experimentation, or autonomous laboratory development. Demonstrated scientific productivity (peer-reviewed publications). Strong hands-on experimental and problem-solving skills, with the ability to develop, integrate, and troubleshoot automated research workflows. Good communication and teamwork skills, with the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive---Public--International-and-Alumni-Relations--PIAR---NIE-_R00025971": {
      "title": "Executive – Public, International and Alumni Relations (PIAR) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAbout The National Institute of Education (NIE)   The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here .   NIE invites suitable candidates for the position of Executive with the Public, International and Alumni Relations (PIAR) department .   The Executive supports NIE’s institutional communications by conceptualising and developing timely, engaging and platform-appropriate content, with a primary focus on video, social media posts and digital storytelling.   The role helps translates institutional content for online audiences, while providing general support for stakeholder engagement, media relations, marketing or alumni communications when required.   Responsibilities Content Creation and Digital Communications   Conceptualise, script, coordinate, produce and edit short-form video and social media content for NIE’s platforms, including reels, event highlights, explainer clips, campaign posts and other digital formats. Plan and adapt content for different social media platforms, taking into account audience needs, platform formats, post timing, captions, visual assets, accessibility considerations and performance insights. Create, schedule and refine social media content in collaboration with the social media team, ensuring that posts are accurate, timely, engaging and aligned with NIE’s tone and positioning. Support NIE departments with content and campaign needs, including coordinating copy, visuals, short-form video, digital assets or other production requirements for institutional communications.   Stakeholder and Event Support   Provide general coordination support for official visits, institutional events and guest-facing activities, including logistics, liaison, on-site support and follow-up where required. Assist with visitor experience touchpoints and other stakeholder engagement activities as required. Support institutional events such as graduation ceremonies by assisting with coordination, capturing content opportunities, and supporting related video or social media production needs.   Media Content and Communications Support Support the identification of mainstream media coverage, stories or institutional announcements that can be repurposed into social media posts, short-form videos or other digital content. Provide general support for media-related activities when required, including coordinating inputs, preparing basic materials, and adapting approved messages for use across NIE’s digital and social channels. Monitor media coverage and digital content performance to identify useful story angles, content opportunities and audience insights for NIE’s communications channels. Provide communications support for selected alumni programmes and activities, including adapting approved messages or event highlights into suitable digital content where required.    Requirements A polytechnic diploma  in Communications, Marketing, Digital Media, Film, Media Production, Journalism or a related field. Prior experience in content creation, social media management, video production, digital communications, journalism, marketing communications or agency work  is advantageous. At least two years of work experience. Strong writing, editing and visual storytelling skills, with the ability to produce clear captions, short-form scripts, social media posts, video storyboards and simple multimedia content for different audiences. Good organisational and project coordination skills, with attention to details. Ability to multi-task and work under tight timelines. Interest in digital communications, social media trends, video storytelling, institutional branding and public sector or education-related content. Proficiency with social media platforms and basic content production tools is essential, including familiarity with short-form video editing, visual design, caption writing and content scheduling tools.   Closing Date: 21 October 2026   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Research-Data-and-Analytics_R00025987-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research Data and Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore invites applications for the position of Team Lead, Research Data & Analytics within its Research & Partnerships Team. Role Overview You will lead the College’s research data and analytics function, strengthening the quality, consistency and usability of research funding, publication and related information. Working across Schools, Research & Partnerships teams and University offices, you will oversee reporting, data governance, process improvement, research data management and the Research & Partnerships intranet portfolio. Key Responsibilities: Lead Team 5’s workplan, priorities and delivery across research data reporting and analytics, research data management and intranet governance. Review data requirements and workflows, and coordinate the accurate collation, verification, reconciliation and interpretation of research funding, publication and citation data. Develop and maintain standard templates, SOPs, data definitions, master datasets and quality-control processes. Produce management reports and insights for College, School and University stakeholders. Identify and implement process improvements, dashboards and appropriate automation to reduce manual effort and strengthen transparency. Coordinate with relevant University offices on Research Driver, RISE, Interfolio–Pure and related data processes. Review research data management requirements, clarify College and School responsibilities and coordinate improvements to the College framework. Lead the development and maintenance of Research & Partnerships intranet content. Manage stakeholder requests, present progress and risks, and guide team members in delivering accurate and timely work. Undertake other related initiatives assigned by the Office. Requirements: A good University Degree in data analytics, information systems, engineering, statistics, public administration or a related discipline. At least 1 year of relevant experience in data analytics, management reporting, data governance, process improvement or research administration. Experience leading projects or small teams and coordinating across multiple stakeholders. Strong analytical, problem-solving, planning and communication skills. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and working proficiency in Power BI or an equivalent data visualisation tool. Exposure to automation, databases, scripting or research information systems will be an advantage. Strong attention to detail and the ability to establish standards, manage competing deadlines and handle sensitive information appropriately. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--AIEH-_R00025989": {
      "title": "AI Engineer (AIEH)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. The AI Engineering Hub (AIEH) aims to promote AI usage in the industry by developing AI solutions for companies. These industry engagements also serve as real-world projects for the AI Apprenticeship Programme (AIAP), which is dedicated to groom local AI talent and enhance their career with AI-related skills. We are seeking an AI Engineer to join the AIEH team. In this role, you will mentor AIAP apprentices by guiding project delivery, defining industry-relevant use cases, and providing technical coaching on cutting-edge AI technologies. You will also contribute to the development of innovative AI solutions and internal technology initiatives. The incumbent will collaborate with external partners to identify meaningful project opportunities while balancing development work with talent nurturing responsibilities, playing a key role in strengthening Singapore's AI ecosystem. Duties & Responsibilities: Drive and work on tasks stemming from AIEH industry partnership projects and other AIAP-related programmes. Lead end-to-end solution development for industry AI projects, from scoping to deployment and maintenance. Train and mentor AI apprentices during the Deep-skilling and Project phase, and other umbrella programmes. Collaborate with industry partners to identify, scope, and define project requirements and deliverables. Conduct technical assessments and feasibility studies for potential industry collaborations. Participate, prepare and execute the AIAP recruitment stages. Support AI Singapore’s industry and community-building activities by contributing to talks, seminars, workshops, journals and other outreach programmes. Requirements: Degree with at least 4 years of work experience. We welcome applicants from all disciplines who can demonstrate the following skills: End-to-End Project Delivery: Have a strong portfolio of AI/ML project(s) that showcases ability to deliver solutions from scoping and data analysis through deployment and documentation. Applied Machine Learning:  Possess deep, practical knowledge of machine learning fundamentals, with proven experience applying algorithms to solve problems in areas like NLP, Computer Vision, or on tabular data. Generative AI & LLMs:  Hands-on experience developing LLM-powered applications, including Prompt Engineering, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and fine-tuning using modern frameworks. Software Engineering Excellence:  Demonstrates expert-level Python skills and a strong commitment to Software Engineering best practices, writing code that is clean, modular, and maintainable. MLOps & Cloud Proficiency:  Fluent in the essential MLOps toolkit, including Git, Docker, and CI/CD principles. Have experience building data and model pipelines on at least one major cloud platform (AWS, Azure, or GCP). Passionate Mentor:  Eager to guide and develop the next generation of AI talent, contributing to AISG Innovation’s collaborative and supportive team culture. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-School-of-Mechanical-and-Aerospace-Engineering_R00025988": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWe are looking for part-time instructors in the areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering within the College of Engineering, School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering. Qualifications: Applicants should possess minimally a recognized MEng degree, preferably PhD, in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching Hours: Classes are mainly conducted during the day/night on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). In view of the current COVID situation, online teaching and assessments are expected to be conducted where required. In addition, applicant must be prepared to act according to the situational changes in number of CAs, CA formats, etc. when required by the School. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-PhD-Programme--CV7003-Engineering-Mathematics-and-Machine-Learning--CEE-_R00025986": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in PhD Programme, CV7003-Engineering Mathematics and Machine Learning (CEE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCEE Graduate Programmes Advertisement AY2026/27 We are looking for experienced part-time lecturers with the relevant expertise to teach in the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering. PhD Programme Courses: 1. CV7003 - Engineering Mathematics and Machine Learning Candidates should have a proven track-record in the area that they are teaching. Responsibilities: Conduct lectures. Prepare and submit editable teaching materials to the School. Prepare, administer and grade continuous assessments and exams. Student consultation. Any other required duties, where applicable. Applicants should have extensive industry and/or academic experience, a passion for teaching and should preferably possess the following requirements: Requirements: 1. Master’s degree or higher; candidates with strong relevant industry experience will be considered. 2. At least 2-3 years of teaching experience at a tertiary level is preferred. 3. Professional experience (min. 3 years) in the related field at managerial level. 4. Demonstrates a profound knowledge of related course. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Employer-Engagement_R00025984": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Employer Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Business School Graduate Studies supports a diverse population of graduate students across specialised Master's, MBAs programmes. The Employer Engagement & Operations function plays a key role in strengthening graduate employability, building strategic employer partnerships, supporting employment outcomes, and ensuring operational excellence across Graduate Studies.   Reporting to the Director of Graduate Studies, the Senior Assistant Director, Employer Engagement is responsible for leading employer engagement initiatives, developing strategic partnerships with employers and industry stakeholders, overseeing employment outcomes reporting and data governance, driving operational excellence, and leading a team to support the strategic objectives of NBS Graduate Studies.   Responsibilities: 1. Employer Engagement & Operations Leadership   Develop and implement employer engagement and operational strategies that support the objectives of NBS Graduate Studies. Lead, manage, and develop the Employer Engagement & Operations team to deliver high-quality services and achieve departmental goals. Drive strategic initiatives, process improvements, and operational enhancements to improve effectiveness, efficiency, and scalability. Oversee resource planning, budgeting, and operational performance within the portfolio.   2. Employer Partnerships and Industry Engagement   Develop and strengthen strategic relationships with employers, recruiters, alumni, industry partners, and professional organisations across key sectors and markets. Identify opportunities to enhance graduate employability through employer engagement initiatives, recruitment activities, and industry collaborations. Provide market intelligence and industry insights to support departmental planning and graduate employment objectives. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to strengthen industry partnerships and employment opportunities.   3. Employment Outcomes, Data and Compliance   Oversee employment outcomes reporting, data governance, and related compliance requirements. Ensure the accuracy, integrity, and timely reporting of employment and employer engagement data for internal and external stakeholders. Support rankings, accreditation, and institutional reporting requirements where applicable. Promote data-informed decision-making through the analysis of employment and stakeholder engagement trends.   4. Stakeholder Management and Strategic Collaboration   Partner with programme teams, student engagement teams, faculty, alumni, employers, and other stakeholders to support Graduate Studies objectives. Manage complex stakeholder relationships and service recovery situations where required. Represent Graduate Studies in discussions with senior internal and external stakeholders.   5. Strategic Projects and Continuous Improvement Lead strategic projects and change initiatives that support organisational priorities. Identify and implement opportunities to improve operational effectiveness through technology, automation, process redesign, and stakeholder engagement. Drive continuous improvement initiatives to enhance service quality and stakeholder experience.   Requirements:   Recognised Bachelor's degree from a reputable university. A postgraduate qualification or MBA would be advantageous. Significant leadership experience with a proven track record of managing teams, stakeholders, and strategic initiatives. Experience in employer engagement, business development, partnership management, industry relations, operations management, talent development, or related functions. Strong stakeholder management and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage and influence senior internal and external stakeholders. Demonstrated experience developing and managing strategic partnerships and collaborative initiatives. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making capabilities. Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills. Experience managing complex projects, operational improvement initiatives, or organisational change programmes. International exposure and experience working across diverse cultures and markets would be advantageous. Experience within higher education, executive education, graduate programmes, career services, or student-related functions would be advantageous. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage competing priorities in a fast-paced environment. Resourceful, adaptable, and able to perform effectively under pressure while maintaining a high standard of professionalism. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager-Manager-Outreach--Admissions---Scholarships_R00025985": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager/Manager Outreach, Admissions & Scholarships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering at NTU Singapore is seeking a Senior Assistant Manager / Manager for the Outreach, Admissions and Scholarships team. The individual will lead and manage the College’s Undergraduate Outreach, Admissions and Scholarship functions.   Reporting to the Head, Undergraduate, the candidate will play a critical role in leading the whole-of-College effort in outreach to prospective students and the admissions and scholarship processes. The incumbent is responsible for the advancement of the College’s student recruitment goal through the co-development and execution of outreach strategies, marketing campaigns, organising and coordinating for outreach events such as NTU Openhouse, Tea parties, etc. The candidate will also be responsible for the coordination of outreach, admission and scholarship efforts and processes across the five engineering schools and between University departments.      Key Responsibilities will include the following: Lead and manage the daily operations of the OAS team, including setting annual performance goals and implementing operational SOPs   Lead and develop outreach and engagement strategies targeted at prospective undergraduates A specialised focus on outreach initiatives, programmes and events for local polytechnic and international student recruitment Direct campus-wide undergraduate recruitment and outreach initiatives, serving as lead coordinator and executive oversight for all flagship events. The individual will also be the main organiser for CoE’s annual EASE Tea Party Cultivate and sustain strategic partnerships with pre-university institutions, polytechnics, industry leaders, alumni networks, and internal university offices to expand recruitment reach and drive collaborative outreach initiatives Support overall admissions and scholarship processes, managing intake plans and submitting weekly application and tracking reports. Spearhead integrated publicity and outreach media strategies to elevate the brand presence, visibility, and market appeal of the College’s undergraduate engineering programmes across local and international prospective student networks Any other projects and tasks assigned   Requirements: Recognized university degree in any discipline. Degree in Business / Marketing / Mass Communications is preferred. At least 8 to 10 years of relevant experience, preferably in student recruitment and outreach in the higher education sector. Experience in event execution and management. Resourceful team player with good interpersonal and people management skills. Highly motivated and meticulous individual with strong analytic and problem-solving skills and keen eye for details. Excellent organizational, time management and planning skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and tasks in an efficient, effective, and timely manner. Excellent oral and written communication and presentation skills. IT savvy and proficient in MS Office applications. Knowledge of the higher education market in Singapore and Asia-Pacific region is advantageous.     We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Plasma-Physics-for-Fusion-Energy-_R00025976": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Plasma Physics for Fusion Energy)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers.   Position Available : Research Associate Plasma physics for Fusion Energy   Key Responsibilities: The successful candidate will study electromagnetic turbulence in tokamak boundary plasmas using a three-dimensional, flux-driven, nonlinear two-fluid simulation code. The project aims to understand how electromagnetic fluctuations affect turbulence and particle and heat transport in the plasma edge and scrape-off layer. The Research Associate will be based at NTU and work closely with the plasma research group and international collaborators.   The holder will: Conduct theoretical and numerical studies of electromagnetic turbulence and transport in tokamak boundary plasmas. Develop and test physical models and numerical capabilities within a three-dimensional two-fluid simulation framework. Perform linear and nonlinear simulations on high-performance computing systems. Verify simulation results against analytical predictions, conservation laws, and benchmark cases. Analyse fluctuations, turbulent transport, and energy transfer using dedicated diagnostics. Contribute to code documentation, scientific reports, publications, and research presentations. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in physics or a closely related discipline. A sound foundation in theoretical physics, particularly electromagnetism and fluid dynamics, with basic knowledge of plasma physics. Familiarity with scientific programming and numerical methods for solving differential equations. Background in theoretical physics, with basic knowledge of plasma physics. Ability to analyse simulation data and interpret results using physical principles. Capability to work effectively in an international environment.   The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-German-Language--SoH-_R00025980-1": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in German Language (SoH)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNTU invites applications for part-time teaching of German language classes at the beginner levels (mainly: A1.1 / A1.2). Requirements Master’s degree in German or German as a Foreign Language (or equivalent German / teaching qualifications (TTI/Goethe/etc.)) Proficient in German or certified at minimum C1 level At least 1-2 years teaching experience and excellent teaching evaluations Experience in teaching in tertiary education or with adult learners preferred Knowledge in the application of IT in language teaching and experience with multimedia course materials (Moodle, Blackboard, etc.) desirable To apply, please send your application to Ms Christiane Holch and Ms Sophie Sager at  German@ntu.edu.sg Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Organic-Chemistry-Biomedical-Engineering-Materials-Science-_R00025975": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Organic Chemistry/Biomedical Engineering/Materials Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) invites applications for the position of Research Associate. Prof. Chen Peng's group conducts research in nanomedicine, with a focus on developing advanced therapeutic technologies for the treatment of metabolic disorders and cancers. The Chen Lab is looking for a Research Associate to support research activities involving nanomaterial synthesis and characterization, cell culture, molecular biology techniques, and mouse experiments.   Job Description The Research Associate will support the successful development, management, implementation, and dissemination of research projects led by the Principal Investigator (PI), Professor Chen Peng. The successful candidate will conduct research in nanomedicine, focusing on the development of advanced therapeutic technologies for the treatment of metabolic disorders and cancers. The role involves leading and supporting research activities, including nanomaterial synthesis and characterization, cell culture, molecular biology techniques, and mouse experiments. The candidate is expected to contribute to scientific publications, collaborate with research team members, and drive research projects towards successful outcomes. Applicants should possess a strong publication record and demonstrated expertise in the relevant research areas.   Key Responsibilities:  Conduct innovative and independent research in nanomedicine, focusing on the development of advanced therapeutic technologies for metabolic disorders and cancers. Take a leading role in the design, execution, analysis, and management of multidisciplinary research projects. Perform research activities involving nanomaterial synthesis and characterization, cell culture, molecular biology techniques, and mouse experiments. Analyse and interpret experimental data, troubleshoot technical challenges, and contribute to the advancement of research objectives. Develop and maintain research collaborations within NTU and with external academic and industry partners. Supervise and mentor undergraduate students and junior researchers involved in research projects. Contribute to the preparation of research proposals and grant applications. Prepare manuscripts and publish research findings in high-impact peer-reviewed journals. Present research findings at laboratory meetings, seminars, workshops, and international conferences. Support the dissemination and reporting of research outcomes and ensure the successful delivery of project milestones. Maintain accurate research records and comply with laboratory safety, ethical, and regulatory requirements.   Job Requirements:  Master’s degree in Organic Chemistry, Biomedical Engineering, Materials Science, or a related discipline. A strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals. Experience in leading research projects. Proven high-level quantitative and qualitative research skills. Proven high-level and comprehensive research skills. A significant track record in attracting research grant funding. Extensive experience in leading the design and development of research programmes. Experience in the supervision of postgraduate and undergraduate students. Experience in teaching and/or supporting research laboratories. Experience in conducting mouse experiments. Expertise in nanomaterials synthesis and characterization. Training in cell culture, molecular biology techniques, and histological analyses. Strong interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills, with the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Demonstrated ability to publish research findings in high-impact peer-reviewed journals and present research outcomes at scientific seminars and conferences. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Curriculum-Planning-and-Operations_R00025977": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Curriculum Planning and Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement.   NBS is looking for a Senior Executive to support the Undergraduate Programmes Office (UPO) in the critical function of curriculum planning and operations.  This role is involved in academic planning, coordination and administering of various academic programmes, to enable a meaningful and impactful student experience for all our undergraduates in the following areas:   Semester Timetabling Coordinate with academic divisions on semester timetabling arrangements, teaching allocations, and resource planning. Support the appointment and maintenance of course coordinator and teaching instructor records. Liaise with stakeholders to facilitate the timely implementation of teaching schedules.   Course Registration and Curriculum Planning Provide course planning and curriculum advice to students. Process course registration requests and maintain related records and documentation. Manage and update academic information on the NBS Intranet, including course outlines, course catalogues, programme structures, and curriculum requirements. Support curriculum planning exercises and the implementation of curriculum changes.   Special / Joint Programmes Administer Double Degree, Second Major and Minor programmes. Coordinate with partner schools on vacancy reservations, admissions, and course registration matters. Ensure programme information and curriculum structures are accurately maintained on the website and intranet. Provide academic advisory to students on programme requirements, curriculum planning, and academic progression. Monitor students’ academic progress and support programme completion requirements.   Change of Programme and Business Streaming Coordinate and administer Change of Programme and Business Streaming exercises. Advise students on eligibility requirements, application procedures, curriculum implications, and academic pathways. Process applications and maintain accurate records and reports. Liaise with academic divisions and stakeholders on change of programme and major allocation matters. Communicate application outcomes and support students in their academic transition.   Others Supporting MOOC administration, including credit transfer processing, and resolving student enquiries in a timely manner. Support the review and implementation of academic policies, procedures, and initiatives within the Academic Programmes portfolio. Manage and update academic information, guidelines, forms, and resources on relevant communication platforms. Assist in shared administrative duties to facilitate office operations, including the management of undergraduate email enquiries. Maintain proper documentation, records management, and archival of information. Support projects, exercises, and events such as Open House and Convocation. Review and improve work processes and maintain SOPs relating to areas of responsibility. Undertake any other duties assigned by the Reporting Officer. Requirements: Degree or Diploma holder. Related qualifications and/or working experiences in the higher education sector will be advantageous. Proficient in MS Office applications, particularly Excel and MS Teams. Able to multitask and work under pressure. Able to exercise discretion in handling confidential and sensitive information. Proactive and tactful team player with the ability to interact well with people from all levels. Possesses good critical thinking and communication skills, and a positive learning attitude. Responsible, self-motivated, meticulous, and adaptive. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Automation-Developer_R00025974": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Automation Developer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU Shared Services (NSS) is a centralized unit within Nanyang Technological University (NTU) that provides a wide range of administrative, operational, and support services to various departments and units within the university. Its primary goal is to streamline and optimize processes, enhance operational efficiency, and deliver high-quality services to support NTU's core mission of education and research. The role is a key member of NTU Shared Services (NSS) Automation team, responsible for driving automation initiatives. Collaborating closely with business stakeholders, their primary responsibility is to understand business needs, design, document, develop, test and implement low-code solutions to automate business processes. They oversee the maintenance of implemented solutions, troubleshoot issues, and implement improvements.   Additionally, the incumbent, if inclined, may be exposed to project management and peer mentoring opportunities.   Responsibilities Collaborate with business and technical stakeholders to understand requirements and design low-code solution Design visual models, business process workflows, user interfaces and data models Document business process workflows, design specification, technical details, user guide Utilize low-code platforms (e.g. UiPath, Outsystems) to develop end-to-end automated applications Ensure data integrity, security and proper error handling Perform testing and quality assurance activities including creating and executing test cases, debugging and troubleshoot issues Provide support and guidance to stakeholders during development, deployment and maintenance phases Provide individual and peer mentoring as appropriate and develop capabilities within the team, function and organization   Requirements Diploma/Degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering Proficiency in UiPath and Power Query Experience in automation development roles Good interpersonal, communication, and organization skills Experience in programming Experience in Outsystems Knowledge of data integration, APIs, data transformation   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTUOne-North-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Commercial-Leasing_R00025972": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Commercial Leasing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) oversees the management of estate leases and commercial services (such as leasing of spaces for F&B, amenities and lifestyle services), and auxiliary services (such as car parks, shuttle bus services) for NTU’s main campus, Novena campus and NTU@One-North campus. In addition, it is dedicated to enhancing and optimizing the utilization and operations of NTU’s hospitality assets, ensuring they meet global standards and deliver exceptional experiences.   The Deputy Director drives operational excellence, strategic execution, and service innovation across NTU’s hospitality assets. This pivotal leadership role translates high-level campus vibrancy and sustainability strategies into robust operational plans, directly manages outsourced vendor performance, and fosters a vibrant, inclusive campus community.   Key Responsibilities Operational Strategy & Execution: Translate the office's long-term vision into actionable business plans and operational roadmaps for commercial leasing, hospitality, and transportation, aligning with NTU's overarching goals. Campus Experience & Placemaking: Lead initiatives to enhance student, employee, and visitor experiences; implement best market practices to foster a vibrant, inclusive, and welcoming campus culture. Commercial & Lease Management: Optimize revenue and lease yields across commercial spaces (F&B, retail, lifestyle amenities) and develop robust metrics to measure commercial investments and performance. Auxiliary Services Oversight: Manage contract performance and service delivery of outsourced vendors for campus-wide carparks and shuttle bus services, driving smart, sustainable, and green transport solutions. Hospitality Asset Optimization: Direct the operations, maintenance, refurbishment, and financial sustainability of key hospitality assets (e.g., Nanyang Executive Centre, Campus Clubhouse) to ensure premier, self-financing dining and accommodation experiences. Risk Management & Governance: Proactively assess, monitor, and mitigate operational, financial, and safety risks across all commercial, auxiliary, and hospitality portfolios.   Job Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Hospitality Management, Real Estate, or a related discipline. 12–15 years of progressive management experience in hospitality, property management, commercial operations, or campus services, with at least 5 years in a significant leadership role. Proven track record in managing large-scale, KPI-driven outsourced vendor contracts and executing service excellence standards. Strong expertise in budget management, revenue optimization, contract negotiation, and business planning within a diverse service portfolio. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills with demonstrated success in building collaborative partnerships with students, university administration, commercial operators, and external agencies.    We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--LKCMedicine-_R00025973-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are seeking a Research Assistant to join our research team to facilitate and support the research activities, which focus on advancing understanding of ageing patterns in Asian populations and their potential mechanisms with disease. The candidate will provide comprehensive support to the Principal Investigator and research team by overseeing the day-to-day coordination and execution of research projects. The candidate will support scientific project planning, research operations administrative coordination, and collaboration with internal and external collaborators to ensure projects are delivered efficiently, accurately and on schedule.   Key Responsibilities:   Coordinate and monitor the research projects, including timelines, milestones, deliverables and supporting documentation Track project progress and identify delays or operational issues, following up with relevant team members to ensure timely resolution Maintain accurate and up-to-date project, research and laboratory records to support grant reporting, audits and compliance requirements Oversee day-to-day laboratory operations, including management of equipment, research materials, samples, procurement and inventory Coordinate meetings, including preparation of agendas and minutes, consolidation of project updates and follow up on action items Ensure compliance with institutional requirements, research agreement and governance, laboratory safety standards and relevant ethical approvals Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies :   Bachelor’s degree in Biology, Biochemistry, Life Sciences, or related fields. Fresh graduates are welcome to apply Experience in research project coordination, laboratory management or research administration would be advantageous Good organisational and documentation skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects, priorities and deadlines. Able to work independently and as a team player Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturers--TEUP---NIE-_R00025962": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturers (TEUP) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNational Institute of Education - Part-time Lecturers (TEUP) The National Institute of Education (NIE) invites applications for the position of Part-time Lecturer in the Office of Teacher Education & Undergraduate Programmes (TEUP). Job Description Part-Time Lecturers are engaged to lead group discussions and activities, while creating a safe and reflective space for open dialogue that promotes both personal and professional growth. Please refer to https://www.ntu.edu.sg/nie/ for more information on NIE courses/programmes. Requirements   A Master’s degree, preferably in Counselling and Guidance or Applied Psychology Other Information Part-time Lecturers will be paid on an hourly basis at the rates prescribed for the various courses/programmes. The engagement will be on a semester basis (January to June, July to December).   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.  Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Civil-Engineering-Ocean-Engineering-_R00025969-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Civil Engineering/Ocean Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Research Fellow position (equivalent to Postdoctoral Fellow in many countries/regions) is available in the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE), Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore. The successful candidate will work on research related to the hydrodynamic behavior of floating structures.   Key Responsibilities: Conduct wave flume tests and develop numerical/analytical models of floating structures. Prepare project reports and publish scientific papers in peer-reviewed journals. Assist the PI in preparing research proposals and supervising research students.   Job Requirements : PhD degree in Civil Engineering, Ocean Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline. Research experience in hydrodynamics and structural dynamics. Strong publication record in relevant research areas. Effective writing and communication skills. Experience in supervising research students and preparing research proposals will be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Materials-Physics-_R00025968": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum Materials Physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges.   The Belopolski Research Group (QuantumX Labs) is hiring ambitious & creative Research Fellows to explore topological quantum materials. Our group aims to discover new topological quantum phases of matter, explore their physics and apply them to address challenges in electronics, photonics, quantum computing, catalysis and biology. We use molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) to synthesize atomically precise crystals, we integrate them with two-dimensional exfoliated materials, and we characterize them using transport and angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES). We have immediate need for enthusiastic postdocs to synthesize novel quantum anomalous Hall phases by MBE, characterize altermagnets and p -wave magnets by ARPES, pursue scalable wafer-scale moiré epitaxy, develop epitaxial superconductors for quantum computing and integrate machine learning for automated high-throughput MBE. We are particularly excited to recruit postdocs with experience in optics, two-dimensional materials and a strong theoretical background. Applicants should have a Ph.D. in quantum physics, electrical engineering or a related field.   Key Responsibilities The Research Fellow will pursue scientific research broadly on topological quantum materials at QuantumX Labs, the research group of Prof. Ilya Belopolski, https://www.quantumx.science . Researchers will have the opportunity to, Synthesize atomically precise thin films of new topological materials using molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) Develop innovative approaches to accelerate MBE materials development using in situ characterization & machine learning Integrate epitaxial synthesis with exfoliated two-dimensional materials & devices Characterize resistivity, Hall response, non-linear transport and magnetization Explore electronic structure with angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES) at synchrotrons such as Diamond Light Source in the UK or the Advanced Light Source in the USA Develop theoretical models of topological materials to understand & interpret experimental data Leverage nanofabrication facilities & collaborate with other leading research groups at the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) and the School of Physical & Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Collaborate worldwide to identify new candidate materials, perform ab initio calculations and complement our results with additional experimental techniques Build out additional in-house experimental capabilities in optics, microwaves and quantum sensing   The researcher is also encouraged to bring in physics & techniques from their Ph.D. which augment or resonate with the interests of our group & the community at NTU.   Job Requirements   Ph.D. in quantum physics, electrical engineering or a related discipline; familiarity with superconductivity, magnetic skyrmions, topological insulators, Mott insulators and/or quantum spin liquids Technical experience with experimental synthesis, transport & optics techniques, such as: Low-temperature transport & characterization by PPMS, MPMS and/or dilution fridge Second harmonic generation, photoluminescence, Raman spectroscopy & other optical techniques Materials synthesis by molecular beam epitaxy (MBE), pulsed laser deposition (PLD) etc. Exfoliation & device fabrication of two-dimensional materials such as graphene & chalcogenides Strong theoretical & mathematical background Interest in leading scientific breakthroughs, as well as working closely with a team, to deepen our understanding of emergent phenomena in quantum physics and pioneer applications to electronics, photonics, quantum computing, catalysis and biology   We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
