    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Project-Officer--Animal-Movement-Ecology-_R00025967": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Project Officer (Animal Movement Ecology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Asian School of the Environment (ASE) at Nanyang Technological University is an interdisciplinary school that aims to be a world leader in environmental research focused on Asian environmental challenges. The ASE integrates earth and environmental life science, ecology, engineering and technology, human ecology, humanities, and the social sciences to address key issues of the environment and sustainability.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/ase.   We are hiring a research assistant/project officer to provide operational support for the establishment and running of a new lab in movement ecology and conservation. The RA will be supporting a project on tracking shorebirds in Southeast Asia and other projects on tracking urban birds in Singapore. This role covers a variety of work and responsibilities, including field work, lab work, data management and administrative tasks.   Key Responsibilities: Provide general administrative support and conduct procurement related to the lab’s ongoing research projects. Manage the inventory of laboratory and field consumables and oversee equipment maintenance Assist in applying for permits for fieldwork and import of specimens Assist in laboratory work, including identifying macrozoobenthic species from sediment samples and determining their biomass, and DNA metabarcoding. Support field operations, including bird catching and deployment of bird trackers in the field. Manage, curate, and maintain databases for research data and biological specimens. Assist in ensuring lab operations compliant with university health, safety, and environmental regulations. Write and update Risk Assessments and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for both lab work and fieldwork. Coordinate logistics of overseas fieldwork Provide training and technical support to students conducting research in the lab   Job Requirements: Possess a Polytechnic Diploma with 3 years of relevant working experience or Bachelor’s degree in Ecology, Environmental Science, Biology, Animal Behaviour, or a closely related field. Organized and meticulous, able to curate and manage large amounts of specimens and data . Good written and oral communication skills. Highly independent, proactive and a good team player Preferred Qualifications (Advantageous but not required): Basic skills and experience in basic molecular taxonomy, such as DNA extraction, PCR, running gels, and processing of sequence data. Prior field experience in bird handling, including mist-netting, bird ringing, and tracker deployment. Familiarity with spatial data, GIS software or basic programming in R for handling ecological data Familiar with relational databases, data quality control and cleaning Familiar with local university’s administration, procurement systems and regulations We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Integrated-Assessment-Modeling-_R00025966": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Integrated Assessment Modeling)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nASE is a diverse school focusing on the connections between geosciences, ecology, society and Earth systems. Our approach integrates these disciplines to examine big environmental challenges both in Southeast Asia and globally. We conduct cutting-edge research on topics that include ecology, geohazards, climate change, sea-level rise, environmental sustainability, conservation of environment and biodiversity, and interactions between environment and society. For more information on ASE please visit https://www.ntu.edu.sg/ase .   The Yanyan Cheng research group is seeking a Research Fellow. This position is part of a Singapore NRF funded research project hosted by ASE. The Research Fellow will help advance research in Regional Integrated Assessment Model (IAM) modeling, especially the GCAM. This research theme can help the understanding of the complex interactions within the Land-Energy-Water nexus, and how land and water constraints shape global and regional pathways toward a resilient future. The research will be shared through peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations that will highlight NTU's contributions to building a resilient future.   This is a one-year appointment and potentially renewable based on performance and funding availability.   Key Responsibilities: Collect and harmonize multi-source datasets for model calibration and validation. Develop new model functionalities in GCAM, with a focus on land, water, and energy systems. Design and conduct scenario simulations to examine how climate and resource constraints influence regional resilience pathways. Participate in mentoring students and RAs on integrated assessment modeling and related workflows. Job Requirements: A PhD in Environmental Science. Posse extensive relevant experience in integrated assessment model (IAM) development and application, specifically with the GCAM. Experience should include designing scenario analyses, developing new model functionalities, and conducting model simulations to evaluate climate mitigation and adaptation pathways. Highly proficient in the GCAM framework, including its land-use (AgLU), water, and energy modules. Familiarity with the GCAM-USA or other regionalized GCAM variants, as well as other integrated assessment or earth system models, is highly desirable. Advanced programming skills in R and Python for data processing and visualization. Strong quantitative and analytical skills in working with large-scale geospatial datasets and socio-economic databases. Proficiency in high-performance computing (HPC) environments and scripting (e.g., Bash). As the position requires stakeholder engagement in English, candidate should have good written and oral communication skills in English. Candidate should have published scientific papers in high-quality research journals. Should be enthusiastic in research and have good spirit in teamwork and collaboration. Ability to work independently, develop solutions under strict timelines, meticulous attention to detail, and excellent organizational and time management skills.   ASE seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-Biomedical-Sciences-and-BioBusiness--SBS-_R00025965": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in Biomedical Sciences and BioBusiness (SBS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA research-intensive public university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in the Engineering, Business, Science, Humanities, Arts, & Social Sciences, and Graduate colleges. It also has a medical school, the Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine, established jointly with Imperial College London.   NTU is also home to world-class autonomous institutes – the National Institute of Education, S Rajaratnam School of International Studies, Earth Observatory of Singapore, and Singapore Centre for Environmental Life Sciences Engineering – and various leading research centres such as the Nanyang Environment & Water Research Institute (NEWRI) and Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N).   Ranked amongst the world’s top universities by QS, NTU has also been named the world’s top young university for the past seven years. The University’s main campus is frequently listed among the Top 15 most beautiful university campuses in the world and has 57 Green Mark-certified (equivalent to LEED-certified) buildings, of which 95% are certified Green Mark Platinum. Apart from its main campus, NTU also has a campus in Novena, Singapore’s healthcare district.   Under the NTU Smart Campus vision, the University harnesses the power of digital technology and tech-enabled solutions to support better learning and living experiences, the discovery of new knowledge, and the sustainability of resources.   School of Biological Sciences Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Part Time Lecturer   The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), College of Science (CoS) at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) in Singapore seeks outstanding candidates to apply for a dedicated and knowledgeable Part-Time Lecturer to join our faculty team, who will be responsible for coordinating and delivering the courses BS3203 Reshaping Healthcare with Engineering and Digital Revolution and BS4209 MedTech Business Implementation and Market. This position requires a passion for teaching and a deep understanding of MedTech in BioBusiness to provide high-quality education to our students. The successful candidate will be responsible for preparing and delivering lectures and tutorials, designing and administering assessments, including quizzes and examinations, and marking assessments.   SBS is searching for individuals with a well-deﬁned research vision and an outstanding track record of publications in top journals. The successful candidate will establish and maintain an independent extramurally funded research program. The successful candidate is expected to show a strong commitment to departmental undergraduate and graduate mentoring and teaching.   SBS and CoS seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. Emoluments The candidate will be offered an attractive compensation package and will be supported by a generous start-up funds and laboratory space. Closing Date:    The closing date for applications is 6 November 2026.   Application Procedure   Interested applicants are invited to submit through the NTU career portal a completed application package which include: Cover letter, Curriculum vitae, Publication list, A summary of the future research, teaching and service plans, and The names/emails of three individuals willing to provide letters of reference.   The post applied for should be clearly stated in your application.   If there are any enquiries, you seek more information from Dr Ardina Gruber (Associate Chair (Academic), Gruber@ntu.edu.sg). Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturers--PCHD---NIE-_R00025961": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturers (PCHD) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNational Institute of Education - Part-time Lecturers (PCHD) The National Institute of Education (NIE) invites applications for the position of Part-time Lecturer in the Psychology and Child & Human Development (PCHD) Department. Job Description Part-Time Lecturers are engaged for teaching duties such as conducting lectures, tutorials and practicum supervision. Please refer to https://www.ntu.edu.sg/nie/ for more information on NIE courses/programmes. Requirements   A Master’s degree. Experience in teaching NIE courses/programmes.    Candidates who do not possess the above qualifications but have proven skills/industry experience are also invited to apply.  Other Information Part-time Lecturers will be paid on an hourly basis at the rates prescribed for the various courses/programmes. The engagement will be on a semester basis (January to June, July to December).   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.  Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
