    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Manager--Science--Engineering--Business-Administration--Public-Administration-_R00025949": {
      "title": "Project Manager (Science/ Engineering/ Business Administration/ Public Administration)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe ExxonMobil-NTU-A*STAR Corporate Lab at ERI@N (Energy Research Institute @ NTU) is a S$60 million research collaboration between NTU, A*STAR, and ExxonMobil, focused on advancing lower-emissions technologies in areas such as biomass conversion, carbon capture, hydrogen production, and carbon-incorporated concrete. We are seeking a Project Manager to oversee all phases of the Corporate Lab's research portfolio. The role encompasses full project lifecycle management across five research programmes, including budgeting, accounting, financial reporting, preparation of progress and annual reports for the Implementing Agency (NRF) and ExxonMobil, and coordination with all key stakeholders — Principal Investigators, A*STAR, NRF, and ExxonMobil. The Project Manager will also lead governance meeting coordination, KPI/milestone tracking, and IP outcome reporting, and will directly supervise the Project Officer. Key Responsibilities : Serve as the primary point of contact and coordination hub between the Corporate Lab's Principal Investigators, ERI@N management, NTU's Research Support Office (RSO), the Implementing Agency (NRF), A*STAR (ISCE²), and ExxonMobil stakeholders for all project management and administrative matters. Oversee end-to-end project management across all five research programmes of the Corporate Lab — encompassing project initiation, planning, execution, monitoring and control, and closure — in alignment with IAF-ICP grant conditions and NTU's project management frameworks. Lead the preparation, consolidation, and submission of all progress reports, annual reports, milestone reports, and final reports to the Implementing Agency (NRF) and ExxonMobil, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and adherence to reporting schedules. Manage the Corporate Lab's budget across all research programmes: prepare detailed budget plans and forecasts, monitor expenditure against approved budgets, process budget revisions and reallocations, perform financial reconciliation, and ensure compliance with NTU and IAF-ICP financial governance rules. Oversee all accounting activities including raising purchase orders, reviewing claims and reimbursements, managing vendor and consultant payments, and liaising with NTU's Finance Office to ensure timely and accurate financial reporting. Prepare and manage all formal correspondence with the Implementing Agency (NRF), A*STAR, and ExxonMobil, including official notifications, requests for extensions or amendments, audit responses, and intellectual property (IP) disclosures. Coordinate and support the organisation of Corporate Lab governance meetings, including Governing Board meetings, Technical Review meetings, and Annual Review meetings — preparing agendas, minutes, action logs, and presentations. Track and report on all key performance indicators (KPIs), milestones, deliverables, and IP outcomes (technical disclosures, patents, prototypes, publications) across the five research programmes. Identify project risks, develop mitigation strategies, and escalate critical issues in a timely manner to ERI@N management and the PI team. Ensure full compliance with NTU institutional policies, NRF grant conditions, and regulatory requirements throughout the life of the Corporate Lab, including timely submission of audit documentation and project closeout reports. Supervise and mentor the Project Officer / Senior Project Officer in their day-to-day tasks, ensuring proper delegation and quality of work. Job Requirements: Bachelor's or higher degree in Science, Engineering, Business Administration, or related field. Minimum 3 years of experience in research project management or grants administration. Prior experience with Singapore government-funded research grants (NRF, A*STAR, IAF-ICP) is preferred. Strong budget management and financial reporting skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills; ability to interface with academic, government, and corporate stakeholders. Proficiency in MS Office and project management tools. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Assistant-Manager--Outreach--Admissions---Scholarships_R00025946": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, Outreach, Admissions & Scholarships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering at NTU Singapore is seeking a Senior Executive / Assistant Manager for the Undergraduate Outreach, Admissions, and Scholarships team. Reporting to the Lead, Outreach, Admissions & Scholarships, the candidate will play a central role in planning, leading, and executing holistic student recruitment, outreach, promotion, digital media, and engagement strategies targeted at prospective undergraduates. This role also serves as a key liaison across Engineering Schools to align recruitment strategies, promotion, and implementation plans.   Key responsibilities include (but not limited to): Develop, plan, and lead undergraduate recruitment and outreach strategies to achieve College objectives.   Conceptualise, write copy for, and produce UG marketing collaterals (UG brochures, slide decks, offer EDMs, top graduate features, etc.)  Draft and implement the annual social media plan and support the production of undergraduate publicity and admissions videos.   Update and maintain general and outreach pages on the CoE website and intranet.   Manage collateral inventory, coordinate photoshoots, and oversee external production vendors. Support the team’s outreach programmes and efforts to local and international students.     Conduct post-event and campaign analytics to extract data-driven insights for continuous improvement.   Build strong relationships with schools, faculty, alumni, and industry partners.   Undertake ad-hoc projects assigned by the Office Requirements: Recognised university degree in any discipline. At least 1 to 3 years of work experience, preferably in Outreach, Student Recruitment, Student Engagement in the higher education industry. Entry-level candidates with relevant internship experience are welcome. Experience in event execution and management. Resourceful team player with good interpersonal, stakeholder engagement and coordination skills. Highly motivated and meticulous individual with strong analytic and problem-solving skills and keen eye for details. Excellent organisational, time management and planning skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and tasks in an efficient, effective, and timely manner. Excellent oral and written communication and presentation skills. IT savvy and proficient in MS office applications. Prior knowledge of content management systems is advantageous Knowledge of the higher education market in Singapore and Asia-Pacific region is advantageous.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager--Programme-Operations-_R00025947-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager (Programme Operations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement.   Senior Executive / Assistant Manager (Programme Operations), Nanyang Executive Education   Nanyang Executive Education (NEE), a division of Nanyang Business School, delivers enterprise and public executive learning programmes for mid- to senior-level professionals across industries. Our programmes are delivered by world-class faculty and industry practitioners, supporting lifelong learning, leadership development, and skills transformation.   Job Purpose   This is a key operational role in the delivery and governance of FlexiMasters programmes, including open-enrolment and corporate-sponsored cohorts. The role is responsible for overseeing end-to-end programme operations, coordinating delivery activities across stakeholders, and ensuring high standards of service quality, financial stewardship, and compliance.   As an operational team member for FlexiMasters programmes, the role provides execution oversight and coordination across multiple concurrent programmes, supporting the effective scaling and sustainability of NEE’s programme portfolio.   Key Responsibilities: Manage programme delivery of FlexiMasters programmes from planning through completion. Coordinate programme delivery activities across faculty, internal teams, vendors, and external stakeholders. Provide operational support to ensure delivery consistency, issue resolution, and service quality across programmes. Manage programme budgets and ensure timely invoicing and revenue reconciliation. Ensure compliance with SkillsFuture Singapore funding requirements and University policies, including audit readiness and accurate reporting. Monitor programme performance and contribute to operational improvements that enhance efficiency, governance, and participant experience. Support the operational delivery and servicing of corporate-sponsored FlexiMasters cohorts, working with internal stakeholders to ensure delivery requirements and service standards are met.   Requirements: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised institution. Relevant experience in programme, project, or operations management within lifelong learning, training, or related professional services environments. Experience managing multiple concurrent programmes or projects with diverse stakeholders and delivery requirements. Strong organisational, planning, and prioritisation skills, with the ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced environment. Effective communication and stakeholder management skills. Attention to detail, sound judgement, and a strong sense of accountability for outcomes. Familiarity with SkillsFuture funding frameworks and compliance requirements is advantageous.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Safe-control-and-robotics-_R00025945": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Safe control and robotics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects.   Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges.   For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee   We are looking for Project Officer to conduct research in the areas of safety-critical control theory and machine learning. The role will focus on combining new theory or method in nonlinear system control and state-of-the-art machine learning systems, with applications to various robotic systems. Key Responsibilities:   Conduct research in the area of control theory and machine learning Conduct experiments on different robotic platforms International collaborations in the above areas Publish papers in related top journals and conferences   Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in control theory, machine learning, robotics, or related field Familiarity with nonlinear systems and control theory/state-of-the-art machine learning systems (diffusion, transformers, etc.)/robotics. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in programing (e.g., Python) and machine learning tools (e.g., PyTorch) Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Science-Computer-Engineering-Electronics-Engineering-AI-Machine-Learning-_R00025948": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Science/Computer Engineering/Electronics Engineering/AI/Machine Learning)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research on 3D/4D scene reconstruction and rendering (e.g., NeRF, 3D Gaussian Splatting, novel view synthesis) and on scene understanding and interaction. Develop generative AI for video and 3D/4D generation, world models, and vision-language models (VLMs) / vision-language-action (VLA) systems, with supporting large-scale data pipelines. Publish in top-tier venues, contribute to open-source releases, mentor junior researchers, and report project progress. Job Requirements: PhD degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electronics Engineering, AI, Machine Learning or equivalent. Strong research record in computer vision / machine learning, with solid programming skills (e.g., Python, PyTorch) and demonstrated ability to conduct innovative research. Independent, highly analytical, proactive, and a strong team player Excellent verbal and written communication skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Material-Science---Civil-Engineering---Chemical-Engineering-_R00024553": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Material Science / Civil Engineering / Chemical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. ERI@N has multiple Interdisciplinary Research Programmes which focus on translational Research, Development & Deployment which focus on specific area of the energy value chain, and a number of Living labs and Testbeds which facilitate large scale technology deployment enabling validation and demonstration of real-world applications. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/erian We are looking for Research Associate (RA) to work on carbon enhanced concrete materials. The role will focus on research and development of new materials related to the project. Key Responsibilities: The RA will be responsible for new carbon materials enhanced concrete development (e.g. via incorporation of various carbon materials where they are securely stored but also enhance concrete property in different ways); The RA will also be in charge of testing of all relevant aspects of advanced concrete material developed; The RA will also be conducting cost-benefit and LCA analysis of the material developed. The appointee will conduct research on carbon material enhanced concretes with various forms of carbon. The developed materials must be demonstrated in suitable large-scale applications. Job Requirements: The candidate must graduate with Master Degree from a reputable university in material science, civil, chemical engineering or related fields with relevant research experience/expertise and strong journal publication record. Prior experience on similar research and strong record of journal publication and/or IP generation will be favourably reviewed. The candidate should have relevant experiment skills such as nano and/or microstructural based material tailoring, novel and sustainable concrete development, geopolymer or other green cement, mechanical testing, thermal and/or electrical conductivity testing, and material chemical and micro-structural analysis. The candidate can have opportunity to interact/collaborate with other colleagues within PI’s group. The topics currently are actively pursed in the group include self-healing material, self-sensing material, sustainable cementless material with regional waste/by-products, 3D printable concrete material, low carbon footprint concrete with carbon materials from different sources and their structural applications. Extensive knowledge on carbon material enhanced concrete/geopolymer material Familiar with relevant analytical and experimental technique/skills, hands-on experience as well as solid theoretical background; excellent paper/report writing skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Mechanical-Engineering---Materials-Science-and-Engineering---Manufacturing-Engineering---Aerospace-Engineering-_R00025898": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Mechanical Engineering / Materials Science and Engineering / Manufacturing Engineering / Aerospace Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world.   For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research .   We are looking for a Project Officer to support research and development in surface engineering and heat exchangers for energy-efficient thermal systems. The position focuses on the development, optimization, and characterization of engineered surfaces and surface treatment processes to enhance heat-transfer performance. The candidate will be involved in surface fabrication, material and surface characterization, experimental testing, and optimization of processing parameters.   In addition, the candidate will contribute to the design and experimental evaluation of heat exchangers and prototypes, including the development and scale-up of surface engineering processes for practical applications. This includes conducting thermal-fluid experiments, developing and operating experimental test setups, analysing performance data, and supporting prototype validation under controlled and practical operating conditions. The candidate will also work closely with the Principal Investigator, research team, and industry collaborators to support technology development and translation. The outcomes of this work will contribute to the development of scalable and energy-efficient heat exchanger technologies, while strengthening the University's research capabilities in surface engineering, heat transfer, and thermal-fluid engineering.   Key Responsibilities:   The candidate will conduct experimental research in the development of ultrascalable surface engineering method to enhance flow boiling of refrigerant. The key responsibilities and job scope are:   Conduct research and development in surface engineering, system cooling and heat exchangers. Develop and optimize engineered surfaces and surface treatment processes for enhanced thermal performance. Design, fabricate and characterize surface-engineered components and prototypes. Plan and conduct thermal-fluid experiments to evaluate heat-transfer and system performance. Develop, modify and operate experimental test rigs, instrumentation and measurement systems. Perform surface and material characterization to establish the relationship between surface characteristics and thermal performance. Analyse experimental data and identify opportunities for process and design optimization. Support the scale-up of laboratory-developed surface engineering processes towards larger-scale prototypes. Conduct performance testing under both controlled laboratory and practical operating conditions. Support prototype installation, testing and field performance validation in collaboration with industry partners. Prepare technical reports, research papers, presentations and other project deliverables.   Job Requirements:   Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies :   Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science and Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a related field, Basic knowledge of materials science, heat transfer, and surface chemistry and engineering, with exposure to two-phase flow and heat transfer applications being an advantage, Familiarity with chemical treatment, alloy development, and material characterization techniques, Understanding of microstructural characterization techniques, including optical microscopy, scanning electron microscopy (SEM), X-ray diffraction (XRD), thermal analysis, and mechanical testing, is preferred, Experience in surface engineering, surface modification, chemical processing, electrochemical techniques, or micro/nanostructured surface development is an advantage, Familiarity with experimental design, laboratory testing, data acquisition, and data analysis for materials and thermal performance evaluation, Exposure to CAD software and engineering design tools, with experience in design for additive manufacturing being an advantage, Ability to support the design, fabrication, and testing of thermal management devices and engineering prototypes, Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and manage multiple research tasks, Good teamwork and communication skills, with the ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment, and Excellent writing and communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    }
  },
